var tipuesearch = {"pages":[{"title":" Rakali ","text":"Rakali Rakali is a GPU-native Fortran solver for coastal, estuarine, and tidal applications. It supports structured Cartesian grids (2D barotropic, 3D hydrostatic multilayer, non-hydrostatic) and unstructured triangular grids (2D barotropic, 3D hydrostatic multilayer with KNP central-upwind). GPU parallelism is expressed with do concurrent + OpenACC, portable across NVHPC (GPU and multicore), gfortran, and ifx. Two grid backends Structured (Cartesian): HLL/HLLC + hydrostatic reconstruction, A-grid. Unstructured (triangular): KNP central-upwind, Green-Gauss gradients. The full architectural overview, repository map, and run lifecycle live in docs/codebase/INDEX.md . The design contract is in src/core/coastal/README.md . Building module load cmake nvhpc\ncmake -B build -S .\ncmake --build build cd build && ctest --output-on-failure Key CMake options: Option Default Description RAKALI_ENABLE_GPU ON OpenACC GPU offload via NVHPC RAKALI_ENABLE_PYTHON OFF Build the librakali.so Python/Julia FFI RAKALI_GPU_ARCH cc70 Target GPU compute capability (cc70/80/90) RAKALI_ENABLE_DOUBLE ON Double-precision working precision The full list lives in CMakeLists.txt . Do not pass -j N to ctest when the GPU build is active — every worker shares one GPU, so parallel test execution produces spurious failures and hangs. Building with -j is fine; only ctest -j N is the problem. Use ctest -R rakali for the ~164-test rakali-only subset (~60 s) for fast regression checks. Documentation Per-module and per-procedure documentation is generated by FORD from !! docstrings in the source — that is the canonical reference. Hand-maintained synthesis documents complement it: docs/CLOSURE_MATRIX.md — which closure/scheme is active on which path, plus tunable knobs (drift-checked by tools/check_closure_matrix.py ). docs/CAPABILITIES_AND_LIMITATIONS.md — what is shipped, what is deferred. docs/REFERENCE.md — physics + namelist reference. FORTRAN_STYLE.md — coding style and the do concurrent + OpenACC GPU programming model. docs/codebase/CONCEPTS.md — glossary of acronyms. docs/codebase/INDEX.md — repository map and run lifecycle. Comments prefixed with !! are documentation comments processed by FORD. Comments prefixed with a single ! are ordinary code comments and are not rendered. Please do not use !! for casual code comments. Dependencies Fortran compiler — NVHPC (GPU + multicore), gfortran, or ifx. CMake ≥ 3.22. NetCDF-Fortran. Internet access at configure time to pull pic and test-drive . Pre-commit workflow Before each commit, in order: pre-commit run --all — formatting (whitespace, trailing newlines, end-of-file). fortitude check — Fortran static checks (also wired up as a pre-commit hook). ctest — full test suite. Never pass -j N on the GPU build. Re-read the synthesis docs ( CLOSURE_MATRIX.md , the design-contract READMEs, docs/howto/ , CAPABILITIES_AND_LIMITATIONS.md ) and update anything that drifted. When code and docs disagree, the code is authoritative. When adding a new capability: namelist knob (default off, preserves bit-identity) → kernel gated on the knob → unit test (analytical tests are high-leverage) → format/lint/test → one commit per capability, one PR per capability. Contributing Contributions are welcome. Please follow the conventions documented in FORTRAN_STYLE.md and the design contract in src/core/coastal/README.md . File a PR against main — FORD docs are rebuilt on every PR merged to main . License See LICENSE in the source tree. Developer Info Jorge Luis Galvez Vallejo","tags":"home","url":"index.html"},{"title":"hgrid_t – Rakali ","text":"type, public :: hgrid_t Inherited by type~~hgrid_t~~InheritedByGraph type~hgrid_t hgrid_t type~state_t state_t type~state_t->type~hgrid_t grid type~solver_handle_t solver_handle_t type~solver_handle_t->type~state_t state Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Sol