 public :: mass_out_tracked = .false. Set .true. once the solver has accumulated mass_out .\nCovered paths: 2D-barotropic SSP-RK2 fused path + coastal\nmultilayer nz>1.  Not set by: nz=1 ML fused fast path (safe\nraw-drift fallback — see solver note), semi-implicit, generic-RK. real(kind=wp), public :: mass_src = 0.0_wp Cumulative volume ADDED to the domain by surface sources since\nt=0 (m³, positive = added), accumulated per RK stage from\nprecipitation ( h += dt·P ), the evaporative mass sink\n( evap_mass_sink=.true. ; negative contribution), and the sponge\nh-relaxation Δh.  Feeds budget%mass_src in rki_console_stats so the residual (total−ref) + out − src stays ~round-off on\nforced runs instead of growing monotonically with the forcing. logical, public :: mass_src_tracked = .false. Set .true. once the solver has accumulated mass_src for the\ncurrent run.  Same coverage as mass_out_tracked : 2D-barotropic\nfused path + coastal multilayer nz>1.  The closed budget\n( budget%mass_active ) is enabled in the console only when BOTH\nflags are set. logical, public :: use_hllc = .false. Use HLLC (with contact wave for transverse momentum) instead\nof HLL for the barotropic Riemann flux.  Structured-only —\nthe unstructured solver always uses KNP central-upwind, which\nresolves contact discontinuities natively.  Default .false. . logical, public :: use_linear_bottom_drag = .false. Use linear (Rayleigh) bottom drag instead of quadratic Manning. logical, public :: wind_surface_layer = .false. Apply wind stress to the top layer (surface-concentrated) instead\nof the depth-uniform barotropic mode.  Multilayer only. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: bytes => barotropic_state_bytes private pure function barotropic_state_bytes (this) result(nbytes) Counted allocatable footprint of the barotropic slot (0 for any\nunallocated array).  One arr_bytes term per allocatable — add a\nterm here whenever a new array joins the type. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( barotropic_state_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=int64) procedure, public, non_overridable :: destroy => barotropic_state_destroy private  subroutine barotropic_state_destroy (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( barotropic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this procedure, public, non_overridable :: init => barotropic_state_init private  subroutine barotropic_state_init (this, grid) Allocate all arrays at the grid size, zero-filled.  Scalars\n( manning_n , coriolis_f ) are populated by state_init_from_config from the namelist after this routine returns. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( barotropic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid Source Code type :: barotropic_state_t !! Depth-integrated conserved variables and the workspace they !! produce / consume each step. ! Conserved variables -- SoA layout: (nx_total, ny_total) real ( wp ), allocatable :: h (:, :) !! Water depth (m) real ( wp ), allocatable :: hu (:, :) !! x-momentum, h * u (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ), allocatable :: hv (:, :) !! y-momentum, h * v (m&#94;2/s) ! Bathymetry (static after initialisation) real ( wp ), allocatable :: b (:, :) !! Bottom elevation (m, positive up) ! Flux divergence (workspace, recomputed each step) real ( wp ), allocatable :: flux_h (:, :) !! Net flux divergence for h real ( wp ), allocatable :: flux_hu (:, :) !! Net flux divergence for hu real ( wp ), allocatable :: flux_hv (:, :) !! Net flux divergence for hv ! Per-face HLL mass flux (workspace).  mass_flux_x(i, j) is the ! HLL h-flux at the right face of cell (i, j) -- i.e. between ! cells (i, j) and (i+1, j).  mass_flux_y(i, j) is the top-face ! flux between cells (i, j) and (i, j+1).  Reused by the tracer ! advection kernels to enforce consistency-with-continuity (CWC). real ( wp ), allocatable :: mass_flux_x (:, :) real ( wp ), allocatable :: mass_flux_y (:, :) ! RK2 storage (saves U&#94;n for the averaging step) real ( wp ), allocatable :: h0 (:, :) !! Saved h at start of RK step real ( wp ), allocatable :: hu0 (:, :) !! Saved hu at start of RK step real ( wp ), allocatable :: hv0 (:, :) !! Saved hv at start of RK step ! Physics scalars used by the barotropic friction / Coriolis ! kernels.  Multilayer-side per-layer bottom-friction (when ! enabled) reads `manning_n` from here too. real ( wp ) :: manning_n = 0.0_wp !! Manning roughness coefficient (s/m&#94;{1/3}) logical :: use_linear_bottom_drag = . false . !! Use linear (Rayleigh) bottom drag instead of quadratic Manning. real ( wp ) :: bottom_drag_r = 0.0_wp !! Linear bottom-drag rate (1/s); used when use_linear_bottom_drag. logical :: wind_surface_layer = . false . !! Apply wind stress to the top layer (surface-concentrated) instead !! of the depth-uniform barotropic mode.  Multilayer only. real ( wp ) :: coriolis_f = 0.0_wp !! Coriolis parameter f (1/s), typically 2*Omega*sin(lat) ! Conservation-budget accumulators (host scalars; not device-mapped). real ( wp ) :: mass_out = 0.0_wp !! Cumulative net volume that has left the domain through its !! boundaries since t=0 (m³, positive = outflow), accumulated per !! RK stage from the scheme's own flux divergence so the console !! conservation `Error` closes to round-off even with open BCs. !! See `rki_console_stats` / the driver's budget wiring. real ( wp ) :: mass_src = 0.0_wp !! Cumulative volume ADDED to the domain by surface sources since !! t=0 (m³, positive = added), accumulated per RK stage from !! precipitation (`h += dt·P`), the evaporative mass sink !! (`evap_mass_sink=.true.`; negative contribution), and the sponge !! h-relaxation Δh.  Feeds `budget%mass_src` in `rki_console_stats` !! so the residual `(total−ref) + out − src` stays ~round-off on !! forced runs instead of growing monotonically with the forcing. logical :: mass_out_tracked = . false . !! Set `.true.` once the solver has accumulated `mass_out`. !! Covered paths: 2D-barotropic SSP-RK2 fused path + coastal !! multilayer nz>1.  Not set by: nz=1 ML fused fast path (safe !! raw-drift fallback — see solver note), semi-implicit, generic-RK. logical :: mass_src_tracked = . false . !! Set `.true.` once the solver has accumulated `mass_src` for the !! current run.  Same coverage as `mass_out_tracked`: 2D-barotropic !! fused path + coastal multilayer nz>1.  The closed budget !! (`budget%mass_active`) is enabled in the console only when BOTH !! flags are set. ! Scheme flags logical :: use_hllc = . false . !! Use HLLC (with contact wave for transverse momentum) instead !! of HLL for the barotropic Riemann flux.  Structured-only — !! the unstructured solver always uses KNP central-upwind, which !! resolves contact discontinuities natively.  Default `.false.`. contains procedure , non_overridable :: init => barotropic_state_init procedure , non_overridable :: destroy => barotropic_state_destroy procedure , non_overridable :: bytes => barotropic_state_bytes end type barotropic_state_t","tags":"","url":"type/barotropic_state_t.html"},{"title":"surface_forcing_t – Rakali ","text":"type, public :: surface_forcing_t Surface flux fields applied by the barotropic friction kernel\nand the multilayer surface-flux kernel. Inherited by type~~surface_forcing_t~~InheritedByGraph type~surface_forcing_t surface_forcing_t type~state_t state_t type~state_t->type~surface_forcing_t forcing type~solver_handle_t solver_handle_t type~solver_handle_t->type~state_t state Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, public :: activ