ean) nonlinear EOS — opt-in via `&tracer_nml eos_form` logical :: eos_use_shared = . false . !! When .true. the EOS call sites route through the shared !! `rki_eos` dispatch (`ml_equation_of_state_shared`) !! instead of the legacy coastal linear kernel.  Default off ⇒ !! every existing coastal config is bit-identical by !! construction.  Set from `&tracer_nml eos_form` via !! `ml_parse_eos_form` (state_init / driver). type ( eos_t ) :: eos !! Shared EOS handle (variant tag + scalar coefficients) for !! the opt-in path.  Flat POD (no allocatable components): !! read on the host at dispatch time and passed by value into !! the device kernels, so it needs NO enter_data/exit_data !! mapping.  `eos%rho0` mirrors `rho_0` (vanishing-layer !! fallback density); `eos%p_ref` stays 0 ⇒ surface/potential !! density. ! Pacanowski-Philander vertical mixing coefficients real ( wp ) :: vmix_nu_max = 0.01_wp !! Pacanowski-Philander max turbulent viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ) :: vmix_nu_bg = 1.0e-4_wp !! Background vertical viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ) :: vmix_ri_alpha = 5.0_wp !! Richardson number scaling coefficient (shared S+T in PP81) ! KPP (Large et al. 1994) surface-boundary-layer overlay.  When ! `vmix_use_kpp` is on, the solver swaps the three PP81 vmix calls ! for the KPP kernels (`rki_ml_kpp`).  The 2D workspace fields ! below are allocated only when `vmix_use_kpp`. logical :: vmix_use_kpp = . false . !! Master switch for the KPP overlay (default off = pure PP81). logical :: vmix_use_keps = . false . !! Master switch for the two-equation k-epsilon closure (default !! off = PP81/KPP).  Interface-shaped prognostic fields below !! are allocated only when this is set. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_tke (:, :, :) !! Turbulent kinetic energy at interfaces (m&#94;2/s&#94;2), shape (nx,ny,nz+1). real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_eps (:, :, :) !! TKE dissipation rate at interfaces (m&#94;2/s&#94;3). real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_nut (:, :, :) !! k-eps turbulent viscosity at interfaces (m&#94;2/s); read as the old !! value by the next diffusion step, so it persists across steps. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_kt (:, :, :) !! k-eps turbulent (scalar) diffusivity at interfaces (m&#94;2/s). real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_ustar_b (:, :) !! Bed friction velocity for the k-eps wall functions (m/s), (nx,ny). !! Recomputed each step from the bottom-drag law; kept as a field !! (not scratch) so it maps to the device like the KPP u_star. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_ustar_s (:, :) !! Surface friction velocity for the k-eps wall functions (m/s). integer :: keps_stability = KEPS_STAB_CONSTANT !! Stability-function scheme for nu_t / kappa_t (KEPS_STAB_*): constant !! c_mu (default) or Galperin stratification-aware quasi-equilibrium. real ( wp ) :: kpp_ri_crit = 0.3_wp !! Critical bulk Richardson number for the BL-depth sweep. real ( wp ) :: kpp_cs_nonlocal = 6.3_wp !! Non-local transport coefficient C_s (LMD94 eq 20). real ( wp ) :: kpp_c_vt2 = 1.8_wp !! Unresolved-turbulence coefficient for V_t&#94;2 (LMD94 eq 23). real ( wp ), allocatable :: kpp_bl_depth (:, :) !! Diagnosed boundary-layer depth (m, positive down).  Persists !! across steps — the previous value seeds the V_t&#94;2 velocity !! scale (self-bootstraps from zero on the first call). real ( wp ), allocatable :: kpp_u_star (:, :) !! Surface friction velocity sqrt(|tau|/rho_0) (m/s), per column. real ( wp ), allocatable :: kpp_buoy_flux (:, :) !! Surface buoyancy flux B_0 (m&#94;2/s&#94;3); <0 = destabilizing. ! Horizontal mixing real ( wp ) :: hdiff_kappa = 0.0_wp !! Horizontal diffusion coefficient for tracers (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ) :: smagorinsky_cs = 0.0_wp !! Smagorinsky horizontal viscosity coefficient real ( wp ) :: biharmonic_nu4 = 0.0_wp !! Biharmonic (del&#94;4) lateral viscosity coefficient (m&#94;4/s); 0 = off ! Scheme flags logical :: use_bpg_jacobian = . true . !! Use the pressure-Jacobian BPG (Shchepetkin & McWilliams 2003). !! DEFAULT ON.  The sigma alternative differences the integrated !! density anomaly at constant SIGMA INDEX, which over sloping !! bathymetry produces a fictitious force proportional to !! (uniform density anomaly) x (bed slope) -- so a column of !! spatially UNIFORM density whose value differs from `rho_0` is !! spuriously accelerated, and the resulting flow leaks mass !! (measured: 1.7e-6 relative over 400 steps, vs 1.3e-14 with the !! Jacobian).  Pinned by `test_bpg_uniform_density`. logical :: use_ppm_tracer = . true . !! Use PPM for tracer advection (false = first-order upwind) logical :: evap_mass_sink = . false . !! When true, net evaporation is a real top-layer water-mass sink !! (h_top -= E*dt) with salt held (concentration rises) and heat !! carried away with the water.  Default false = virtual salt flux. logical :: evap_latent_cooling = . false . !! When true (needs evap_mass_sink), evaporation also withdraws its !! latent heat of vaporization from the surface layer (k=nz) — an !! additional cooling on top of the sensible heat that leaves with !! the removed water.  Default false = bit-identical. integer :: tracer_recon_code = 0 !! Parsed TRACER_RECON_* code (0 = PPM, 1 = WENO5, 2 = WENO7, !! 3 = WENO9).  Set at state init from config%tracer_recon. ! Sediment transport (single class, default off = bit-identical). ! Suspended sediment is a registered tracer (idx_sediment) so its ! advection / diffusion / clamp come from the registry; settling + ! bed exchange are separate kernels.  Bed is a 2D mass reservoir. logical :: use_sediment = . false . !! Master switch for sediment transport (default off). real ( wp ) :: sediment_w_s = 0.0_wp !! Settling (sinking) velocity (m/s, downward; 0 = no settling). real ( wp ) :: sediment_initial_conc = 0.0_wp !! Uniform initial suspended-sediment concentration (kg/m&#94;3). real ( wp ) :: sediment_bed_init = 0.0_wp !! Uniform initial bed sediment mass (kg/m&#94;2). real ( wp ) :: sediment_tau_crit_erosion = 0.0_wp !! Critical bed shear stress for erosion (Pa; 0 = erosion off). real ( wp ) :: sediment_erosion_rate = 0.0_wp !! Ariathurai erosion-rate coefficient E0 (kg/m&#94;2/s; 0 = off). real ( wp ) :: sediment_porosity = 0.0_wp !! Bed porosity (0-1); erosion scaled by (1 - porosity). integer :: idx_sediment = 0 !! Index into tracers(:) for suspended sediment. 0 = not registered. real ( wp ), allocatable :: bed_sediment (:, :) !! Bed sediment mass reservoir (kg/m&#94;2), per column.  Allocated when !! use_sediment.  Settling deposits into it; total (suspended + bed) !! sediment is conserved. contains procedure , non_overridable :: init => multilayer_state_init procedure , non_overridable :: destroy => multilayer_state_destroy procedure , non_overridable :: register_passive_tracer => multilayer_register_passive_tracer procedure , non_overridable :: init_layers => multilayer_init_layers procedure , non_overridable :: build_vcoord_reference => multilayer_build_vcoord_reference procedure , non_overridable :: seed_tracers => multilayer_seed_tracers procedure , non_overridable :: bytes => multilayer_state_bytes end type multilayer_state_t","tags":"","url":"type/multilayer_state_t.html"},{"title":"config_t – Rakali ","text":"type, public :: config_t Container for all runtime simulation parameters Inherited by type~~config_t~~InheritedByGraph type~config_t config_t type~solver_handle_t solver_handle_t type~solver_handle_t->type~config_t cfg Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public :: S_init_bottom = 0.0_wp Initial salinity at the bed (k=1, PSU). real(kind=wp), public :: S_init_surface = 0.0_wp Initial salinity at the surface layer (k=nz_ml, PSU).\nActivates linear S(z) stratification when set non-zero\ntogether with S_init_bottom . real(kind=wp), public :: S_max = 40.0_wp Upper physical bound for salinity (PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: S_min = 0.0_wp Lower physical bound for salinity (PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: S_ref = 0.0_wp Reference salinity in EOS (PSU); density anomaly = beta_S*(S - S_ref) real(kind=wp), public :: T_init_bottom = 0.0_wp Initial temperature at the bed (k=1, degC). real(kind=wp), public :: T_init_surface = 0.0_wp Initial temperature at the surface layer (k=nz_ml, degC).\nActivates linear T(z) stratification when set non-zero\ntogether with T_init_bottom . real(kind=wp), public :: T_max = 40.0_wp Upper physical bound for temperature (degC) real(kind=wp), public :: T_min = -2.0_wp Lower physical bound for temperature (degC); seawater freezing real(kind=wp), public :: T_ref = 15.0_wp Reference temperature in EOS (degC); density anomaly = -alpha_T*(T - T_ref) real(kind=wp), public :: alpha_T = 0.17_wp Thermal expansion coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per degC); ~0.17 near 15 degC.\nSet to 0 to decouple temperature from dynamics (pure passive tracer). integer, public :: async_buffer_slots = 4 Number of ring buffer slots for async output (default: 4) logical, public :: async_output = .false. Use async ring-buffered output (CUDA Fortran only, ignored otherwise) character(len=256), public :: bathymetry_file = \"\" Path to NetCDF bathymetry file (empty = flat bottom) character(len=16), public :: bc_east = \"wall\" East boundary: “wall”, “open”, “tidal”, “nested” character(len=16), public :: bc_north = \"wall\" North boundary: “wall”, “open”, “tidal”, “nested” character(len=16), public :: bc_south = \"wall\" South boundary: “wall”, “open”, “tidal”, “nested” character(len=16), public :: bc_west = \"wall\" West boundary: “wall”, “open”, “tidal”, “nested” real(kind=wp), public :: beta_S = 0.78_wp Haline contraction coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: biharmonic_nu4 = 0.0_wp Biharmonic (del&#94;4) lateral viscosity coefficient (m&#94;4/s) for layer\nmomentum; 0 = off.  Capped at the explicit-step stability limit.\nnu_h = (Cs * dx)&#94;2 * |S| where |S| is the strain rate.\nProvides grid-aware dissipation at sharp velocity gradients. real(kind=wp), public :: bottom_drag_r = 0.0_wp Linear bottom-drag rate (1/s); used when use_linear_bottom_drag. character(len=16), public :: bpg_method = \"jacobian\" BPG computation method: “jacobian” (Shchepetkin-McWilliams,\nDEFAULT) or “sigma” (cheaper, but see below). \"sigma\" differences the integrated density anomaly at constant\nSIGMA INDEX.  Over sloping bathymetry layer k sits at a different\nphysical depth in each column, so a spatially UNIFORM density\nwhose value differs from rho_0 yields a non-zero gradient –\na fictitious force proportional to (uniform anomaly) x (bed\nslope).  Measured on a closed box over a sinusoidal bed, 400\nsteps: relative mass change 1.7e-6 with “sigma” vs 1.3e-14 with\n“jacobian”.  Retained only for reproducing legacy runs; the\nidentity it violates is pinned by test_bpg_uniform_density . real(kind=wp), public :: cfl = 0.45_wp CFL number for adaptive timestep integer, public :: cfl_interval = 1 Recompute CFL timestep every N steps (1 = every step) real(kind=wp), public :: clamped_elevation = 0.0_wp Prescribed surface elevation for clamped BC (m) integer, public :: compress_level = 1 Deflate compression level (1=fast, 9=max). 1 is usually optimal. logical, public :: compress_output = .false. Enable deflate compression for NetCDF output (NetCDF4/HDF5) real(kind=wp), public :: coriolis_f = 0.0_wp Coriolis parameter f (1/s), typically 2 Omega sin(lat) real(kind=wp), public :: discharge_flux = 0.0_wp Prescribed volume flux for discharge BC (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: dry_threshold = 0.001_wp Depth below which a cell is considered dry (m) real(kind=wp), public :: dt_fixed = 0.0_wp Fixed timestep (s), 0 = adaptive CFL.  Same convention\nas dt_max — always seconds. real(kind=wp), public :: dt_max = 1.0e10_wp Maximum allowable timestep (s) — always in seconds, NOT\naffected by time_unit .  Timesteps are naturally short\nand CFL-bounded; writing them in \"day\" would force\nawkward fractional values. real(kind=wp), public :: dx = 1.0_wp Cell size in x-direction (m) real(kind=wp), public :: dy = 1.0_wp Cell size in y-direction (m) character(len=16), public :: eos_form = \"linear\" COASTAL equation-of-state selector (both backends):\n“linear” (default) keeps the legacy coastal linear kernel rho = rho_0 + beta_S*(S-S_ref) - alpha_T*(T-T_ref) —\nbit-identical by construction for every existing config.\n“wright” (Wright 1997 rational) / “roquet_spv” (Roquet et\nal. 2015 TEOS-10 polynomial) route density through the\nSHARED nonlinear EOS ( rki_eos ), evaluated at p=0\n(surface/potential density); alpha_T/beta_S/S_ref/T_ref\nare then ignored by the density computation.  CAVEAT: the\ncoastal KPP surface buoyancy-flux estimate B_0 =\n(g/rho_0)(alpha_T F_T - beta_S F_S) still reads the\nnamelist alpha_T/beta_S as constant expansion coefficients\n— set them to locally representative values when pairing\neos_form with vmix_use_kpp (interior Ri mixing reads\nrho_layer directly and is fully consistent).  The ocean\nregime ignores this knob ( &ocean_pgf_nml eos= instead). real(kind=wp), public :: eta_initial = 0.0_wp Initial free-surface elevation for still_water IC (m, relative to bathymetry datum) logical, public :: evap_latent_cooling = .false. Latent-heat cooling of the surface from evaporation (v2).  When\ntrue (and evap_mass_sink is also true), the water that evaporates\nwithdraws its latent heat of vaporization from the top layer:\nan ADDITIONAL surface heat sink Q_lat = rho_water E_eff L_v [W/m²]\napplied to k=nz, where E_eff is the effective (clamped) evaporation\nrate actually removed.  This is distinct from — and does NOT\ndouble-count — the sensible heat that already leaves with the\nremoved water mass (that is handled by the proportional hT scaling\nin evap_mass_sink).  Requires evap_mass_sink=.true.; no-op\notherwise (fail-loud at configure).  Default .false. = bit-identical. logical, public :: evap_mass_sink = .false. Treat net evaporation (evap_minus_precip > 0) as a real surface\nwater-mass sink at the top layer (k=nz) instead of a virtual salt\nflux.  Removes water: h_top -= E dt; salinity mass hS is left\nunchanged so concentration rises; heat leaves with the water\n(hT_top -= E dt*T_top) so temperature concentration is preserved.\nDefault .false. = bit-identical (legacy virtual-salt-flux path). character(len=256), public :: forcing_file = \"\" Path to NetCDF atmospheric forcing file (empty = uniform config values) real(kind=wp), public :: forcing_x_origin = 0.0_wp Model grid x-origin in forcing file coordinates real(kind=wp), public :: forcing_y_origin = 0.0_wp Model grid y-origin in forcing file coordinates character(len=256), public :: gauge_file = \"\" Path to gauge locations text file (empty = no gauge output) real(kind=wp), public :: gauge_output_interval = 0.0_wp Gauge output interval in seconds (0 = every timestep) character(len=16), public :: grid_type = \"structured\" Grid discretization: “structured” (Cartesian) or “unstructured”\n(triangular).  “unstructured” routes the coastal regime through the\nnative mesh generator + unstructured solver (Python-free). real(kind=wp), public :: h0 = 1.0_wp Background depth for gaussian_hump IC (m) real(kind=wp), public :: hdiff_kappa = 0.0_wp Horizontal diffusion coefficient for tracers (m&#94;2/s).\nSmooths sharp density fronts to reduce BPG overshoot.\nTypical values: 1-10 m&#94;2/s depending on grid resolution. real(kind=wp), public :: hump_amplitude = 0.05_wp Perturbation amplitude for gaussian_hump IC (m) real(kind=wp), public :: hump_sigma = 5.0_wp Gaussian width for gaussian_hump IC (m) real(kind=wp), public :: hump_x_offset = 0.0_wp Hump centre x-offset from domain centre (m) real(kind=wp), public :: hump_y_offset = 0.0_wp Hump centre y-offset from domain centre (m) real(kind=wp), public :: inflow_salinity = -1.0_wp Prescribed salinity for inflow BC (PSU); <0 = zero-gradient real(kind=wp), public :: inflow_temperature = -999.0_wp Prescribed temperature for inflow BC (degC); <0 = zero-gradient real(kind=wp), public :: inflow_velocity = 0.0_wp Prescribed normal velocity for inflow BC (m/s) character(len=32), public :: init_condition = \"dam_break\" Initial condition: “dam_break”, “gaussian_hump”, “castro_dam_break”, or “still_water” real(kind=wp), public :: init_u_shear = 0.0_wp Initial vertical shear: top layer gets +val, bottom gets -val (m/s) real(kind=wp), public :: initial_salinity = 35.0_wp Initial salinity for all layers (PSU).  Used as a uniform IC\nunless S_init_surface and S_init_bottom are BOTH set\nnon-zero, in which case the seed builds a linear S(z) profile\nfrom S_init_bottom at k=1 (bed) to S_init_surface at\nk=nz (surface).  NOTE the stable polarity is the inverse of\ntemperature: salty/dense water belongs at the bed, so a stable\nhaline column has S_init_bottom > S_init_surface (fresh\nsurface, e.g. a river-plume column). real(kind=wp), public :: initial_temperature = 15.0_wp Initial potential temperature for all layers (degC).  Used\nas a uniform IC unless T_init_surface and T_init_bottom are BOTH set non-zero, in which case the seed builds a\nlinear T(z) profile from T_init_bottom at k=1 (bed) to T_init_surface at k=nz (surface).  Stratified IC is the\nprerequisite for baroclinic-instability-driven eddies. character(len=256), public :: institution = \"\" Institution name for CF global attribute (empty = omitted) real(kind=wp), public :: kappa_S_bg = 1.0e-5_wp Background vertical salinity diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: kappa_T_bg = 1.0e-5_wp Background vertical temperature diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) integer, public :: keps_si_picard = 1 Picard passes of the k<->eps coupling per semi-implicit step\n( time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\" + vmix_use_keps only; the\nexplicit path ignores it).  1 (default) = single pass, the\nshipped explicit cadence — steady-state-exact per the Q1\nprototype (local_archive/prototypes/si_closures).  2 (the certified\nsetting; up to 3 accepted) re-runs the k/eps solve with the\nrefreshed nu_t production coefficient for transient-fidelity\nstudies.  Fixed pass count (GPU column-parallel, no per-column\ndivergence). character(len=16), public :: keps_stability = \"constant\" k-epsilon stability functions: “constant” (default; c_mu=0.09,\nPr_t=1), “galperin” (quasi-equilibrium), or “canuto” (Canuto-A). real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_c_vt2 = 1.8_wp Unresolved-turbulence coefficient for the V_t&#94;2 term in the\nbulk-Ri denominator (LMD94 eq 23).  Set 0 to disable V_t&#94;2. real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_cs_nonlocal = 6.3_wp Non-local (counter-gradient) transport coefficient C_s\n(LMD94 eq 20, limit value). real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_ri_crit = 0.3_wp Critical bulk Richardson number for the KPP BL-depth sweep. character(len=16), public :: log_level = \"info\" Log verbosity: “debug”, “verbose”, “info”, “performance”, “warning”, “error” real(kind=wp), public :: manning_n = 0.0_wp Manning roughness coefficient real(kind=wp), public :: ml_min_depth = 0.5_wp Minimum total water depth for vertical layer operations (m).\nColumns shallower than this skip vertical exchange, mixing,\nsalinity advection, and BPG.  Increase if instabilities appear\nnear wetting/drying fronts. integer, public :: n_tidal_constituents = 0 Number of active tidal constituents (0 = use legacy single) character(len=256), public :: nesting_file = \"\" Path to parent domain NetCDF output (empty = no nesting) real(kind=wp), public :: nesting_x_origin = 0.0_wp Child grid x-origin in parent coordinates (m) real(kind=wp), public :: nesting_y_origin = 0.0_wp Child grid y-origin in parent coordinates (m) integer, public :: nghost = 3 Number of ghost cells on each side.  Default 3 (not 2): a\n5-point PPM reconstruction stencil means a rank-seam face’s\nghost-side donor needs two neighbours beyond itself —\nfull-order reconstruction AT the seam requires three ghost\ncolumns.  At nghost=2 the PPM\nlocal-array-edge fallback fires at the seam and degrades the\nface to first order, producing a seam-inconsistent tracer mass\nflux: it conserves a uniform tracer (constant field cancels)\nbut LEAKS a structured one (advecting T with rank-A-out /=\nrank-B-in on the shared seam face drifts hT), invisible to the\nmass/salt closure gates.  Measured on seamount_bench_full\n(np2 x-split): heat closure grew to +5e-11 by day 2 at nghost=2,\nstays at round-off (~5e-14, no growth) at nghost=3.  Single-rank\nruns are unaffected by the wider halo (same interior); the extra\nghost column only costs a little memory. integer, public :: nh_max_iterations = 100 Maximum CG iterations for NH pressure logical, public :: nh_preconditioner = .false. Enable vertical-line preconditioner for CG solver integer, public :: nh_solve_interval = 1 Solve NH pressure every N steps (1 = every step, N > 1 = reuse q_nh) real(kind=wp), public :: nh_tolerance = 1.0e-6_wp CG convergence tolerance for NH pressure integer, public :: nx = 200 Number of physical cells in x-direction integer, public :: ny = 1 Number of physical cells in y-direction integer, public :: nz_layers = 2 Number of sigma layers for NH solver logical, public :: out_density = .false. Output layer density logical, public :: out_h_layer = .true. Output layer thickness logical, public :: out_salinity = .true. Output layer salinity logical, public :: out_temperature = .true. Output layer temperature logical, public :: out_velocity = .true. Output layer velocity (u_ml, v_ml) logical, public :: out_w = .false. Output vertical velocity at interfaces character(len=256), public :: output_dir = \"./output\" Directory for output files character(len=16), public :: output_format = \"netcdf\" Output format: “ascii” or “netcdf” real(kind=wp), public :: output_interval = 0.0_wp Time between output snapshots (s) logical, public :: output_to_file = .false. Enable file output (NetCDF snapshots) character(len=64), public :: reference_time = \"\" Time origin for CF output, e.g. “2026-01-01 00:00:00” (empty = idealized run) character(len=16), public :: remap_method = \"ppm\" Vertical remapping method: “pcm”, “plm”, “ppm”, “ppm_h4”, “pqm”.  Default PPM\n(piecewise parabolic, Colella & Woodward 1984) — the state-of-the-art\nconservative vertical-remap stencil for the coastal ALE coords. “pqm” is\npiecewise quartic (White & Adcroft 2008); it falls back to PPM for nz < 5. character(len=256), public :: restart_file = \"\" Path to restart file for warm start (empty = cold start) real(kind=wp), public :: restart_interval = 0.0_wp Time between restart file writes (s), 0 = no restarts real(kind=wp), public :: rho_0 = 1000.0_wp Reference density for EOS (kg/m&#94;3) real(kind=wp), public :: rho_ref_pressure = 2.0e7_wp Reference pressure (Pa, default 2e7 = 2000 dbar) for the\npotential density that defines the VCOORD_RHO coordinate. real(kind=wp), public :: rho_target_dense = 1030.0_wp Densest target interface potential density (kg/m³) — the bed\ninterface for VCOORD_RHO.  See rho_target_light . real(kind=wp), public :: rho_target_light = 1020.0_wp Lightest target interface potential density (kg/m³) — the\nsurface interface for VCOORD_RHO.  With rho_target_dense builds the uniform light→dense target-density linspace\n(MOM6 ALE_COORDINATE_CONFIG=UNIFORM analogue for the RHO\nmode).  A stretched (RFNC1-style) profile is a P3 follow-up. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_bed_init = 0.0_wp Uniform initial bed sediment mass (kg/m&#94;2). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_erosion_rate = 0.0_wp Ariathurai erosion-rate coefficient E0 (kg/m&#94;2/s). 0 = erosion off. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_initial_conc = 0.0_wp Uniform initial suspended-sediment concentration (kg/m&#94;3). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_porosity = 0.0_wp Bed porosity (0-1); erosion scaled by (1 - porosity).\n0 = off, typical 0.1-0.2. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_tau_crit_erosion = 0.0_wp Critical bed shear stress for erosion (Pa). 0 = erosion off. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_w_s = 0.0_wp Settling (sinking) velocity (m/s, downward; 0 = no settling). logical, public :: semi_implicit = .false. Derived (not a namelist key): .true. when time_scheme==”semi_implicit”.\nSet in apply_time_unit_cascade (runs at the end of the config read,\nbefore validate_config ) so downstream code branches on the logical,\nnot the string. integer, public :: si_newton_max = 10 Casulli wet/dry Newton outer-iteration cap ( &si_nml newton_max ).\nDefault 10 matches the historical hardcoded value (bit-identical).\nReal intertidal bathymetry with a shuffling active set may need\nmore.  Only consulted when si_wetdry=.true. . real(kind=wp), public :: si_newton_tol = 1.0e-11_wp Casulli wet/dry Newton RELATIVE residual tolerance\n( &si_nml newton_tol ): converged when ||F||&#94;2 < newton_tol&#94;2 * ||rhs||&#94;2 AND the active set is frozen.\nDefault 1e-11 matches the historical hardcoded value\n(bit-identical) — tight, tuned for smooth validation cases; real\nbathymetry typically converges to ~1e-7 and wants that here.\nOnly consulted when si_wetdry=.true. . character(len=8), public :: si_precond = \"none\" Preconditioner for the SI Helmholtz eta-solve: \"none\" (unpreconditioned CG, default), \"jacobi\" (diagonal PCG, z = eta_diag*r ), or \"mg\" (aggregation-multigrid V-cycle\nPCG).\nFail-loud allowlist.  Default \"none\" is byte-identical to the\npre-knob plain-CG path. real(kind=wp), public :: si_rtol = 1.0e-10_wp CG RELATIVE residual tolerance: converge when ||r||&#94;2 < si_rtol&#94;2 * ||rhs||&#94;2 .  Default 1e-10 reproduces\nthe historical hardcoded SI_TOL_REL bit-for-bit; relaxable\n(1e-8/1e-6) to cut iterations — si%mass_res is the audit\ninstrument for the resulting mass consistency. logical, public :: si_wetdry = .false. Casulli (2009) subgrid wetting/drying for the SI free surface:\nreplaces the linear 1.0 cell-mass term by the exact wetted-\nvolume V(eta) (per-cell wet-fraction Newton diagonal) so\nintertidal flats dry at minute-scale dt.  Default .false. is\nbyte-identical (all-wet configs unchanged).  Structured coastal\nSI: 2D barotropic + 3D sigma multilayer.  Unstructured coastal\nSI: 2D barotropic + 3D sigma multilayer (the triangular wet/dry\nNewton).  See si_wetdry_bsub_fill for the subgrid bed option. character(len=32), public :: si_wetdry_bsub_fill = \"flat\" Sub-bottom table fill mode when si_wetdry_nsub>=2 : \"flat\" (default) — all sub-bottoms = the plain bed b , so the\n    volume reduces to the flat-bottom case ⇒ BIT-IDENTICAL to nsub=1 (and to today’s behaviour). \"linear\" — the analytic subgrid variant: n_sub equal-area\n    sub-bottoms evenly spaced across a per-cell relief band [b - half, b + half] where half = 0.5*max neighbour bed\n    difference (a linear sub-cell bed ramp; Casulli 2009 subgrid\n    bathymetry).  The mean sub-bottom is exactly b , so the\n    still-water volume is unchanged; only the partial-flooding\n    regime near eta≈b gains breakpoints ⇒ a coarse tidal flat\n    drains/floods SMOOTHLY (wet fraction ramps 1/n_sub per\n    breakpoint instead of a binary 0→1 cell jump).  On flat bed\n    ( half=0 ) ⇒ identical to \"flat\" .  Only consulted when si_wetdry=.true. and si_wetdry_nsub>=2 . integer, public :: si_wetdry_nsub = 1 Subgrid sub-bottoms per cell for the wet/dry volume function\n(>=1). 1 (default) = v1 flat cell bottoms (V piecewise-linear,\none breakpoint per cell). >=2 = the subgrid variant (a per-cell\ndepth distribution; see si_wetdry_bsub_fill ).  Only consulted\nwhen si_wetdry=.true. . character(len=16), public :: sim_type = \"coastal\" Simulation regime: “coastal” is the only supported value real(kind=wp), public :: smagorinsky_cs = 0.0_wp Smagorinsky horizontal viscosity coefficient for layer momentum. logical, public :: split_averaging = .true. ROMS-style time averaging over barotropic substeps integer, public :: split_ratio = 1 Barotropic-baroclinic split ratio: 0=auto, 1=unsplit, N>1=fixed real(kind=wp), public :: sponge_h_ref = 0.0_wp Sponge reference depth (m) real(kind=wp), public :: sponge_strength = 0.0_wp Sponge relaxation rate (1/s) integer, public :: sponge_width = 0 Sponge layer width in cells real(kind=wp), public :: status_interval = 0.0_wp Print status every N seconds of simulation time (0 = default every 100 steps) real(kind=wp), public :: t_end = 1.0_wp Simulation end time, interpreted in time_unit (default s). real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_amp (MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS) = 0.0_wp Constituent amplitudes (m) real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_amplitude = 0.0_wp Tidal elevation amplitude (m) — single-constituent legacy real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_omega (MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS) = 0.0_wp Constituent angular frequencies (rad/s) real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_period = 44712.0_wp Tidal period (s), default M2 = 12.42 h — single-constituent legacy real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_phase (MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS) = 0.0_wp Constituent phases (radians) character(len=16), public :: time_scheme = \"rk2\" Explicit time integrator (coastal 2D barotropic path):\n“euler” (1st), “rk2” (default, 2nd), “rk3” (3rd), “rk43”\n(3rd, SSP coeff 2 -> 2x dt).  All SSP for wet/dry positivity. character(len=8), public :: time_unit = \"s\" Unit applied to the long-time fields: t_end and status_interval (logging cadence). dt_fixed and dt_max stay in\nseconds — see their docstrings.  Read at namelist parse,\nthen multiplied through so the rest of the code keeps\nusing seconds internally.  Valid values: \"s\" , \"min\" , \"hr\" , \"day\" , \"year\" .  Year is 365.25 days (Julian,\nmatches MOM6 / UDUNITS convention).  Default \"s\" preserves backward compatibility — every existing nml is\nbit-identical. character(len=8), public :: tracer_recon = \"ppm\" Tracer horizontal-advection face reconstruction (structured coastal):\n“ppm” (default, CW84 PPM), “weno5” (Jiang-Shu 1996 + Borges 2008,\nnghost>=3), “weno7” (Balsara-Shu 2000, nghost>=4), “weno9”\n(Balsara-Shu 2000, nghost>=5). “pqm” is deferred.\nBit-identical to ppm when tracer_recon=”ppm”. logical, public :: use_hllc = .false. Use the HLLC approximate Riemann solver for the structured\nbarotropic flux instead of HLL.  HLLC adds a contact wave so\ntransverse momentum ( hv across an x-face, hu across a\ny-face) is upwinded across the shear interface; reduces\nnumerical diffusion for shear-aligned flow at the cost of\na few extra flops per face.  Default .false. (HLL). logical, public :: use_linear_bottom_drag = .false. Use linear (Rayleigh) bottom drag instead of quadratic Manning. logical, public :: use_multilayer = .false. Enable coupled hydrostatic vertical layers (alternative to NH) logical, public :: use_nonhydrostatic = .false. Enable multi-layer NH pressure correction logical, public :: use_ppm_tracer = .true. Use high-order tracer advection: PPM (structured) or MUSCL\n(unstructured). When false, falls back to first-order upwind. logical, public :: use_sediment = .false. Master switch for suspended-sediment transport. real(kind=wp), public :: vcoord_blend_width = 50.0_wp z-sigma hybrid: blending zone width (m) real(kind=wp), public :: vcoord_depth_transition = 100.0_wp z-sigma hybrid: depth (m) where blending starts character(len=16), public :: vcoord_type = \"sigma\" Vertical coordinate type: “sigma”, “zsigma”, “zstar”, etc. real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_nu_bg = 1.0e-4_wp Background vertical viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_nu_max = 0.01_wp Pacanowski-Philander max turbulent viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_ri_alpha = 5.0_wp Richardson number scaling coefficient (shared between momentum and tracers) logical, public :: vmix_use_keps = .false. Enable the two-equation k-epsilon vertical-mixing closure\n(rki_ml_keps).  Default off = PP81.  When on it overrides\nboth PP81 and the KPP overlay: the solver advances k/eps and\napplies the k-epsilon eddy viscosity to momentum (tracer\nmixing is wired in a later increment). logical, public :: vmix_use_kpp = .false. Enable the KPP (Large et al. 1994) surface-boundary-layer\noverlay on top of the PP81 interior closure.  Default off:\nthe coastal multilayer path runs pure PP81 (bit-identical\nto pre-KPP).  When on, the solver swaps the three PP81\nvmix calls for the KPP kernels (BL-depth + shape-function\nenhanced diffusivity + non-local transport). real(kind=wp), public :: wind_stress_x = 0.0_wp Surface wind stress in x-direction (Pa) real(kind=wp), public :: wind_stress_y = 0.0_wp Surface wind stress in y-direction (Pa) logical, public :: wind_surface_layer = .false. Apply surface wind stress to the top layer only (surface-\nconcentrated, generates vertical shear) instead of the\ndepth-uniform barotropic mode.  Multilayer (nz>1) only; off by\ndefault (= bit-identical depth-uniform forcing). real(kind=wp), public :: zstar_h_min = 1.0e-4_wp Vanishing-layer floor (m).  Layers that would land below the\nlocal bed get clipped to this thickness rather than going to zero. real(kind=wp), public :: zstar_h_surf_target = 0.0_wp Target physical thickness of the surface layer (m).\n0 => auto: fall back to the lite (uniform sigma) profile\nper column (effectively zstar-lite per-column).  Set > 0 to\nanchor the surface layer at a fixed thickness regardless of H. integer, public :: zstar_n_surf = 0 Number of “fine” near-surface layers using stretching.\n0 => auto (use max(1, nz/3)) character(len=16), public :: zstar_stretching = \"log\" Surface-concentration stretching: “log” | “uniform” Source Code type :: config_t !! Container for all runtime simulation parameters ! Simulation regime — selects the dynamical core path: !   \"coastal\" → HLL/HLLC (structured) or KNP central-upwind (unstructured) !               + nonhydrostatic option (structured only). Shock-capturing, !               wet/dry friendly, default for the existing test suite. character ( len = 16 ) :: sim_type = \"coastal\" !! Simulation regime: \"coastal\" is the only supported value ! Grid parameters character ( len = 16 ) :: grid_type = \"structured\" !! Grid discretization: \"structured\" (Cartesian) or \"unstructured\" !! (triangular).  \"unstructured\" routes the coastal regime through the !! native mesh generator + unstructured solver (Python-free). integer :: nx = 200 !! Number of physical cells in x-direction integer :: ny = 1 !! Number of physical cells in y-direction real ( wp ) :: dx = 1.0_wp !! Cell size in x-direction (m) real ( wp ) :: dy = 1.0_wp !! Cell size in y-direction (m) integer :: nghost = 3 !! Number of ghost cells on each side.  Default 3 (not 2): a !! 5-point PPM reconstruction stencil means a rank-seam face's !! ghost-side donor needs two neighbours beyond itself — !! full-order reconstruction AT the seam requires three ghost !! columns.  At nghost=2 the PPM !! local-array-edge fallback fires at the seam and degrades the !! face to first order, producing a seam-inconsistent tracer mass !! flux: it conserves a uniform tracer (constant field cancels) !! but LEAKS a structured one (advecting T with rank-A-out /= !! rank-B-in on the shared seam face drifts hT), invisible to the !! mass/salt closure gates.  Measured on seamount_bench_full !! (np2 x-split): heat closure grew to +5e-11 by day 2 at nghost=2, !! stays at round-off (~5e-14, no growth) at nghost=3.  Single-rank !! runs are unaffected by the wider halo (same interior); the extra !! ghost column only costs a little memory. ! Time parameters real ( wp ) :: t_end = 1.0_wp !! Simulation end time, interpreted in `time_unit` (default s). real ( wp ) :: cfl = 0.45_wp !! CFL number for adaptive timestep real ( wp ) :: dt_max = 1.0e10_wp !! Maximum allowable timestep (s) — always in seconds, NOT !! affected by `time_unit`.  Timesteps are naturally short !! and CFL-bounded; writing them in `\"day\"` would force !! awkward fractional values. real ( wp ) :: dt_fixed = 0.0_wp !! Fixed timestep (s), 0 = adaptive CFL.  Same convention !! as `dt_max` — always seconds. integer :: cfl_interval = 1 !! Recompute CFL timestep every N steps (1 = every step) character ( len = 16 ) :: time_scheme = \"rk2\" !! Explicit time integrator (coastal 2D barotropic path): !! \"euler\" (1st), \"rk2\" (default, 2nd), \"rk3\" (3rd), \"rk43\" !! (3rd, SSP coeff 2 -> 2x dt).  All SSP for wet/dry positivity. logical :: semi_implicit = . false . !! Derived (not a namelist key): .true. when time_scheme==\"semi_implicit\". !! Set in `apply_time_unit_cascade` (runs at the end of the config read, !! before `validate_config`) so downstream code branches on the logical, !! not the string. character ( len = 8 ) :: time_unit = \"s\" !! Unit applied to the long-time fields: `t_end` and !! `status_interval` (logging cadence).  `dt_fixed` and `dt_max` stay in !! seconds — see their docstrings.  Read at namelist parse, !! then multiplied through so the rest of the code keeps !! using seconds internally.  Valid values: `\"s\"`, `\"min\"`, !! `\"hr\"`, `\"day\"`, `\"year\"`.  Year is 365.25 days (Julian, !! matches MOM6 / UDUNITS convention).  Default `\"s\"` !! preserves backward compatibility — every existing nml is !! bit-identical. ! Semi-implicit free-surface CG solver (`&si_nml`).  Only consulted ! when `time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\"`; ignored otherwise. character ( len = 8 ) :: si_precond = \"none\" !! Preconditioner for the SI Helmholtz eta-solve: `\"none\"` !! (unpreconditioned CG, default), `\"jacobi\"` (diagonal PCG, !! `z = eta_diag*r`), or `\"mg\"` (aggregation-multigrid V-cycle !! PCG). !! Fail-loud allowlist.  Default `\"none\"` is byte-identical to the !! pre-knob plain-CG path. real ( wp ) :: si_rtol = 1.0e-10_wp !! CG RELATIVE residual tolerance: converge when !! `||r||&#94;2 < si_rtol&#94;2 * ||rhs||&#94;2`.  Default `1e-10` reproduces !! the historical hardcoded `SI_TOL_REL` bit-for-bit; relaxable !! (1e-8/1e-6) to cut iterations — `si%mass_res` is the audit !! instrument for the resulting mass consistency. logical :: si_wetdry = . false . !! Casulli (2009) subgrid wetting/drying for the SI free surface: !! replaces the linear `1.0` cell-mass term by the exact wetted- !! volume `V(eta)` (per-cell wet-fraction Newton diagonal) so !! intertidal flats dry at minute-scale dt.  Default `.false.` is !! byte-identical (all-wet configs unchanged).  Structured coastal !! SI: 2D barotropic + 3D sigma multilayer.  Unstructured coastal !! SI: 2D barotropic + 3D sigma multilayer (the triangular wet/dry !! Newton).  See `si_wetdry_bsub_fill` for the subgrid bed option. integer :: si_wetdry_nsub = 1 !! Subgrid sub-bottoms per cell for the wet/dry volume function !! (>=1).  `1` (default) = v1 flat cell bottoms (V piecewise-linear, !! one breakpoint per cell).  `>=2` = the subgrid variant (a per-cell !! depth distribution; see `si_wetdry_bsub_fill`).  Only consulted !! when `si_wetdry=.true.`. character ( len = 32 ) :: si_wetdry_bsub_fill = \"flat\" !! Sub-bottom table fill mode when `si_wetdry_nsub>=2`: !!   `\"flat\"` (default) — all sub-bottoms = the plain bed `b`, so the !!     volume reduces to the flat-bottom case ⇒ BIT-IDENTICAL to !!     `nsub=1` (and to today's behaviour). !!   `\"linear\"` — the analytic subgrid variant: `n_sub` equal-area !!     sub-bottoms evenly spaced across a per-cell relief band !!     `[b - half, b + half]` where `half = 0.5*max` neighbour bed !!     difference (a linear sub-cell bed ramp; Casulli 2009 subgrid !!     bathymetry).  The mean sub-bottom is exactly `b`, so the !!     still-water volume is unchanged; only the partial-flooding !!     regime near `eta≈b` gains breakpoints ⇒ a coarse tidal flat !!     drains/floods SMOOTHLY (wet fraction ramps 1/n_sub per !!     breakpoint instead of a binary 0→1 cell jump).  On flat bed !!     (`half=0`) ⇒ identical to `\"flat\"`.  Only consulted when !!     `si_wetdry=.true.` and `si_wetdry_nsub>=2`. integer :: si_newton_max = 10 !! Casulli wet/dry Newton outer-iteration cap (`&si_nml newton_max`). !! Default `10` matches the historical hardcoded value (bit-identical). !! Real intertidal bathymetry with a shuffling active set may need !! more.  Only consulted when `si_wetdry=.true.`. real ( wp ) :: si_newton_tol = 1.0e-11_wp !! Casulli wet/dry Newton RELATIVE residual tolerance !! (`&si_nml newton_tol`): converged when !! `||F||&#94;2 < newton_tol&#94;2 * ||rhs||&#94;2` AND the active set is frozen. !! Default `1e-11` matches the historical hardcoded value !! (bit-identical) — tight, tuned for smooth validation cases; real !! bathymetry typically converges to ~1e-7 and wants that here. !! Only consulted when `si_wetdry=.true.`. ! Physics parameters real ( wp ) :: manning_n = 0.0_wp !! Manning roughness coefficient logical :: use_linear_bottom_drag = . false . !! Use linear (Rayleigh) bottom drag instead of quadratic Manning. real ( wp ) :: bottom_drag_r = 0.0_wp !! Linear bottom-drag rate (1/s); used when use_linear_bottom_drag. logical :: wind_surface_layer = . false . !! Apply surface wind stress to the top layer only (surface- !! concentrated, generates vertical shear) instead of the !! depth-uniform barotropic mode.  Multilayer (nz>1) only; off by !! default (= bit-identical depth-uniform forcing). real ( wp ) :: dry_threshold = 0.001_wp !! Depth below which a cell is considered dry (m) real ( wp ) :: wind_stress_x = 0.0_wp !! Surface wind stress in x-direction (Pa) real ( wp ) :: wind_stress_y = 0.0_wp !! Surface wind stress in y-direction (Pa) real ( wp ) :: coriolis_f = 0.0_wp !! Coriolis parameter f (1/s), typically 2*Omega*sin(lat) logical :: use_hllc = . false . !! Use the HLLC approximate Riemann solver for the structured !! barotropic flux instead of HLL.  HLLC adds a contact wave so !! transverse momentum (`hv` across an x-face, `hu` across a !! y-face) is upwinded across the shear interface; reduces !! numerical diffusion for shear-aligned flow at the cost of !! a few extra flops per face.  Default `.false.` (HLL). ! Output parameters logical :: output_to_file = . false . !! Enable file output (NetCDF snapshots) character ( len = 256 ) :: output_dir = \"./output\" !! Directory for output files real ( wp ) :: output_interval = 0.0_wp !! Time between output snapshots (s) character ( len = 16 ) :: output_format = \"netcdf\" !! Output format: \"ascii\" or \"netcdf\" real ( wp ) :: restart_interval = 0.0_wp !! Time between restart file writes (s), 0 = no restarts logical :: async_output = . false . !! Use async ring-buffered output (CUDA Fortran only, ignored otherwise) integer :: async_buffer_slots = 4 !! Number of ring buffer slots for async output (default: 4) logical :: compress_output = . false . !! Enable deflate compression for NetCDF output (NetCDF4/HDF5) integer :: compress_level = 1 !! Deflate compression level (1=fast, 9=max). 1 is usually optimal. ! Output variable selection (multilayer) logical :: out_h_layer = . true . !! Output layer thickness logical :: out_velocity = . true . !! Output layer velocity (u_ml, v_ml) logical :: out_salinity = . true . !! Output layer salinity logical :: out_temperature = . true . !! Output layer temperature logical :: out_density = . false . !! Output layer density logical :: out_w = . false . !! Output vertical velocity at interfaces ! I/O file parameters character ( len = 256 ) :: bathymetry_file = \"\" !! Path to NetCDF bathymetry file (empty = flat bottom) character ( len = 256 ) :: restart_file = \"\" !! Path to restart file for warm start (empty = cold start) character ( len = 256 ) :: forcing_file = \"\" !! Path to NetCDF atmospheric forcing file (empty = uniform config values) real ( wp ) :: forcing_x_origin = 0.0_wp !! Model grid x-origin in forcing file coordinates real ( wp ) :: forcing_y_origin = 0.0_wp !! Model grid y-origin in forcing file coordinates character ( len = 256 ) :: gauge_file = \"\" !! Path to gauge locations text file (empty = no gauge output) real ( wp ) :: gauge_output_interval = 0.0_wp !! Gauge output interval in seconds (0 = every timestep) ! Nesting parameters character ( len = 256 ) :: nesting_file = \"\" !! Path to parent domain NetCDF output (empty = no nesting) real ( wp ) :: nesting_x_origin = 0.0_wp !! Child grid x-origin in parent coordinates (m) real ( wp ) :: nesting_y_origin = 0.0_wp !! Child grid y-origin in parent coordinates (m) ! Boundary parameters character ( len = 16 ) :: bc_west = \"wall\" !! West boundary: \"wall\", \"open\", \"tidal\", \"nested\" character ( len = 16 ) :: bc_east = \"wall\" !! East boundary: \"wall\", \"open\", \"tidal\", \"nested\" character ( len = 16 ) :: bc_south = \"wall\" !! South boundary: \"wall\", \"open\", \"tidal\", \"nested\" character ( len = 16 ) :: bc_north = \"wall\" !! North boundary: \"wall\", \"open\", \"tidal\", \"nested\" ! Tidal forcing parameters real ( wp ) :: tidal_amplitude = 0.0_wp !! Tidal elevation amplitude (m) — single-constituent legacy real ( wp ) :: tidal_period = 4471 2.0_wp !! Tidal period (s), default M2 = 12.42 h — single-constituent legacy ! Multi-constituent tidal forcing integer :: n_tidal_constituents = 0 !! Number of active tidal constituents (0 = use legacy single) real ( wp ) :: tidal_amp ( MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS ) = 0.0_wp !! Constituent amplitudes (m) real ( wp ) :: tidal_phase ( MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS ) = 0.0_wp !! Constituent phases (radians) real ( wp ) :: tidal_omega ( MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS ) = 0.0_wp !! Constituent angular frequencies (rad/s) ! Inflow/discharge/clamped BC parameters real ( wp ) :: inflow_velocity = 0.0_wp !! Prescribed normal velocity for inflow BC (m/s) real ( wp ) :: inflow_salinity = - 1.0_wp !! Prescribed salinity for inflow BC (PSU); <0 = zero-gradient real ( wp ) :: inflow_temperature = - 99 9.0_wp !! Prescribed temperature for inflow BC (degC); <0 = zero-gradient real ( wp ) :: discharge_flux = 0.0_wp !! Prescribed volume flux for discharge BC (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ) :: clamped_elevation = 0.0_wp !! Prescribed surface elevation for clamped BC (m) ! Sponge layer parameters integer :: sponge_width = 0 !! Sponge layer width in cells real ( wp ) :: sponge_strength = 0.0_wp !! Sponge relaxation rate (1/s) real ( wp ) :: sponge_h_ref = 0.0_wp !! Sponge reference depth (m) ! Metadata parameters character ( len = 64 ) :: reference_time = \"\" !! Time origin for CF output, e.g. \"2026-01-01 00:00:00\" (empty = idealized run) character ( len = 256 ) :: institution = \"\" !! Institution name for CF global attribute (empty = omitted) ! Non-hydrostatic pressure correction logical :: use_nonhydrostatic = . false . !! Enable multi-layer NH pressure correction integer :: nz_layers = 2 !! Number of sigma layers for NH solver ! Coupled hydrostatic multi-layer logical :: use_multilayer = . false . !! Enable coupled hydrostatic vertical layers (alternative to NH) real ( wp ) :: rho_0 = 100 0.0_wp !! Reference density for EOS (kg/m&#94;3) real ( wp ) :: vmix_nu_max = 0.01_wp !! Pacanowski-Philander max turbulent viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ) :: vmix_nu_bg = 1.0e-4_wp !! Background vertical viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ) :: vmix_ri_alpha = 5.0_wp !! Richardson number scaling coefficient (shared between momentum and tracers) logical :: vmix_use_kpp = . false . !! Enable the KPP (Large et al. 1994) surface-boundary-layer !! overlay on top of the PP81 interior closure.  Default off: !! the coastal multilayer path runs pure PP81 (bit-identical !! to pre-KPP).  When on, the solver swaps the three PP81 !! vmix calls for the KPP kernels (BL-depth + shape-function !! enhanced diffusivity + non-local transport). logical :: vmix_use_keps = . false . !! Enable the two-equation k-epsilon vertical-mixing closure !! (rki_ml_keps).  Default off = PP81.  When on it overrides !! both PP81 and the KPP overlay: the solver advances k/eps and !! applies the k-epsilon eddy viscosity to momentum (tracer !! mixing is wired in a later increment). character ( len = 16 ) :: keps_stability = \"constant\" !! k-epsilon stability functions: \"constant\" (default; c_mu=0.09, !! Pr_t=1), \"galperin\" (quasi-equilibrium), or \"canuto\" (Canuto-A). integer :: keps_si_picard = 1 !! Picard passes of the k<->eps coupling per semi-implicit step !! (`time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\"` + `vmix_use_keps` only; the !! explicit path ignores it).  1 (default) = single pass, the !! shipped explicit cadence — steady-state-exact per the Q1 !! prototype (local_archive/prototypes/si_closures).  2 (the certified !! setting; up to 3 accepted) re-runs the k/eps solve with the !! refreshed nu_t production coefficient for transient-fidelity !! studies.  Fixed pass count (GPU column-parallel, no per-column !! divergence). real ( wp ) :: kpp_ri_crit = 0.3_wp !! Critical bulk Richardson number for the KPP BL-depth sweep. real ( wp ) :: kpp_cs_nonlocal = 6.3_wp !! Non-local (counter-gradient) transport coefficient C_s !! (LMD94 eq 20, limit value). real ( wp ) :: kpp_c_vt2 = 1.8_wp !! Unresolved-turbulence coefficient for the V_t&#94;2 term in the !! bulk-Ri denominator (LMD94 eq 23).  Set 0 to disable V_t&#94;2. real ( wp ) :: hdiff_kappa = 0.0_wp !! Horizontal diffusion coefficient for tracers (m&#94;2/s). !! Smooths sharp density fronts to reduce BPG overshoot. !! Typical values: 1-10 m&#94;2/s depending on grid resolution. ! Tracer parameters (salinity + temperature) real ( wp ) :: initial_salinity = 3 5.0_wp !! Initial salinity for all layers (PSU).  Used as a uniform IC !! unless `S_init_surface` and `S_init_bottom` are BOTH set !! non-zero, in which case the seed builds a linear S(z) profile !! from `S_init_bottom` at k=1 (bed) to `S_init_surface` at !! k=nz (surface).  NOTE the stable polarity is the inverse of !! temperature: salty/dense water belongs at the bed, so a stable !! haline column has `S_init_bottom > S_init_surface` (fresh !! surface, e.g. a river-plume column). real ( wp ) :: S_init_surface = 0.0_wp !! Initial salinity at the surface layer (k=nz_ml, PSU). !! Activates linear S(z) stratification when set non-zero !! together with `S_init_bottom`. real ( wp ) :: S_init_bottom = 0.0_wp !! Initial salinity at the bed (k=1, PSU). real ( wp ) :: S_ref = 0.0_wp !! Reference salinity in EOS (PSU); density anomaly = beta_S*(S - S_ref) real ( wp ) :: beta_S = 0.78_wp !! Haline contraction coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per PSU) real ( wp ) :: S_min = 0.0_wp !! Lower physical bound for salinity (PSU) real ( wp ) :: S_max = 4 0.0_wp !! Upper physical bound for salinity (PSU) real ( wp ) :: kappa_S_bg = 1.0e-5_wp !! Background vertical salinity diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ) :: initial_temperature = 1 5.0_wp !! Initial potential temperature for all layers (degC).  Used !! as a uniform IC unless `T_init_surface` and `T_init_bottom` !! are BOTH set non-zero, in which case the seed builds a !! linear T(z) profile from `T_init_bottom` at k=1 (bed) to !! `T_init_surface` at k=nz (surface).  Stratified IC is the !! prerequisite for baroclinic-instability-driven eddies. real ( wp ) :: T_init_surface = 0.0_wp !! Initial temperature at the surface layer (k=nz_ml, degC). !! Activates linear T(z) stratification when set non-zero !! together with `T_init_bottom`. real ( wp ) :: T_init_bottom = 0.0_wp !! Initial temperature at the bed (k=1, degC). real ( wp ) :: T_ref = 1 5.0_wp !! Reference temperature in EOS (degC); density anomaly = -alpha_T*(T - T_ref) real ( wp ) :: alpha_T = 0.17_wp !! Thermal expansion coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per degC); ~0.17 near 15 degC. !! Set to 0 to decouple temperature from dynamics (pure passive tracer). real ( wp ) :: T_min = - 2.0_wp !! Lower physical bound for temperature (degC); seawater freezing real ( wp ) :: T_max = 4 0.0_wp !! Upper physical bound for temperature (degC) real ( wp ) :: kappa_T_bg = 1.0e-5_wp !! Background vertical temperature diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) character ( len = 16 ) :: eos_form = \"linear\" !! COASTAL equation-of-state selector (both backends): !! \"linear\" (default) keeps the legacy coastal linear kernel !! `rho = rho_0 + beta_S*(S-S_ref) - alpha_T*(T-T_ref)` — !! bit-identical by construction for every existing config. !! \"wright\" (Wright 1997 rational) / \"roquet_spv\" (Roquet et !! al. 2015 TEOS-10 polynomial) route density through the !! SHARED nonlinear EOS (`rki_eos`), evaluated at p=0 !! (surface/potential density); alpha_T/beta_S/S_ref/T_ref !! are then ignored by the density computation.  CAVEAT: the !! coastal KPP surface buoyancy-flux estimate `B_0 = !! (g/rho_0)(alpha_T F_T - beta_S F_S)` still reads the !! namelist alpha_T/beta_S as constant expansion coefficients !! — set them to locally representative values when pairing !! eos_form with vmix_use_kpp (interior Ri mixing reads !! rho_layer directly and is fully consistent).  The ocean !! regime ignores this knob (`&ocean_pgf_nml eos=` instead). logical :: use_ppm_tracer = . true . !! Use high-order tracer advection: PPM (structured) or MUSCL !! (unstructured). When false, falls back to first-order upwind. character ( len = 8 ) :: tracer_recon = \"ppm\" !! Tracer horizontal-advection face reconstruction (structured coastal): !! \"ppm\" (default, CW84 PPM), \"weno5\" (Jiang-Shu 1996 + Borges 2008, !! nghost>=3), \"weno7\" (Balsara-Shu 2000, nghost>=4), \"weno9\" !! (Balsara-Shu 2000, nghost>=5). \"pqm\" is deferred. !! Bit-identical to ppm when tracer_recon=\"ppm\". real ( wp ) :: smagorinsky_cs = 0.0_wp !! Smagorinsky horizontal viscosity coefficient for layer momentum. real ( wp ) :: biharmonic_nu4 = 0.0_wp !! Biharmonic (del&#94;4) lateral viscosity coefficient (m&#94;4/s) for layer !! momentum; 0 = off.  Capped at the explicit-step stability limit. !! nu_h = (Cs * dx)&#94;2 * |S| where |S| is the strain rate. !! Provides grid-aware dissipation at sharp velocity gradients. logical :: evap_mass_sink = . false . !! Treat net evaporation (evap_minus_precip > 0) as a real surface !! water-mass sink at the top layer (k=nz) instead of a virtual salt !! flux.  Removes water: h_top -= E*dt; salinity mass hS is left !! unchanged so concentration rises; heat leaves with the water !! (hT_top -= E*dt*T_top) so temperature concentration is preserved. !! Default .false. = bit-identical (legacy virtual-salt-flux path). logical :: evap_latent_cooling = . false . !! Latent-heat cooling of the surface from evaporation (v2).  When !! true (and evap_mass_sink is also true), the water that evaporates !! withdraws its latent heat of vaporization from the top layer: !! an ADDITIONAL surface heat sink Q_lat = rho_water*E_eff*L_v [W/m²] !! applied to k=nz, where E_eff is the effective (clamped) evaporation !! rate actually removed.  This is distinct from — and does NOT !! double-count — the sensible heat that already leaves with the !! removed water mass (that is handled by the proportional hT scaling !! in evap_mass_sink).  Requires evap_mass_sink=.true.; no-op !! otherwise (fail-loud at configure).  Default .false. = bit-identical. ! Sediment transport (single class, gated; default off = bit-identical). logical :: use_sediment = . false . !! Master switch for suspended-sediment transport. real ( wp ) :: sediment_w_s = 0.0_wp !! Settling (sinking) velocity (m/s, downward; 0 = no settling). real ( wp ) :: sediment_initial_conc = 0.0_wp !! Uniform initial suspended-sediment concentration (kg/m&#94;3). real ( wp ) :: sediment_bed_init = 0.0_wp !! Uniform initial bed sediment mass (kg/m&#94;2). real ( wp ) :: sediment_tau_crit_erosion = 0.0_wp !! Critical bed shear stress for erosion (Pa). 0 = erosion off. real ( wp ) :: sediment_erosion_rate = 0.0_wp !! Ariathurai erosion-rate coefficient E0 (kg/m&#94;2/s). 0 = erosion off. real ( wp ) :: sediment_porosity = 0.0_wp !! Bed porosity (0-1); erosion scaled by (1 - porosity). !! 0 = off, typical 0.1-0.2. character ( len = 16 ) :: bpg_method = \"jacobian\" !! BPG computation method: \"jacobian\" (Shchepetkin-McWilliams, !! DEFAULT) or \"sigma\" (cheaper, but see below). !! !! `\"sigma\"` differences the integrated density anomaly at constant !! SIGMA INDEX.  Over sloping bathymetry layer k sits at a different !! physical depth in each column, so a spatially UNIFORM density !! whose value differs from `rho_0` yields a non-zero gradient -- !! a fictitious force proportional to (uniform anomaly) x (bed !! slope).  Measured on a closed box over a sinusoidal bed, 400 !! steps: relative mass change 1.7e-6 with \"sigma\" vs 1.3e-14 with !! \"jacobian\".  Retained only for reproducing legacy runs; the !! identity it violates is pinned by `test_bpg_uniform_density`. real ( wp ) :: ml_min_depth = 0.5_wp !! Minimum total water depth for vertical layer operations (m). !! Columns shallower than this skip vertical exchange, mixing, !! salinity advection, and BPG.  Increase if instabilities appear !! near wetting/drying fronts. real ( wp ) :: nh_tolerance = 1.0e-6_wp !! CG convergence tolerance for NH pressure integer :: nh_max_iterations = 100 !! Maximum CG iterations for NH pressure logical :: nh_preconditioner = . false . !! Enable vertical-line preconditioner for CG solver integer :: nh_solve_interval = 1 !! Solve NH pressure every N steps (1 = every step, N > 1 = reuse q_nh) ! Initial condition selection character ( len = 32 ) :: init_condition = \"dam_break\" !! Initial condition: \"dam_break\", \"gaussian_hump\", \"castro_dam_break\", or \"still_water\" real ( wp ) :: eta_initial = 0.0_wp !! Initial free-surface elevation for still_water IC (m, relative to bathymetry datum) real ( wp ) :: h0 = 1.0_wp !! Background depth for gaussian_hump IC (m) real ( wp ) :: hump_amplitude = 0.05_wp !! Perturbation amplitude for gaussian_hump IC (m) real ( wp ) :: hump_sigma = 5.0_wp !! Gaussian width for gaussian_hump IC (m) real ( wp ) :: hump_x_offset = 0.0_wp !! Hump centre x-offset from domain centre (m) real ( wp ) :: hump_y_offset = 0.0_wp !! Hump centre y-offset from domain centre (m) real ( wp ) :: init_u_shear = 0.0_wp !! Initial vertical shear: top layer gets +val, bottom gets -val (m/s) ! Mode splitting parameters integer :: split_ratio = 1 !! Barotropic-baroclinic split ratio: 0=auto, 1=unsplit, N>1=fixed logical :: split_averaging = . true . !! ROMS-style time averaging over barotropic substeps ! Vertical coordinate parameters character ( len = 16 ) :: vcoord_type = \"sigma\" !! Vertical coordinate type: \"sigma\", \"zsigma\", \"zstar\", etc. character ( len = 16 ) :: remap_method = \"ppm\" !! Vertical remapping method: \"pcm\", \"plm\", \"ppm\", \"ppm_h4\", \"pqm\".  Default PPM !! (piecewise parabolic, Colella & Woodward 1984) — the state-of-the-art !! conservative vertical-remap stencil for the coastal ALE coords. \"pqm\" is !! piecewise quartic (White & Adcroft 2008); it falls back to PPM for nz < 5. real ( wp ) :: vcoord_depth_transition = 10 0.0_wp !! z-sigma hybrid: depth (m) where blending starts real ( wp ) :: vcoord_blend_width = 5 0.0_wp !! z-sigma hybrid: blending zone width (m) ! Full MOM6 z* parameters (VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL) real ( wp ) :: zstar_h_surf_target = 0.0_wp !! Target physical thickness of the surface layer (m). !! 0 => auto: fall back to the lite (uniform sigma) profile !! per column (effectively zstar-lite per-column).  Set > 0 to !! anchor the surface layer at a fixed thickness regardless of H. character ( len = 16 ) :: zstar_stretching = \"log\" !! Surface-concentration stretching: \"log\" | \"uniform\" real ( wp ) :: zstar_h_min = 1.0e-4_wp !! Vanishing-layer floor (m).  Layers that would land below the !! local bed get clipped to this thickness rather than going to zero. integer :: zstar_n_surf = 0 !! Number of \"fine\" near-surface layers using stretching. !! 0 => auto (use max(1, nz/3)) ! Isopycnal coordinate (VCOORD_RHO) parameters real ( wp ) :: rho_ref_pressure = 2.0e7_wp !! Reference pressure (Pa, default 2e7 = 2000 dbar) for the !! potential density that defines the VCOORD_RHO coordinate. real ( wp ) :: rho_target_light = 102 0.0_wp !! Lightest target interface potential density (kg/m³) — the !! surface interface for VCOORD_RHO.  With `rho_target_dense` !! builds the uniform light→dense target-density linspace !! (MOM6 `ALE_COORDINATE_CONFIG=UNIFORM` analogue for the RHO !! mode).  A stretched (RFNC1-style) profile is a P3 follow-up. real ( wp ) :: rho_target_dense = 103 0.0_wp !! Densest target interface potential density (kg/m³) — the bed !! interface for VCOORD_RHO.  See `rho_target_light`. ! Logging parameters character ( len = 16 ) :: log_level = \"info\" !! Log verbosity: \"debug\", \"verbose\", \"info\", \"performance\", \"warning\", \"error\" real ( wp ) :: status_interval = 0.0_wp !! Print status every N seconds of simulation time (0 = default every 100 steps) end type config_t","tags":"","url":"type/config_t.html"},{"title":"solver_handle_t – Rakali ","text":"type, public :: solver_handle_t Structured-solver handle. Mirrors the module-static state in rki_api so the Phase 2 cutover is a mechanical rename of\nbare state / cfg /flags to h%state / h%cfg /etc. Inherits type~~solver_handle_t~~InheritsGraph type~solver_handle_t solver_handle_t type~config_t config_t type~solver_handle_t->type~config_t cfg type~state_t state_t type~solver_handle_t->type~state_t state type~barotropic_state_t barotropic_state_t type~state_t->type~barotropic_state_t barotropic type~bc_params_t bc_params_t type~state_t->type~bc_params_t bc type~hgrid_t hgrid_t type~state_t->type~hgrid_t grid type~multilayer_state_t multilayer_state_t type~state_t->type~multilayer_state_t multilayer type~nonhydrostatic_state_t nonhydrostatic_state_t type~state_t->type~nonhydrostatic_state_t nh type~surface_forcing_t surface_forcing_t type~state_t->type~surface_forcing_t forcing type~eos_t eos_t type~multilayer_state_t->type~eos_t eos type~tracer_t tracer_t type~multilayer_state_t->type~tracer_t tracers type~vcoord_t vcoord_t type~multilayer_state_t->type~vcoord_t vcoord Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( config_t ), public :: cfg logical, public :: host_is_current = .false. logical, public :: is_finalised = .false. logical, public :: is_initialised = .false. integer, public :: magic = 0 logical, public :: on_device = .false. type( state_t ), public, pointer :: state => null() Pointer (not value) so c_loc(h%state%barotropic%h) keeps a stable\naddress across handle moves. Allocated in handle_create. real(kind=wp), public :: t_current = 0.0_wp logical, public :: user_set_bathymetry = .false. logical, public :: user_set_h = .false. logical, public :: user_set_layers = .false. Source Code type :: solver_handle_t !! Structured-solver handle. Mirrors the module-static state in !! `rki_api` so the Phase 2 cutover is a mechanical rename of !! bare `state`/`cfg`/flags to `h%state`/`h%cfg`/etc. integer :: magic = 0 type ( config_t ) :: cfg type ( state_t ), pointer :: state => null () !! Pointer (not value) so `c_loc(h%state%barotropic%h)` keeps a stable !! address across handle moves. Allocated in handle_create. real ( wp ) :: t_current = 0.0_wp logical :: is_initialised = . false . logical :: is_finalised = . false . logical :: on_device = . false . logical :: host_is_current = . false . logical :: user_set_bathymetry = . false . logical :: user_set_h = . false . logical :: user_set_layers = . false . end type solver_handle_t","tags":"","url":"type/solver_handle_t.html"},{"title":"solver_handle_unstr_t – Rakali ","text":"type, public :: solver_handle_unstr_t Unstructured-solver handle. Mirrors the module-static state in rki_api_unstr . Inherits type~~solver_handle_unstr_t~~InheritsGraph type~solver_handle_unstr_t solver_handle_unstr_t type~gauge_unstr_t gauge_unstr_t type~solver_handle_unstr_t->type~gauge_unstr_t gauges type~mesh_unstr_t mesh_unstr_t type~solver_handle_unstr_t->type~mesh_unstr_t mesh type~output_unstr_state_t output_unstr_state_t type~solver_handle_unstr_t->type~output_unstr_state_t ostate type~unstr_state_t unstr_state_t type~solver_handle_unstr_t->type~unstr_state_t state type~semi_implicit_state_unstr_t semi_implicit_state_unstr_t type~unstr_state_t->type~semi_implicit_state_unstr_t si type~unstr_barotropic_state_t unstr_barotropic_state_t type~unstr_state_t->type~unstr_barotropic_state_t barotropic type~unstr_multilayer_state_t unstr_multilayer_state_t type~unstr_state_t->type~unstr_multilayer_state_t multilayer type~unstr_surface_forcing_t unstr_surface_forcing_t type~unstr_state_t->type~unstr_surface_forcing_t forcing type~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t type~semi_implicit_state_unstr_t->type~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t mg type~eos_t eos_t type~unstr_multilayer_state_t->type~eos_t eos type~unstr_tracer_t unstr_tracer_t type~unstr_multilayer_state_t->type~unstr_tracer_t tracers type~vcoord_t vcoord_t type~unstr_multilayer_state_t->type~vcoord_t vcoord type~agglom_level_unstr_t agglom_level_unstr_t type~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t->type~agglom_level_unstr_t lev Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( gauge_unstr_t ), public :: gauges logical, public :: gauges_open = .false. logical, public :: is_finalised = .false. logical, public :: is_initialised = .false. integer, public :: magic = 0 type( mesh_unstr_t ), public, pointer :: mesh => null() logical, public :: on_device = .false. type( output_unstr_state_t ), public :: ostate logical, public :: output_open = .false. type( unstr_state_t ), public, pointer :: state => null() Source Code type :: solver_handle_unstr_t !! Unstructured-solver handle. Mirrors the module-static state in !! `rki_api_unstr`. integer :: magic = 0 type ( mesh_unstr_t ), pointer :: mesh => null () type ( unstr_state_t ), pointer :: state => null () type ( output_unstr_state_t ) :: ostate type ( gauge_unstr_t ) :: gauges logical :: is_initialised = . false . logical :: is_finalised = . false . logical :: on_device = . false . logical :: output_open = . false . logical :: gauges_open = . false . end type solver_handle_unstr_t","tags":"","url":"type/solver_handle_unstr_t.html"},{"title":"output_unstr_state_t – Rakali ","text":"type, public :: output_unstr_state_t Tracks the state of an open UGRID output file Inherited by type~~output_unstr_state_t~~InheritedByGraph type~output_unstr_state_t output_unstr_state_t type~solver_handle_unstr_t solver_handle_unstr_t type~solver_handle_unstr_t->type~output_unstr_state_t ostate Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, public :: has_ml = .false. True when 3D layer / tracer variables were defined. integer, public :: ml_h_layer_varid = -1 Layer thickness variable ID integer, public :: ml_rho_varid = -1 Layer density variable ID integer, public, allocatable :: ml_tracer_varids (:) Per-tracer NetCDF variable IDs, one per state%multilayer%tracers(:) entry. -1 for tracers that\naren’t being written.  Adding a sediment / passive scalar\nrequires no I/O changes — this loop picks it up. integer, public :: ml_u_varid = -1 Layer x-velocity variable ID (derived: hu_layer / h_layer) integer, public :: ml_v_varid = -1 Layer y-velocity variable ID integer, public :: ml_w_varid = -1 Vertical velocity at interfaces variable ID integer, public :: ncells = 0 Number of owned cells written per snapshot integer, public :: ncid = -1 NetCDF file ID (-1 = not open) integer, public :: nz_ml = 0 Number of sigma layers (cached for snapshot writes). integer, public :: stage_varid = -1 Free-surface elevation variable ID integer, public :: time_dimid = -1 Time dimension ID integer, public :: time_index = 0 Current time record index integer, public :: time_varid = -1 Time variable ID integer, public :: xmom_varid = -1 x-momentum variable ID integer, public :: ymom_varid = -1 y-momentum variable ID Source Code type :: output_unstr_state_t !! Tracks the state of an open UGRID output file integer :: ncid = - 1 !! NetCDF file ID (-1 = not open) integer :: time_dimid = - 1 !! Time dimension ID integer :: time_varid = - 1 !! Time variable ID integer :: stage_varid = - 1 !! Free-surface elevation variable ID integer :: xmom_varid = - 1 !! x-momentum variable ID integer :: ymom_varid = - 1 !! y-momentum variable ID integer :: time_index = 0 !! Current time record index integer :: ncells = 0 !! Number of owned cells written per snapshot ! ---- multilayer (only populated when state%use_multilayer) ---- logical :: has_ml = . false . !! True when 3D layer / tracer variables were defined. integer :: nz_ml = 0 !! Number of sigma layers (cached for snapshot writes). integer :: ml_h_layer_varid = - 1 !! Layer thickness variable ID integer :: ml_u_varid = - 1 !! Layer x-velocity variable ID (derived: hu_layer / h_layer) integer :: ml_v_varid = - 1 !! Layer y-velocity variable I