hgrid_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer , intent ( in ) :: nx_phys , ny_phys , nghost real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dx , dy this % nx_phys = nx_phys this % ny_phys = ny_phys this % nghost = nghost this % dx = dx this % dy = dy this % nx_total = nx_phys + 2 * nghost this % ny_total = ny_phys + 2 * nghost end subroutine grid_init","tags":"","url":"proc/grid_init.html"},{"title":"edge_prescribes – Rakali","text":"private pure function edge_prescribes(edge_type) result(prescribes) An edge accepts a prescribed inflow tracer value when it is an\ninflow (BC_INFLOW) or a Dirichlet-eta OPEN edge (BC_TIDAL /\nBC_CLAMPED) — the edges through which water can enter the domain\ncarrying a specified concentration.  The prescription still only\ntakes effect when tr_inflow >= 0 (checked at the call site), and the\nprescribed ghost is only READ on inflow (upwind), so a reversing\ntidal edge is inflow-value on flood and zero-gradient on ebb. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: edge_type Return Value logical Called by proc~~edge_prescribes~~CalledByGraph proc~edge_prescribes edge_prescribes proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs ml_apply_tracer_bcs proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs->proc~edge_prescribes proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1->proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function edge_prescribes ( edge_type ) result ( prescribes ) !! An edge accepts a prescribed inflow tracer value when it is an !! inflow (BC_INFLOW) or a Dirichlet-eta OPEN edge (BC_TIDAL / !! BC_CLAMPED) — the edges through which water can enter the domain !! carrying a specified concentration.  The prescription still only !! takes effect when tr_inflow >= 0 (checked at the call site), and the !! prescribed ghost is only READ on inflow (upwind), so a reversing !! tidal edge is inflow-value on flood and zero-gradient on ebb. integer , intent ( in ) :: edge_type logical :: prescribes prescribes = ( edge_type == BC_INFLOW . or . edge_type == BC_TIDAL & . or . edge_type == BC_CLAMPED ) end function edge_prescribes","tags":"","url":"proc/edge_prescribes.html"},{"title":"ml_advect_tracer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_advect_tracer(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, mass_flux_x, mass_flux_y, hTr_layer, adv_hTr_snap, grid, nz, dt) Per-layer horizontal advection of a scalar tracer hTr = h*Tr\nusing first-order upwind reconstruction. Per-face per-layer mass flux uses centred per-layer velocity\nwith a vanishing-layer GUARD that excludes layers where either\nside has h_layer(k) <= VANISHING_LAYER_TOL from the per-layer\nsplit, redistributing the residual across the active layers\nvia a per-face symmetric frac: ! For each face (one cell-side shown, the other is symmetric):\n  if h_self(k) > tol .and. h_nbr(k) > tol then\n     v_face(k)         = 0.5 * (hu_self(k) + hu_nbr(k))\n     h_face_active(k)  = 0.5 * (h_self(k)  + h_nbr(k))\n  else\n     v_face(k)         = 0\n     h_face_active(k)  = 0     ! vanishing layer carries no flux\n  end if\n  H_active   = sum_k h_face_active(k)\n  corr       = mass_flux_face - sum_k v_face(k)\n  frac(k)    = h_face_active(k) / H_active   ! 0 if vanishing\n  f_layer(k) = v_face(k) + frac(k) * corr v_face , h_face_active , and frac_face_active are all\ncomputed from 0.5*(self + nbr) quantities, so they are\nIDENTICAL when computed from cell A’s right-face perspective\nversus cell A+1’s left-face perspective → per-layer face mass\nconservation holds. sum_k(f_layer) = sum_k v_face + corr =\nmass_flux_face (CWC). For sigma / zsigma / zstar-lite where every layer is non-\nvanishing on both sides, frac_active(k) = h_face(k)/H_face =\n1/nz for uniform sigma, and the formula degenerates to the\noriginal centred CWC scheme — zero risk to existing tests. For ZSTAR_FULL deep-shallow interfaces, vanishing bed layers\nin the shallow cell are excluded from the per-layer split, so\nthe column flux is redistributed across the (active) non-\nvanishing layers instead of being centred-averaged into the\ntiny vanishing receivers.  No bloat of S in vanishing layers,\nno clamp clipping, no salt-mass leak. History: the original formulation used v_centred = 0.5 *\n(hu_self + hu_nbr) plus a frac_self-weighted correction.\nUnder sharp h_layer mismatches between cells (ZSTAR_FULL deep-\nshallow faces) the centred average over-allocated flux to\nvanishing layers, producing per-layer S drift that the\n[S_min, S_max] clamp then destroyed (~4 % salt-mass leak on\nthe LE 4 h tidal validation, 2026-05-11). Jacobi snapshot: all neighbour and own-cell tracer-value reads\n(tr_here, tr_up for each of the four upwind faces) are taken\nfrom adv_hTr_snap , a caller-owned scratch dummy that this\nkernel fills with hTr_layer (frozen at entry via a full-array do concurrent ) before the main kernel.\nWithout this, the read-neighbour / write-own pattern inside do concurrent is a race (UB): on sequential backends (gfortran\nCPU, nvfortran serial) later iterations see already-updated\nneighbour values, so the two cell-visits of a shared face\ndisagree and ~1e-7 tracer mass leaks per step.  The snapshot\ngives Jacobi semantics: CPU-serial and GPU-parallel launches\napply the same frozen input and produce bit-identical,\nconservative results.  Mirrors the identical fix in ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer (hdiff_hTr_pre). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: adv_hTr_snap (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Caller-owned Jacobi snapshot scratch (filled then read here). type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_advect_tracer~~CallsGraph proc~ml_advect_tracer ml_advect_tracer local local proc~ml_advect_tracer->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_advect_tracer~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_advect_tracer ml_advect_tracer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_advect_tracer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1->proc~ml_advect_tracer proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: H_active_xL real(kind=wp), private :: H_active_xR real(kind=wp), private :: H_active_yB real(kind=wp), private :: H_active_yT real(kind=wp), private :: corr_xL real(kind=wp), private :: corr_xR real(kind=wp), private :: corr_yB real(kind=wp), private :: corr_yT real(kind=wp), private :: dx real(kind=wp), private :: dy real(kind=wp), private :: f_layer real(kind=wp), private :: flux_x_left real(kind=wp), private :: flux_x_right real(kind=wp), private :: flux_y_bot real(kind=wp), private :: flux_y_top real(kind=wp), private :: h_col real(kind=wp), private :: h_iL real(kind=wp), private :: h_iR real(kind=wp), private :: h_jB real(kind=wp), private :: h_jT real(kind=wp), private :: h_val real(kind=wp), private :: hf_xL (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: hf_xR (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: hf_yB (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: hf_yT (NZ_STACK_MAX) integer, private :: i real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_xL real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_xR real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_yB real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_yT real(kind=wp), private :: inv_dx real(kind=wp), private :: inv_dy integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: kk integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: tr_here real(kind=wp), private :: tr_up real(kind=wp), private :: v_xL (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: v_xR (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: v_yB (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: v_yT (NZ_STACK_MAX) Source Code pure subroutine ml_advect_tracer ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & mass_flux_x , mass_flux_y , & hTr_layer , adv_hTr_snap , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Per-layer horizontal advection of a scalar tracer hTr = h*Tr !! using first-order upwind reconstruction. !! !! Per-face per-layer mass flux uses centred per-layer velocity !! with a vanishing-layer GUARD that excludes layers where either !! side has h_layer(k) <= VANISHING_LAYER_TOL from the per-layer !! split, redistributing the residual across the active layers !! via a per-face symmetric frac: !! !!   ! For each face (one cell-side shown, the other is symmetric): !!   if h_self(k) > tol .and. h_nbr(k) > tol then !!      v_face(k)         = 0.5 * (hu_self(k) + hu_nbr(k)) !!      h_face_active(k)  = 0.5 * (h_self(k)  + h_nbr(k)) !!   else !!      v_face(k)         = 0 !!      h_face_active(k)  = 0     ! vanishing layer carries no flux !!   end if !!   H_active   = sum_k h_face_active(k) !!   corr       = mass_flux_face - sum_k v_face(k) !!   frac(k)    = h_face_active(k) / H_active   ! 0 if vanishing !!   f_layer(k) = v_face(k) + frac(k) * corr !! !! `v_face`, `h_face_active`, and `frac_face_active` are all !! computed from `0.5*(self + nbr)` quantities, so they are !! IDENTICAL when computed from cell A's right-face perspective !! versus cell A+1's left-face perspective → per-layer face mass !! conservation holds.  `sum_k(f_layer) = sum_k v_face + corr = !! mass_flux_face` (CWC). !! !! For sigma / zsigma / zstar-lite where every layer is non- !! vanishing on both sides, `frac_active(k) = h_face(k)/H_face = !! 1/nz` for uniform sigma, and the formula degenerates to the !! original centred CWC scheme — zero risk to existing tests. !! !! For ZSTAR_FULL deep-shallow interfaces, vanishing bed layers !! in the shallow cell are excluded from the per-layer split, so !! the column flux is redistributed across the (active) non- !! vanishing layers instead of being centred-averaged into the !! tiny vanishing receivers.  No bloat of S in vanishing layers, !! no clamp clipping, no salt-mass leak. !! !! History: the original formulation used `v_centred = 0.5 * !! (hu_self + hu_nbr)` plus a frac_self-weighted correction. !! Under sharp h_layer mismatches between cells (ZSTAR_FULL deep- !! shallow faces) the centred average over-allocated flux to !! vanishing layers, producing per-layer S drift that the !! [S_min, S_max] clamp then destroyed (~4 % salt-mass leak on !! the LE 4 h tidal validation, 2026-05-11). !! !! Jacobi snapshot: all neighbour and own-cell tracer-value reads !! (tr_here, tr_up for each of the four upwind faces) are taken !! from `adv_hTr_snap`, a caller-owned scratch dummy that this !! kernel fills with `hTr_layer` (frozen at entry via a full-array !! `do concurrent`) before the main kernel. !! Without this, the read-neighbour / write-own pattern inside !! `do concurrent` is a race (UB): on sequential backends (gfortran !! CPU, nvfortran serial) later iterations see already-updated !! neighbour values, so the two cell-visits of a shared face !! disagree and ~1e-7 tracer mass leaks per step.  The snapshot !! gives Jacobi semantics: CPU-serial and GPU-parallel launches !! apply the same frozen input and produce bit-identical, !! conservative results.  Mirrors the identical fix in !! `ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer` (hdiff_hTr_pre). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mass_flux_x ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mass_flux_y ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: adv_hTr_snap ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) !! Caller-owned Jacobi snapshot scratch (filled then read here). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: i , j , k , kk , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: dx , dy real ( wp ) :: h_val , tr_here , h_col real ( wp ) :: f_layer , tr_up real ( wp ) :: flux_x_left , flux_x_right , flux_y_bot , flux_y_top real ( wp ) :: inv_dx , inv_dy real ( wp ) :: corr_xL , corr_xR , corr_yB , corr_yT real ( wp ) :: H_active_xL , H_active_xR , H_active_yB , H_active_yT real ( wp ) :: inv_H_xL , inv_H_xR , inv_H_yB , inv_H_yT real ( wp ) :: v_xL ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), v_xR ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: v_yB ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), v_yT ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: hf_xL ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), hf_xR ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: hf_yB ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), hf_yT ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: h_iL , h_iR , h_jB , h_jT nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost dx = grid % dx dy = grid % dy inv_dx = 1.0_wp / dx inv_dy = 1.0_wp / dy ! Jacobi snapshot: freeze hTr_layer before the main kernel so that ! all neighbour reads come from the pre-step values.  See docstring. do concurrent ( k = 1 : nz , j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx ) adv_hTr_snap ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) end do do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , kk , h_val , tr_here , h_col , & f_layer , tr_up , & flux_x_left , flux_x_right , flux_y_bot , flux_y_top , & corr_xL , corr_xR , corr_yB , corr_yT , & H_active_xL , H_active_xR , H_active_yB , H_active_yT , & inv_H_xL , inv_H_xR , inv_H_yB , inv_H_yT , & v_xL , v_xR , v_yB , v_yT , & hf_xL , hf_xR , hf_yB , hf_yT , & h_iL , h_iR , h_jB , h_jT ) h_col = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then ! Vanishing-layer-gated centred CWC.  For each face, layers ! where either side has h_layer(k) <= VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ! contribute zero per-layer flux; the residual is ! redistributed across active layers via a per-face ! symmetric frac (h_face_active(k) / sum h_face_active). ! See kernel docstring. corr_xL = mass_flux_x ( i - 1 , j ) corr_xR = mass_flux_x ( i , j ) corr_yB = mass_flux_y ( i , j - 1 ) corr_yT = mass_flux_y ( i , j ) H_active_xL = 0.0_wp H_active_xR = 0.0_wp H_active_yB = 0.0_wp H_active_yT = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_val = h_layer ( i , j , k ) h_iL = h_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) h_iR = h_layer ( i + 1 , j , k ) h_jB = h_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) h_jT = h_layer ( i , j + 1 , k ) if ( h_val > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . h_iL > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then v_xL ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( hu_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) + hu_layer ( i , j , k )) hf_xL ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_iL + h_val ) else v_xL ( k ) = 0.0_wp hf_xL ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_val > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . h_iR > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then v_xR ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( hu_layer ( i , j , k ) + hu_layer ( i + 1 , j , k )) hf_xR ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_val + h_iR ) else v_xR ( k ) = 0.0_wp hf_xR ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_val > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . h_jB > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then v_yB ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( hv_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) + hv_layer ( i , j , k )) hf_yB ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_jB + h_val ) else v_yB ( k ) = 0.0_wp hf_yB ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_val > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . h_jT > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then v_yT ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( hv_layer ( i , j , k ) + hv_layer ( i , j + 1 , k )) hf_yT ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_val + h_jT ) else v_yT ( k ) = 0.0_wp hf_yT ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if corr_xL = corr_xL - v_xL ( k ) corr_xR = corr_xR - v_xR ( k ) corr_yB = corr_yB - v_yB ( k ) corr_yT = corr_yT - v_yT ( k ) H_active_xL = H_active_xL + hf_xL ( k ) H_active_xR = H_active_xR + hf_xR ( k ) H_active_yB = H_active_yB + hf_yB ( k ) H_active_yT = H_active_yT + hf_yT ( k ) end do if ( H_active_xL > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_xL = 1.0_wp / H_active_xL else inv_H_xL = 0.0_wp end if if ( H_active_xR > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_xR = 1.0_wp / H_active_xR else inv_H_xR = 0.0_wp end if if ( H_active_yB > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_yB = 1.0_wp / H_active_yB else inv_H_yB = 0.0_wp end if if ( H_active_yT > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_yT = 1.0_wp / H_active_yT else inv_H_yT = 0.0_wp end if do k = 1 , nz h_val = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_val > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_here = adv_hTr_snap ( i , j , k ) / h_val else tr_here = 0.0_wp end if ! Left face (i-1/2) f_layer = v_xL ( k ) + hf_xL ( k ) * inv_H_xL * corr_xL if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then if ( h_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_up = adv_hTr_snap ( i - 1 , j , k ) / h_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if else tr_up = tr_here end if flux_x_left = f_layer * tr_up ! Right face (i+1/2) f_layer = v_xR ( k ) + hf_xR ( k ) * inv_H_xR * corr_xR if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then tr_up = tr_here else if ( h_layer ( i + 1 , j , k ) > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_up = adv_hTr_snap ( i + 1 , j , k ) / h_layer ( i + 1 , j , k ) else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if end if flux_x_right = f_layer * tr_up ! Bottom face (j-1/2) f_layer = v_yB ( k ) + hf_yB ( k ) * inv_H_yB * corr_yB if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then if ( h_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_up = adv_hTr_snap ( i , j - 1 , k ) / h_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if else tr_up = tr_here end if flux_y_bot = f_layer * tr_up ! Top face (j+1/2) f_layer = v_yT ( k ) + hf_yT ( k ) * inv_H_yT * corr_yT if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then tr_up = tr_here else if ( h_layer ( i , j + 1 , k ) > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_up = adv_hTr_snap ( i , j + 1 , k ) / h_layer ( i , j + 1 , k ) else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if end if flux_y_top = f_layer * tr_up hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) & - dt * (( flux_x_right - flux_x_left ) * inv_dx & + ( flux_y_top - flux_y_bot ) * inv_dy ) end do end if end do end subroutine ml_advect_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_advect_tracer.html"},{"title":"ml_advect_tracer_ppm – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_advect_tracer_ppm(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, mass_flux_x, mass_flux_y, hTr_layer, ppm_tr_snap, ppm_ql_x, ppm_qr_x, ppm_ql_y, ppm_qr_y, grid, nz, dt) Per-layer horizontal advection of a scalar tracer using the\nPiecewise Parabolic Method (Colella & Woodward 1984). Two-phase unsplit approach:\n  Phase 1 — PPM reconstruction: 4th-order edge interpolation with\n            Colella-Woodward monotonicity limiting.\n  Phase 2 — Flux + update: time-averaged parabolic integration\n            over the CFL-swept region at each face. Falls back to piecewise-constant (first-order upwind) at ghost\ncells where the 5-point stencil extends outside the domain. Per-face mass flux uses the same vanishing-layer-gated centred\nCWC split as ml_advect_tracer — see that kernel’s docstring\nfor the algebra and the ZSTAR_FULL deep-shallow motivation. h_face(k) = 0.5 * (h_layer(here) + h_layer(nbr)) is symmetric\nacross the face: the PPM CFL sigma = u_eff*dt/dx (with u_eff = f_layer / h_face ) drives the parabolic-profile\nintegration, and an asymmetric h_face would make the two\ncells at a face see different sigma and integrate the\nupwind profile to different tr_avg_up values, leaking mass\nfor any non-uniform tracer profile (the nz=1 closed-basin\nmass conservation test at 1e-12 catches this). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ppm_tr_snap (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Caller-owned concentration snapshot scratch. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ppm_ql_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Caller-owned limited left/right edge scratch (x/y directions). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ppm_qr_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ppm_ql_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ppm_qr_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_advect_tracer_ppm~~CallsGraph proc~ml_advect_tracer_ppm ml_advect_tracer_ppm local local proc~ml_advect_tracer_ppm->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_advect_tracer_ppm~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_advect_tracer_ppm ml_advect_tracer_ppm proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_advect_tracer_ppm proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1->proc~ml_advect_tracer_ppm proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: H_active_xL real(kind=wp), private :: H_active_xR real(kind=wp), private :: H_active_yB real(kind=wp), private :: H_active_yT real(kind=wp), private :: corr_xL real(kind=wp), private :: corr_xR real(kind=wp), private :: corr_yB real(kind=wp), private :: corr_yT real(kind=wp), private :: dq real(kind=wp), private :: dq_up real(kind=wp), private :: dx real(kind=wp), private :: dy real(kind=wp), private :: f_layer real(kind=wp), private :: flux_bot real(kind=wp), private :: flux_left real(kind=wp), private :: flux_right real(kind=wp), private :: flux_top real(kind=wp), private :: h_col real(kind=wp), private :: h_face real(kind=wp), private :: h_iL real(kind=wp), private :: h_iR real(kind=wp), private :: h_jB real(kind=wp), private :: h_jT real(kind=wp), private :: h_val real(kind=wp), private :: hf_xL (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: hf_xR (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: hf_yB (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: hf_yT (NZ_STACK_MAX) integer, private :: i real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_xL real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_xR real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_yB real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_yT real(kind=wp), private :: inv_dx real(kind=wp), private :: inv_dy integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: kk integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: q6 real(kind=wp), private :: q6_up real(kind=wp), private :: q_L real(kind=wp), private :: q_L_up real(kind=wp), private :: q_R real(kind=wp), private :: q_R_up real(kind=wp), private :: q_i real(kind=wp), private :: q_im1 real(kind=wp), private :: q_im2 real(kind=wp), private :: q_ip1 real(kind=wp), private :: q_ip2 real(kind=wp), private :: sigma real(kind=wp), private :: tr_avg_up real(kind=wp), private :: u_eff real(kind=wp), private :: v_xL (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: v_xR (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: v_yB (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: v_yT (NZ_STACK_MAX) Source Code pure subroutine ml_advect_tracer_ppm ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & mass_flux_x , mass_flux_y , & hTr_layer , & ppm_tr_snap , ppm_ql_x , ppm_qr_x , & ppm_ql_y , ppm_qr_y , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Per-layer horizontal advection of a scalar tracer using the !! Piecewise Parabolic Method (Colella & Woodward 1984). !! !! Two-phase unsplit approach: !!   Phase 1 — PPM reconstruction: 4th-order edge interpolation with !!             Colella-Woodward monotonicity limiting. !!   Phase 2 — Flux + update: time-averaged parabolic integration !!             over the CFL-swept region at each face. !! !! Falls back to piecewise-constant (first-order upwind) at ghost !! cells where the 5-point stencil extends outside the domain. !! !! Per-face mass flux uses the same vanishing-layer-gated centred !! CWC split as `ml_advect_tracer` — see that kernel's docstring !! for the algebra and the ZSTAR_FULL deep-shallow motivation. !! !! `h_face(k) = 0.5 * (h_layer(here) + h_layer(nbr))` is symmetric !! across the face: the PPM CFL `sigma = u_eff*dt/dx` (with !! `u_eff = f_layer / h_face`) drives the parabolic-profile !! integration, and an asymmetric `h_face` would make the two !! cells at a face see different `sigma` and integrate the !! upwind profile to different `tr_avg_up` values, leaking mass !! for any non-uniform tracer profile (the nz=1 closed-basin !! mass conservation test at 1e-12 catches this). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mass_flux_x ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mass_flux_y ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ppm_tr_snap ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) !! Caller-owned concentration snapshot scratch. real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ppm_ql_x ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) !! Caller-owned limited left/right edge scratch (x/y directions). real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ppm_qr_x ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ppm_ql_y ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ppm_qr_y ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: i , j , k , kk , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: dx , dy real ( wp ) :: inv_dx , inv_dy , h_col , h_val ! PPM reconstruction variables real ( wp ) :: q_im2 , q_im1 , q_i , q_ip1 , q_ip2 real ( wp ) :: q_L , q_R , dq , q6 ! Flux computation variables real ( wp ) :: f_layer , u_eff , h_face , sigma real ( wp ) :: flux_left , flux_right , flux_bot , flux_top real ( wp ) :: q_L_up , q_R_up , dq_up , q6_up , tr_avg_up real ( wp ) :: corr_xL , corr_xR , corr_yB , corr_yT real ( wp ) :: H_active_xL , H_active_xR , H_active_yB , H_active_yT real ( wp ) :: inv_H_xL , inv_H_xR , inv_H_yB , inv_H_yT real ( wp ) :: v_xL ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), v_xR ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: v_yB ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), v_yT ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: hf_xL ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), hf_xR ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: hf_yB ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), hf_yT ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: h_iL , h_iR , h_jB , h_jT nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost dx = grid % dx dy = grid % dy inv_dx = 1.0_wp / dx inv_dy = 1.0_wp / dy ! Short-name aliases onto the caller-owned scratch dummies. associate ( tr_snap => ppm_tr_snap , & ql_x => ppm_ql_x , qr_x => ppm_qr_x , & ql_y => ppm_ql_y , qr_y => ppm_qr_y ) ! ---- Phase 0: concentration snapshot + fallback initialisation ---- ! Ghost cells keep ql = qr = cell average (piecewise constant), ! so boundary faces degrade gracefully to first-order upwind. do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) if ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_snap ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_layer ( i , j , k ) else tr_snap ( i , j , k ) = 0.0_wp end if ql_x ( i , j , k ) = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) qr_x ( i , j , k ) = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) ql_y ( i , j , k ) = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) qr_y ( i , j , k ) = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) end do ! ---- Phase 1: PPM reconstruction for interior cells ---- ! Stencil: i-2..i+2, fits within nghost=2. do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , kk , q_im2 , q_im1 , q_i , q_ip1 , q_ip2 , q_L , q_R , dq , q6 , h_col ) h_col = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then do k = 1 , nz ! --- x-direction --- q_im2 = tr_snap ( i - 2 , j , k ) q_im1 = tr_snap ( i - 1 , j , k ) q_i = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) q_ip1 = tr_snap ( i + 1 , j , k ) q_ip2 = tr_snap ( i + 2 , j , k ) ! 4th-order interpolation to cell edges q_L = ( 7.0_wp / 1 2.0_wp ) * ( q_im1 + q_i ) & - ( 1.0_wp / 1 2.0_wp ) * ( q_im2 + q_ip1 ) q_R = ( 7.0_wp / 1 2.0_wp ) * ( q_i + q_ip1 ) & - ( 1.0_wp / 1 2.0_wp ) * ( q_im1 + q_ip2 ) ! Colella-Woodward monotonicity limiting if (( q_R - q_i ) * ( q_i - q_L ) <= 0.0_wp ) then ! Local extremum: flatten to constant q_L = q_i q_R = q_i else dq = q_R - q_L q6 = 6.0_wp * ( q_i - 0.5_wp * ( q_L + q_R )) if ( dq * q6 > dq * dq ) then q_L = 3.0_wp * q_i - 2.0_wp * q_R end if if ( dq * q6 < - ( dq * dq )) then q_R = 3.0_wp * q_i - 2.0_wp * q_L end if end if ql_x ( i , j , k ) = q_L qr_x ( i , j , k ) = q_R ! --- y-direction --- q_im2 = tr_snap ( i , j - 2 , k ) q_im1 = tr_snap ( i , j - 1 , k ) q_i = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) q_ip1 = tr_snap ( i , j + 1 , k ) q_ip2 = tr_snap ( i , j + 2 , k ) q_L = ( 7.0_wp / 1 2.0_wp ) * ( q_im1 + q_i ) & - ( 1.0_wp / 1 2.0_wp ) * ( q_im2 + q_ip1 ) q_R = ( 7.0_wp / 1 2.0_wp ) * ( q_i + q_ip1 ) & - ( 1.0_wp / 1 2.0_wp ) * ( q_im1 + q_ip2 ) if (( q_R - q_i ) * ( q_i - q_L ) <= 0.0_wp ) then q_L = q_i q_R = q_i else dq = q_R - q_L q6 = 6.0_wp * ( q_i - 0.5_wp * ( q_L + q_R )) if ( dq * q6 > dq * dq ) then q_L = 3.0_wp * q_i - 2.0_wp * q_R end if if ( dq * q6 < - ( dq * dq )) then q_R = 3.0_wp * q_i - 2.0_wp * q_L end if end if ql_y ( i , j , k ) = q_L qr_y ( i , j , k ) = q_R end do end if end do ! ---- Phase 2: flux computation and conservative update ---- do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , kk , h_val , f_layer , u_eff , h_face , sigma , & q_L_up , q_R_up , dq_up , q6_up , tr_avg_up , & flux_left , flux_right , flux_bot , flux_top , h_col , & corr_xL , corr_xR , corr_yB , corr_yT , & H_active_xL , H_active_xR , H_active_yB , H_active_yT , & inv_H_xL , inv_H_xR , inv_H_yB , inv_H_yT , & v_xL , v_xR , v_yB , v_yT , & hf_xL , hf_xR , hf_yB , hf_yT , & h_iL , h_iR , h_jB , h_jT ) h_col = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then ! Vanishing-layer-gated centred CWC (matches ! ml_advect_tracer above).  Layers with either side ! h_layer(k) <= VANISHING_LAYER_TOL contribute zero per- ! layer flux; residual goes to active layers via per-face ! symmetric frac (h_face_active(k) / sum h_face_active). corr_xL = mass_flux_x ( i - 1 , j ) corr_xR = mass_flux_x ( i , j ) corr_yB = mass_flux_y ( i , j - 1 ) corr_yT = mass_flux_y ( i , j ) H_active_xL = 0.0_wp H_active_xR = 0.0_wp H_active_yB = 0.0_wp H_active_yT = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_val = h_layer ( i , j , k ) h_iL = h_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) h_iR = h_layer ( i + 1 , j , k ) h_jB = h_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) h_jT = h_layer ( i , j + 1 , k ) if ( h_val > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . h_iL > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then v_xL ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( hu_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) + hu_layer ( i , j , k )) hf_xL ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_iL + h_val ) else v_xL ( k ) = 0.0_wp hf_xL ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_val > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . h_iR > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then v_xR ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( hu_layer ( i , j , k ) + hu_layer ( i + 1 , j , k )) hf_xR ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_val + h_iR ) else v_xR ( k ) = 0.0_wp hf_xR ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_val > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . h_jB > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then v_yB ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( hv_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) + hv_layer ( i , j , k )) hf_yB ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_jB + h_val ) else v_yB ( k ) = 0.0_wp hf_yB ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_val > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . h_jT > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then v_yT ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( hv_layer ( i , j , k ) + hv_layer ( i , j + 1 , k )) hf_yT ( k ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_val + h_jT ) else v_yT ( k ) = 0.0_wp hf_yT ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if corr_xL = corr_xL - v_xL ( k ) corr_xR = corr_xR - v_xR ( k ) corr_yB = corr_yB - v_yB ( k ) corr_yT = corr_yT - v_yT ( k ) H_active_xL = H_active_xL + hf_xL ( k ) H_active_xR = H_active_xR + hf_xR ( k ) H_active_yB = H_active_yB + hf_yB ( k ) H_active_yT = H_active_yT + hf_yT ( k ) end do if ( H_active_xL > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_xL = 1.0_wp / H_active_xL else inv_H_xL = 0.0_wp end if if ( H_active_xR > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_xR = 1.0_wp / H_active_xR else inv_H_xR = 0.0_wp end if if ( H_active_yB > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_yB = 1.0_wp / H_active_yB else inv_H_yB = 0.0_wp end if if ( H_active_yT > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_yT = 1.0_wp / H_active_yT else inv_H_yT = 0.0_wp end if do k = 1 , nz ! ---- x-direction fluxes ---- ! Left face (i-1/2) f_layer = v_xL ( k ) + hf_xL ( k ) * inv_H_xL * corr_xL h_face = 0.5_wp * ( h_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) + h_layer ( i , j , k )) if ( h_face > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_eff = f_layer / h_face sigma = min ( abs ( u_eff ) * dt * inv_dx , 1.0_wp ) else u_eff = 0.0_wp sigma = 0.0_wp end if if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then ! Upwind is cell i-1: sweep from right edge of i-1 q_L_up = ql_x ( i - 1 , j , k ) q_R_up = qr_x ( i - 1 , j , k ) tr_avg_up = tr_snap ( i - 1 , j , k ) dq_up = q_R_up - q_L_up q6_up = 6.0_wp * ( tr_avg_up - 0.5_wp * ( q_L_up + q_R_up )) flux_left = f_layer * ( q_R_up & - 0.5_wp * sigma * ( dq_up - q6_up * ( 1.0_wp - ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) * sigma ))) else if ( f_layer < 0.0_wp ) then ! Upwind is cell i: sweep from left edge of i q_L_up = ql_x ( i , j , k ) q_R_up = qr_x ( i , j , k ) tr_avg_up = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) dq_up = q_R_up - q_L_up q6_up = 6.0_wp * ( tr_avg_up - 0.5_wp * ( q_L_up + q_R_up )) flux_left = f_layer * ( q_L_up & + 0.5_wp * sigma * ( dq_up + q6_up * ( 1.0_wp - ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) * sigma ))) else flux_left = 0.0_wp end if ! Right face (i+1/2) f_layer = v_xR ( k ) + hf_xR ( k ) * inv_H_xR * corr_xR h_face = 0.5_wp * ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) + h_layer ( i + 1 , j , k )) if ( h_face > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_eff = f_layer / h_face sigma = min ( abs ( u_eff ) * dt * inv_dx , 1.0_wp ) else u_eff = 0.0_wp sigma = 0.0_wp end if if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then q_L_up = ql_x ( i , j , k ) q_R_up = qr_x ( i , j , k ) tr_avg_up = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) dq_up = q_R_up - q_L_up q6_up = 6.0_wp * ( tr_avg_up - 0.5_wp * ( q_L_up + q_R_up )) flux_right = f_layer * ( q_R_up & - 0.5_wp * sigma * ( dq_up - q6_up * ( 1.0_wp - ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) * sigma ))) else if ( f_layer < 0.0_wp ) then q_L_up = ql_x ( i + 1 , j , k ) q_R_up = qr_x ( i + 1 , j , k ) tr_avg_up = tr_snap ( i + 1 , j , k ) dq_up = q_R_up - q_L_up q6_up = 6.0_wp * ( tr_avg_up - 0.5_wp * ( q_L_up + q_R_up )) flux_right = f_layer * ( q_L_up & + 0.5_wp * sigma * ( dq_up + q6_up * ( 1.0_wp - ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) * sigma ))) else flux_right = 0.0_wp end if ! ---- y-direction fluxes ---- ! Bottom face (j-1/2) f_layer = v_yB ( k ) + hf_yB ( k ) * inv_H_yB * corr_yB h_face = 0.5_wp * ( h_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) + h_layer ( i , j , k )) if ( h_face > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_eff = f_layer / h_face sigma = min ( abs ( u_eff ) * dt * inv_dy , 1.0_wp ) else u_eff = 0.0_wp sigma = 0.0_wp end if if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then q_L_up = ql_y ( i , j - 1 , k ) q_R_up = qr_y ( i , j - 1 , k ) tr_avg_up = tr_snap ( i , j - 1 , k ) dq_up = q_R_up - q_L_up q6_up = 6.0_wp * ( tr_avg_up - 0.5_wp * ( q_L_up + q_R_up )) flux_bot = f_layer * ( q_R_up & - 0.5_wp * sigma * ( dq_up - q6_up * ( 1.0_wp - ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) * sigma ))) else if ( f_layer < 0.0_wp ) then q_L_up = ql_y ( i , j , k ) q_R_up = qr_y ( i , j , k ) tr_avg_up = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) dq_up = q_R_up - q_L_up q6_up = 6.0_wp * ( tr_avg_up - 0.5_wp * ( q_L_up + q_R_up )) flux_bot = f_layer * ( q_L_up & + 0.5_wp * sigma * ( dq_up + q6_up * ( 1.0_wp - ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) * sigma ))) else flux_bot = 0.0_wp end if ! Top face (j+1/2) f_layer = v_yT ( k ) + hf_yT ( k ) * inv_H_yT * corr_yT h_face = 0.5_wp * ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) + h_layer ( i , j + 1 , k )) if ( h_face > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_eff = f_layer / h_face sigma = min ( abs ( u_eff ) * dt * inv_dy , 1.0_wp ) else u_eff = 0.0_wp sigma = 0.0_wp end if if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then q_L_up = ql_y ( i , j , k ) q_R_up = qr_y ( i , j , k ) tr_avg_up = tr_snap ( i , j , k ) dq_up = q_R_up - q_L_up q6_up = 6.0_wp * ( tr_avg_up - 0.5_wp * ( q_L_up + q_R_up )) flux_top = f_layer * ( q_R_up & - 0.5_wp * sigma * ( dq_up - q6_up * ( 1.0_wp - ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) * sigma ))) else if ( f_layer < 0.0_wp ) then q_L_up = ql_y ( i , j + 1 , k ) q_R_up = qr_y ( i , j + 1 , k ) tr_avg_up = tr_snap ( i , j + 1 , k ) dq_up = q_R_up - q_L_up q6_up = 6.0_wp * ( tr_avg_up - 0.5_wp * ( q_L_up + q_R_up )) flux_top = f_layer * ( q_L_up & + 0.5_wp * sigma * ( dq_up + q6_up * ( 1.0_wp - ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) * sigma ))) else flux_top = 0.0_wp end if ! Conservative update hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) & - dt * (( flux_right - flux_left ) * inv_dx & + ( flux_top - flux_bot ) * inv_dy ) end do end if end do end associate end subroutine ml_advect_tracer_ppm","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_advect_tracer_ppm.html"},{"title":"ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes(hS_layer, hT_layer, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, heat_flux, evap_minus_precip, evap_mass_sink, evap_latent_cooling, rho_0, cp, grid, nz, dt) Apply prescribed surface fluxes to the top layer (k=nz). Two modes, selected by evap_mass_sink : Default (evap_mass_sink = .false.) — virtual salt flux: hT(nz) += dt * heat_flux / (rho_0 * cp)    ! thermal\n  hS(nz) += dt * (E - P) * S_top             ! virtual salt flux\nNeither term changes h_layer — real volume forcing is the job of\nthe existing precipitation field (applied to the barotropic h in\napply_friction). Mass-sink mode (evap_mass_sink = .true.) — real water removal: net evaporation dh = E dt is removed COLUMN-PROPORTIONALLY — every\nlayer’s h, hu, hv, hT is scaled by fac = 1 - dh/h_col while hS is\nheld.  Consequences (all exact, any tracer profile):\n  - water mass:  column loses exactly dh;\n  - salt:        evaporation removes WATER not salt — hS unchanged,\n                 so S = hS/h rises by 1/fac;\n  - heat:        the evaporated water carries its own temperature\n                 away (hT scales with h), so T = hT/h is invariant —\n                 no spurious warming.  This is the SENSIBLE heat of\n                 the removed liquid mass;\n  - latent heat: with evap_latent_cooling, evaporation ALSO withdraws\n                 the latent heat of vaporization of the removed mass,\n                 Q_lat = rho_water E_eff L_v [W/m²], applied as an\n                 additional surface cooling to hT(nz).  hT(nz) is\n                 fac-scaled by the sensible sink FIRST; the latent\n                 term is the additive increment applied AFTER that\n                 scaling (it is NOT the full hT(nz) update):\n                   hT(nz) += -(rho_water L_v/(rho_0 cp)) dh_eff  [°C·m].\n                 E_eff = dh_eff/dt is the effective (clamped) rate, so\n                 a dried-out column withdraws no latent heat.  This is\n                 DISTINCT from the sensible term above (phase-change\n                 energy vs. enthalpy of the departing liquid) — no\n                 double-count;\n  - momentum:    the water leaves at its own velocity (hu, hv scale\n                 with h), so u, v are invariant — no spurious\n                 acceleration.\nThe proportional form deliberately preserves the CURRENT layer\nlayout (sigma fractions are untouched), so the vcoord distribute /\nremap machinery sees a consistent column and no spurious\nlayer-reshape transport arises.  This mirrors how the barotropic\nprecipitation source dilutes the column as a whole; a\nsurface-INTENSIFIED evaporative salinity structure (sink localised\nto k=nz with w-coupled tracer transport) is a documented follow-up. Precipitation (evap_minus_precip < 0) is NOT added in mass-sink\nmode — real freshwater input remains the job of the barotropic\nprecipitation field. WET/DRY: the removal is clamped to the water available above\nML_MIN_DEPTH (dh_eff = min(dh, h_col - ML_MIN_DEPTH)); a column at\nor below ML_MIN_DEPTH stops evaporating.  The clamped (unsatisfied)\nfraction of the demand is dropped honestly — the water simply was\nnot there to evaporate; no compensating source is invented. Layer-index convention: the structured solver indexes layers\nbottom-up (k=1 is the bottom layer, k=nz is the surface layer\njust below the free surface).  This matches the BPG, rho_ref\nbuilder, and NH init.  Surface forcings therefore land at k=nz. Heat flux is in W/m&#94;2, positive into the ocean.  Evaporation\nminus precipitation is in m/s, positive for net evaporation. Skips columns shallower than ML_MIN_DEPTH and cells with a\nthin top layer (h_top < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD).  The clamp\nkernel that follows enforces physical bounds. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hS_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hT_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: heat_flux (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: evap_minus_precip (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) logical, intent(in) :: evap_mass_sink logical, intent(in) :: evap_latent_cooling real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: cp type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes~~CallsGraph proc~ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes local local proc~ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: S_top real(kind=wp), private :: dh_eff real(kind=wp), private :: dh_req real(kind=wp), private :: fac real(kind=wp), private :: h_col real(kind=wp), private :: h_top integer, private :: i real(kind=wp), private :: inv_rho0cp integer, private :: j real(kind=wp), private :: kin_heat_flux integer, private :: kk real(kind=wp), private :: latent_gain integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny Source Code pure subroutine ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes ( hS_layer , hT_layer , h_layer , & hu_layer , hv_layer , & heat_flux , evap_minus_precip , & evap_mass_sink , evap_latent_cooling , & rho_0 , cp , grid , nz , & dt ) !! Apply prescribed surface fluxes to the top layer (k=nz). !! !! Two modes, selected by `evap_mass_sink`: !! !! **Default (evap_mass_sink = .false.) — virtual salt flux:** !!   hT(nz) += dt * heat_flux / (rho_0 * cp)    ! thermal !!   hS(nz) += dt * (E - P) * S_top             ! virtual salt flux !! Neither term changes h_layer — real volume forcing is the job of !! the existing precipitation field (applied to the barotropic h in !! apply_friction). !! !! **Mass-sink mode (evap_mass_sink = .true.) — real water removal:** !! net evaporation dh = E*dt is removed COLUMN-PROPORTIONALLY — every !! layer's h, hu, hv, hT is scaled by fac = 1 - dh/h_col while hS is !! held.  Consequences (all exact, any tracer profile): !!   - water mass:  column loses exactly dh; !!   - salt:        evaporation removes WATER not salt — hS unchanged, !!                  so S = hS/h rises by 1/fac; !!   - heat:        the evaporated water carries its own temperature !!                  away (hT scales with h), so T = hT/h is invariant — !!                  no spurious warming.  This is the SENSIBLE heat of !!                  the removed liquid mass; !!   - latent heat: with evap_latent_cooling, evaporation ALSO withdraws !!                  the latent heat of vaporization of the removed mass, !!                  Q_lat = rho_water*E_eff*L_v [W/m²], applied as an !!                  additional surface cooling to hT(nz).  hT(nz) is !!                  fac-scaled by the sensible sink FIRST; the latent !!                  term is the additive increment applied AFTER that !!                  scaling (it is NOT the full hT(nz) update): !!                    hT(nz) += -(rho_water*L_v/(rho_0*cp))*dh_eff  [°C·m]. !!                  E_eff = dh_eff/dt is the effective (clamped) rate, so !!                  a dried-out column withdraws no latent heat.  This is !!                  DISTINCT from the sensible term above (phase-change !!                  energy vs. enthalpy of the departing liquid) — no !!                  double-count; !!   - momentum:    the water leaves at its own velocity (hu, hv scale !!                  with h), so u, v are invariant — no spurious !!                  acceleration. !! The proportional form deliberately preserves the CURRENT layer !! layout (sigma fractions are untouched), so the vcoord distribute / !! remap machinery sees a consistent column and no spurious !! layer-reshape transport arises.  This mirrors how the barotropic !! precipitation source dilutes the column as a whole; a !! surface-INTENSIFIED evaporative salinity structure (sink localised !! to k=nz with w-coupled tracer transport) is a documented follow-up. !! !! Precipitation (evap_minus_precip < 0) is NOT added in mass-sink !! mode — real freshwater input remains the job of the barotropic !! precipitation field. !! !! WET/DRY: the removal is clamped to the water available above !! ML_MIN_DEPTH (dh_eff = min(dh, h_col - ML_MIN_DEPTH)); a column at !! or below ML_MIN_DEPTH stops evaporating.  The clamped (unsatisfied) !! fraction of the demand is dropped honestly — the water simply was !! not there to evaporate; no compensating source is invented. !! !! Layer-index convention: the structured solver indexes layers !! bottom-up (k=1 is the bottom layer, k=nz is the surface layer !! just below the free surface).  This matches the BPG, rho_ref !! builder, and NH init.  Surface forcings therefore land at k=nz. !! !! Heat flux is in W/m&#94;2, positive into the ocean.  Evaporation !! minus precipitation is in m/s, positive for net evaporation. !! !! Skips columns shallower than ML_MIN_DEPTH and cells with a !! thin top layer (h_top < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD).  The clamp !! kernel that follows enforces physical bounds. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hS_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hT_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: heat_flux ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: evap_minus_precip ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) logical , intent ( in ) :: evap_mass_sink logical , intent ( in ) :: evap_latent_cooling real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho_0 , cp , dt integer :: i , j , kk , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: h_top , kin_heat_flux , S_top , inv_rho0cp , h_col real ( wp ) :: dh_req , dh_eff , fac , latent_gain nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost inv_rho0cp = 1.0_wp / ( rho_0 * cp ) ! Kinematic latent-heat withdrawal per metre of evaporated water: ! d(hT) = -latent_gain*dh_eff  [°C·m].  Zero unless latent cooling is on. latent_gain = 0.0_wp if ( evap_latent_cooling ) latent_gain = RHO_WATER * LATENT_HEAT_VAPORIZATION * inv_rho0cp do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( kk , h_top , kin_heat_flux , S_top , h_col , dh_req , dh_eff , fac ) h_col = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then h_top = h_layer ( i , j , nz ) if ( h_top > THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) then ! Thermal (unchanged in both modes): dt * Q_net / (rho_0 * cp) kin_heat_flux = heat_flux ( i , j ) * inv_rho0cp hT_layer ( i , j , nz ) = hT_layer ( i , j , nz ) + dt * kin_heat_flux if ( evap_mass_sink ) then ! Column-proportional water-mass sink (see docstring). ! Salt mass hS is held; h, hu, hv, hT scale by fac so S ! concentrates while T, u, v stay invariant. dh_req = dt * max ( evap_minus_precip ( i , j ), 0.0_wp ) dh_eff = min ( dh_req , max ( h_col - ML_MIN_DEPTH , 0.0_wp )) if ( dh_eff > 0.0_wp ) then fac = 1.0_wp - dh_eff / h_col do kk = 1 , nz h_layer ( i , j , kk ) = h_layer ( i , j , kk ) * fac hu_layer ( i , j , kk ) = hu_layer ( i , j , kk ) * fac hv_layer ( i , j , kk ) = hv_layer ( i , j , kk ) * fac hT_layer ( i , j , kk ) = hT_layer ( i , j , kk ) * fac ! hS_layer held -> concentration rises naturally. end do ! Latent-heat cooling (additive, top layer only; not ! scaled by fac so the withdrawal equals Q_lat exactly). ! latent_gain == 0 when the knob is off -> bit-identical. hT_layer ( i , j , nz ) = hT_layer ( i , j , nz ) - latent_gain * dh_eff end if else ! Legacy virtual salt flux (bit-identical default). S_top = hS_layer ( i , j , nz ) / h_top hS_layer ( i , j , nz ) = hS_layer ( i , j , nz ) & + dt * evap_minus_precip ( i , j ) * S_top end if end if end if end do end subroutine ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes.html"},{"title":"ml_apply_tracer_bcs – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_apply_tracer_bcs(hTr_layer, h_layer, tr_inflow, grid, nz, bc) Set a scalar tracer in ghost cells. Default: zero-gradient extrapolation (copy hTr from nearest interior\ncell, scaled by local layer thickness).  For OPEN boundaries with a\nprescribed tracer value (tr_inflow >= 0) — inflow (BC_INFLOW) and the\nDirichlet-eta open edges (BC_TIDAL / BC_CLAMPED) — ghost cells are set\nto h_layer * tr_inflow so that INFLOWING water carries the prescribed\nvalue rather than the interior one.  The ghost value is only READ by\nthe upwind advection when the face flux is INTO the domain (flood on\na tidal edge); on OUTFLOW (ebb) the interior cell is upwind, so the\nprescribed ghost is ignored and the edge is zero-gradient — the\nreversing tidal edge gets the correct inflow-value / zero-gradient-\noutflow behaviour automatically.  With tr_inflow < 0 (the default,\nunset) every edge is zero-gradient — bit-identical to before. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_inflow type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz type( bc_params_t ), intent(in) :: bc Calls proc~~ml_apply_tracer_bcs~~CallsGraph proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs ml_apply_tracer_bcs proc~edge_prescribes edge_prescribes proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs->proc~edge_prescribes Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_apply_tracer_bcs~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs ml_apply_tracer_bcs proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1->proc~ml_apply_tracer_bcs proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: g integer, private :: i integer, private :: i_int integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny logical, private :: prescribe_east logical, private :: prescribe_north logical, private :: prescribe_south logical, private :: prescribe_west Source Code pure subroutine ml_apply_tracer_bcs ( hTr_layer , h_layer , tr_inflow , & grid , nz , bc ) !! Set a scalar tracer in ghost cells. !! !! Default: zero-gradient extrapolation (copy hTr from nearest interior !! cell, scaled by local layer thickness).  For OPEN boundaries with a !! prescribed tracer value (tr_inflow >= 0) — inflow (BC_INFLOW) and the !! Dirichlet-eta open edges (BC_TIDAL / BC_CLAMPED) — ghost cells are set !! to h_layer * tr_inflow so that INFLOWING water carries the prescribed !! value rather than the interior one.  The ghost value is only READ by !! the upwind advection when the face flux is INTO the domain (flood on !! a tidal edge); on OUTFLOW (ebb) the interior cell is upwind, so the !! prescribed ghost is ignored and the edge is zero-gradient — the !! reversing tidal edge gets the correct inflow-value / zero-gradient- !! outflow behaviour automatically.  With tr_inflow < 0 (the default, !! unset) every edge is zero-gradient — bit-identical to before. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tr_inflow type ( bc_params_t ), intent ( in ) :: bc integer :: i , j , k , g , i_int , nx , ny , nghost logical :: prescribe_west , prescribe_east , prescribe_south , prescribe_north nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost prescribe_west = ( edge_prescribes ( bc % west ) . and . tr_inflow >= 0.0_wp ) prescribe_east = ( edge_prescribes ( bc % east ) . and . tr_inflow >= 0.0_wp ) prescribe_south = ( edge_prescribes ( bc % south ) . and . tr_inflow >= 0.0_wp ) prescribe_north = ( edge_prescribes ( bc % north ) . and . tr_inflow >= 0.0_wp ) ! West do g = 1 , nghost i_int = nghost + 1 if ( prescribe_west ) then do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , k = 1 : nz ) hTr_layer ( g , j , k ) = h_layer ( g , j , k ) * tr_inflow end do else do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , k = 1 : nz ) hTr_layer ( g , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i_int , j , k ) & * h_layer ( g , j , k ) & / max ( h_layer ( i_int , j , k ), DRY_TOLERANCE ) end do end if end do ! East do g = nx - nghost + 1 , nx i_int = nx - nghost if ( prescribe_east ) then do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , k = 1 : nz ) hTr_layer ( g , j , k ) = h_layer ( g , j , k ) * tr_inflow end do else do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , k = 1 : nz ) hTr_layer ( g , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i_int , j , k ) & * h_layer ( g , j , k ) & / max ( h_layer ( i_int , j , k ), DRY_TOLERANCE ) end do end if end do ! South do g = 1 , nghost i_int = nghost + 1 if ( prescribe_south ) then do concurrent ( i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) hTr_layer ( i , g , k ) = h_layer ( i , g , k ) * tr_inflow end do else do concurrent ( i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) hTr_layer ( i , g , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , i_int , k ) & * h_layer ( i , g , k ) & / max ( h_layer ( i , i_int , k ), DRY_TOLERANCE ) end do end if end do ! North do g = ny - nghost + 1 , ny i_int = ny - nghost if ( prescribe_north ) then do concurrent ( i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) hTr_layer ( i , g , k ) = h_layer ( i , g , k ) * tr_inflow end do else do concurrent ( i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) hTr_layer ( i , g , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , i_int , k ) & * h_layer ( i , g , k ) & / max ( h_layer ( i , i_int , k ), DRY_TOLERANCE ) end do end if end do end subroutine ml_apply_tracer_bcs","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_apply_tracer_bcs.html"},{"title":"ml_clamp_tracer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_clamp_tracer(hTr_layer, h_layer, tr_min, tr_max, grid, nz) Enforce physical tracer bounds tr_min <= Tr <= tr_max\nconservatively within each column. Two-pass column-conservative limiter (MOM6/NEMO style): Pass 1 — clip violators.  For any layer with S = hTr/h outside [tr_min, tr_max], reset hTr to the bound and\n           accumulate the rejected excess_above (above tr_max,\n           destroyed) and deficit_below (below tr_min, created)\n           in PSU·m.  Track the per-cell cap_to_add (room\n           still available to push concentration up toward\n           tr_max in non-saturated layers) and cap_to_remove (room to pull concentration down toward tr_min). Pass 2 — redistribute the net imbalance net = excess_above\n           - deficit_below into the column’s spare capacity.\n           If net > 0 (more destroyed than created): push it\n           back into layers with cap_to_add, proportionally to\n           each layer’s room-to-fill.  If net < 0: pull it\n           from layers with cap_to_remove, proportionally to\n           each layer’s room-to-empty.  When the column-mean\n           S is itself outside [tr_min, tr_max] (rare for\n           normal seawater) the redistribution saturates and\n           the residual imbalance is unavoidably destroyed /\n           created — this is the irreducible cost of holding\n           a hard bound. Per-cell tracer total is preserved exactly when the column-\nmean concentration is in bounds, even though individual layers\nwere violating.  This is the right behaviour for the rescaled-\nS inflation produced by ml_distribute_with_remap_full under\nVCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL: the per-layer S after the conservative\nremap can sit above tr_max as a numerical artefact of the dz_old_col = remap_dz_old * scale_old rescaling, while the\nphysical column-mean is still well inside bounds; the previous\nhard clip would have destroyed the very tracer the conservative\nremap had just preserved. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_min real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_max type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz Calls proc~~ml_clamp_tracer~~CallsGraph proc~ml_clamp_tracer ml_clamp_tracer local local proc~ml_clamp_tracer->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_clamp_tracer~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_clamp_tracer ml_clamp_tracer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_clamp_tracer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1->proc~ml_clamp_tracer proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: TINY_CAP = 1.0e-30_wp real(kind=wp), private :: cap_to_add real(kind=wp), private :: cap_to_remove real(kind=wp), private :: col_h real(kind=wp), private :: col_hTr real(kind=wp), private :: deficit_below real(kind=wp), private :: excess_above real(kind=wp), private :: frac real(kind=wp), private :: h_k integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: net integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: room_k real(kind=wp), private :: tr_k Source Code pure subroutine ml_clamp_tracer ( hTr_layer , h_layer , tr_min , tr_max , & grid , nz ) !! Enforce physical tracer bounds tr_min <= Tr <= tr_max !! conservatively within each column. !! !! Two-pass column-conservative limiter (MOM6/NEMO style): !! !!   Pass 1 — clip violators.  For any layer with `S = hTr/h` !!            outside [tr_min, tr_max], reset hTr to the bound and !!            accumulate the rejected `excess_above` (above tr_max, !!            destroyed) and `deficit_below` (below tr_min, created) !!            in PSU·m.  Track the per-cell `cap_to_add` (room !!            still available to push concentration up toward !!            tr_max in non-saturated layers) and `cap_to_remove` !!            (room to pull concentration down toward tr_min). !! !!   Pass 2 — redistribute the net imbalance `net = excess_above !!            - deficit_below` into the column's spare capacity. !!            If net > 0 (more destroyed than created): push it !!            back into layers with cap_to_add, proportionally to !!            each layer's room-to-fill.  If net < 0: pull it !!            from layers with cap_to_remove, proportionally to !!            each layer's room-to-empty.  When the column-mean !!            S is itself outside [tr_min, tr_max] (rare for !!            normal seawater) the redistribution saturates and !!            the residual imbalance is unavoidably destroyed / !!            created — this is the irreducible cost of holding !!            a hard bound. !! !! Per-cell tracer total is preserved exactly when the column- !! mean concentration is in bounds, even though individual layers !! were violating.  This is the right behaviour for the rescaled- !! S inflation produced by `ml_distribute_with_remap_full` under !! VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL: the per-layer S after the conservative !! remap can sit above tr_max as a numerical artefact of the !! `dz_old_col = remap_dz_old * scale_old` rescaling, while the !! physical column-mean is still well inside bounds; the previous !! hard clip would have destroyed the very tracer the conservative !! remap had just preserved. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tr_min , tr_max integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: tr_k , h_k , room_k real ( wp ) :: excess_above , deficit_below , cap_to_add , cap_to_remove real ( wp ) :: net , frac real ( wp ) :: col_hTr , col_h real ( wp ), parameter :: TINY_CAP = 1.0e-30_wp nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , tr_k , h_k , room_k , & excess_above , deficit_below , cap_to_add , cap_to_remove , & net , frac , col_hTr , col_h ) ! Pass 0: column mean.  The two-pass clip+redistribute below is ! EXACTLY conservative if and only if the column-mean concentration ! lies within [tr_min, tr_max].  Proof for the upper bound: !   mean <= tr_max !     <=> sum_k (tr_max - tr_k) h_k >= 0 !     <=> -excess_above + cap_unsat + (cap_below + deficit_below) >= 0 !     <=> excess_above - deficit_below <= cap_unsat + cap_below !     <=> net <= cap_to_add ! so `frac = min(1, net/cap_to_add)` never saturates and every unit ! removed in pass 1 is returned in pass 2.  Symmetrically for tr_min. ! ! When the mean is OUTSIDE the bounds no clamp can both hold the ! bound and conserve, and the old code silently destroyed the ! un-absorbable residual `net - cap_to_add`.  With the default ! S_max sitting at 40 PSU that fired continuously at sharp fronts ! and leaked ~9e-6 of the domain salt per 400 steps.  Conservation ! wins: skip the column instead.  Leaving the value visibly out of ! range also surfaces the upstream problem rather than hiding it. col_hTr = 0.0_wp col_h = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then col_hTr = col_hTr + hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) col_h = col_h + h_k else hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = 0.0_wp end if end do if ( col_h > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = col_hTr / col_h if ( tr_k > tr_max . or . tr_k < tr_min ) cycle else cycle end if ! Pass 1: hard clip violators, accumulate per-cell excess/deficit ! and the spare capacity remaining in non-saturated layers. excess_above = 0.0_wp deficit_below = 0.0_wp cap_to_add = 0.0_wp cap_to_remove = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k if ( tr_k > tr_max ) then excess_above = excess_above + ( tr_k - tr_max ) * h_k hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = tr_max * h_k ! Saturated above: no room to add, all room to remove. cap_to_remove = cap_to_remove + ( tr_max - tr_min ) * h_k else if ( tr_k < tr_min ) then deficit_below = deficit_below + ( tr_min - tr_k ) * h_k hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = tr_min * h_k ! Saturated below: all room to add, none to remove. cap_to_add = cap_to_add + ( tr_max - tr_min ) * h_k else cap_to_add = cap_to_add + ( tr_max - tr_k ) * h_k cap_to_remove = cap_to_remove + ( tr_k - tr_min ) * h_k end if else hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = 0.0_wp end if end do ! Pass 2: redistribute net imbalance into available capacity. ! Conservative within the cell when capacity is sufficient; ! falls back to leaving the residual outside bounds when the ! column-mean itself is out of range. net = excess_above - deficit_below if ( net > 0.0_wp . and . cap_to_add > TINY_CAP ) then frac = min ( 1.0_wp , net / cap_to_add ) do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k room_k = ( tr_max - tr_k ) * h_k if ( room_k > 0.0_wp ) then hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) + frac * room_k end if end if end do else if ( net < 0.0_wp . and . cap_to_remove > TINY_CAP ) then frac = min ( 1.0_wp , ( - net ) / cap_to_remove ) do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k room_k = ( tr_k - tr_min ) * h_k if ( room_k > 0.0_wp ) then hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) - frac * room_k end if end if end do end if end do end subroutine ml_clamp_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_clamp_tracer.html"},{"title":"ml_distribute_tracer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_distribute_tracer(h_layer, hTr_layer, dsig, h_new, grid, nz) Update hTr through the barotropic step: preserve tracer Tr,\nset h_k = dsig_k * H_new, hTr_k = h_k_new * Tr_k_old. Call BEFORE ml_distribute_barotropic (which overwrites h_layer). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Old layer depths (before barotropic update) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Tracer h*Tr (updated using old Tr and new h) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_new (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) Total depth AFTER barotropic update type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz Calls proc~~ml_distribute_tracer~~CallsGraph proc~ml_distribute_tracer ml_distribute_tracer local local proc~ml_distribute_tracer->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: h_k_new real(kind=wp), private :: h_k_old integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: tr_k Source Code pure subroutine ml_distribute_tracer ( h_layer , hTr_layer , dsig , h_new , & grid , nz ) !! Update hTr through the barotropic step: preserve tracer Tr, !! set h_k = dsig_k * H_new, hTr_k = h_k_new * Tr_k_old. !! !! Call BEFORE ml_distribute_barotropic (which overwrites h_layer). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) !! Old layer depths (before barotropic update) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) !! Tracer h*Tr (updated using old Tr and new h) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dsig ( nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_new ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) !! Total depth AFTER barotropic update integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: tr_k , h_k_old , h_k_new nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , tr_k , h_k_old , h_k_new ) do k = 1 , nz h_k_old = h_layer ( i , j , k ) h_k_new = dsig ( k ) * h_new ( i , j ) if ( h_k_old > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k_old else tr_k = 0.0_wp end if hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = h_k_new * tr_k end do end do end subroutine ml_distribute_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_distribute_tracer.html"},{"title":"ml_erode_bed_sediment – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_erode_bed_sediment(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, hTr_sed, bed, manning_n, rho_0, tau_ce, e_rate, porosity, grid, nz, dt) Ariathurai-Arulanandan (1978) bed erosion of suspended sediment.\nWhere the bed shear stress exceeds the critical erosion stress tau_ce , lift bed sediment into the bottom (lowest active) layer: E = e_rate * (1 - porosity) * (tau_b/tau_ce - 1)   [kg/m&#94;2/s], +ve only integrated over dt and capped at the available bed mass for\npositivity.  Conservative against the bed: the suspended bottom\nlayer gains exactly what bed loses, so total (suspended + bed) is\npreserved.  The bed stress is the same one the momentum drag\napplies (Manning-consistent, mirrors ml_apply_bottom_friction ): cf = g * n&#94;2 / H&#94;(1/3),   tau_b = rho_0 * cf * |u_b|&#94;2 so erosion responds to the resolved bed shear without a separate\nsediment-only drag law.  Bottom-up convention: k=1 is the bed; the\nlowest non-vanishing layer receives the eroded mass (handles\nZSTAR_FULL parked bottom layers like the friction kernel). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_sed (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: bed (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: manning_n real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tau_ce real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: e_rate real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: porosity type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_erode_bed_sediment~~CallsGraph proc~ml_erode_bed_sediment ml_erode_bed_sediment local local proc~ml_erode_bed_sediment->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_erode_bed_sediment~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_erode_bed_sediment ml_erode_bed_sediment proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~ml_erode_bed_sediment proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: cf real(kind=wp), private :: dm real(kind=wp), private :: h_k real(kind=wp), private :: h_total integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k_bot integer, private :: kk integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: speed_b real(kind=wp), private :: tau_b real(kind=wp), private :: u_b real(kind=wp), private :: v_b Source Code pure subroutine ml_erode_bed_sediment ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , hTr_sed , bed , & manning_n , rho_0 , tau_ce , e_rate , porosity , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Ariathurai-Arulanandan (1978) bed erosion of suspended sediment. !! Where the bed shear stress exceeds the critical erosion stress !! `tau_ce`, lift bed sediment into the bottom (lowest active) layer: !! !!   E = e_rate * (1 - porosity) * (tau_b/tau_ce - 1)   [kg/m&#94;2/s], +ve only !! !! integrated over `dt` and capped at the available bed mass for !! positivity.  Conservative against the bed: the suspended bottom !! layer gains exactly what `bed` loses, so total (suspended + bed) is !! preserved.  The bed stress is the *same* one the momentum drag !! applies (Manning-consistent, mirrors `ml_apply_bottom_friction`): !! !!   cf = g * n&#94;2 / H&#94;(1/3),   tau_b = rho_0 * cf * |u_b|&#94;2 !! !! so erosion responds to the resolved bed shear without a separate !! sediment-only drag law.  Bottom-up convention: k=1 is the bed; the !! lowest non-vanishing layer receives the eroded mass (handles !! ZSTAR_FULL parked bottom layers like the friction kernel). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_sed ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: bed ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: manning_n , rho_0 , tau_ce , e_rate , porosity , dt integer :: i , j , kk , k_bot , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: h_k , h_total , u_b , v_b , speed_b , cf , tau_b , dm if ( e_rate <= 0.0_wp . or . tau_ce <= 0.0_wp . or . manning_n <= 0.0_wp ) return nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( kk , k_bot , h_k , h_total , u_b , v_b , speed_b , cf , tau_b , dm ) ! Lowest active layer (mirrors ml_apply_bottom_friction). k_bot = 1 do kk = 1 , nz if ( h_layer ( i , j , kk ) > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then k_bot = kk exit end if end do h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) if ( h_k < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) cycle h_total = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_total = h_total + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_total < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) cycle u_b = hu_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) / h_k v_b = hv_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) / h_k speed_b = sqrt ( u_b * u_b + v_b * v_b ) cf = GRAVITY * manning_n * manning_n / ( h_total ** ( 1.0_wp / 3.0_wp )) tau_b = rho_0 * cf * speed_b * speed_b if ( tau_b <= tau_ce ) cycle ! Eroded mass this step, capped at what the bed holds. dm = e_rate * ( 1.0_wp - porosity ) * ( tau_b / tau_ce - 1.0_wp ) * dt dm = min ( dm , bed ( i , j )) bed ( i , j ) = bed ( i , j ) - dm hTr_sed ( i , j , k_bot ) = hTr_sed ( i , j , k_bot ) + dm end do end subroutine ml_erode_bed_sediment","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_erode_bed_sediment.html"},{"title":"ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer(h_layer, hTr_layer, kappa, hdiff_hTr_pre, grid, nz, dt) Horizontal Laplacian diffusion of a scalar tracer in flux form,\nconservative per-face under non-uniform layer thicknesses. Per face the diffusive flux is\n  flux_face_x = h_face * kappa_eff * (Tr_nbr - Tr_self) / dx\nwhere h_face = 0.5 * (h_self + h_nbr) is symmetric across the\nface.  Applied with opposite signs to the two adjacent cells\nthrough the divergence form\n  d(hTr)/dt = (flux_x_right - flux_x_left)/dx + (flux_y_top - flux_y_bot)/dy\nso what cell A gains from face A-B equals what cell B loses\nthrough the same face; mass conservation holds even when the\nper-cell layer thicknesses differ across the face. History: the previous formulation computed dtr = kappa·dt·∇²Tr and updated hTr_new = h_self · (Tr_self + dtr) .  Each cell\nused its OWN h on the RHS, so adjacent cells with different h_layer(k) (e.g., zsigma / zstar at bathymetric transitions)\nsaw different mass changes through the same shared face,\nleaking total mass.  Currently dormant in production runs\n( hdiff_kappa = 0 in the LE / Sydney Harbour configs) but\nwould bite the moment any user enables it. Skips dry columns (sum(h_layer) < ML_MIN_DEPTH) and treats dry\nneighbours as zero-flux walls (face flux = 0), preserving the\nsymmetric per-face conservation property.  Includes a\ndiffusive stability limiter: kappa_eff <= 0.5 / (dt·(1/dx² + 1/dy²)). Jacobi vs Gauss-Seidel: snapshot hTr_layer into a local\nscratch on entry and read neighbour concentrations from the\nfrozen copy, so CPU-sequential and GPU-parallel builds give\nbit-identical results. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: hdiff_hTr_pre (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Caller-owned Jacobi pre-step snapshot scratch. type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer~~CallsGraph proc~ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer local local proc~ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1->proc~ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: dx real(kind=wp), private :: dy real(kind=wp), private :: flux_x_left real(kind=wp), private :: flux_x_right real(kind=wp), private :: flux_y_bot real(kind=wp), private :: flux_y_top real(kind=wp), private :: h_col real(kind=wp), private :: h_self integer, private :: i real(kind=wp), private :: inv_dx real(kind=wp), private :: inv_dx2 real(kind=wp), private :: inv_dy real(kind=wp), private :: inv_dy2 integer, private :: j integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: kappa_eff integer, private :: kk integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: tr_c real(kind=wp), private :: tr_im real(kind=wp), private :: tr_ip real(kind=wp), private :: tr_jm real(kind=wp), private :: tr_jp Source Code pure subroutine ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer ( h_layer , hTr_layer , kappa , & hdiff_hTr_pre , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Horizontal Laplacian diffusion of a scalar tracer in flux form, !! conservative per-face under non-uniform layer thicknesses. !! !! Per face the diffusive flux is !!   flux_face_x = h_face * kappa_eff * (Tr_nbr - Tr_self) / dx !! where `h_face = 0.5 * (h_self + h_nbr)` is symmetric across the !! face.  Applied with opposite signs to the two adjacent cells !! through the divergence form !!   d(hTr)/dt = (flux_x_right - flux_x_left)/dx + (flux_y_top - flux_y_bot)/dy !! so what cell A gains from face A-B equals what cell B loses !! through the same face; mass conservation holds even when the !! per-cell layer thicknesses differ across the face. !! !! History: the previous formulation computed `dtr = kappa·dt·∇²Tr` !! and updated `hTr_new = h_self · (Tr_self + dtr)`.  Each cell !! used its OWN h on the RHS, so adjacent cells with different !! `h_layer(k)` (e.g., zsigma / zstar at bathymetric transitions) !! saw different mass changes through the same shared face, !! leaking total mass.  Currently dormant in production runs !! (`hdiff_kappa = 0` in the LE / Sydney Harbour configs) but !! would bite the moment any user enables it. !! !! Skips dry columns (sum(h_layer) < ML_MIN_DEPTH) and treats dry !! neighbours as zero-flux walls (face flux = 0), preserving the !! symmetric per-face conservation property.  Includes a !! diffusive stability limiter: kappa_eff <= 0.5 / (dt·(1/dx² + 1/dy²)). !! !! Jacobi vs Gauss-Seidel: snapshot `hTr_layer` into a local !! scratch on entry and read neighbour concentrations from the !! frozen copy, so CPU-sequential and GPU-parallel builds give !! bit-identical results. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: hdiff_hTr_pre ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) !! Caller-owned Jacobi pre-step snapshot scratch. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: kappa , dt integer :: i , j , k , kk , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: dx , dy real ( wp ) :: tr_c , tr_ip , tr_im , tr_jp , tr_jm , h_col , h_self real ( wp ) :: kappa_eff , inv_dx , inv_dy , inv_dx2 , inv_dy2 real ( wp ) :: flux_x_right , flux_x_left , flux_y_top , flux_y_bot nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost dx = grid % dx dy = grid % dy if ( kappa <= 0.0_wp ) return ! Stability limiter: kappa * dt * (1/dx&#94;2 + 1/dy&#94;2) <= 0.5 inv_dx = 1.0_wp / dx inv_dy = 1.0_wp / dy inv_dx2 = inv_dx * inv_dx inv_dy2 = inv_dy * inv_dy kappa_eff = min ( kappa , 0.5_wp / ( dt * ( inv_dx2 + inv_dy2 ) + 1.0e-30_wp )) associate ( hTr_pre => hdiff_hTr_pre ) do concurrent ( k = 1 : nz , j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx ) hTr_pre ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) end do do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , kk , tr_c , tr_ip , tr_im , tr_jp , tr_jm , h_col , h_self , & flux_x_right , flux_x_left , flux_y_top , flux_y_bot ) h_col = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_col < ML_MIN_DEPTH ) cycle do k = 1 , nz h_self = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_self < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) cycle tr_c = hTr_pre ( i , j , k ) / h_self ! Per-face flux: h_face = 0.5*(h_self + h_nbr) is symmetric, ! face flux = h_face*kappa*(tr_nbr - tr_self)/dx.  Dry ! neighbours close the face (zero-flux wall). if ( h_layer ( i + 1 , j , k ) > THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) then tr_ip = hTr_pre ( i + 1 , j , k ) / h_layer ( i + 1 , j , k ) flux_x_right = 0.5_wp * ( h_self + h_layer ( i + 1 , j , k )) & * kappa_eff * ( tr_ip - tr_c ) * inv_dx else flux_x_right = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) > THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) then tr_im = hTr_pre ( i - 1 , j , k ) / h_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) flux_x_left = 0.5_wp * ( h_layer ( i - 1 , j , k ) + h_self ) & * kappa_eff * ( tr_c - tr_im ) * inv_dx else flux_x_left = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_layer ( i , j + 1 , k ) > THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) then tr_jp = hTr_pre ( i , j + 1 , k ) / h_layer ( i , j + 1 , k ) flux_y_top = 0.5_wp * ( h_self + h_layer ( i , j + 1 , k )) & * kappa_eff * ( tr_jp - tr_c ) * inv_dy else flux_y_top = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) > THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) then tr_jm = hTr_pre ( i , j - 1 , k ) / h_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) flux_y_bot = 0.5_wp * ( h_layer ( i , j - 1 , k ) + h_self ) & * kappa_eff * ( tr_c - tr_jm ) * inv_dy else flux_y_bot = 0.0_wp end if hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) & + dt * (( flux_x_right - flux_x_left ) * inv_dx & + ( flux_y_top - flux_y_bot ) * inv_dy ) end do end do end associate end subroutine ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer.html"},{"title":"ml_init_tracer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_init_tracer(h_layer, hTr_layer, tr_init, grid, nz) Initialise hTr = h_k * tr_init for all layers Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_init type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz Called by proc~~ml_init_tracer~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_init_tracer ml_init_tracer proc~ml_seed_tracer ml_seed_tracer proc~ml_seed_tracer->proc~ml_init_tracer proc~multilayer_seed_tracers multilayer_state_t%multilayer_seed_tracers proc~multilayer_seed_tracers->proc~ml_seed_tracer proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->proc~multilayer_seed_tracers proc~api_init_multilayer api_init_multilayer proc~api_init_multilayer->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_from_config init_from_config proc~init_from_config->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~rki_finalize rki_finalize proc~rki_finalize->proc~api_init_multilayer proc~rki_finalize->proc~init_from_config Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface t