s Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure subroutine ml_seed_tracer ( h_layer , hTr_layer , tr_uniform , & tr_bottom , tr_surface , grid , nz ) !! Seed one tracer's `hTr` field, dispatching between the uniform and !! the linear-stratified profile from the tracer's IC scalars.  When !! both `tr_bottom` and `tr_surface` are set (non-zero) and nz > 1 a !! linear profile is laid down from `tr_bottom` at the bed (k=1) to !! `tr_surface` at the surface (k=nz); otherwise every layer is filled !! with `tr_uniform`.  This is the single stratified-vs-uniform gate !! shared by all IC seed sites (rki_init, rki_api), so the polarity !! convention lives in exactly one place.  Mirrors `ml_seed_tracer_unstr`. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tr_uniform , tr_bottom , tr_surface if ( tr_bottom /= 0.0_wp . and . tr_surface /= 0.0_wp . and . nz > 1 ) then call ml_init_tracer_stratified ( h_layer , hTr_layer , tr_bottom , & tr_surface , grid , nz ) else call ml_init_tracer ( h_layer , hTr_layer , tr_uniform , grid , nz ) end if end subroutine ml_seed_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_seed_tracer.html"},{"title":"ml_settling_tracer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_settling_tracer(h_layer, hTr_layer, bed, w_s, grid, nz, dt) Constant-velocity downward settling of one tracer (e.g. suspended\nsediment), conservative + positivity-preserving.  Bottom-up\nconvention: k=1 is the bed layer, k=nz the surface.  The whole\nsuspended profile sinks at w_s ; whatever crosses the bed deposits\ninto the 2D bed reservoir, so total sum_k hTr + bed is conserved. Implemented as a conservative PPM remap (Colella & Woodward 1984) on\nan augmented column.  Settling by s = w_s*dt is a downward\nadvection of the concentration profile by s ; expressed as a remap,\nthe new content of fixed layer k is the old reconstruction integrated\nover [z_{k-1}+s, z_k+s].  To keep that a same-total (hence exactly\nconservative) remap we add two cells: a clean cap (conc 0, thickness s ) above the surface to supply the zero-inflow surface BC, and a\ndeposition slab (thickness s ) below the bed to catch settled-out\nmass. remap_column_ppm then does the parabolic reconstruction +\nColella-Woodward limiting; target cell 1 is the deposition, target\ncell k+1 is the new layer k. Unlike the old donor-cell flux this is 2nd-order (less numerical\ndiffusion) and has no one-layer-per-step limit: s may span several\nlayers (or the whole column) in a single call and still conserve and\nstay non-negative.  nz=1 reduces to the same linear sink as before;\ndry / vanishing layers (zero thickness) carry zero mass. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: bed (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: w_s type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_settling_tracer~~CallsGraph proc~ml_settling_tracer ml_settling_tracer local local proc~ml_settling_tracer->local proc~remap_column_ppm remap_column_ppm proc~ml_settling_tracer->proc~remap_column_ppm proc~remap_column_plm remap_column_plm proc~remap_column_ppm->proc~remap_column_plm Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_settling_tracer~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_settling_tracer ml_settling_tracer proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~ml_settling_tracer proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: c_src (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: c_tgt (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: dz_src (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: dz_tgt (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: h_col integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: mass_new real(kind=wp), private :: mass_old integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: settle Source Code pure subroutine ml_settling_tracer ( h_layer , hTr_layer , bed , w_s , grid , nz , dt ) !! Constant-velocity downward settling of one tracer (e.g. suspended !! sediment), conservative + positivity-preserving.  Bottom-up !! convention: k=1 is the bed layer, k=nz the surface.  The whole !! suspended profile sinks at `w_s`; whatever crosses the bed deposits !! into the 2D `bed` reservoir, so total `sum_k hTr + bed` is conserved. !! !! Implemented as a conservative PPM remap (Colella & Woodward 1984) on !! an *augmented* column.  Settling by `s = w_s*dt` is a downward !! advection of the concentration profile by `s`; expressed as a remap, !! the new content of fixed layer k is the old reconstruction integrated !! over [z_{k-1}+s, z_k+s].  To keep that a same-total (hence exactly !! conservative) remap we add two cells: a clean cap (conc 0, thickness !! `s`) above the surface to supply the zero-inflow surface BC, and a !! deposition slab (thickness `s`) below the bed to catch settled-out !! mass.  `remap_column_ppm` then does the parabolic reconstruction + !! Colella-Woodward limiting; target cell 1 is the deposition, target !! cell k+1 is the new layer k. !! !! Unlike the old donor-cell flux this is 2nd-order (less numerical !! diffusion) and has no one-layer-per-step limit: `s` may span several !! layers (or the whole column) in a single call and still conserve and !! stay non-negative.  nz=1 reduces to the same linear sink as before; !! dry / vanishing layers (zero thickness) carry zero mass. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: bed ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: w_s , dt integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: settle , h_col , mass_old , mass_new real ( wp ) :: dz_src ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), dz_tgt ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: c_src ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), c_tgt ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) if ( w_s <= 0.0_wp ) return nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost settle = w_s * dt do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , h_col , mass_old , mass_new , dz_src , dz_tgt , c_src , c_tgt ) ! Skip dry columns — nothing to settle. h_col = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do if ( h_col > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Source: real layers (bed..surface) then a clean cap of ! thickness `settle` (concentration 0). mass_old = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz dz_src ( k ) = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) > 0.0_wp ) then c_src ( k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_layer ( i , j , k ) else c_src ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if mass_old = mass_old + hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) end do dz_src ( nz + 1 ) = settle c_src ( nz + 1 ) = 0.0_wp ! Target: deposition slab (thickness `settle`) at the bed, then the ! real layer thicknesses shifted up one index.  Same total height ! as the source, so remapping onto it advects the profile down by ! `settle` exactly conservatively. dz_tgt ( 1 ) = settle do k = 1 , nz dz_tgt ( k + 1 ) = h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do call remap_column_ppm ( nz + 1 , dz_src , dz_tgt , c_src , c_tgt ) ! Target cell k+1 is the new content of real layer k; target ! cell 1 is the deposition.  Bank the column-mass deficit into the ! bed so total (suspended + bed) is conserved to round-off. mass_new = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = c_tgt ( k + 1 ) * h_layer ( i , j , k ) mass_new = mass_new + hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) end do bed ( i , j ) = bed ( i , j ) + ( mass_old - mass_new ) end if end do end subroutine ml_settling_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_settling_tracer.html"},{"title":"ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, hTr_layer, rho_layer, rho_0, nu_max, kappa_bg, ri_alpha, grid, nz, dt) Ri-dependent vertical diffusion of a scalar tracer (Pacanowski-Philander 1981).\nUses stronger Ri suppression for tracers: kappa_t = nu_max / (1 + alpha*Ri)&#94;3 + kappa_bg. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 Reference density (kg/m&#94;3) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: nu_max Maximum turbulent viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_bg Background tracer diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: ri_alpha Richardson number scaling coefficient type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer~~CallsGraph proc~ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer local local proc~ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: EPS = 1.0e-20_wp real(kind=wp), private :: Ri real(kind=wp), private :: denom real(kind=wp), private :: drho real(kind=wp), private :: dtr real(kind=wp), private :: du real(kind=wp), private :: dv real(kind=wp), private :: flux_tr real(kind=wp), private :: h_avg real(kind=wp), private :: h_col real(kind=wp), private :: h_k real(kind=wp), private :: h_k1 integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: kappa_t integer, private :: kk integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: tr_k real(kind=wp), private :: tr_k1 real(kind=wp), private :: u_k real(kind=wp), private :: u_k1 real(kind=wp), private :: v_k real(kind=wp), private :: v_k1 Source Code pure subroutine ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & hTr_layer , rho_layer , & rho_0 , nu_max , kappa_bg , ri_alpha , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Ri-dependent vertical diffusion of a scalar tracer (Pacanowski-Philander 1981). !! Uses stronger Ri suppression for tracers: kappa_t = nu_max / (1 + alpha*Ri)&#94;3 + kappa_bg. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho_0 !! Reference density (kg/m&#94;3) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: nu_max !! Maximum turbulent viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: kappa_bg !! Background tracer diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ri_alpha !! Richardson number scaling coefficient real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: i , j , k , kk , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: h_avg , h_k , h_k1 , u_k , v_k , u_k1 , v_k1 , tr_k , tr_k1 , h_col real ( wp ) :: du , dv , dtr , drho , Ri , denom , kappa_t , flux_tr real ( wp ), parameter :: EPS = 1.0e-20_wp nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost if ( nz < 2 ) return do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , kk , h_k , h_k1 , h_avg , u_k , v_k , u_k1 , v_k1 , tr_k , tr_k1 , & du , dv , dtr , drho , Ri , denom , kappa_t , flux_tr , h_col ) h_col = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then do k = 1 , nz - 1 h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k ) h_k1 = h_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) h_avg = 0.5_wp * ( h_k + h_k1 ) ! VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL: vanishing layers on either side make ! kappa_t*dtr/h_avg pathological.  No-flux through such ! interfaces. if ( h_avg > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . & h_k > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL . and . & h_k1 > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_k = hu_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k v_k = hv_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k tr_k = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k else u_k = 0.0_wp v_k = 0.0_wp tr_k = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_k1 > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_k1 = hu_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) / h_k1 v_k1 = hv_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) / h_k1 tr_k1 = hTr_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) / h_k1 else u_k1 = 0.0_wp v_k1 = 0.0_wp tr_k1 = 0.0_wp end if du = u_k1 - u_k dv = v_k1 - v_k drho = rho_layer ( i , j , k ) - rho_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) Ri = GRAVITY * ( drho / rho_0 ) * h_avg / ( du * du + dv * dv + EPS ) if ( Ri < 0.0_wp ) Ri = 0.0_wp denom = 1.0_wp + ri_alpha * Ri kappa_t = nu_max / ( denom * denom * denom ) + kappa_bg ! Limit diffusive flux: stability requires kappa_t*dt/h_avg&#94;2 < 0.5 if ( kappa_t * dt > 0.5_wp * h_avg * h_avg ) then kappa_t = 0.5_wp * h_avg * h_avg / dt end if dtr = tr_k1 - tr_k flux_tr = kappa_t * dtr / h_avg * dt ! Conservative + dimensionally correct: hTr has units [tr]*m, ! flux_tr = kappa*dtr/h_avg*dt has units [tr]*m. Same quantity ! moves across the interface so both layers see the same mass ! change (previously multiplied each side by its own h, which ! leaks mass under non-uniform layers, e.g. VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL). hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) + flux_tr hTr_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) - flux_tr end if end do end if end do end subroutine ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer.html"},{"title":"ml_vertical_exchange_tracer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_vertical_exchange_tracer(h_layer, hTr_layer, w, grid, nz, dt) Vertical tracer exchange using upwind advection at interfaces. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: w (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz+1) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer~~CallsGraph proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer ml_vertical_exchange_tracer local local proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer ml_vertical_exchange_tracer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: flux_tr real(kind=wp), private :: h_col real(kind=wp), private :: h_val integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: kk integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: tr_up real(kind=wp), private :: w_face Source Code pure subroutine ml_vertical_exchange_tracer ( h_layer , hTr_layer , w , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Vertical tracer exchange using upwind advection at interfaces. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: w ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz + 1 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: i , j , k , kk , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: w_face , tr_up , flux_tr , h_val , h_col nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost if ( nz < 2 ) return do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , kk , w_face , tr_up , flux_tr , h_val , h_col ) h_col = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then do k = 1 , nz - 1 w_face = w ( i , j , k + 1 ) if ( w_face > 0.0_wp ) then h_val = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_val > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_up = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_val else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if else h_val = h_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) if ( h_val > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_up = hTr_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) / h_val else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if end if flux_tr = w_face * tr_up * dt ! Limit: don't extract more than 50% of donor layer tracer if ( w_face > 0.0_wp ) then if ( abs ( flux_tr ) > 0.5_wp * abs ( hTr_layer ( i , j , k ))) then flux_tr = sign ( 0.5_wp * abs ( hTr_layer ( i , j , k )), flux_tr ) end if else if ( abs ( flux_tr ) > 0.5_wp * abs ( hTr_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ))) then flux_tr = sign ( 0.5_wp * abs ( hTr_layer ( i , j , k + 1 )), flux_tr ) end if end if hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k ) - flux_tr hTr_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) = hTr_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) + flux_tr end do end if end do end subroutine ml_vertical_exchange_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_vertical_exchange_tracer.html"},{"title":"tracer_scratch_destroy – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine tracer_scratch_destroy(scratch) Detach and deallocate every allocated scratch group.  Called by\nthe solver at simulation end (mirror of tracer_scratch_ensure ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( tracer_scratch_t ), intent(inout) :: scratch Calls proc~~tracer_scratch_destroy~~CallsGraph proc~tracer_scratch_destroy tracer_scratch_destroy proc~scratch_array_destroy scratch_array_destroy proc~tracer_scratch_destroy->proc~scratch_array_destroy Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Pro