:"public  subroutine tracer_scratch_ensure(scratch, nx, ny, nz, want_ppm, want_upwind, want_hdiff, want_weno) Allocate (or resize) the caller-owned tracer-kernel scratch and\nattach it to the GPU.  Idempotent: a no-op once each requested\ngroup exists at the requested size; resizes if (nx,ny,nz) changes\n(e.g. a unit test re-running at a different grid size).  Each\ngroup is guarded so only the kernels actually in use allocate\n(PPM-only run skips the upwind snapshot and vice-versa). Call once up front (solver_enter_data), never per step — the\nkernels themselves are pure and must not allocate. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( tracer_scratch_t ), intent(inout) :: scratch integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz logical, intent(in) :: want_ppm logical, intent(in) :: want_upwind logical, intent(in) :: want_hdiff logical, intent(in), optional :: want_weno WENO5/7/9 reconstruction snapshot ( tracer_recon /= ppm).\nOptional so pre-WENO callers stay source-compatible. Calls proc~~tracer_scratch_ensure~~CallsGraph proc~tracer_scratch_ensure tracer_scratch_ensure proc~scratch_array_ensure scratch_array_ensure proc~tracer_scratch_ensure->proc~scratch_array_ensure Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~tracer_scratch_ensure~~CalledByGraph proc~tracer_scratch_ensure tracer_scratch_ensure proc~solver_enter_data solver_enter_data proc~solver_enter_data->proc~tracer_scratch_ensure proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_enter_data proc~flush_restart flush_restart proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_restart proc~flush_snapshot flush_snapshot proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_snapshot proc~ensure_device ensure_device proc~ensure_device->proc~solver_enter_data proc~flush_restart->proc~solver_enter_data proc~flush_snapshot->proc~solver_enter_data proc~rki_finalize rki_finalize proc~rki_finalize->proc~solver_enter_data proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~ensure_device proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_finalize proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_finalize proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~ensure_device Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine tracer_scratch_ensure ( scratch , nx , ny , nz , & want_ppm , want_upwind , want_hdiff , want_weno ) !! Allocate (or resize) the caller-owned tracer-kernel scratch and !! attach it to the GPU.  Idempotent: a no-op once each requested !! group exists at the requested size; resizes if (nx,ny,nz) changes !! (e.g. a unit test re-running at a different grid size).  Each !! group is guarded so only the kernels actually in use allocate !! (PPM-only run skips the upwind snapshot and vice-versa). !! !! Call once up front (solver_enter_data), never per step — the !! kernels themselves are `pure` and must not allocate. type ( tracer_scratch_t ), intent ( inout ) :: scratch integer , intent ( in ) :: nx , ny , nz logical , intent ( in ) :: want_ppm , want_upwind , want_hdiff logical , intent ( in ), optional :: want_weno !! WENO5/7/9 reconstruction snapshot (`tracer_recon` /= ppm). !! Optional so pre-WENO callers stay source-compatible. if ( want_upwind ) then call scratch_array_ensure ( scratch % adv_hTr_snap , nx , ny , nz ) end if if ( want_ppm ) then call scratch_array_ensure ( scratch % ppm_tr_snap , nx , ny , nz ) call scratch_array_ensure ( scratch % ppm_ql_x , nx , ny , nz ) call scratch_array_ensure ( scratch % ppm_qr_x , nx , ny , nz ) call scratch_array_ensure ( scratch % ppm_ql_y , nx , ny , nz ) call scratch_array_ensure ( scratch % ppm_qr_y , nx , ny , nz ) end if if ( present ( want_weno )) then if ( want_weno ) then call scratch_array_ensure ( scratch % weno_tr_snap , nx , ny , nz ) end if end if if ( want_hdiff ) then call scratch_array_ensure ( scratch % hdiff_hTr_pre , nx , ny , nz ) end if end subroutine tracer_scratch_ensure","tags":"","url":"proc/tracer_scratch_ensure.html"},{"title":"scratch_array_destroy – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine scratch_array_destroy(arr) Detach + deallocate a single scratch array (no-op if unallocated). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout), allocatable :: arr (:,:,:) Called by proc~~scratch_array_destroy~~CalledByGraph proc~scratch_array_destroy scratch_array_destroy proc~tracer_scratch_destroy tracer_scratch_destroy proc~tracer_scratch_destroy->proc~scratch_array_destroy proc~solver_exit_data solver_exit_data proc~solver_exit_data->proc~tracer_scratch_destroy 