e Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine scratch_array_destroy ( arr ) !! Detach + deallocate a single scratch array (no-op if unallocated). real ( wp ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: arr (:, :, :) if (. not . allocated ( arr )) return !$acc exit data delete(arr) deallocate ( arr ) end subroutine scratch_array_destroy","tags":"","url":"proc/scratch_array_destroy.html"},{"title":"scratch_array_ensure – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine scratch_array_ensure(arr, nx, ny, nz) Allocate arr to (nx,ny,nz) + attach to the device, resizing if\nit already exists at a different shape.  The array is passed as a\nplain dummy so the !$acc directives carry no derived-type\ndereference (the leaf form the OpenMP-portability rule requires). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout), allocatable :: arr (:,:,:) integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz Called by proc~~scratch_array_ensure~~CalledByGraph proc~scratch_array_ensure scratch_array_ensure proc~tracer_scratch_ensure tracer_scratch_ensure proc~tracer_scratch_ensure->proc~scratch_array_ensure proc~solver_enter_data solver_enter_data proc~solver_enter_data->proc~tracer_scratch_ensure proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_enter_data proc~flush_restart flush_restart proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_restart proc~flush_snapshot flush_snapshot proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_snapshot proc~ensure_device ensure_device proc~ensure_device->proc~solver_e