vate, parameter :: CA_D5 = 0.25_wp*(L2**2-3.0_wp*L3**2)*(L6**2-L7**2) real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CA_S0 = 1.5_wp*L1*L5**2 real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CA_S1 = -L4*(L6+L7)+2.0_wp*L4*L5*(L1-L2/3.0_wp-L3)+1.5_wp*L1*L5*L8 real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CA_S2 = -3.0_wp/8.0_wp*L1*(L6**2-L7**2) real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CA_S4 = 2.0_wp*L5 real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CA_S5 = 2.0_wp*L4 real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CA_S6 = 2.0_wp/3.0_wp*L5*(3.0_wp*L3**2-L2**2)-0.5_wp*L5*L1*(3.0_wp*L3-L2)+0.75_wp*L1*(L6-L7) real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: GH_MAX = 0.0233_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: GH_MIN = -0.28_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: L1 = 0.107_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: L2 = 0.0032_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: L3 = 0.0864_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: L4 = 0.12_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: L5 = 11.9_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: L6 = 0.4_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: L7 = 0.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: L8 = 0.48_wp real(kind=wp), private :: alpha_m real(kind=wp), private :: alpha_n real(kind=wp), private :: denom real(kind=wp), private :: eok2 real(kind=wp), private :: gh real(kind=wp), private :: sh real(kind=wp), private :: sm real(kind=wp), private :: tn real(kind=wp), private :: ts Source Code pure subroutine keps_stability_funcs ( scheme , s2 , n2 , k , e , cmu_o , cmup_o ) !$acc routine seq !! Stability functions (c_mu, c_mu') for the chosen scheme, given shear S&#94;2 !! and buoyancy N&#94;2 at the interface. !! Result dummies are cmu_o/cmup_o, NOT cmu/cmup: a `cmu` dummy shadows the !! module parameter CMU (case-insensitive) -> self-assignment of undefined !! intent(out) -> nu_t floored on GPU/gfortran. integer , intent ( in ) :: scheme real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: s2 , n2 , k , e real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: cmu_o , cmup_o ! Galperin (1988) / Mellor-Yamada level-2.5 constants. real ( wp ), parameter :: A1 = 0.92_wp , A2 = 0.74_wp , B1 = 1 6.6_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: B2 = 1 0.1_wp , C1 = 0.08_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: GH_MIN = - 0.28_wp , GH_MAX = 0.0233_wp ! Canuto (2001) Model A structural constants (L*) + derived numerator ! (CA_S*) and denominator (CA_D*) coefficients of the rational form. real ( wp ), parameter :: L1 = 0.107_wp , L2 = 0.0032_wp , L3 = 0.0864_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: L4 = 0.12_wp , L5 = 1 1.9_wp , L6 = 0.4_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: L7 = 0.0_wp , L8 = 0.48_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_S0 = 1.5_wp * L1 * L5 ** 2 real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_S1 = - L4 * ( L6 + L7 ) + 2.0_wp * L4 * L5 * ( L1 - L2 / 3.0_wp - L3 ) & + 1.5_wp * L1 * L5 * L8 real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_S2 = - 3.0_wp / 8.0_wp * L1 * ( L6 ** 2 - L7 ** 2 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_S4 = 2.0_wp * L5 real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_S5 = 2.0_wp * L4 real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_S6 = 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp * L5 * ( 3.0_wp * L3 ** 2 - L2 ** 2 ) & - 0.5_wp * L5 * L1 * ( 3.0_wp * L3 - L2 ) + 0.75_wp * L1 * ( L6 - L7 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_D0 = 3.0_wp * L5 ** 2 real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_D1 = L5 * ( 7.0_wp * L4 + 3.0_wp * L8 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_D2 = L5 ** 2 * ( 3.0_wp * L3 ** 2 - L2 ** 2 ) - 0.75_wp * ( L6 ** 2 - L7 ** 2 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_D3 = L4 * ( 4.0_wp * L4 + 3.0_wp * L8 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_D4 = L4 * ( L2 * L6 - 3.0_wp * L3 * L7 - L5 * ( L2 ** 2 - L3 ** 2 )) & + L5 * L8 * ( 3.0_wp * L3 ** 2 - L2 ** 2 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: CA_D5 = 0.25_wp * ( L2 ** 2 - 3.0_wp * L3 ** 2 ) * ( L6 ** 2 - L7 ** 2 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: AN_MIN = - 1.5_wp , AN_MAX = 1 9.0_wp , AM_MAX = 20 0.0_wp real ( wp ) :: alpha_n , gh , sh , sm , alpha_m , tn , ts , denom , eok2 select case ( scheme ) case ( KEPS_STAB_GALPERIN ) alpha_n = ( k / max ( e , EPS_MIN )) ** 2 * n2 gh = min ( max ( - ( 4.0_wp / ( B1 * B1 )) * alpha_n , GH_MIN ), GH_MAX ) sh = A2 * ( 1.0_wp - 6.0_wp * A1 / B1 ) & / ( 1.0_wp - ( 1 8.0_wp * A1 * A2 + 3.0_wp * A2 * B2 ) * gh ) sm = ( A1 * ( 1.0_wp - 3.0_wp * C1 - 6.0_wp * A1 / B1 ) & + sh * ( 1 8.0_wp * A1 * A1 + 9.0_wp * A1 * A2 ) * gh ) & / ( 1.0_wp - 9.0_wp * A1 * A2 * gh ) cmu_o = 4.0_wp * sm / B1 cmup_o = 4.0_wp * sh / B1 case ( KEPS_STAB_CANUTO ) eok2 = ( k / max ( e , EPS_MIN )) ** 2 alpha_n = min ( max ( eok2 * n2 , AN_MIN ), AN_MAX ) alpha_m = min ( max ( eok2 * s2 , 0.0_wp ), AM_MAX ) tn = 4.0_wp * alpha_n ts = 4.0_wp * alpha_m denom = CA_D0 + CA_D1 * tn + CA_D2 * ts + CA_D3 * tn * tn + CA_D4 * tn * ts + CA_D5 * ts * ts cmu_o = 2.0_wp * ( CA_S0 + CA_S1 * tn + CA_S2 * ts ) / denom cmup_o = 2.0_wp * ( CA_S4 + CA_S5 * tn + CA_S6 * ts ) / denom case default cmu_o = CMU cmup_o = CMU / PR_T end select end subroutine keps_stability_funcs","tags":"","url":"proc/keps_stability_funcs.html"},{"title":"bpg_nz_is_sufficient – Rakali","text":"public pure function bpg_nz_is_sufficient(nz) result(ok) .true. when the COMPILED BPG_NZ_MAX covers nz layers on\nthe unstructured multilayer path.  Callers that get .false. must refuse the run: exceeding the bound is NOT a crash — the\nunstructured BPG kernels silently return (no baroclinic\npressure gradient at all) and the unguarded column kernels\nsilently overrun thread-local storage. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Return Value logical Calls proc~~bpg_nz_is_sufficient~~CallsGraph proc~bpg_nz_is_sufficient bpg_nz_is_sufficient proc~bpg_nz_required bpg_nz_required proc~bpg_nz_is_sufficient->proc~bpg_nz_required Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~bpg_nz_is_sufficient~~CalledByGraph proc~bpg_nz_is_sufficient bpg_nz_is_sufficient proc~validate_config validate_config proc~validate_config->proc~bpg_nz_is_sufficient proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function bpg_nz_is_sufficient ( nz ) result ( ok ) !! `.true.` when the COMPILED `BPG_NZ_MAX` covers `nz` layers on !! the unstructured multilayer path.  Callers that get `.false.` !! must refuse the run: exceeding the bound is NOT a crash — the !! unstructured BPG kernels silently return (no baroclinic !! pressure gradient at all) and the unguarded column kernels !! silently overrun thread-local storage. integer , intent ( in ) :: nz logical :: ok ok = bpg_nz_required ( nz ) <= BPG_NZ_MAX end function bpg_nz_is_sufficient","tags":"","url":"proc/bpg_nz_is_sufficient.html"},{"title":"bpg_nz_required – Rakali","text":"public pure function bpg_nz_required(nz) result(req) Smallest BPG_NZ_MAX that safely covers an unstructured\nmultilayer run of nz layers. nz + 1 .  Derived from a survey (2026-08) of every BPG_NZ_MAX -dimensioned local in the unstructured kernels; the\nbinding consumer is the one that indexes a plainly- BPG_NZ_MAX array to nz + 1 rather than the BPG_NZ_MAX + 1 an interface\narray would use: rki_ml_keps_unstr ml_keps_update_unstr_impl S2 / N2 / dz_if / a / b / c / rhs / cp — written and read\n    at ni = nz + 1 (interface-indexed; keps_tridiag_solve_u touches rows 1..ni of all five solver arrays). Every other consumer needs only nz : rki_ml_pressure_unstr p_int / p_int_nbr — max index nz (the interface arrays z_if / p_if / zn_if_e / pn_if_e are\n    declared BPG_NZ_MAX + 1 and carry their own slack). rki_ml_tracers_unstr v_layer / hf_layer / frac — max nz ; flux_iface — max nz - 1 . rki_ml_dynamics_unstr , rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr , rki_ml_kpp_unstr flux_*_iface — max nz - 1 . rki_ml_keps_unstr momentum/tracer applies a / b / c / ru / rv / r / cp — max nz . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Return Value integer Called by proc~~bpg_nz_required~~CalledByGraph proc~bpg_nz_required bpg_nz_required proc~bpg_nz_is_sufficient bpg_nz_is_sufficient proc~bpg_nz_is_sufficient->proc~bpg_nz_required proc~validate_config validate_config proc~validate_config->proc~bpg_nz_required proc~validate_config->proc~bpg_nz_is_sufficient proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function bpg_nz_required ( nz ) result ( req ) !! Smallest `BPG_NZ_MAX` that safely covers an unstructured !! multilayer run of `nz` layers. !! !! `nz + 1`.  Derived from a survey (2026-08) of every !! `BPG_NZ_MAX`-dimensioned local in the unstructured kernels; the !! binding consumer is the one that indexes a plainly-`BPG_NZ_MAX` !! array to `nz + 1` rather than the `BPG_NZ_MAX + 1` an interface !! array would use: !! !!   * `rki_ml_keps_unstr` `ml_keps_update_unstr_impl` !!     `S2`/`N2`/`dz_if`/`a`/`b`/`c`/`rhs`/`cp` — written and read !!     at `ni = nz + 1` (interface-indexed; `keps_tridiag_solve_u` !!     touches rows `1..ni` of all five solver arrays). !! !! Every other consumer needs only `nz`: !! !!   * `rki_ml_pressure_unstr` `p_int`/`p_int_nbr` — max index `nz` !!     (the interface arrays `z_if`/`p_if`/`zn_if_e`/`pn_if_e` are !!     declared `BPG_NZ_MAX + 1` and carry their own slack). !!   * `rki_ml_tracers_unstr` `v_layer`/`hf_layer`/`frac` — max !!     `nz`; `flux_iface` — max `nz - 1`. !!   * `rki_ml_dynamics_unstr`, `rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr`, !!     `rki_ml_kpp_unstr` `flux_*_iface` — max `nz - 1`. !!   * `rki_ml_keps_unstr` momentum/tracer applies !!     `a`/`b`/`c`/`ru`/`rv`/`r`/`cp` — max `nz`. integer , intent ( in ) :: nz integer :: req req = nz + 1 end function bpg_nz_required","tags":"","url":"proc/bp