agorinsky_cs.html"},{"title":"rki_unstr_set_time_scheme – Rakali","text":"private  function rki_unstr_set_time_scheme(c_handle, c_name, c_len) result(ierr) bind(c, name=\"rki_unstr_set_time_scheme\") Select the explicit time integrator on the unstructured 2D\nbarotropic path. c_name is one of “euler”/”rk2”/”rk3”/”rk43”\n(unrecognised falls back to “rk2”).  Returns:\n  0  on success,\n -1  if the handle is not initialised,\n -2  if a non-rk2 scheme is requested on a multilayer handle\n     (multilayer keeps SSP-RK2; the state field is left unchanged). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: c_handle type(c_ptr), value :: c_name integer(kind=c_int), value :: c_len Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Calls proc~~rki_unstr_set_time_scheme~~CallsGraph proc~rki_unstr_set_time_scheme rki_unstr_set_time_scheme proc~parse_time_scheme parse_time_scheme proc~rki_unstr_set_time_scheme->proc~parse_time_scheme proc~resolve resolve proc~rki_unstr_set_time_scheme->proc~resolve proc~handle_check_unstr handle_check_unstr proc~resolve->proc~handle_check_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=1), private, pointer :: cstr (:) type( solver_handle_unstr_t ), private, pointer :: h integer, private :: i character(len=:), private, allocatable :: name integer, private :: scheme Source Code function rki_unstr_set_time_scheme ( c_handle , c_name , c_len ) result ( ierr ) & bind ( c , name = \"rki_unstr_set_time_scheme\" ) !! Select the explicit time integrator on the unstructured 2D !! barotropic path.  `c_name` is one of \"euler\"/\"rk2\"/\"rk3\"/\"rk43\" !! (unrecognised falls back to \"rk2\").  Returns: !!   0  on success, !!  -1  if the handle is not initialised, !!  -2  if a non-rk2 scheme is requested on a multilayer handle !!      (multilayer keeps SSP-RK2; the state field is left unchanged). type ( c_ptr ), value :: c_handle type ( c_ptr ), value :: c_name integer ( c_int ), value :: c_len integer ( c_int ) :: ierr type ( solver_handle_unstr_t ), pointer :: h character ( len = :), allocatable :: name character , pointer :: cstr (:) integer :: i , scheme ierr = resolve ( c_handle , h ) if ( ierr /= 0 ) return if (. not . h % is_initialised ) then ierr = - 1 return end if call c_f_pointer ( c_name , cstr , [ c_len ]) allocate ( character ( len = c_len ) :: name ) do i = 1 , c_len name ( i : i ) = cstr ( i ) end do scheme = parse_time_scheme ( name ) if ( scheme /= TIME_RK2 . and . h % state % use_multilayer ) then ierr = - 2 return end if h % state % time_scheme = scheme ierr = 0 end function rki_unstr_set_time_scheme","tags":"","url":"proc/rki_unstr_set_time_scheme.html"},{"title":"rki_unstr_set_use_ppm_tracer – Rakali","text":"private  function rki_unstr_set_use_ppm_tracer(c_handle, flag) result(ierr) bind(c, name=\"rki_unstr_set_use_ppm_tracer\") Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: c_handle integer(kind=c_int), value :: flag Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Calls proc~~rki_unstr_set_use_ppm_tracer~~CallsGraph proc~rki_unstr_set_use_ppm_tracer rki_unstr_set_use_ppm_tracer proc~resolve resolve proc~rki_unstr_set_use_ppm_tracer->proc~resolve proc~handle_check_unstr handle_check_unstr proc~resolve->proc~handle_check_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Gra