rotropic momentum in the fused update\nkernel on top of any spatially-uniform stress from rki_unstr_set_wind .  Same sizing convention as rki_unstr_set_heat_flux (length == state%ncells_owned).\nMarks the per-cell wind active so the\nkernel applies it; the caller converts wind speed to stress. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: c_handle type(c_ptr), value :: c_wx type(c_ptr), value :: c_wy Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Calls proc~~rki_unstr_set_wind_field~~CallsGraph proc~rki_unstr_set_wind_field rki_unstr_set_wind_field proc~resolve resolve proc~rki_unstr_set_wind_field->proc~resolve proc~solver_unstr_update_forcing solver_unstr_update_forcing proc~rki_unstr_set_wind_field->proc~solver_unstr_update_forcing proc~handle_check_unstr handle_check_unstr proc~resolve->proc~handle_check_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( solver_handle_unstr_t ), private, pointer :: h integer, private :: k real(kind=c_double), private, pointer :: wx (:) real(kind=c_double), private, pointer :: wy (:) Source Code function rki_unstr_set_wind_field ( c_handle , c_wx , c_wy ) result ( ierr ) & bind ( c , name = \"rki_unstr_set_wind_field\" ) !! Set per-cell surface wind STRESS (Pa), x and y components, on every !! owned cell.  Added to the barotropic momentum in the fused update !! kernel on top of any spatially-uniform stress from !! `rki_unstr_set_wind`.  Same sizing convention as !! `rki_unstr_set_heat_flux` (length == state%ncells_owned). !! Marks the per-cell wind active so the !! kernel applies it; the caller converts wind speed to stress. type ( c_ptr ), value :: c_handle type ( c_ptr ), value :: c_wx , c_wy integer ( c_int ) :: ierr type ( solver_handle_unstr_t ), pointer :: h real ( c_double ), pointer :: wx (:), wy (:) integer :: k ierr = resolve ( c_handle , h ) if ( ierr /= 0 ) return if (. not . h % is_initialised . or . h % is_finalised ) then ierr = - 1 return end if call c_f_pointer ( c_wx , wx , [ h % state % ncells_owned ]) call c_f_pointer ( c_wy , wy , [ h % state % ncells_owned ]) do k = 1 , h % state % ncells_owned h % state % forcing % wind_x ( k ) = real ( wx ( k ), wp ) h % state % forcing % wind_y ( k ) = real ( wy ( k ), wp ) end do h % state % forcing % wind_active = . true . if ( h % on_device ) call solver_unstr_update_forcing ( h % state ) ierr = 0 end function rki_unstr_set_wind_field","tags":"","url":"proc/rki_unstr_set_wind_field.html"},{"title":"rki_unstr_set_zstar_full_params – Rakali","text":"private  function rki_unstr_set_zstar_full_params(c_handle, h_surf_target, h_min, n_surf, stretching) result(ierr) bind(c, name=\"rki_unstr_set_zstar_full_params\") Set VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL parameters: surface-layer target thickness\n(m), vanishing-layer floor (m), number of fine surface layers\n(0 = auto), and stretching mode (0=uniform, 1=log). Must be called after rki_unstr_set_vcoord(..., 'zstar_full') and before rki_unstr_finalize . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: c_handle real(kind=c_double), value :: h_surf_target real(kind=c_double), value :: h_min integer(kind=c_int), value :: n_surf integer(kind=c_int), value :: stretching Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Calls proc~~rki_unstr_set_zstar_full_params~~CallsGraph proc~rki_unstr_set_zstar_full_params rki_un