n ), value :: c_handle integer ( c_int ), intent ( in ), value :: n_steps integer ( c_int ) :: ierr type ( solver_handle_t ), pointer :: h integer :: i ierr = resolve ( c_handle , h ) if ( ierr /= 0 ) return if (. not . h % is_finalised ) then ierr = - 1 return end if call ensure_device ( h ) h % host_is_current = . false . do i = 1 , n_steps call solver_step ( h % state , & dt_max = ( h % cfg % t_end - h % t_current ), & time = h % t_current ) h % t_current = h % t_current + h % state % dt end do ierr = 0 end function rki_step","tags":"","url":"proc/rki_step.html"},{"title":"rki_working_precision – Rakali","text":"private  function rki_working_precision() result(nbytes) bind(c, name=\"rki_working_precision\") Working-precision width in bytes (8 = double, 4 = single) for the\nsolver real kind wp .  Process-global (compile-time), handle-less:\nlets the Python/ctypes layer pick the numpy dtype matching the\nzero-copy field views, which are c_loc of real(wp) arrays.\nShared by the structured and unstructured Python paths (one\nsymbol in librakali, since wp is identical for both). Arguments None Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Source Code function rki_working_precision () result ( nbytes ) & bind ( c , name = \"rki_working_precision\" ) !! Working-precision width in bytes (8 = double, 4 = single) for the !! solver real kind `wp`.  Process-global (compile-time), handle-less: !! lets the Python/ctypes layer pick the numpy dtype matching the !! zero-copy field views, which are `c_loc` of `real(wp)` arrays. !! Shared by the structured and unstructured Python paths (one !! symbol in librakali, since `wp` is identical for both). integer ( c_int ) :: nbytes nbytes = int ( storage_size ( 1.0_wp ) / 8 , c_int ) end function rki_working_precision","tags":"","url":"proc/rki_working_precision.html"},{"title":"api_init_multilayer – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine api_init_multilayer(h) Initialise multilayer arrays from the barotropic state. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attrib