ks (no full exit/enter round-trip). type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state !! Solution state to sync integer :: it !$acc update self(state%barotropic%h, state%barotropic%hu, state%barotropic%hv) ! Coupled hydrostatic multi-layer arrays if ( state % use_multilayer ) then !$acc update self(state%multilayer%h_layer, state%multilayer%hu_layer, state%multilayer%hv_layer, & !$acc&                   state%multilayer%w_ml, state%multilayer%rho_layer) ! Generic tracer registry: pull each element's hTr back if ( allocated ( state % multilayer % tracers )) then do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) !$acc update self(state%multilayer%tracers(it)%hTr) end do end if ! Bed sediment reservoir (2D), present only with sediment on. if ( allocated ( state % multilayer % bed_sediment )) then !$acc update self(state%multilayer%bed_sediment) end if end if ! Non-hydrostatic arrays if ( state % use_nonhydrostatic ) then !$acc update self(state%nh%u_layer, state%nh%v_layer, state%nh%w, state%nh%q_nh) end if end subroutine solver_update_host","tags":"","url":"proc/solver_update_host.html"},{"title":"solver_update_state – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine solver_update_state(state) Copy solution fields host->GPU (in-place !$acc update device ).\nMirror of solver_update_host (pushes the same arrays it pulls);\ncalled after Python/C injects new state mid-simulation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Solution state whose solution arrays to push to device Called by proc~~solver_update_state~~CalledByGraph proc~solver_update_state solver_update_state proc~push_state_to_device push_state_to_device proc~push_state_to_device->proc~solver_update_state proc~rki_set_h rki_set_h proc~rki_set_h->proc~push_state_to_device proc~rki_set_hu rki_set_hu proc~rki_set_hu->proc~push_state_to_device proc~rki_set_hv rki_set_hv proc~rki_set_hv->proc~push_state_to_device proc~rki_set_salinity rki_set_salinity proc~rki_set_salinity->proc~push_state_to_device proc~rki_set_temperature rki_set_temperature proc~rki_set_temperature->proc~push_state_to_device Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: it Source Code subroutine solver_update_state ( state ) !! Copy solution fields host->GPU (in-place `!$acc update device`). !! Mirror of solver_update_host (pushes the same arrays it pulls); !! called after Python/C injects new state mid-simulation. type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state !! Solution state whose solution arrays to push to device integer :: it !$acc update device(state%barotropic%h, state%barotropic%hu, state%barotropic%hv) ! Coupled hydrostatic multi-layer arrays if ( state % use_multilayer ) then !$acc update device(state%multilayer%h_layer, state%multilayer%hu_layer, state%multilayer%hv_layer, & !$acc&                 state%multilayer%w_ml, state%multilayer%rho_layer) ! Generic tracer registry: push each element's hTr to device if ( allocated ( state % multilayer % tracers )) then do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) !$acc update device(state%multilayer%tracers(it)%hTr) end do end if end if ! Non-hydrostatic arrays if ( state % use_nonhydrostatic ) then !$acc update device(state%nh%u_layer, state%nh%v_layer, state%nh%w, state%nh%q_nh) end if end subroutine solver_update_state","tags":"","url":"proc/solver_update_state.html"},{"title":"accumulate_sponge_mass_src – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine accumulate_sponge_mass_src(state, stage_weight) Accumulate the net volume change caused by the sponge h-relaxation\nthis RK stage into state%barotropic%mass_src .  The sponge applies Δh = −dt·α·(h − h_ref) , which can add or remove mass; this routine\nmeasures the actual h-change by summing h over interior cells before\nand after apply_sponge .  No-op when no sponge edge is configured. Must be called IN PLACE OF a bare apply_sponge call — it calls apply_sponge internally. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: stage_weight Stage contribution (0.5 per SSP-RK2 stage). Calls proc~~accumulate_sponge_mass_src~~CallsGraph proc~accumulate_sponge_mass_src accumulate_sponge_mass_src proc~apply_sponge apply_sponge proc~accumulate_sponge_mass_src->proc~apply_sponge reduce reduce proc~accumulate_sponge_mass_src->reduce local local proc~apply_sponge->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~accumulate_sponge_mass_src~~CalledByGraph proc~accumulate_sponge_mass_src accumulate_sponge_mass_src proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~accumulate_sponge_mass_src proc~solver_step_impl solver_step_impl proc~solver_step_impl->proc~accumulate_sponge_mass_src proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: area real(kind=wp), private :: h_after real(kind=wp), private :: h_before integer, private :: i integer, private :: i_hi integer, private :: i_lo integer, private :: j integer, private :: j_hi integer, private :: j_lo integer, private :: ng Source Code subroutine accumulate_sponge_mass_src ( state , stage_weight ) !! Accumulate the net volume change caused by the sponge h-relaxation !! this RK stage into `state%barotropic%mass_src`.  The sponge applies !! `Δh = −dt·α·(h − h_ref)`, which can add or remove mass; this routine !! measures the actual h-change by summing h over interior cells before !! and after `apply_sponge`.  No-op when no sponge edge is configured. !! !! Must be called IN PLACE OF a bare `apply_sponge` call — it calls !! `apply_sponge` internally. type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: stage_weight !! Stage contribution (0.5 per SSP-RK2 stage). integer :: i , j , ng , i_lo , i_hi , j_lo , j_hi real ( wp ) :: h_before , h_after , area ! Fast-exit when no sponge is configured (bc%sponge_width <= 0). if ( state % bc % sponge_width <= 0 ) then call apply_sponge ( state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % grid , state % dt , state % bc ) return end if ng = state % grid % nghost i_lo = ng + 1 i_hi = state % grid % nx_total - ng j_lo = ng + 1 j_hi = state % grid % ny_total - ng area = state % grid % dx * state % grid % dy ! Sum h over interior before the sponge update. h_before = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( j = j_lo : j_hi , i = i_lo : i_hi ) reduce ( + : h_before ) h_before = h_before + state % barotropic % h ( i , j ) end do call apply_sponge ( state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % grid , state % dt , state % bc ) ! Sum h after the sponge update. h_after = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( j = j_lo : j_hi , i = i_lo : i_hi ) reduce ( + : h_after ) h_after = h_after + state % barotropic % h ( i , j ) end do ! Δh > 0: sponge added mass; Δh < 0: sponge removed mass. ! stage_weight accounts for the RK2 contribution (0.5 per stage). state % barotropic % mass_src = state % barotropic % mass_src & + stage_weight * ( h_after - h_before ) * area end subroutine accumulate_sponge_mass_src","tags":"","url":"proc/accumulate_sponge_mass_src.html"},{"title":"solver_accumulate_2d – Rakali","text":"private pure subroutine solver_accumulate_2d(acc, f, grid) Accumulate: acc = acc + f Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: acc (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: f (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid Called by proc~~solver_accumulate_2d~~CalledByGraph proc~solver_accumulate_2d solver_accumulate_2d proc~solver_step_split_impl solver_step_split_impl proc~solver_step_split_impl->proc~solver_accumulate_2d proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_split_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny Source Code pure subroutine solver_accumulate_2d ( acc , f , grid ) !! Accumulate: acc = acc + f type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: acc ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: f ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) integer :: i , j , nx , ny nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx ) acc ( i , j ) = acc ( i , j ) + f ( i , j ) end do end subroutine solver_accumulate_2d","tags":"","url":"proc/solver_accumulate_2d.html"},{"title":"solver_advance_2d_generic – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine solver_advance_2d_generic(state, ts) Generic N-stage explicit SSP advance for the 2D barotropic path\n(euler / rk3 / rk43).  Loops the same forward-Euler stage\nprimitive used by the fused RK2 fast path, then applies the\nShu-Osher convex blend with the start-of-step state U&#94;n: E      = U&#94;(i-1) + beta(i)*dt * L(U&#94;(i-1))   (fused stage)\nU&#94;(i)  = alpha(i)*U&#94;n + (1 - alpha(i))*E      (combine) state%dt already carries the ssp_coeff scaling.  No save/average\nkernels are reused from RK2 — U&#94;n is backed up once, the blend is\na per-stage compute_ssp_combine, both wet/dry-positive (SSP). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( timestepper_t ), intent(in) :: ts Calls proc~~solver_advance_2d_generic~~CallsGraph proc~solver_advance_2d_generic solver_advance_2d_generic proc~apply_boundary_conditions apply_boundary_conditions proc~solver_advance_2d_generic->proc~apply_boundary_conditions proc~apply_sponge apply_sponge proc~solver_advance_2d_generic->proc~apply_sponge proc~compute_ssp_combine compute_ssp_combine proc~solver_advance_2d_generic->proc~compute_ssp_combine proc~fused_update_stage_generic fused_update_stage_generic proc~solver_advance_2d_generic->proc~fused_update_stage_generic proc~profiler_start profiler_start proc~solver_advance_2d_generic->proc~profiler_start proc~profiler_stop profiler_stop proc~solver_advance_2d_generic->proc~profiler_stop proc~solver_compute_barotropic_flux solver_compute_barotropic_flux proc~solver_advance_2d_generic->proc~solver_compute_barotropic_flux proc~solver_save_state solver_save_state proc~solver_advance_2d_generic->proc~solver_save_state proc~bc_chapman_edge bc_chapman_edge proc~apply_boundary_conditions->proc~bc_chapman_edge proc~bc_clamped_edge bc_clamped_edge proc~apply_boundary_conditions->proc~bc_clamped_edge proc~bc_disch_edge bc_disch_edge proc~apply_boundary_conditions->proc~bc_disch_edge proc~bc_flather_edge bc_flather_edge proc~apply_boundary_conditions->proc~bc_flather_edge proc~bc_inflow_edge bc_inflow_edge proc~apply_boundary_conditions->proc~bc_inflow_edge proc~bc_wall_edge bc_wall_edge proc~apply_boundary_conditions->proc~bc_wall_edge local local proc~apply_sponge->local proc~compute_ssp_combine->local proc~fused_update_stage_generic->local proc~find_or_create_region find_or_create_region proc~profiler_start->proc~find_or_create_region proc~get_wall_time get_wall_time proc~profiler_start->proc~get_wall_time proc~nvtx_range_push nvtx_range_push proc~profiler_start->proc~nvtx_range_push proc~profiler_stop->proc~get_wall_time proc~nvtx_range_pop nvtx_range_pop proc~profiler_stop->proc~nvtx_range_pop proc~compute_flux_hll compute_flux_hll proc~solver_compute_barotropic_flux->proc~compute_flux_hll proc~compute_flux_hllc compute_flux_hllc proc~solver_compute_barotropic_flux->proc~compute_flux_hllc proc~bc_chapman_edge->local proc~bc_clamped_edge->local proc~bc_disch_edge->local proc~bc_flather_edge->local proc~bc_inflow_edge->local proc~bc_wall_edge->local proc~compute_flux_hll->local proc~flux_cell flux_cell proc~compute_flux_hll->proc~flux_cell proc~compute_flux_hllc->local proc~compute_flux_hllc->proc~flux_cell proc~extract_velocity extract_velocity proc~flux_cell->proc~extract_velocity proc~hll_flux_x hll_flux_x proc~flux_cell->proc~hll_flux_x proc~hll_flux_y hll_flux_y proc~flux_cell->proc~hll_flux_y proc~hllc_flux_x hllc_flux_x proc~flux_cell->proc~hllc_flux_x proc~hllc_flux_y hllc_flux_y proc~flux_cell->proc~hllc_flux_y proc~minmod minmod proc~flux_cell->proc~minmod Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic