hat interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: it Source Code subroutine solver_multilayer_rk_stage ( state , nz , is_stage1 ) !! One RK stage: barotropic HLL (well-balanced, handles all pressure !! gradients), distribute acceleration to layers preserving shear, !! vertical exchange. `is_stage1` (nz=1 fused fast path only): also save !! pre-update state into the `*_0` arrays; ignored on the nz>1 path. type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state integer , intent ( in ) :: nz logical , intent ( in ) :: is_stage1 integer :: it ! Mirror the S/T scalar config (held on the multilayer state + BC) onto ! their tracer-registry entries so the generic per-tracer kernels (both ! fast and nz>1 paths) read config uniformly. Extra passive tracers keep ! their own config. Cheap host-side scalar copies, idempotent; before ! the nz=1 dispatch so the fast path sees the synced config. it = state % multilayer % idx_salinity if ( it > 0 ) then state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg = state % multilayer % kappa_S_bg state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hdiff_kappa = state % multilayer % hdiff_kappa state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_min = state % multilayer % S_min state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_max = state % multilayer % S_max state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_inflow = state % bc % inflow_salinity end if it = state % multilayer % idx_temperature if ( it > 0 ) then state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg = state % multilayer % kappa_T_bg state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hdiff_kappa = state % multilayer % hdiff_kappa state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_min = state % multilayer % T_min state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_max = state % multilayer % T_max state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_inflow = state % bc % inflow_temperature end if ! At nz=1 the post-update sequence collapses into one fused per-cell ! kernel (+ fused tracer surface-flux/clamp): the depth-averaged-with- ! tracers fast path. nz>1 falls through to the un-fused logic below. if ( nz == 1 ) then call solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 ( state , is_stage1 ) return end if ! Apply barotropic BCs call profiler_start ( \"boundary\" ) call apply_boundary_conditions ( state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , state % barotropic % b , & state % grid , state % bc ) if ( state % multilayer % vcoord % coord_type == VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL ) then call ml_apply_layer_bcs_full ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % multilayer % dsig_ml , state % multilayer % vcoord_z_ref_col , & state % multilayer % vcoord % zstar_h_min , & state % grid , nz ) else call ml_apply_layer_bcs ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , state % multilayer % dsig_ml , & state % grid , nz , & bc_west = state % bc % west , bc_east = state % bc % east , & bc_south = state % bc % south , bc_north = state % bc % north ) end if call profiler_stop ( \"boundary\" ) ! Save barotropic momentum before HLL update call solver_copy_2d ( state % multilayer % hu_ml_pre , state % barotropic % hu , state % grid ) call solver_copy_2d ( state % multilayer % hv_ml_pre , state % barotropic % hv , state % grid ) ! Barotropic HLL flux and update (well-balanced) call profiler_start ( \"flux\" ) call solver_compute_barotropic_flux ( state ) ! Mass budget: the layers are kept consistent with the barotropic h, and ! the RK2 finalise recomputes h from the averaged layers, so the total ! mass change is 0.5·dt·(flux_h&#94;1 + flux_h&#94;2) — the same telescoping as ! the 2D path.  Fires for both stages (this routine is called twice). call accumulate_boundary_mass_out ( state , 0.5_wp ) call profiler_stop ( \"flux\" ) call profiler_start ( \"update\" ) call compute_update ( state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % barotropic % flux_h , state % barotropic % flux_hu , state % barotropic % flux_hv , & state % grid , state % dt ) call profiler_stop ( \"update\" ) ! Tracer step ordering (mirrors unstructured solver): !   1. Tracer BCs on OLD h_layer (before redistribution). !   2. CWC tracer advection: f_layer built from the HLL mass flux so !      `sum_k f_layer = mass_flux_h` (the barotropic continuity !      divergence) — uniform tracers exactly invariant, mass conserved. !   3. Distribute barotropic update to layers (does NOT touch tracer !      mass; step 2 already produced the right hTr for the new h_layer). ! For zsigma (`vcoord%needs_remap()`) the remap path reorders internally ! and conservatively remaps tracers between old and new thicknesses. ! Tracer BCs (operate on OLD h_layer) — loop the registry. do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) call ml_apply_tracer_bcs ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_inflow , & state % grid , nz , state % bc ) end do ! CWC tracer advection on OLD h_layer with NEW mass_flux (same ! ordering as unstructured solver_unstr_step). do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if (. not . state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_horizontal_advection ) cycle if ( state % multilayer % use_ppm_tracer ) then if ( state % multilayer % tracer_recon_code /= TRACER_RECON_PPM ) then call ml_advect_tracer_weno ( & state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % barotropic % mass_flux_x , state % barotropic % mass_flux_y , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , tracer_scratch % weno_tr_snap , state % grid , nz , & state % dt , state % multilayer % tracer_recon_code ) else call ml_advect_tracer_ppm ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % barotropic % mass_flux_x , state % barotropic % mass_flux_y , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & tracer_scratch % ppm_tr_snap , tracer_scratch % ppm_ql_x , tracer_scratch % ppm_qr_x , & tracer_scratch % ppm_ql_y , tracer_scratch % ppm_qr_y , & state % grid , nz , & state % dt ) end if else call ml_advect_tracer ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % barotropic % mass_flux_x , state % barotropic % mass_flux_y , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , tracer_scratch % adv_hTr_snap , state % grid , nz , & state % dt ) end if end do ! Distribute barotropic to layers (sigma) or remap to the zsigma target ! layout (the remap path conservatively projects the post-advection ! tracer profile onto the new vcoord-prescribed thicknesses per cell). if ( state % multilayer % vcoord % needs_remap ()) then if ( state % multilayer % vcoord % coord_type == VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL ) then call ml_distribute_with_remap_full ( state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % multilayer % hu_ml_pre , state % multilayer % hv_ml_pre , & state % multilayer % vcoord_z_ref_col , & state % multilayer % vcoord % zstar_h_min , & state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % grid , nz ) else call ml_distribute_with_remap ( state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % multilayer % hu_ml_pre , state % multilayer % hv_ml_pre , & state % multilayer % vcoord % coord_type , & state % multilayer % dsig_ml , state % multilayer % vcoord_z_ref , & state % multilayer % vcoord % depth_transition , & state % multilayer % vcoord % blend_width , & state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % grid , nz ) end if ! Conservative per-tracer remap (saved remap_dz_old -> new h_layer), ! looped over the whole registry. do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) call ml_remap_tracer ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , state % barotropic % h , & state % multilayer % vcoord % remap_method , & state % multilayer % h_layer , state % grid , nz ) end do else call ml_distribute_barotropic ( state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % multilayer % hu_ml_pre , state % multilayer % hv_ml_pre , & state % multilayer % dsig_ml , & state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % grid , nz ) end if ! Horizontal diffusion of tracers (smooths sharp density fronts) — ! per-tracer hdiff_kappa (synced from the state scalar for S/T). do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_horizontal_diffusion . and . & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hdiff_kappa > 0.0_wp ) then call ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer ( state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hdiff_kappa , & tracer_scratch % hdiff_hTr_pre , & state % grid , nz , & state % dt ) end if end do ! Diagnostic vertical velocity and vertical exchange (momentum + tracers). ! Skipped at nz=1 (no interior interface; all w terms vanish). if ( nz > 1 ) then call ml_compute_vertical_velocity ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % dsig_ml , & state % multilayer % w_ml , & state % grid , nz ) call ml_compute_vertical_exchange ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % w_ml , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_vertical_exchange ) then call ml_vertical_exchange_tracer ( state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , state % multilayer % w_ml , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) end if end do end if ! Equation of state + Ri-dependent vertical mixing. EOS feeds only BPG ! and the vertical-mixing kernels (both nz>1-guarded). At alpha_T=beta_S ! =0 EOS is a no-op; vmix still reads the init-populated rho_layer. if ( nz > 1 ) then if ( state % multilayer % eos_use_shared ) then ! Shared nonlinear EOS (&tracer_nml eos_form) — refresh ! unconditionally (alpha_T/beta_S don't gate this path). call ml_equation_of_state_shared ( state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_temperature )% hTr , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , state % multilayer % eos , & state % grid , nz ) else if ( state % multilayer % alpha_T /= 0.0_wp . or . state % multilayer % beta_S /= 0.0_wp ) then call ml_equation_of_state ( state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_temperature )% hTr , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % beta_S , state % multilayer % S_ref , & state % multilayer % alpha_T , state % multilayer % T_ref , & state % grid , nz ) end if if ( state % multilayer % vmix_use_keps ) then ! k-epsilon closure: advance k/eps, recover nu_t, apply to ! momentum via implicit vertical-diffusion sweep. Takes precedence ! over KPP / PP81. call ml_keps_friction_velocities ( state % forcing % wind_x , state % forcing % wind_y , & state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % barotropic % manning_n , & state % barotropic % use_linear_bottom_drag , & state % barotropic % bottom_drag_r , state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % keps_ustar_s , state % multilayer % keps_ustar_b , & state % grid , nz ) call ml_keps_update ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % rho_layer , & state % multilayer % keps_tke , state % multilayer % keps_eps , & state % multilayer % keps_nut , state % multilayer % keps_kt , & state % multilayer % rho_0 , state % dt , state % grid , nz , & state % multilayer % keps_ustar_b , state % multilayer % keps_ustar_s , & scheme = state % multilayer % keps_stability ) call ml_keps_apply_momentum ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % keps_nut , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) ! Tracer vertical mixing with k-eps scalar diffusivity kt ! (+ per-tracer background floor), implicit + conservative. do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_vertical_diffusion ) then call ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer ( state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % keps_kt , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) end if end do else if ( state % multilayer % vmix_use_kpp ) then ! KPP overlay: one BL-depth sweep feeds the momentum + tracer apply ! kernels (max shape-function diffusivity onto PP81 + non-local ! transport). Replaces the three PP81 calls below. call ml_kpp_boundary_layer ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % rho_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , & state % multilayer % rho_0 , state % multilayer % alpha_T , & state % multilayer % beta_S , CP_WATER , & state % forcing % wind_x , state % forcing % wind_y , & state % forcing % heat_flux , state % forcing % evap_minus_precip , & state % multilayer % kpp_ri_crit , state % multilayer % kpp_c_vt2 , & state % multilayer % kpp_u_star , state % multilayer % kpp_buoy_flux , & state % multilayer % kpp_bl_depth , state % grid , nz ) call ml_kpp_viscosity ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % rho_layer , & state % multilayer % rho_0 , state % multilayer % vmix_nu_max , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_bg , state % multilayer % vmix_ri_alpha , & state % multilayer % kpp_u_star , state % multilayer % kpp_buoy_flux , & state % multilayer % kpp_bl_depth , state % grid , nz , state % dt ) call ml_kpp_diffusion_tracers ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_temperature )% hTr , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_max , state % multilayer % kappa_S_bg , & state % multilayer % kappa_T_bg , state % multilayer % vmix_ri_alpha , & state % multilayer % kpp_cs_nonlocal , state % forcing % heat_flux , & state % forcing % evap_minus_precip , CP_WATER , & state % multilayer % kpp_u_star , state % multilayer % kpp_buoy_flux , & state % multilayer % kpp_bl_depth , state % grid , nz , state % dt ) ! KPP fuses S/T only; extra passive tracers fall back to the ! PP81 interior closure for vertical diffusion. do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( it == state % multilayer % idx_salinity . or . it == state % multilayer % idx_temperature ) cycle if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_vertical_diffusion ) then call ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_max , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg , & state % multilayer % vmix_ri_alpha , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) end if end do else call ml_vertical_viscosity ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_max , state % multilayer % vmix_nu_bg , & state % multilayer % vmix_ri_alpha , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_vertical_diffusion ) then call ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_max , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg , & state % multilayer % vmix_ri_alpha , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) end if end do end if end if ! Surface tracer fluxes (net heat + virtual freshwater): top-layer BC ! for vertical diffusion; before the clamp so overshoot is caught. call ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes ( state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_temperature )% hTr , & state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % forcing % heat_flux , state % forcing % evap_minus_precip , & state % multilayer % evap_mass_sink , & state % multilayer % evap_latent_cooling , & state % multilayer % rho_0 , CP_WATER , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) ! Enforce physical tracer bounds (catches mode-split overshoot) — ! per-tracer bounds (synced from the state scalars for S/T). do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_clamp ) then call ml_clamp_tracer ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_min , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_max , & state % grid , nz ) end if end do ! BPG: skipped at nz=1 (single-layer pressure column is constant, so ! the horizontal gradient is zero). if ( nz > 1 ) then if ( state % multilayer % use_bpg_jacobian ) then call ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient_jacobian ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % rho_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % rho_0 , state % multilayer % rho_ref , & state % multilayer % rho_ref_dz , state % multilayer % nz_ref , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) else call ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % rho_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % rho_0 , state % multilayer % rho_ref , & state % multilayer % rho_ref_dz , state % multilayer % nz_ref , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) end if end if ! Per-layer bottom friction (damps baroclinic shear that depth-averaged friction misses) call ml_apply_bottom_friction ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % barotropic % manning_n , state % barotropic % use_linear_bottom_drag , & state % barotropic % bottom_drag_r , state % grid , nz , state % dt ) ! Smagorinsky horizontal viscosity (damps sharp velocity gradients at fronts) if ( state % multilayer % smagorinsky_cs > 0.0_wp ) then call ml_horizontal_viscosity_smag ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % smagorinsky_cs , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) end if ! Biharmonic (del&#94;4) lateral viscosity (scale-selective grid-noise damping) if ( state % multilayer % biharmonic_nu4 > 0.0_wp ) then call ml_horizontal_viscosity_biharmonic ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % multilayer % biharmonic_nu4 , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) end if ! CFL-based velocity truncation (MOM6-style) call ml_truncate_velocity ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % grid , nz , state % dt , & 0.8_wp ) ! Per-layer Coriolis: rotate each layer's (hu_k, hv_k) through f*dt ! before recomputing the depth-average — correctly rotates baroclinic ! shear (reduces to depth-averaged for uniform columns). call profiler_start ( \"friction\" ) call ml_apply_coriolis ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % grid , nz , state % dt , state % barotropic % coriolis_f ) call profiler_stop ( \"friction\" ) ! Surface-concentrated wind stress: apply to the top layer so it ! generates vertical shear (proper Ekman / mixed-layer dynamics), ! instead of the depth-uniform barotropic forcing below.  The recompute ! folds it into the barotropic; the wind is then suppressed in ! apply_friction so it is not applied twice. if ( state % barotropic % wind_surface_layer . and . state % forcing % active ) then call ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer ( state % multilayer % hu_layer , state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % forcing % wind_x , state % forcing % wind_y , & state % grid , nz , state % dt ) end if ! Recompute barotropic from layers (BPG + vertical exchange + Coriolis shift momentum) call ml_compute_barotropic_momentum ( state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % grid , nz ) ! Wind/pressure/precip on barotropic (friction + Coriolis already applied per-layer above) call profiler_start ( \"friction\" ) call apply_friction ( state % barotropic % h , state % barotropic % hu , state % barotropic % hv , & state % grid , state % dt , & state % barotropic % manning_n , state % forcing % wind_x , state % forcing % wind_y , & state % forcing % atm_pressure , state % forcing % precipitation , & forcing_active = state % forcing % active , & include_wind = . not . state % barotropic % wind_surface_layer ) call profiler_stop ( \"friction\" ) ! Accumulate precipitation + evap mass-source for this RK stage. ! apply_friction adds `h += dt·precip` (barotropic); ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes ! adds the evap mass sink on the layer thickness.  Both contribute to mass_src. call accumulate_mass_src ( state , 0.5_wp , & evap_mass_sink = state % multilayer % evap_mass_sink ) ! Sponge: accumulate the h-change from sponge relaxation in the budget. call accumulate_sponge_mass_src ( state , 0.5_wp ) end subroutine solver_multilayer_rk_stage","tags":"","url":"proc/solver_multilayer_rk_stage.html"},{"title":"solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1(state, is_stage1) Fused RK-stage path specialised for nz_ml=1 (depth-averaged\n2D with optional tracers). Reorders the tracer pipeline to run before the per-cell post-\nupdate sequence so that (compute_update + distribute_barotropic\n+ bottom_friction + truncate_velocity + recompute_barotropic +\nwind / atm_pressure / precip + coriolis) collapses into a\nsingle fused kernel ml_fused_post_update . Mirrors what the\n2D HLL path does with fused_update_stage1/2 . At nz_ml=1 the\nvertical-mixing block (vert_exchange, EOS, vmix, BPG) is\ndefinitionally empty, so this path is complete; for nz_ml>1\nthe un-fused stage above runs instead. When is_stage1 is true the fused kernel additionally saves\nthe pre-update barotropic and layer state into the *_0 arrays, absorbing solver_save_state and ml_save_layer_state . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state logical, intent(in) :: is_stage1 Calls proc~~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1~~CallsGraph proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~apply_boundary_conditions apply_boundary_conditions pro