oc/unstr_barotropic_destroy.html"},{"title":"unstr_barotropic_enter_data – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine unstr_barotropic_enter_data(this) Map the barotropic allocatables onto the device (the parent\nvalue-type member rides over with copyin(state) ; only the inner\narrays need explicit attaches).  Read+write fields use copyin ,\npure-workspace fields use create . Type Bound unstr_barotropic_state_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( unstr_barotropic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this Called by proc~~unstr_barotropic_enter_data~~CalledByGraph proc~unstr_barotropic_enter_data unstr_barotropic_state_t%unstr_barotropic_enter_data proc~state_unstr_enter_data state_unstr_enter_data proc~state_unstr_enter_data->proc~unstr_barotropic_enter_data proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~state_unstr_enter_data proc~rki_unstr_finalize rki_unstr_finalize proc~rki_unstr_finalize->proc~state_unstr_enter_data proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine unstr_barotropic_enter_data ( this ) !! Map the barotropic allocatables onto the device (the parent !! value-type member rides over with `copyin(state)`; only the inner !! arrays need explicit attaches).  Read+write fields use `copyin`, !! pure-workspace fields use `create`. class ( unstr_barotropic_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this ! Conserved + bathymetry + height: read first, then written.  Backup ! arrays are also copyin so test setups can pre-fill them. !$acc enter data copyin(this%stage_cv, this%xmom_cv, this%ymom_cv, & !$acc&                  this%bed_cv, this%height_cv, & !$acc&                  this%stage_eu, this%xmom_eu, this%ymom_eu, & !$acc&                  this%stage_backup, this%xmom_backup, this%ymom_backup, & !$acc&                  this%chapman_eta_old) ! Pure scratch / written-before-read: create-only. !$acc enter data create(this%x_centroid_work, this%y_centroid_work, & !$acc&                  this%stage_ev, this%xmom_ev, this%ymom_ev, & !$acc&                  this%bed_ev, this%height_ev, & !$acc&                  this%xmom_siu, this%ymom_siu, & !$acc&                  this%mass_flux_e) ! `max_speed` feeds the CFL reduction; copyin so a defined value ! is present if the timestep kernel runs before the flux kernel ! (production paths overwrite it every flux pass). !$acc enter data copyin(this%max_speed) end subroutine unstr_barotropic_enter_data","tags":"","url":"proc/unstr_barotropic_enter_data.html"},{"title":"unstr_barotropic_exit_data – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine unstr_barotropic_exit_data(this) Reverse of enter_data — copy out host-visible fields, drop\npure scratch.  Components first, parent last (handled by the\ncaller state_unstr_exit_data ). Type Bound unstr_barotropic_state_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( unstr_barotropic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this Source Code subroutine unstr_barotropic_exit_data ( this ) !! Reverse of `enter_data` — copy out host-visible fields, drop !! pure scratch.  Components first, parent last (handled by the !! caller `state_unstr_exit_data`). class ( unstr_barotropic_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this !$acc exit data copyout(this%stage_cv, this%xmom_cv, this%ymom_cv, & !$acc&                  this%height_cv, & !$acc&                  this%stage_ev, this%xmom_ev, this%ymom_ev, & !$acc&                  this%bed_ev, this%height_ev, & !$acc&                  this%stage_eu, this%xmom_eu, this%ymom_eu, & !$acc&                  this%stage_backup, this%xmom_backup, this%ymom_backup, & !$acc&                  this%max_speed) !$acc exit data delete(this%chapman_eta_old) !$acc exit data delete(this%bed_cv, & !$acc&                 this%x_centroid_work, this%y_centroid_work, & !$acc&                 this%xmom_siu, this%ymom_siu, & !$acc&                 this%mass_flux_e) end subroutine unstr_barotropic_exit_data","tags":"","url":"proc/unstr_barotropic_exit_data.html"},{"title":"unstr_barotropic_init – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine unstr_barotropic_init(this, mesh) Allocate every array at the cell counts in mesh . All arrays\nare zero-initialised.  Calling on an already-initialised\nsub-object is safe – it destroys first. Type Bound unstr_barotropic_state_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( unstr_barotropic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh Calls proc~~unstr_barotropic_init~~CallsGraph proc~unstr_barotropic_init unstr_barotropic_state_t%unstr_barotropic_init proc~unstr_barotropic_destroy unstr_barotropic_state_t%unstr_barotropic_destroy proc~unstr_barotropic_init->proc~unstr_barotropic_destroy Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colour