d ignored) so callers can pass the\nconfigured regime tag without branching. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: sim_type Calls proc~~print_banner~~CallsGraph proc~print_banner print_banner get_knowledge get_knowledge proc~print_banner->get_knowledge info info proc~print_banner->info Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~print_banner~~CalledByGraph proc~print_banner print_banner proc~log_run_header log_run_header proc~log_run_header->proc~print_banner proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~print_banner proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~print_banner proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~log_run_header proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=54), private :: subtitle Source Code subroutine print_banner ( sim_type ) !! Print a cute banner to the console when the simulation starts. !! `sim_type` is accepted (and ignored) so callers can pass the !! configured regime tag without branching. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: sim_type character ( len = 54 ) :: subtitle ! 54 = interior box width (the ═ border) subtitle = \"       2D/3D Coastal Hydrodynamics Model\" if ( present ( sim_type )) continue ! single-regime build: no variants call logger % info ( \"\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║                                                      ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║    ██████╗  █████╗ ██╗  ██╗ █████╗ ██╗     ██╗       ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║    ██╔══██╗██╔══██╗██║ ██╔╝██╔══██╗██║     ██║       ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║    ██████╔╝███████║█████╔╝ ███████║██║     ██║       ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║    ██╔══██╗██╔══██║██╔═██╗ ██╔══██║██║     ██║       ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║    ██║  ██║██║  ██║██║  ██╗██║  ██║███████╗██║       ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║    ╚═╝  ╚═╝╚═╝  ╚═╝╚═╝  ╚═╝╚═╝  ╚═╝╚══════╝╚═╝       ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║                                                      ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║        A GPU accelerated, Fortran native             ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║\" // subtitle // \"║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║                                                      ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ║                                                      ║\" ) call logger % info ( \"  ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\" ) call logger % info ( \"\" ) call logger % info ( \"  Contributors:\" ) call logger % info ( \"    Jorge Luis Galvez Vallejo\" ) call logger % info ( \"    Albert Sietze Thie\" ) ! add your name here after you've contributed! call logger % info ( \"\" ) call get_knowledge () end subroutine print_banner","tags":"","url":"proc/print_banner.html"},{"title":"find_slot – Rakali","text":"private  function find_slot(nbr, n, tgt) result(t) Locate the coarse-edge slot for neighbour tgt in nbr(1:n).  The\ntarget is ALWAYS present — the coarse adjacency + the Galerkin fold\nare built from the same aggregation map, so every folded fine edge has\na coarse slot.  A not-found here means that invariant broke; fail loud\n(host-only build path) rather than silently mislocate a coefficient\ninto slot 1. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nbr (:) integer, intent(in) :: n integer, intent(in) :: tgt Return Value integer Calls proc~~find_slot~~CallsGraph proc~find_slot find_slot error error proc~find_slot->error proc~itoa itoa proc~find_slot->proc~itoa Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to dis