resent — the coarse adjacency + the Galerkin fold !! are built from the same aggregation map, so every folded fine edge has !! a coarse slot.  A not-found here means that invariant broke; fail loud !! (host-only build path) rather than silently mislocate a coefficient !! into slot 1. integer , intent ( in ) :: nbr (:) integer , intent ( in ) :: n , tgt integer :: s t = 0 do s = 1 , n if ( nbr ( s ) == tgt ) then t = s return end if end do call global_logger % error ( \"si_unstr_mg: find_slot could not locate coarse \" // & \"neighbour \" // itoa ( tgt ) // \" in the coarse adjacency \" // & \"— Galerkin fold inconsistent with the aggregation map\" ) error stop \"si_unstr_mg: find_slot: coarse neighbour not found\" end function find_slot","tags":"","url":"proc/find_slot.html"},{"title":"itoa – Rakali","text":"private pure function itoa(i) result(s) Minimal integer->string for the build log line. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: i Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~itoa~~CalledByGraph proc~itoa itoa proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build->proc~itoa proc~galerkin_operator galerkin_operator proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build->proc~galerkin_operator proc~find_slot find_slot proc~find_slot->proc~itoa proc~galerkin_operator->proc~find_slot proc~si_unstr_state_build_mg semi_implicit_state_unstr_t%si_unstr_state_build_mg proc~si_unstr_state_build_mg->proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh->proc~galerkin_operator proc~state_unstr_enable_si state_unstr_enable_si proc~state_unstr_enable_si->proc~si_unstr_state_build_mg proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~state_unstr_enable_si proc~si_unstr_advance si_unstr_advance proc~si_unstr_advance->proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_r