lement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, private :: do_write integer, private :: it integer, private :: varid character(len=32), private :: varname Source Code subroutine define_tracer_outputs ( ostate , state , cfg , dimids_4d , dlevel ) !! Define one NetCDF variable per entry in !! `state%multilayer%tracers(:)`, using each tracer's identity !! strings (`name`, `long_name`, `units`, `standard_name`) so !! the registry alone determines what gets written.  Sets !! `ostate%ml_tracer_varids(it)` to `-1` when the tracer is !! gated off (the legacy `cfg%out_salinity` / !! `cfg%out_temperature` switches still apply for those two !! built-in tracers; new tracers default to write-enabled). type ( output_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: ostate type ( state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg integer , intent ( in ) :: dimids_4d ( 4 ) integer , intent ( in ) :: dlevel integer :: it , varid logical :: do_write character ( len = 32 ) :: varname allocate ( ostate % ml_tracer_varids ( size ( state % multilayer % tracers ))) ostate % ml_tracer_varids = - 1 do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) associate ( tr => state % multilayer % tracers ( it )) varname = trim ( tr % name ) do_write = . true . ! Honour the legacy out_<name> switches for the built-in ! tracers; new tracers fall through to \"always write\". if ( varname == \"salinity\" ) do_write = cfg % out_salinity if ( varname == \"temperature\" ) do_write = cfg % out_temperature if (. not . do_write ) cycle if ( len_trim ( varname ) == 0 ) cycle ! skip un-named tracers call nc_def_var_4d ( ostate % ncid , trim ( varname ), dimids_4d , varid , dlevel ) ostate % ml_tracer_varids ( it ) = varid if ( len_trim ( tr % units ) > 0 ) then call nc_put_att ( ostate % ncid , varid , \"units\" , trim ( tr % units )) end if if ( len_trim ( tr % long_name ) > 0 ) then call nc_put_att ( ostate % ncid , varid , \"long_name\" , trim ( tr % long_name )) end if if ( len_trim ( tr % standard_name ) > 0 ) then call nc_put_att ( ostate % ncid , varid , \"standard_name\" , & trim ( tr % standard_name )) end if call nc_put_att_real ( ostate % ncid , varid , \"_FillValue\" , FILL_VALUE ) end associate end do end subroutine define_tracer_outputs","tags":"","url":"proc/define_tracer_outputs.html"},{"title":"write_tracer_snapshots – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine write_tracer_snapshots(ostate, state, nx, ny, ng, nz_ml, buf3d) Per-tracer host-side write loop.  Divides the conserved tracers(it)%hTr (= h * Tr) by h_layer to recover the\nprimitive variable, then writes through ostate%ml_tracer_varids(it) for each tracer that has output\nenabled. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( output_state_t ), intent(inout) :: ostate type( state_t ), intent(in) :: state integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: ng integer, intent(in) :: nz_ml real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: buf3d (nx,ny,nz_ml) Calls proc~~write_tracer_snapshots~~CallsGraph proc~write_tracer_snapshots write_tracer_snapshots proc~nc_put_var_4d_slice nc_put_var_4d_slice proc~write_tracer_snapshots->proc~nc_put_var_4d_slice nf90_put_var nf90_put_var proc~nc_put_var_4d_slice->nf90_put_var proc~nc_check nc_check proc~nc_put_var_4d_slice->proc~nc_check error error proc~nc_check->error nf90_strerror nf90_strerror proc~nc_check->nf90_strerror Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~write_tracer_snapshots~~CalledByGraph proc~write_tracer_snapshots write_tracer_snapshots proc~output_write_snapshot output_write_snapshot proc~output_write_snapshot->proc~write_tracer_snapshots proc~finalize_output finalize_output proc~finalize_output->proc~output_write_snapshot proc~flush_snapshot flush_snapshot proc~flush_snapshot->proc~output_write_snapshot proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~finalize_output proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_snapshot proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: h_k integer, private :: ii integer, private :: it integer, private :: jj integer, private :: kk Source Code subroutine write_tracer_snapshots ( ostate , state , nx , ny , ng , nz_ml , buf3d ) !! Per-tracer host-side write loop.  Divides the conserved !! `tracers(it)%hTr` (= h * Tr) by `h_layer` to recover the !! primitive variable, then writes through !! `ostate%ml_tracer_varids(it)` for each tracer that has output !! enabled. type ( output_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: ostate type ( state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state integer , intent ( in ) :: nx , ny , ng , nz_ml real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: buf3d ( nx , ny , nz_ml ) integer :: it , ii , jj , kk real ( wp ) :: h_k do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( ostate % ml_tracer_varids ( it ) < 0 ) cycle do kk = 1 , nz_ml do jj = 1 , ny do ii = 1 , nx h_k = state % multilayer % h_layer ( ng + ii , ng + jj , kk ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then buf3d ( ii , jj , kk ) = & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr ( ng + ii , ng + jj , kk ) / h_k else buf3d ( ii , jj , kk ) = 0.0_wp end if end do end do end do call nc_put_var_4d_slice ( ostate % ncid , ostate % ml_tracer_varids ( it ), & buf3d , ostate % time_index ) end do end subroutine write_tracer_snapshots","tags":"","url":"proc/write_tracer_snapshots.html"},{"title":"profiler_get_time – Rakali","text":"public  function profiler_get_time(name) result(t) Accumulated time (s) for a named region. Public for the unit-test suite only. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Return Value real(kind=dp) Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: idx Source Code function profiler_get_time ( name ) result ( t ) !! Accumulated time (s) for a named region. Public for the unit-test suite only. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( dp ) :: t integer :: idx t = 0.0_dp do idx = 1 , state % num_regions if ( trim ( state % regions ( idx )% name ) == trim ( name )) then t = state % regions ( idx )% total_time return end if end do end function profiler_get_time","tags":"","url":"proc/profiler_get_time.html"},{"title":"find_or_create_region – Rakali","text":"private  function find_or_create_region(name) result(idx) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Return