eference_density_unstr – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine ml_compute_reference_density_unstr(state, mesh) Build the horizontally-uniform reference-density profile rho_ref(z) from the current rho_layer , sampled on a uniform\nz-grid 0..rho_ref_dz*nz_ref and area-weighted across owned\ncells. Subtracted by both BPG kernels so the integrand is the\nanomaly rho - rho_ref(z) , scaling the residual sigma PGE down.\nCalled once at solver init after the first EOS evaluation, on\nthe host (one-time D2H+H2D). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh Called by proc~~ml_compute_reference_density_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_compute_reference_density_unstr ml_compute_reference_density_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_compute_reference_density_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~rki_unstr_finalize rki_unstr_finalize proc~rki_unstr_finalize->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: H_col real(kind=wp), private :: H_max real(kind=wp), private :: area_w integer, private :: cell real(kind=wp), private :: dz integer, private :: iz integer, private :: k integer, private :: nz integer, private :: nz_ref real(kind=wp), private :: rho_at_z real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: sum_rho_w (:) real(kind=wp), private :: sum_w real(kind=wp), private :: z real(kind=wp), private :: z_bot real(kind=wp), private :: z_top Source Code subroutine ml_compute_reference_density_unstr ( state , mesh ) !! Build the horizontally-uniform reference-density profile !! `rho_ref(z)` from the current `rho_layer`, sampled on a uniform !! z-grid `0..rho_ref_dz*nz_ref` and area-weighted across owned !! cells. Subtracted by both BPG kernels so the integrand is the !! anomaly `rho - rho_ref(z)`, scaling the residual sigma PGE down. !! Called once at solver init after the first EOS evaluation, on !! the host (one-time D2H+H2D). type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer :: cell , k , iz , nz , nz_ref real ( wp ) :: H_max , H_col , dz , z , z_top , z_bot , rho_at_z , area_w , sum_w real ( wp ), allocatable :: sum_rho_w (:) if (. not . state % use_multilayer ) return if (. not . allocated ( state % multilayer % rho_ref )) return nz = state % multilayer % nz_ml nz_ref = state % multilayer % nz_ref ! Pull layer data back so we can scan it on the host. !$acc update self(state%multilayer%h_layer, state%multilayer%rho_layer) if_present H_max = 0.0_wp do cell = 1 , mesh % ncells_owned H_col = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz H_col = H_col + state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , cell ) end do if ( H_col > H_max ) H_max = H_col end do if ( H_max <= 0.0_wp ) then state % multilayer % rho_ref = state % multilayer % rho_0 state % multilayer % rho_ref_dz = 0.0_wp !$acc update device(state%multilayer%rho_ref) if_present return end if ! Small margin so all columns fit strictly inside the grid even ! after stage variations. H_max = 1.05_wp * H_max dz = H_max / real ( nz_ref , wp ) state % multilayer % rho_ref_dz = dz allocate ( sum_rho_w ( 0 : nz_ref ), source = 0.0_wp ) sum_w = 0.0_wp do cell = 1 , mesh % ncells_owned H_col = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz H_col = H_col + state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , cell ) end do if ( H_col < ML_MIN_DEPTH_UNSTR ) cycle area_w = mesh % area ( cell ) sum_w = sum_w + area_w ! Walk the column from the surface (k = nz) downward to the ! bed (k = 1), tracking the depth `z_top` of the upper layer ! interface. For each ref grid point, find the layer that ! contains `z` and use its density. do iz = 0 , nz_ref z = real ( iz , wp ) * dz z_top = 0.0_wp rho_at_z = state % multilayer % rho_layer ( nz , cell ) if ( z >= H_col ) then rho_at_z = state % multilayer % rho_layer ( 1 , cell ) else do k = nz , 1 , - 1 z_bot = z_top + state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( z >= z_top . and . z <= z_bot ) then rho_at_z = state % multilayer % rho_layer ( k , cell ) exit end if z_top = z_bot end do end if sum_rho_w ( iz ) = sum_rho_w ( iz ) + area_w * rho_at_z end do end do if ( sum_w > 0.0_wp ) then do iz = 0 , nz_ref state % multilayer % rho_ref ( iz ) = sum_rho_w ( iz ) / sum_w end do else state % multilayer % rho_ref = state % multilayer % rho_0 end if deallocate ( sum_rho_w ) !$acc update device(state%multilayer%rho_ref) if_present end subroutine ml_compute_reference_density_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_compute_reference_density_unstr.html"},{"title":"ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr(h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer, eos, nz, n) Opt-in SHARED (ocean) equation of state on the unstructured (nz, ncells) layout — the axis order is opposite to the\nstructured shim, so this evaluates eos_density_point per\n(layer, cell) instead of forwarding to the structured 3D impls. eos_density_point is pure + !$acc routine seq and takes\nthe flat-POD eos_t by value, so the handle rides into\nthe kernel as a register copy — no device mapping.  Evaluation\nis at eos%p_ref (default 0 ⇒ surface/potential density). Vanishing-layer gate is the shared path’s H_VANISHED (not the\nlegacy kernel’s DRY_TOLERANCE ), matching the structured shared\nimpls: layers at or below it fall back to eos%rho0 . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_layer (nz,n) type( eos_t ), intent(in) :: eos integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n Calls proc~~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr~~CallsGraph proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr local local proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr->local proc~eos_density_point eos_density_point proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr->proc~eos_density_point proc~roquet_spv_point roquet_spv_point proc~eos_density_point->proc~roquet_spv_point Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr proc~si_unstr_step_ml si_unstr_step_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_finalize rki_unstr_finalize proc~rki_unstr_finalize->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit->proc~si_unstr_step_ml proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: S_k real(kind=wp), private :: T_k integer, private :: cell real(kind=wp), private :: h_k real(kind=wp), private :: inv_h integer, private :: k Source Code pure subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , & rho_layer , eos , nz , n ) !! Opt-in SHARED (ocean) equation of state on the unstructured !! `(nz, ncells)` layout — the axis order is opposite to the !! structured shim, so this evaluates `eos_density_point` per !! (layer, cell) instead of forwarding to the structured 3D impls. !! `eos_density_point` is `pure` + `!$acc routine seq` and takes !! the flat-POD `eos_t` by value, so the handle rides into !! the kernel as a register copy — no device mapping.  Evaluation !! is at `eos%p_ref` (default 0 ⇒ surface/potential density). !! !! Vanishing-layer gate is the shared path's `H_VANISHED` (not the !! legacy kernel's `DRY_TOLERANCE`), matching the structured shared !! impls: layers at or below it fall back to `eos%rho0`. integer , intent ( in ) :: nz , n real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( nz , n ), hS_layer ( nz , n ), hT_layer ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_layer ( nz , n ) type ( eos_t ), intent ( in ) :: eos integer :: cell , k real ( wp ) :: h_k , S_k , T_k , inv_h do concurrent ( cell = 1 : n , k = 1 : nz ) local ( h_k , S_k , T_k , inv_h ) h_k = h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( h_k > H_VANISHED ) then inv_h = 1.0_wp / h_k S_k = hS_layer ( k , cell ) * inv_h T_k = hT_layer ( k , cell ) * inv_h rho_layer ( k , cell ) = eos_density_point ( eos , T_k , S_k , eos % p_ref ) else rho_layer ( k , cell ) = eos % rho0 end if end do end subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr.html"},{"title":"ml_equation_of_state_unstr – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine ml_equation_of_state_unstr(state) Linear two-tracer EOS, per-cell, per-layer:\n  rho_k = rho_0 + beta_S (S_k - S_ref) - alpha_T (T_k - T_ref)\nwith S_k = hS_k/h_k, T_k = hT_k/h_k. Dry layers fall back to the\nreference state. Computed over all cells (interior + halo) so the\nBPG gradient kernel reads neighbour rho without a separate halo. Outer shim: dereferences tracers(idx)%hTr on the host and passes\nflat 2D arrays into the impl — the array-of-derived-types descriptor\ncan’t be walked on the device under NVHPC stdpar. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Calls proc~~ml_equation_of_state_unstr~~CallsGraph proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~ml_equation_of_state_impl ml_equation_of_state_impl proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr->proc~ml_equation_of_state_impl proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr local local proc~ml_equation_of_state_impl->local proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr->local proc~eos_density_point eos_density_point proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr->proc~eos_density_point proc~roquet_spv_point roquet_spv_point proc~eos_density_point->proc~roquet_spv_point Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_equation_of_state_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~si_unstr_step_ml si_unstr_step_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit