nt64 ) :: nbytes nbytes = this % barotropic % bytes () + this % forcing % bytes () if ( this % use_multilayer ) nbytes = nbytes + this % multilayer % bytes () if ( this % use_nonhydrostatic ) nbytes = nbytes + this % nh % bytes () ! Chapman persistent-state arrays live directly on the bc slot. nbytes = nbytes + arr_bytes ( this % bc % eta_old_west ) & + arr_bytes ( this % bc % eta_old_east ) & + arr_bytes ( this % bc % eta_old_south ) & + arr_bytes ( this % bc % eta_old_north ) end function state_bytes","tags":"","url":"proc/state_bytes.html"},{"title":"fill_bathymetry_ghosts – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine fill_bathymetry_ghosts(state) Wrapper mirror of load_bathymetry — populates ghost rows on state%barotropic%b after a custom bathy load (e.g. via the\nPython FFI). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Calls proc~~fill_bathymetry_ghosts~~CallsGraph proc~fill_bathymetry_ghosts fill_bathymetry_ghosts proc~fill_bathymetry_ghosts_array fill_bathymetry_ghosts_array proc~fill_bathymetry_ghosts->proc~fill_bathymetry_ghosts_array Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~fill_bathymetry_ghosts~~CalledByGraph proc~fill_bathymetry_ghosts fill_bathymetry_ghosts proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~fill_bathymetry_ghosts proc~rki_finalize rki_final