ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine load_bathymetry ( filename , state ) !! Coastal-state entry point — forwards to the array-based loader !! in `rki_bathymetry`.  Lives here (not there) to avoid a USE cycle. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: filename type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state #ifndef RAKALI_NO_NETCDF call load_bathymetry_into_array ( filename , state % barotropic % b , state % grid ) #else ! File-loaded bathymetry needs the NetCDF reader, compiled out when ! RAKALI_ENABLE_NETCDF=OFF.  Fail fast; embed `filename` (also avoids ! an unused-arg warning). if ( state % grid % nghost < 0 ) return ! refs `state` to silence warn error stop \"load_bathymetry: requires RAKALI_ENABLE_NETCDF=ON at \" // & \"build time (the NetCDF-backed rki_bathymetry reader is needed \" // & \"to load '\" // trim ( filename ) // \"').\" #endif end subroutine load_bathymetry","tags":"","url":"proc/load_bathymetry.html"},{"title":"register_default_tracers – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine register_default_tracers(tr_S, tr_T, cfg) Overlay scalar config onto the already-allocated salinity /\ntemperature tracer slots (by reference so coastal + ocean paths\nshare the overlay).  Does not touch hTr / hTr0 — those are\npopulated by the path’s IC step once h_layer is known. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( tracer_t ), intent(inout) :: tr_S type( tracer_t ), intent(inout) :: tr_T type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg Called by proc~~register_default_tracers~~CalledByGraph proc~register_default_tracers register_default_tracers proc~state_init_from_config state_t%state_init_from_config proc~state_init_from_config->proc~register_default_tracers proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~state_init_from_config proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~state_init_from_config proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~state_init_from_config proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine register_default_tracers ( tr_S , tr_T , cfg ) !! Overlay scalar config onto the already-allocated salinity / !! temperature tracer slots (by reference so coastal + ocean paths !! share the overlay).  Does not touch hTr / hTr0 — those are !! populated by the path's IC step once h_layer is known. type ( tracer_t ), intent ( inout ) :: tr_S type ( tracer_t ), intent ( inout ) :: tr_T type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg ! Salinity tr_S % name = \"salinity\" tr_S % long_name = \"Sea water salinity\" tr_S % units = \"PSU\" tr_S % standard_name = \"sea_water_salinity\" tr_S % tr_init = cfg % initial_salinity tr_S % tr_inflow = cfg % inflow_salinity tr_S % tr_min = cfg % S_min tr_S % tr_max = cfg % S_max tr_S % kappa_bg = cfg % kappa_S_bg tr_S % hdiff_kappa = cfg % hdiff_kappa tr_S % eos_coeff = cfg % beta_S tr_S % eos_ref = cfg % S_ref ! Temperature tr_T % name = \"temperature\" tr_T % long_name = \"Sea water potential temperature\" tr_T % units = \"degC\" tr_T % standard_name = \"sea_water_potential_temperature\" tr_T % tr_init = cfg % initial_temperature tr_T % tr_inflow = cfg % inflow_temperature tr_T % tr_min = cfg % T_min tr_T % tr_max = cfg % T_max tr_T % kappa_bg = cfg % kappa_T_bg tr_T % hdiff_kappa = cfg % hdiff_kappa tr_T % eos_coeff = - cfg % alpha_T tr_T % eos_ref = cfg % T_ref end subroutine register_default_tracers","tags":"","url":"proc/register_default_tracers.html"},{"title":"state_destroy – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine state_destroy(this) Deallocate all arrays Type Bound state_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( state_t ), intent(inout) :: this Calls proc~~state_destroy~~CallsGraph proc~state_destroy state_t%state_destroy proc~barotropic_state_destroy barotropic_state_t%barotropic_state_destroy proc~state_destroy->proc~barotropic_state_destroy Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~state_destroy~~CalledByGraph proc~state_destroy state_t%state_destroy proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~state_destroy proc~rki_destroy rki_destroy proc~rki_destroy->proc~state_destroy proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine state_destroy ( this ) !! Deallocate all arrays class ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this call this % barotropic % destroy () call this % forcing % destroy () call this % multilayer % destroy () call this % nh % destroy () ! Chapman BC arrays if ( allocated ( this % bc % eta_old_west )) deallocate ( this % bc % eta_old_west ) if ( allocated ( this % bc % eta_old_east )) deallocate ( this % bc % eta_old_east ) if ( allocated ( this % bc % eta_old_south )) deallocate ( this % bc % eta_old_south ) if ( allocated ( this % bc % eta_old_north )) deallocate ( this % bc % eta_old_north ) end subroutine state_destroy","tags":"","url":"proc/state_destroy.html"},{"title":"state_init – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine state_init(this, nx_phys, ny_phys, nghost, dx, dy, cfl) Allocate all arrays and set grid metadata Type Bound state_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( state_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer, intent(in) :: nx_phys Number of physical cells in x integer, intent(in) :: ny_phys Number of physical cells in y integer, intent(in) :: nghost Ghost cell width real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dx Cell size in x (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dy Cell size in y (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: cfl CFL number Calls proc~~state_init~~CallsGraph proc~state_init state_t%state_init proc~grid_init hgrid_t%grid_init proc~state_init->proc~grid_ini