 a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny Source Code subroutine state_init ( this , nx_phys , ny_phys , nghost , dx , dy , cfl ) !! Allocate all arrays and set grid metadata class ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer , intent ( in ) :: nx_phys !! Number of physical cells in x integer , intent ( in ) :: ny_phys !! Number of physical cells in y integer , intent ( in ) :: nghost !! Ghost cell width real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dx !! Cell size in x (m) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dy !! Cell size in y (m) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: cfl !! CFL number integer :: nx , ny this % cfl = cfl call this % grid % init ( nx_phys , ny_phys , nghost , dx , dy ) nx = this % grid % nx_total ny = this % grid % ny_total ! Barotropic state arrays (h, hu, hv + RK saves, bathymetry, ! flux + mass-flux scratch) call this % barotropic % init ( this % grid ) ! Surface forcing arrays (initialised to zero = no forcing) call this % forcing % init ( this % grid ) ! Coupled hydrostatic multi-layer arrays + tracer registry. ! Caller must set nz_ml + vcoord params first; multilayer%init reads them. if ( this % use_multilayer ) then call this % multilayer % init ( this % grid ) end if ! Non-hydrostatic arrays + mode-splitting buffers.  Caller must set ! nz, CG/NH config, and split_ratio first; nh%init reads them. if ( this % use_nonhydrostatic ) then call this % nh % init ( this % grid ) end if end subroutine state_init","tags":"","url":"proc/state_init.html"},{"title":"state_init_from_config – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine state_init_from_config(this, cfg) Uses rki_recon_weno rki_ml_eos proc~~state_init_from_config~~UsesGraph proc~state_init_from_config state_t%state_init_from_config module~rki_ml_eos rki_ml_eos p