ogram This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: c real(kind=wp), private :: res2 Source Code subroutine si_unstr_wetdry_newton_residual ( nct , nco , eta , Jeta , mass_diag , & v_cell , rhs , res , res2_out ) !! Form the Newton nonlinear residual and its squared interior norm: !!   F_c = v_c(eta) + [T eta]_c - rhs_c, !! with the stiffness recovered matmul-free from the full mass-diag !! operator apply:  T*eta = Jeta - mass_diag*eta.  Returns sum(F&#94;2) !! over the owned cells (the Newton convergence norm — plain, not !! area-weighted, matching the prototype/structured gate; it is a !! convergence heuristic, not the CG inner product). integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta ( nct ), Jeta ( nct ), mass_diag ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: v_cell ( nct ), rhs ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: res ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: res2_out integer :: c real ( wp ) :: res2 do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) res ( c ) = v_cell ( c ) + ( Jeta ( c ) - mass_diag ( c ) * eta ( c )) - rhs ( c ) end do res2 = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) reduce ( + : res2 ) res2 = res2 + res ( c ) * res ( c ) end do res2_out = res2 end subroutine si_unstr_wetdry_newton_residual","tags":"","url":"proc/si_unstr_wetdry_newton_residual.html"},{"title":"si_unstr_wetdry_volume – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine si_unstr_wetdry_volume(nsub, nct, nco, eta, b_sub, v_cell) Per-cell wetted mean depth