roc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_finalize proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_finalize Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , & rho_layer , eos , grid , nz ) !! Opt-in coastal entry to the SHARED (ocean) equation of state — !! selected by `&tracer_nml eos_form = \"wright\" | \"roquet_spv\"`. !! Thin forwarding shim onto the regime-agnostic !! `eos_compute_arrays` variant dispatch; evaluation is at !! `eos%p_ref` (default 0 Pa ⇒ surface/potential density — the !! right choice for the coastal depth range) with the shared !! `H_VANISHED` vanishing-layer fallback to `eos%rho0` (note: the !! legacy coastal kernel gates on `DRY_TOLERANCE` instead).  The !! `eos_t` handle is a flat POD — its scalars are read on !! the host here and passed by value into the device kernels, so !! no device mapping of the handle is required. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hS_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hT_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) type ( eos_t ), intent ( in ) :: eos !! Shared EOS handle (variant + scalar coefficients). call eos_compute_arrays ( eos , h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , & rho_layer , grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) end subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_equation_of_state_shared.html"},{"title":"ml_parse_eos_form – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine ml_parse_eos_form(name, use_shared, variant) Translate the coastal &tracer_nml eos_form knob into the\n(use_shared, EOS_VARIANT_*) pair held on the multilayer state. \"linear\" (the default) keeps the legacy coastal linear kernel\n( ml_equation_of_state / ml_equation_of_state_unstr ) — the\nbit-identity-by-construction path. \"wright\" / \"roquet_spv\" opt in to the shared nonlinear EOS ( rki_eos ) via ml_equation_of_state_shared{,_unstr} .  The shared EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR is deliberately NOT reachable from this\nknob: it is a different linear formulation from the coastal\nkernel and exposing both invites silent near-miss configs.\nUnknown strings fail loud (configure time). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name logical, intent(out) :: use_shared integer, intent(out) :: variant Called by proc~~ml_parse_eos_form~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_parse_eos_form ml_parse_eos_form proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~ml_parse_eos_form proc~state_init_from_config state_t%state_init_from_config proc~state_init_from_config->proc~ml_parse_eos_form proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~state_init_from_config proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~state_init_from_config proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~state_init_from_config proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine ml_parse_eos_form ( name , use_shared , variant ) !! Translate the coastal `&tracer_nml eos_form` knob into the !! (use_shared, EOS_VARIANT_*) pair held on the multilayer state. !! !! `\"linear\"` (the default) keeps the legacy coastal linear kernel !! (`ml_equation_of_state` / `ml_equation_of_state_unstr`) — the !! bit-identity-by-construction path.  `\"wright\"` / `\"roquet_spv\"` !! opt in to the shared nonlinear EOS (`rki_eos`) via !! `ml_equation_of_state_shared{,_unstr}`.  The shared !! `EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR` is deliberately NOT reachable from this !! knob: it is a different linear formulation from the coastal !! kernel and exposing both invites silent near-miss configs. !! Unknown strings fail loud (configure time). character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name logical , intent ( out ) :: use_shared integer , intent ( out ) :: variant select case ( trim ( adjustl ( name ))) case ( \"linear\" , \"\" ) use_shared = . false . variant = EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR case ( \"wright\" , \"wright_97\" , \"wright97\" ) use_shared = . true . variant = EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 case ( \"roquet_spv\" , \"roquet\" ) use_shared = . true . variant = EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV case default error stop \"ml_parse_eos_form: unknown eos_form (use linear | \" // & \"wright | roquet_spv)\" end select end subroutine ml_parse_eos_form","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_parse_eos_form.html"},{"title":"compute_rk2_average – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine compute_rk2_average(h, hu, hv, h0, hu0, hv0, grid) SSP-RK2 averaging step: U&#94;{n+1} = 0.5 (U&#94;n + U *), averaging the\noriginal state (h0, hu0, hv0) with the twice-advanced (h, hu, hv). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid Calls proc~~compute_rk2_average~~CallsGraph proc~compute_rk2_average compute_rk2_average local local proc~compute_rk2_average->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~compute_rk2_average~~CalledByGraph proc~compute_rk2_average compute_rk2_average proc~solver_step_impl solver_step_impl proc~solver_step_impl->proc~compute_rk2_average proc~solver_step_split_impl solver_step_split_impl proc~solver_step_split_impl->proc~compute_rk2_average proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_impl proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_split_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: eps4 real(kind=wp), private :: fr_max_sq real(kind=wp), private :: fr_scale real(kind=wp), private :: h4 integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: speed_sq real(kind=wp), private :: u_val real(kind=wp), private :: v_val Source Code pure subroutine compute_rk2_average ( h , hu , hv , h0 , hu0 , hv0 , grid ) !! SSP-RK2 averaging step: U&#94;{n+1} = 0.5*(U&#94;n + U**), averaging the !! original state (h0, hu0, hv0) with the twice-advanced (h, hu, hv). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) integer :: i , j , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: eps4 , h4 , u_val , v_val , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost eps4 = DESING_EPS ** 4 do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( h4 , u_val , v_val , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale ) h ( i , j ) = 0.5_wp * ( h0 ( i , j ) + h ( i , j )) hu ( i , j ) = 0.5_wp * ( hu0 ( i , j ) + hu ( i , j )) hv ( i , j ) = 0.5_wp * ( hv0 ( i , j ) + hv ( i , j )) ! Same dry clamp + KP07 desingularization + backstop as ! compute_update. if ( h ( i , j ) < 0.0_wp ) then h ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp else if ( h ( i , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp else h4 = h ( i , j ) ** 4 if ( h4 < eps4 ) then u_val = sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h ( i , j ) * hu ( i , j ) / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 ) v_val = sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h ( i , j ) * hv ( i , j ) / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 ) hu ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) * u_val hv ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) * v_val end if speed_sq = ( hu ( i , j ) ** 2 + hv ( i , j ) ** 2 ) / h ( i , j ) ** 2 fr_max_sq = FROUDE_BACKSTOP ** 2 * GRAVITY * h ( i , j ) if ( speed_sq > fr_max_sq ) then fr_scale = sqrt ( fr_max_sq / speed_sq ) hu ( i , j ) = hu ( i , j ) * fr_scale hv ( i , j ) = hv ( i , j ) * fr_scale end if end if end do end subroutine compute_rk2_average","tags":"","url":"proc/compute_rk2_average.html"},{"title":"compute_ssp_combine – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine compute_ssp_combine(h, hu, hv, h0, hu0, hv0, a_n, grid) Generalized SSP Shu-Osher combi