rocedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: a (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: b (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: c (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: cd real(kind=wp), private :: cp (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: cu real(kind=wp), private :: dz_dn real(kind=wp), private :: dz_up real(kind=wp), private :: h_col real(kind=wp), private :: h_dn real(kind=wp), private :: h_k real(kind=wp), private :: h_up integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: r (NZ_STACK_MAX) Source Code pure subroutine ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer ( h_layer , hTr , kt , kappa_bg , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Implicit (Thomas) vertical diffusion of one tracer using k-eps !! diffusivity `kt` (interface-shaped) plus background floor `kappa_bg`. !! No-flux at bed/surface (surface tracer fluxes are a separate kernel); !! conserves column tracer content sum_k hTr_k exactly. Implicit (not !! explicit PP81) because kt can reach NUT_MAX. Pass `tracers(it)%hTr`. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: kt ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz + 1 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: kappa_bg , dt integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: h_col , h_k , h_dn , h_up , dz_dn , dz_up , cd , cu real ( wp ) :: a ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), b ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), c ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: r ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), cp ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) if ( nz < 2 ) return nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , h_col , h_k , h_dn , h_up , dz_dn , dz_up , cd , cu , a , b , c , r , cp ) h_col = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do if ( h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then ! Same tridiagonal as ml_keps_apply_momentum, but with the ! scalar diffusivity kt + kappa_bg and a single RHS (the tracer ! concentration hTr/h).  Vanishing layers drop the coupling. do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_k > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then cd = 0.0_wp if ( k > 1 ) then h_dn = h_layer ( i , j , k - 1 ) dz_dn = 0.5_wp * ( h_dn + h_k ) if ( h_dn > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then cd = dt * ( kt ( i , j , k ) + kappa_bg ) / ( h_k * dz_dn ) end if end if cu = 0.0_wp if ( k < nz ) then h_up = h_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) dz_up = 0.5_wp * ( h_k + h_up ) if ( h_up > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then cu = dt * ( kt ( i , j , k + 1 ) + kappa_bg ) / ( h_k * dz_up ) end if end if a ( k ) = - cd c ( k ) = - cu b ( k ) = 1.0_wp + cd + cu r ( k ) = hTr ( i , j , k ) / h_k else a ( k ) = 0.0_wp c ( k ) = 0.0_wp b ( k ) = 1.0_wp if ( h_k > 0.0_wp ) then r ( k ) = hTr ( i , j , k ) / h_k else r ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if end if end do call keps_tridiag_solve_noflux ( a , b , c , r , cp , nz ) do k = 1 , nz hTr ( i , j , k ) = r ( k ) * h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do end if end do end subroutine ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer.html"},{"title":"ml_keps_apply_momentum – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_keps_apply_momentum(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, nut, grid, nz, dt) Apply k-epsilon eddy viscosity nut (interface-shaped nz+1, from ml_keps_update ) to layer momentum via an implicit (Thomas) vertical-\ndiffusion sweep. No-flux at bed/surface (wind stress and bottom drag\nare separate kernels); conserves column total sum_k h_k u_k exactly.\nImplicit (not explicit PP81) because nu_t can reach NUT_MAX. One do concurrent over columns; shared matrix, two RHS (u, v). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: nut (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz+1) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_keps_apply_momentum~~CallsGraph proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum ml_keps_apply_momentum local local proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum->local proc~keps_tridiag_solve_noflux keps_tridiag_solve_noflux proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum->proc~keps_tridiag_solve_noflux Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_keps_apply_momentum~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum ml_keps_apply_momentum proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: a (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: b (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: c (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: cd real(kind=wp), private :: cp (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: cu real(kind=wp), private :: dz_dn real(kind=wp), private :: dz_up real(kind=wp), private :: h_col real(kind=wp), private :: h_dn real(kind=wp), private :: h_k real(kind=wp), private :: h_up integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: ru (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: rv (NZ_STACK_MAX) Source Code pure subroutine ml_keps_apply_momentum ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , nut , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Apply k-epsilon eddy viscosity `nut` (interface-shaped nz+1, from !! `ml_keps_update`) to layer momentum via an implicit (Thomas) vertical- !! diffusion sweep. No-flux at bed/surface (wind stress and bottom drag !! are separate kernels); conserves column total sum_k h_k u_k exactly. !! Implicit (not explicit PP81) because nu_t can reach NUT_MAX. One !! `do concurrent` over columns; shared matrix, two RHS (u, v). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: nut ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz + 1 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: h_col , h_k , h_dn , h_up , dz_dn , dz_up , cd , cu real ( wp ) :: a ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), b ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), c ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: ru ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), rv ( NZ_STACK_MAX ), cp ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) if ( nz < 2 ) return nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , h_col , h_k , h_dn , h_up , dz_dn , dz_up , cd , cu , & a , b , c , ru , rv , cp ) h_col = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do if ( h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then ! Build the tridiagonal.  Row k couples to k-1 across interface ! k and to k+1 across interface k+1; cd / cu are the implicit ! coupling coefficients dt*nu_t/(h_k * dz_interface).  A ! vanishing layer on either side drops that coupling (no-flux), ! so dividing by a near-zero thickness can't blow up (same guard ! philosophy as ml_vertical_viscosity). do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_k > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then cd = 0.0_wp if ( k > 1 ) then h_dn = h_layer ( i , j , k - 1 ) dz_dn = 0.5_wp * ( h_dn + h_k ) if ( h_dn > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then cd = dt * nut ( i , j , k ) / ( h_k * dz_dn ) end if end if cu = 0.0_wp if ( k < nz ) then h_up = h_layer ( i , j , k + 1 ) dz_up = 0.5_wp * ( h_k + h_up ) if ( h_up > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then cu = dt * nut ( i , j , k + 1 ) / ( h_k * dz_up ) end if end if a ( k ) = - cd c ( k ) = - cu b ( k ) = 1.0_wp + cd + cu ru ( k ) = hu_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k rv ( k ) = hv_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k else ! Vanishing / dry layer: decouple, leave momentum unchanged. a ( k ) = 0.0_wp c ( k ) = 0.0_wp b ( k ) = 1.0_wp if ( h_k > 0.0_wp ) then ru ( k ) = hu_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k rv ( k ) = hv_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k else ru ( k ) = 0.0_wp rv ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if end if end do call keps_tridiag_solve_noflux ( a , b , c , ru , cp , nz ) call keps_tridiag_solve_noflux ( a , b , c , rv , cp , nz ) do k = 1 , nz hu_layer ( i , j , k ) = ru ( k ) * h_layer ( i , j , k ) hv_layer ( i , j , k ) = rv ( k ) * h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do end if end do end subroutine ml_keps_apply_momentum","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_keps_apply_momentum.html"},{"title":"ml_keps_friction_velocities – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_keps_friction_velocities(wind_x, wind_y, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, manning_n, use_linear_drag, drag_r, rho_0, ustar_s, ustar_b, grid, nz) Per-column surface and bed friction velocities feeding the k-eps\nwall functions ( ml_keps_update ).\n  surface: u_ s = sqrt(|tau_wind| / rho_0), tau_wind = (wind_x,\n           wind_y) the wind-stress components (Pa).\n  bed:     from the active bottom-drag law — quadratic Manning\n           u_ b = sqrt(C_d) |u_b|, C_d = g n&#94;2 / H&#94;(1/3); or linear\n           (Rayleigh) u_ b = sqrt(r * h_b * |u_b|).\nBottom velocity is the k=1 (bed) layer; H is the column depth. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: manning_n logical, intent(in) :: use_linear_drag real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: drag_r real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ustar_s (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ustar_b (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz Calls proc~~ml_keps_friction_velocities~~CallsGraph proc~ml_keps_friction_velocities ml_keps_friction_velocities local local proc~ml_keps_friction_velocities->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_keps_friction_velocities~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_keps_friction_velocities ml_keps_friction_velocities proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_keps_friction_velocities proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: cf real(kind=wp), private :: h_b real(kind=wp), private :: h_col integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: m integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: speed_b real(kind=wp), private :: u_b real(kind=wp), private :: v_b Source Code pure subroutine ml_keps_friction_velocities ( wind_x , wind_y , h_layer , & hu_layer , hv_layer , manning_n , & use_linear_drag , drag_r , rho_0 , & ustar_s , ustar_b , grid , nz ) !! Per-column surface and bed friction velocities feeding the k-eps !! wall functions (`ml_keps_update`). !!   surface: u_*s = sqrt(|tau_wind| / rho_0), tau_wind = (wind_x, !!            wind_y) the wind-stress components (Pa). !!   bed:     from the active bottom-drag law — quadratic Manning !!            u_*b = sqrt(C_d)*|u_b|, C_d = g n&#94;2 / H&#94;(1/3); or linear !!            (Rayleigh) u_*b = sqrt(r * h_b * |u_b|). !! Bottom velocity is the k=1 (bed) layer; H is the column depth. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: wind_x ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: wind_y ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: manning_n , drag_r , rho_0 logical , intent ( in ) :: use_linear_drag real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ustar_s ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ustar_b ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) integer :: i , j , m , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: h_col , h_b , u_b , v_b , speed_b , cf nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( m , h_col , h_b , u_b , v_b , speed_b , cf ) ! surface: wind-stress magnitude -> u_*s = sqrt(|tau|/rho_0) ustar_s ( i , j ) = sqrt ( sqrt ( wind_x ( i , j ) * wind_x ( i , j ) & + wind_y ( i , j ) * wind_y ( i , j )) / rho_0 ) ! bed: bottom-layer (k=1) speed + column depth h_col = 0.0_wp do m = 1 , nz h_col = h_col + h_layer ( i , j , m ) end do h_b = h_layer ( i , j , 1 ) if ( h_b > DRY_TOLERANCE . and . h_col > ML_MIN_DEPTH ) then u_b = hu_layer ( i , j , 1 ) / h_b v_b = hv_layer ( i , j , 1 ) / h_b speed_b = sqrt ( u_b * u_b + v_b * v_b ) if ( use_linear_drag ) then ustar_b ( i , j ) = sqrt ( drag_r * h_b * speed_b ) else cf = GRAVITY * manning_n * manning_n / ( h_col ** ( 1.0_wp / 3.0_wp )) ustar_b ( i , j ) = sqrt ( cf ) * speed_b end if else ustar_b ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp end if end do end subroutine ml_keps_friction_velocities","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_keps_friction_velocities.html"},{"title":"ml_keps_update – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_keps_update(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, rho_layer, tke, eps, nut, kt, rho_0, dt, grid, nz, ustar_b, ustar_s, scheme) Advance k and eps one step per column and recover nu_t / kappa_t. tke , eps , nut , kt are interface-shaped (nz+1); tke / eps / nut carry state across steps (the diffusion reads the old nut ). Boundary closure: if the optional friction velocities ustar_b (bed) and ustar_s (surface) are present, Dirichlet log-law wall\nfunctions are imposed at the first interior interfaces (interface 2\nabove the bed, interface nz below the surface):\n  k = u_ &#94;2 / sqrt(c_mu),   eps = u_ &#94;3 / (kappa_eff*(z + z0))\nwith z the interface distance from the wall (= the adjacent layer\nthickness).  Absent both, the boundary interfaces fall back to the\nzero-gradient (no-flux) closure (used by the standalone unit tests). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: tke (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz+1) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eps (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz+1) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: nut (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz+1) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: kt (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz+1) Scalar diffusivity, carried across steps: the buoyancy term reads\nthe old value, so a stratification-aware scheme stays consistent. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: ustar_b (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) Bed friction velocity sqrt(|tau_b|/rho_0) (m/s), per column. real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: ustar_s (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) Surface friction velocity sqrt(|tau_wind|/rho_0) (m/s), per column. integer, intent(in), optional :: scheme Stability-function scheme (KEPS_STAB_*): absent / CONSTANT -> the\nstandard constant c_mu = 0.09 (bit-identical to the original);\nGALPERIN -> stratification-aware quasi-equilibrium. Calls proc~~ml_keps_update~~CallsGraph proc~ml_keps_update ml_keps_update local local proc~ml_keps_update->local proc~keps_stability_funcs keps_stability_funcs proc~ml_keps_update->proc~keps_stability_funcs proc~keps_tridiag_solve keps_tridiag_solve proc~ml_keps_