a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: cg_it integer, private :: cg_it_total logical, private :: converged real(kind=wp), private :: f2 integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: mass_res integer, private :: nit real(kind=wp), private :: rhs2 real(kind=wp), private :: tol2 integer, private :: wetcount integer, private :: wetcount_prev Source Code subroutine si_ml_wetdry_newton ( state , mesh , nct , nco , g_theta2_dt2 , iter_out ) !! Newton outer loop for the 3D column-integrated wet/dry eta-solve on !! the triangulation — the triangular twin of the structured !! `si_ml_wetdry_newton` (and the 2D-unstr `si_unstr_advance_wetdry`'s !! Newton loop).  The column responses (g_col/r_col/Hhat/Gbar) and the !! frozen Hf are held FIXED (they depend on h_layer at time n, not eta), !! so only the surface mass system F = v(eta) + T*eta - rhs_d iterates, !! with T the Hhat-weighted TPFA stiffness and the surface wet-fraction !! Newton diagonal a(eta)+floor.  On entry `state%si%eta_r` holds the !! LINEAR RHS (leading eta&#94;n from si_unstr_compute_rhs); this swaps the !! leading term for v(eta&#94;n) once, then Newton-solves.  Host-side !! orchestration; flat device kernels.  Writes state%si%newton_iters !! and state%si%mass_res = the NONLINEAR mass residual ||F||&#94;2 at !! Newton exit (the conservation diagnostic — NOT the inner-CG residual !! of the last delta-solve, which is an internal solver number). type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nct , nco real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: g_theta2_dt2 integer , intent ( out ) :: iter_out !! Inner CG iterations summed over the Newton outers. integer :: k , nit , cg_it , cg_it_total , wetcount , wetcount_prev real ( wp ) :: rhs2 , f2 , tol2 , mass_res logical :: converged associate ( si => state % si ) ! rhs_d = eta_r + (v(eta&#94;n) - eta&#94;n): swap the linear RHS leading ! term for the wetted volume (same as the 2D/structured wet/dry). call si_unstr_wetdry_volume ( si % n_sub , nct , nco , si % eta , si % b_sub , si % v_cell ) do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) si % rhs_d ( k ) = si % eta_r ( k ) + ( si % v_cell ( k ) - si % eta ( k )) end do rhs2 = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) reduce ( + : rhs2 ) rhs2 = rhs2 + si % rhs_d ( k ) * si % rhs_d ( k ) end do tol2 = max ( SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_TOL * SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_TOL * rhs2 , 1.0e-60_wp ) cg_it_total = 0 cg_it = 0 mass_res = 0.0_wp wetcount_prev = - 1 converged = . false . do nit = 1 , SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_MAX call si_unstr_wetdry_wetfrac ( si % n_sub , nct , nco , si % eta , si % b_sub , si % a_wet ) call si_unstr_wetdry_volume ( si % n_sub , nct , nco , si % eta , si % b_sub , si % v_cell ) call si_unstr_wetdry_mass_diag ( nct , nco , si % a_wet , si % Hf_edge , si % mass_diag ) call si_unstr_apply_helmholtz ( mesh , nct , nco , si % eta , si % newton_Jeta , & si % Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , & mass_diag = si % mass_diag ) call si_unstr_wetdry_newton_residual ( nct , nco , si % eta , si % newton_Jeta , & si % mass_diag , si % v_cell , & si % rhs_d , si % newton_F , f2 ) call si_unstr_wetdry_wetcount ( si % n_sub , nct , nco , si % eta , si % b_sub , wetcount ) if ( nit > 1 . and . wetcount == wetcount_prev . and . f2 < tol2 ) then converged = . true . exit end if wetcount_prev = wetcount ! Solve J*dz = -F from zero (full-array zero so the ghost band of ! the search space stays 0); eta += dz. do concurrent ( k = 1 : nct ) si % newton_dz ( k ) = 0.0_wp end do do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) si % eta_r ( k ) = - si % newton_F ( k ) end do call si_unstr_cg_solve ( mesh , nct , nco , si % newton_dz , si % eta_r , & si % eta_p , si % eta_Ap , si % eta_z , si % eta_diag , & si % Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , si % precond , & si % rtol , cg_it , mass_res , & mass_diag = si % mass_diag ) cg_it_total = cg_it_total + cg_it do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) si % eta ( k ) = si % eta ( k ) + si % newton_dz ( k ) end do end do si % newton_iters = min ( nit , SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_MAX ) ! Report the NONLINEAR mass residual ||F||&#94;2 (the conservation ! diagnostic), not `mass_res` (the inner-CG residual of the final ! delta-solve — an internal solver number that misleads anyone ! reading state%si%mass_res as a mass defect). si % mass_res = f2 if (. not . converged ) then call global_logger % warning ( \"si_ml_wetdry_newton: Newton did not \" // & \"converge in the iteration cap; last ||F||&#94;2 above tol.\" ) end if end associate iter_out = cg_it_total end subroutine si_ml_wetdry_newton","tags":"","url":"proc/si_ml_wetdry_newton.html"},{"title":"si_ml_zero_dead_edges – Rakali","text":"private pure subroutine si_ml_zero_dead_edges(nct, nco, Hf_edge, u_n_edge) Zero the saved U&#94;n on dead (wall / Hf=0) edges — Casulli rule R3:\na dead edge carries no (1-theta) flux into the theta-blend RHS. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: u_n_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Calls proc~~si_ml_zero_dead_edges~~CallsGraph proc~si_ml_zero_dead_edges si_ml_zero_dead_edges local local proc~si_ml_zero_dead_edges->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where poss