e Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: a (BPG_NZ_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: b (BPG_NZ_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: c (BPG_NZ_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: cd integer, private :: cell real(kind=wp), private :: cp (BPG_NZ_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: cu real(kind=wp), private :: dz_dn real(kind=wp), private :: dz_up real(kind=wp), private :: h_dn real(kind=wp), private :: h_k real(kind=wp), private :: h_up integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: r (BPG_NZ_MAX) Source Code pure subroutine ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer_unstr_impl ( nz , n , h_layer , hTr , kt , kappa_bg , & height_cv , dt ) !! Per-cell implicit tracer diffusion on flat explicit-shape arrays.  Same !! tridiagonal as the momentum apply but with the scalar diffusivity !! kt + kappa_bg and a single RHS (the tracer concentration hTr/h). integer , intent ( in ) :: nz , n real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: kt ( nz + 1 , n ), height_cv ( n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: kappa_bg , dt integer :: cell , k real ( wp ) :: h_k , h_dn , h_up , dz_dn , dz_up , cd , cu real ( wp ) :: a ( BPG_NZ_MAX ), b ( BPG_NZ_MAX ), c ( BPG_NZ_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: r ( BPG_NZ_MAX ), cp ( BPG_NZ_MAX ) do concurrent ( cell = 1 : n ) & local ( k , h_k , h_dn , h_up , dz_dn , dz_up , cd , cu , a , b , c , r , cp ) if ( height_cv ( cell ) >= ML_MIN_DEPTH_UNSTR ) then do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( h_k > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL_UNSTR ) then cd = 0.0_wp if ( k > 1 ) then h_dn = h_layer ( k - 1 , cell ) dz_dn = 0.5_wp * ( h_dn + h_k ) if ( h_dn > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL_UNSTR ) cd = dt * ( kt ( k , cell ) + kappa_bg ) / ( h_k * dz_dn ) end if cu = 0.0_wp if ( k < nz ) then h_up = h_layer ( k + 1 , cell ) dz_up = 0.5_wp * ( h_k + h_up ) if ( h_up > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL_UNSTR ) cu = dt * ( kt ( k + 1 , cell ) + kappa_bg ) / ( h_k * dz_up ) end if a ( k ) = - cd c ( k ) = - cu b ( k ) = 1.0_wp + cd + cu r ( k ) = hTr ( k , cell ) / h_k else a ( k ) = 0.0_wp c ( k ) = 0.0_wp b ( k ) = 1.0_wp if ( h_k > 0.0_wp ) then r ( k ) = hTr ( k , cell ) / h_k else r ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if end if end do call keps_tridiag_solve_noflux_u ( a , b , c , r , cp , nz ) do k = 1 , nz hTr ( k , cell ) = r ( k ) * h_layer ( k , cell ) end do end if end do end subroutine ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer_unstr_impl","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer_unstr_impl.html"},{"title":"ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr(state, dt) State-passed shim: apply the keps eddy viscosity to layer momentum by\nan implicit (Thomas) vertical-diffusion sweep.  No-flux at bed/surface\n(wind + bottom drag are separate kernels), conserves the column total. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr~~CallsGraph proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr_impl ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr_impl proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr->proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr_impl local local proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr_impl->local proc~keps_tridiag_solve_noflux_u keps_tridiag_solve_noflux_u proc~ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr_impl->proc~keps_tridiag_solve_noflux_u Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Proce