l proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl proc~eos_wright_impl eos_wright_impl proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_wright_impl proc~zstar_full_build_column zstar_full_build_column proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full->proc~zstar_full_build_column Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~init_from_config~~CalledByGraph proc~init_from_config init_from_config proc~rki_finalize rki_finalize proc~rki_finalize->proc~init_from_config proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_finalize proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_finalize Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine init_from_config ( s , cfg ) !! Select and apply initial condition based on config type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: s type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg select case ( trim ( cfg % init_condition )) case ( \"still_water\" ) call init_still_water ( s , cfg % eta_initial ) case ( \"gaussian_hump\" ) call init_gaussian_hump ( s , cfg % h0 , cfg % hump_amplitude , cfg % hump_sigma , & cfg % hump_x_offset , cfg % hump_y_offset , cfg % init_u_shear ) case ( \"castro_dam_break\" ) call init_castro_dam_break ( s ) case default call init_dam_break ( s ) end select ! Initialise multilayer arrays from barotropic state if ( s % use_multilayer ) call init_multilayer_from_barotropic ( s , cfg ) end subroutine init_from_config","tags":"","url":"proc/init_from_config.html"},{"title":"init_gaussian_hump – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine init_gaussian_hump(s, h0, amplitude, sigma, x_off, y_off, u_shear) Initialise a Gaussian hump perturbation. When u_shear /= 0 and NH\nis enabled, the top layer gets +u_shear and the bottom -u_shear\n(vertical shear → non-zero vorticity). Bathymetry preserved if\nalready loaded. Public only for the unit-test suite. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: s real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h0 Background water depth (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: amplitude Hump amplitude (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: sigma Gaussian width (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x_off Hump centre x-offset from domain centre (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: y_off Hump centre y-offset from domain centre (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_shear Initial vertical shear: top +val, bottom -val (m/s) Called by proc~~init_gaussian_hump~~CalledByGraph proc~init_gaussian_hump init_gaussian_hump proc~init_from_config init_from_config proc~init_from_config->proc~init_gaussian_hump proc~rki_finalize rki_finalize proc~rki_finalize->proc~init_from_config proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_finalize proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_finalize Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, private :: has_bathymetry integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: layer_sign real(kind=wp), private :: r2 real(kind=wp), private :: u_bar real(kind=wp), private :: x real(kind=wp), private :: x_c real(kind=wp), private :: y real(kind=wp), private :: y_c Source Code subroutine init_gaussian_hump ( s , h0 , amplitude , sigma , x_off , y_off , u_shear ) !! Initialise a Gaussian hump perturbation. When u_shear /= 0 and NH !! is enabled, the top layer gets +u_shear and the bottom -u_shear !! (vertical shear → non-zero vorticity). Bathymetry preserved if !! already loaded. Public only for the unit-test suite. type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: s real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h0 !! Background water depth (m) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: amplitude !! Hump amplitude (m) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: sigma !! Gaussian width (m) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x_off !! Hump centre x-offset from domain centre (m) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: y_off !! Hump centre y-offset from domain centre (m) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_shear !! Initial vertical shear: top +val, bottom -val (m/s) integer :: i , j , k real ( wp ) :: x , y , x_c , y_c , r2 , u_bar real ( wp ) :: layer_sign logical :: has_bathymetry x_c = real ( s % grid % nx_phys , wp ) * s % grid % dx * 0.5_wp + x_off y_c = real ( s % grid % ny_phys , wp ) * s % grid % dy * 0.5_wp + y_off ! Check if bathymetry was already loaded (non-zero values present) has_bathymetry = any ( s % barotropic % b /= 0.0_wp ) do j = 1 , s % grid % ny_total do i = 1 , s % grid % nx_total x = ( real ( i - s % grid % nghost , wp ) - 0.5_wp ) * s % grid % dx y = ( real ( j - s % grid % nghost , wp ) - 0.5_wp ) * s % grid % dy r2 = ( x - x_c ) ** 2 + ( y - y_c ) ** 2 if (. not . has_bathymetry ) s % barotropic % b ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp s % barotropic % h ( i , j ) = h0 + amplitude * exp ( - r2 / ( 2.0_wp * sigma ** 2 )) s % barotropic % hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp s % barotropic % hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp end do end do ! NH layer velocities with optional vertical shear if ( s % use_nonhydrostatic ) then do k = 1 , s % nh % nz ! Linear shear: top layer positive, bottom negative ! layer_sign goes from -(nz-1)/nz to +(nz-1)/nz layer_sign = ( 2.0_wp * real ( k , wp ) - real ( s % nh % nz + 1 , wp )) / real ( s % nh % nz , wp ) do j = 1 , s % grid % ny_total do i = 1 , s % grid % nx_total s % nh % u_layer ( i , j , k ) = u_shear * layer_sign s % nh % v_layer ( i , j , k ) = 0.0_wp end do end do end do ! Set depth-averaged momentum consistent with layer velocities ! hu = h * sum(dsig(k) * u_layer(k)) do j = 1 , s % grid % ny_total do i = 1 , s % grid % nx_total u_bar = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , s % nh % nz u_bar = u_bar + s % nh % dsig ( k ) * s % nh % u_layer ( i , j , k ) end do s % barotropic % hu ( i , j ) = s % barotropic % h ( i , j ) * u_bar end do end do end if end subroutine init_gaussian_hump","tags":"","url":"proc/init_gaussian_hump.html"},{"title":"init_multilayer_from_barotropic – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine init_multilayer_from_barotropic(s, cfg) Cold-start multilayer initialisation from the barotropic state:\nlay out the layers, seed the tracers from their IC scalars, then\nderive density and the reference-density profile. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: s type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg Calls proc~~init_multilayer_from_barotropic~~CallsGraph proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic init_multilayer_from_barotropic info info proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->info proc~ml_set_min_depth ml_set_min_depth proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->proc~ml_set_min_depth proc~multilayer_init_layers multilayer_state_t%multilayer_init_layers proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->proc~multilayer_init_layers proc~multilayer_seed_tracers multilayer_state_t%multilayer_seed_tracers proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->proc~multilayer_seed_tracers proc~refresh_multilayer_derived refresh_multilayer_derived proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->proc~refresh_multilayer_derived to_string to_string proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->to_string warning warning proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->warning proc~ml_init_layers_from_barotropic ml_init_layers_from_barotropic proc~multilayer_init_layers->proc~ml_init_layers_from_barotropic proc~multilayer_build_vcoord_reference multilayer_state_t%multilayer_build_vcoord_reference proc~multilayer_init_layers->proc~multilayer_build_vcoord_reference proc~ml_seed_tracer ml_seed_tracer proc~multilayer_seed_tracers->proc~ml_seed_tracer proc~ml_compute_reference_density ml_compute_reference_density proc~refresh_multilayer_derived->proc~ml_compute_reference_density proc~ml_equation_of_state ml_equation_of_state proc~refresh_multilayer_derived->proc~ml_equation_of_state proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~refresh_multilayer_derived->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared local local proc~ml_equation_of_state->local proc~eos_compute_arrays eos_compute_arrays proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared->proc~eos_compute_arrays proc~ml_init_tracer ml_init_tracer proc~ml_seed_tracer->proc~ml_init_tracer proc~ml_init_tracer_stratified ml_init_tracer_stratified proc~ml_seed_tracer->proc~ml_init_tracer_stratified proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full proc~multilayer_build_vcoord_reference->proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full proc~eos_linear_impl eos_linear_impl proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_linear_impl proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl eos_roquet_spv_impl proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl proc~eos_wright_impl eos_wright_impl proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_wright_impl proc~zstar_full_build_column zstar_full_build_column proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full->proc~zstar_full_build_column proc~eos_linear_impl->local proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl->local proc~roquet_spv_point roquet_spv_point proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl->proc~roquet_spv_point proc~eos_wright_impl->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~init_multilayer_from_barotropic~~CalledByGraph proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~api_init_multilayer api_init_multilayer proc~api_init_multilayer->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_from_config init_from_config proc~init_from_config->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~rki_finalize rki_finalize proc~rki_finalize->proc~api_init_multilayer proc~rki_finalize->proc~init_from_config proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_finalize proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_finalize Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine init_multilayer_from_barotropic ( s , cfg ) !! Cold-start multilayer initialisation from the barotropic state: !! lay out the layers, seed the tracers from their IC scalars, then !! derive density and the reference-density profile. type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: s type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg call ml_set_min_depth ( cfg % ml_min_depth ) ! Lay out the initial layer distribution from the barotropic state ! (builds the VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL reference z-levels first if needed). call s % multilayer % init_layers ( s % barotropic , s % grid ) ! Seed salinity + temperature from their IC scalars (each dispatching ! uniform-vs-stratified; S_init_bottom > S_init_surface = salty bed). call s % multilayer % seed_tracers ( s % grid ) call refresh_multilayer_derived ( s ) call logger % info ( \"Multilayer initialised: \" // to_string ( s % multilayer % nz_ml ) // & \" layers, S = \" // to_string ( s % multilayer % initial_salinity ) // & \" PSU, T = \" // to_string ( s % multilayer % initial_temperature ) // & \" degC, ml_min_depth = \" // to_string ( cfg % ml_min_depth ) // & \" m, BPG = \" // trim ( cfg % bpg_method )) if ( cfg % ml_min_depth < 0.1_wp * s % multilayer % nz_ml ) then call logger % warning ( \"ml_min_depth = \" // to_string ( cfg % ml_min_depth ) // & \" m may be too small for \" // to_string ( s % multilayer % nz_ml ) // & \" layers (min layer = \" // & to_string ( cfg % ml_min_depth / s % multilayer % nz_ml ) // \" m). \" // & \"Consider increasing to \" // & to_string ( 0.1_wp * s % multilayer % nz_ml ) // \" m if instabilities appear.\" ) end if end subroutine init_multilayer_from_barotropic","tags":"","url":"proc/init_multilayer_from_barotropic.html"},{"title":"init_still_water – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine init_still_water(s, eta0) Initialise a flat free surface at elevation eta0:\nh = max(eta0 - b, 0) everywhere, zero velocity. Requires\nbathymetry already loaded into s%barotropic%b. Public only for tests. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: s real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta0 Initial free-surface elevation (m, same datum as bathymetry) Called by proc~~init_still_water~~CalledByGraph proc~init_still_water init_still_water proc~init_from_config init_from_config proc~init_from_config->proc~init_still_water proc~rki_finalize rki_finalize proc~rki_finalize->proc~init_from_config proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_finalize proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_finalize Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: i integer, private :: j Source Code subroutine init_still_water ( s , eta0 ) !! Initialise a flat free surface at elevation eta0: !! h = max(eta0 - b, 0) everywhere, zero velocity. Requires !! bathymetry already loaded into s%barotropic%b. Public only for tests. type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: s real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta0 !! Initial free-surface elevation (m, same datum as bathymetry) integer :: i , j do j = 1 , s % grid % ny_total do i = 1 , s % grid % nx_total s % barotropic % h ( i , j ) = max ( eta0 - s % barotropic % b ( i , j ), 0.0_wp ) s % barotropic % hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp s % barotropic % hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp end do end do end subroutine init_still_water","tags":"","url":"proc/init_still_water.html"},{"title":"refresh_multilayer_derived – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine refresh_multilayer_derived(s) Recompute the multilayer fields that are derived from the layer\nthicknesses and tracers: the equation of state ( rho_layer ) and\nthe reference-density profile ( rho_ref ) that the baroclinic\npressure-gradient kernels subtract. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: s Calls proc~~refresh_multilayer_derived~~CallsGraph proc~refresh_multilayer_derived refresh_multilayer_derived proc~ml_compute_reference_density ml_compute_reference_density proc~refresh_multilayer_derived->proc~ml_compute_reference_density proc~ml_equation_of_state ml_equation_of_state proc~re