layer , s % multilayer % eos , & s % grid , s % multilayer % nz_ml ) else call ml_equation_of_state ( s % multilayer % h_layer , & s % multilayer % tracers ( s % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , & s % multilayer % tracers ( s % multilayer % idx_temperature )% hTr , & s % multilayer % rho_layer , & s % multilayer % rho_0 , s % multilayer % beta_S , s % multilayer % S_ref , & s % multilayer % alpha_T , s % multilayer % T_ref , & s % grid , s % multilayer % nz_ml ) end if call ml_compute_reference_density ( s % multilayer % h_layer , s % multilayer % rho_layer , & s % multilayer % rho_ref , s % multilayer % rho_ref_dz , s % multilayer % nz_ref , & s % multilayer % rho_0 , & s % grid , s % multilayer % nz_ml ) end subroutine refresh_multilayer_derived","tags":"","url":"proc/refresh_multilayer_derived.html"},{"title":"restore_multilayer_after_restart – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine restore_multilayer_after_restart(s) A restart file restores the prognostic multilayer fields (layer\nthicknesses, momenta, tracers) but not the derived ones.  Rebuild\nthe z*-full reference levels and the density / reference-density\nprofile so a warm start sees the same state a continuous run does. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: s Calls proc~~restore_multilayer_after_restart~~CallsGraph proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart restore_multilayer_after_restart proc~multilayer_build_vcoord_reference multilayer_state_t%multilayer_build_vcoord_reference proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart->proc~multilayer_build_vcoord_reference proc~refresh_multilayer_derived refresh_multilayer_derived proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart->proc~refresh_multilayer_derived proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full proc~multilayer_build_vcoord_reference->proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full proc~ml_compute_reference_density ml_compute_reference_density proc~refresh_multilayer_derived->proc~ml_compute_reference_density proc~ml_equation_of_state ml_e