ended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Inner reduction kernel for compute_layer_sums; takes flat 3D arrays\nso the device kernel avoids the tracer-registry indirection. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: sum_h real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: sum_hS real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: sum_hT Calls proc~~compute_layer_sums_impl~~CallsGraph proc~compute_layer_sums_impl compute_layer_sums_impl local local proc~compute_layer_sums_impl->local reduce reduce proc~compute_layer_sums_impl->reduce Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~compute_layer_sums_impl~~CalledByGraph proc~compute_layer_sums_impl compute_layer_sums_impl proc~compute_layer_sums compute_layer_sums proc~compute_layer_sums->proc~compute_layer_sums_impl proc~coastal_console_stats_report coastal_console_stats_report proc~coastal_console_stats_report->proc~compute_layer_sums proc~emit_periodic_status emit_periodic_status proc~emit_periodic_status->proc~coastal_console_stats_report proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~emit_periodic_status proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: acc_S real(kind=wp), private :: acc_T real(kind=wp), private :: acc_h real(kind=wp), private :: h_ijk integer, private :: i integer, private :: i_hi integer, private :: i_lo integer, private :: j integer, private :: j_hi integer, private :: j_lo integer, private :: k integer, private :: ng Source Code subroutine compute_layer_sums_impl ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , grid , nz , & sum_h , sum_hS , sum_hT ) !! Inner reduction kernel for compute_layer_sums; takes flat 3D arrays !! so the device kernel avoids the tracer-registry indirection. use rki_grid , only : hgrid_t type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hS_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hT_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: sum_h , sum_hS , sum_hT integer :: i , j , k , ng , i_lo , i_hi , j_lo , j_hi real ( wp ) :: h_ijk , acc_h , acc_S , acc_T ng = grid % nghost i_lo = ng + 1 i_hi = grid % nx_total - ng j_lo = ng + 1 j_hi = grid % ny_total - ng acc_h = 0.0_wp acc_S = 0.0_wp acc_T = 0.0_wp ! Explicit present_or_copyin (as in compute_total_mass) so the kernel ! works in both production and unit-test contexts. do concurrent ( k = 1 : nz , j = j_lo : j_hi , i = i_lo : i_hi ) local ( h_ijk ) reduce ( + : acc_h , acc_S , acc_T ) h_ijk = h_layer ( i , j , k ) ! Skip NaN / dry-cell garbage with the same guard as mass. if ( h_ijk > 0.0_wp . and . h_ijk < 1.0e6_wp ) then acc_h = acc_h + h_ijk acc_S = acc_S + hS_layer ( i , j , k ) acc_T = acc_T + hT_layer ( i , j , k ) end if end do sum_h = acc_h sum_hS = acc_S sum_hT = acc_T end subroutine compute_layer_sums_impl","tags":"","url":"proc/compute_layer_sums_impl.html"},{"title":"remap_column – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine remap_column(method, nz, dz_old, dz_new, q_old, q_new) Dispatch to the requested remapping method. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: method REMAP_PCM, REMAP_PLM, REMAP_PPM, REMAP_PPM_H4, or REMAP_PQM integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dz_old (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dz_new (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: q_old (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: q_new (nz) Calls proc~~remap_column~~CallsGraph proc~remap_column remap_column proc~remap_column_pcm remap_column_pcm proc~remap_column->proc~remap_column_pcm proc~remap_column_plm remap_column_plm proc~remap_column->proc~remap_column_plm proc~remap_column_ppm remap_column_ppm proc~remap_column->proc~remap_column_ppm proc~remap_column_ppm_h4 remap_column_ppm_h4 proc~remap_column->proc~remap_column_ppm_h4 proc~remap_column_pqm remap_column_pqm proc~remap_column->proc~remap_column_pqm proc~remap_column_ppm->proc~remap_column_plm proc~remap_column_ppm_h4->proc~remap_column_plm proc~remap_column_pqm->proc~remap_column_ppm proc~pqm_end_value_h4 pqm_end_value_h4 proc~remap_column_p