this % hv ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % b ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % flux_h ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % flux_hu ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % flux_hv ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % mass_flux_x ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % mass_flux_y ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % h0 ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hu0 ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hv0 ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) end subroutine barotropic_state_init","tags":"","url":"proc/barotropic_state_init.html"},{"title":"si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta(mesh, nct, nco, u_edge, xmom, ymom) Least-squares reconstruction of the cell-centre transport vector\n(hu, hv) from the three edge-normal transports U_e = (hu,hv)·n_e:\n  M = sum_e len_e * n_e n_e&#94;T,   rhs = sum_e len_e * U_e * n_e,\n  (hu, hv) = M&#94;{-1} rhs.\nExact for a constant transport field (the three normals span R&#94;2 on\na non-degenerate triangle => M SPD, invertible).  The KNP seam only\nneeds a diagnostic cell momentum; eta/mass already closed on the\nedges.  Shared by the 2D step and (per layer) the ML step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total) — the explicit-shape dim. integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Edge-normal transports (m&#94;2/s), + along the outward normal. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: xmom (nct) Reconstructed cell transport vector (m&#94;2/s). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ymom (nct) Reconstructed cell transport vector (m&#94;2/s). Calls proc~~si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta~~CallsGraph proc~si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta local local proc~si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta->local He