 could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: det real(kind=wp), private :: enx real(kind=wp), private :: eny integer, private :: i integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: m11 real(kind=wp), private :: m12 real(kind=wp), private :: m22 real(kind=wp), private :: rx real(kind=wp), private :: ry real(kind=wp), private :: ue real(kind=wp), private :: wlen Source Code pure subroutine si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta ( mesh , nct , nco , u_edge , & xmom , ymom ) !! Least-squares reconstruction of the cell-centre transport vector !! (hu, hv) from the three edge-normal transports U_e = (hu,hv)·n_e: !!   M = sum_e len_e * n_e n_e&#94;T,   rhs = sum_e len_e * U_e * n_e, !!   (hu, hv) = M&#94;{-1} rhs. !! Exact for a constant transport field (the three normals span R&#94;2 on !! a non-degenerate triangle => M SPD, invertible).  The KNP seam only !! needs a diagnostic cell momentum; eta/mass already closed on the !! edges.  Shared by the 2D step and (per layer) the ML step. type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total) — the explicit-shape dim. integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) !! Edge-normal transports (m&#94;2/s), + along the outward normal. real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: xmom ( nct ), ymom ( nct ) !! Reconstructed cell transport vector (m&#94;2/s). integer :: k , i real ( wp ) :: m11 , m12 , m22 , rx , ry , det , wlen , enx , eny , ue do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) & local ( i , m11 , m12 , m22 , rx , ry , det , wlen , enx , eny , ue ) m11 = 0.0_wp m12 = 0.0_wp m22 = 0.0_wp rx = 0.0_wp ry = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI wlen = mesh % edge_len ( i , k ) enx = mesh % edge_n1 ( i , k ) eny = mesh % edge_n2 ( i , k ) ue = u_edge ( i , k ) m11 = m11 + wlen * enx * enx m12 = m12 + wlen * enx * eny m22 = m22 + wlen * eny * eny rx = rx + wlen * ue * enx ry = ry + wlen * ue * eny end do det = m11 * m22 - m12 * m12 ! det ~ 0 only for a degenerate cell (collinear edge normals) — ! excluded by the fail-loud mesh quality gate at enable_si; the ! zero fallback is 1/0 armour for a diagnostic-only quantity ! (mass/eta close on the edges regardless). if ( abs ( det ) > tiny ( 1.0_wp )) then xmom ( k ) = ( m22 * rx - m12 * ry ) / det ymom ( k ) = ( m11 * ry - m12 * rx ) / det else xmom ( k ) = 0.0_wp ymom ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if end do end subroutine si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta","tags":"","url":"proc/si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta.html"},{"title":"si_unstr_step – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine si_unstr_step(state, mesh, dt, iter_out) Advance the 2D barotropic free surface one semi-implicit step on the\ntriangulation.  Reads the frozen Hf / ghost from the current\nsurface, solves the Helmholtz eta-system, and back-substitutes the\nedge transports. iter_out returns the CG iteration count (summed\nover the Newton outers in wet/dry mode). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt integer, intent(out) :: iter_out Calls proc~~si_unstr_step~~CallsGraph proc~si_unstr_step si_unstr_step proc~si_unstr_advance si_unstr_advance proc~si_unstr_step->proc~si_unstr_advance proc~si_unstr_advance_wetdry si_unstr_advance_wetdry proc~si_unstr_step->proc~si_unstr_advance_wetdry local local proc~si_unstr_advance->local proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh proc~si_unstr_advance->proc~agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh proc~si_unstr_cg_solve si_unstr_cg_solve proc~si_unstr_advance->proc~si_unstr_cg_solve proc~si_unstr_compute_rhs si_unstr_compute_rhs proc~si_unstr_advance->proc~si_u