terface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: c real(kind=wp), private :: det real(kind=wp), private :: enx real(kind=wp), private :: eny integer, private :: i integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: m11 real(kind=wp), private :: m12 real(kind=wp), private :: m22 real(kind=wp), private :: rx real(kind=wp), private :: ry real(kind=wp), private :: ue real(kind=wp), private :: wlen Source Code pure subroutine si_unstr_edge_layers_to_cells ( mesh , nz , nct , nco , & u_edge_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer ) !! Per-layer least-squares A-grid cell-momentum reconstruction from !! the three per-layer edge-normal transports — the 2D !! `si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta`, per layer (the documented !! reconstruction compromise; restart round-trips through the cell !! layer momenta). type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nz !! Number of layers. integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_edge_layer ( nz , EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( nz , nct ), hv_layer ( nz , nct ) !! Cell layer momenta [m&#94;2/s]; owned cells overwritten. integer :: c , i , k real ( wp ) :: m11 , m12 , m22 , rx , ry , det , wlen , enx , eny , ue do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) & local ( i , k , m11 , m12 , m22 , rx , ry , det , wlen , enx , eny , ue ) ! The 2x2 normal matrix is layer-independent (mesh only). m11 = 0.0_wp m12 = 0.0_wp m22 = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI wlen = mesh % edge_len ( i , c ) enx = mesh % edge_n1 ( i , c ) eny = mesh % edge_n2 ( i , c ) m11 = m11 + wlen * enx * enx m12 = m12 + wlen * enx * eny m22 = m22 + wlen * eny * eny end do det = m11 * m22 - m12 * m12 do k = 1 , nz rx = 0.0_wp ry = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI wlen = mesh % edge_len ( i , c ) enx = mesh % edge_n1 ( i , c ) eny = mesh % edge_n2 ( i , c ) ue = u_edge_layer ( k , i , c ) rx = rx + wlen * ue * enx ry = ry + wlen * ue * eny end do ! det ~ 0 only for a degenerate cell (collinear edge normals) — ! excluded by the fail-loud mesh quality gate at enable_si; the ! zero fallback is 1/0 armour for a diagnostic-only quantity ! (mass/eta close on the edges regardless). if ( abs ( det ) > tiny ( 1.0_wp )) then hu_layer ( k , c ) = ( m22 * rx - m12 * ry ) / det hv_layer ( k , c ) = ( m11 * ry - m12 * rx ) / det else hu_layer ( k , c ) = 0.0_wp hv_layer ( k , c ) = 0.0_wp end if end do end do end subroutine si_unstr_edge_layers_to_cells","tags":"","url":"proc/si_unstr_edge_layers_to_cells.html"},{"title":"si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges(nz, nct, nco, u_edge_layer, u_n_edge, Hf_edge, theta, mass_flux_edge, u_edge) The blended column edge flux the eta update used:\n  F_e = theta sum_k u_edge_layer_k + (1-theta) U&#94;n_e\n(gated Hf > 0; dead edges exactly 0) — feeds the dsig tracer split\nso continuity and tracers share edge fluxes exactly.  Also stores\nthe NEW column-total edge transport U&#94;{n+1}_e = sum_k u_edge_layer\ninto u_edge (the 2D prognostic the next step’s (1-theta) side\nreads — the telescoped 2D back-substitution). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_edge_layer (nz,EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_n_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Saved U&#94;n edge transports (dead edges already zeroed, R3). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: mass_flux_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Blended column edge flux [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: u_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) New column-total edge transport [m&#94;2/s]. Calls proc~~si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges~~CallsGraph proc~si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges local local proc~si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges~~CalledByGraph proc~si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges proc~si_unstr_step_ml si_unstr_step_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml->proc~si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit->proc~si_unstr_step_ml proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: c real(kind=wp), private :: fsum integer, private :: i integer, private :: k Source Code pure subroutine si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges ( nz , nct , nco , u_edge_layer , & u_n_edge , Hf_edge , theta , & mass_flux_edge , u_edge ) !! The blended column edge flux the eta update used: !!   F_e = theta*sum_k u_edge_layer_k + (1-theta)*U&#94;n_e !! (gated Hf > 0; dead edges exactly 0) — feeds the dsig tracer split !! so continuity and tracers share edge fluxes exactly.  Also stores !! the NEW column-total edge transport U&#94;{n+1}_e = sum_k u_edge_layer !! into `u_edge` (the 2D prognostic the next step's (1-theta) side !! reads — the telescoped 2D back-substitution). integer , intent ( in ) :: nz !! Number of layers. integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_edge_layer ( nz , EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_n_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) !! Saved U&#94;n edge transports (dead edges already zeroed, R3). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: theta real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: mass_flux_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) !! Blended column edge flux [m&#94;2/s]. real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: u_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) !! New column-total edge transport [m&#94;2/s]. integer :: c , i , k real ( wp ) :: fsum do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) local ( i , k , fsum ) do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI if ( Hf_edge ( i , c ) > 0.0_wp ) then fsum = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz fsum = fsum + u_edge_layer ( k , i , c ) end do u_edge ( i , c ) = fsum mass_flux_edge ( i , c ) = theta * fsum + ( 1.0_wp - theta ) * u_n_edge ( i , c ) else u_edge ( i , c ) = 0.0_wp mass_flux_edge ( i , c ) = 0.0_wp end if end do end do end subroutine si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges","tags":"","url":"proc/si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges.html"},{"title":"si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges(mesh, nz, nct, nco, Gbar_cell_x, Gbar_cell_y, hu_layer0, hv_layer0, u_n_edge, eta, Hf_edge, eta_ghost_edge, u_star, g_omtheta_dt) EDGE predictor for the theta-blend RHS — ANCHOR + INCREMENT form: U _e = U&#94;n_e + 0.5 ((Gbar - X0)_c + (Gbar - X0)_nbr)·n_e\n              - g(1-theta) dt Hf*(deta&#94;n/dn) where U&#94;n_e is the PERSISTED per-edge column transport (the 2D\nprognostic — full edge-local fidelity, no cell round-trip) and Gbar - X0 is the column-integrated IMPLICIT-MIXING + explicit-\ntendency INCREMENT (X0 = sum_k hu0_k, the PRE-tendency saved\ntransport), cell-averaged onto the edge.  This differs from the\nstructured si_ml_fill_predictor_faces (which cell-averages the\nWHOLE Gbar — consistent there because the structured 2D predictor\nalso rebuilds faces from cell momenta) precisely so that the\nuniform-density inviscid limit (Gbar == X0) reduces EXACTLY to the\nedge-persistent 2D unstructured predictor — the baroclinic-limit\ngate.  Mixing / drag / wind / BPG enter through the increment with\nthe same cell-average quality as the structured path. GATED on Hf > 0 (dead edges exactly 0; U&#94;n_e already dead-zeroed,\nR3).  Dirichlet boundary edge: ghost increment = 0 (the Dirichlet\nDOF has no solved column response and no saved momentum) and the\neta gradient reads the seeded ghost surface. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Gbar_cell_x (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Gbar_cell_y (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer0 (nz,nct) PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the X0 columns). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer0 (nz,nct) PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the X0 columns). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_n_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Persisted U&#94;n edge transports (dead edges zeroed). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta (nct) eta&#94;n at circumcentres. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_ghost_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: u_star (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_omtheta_dt g (1-theta) dt. Calls proc~~si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges~~CallsGraph proc~si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges local local proc~si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges~~CalledByGraph proc~si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges proc~si_unstr_step_ml si_unstr_step_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml->proc~si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit->proc~si_unstr_step_ml proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: c real(kind=wp), private :: dgdn real(kind=wp), private :: enx real(kind=wp), private :: eny integer, private :: i real(kind=wp), private :: inc_n real(kind=wp), private :: inv_delta integer, private :: k integer, private :: kn real(kind=wp), private :: x0x_c real(kind=wp), private :: x0x_n real(kind=wp), private :: x0y_c real(kind=wp), private :: x0y_n Source Code pure subroutine si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges ( mesh , nz , nct , nco , & Gbar_cell_x , Gbar_cell_y , & hu_layer0 , hv_layer0 , & u_n_edge , eta , Hf_edge , & eta_ghost_edge , u_star , & g_omtheta_dt ) !! EDGE predictor for the theta-blend RHS — ANCHOR + INCREMENT form: !! !!   U*_e = U&#94;n_e + 0.5*((Gbar - X0)_c + (Gbar - X0)_nbr)·n_e !!               - g(1-theta)*dt*Hf*(deta&#94;n/dn) !! !! where U&#94;n_e is the PERSISTED per-edge column transport (the 2D !! prognostic — full edge-local fidelity, no cell round-trip) and !! `Gbar - X0` is the column-integrated IMPLICIT-MIXING + explicit- !! tendency INCREMENT (X0 = sum_k hu0_k, the PRE-tendency saved !! transport), cell-averaged onto the edge.  This differs from the !! structured `si_ml_fill_predictor_faces` (which cell-averages the !! WHOLE Gbar — consistent there because the structured 2D predictor !! also rebuilds faces from cell momenta) precisely so that the !! uniform-density inviscid limit (Gbar == X0) reduces EXACTLY to the !! edge-persistent 2D unstructured predictor — the baroclinic-limit !! gate.  Mixing / drag / wind / BPG enter through the increment with !! the same cell-average quality as the structured path. !! !! GATED on Hf > 0 (dead edges exactly 0; U&#94;n_e already dead-zeroed, !! R3).  Dirichlet boundary edge: ghost increment = 0 (the Dirichlet !! DOF has no solved column response and no saved momentum) and the !! eta gradient reads the seeded ghost surface. type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nz !! Number of layers. integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Gbar_cell_x ( nct ), Gbar_cell_y ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu_layer0 ( nz , nct ), hv_layer0 ( nz , nct ) !! PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the X0 columns). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_n_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) !! Persisted U&#94;n edge transports (dead edges zeroed). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta ( nct ) !! eta&#94;n at circumcentres. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_ghost_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: u_star ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: g_omtheta_dt !! g*(1-theta)*dt. integer :: c , i , k , kn real ( wp ) :: inv_delta , dgdn , inc_n , enx , eny real ( wp ) :: x0x_c , x0y_c , x0x_n , x0y_n do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) & local ( i , k , kn , inv_delta , dgdn , inc_n , enx , eny , & x0x_c , x0y_c , x0x_n , x0y_n ) ! Own-cell pre-tendency column transport X0 (hoisted out of edges). x0x_c = 0.0_wp x0y_c = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz x0x_c = x0x_c + hu_layer0 ( k , c ) x0y_c = x0y_c + hv_layer0 ( k , c ) end do do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI if ( Hf_edge ( i , c ) > 0.0_wp ) then inv_delta = 1.0_wp / max ( mesh % edge_delta ( i , c ), DELTA_EPS ) enx = mesh % edge_n1 ( i , c ) eny = mesh % edge_n2 ( i , c ) kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , c ) if ( kn > 0 ) then x0x_n = 0.0_wp x0y_n = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz x0x_n = x0x_n + hu_layer0 ( k , kn ) x0y_n = x0y_n + hv_layer0 ( k , kn ) end do inc_n = 0.5_wp * ((( Gbar_cell_x ( c ) - x0x_c ) & + ( Gbar_cell_x ( kn ) - x0x_n )) * enx & + (( Gbar_cell_y ( c ) - x0y_c ) & + ( Gbar_cell_y ( kn ) - x0y_n )) * eny ) dgdn = Hf_edge ( i , c ) * ( eta ( kn ) - eta ( c )) * inv_delta else ! Dirichlet edge: ghost increment 0; gradient vs ghost eta. inc_n = 0.5_wp * (( Gbar_cell_x ( c ) - x0x_c ) * enx & + ( Gbar_cell_y ( c ) - x0y_c ) * eny ) dgdn = Hf_edge ( i , c ) * ( eta_ghost_edge ( i , c ) - eta ( c )) * inv_delta end if u_star ( i , c ) = u_n_edge ( i , c ) + inc_n - g_omtheta_dt * dgdn else u_star ( i , c ) = 0.0_wp end if end do end do end subroutine si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges","tags":"","url":"proc/si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges.html"},{"title":"si_unstr_recover_edge_layers – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine si_unstr_recover_edge_layers(mesh, nz, nct, nco, h_layer, hu_layer0, hv_layer0, dsig, bed, g_col_u, g_col_v, r_col, eta_n, eta_np1, Hf_edge, eta_ghost_edge, dt, theta, u_edge_layer) Recover the per-layer EDGE transports after the eta solve — the\nstructured si_recover_face_transports in the ANCHOR + INCREMENT\nform matching si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges .  Per edge i of cell\nc (gated Hf > 0; dead edges stay exactly 0) and layer k: anchor_k = u_edge_layer(k,i,c)                (the PERSISTED\n             per-layer edge transport — read before overwrite;\n             own-entry read/write only, race-free)\n  inc_k = 0.5 ((h_k G_k - hu0_k)_c·n_e + (h_k G_k - hu0_k)_nbr·n_e)\n  hhf_k = 0.5 (h_k(c) R_k(c) + h_k(nbr) R_k(nbr))          (<= 0)\n  grad_blend = ((1-theta) deta&#94;n + theta deta&#94;{n+1})/delta_e\n  u_edge_layer(k,i,c) = anchor_k + inc_k + g dt grad_blend*hhf_k MASS-CONSISTENCY INVARIANT: sum_k anchor_k = U&#94;n_e (the persisted\ncolumn total), sum_k inc_k = the predictor’s increment, and\nsum_k hhf_k = -Hf, so the column sum telescopes EXACTLY to\nU _e - g theta dt Hf grad(eta&#94;{n+1}) — the 2D back-substitution.\nIn the uniform-density inviscid limit inc_k = 0 and\nhhf_k = -dsig_k Hf, so every layer is EXACTLY dsig_k times the 2D\nedge update (the baroclinic-limit gate); sheared columns keep\ntheir per-layer structure in the anchor (no cell-average\nflattening — the reason for this form over the structured pure\ncell-average, whose 2D twin averages cells too). h_layer MUST\nbe the SAME time-n field that fed the tridiagonal. DIRICHLET boundary edge (the structured estuary-mouth lesson,\napplied inline): the ghost is a Dirichlet DOF with NO solved\ncolumn response and no saved momentum, so ghost increment = 0,\nghost R = -1 exactly, and the ghost per-layer thickness is the\nsigma split of the prescribed column h_ghost = max(eta_bc - b_c,\n0): h_k_ghost = dsig_k h_ghost.  Then sum_k hhf = -0.5 (Hhat_c +\nh_ghost) = -Hf exactly — the recovered open-edge transport matches\nthe Helmholtz flux, so continuity and tracers share the mouth flux\nand uniform tracers stay invariant (the freshening-defect guard). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,nct) Layer thicknesses [m] at time n (the tridiagonal’s field). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer0 (nz,nct) PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the increment reference). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer0 (nz,nct) PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the increment reference). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig (nz) Sigma layer fractions (sum = 1). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bed (nct) Bed elevation [m] (the Dirichlet ghost column depth). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_col_u (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_col_v (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r_col (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_n (nct) Old-time surface eta&#94;n at circumcentres. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_np1 (nct) New-time surface eta&#94;{n+1} (the CG solution). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_ghost_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Seeded Dirichlet ghost surface (frozen over the step — used for\nBOTH the eta&#94;n and eta&#94;{n+1} gradients, as on the structured\npath where the ghost persists across the interior-only CG). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: u_edge_layer (nz,EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Per-layer edge transports [m&#94;2/s], + outward normal: the\npersisted anchor on entry, the recovered U&#94;{n+1} on exit. Calls proc~~si_unstr_recover_edge_layers~~CallsGraph proc~si_unstr_recover_edge_layers si_unstr_recover_edge_layers local local proc~si_unstr_recover_edge_layers->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~si_unstr_recover_edge_layers~~CalledByGraph proc~si_unstr_recover_edge_layers si_unstr_recover_edge_layers proc~si_unstr_step_ml si_unstr_step_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml->proc~si_unstr_recover_edge_layers proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit->proc~si_unstr_step_ml proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: c real(kind=wp), private :: enx real(kind=wp), private :: eny real(kind=wp), private :: grad_blend real(kind=wp), private :: h_ghost real(kind=wp), private :: hhf real(kind=wp), private :: hk_ghost integer, private :: i real(kind=wp), private :: inc_k real(kind=wp), private :: inv_delta integer, private :: k integer, private :: kn Source Code pure subroutine si_unstr_recover_edge_layers ( mesh , nz , nct , nco , h_layer , & hu_layer0 , hv_layer0 , dsig , & bed , g_col_u , g_col_v , & r_col , eta_n , eta_np1 , Hf_edge , & eta_ghost_edge , dt , theta , & u_edge_layer ) !! Recover the per-layer EDGE transports after the eta solve — the !! structured `si_recover_face_transports` in the ANCHOR + INCREMENT !! form matching `si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges`.  Per edge i of cell !! c (gated Hf > 0; dead edges stay exactly 0) and layer k: !! !!   anchor_k = u_edge_layer(k,i,c)                (the PERSISTED !!              per-layer edge transport — read before overwrite; !!              own-entry read/write only, race-free) !!   inc_k = 0.5*((h_k*G_k - hu0_k)_c·n_e + (h_k*G_k - hu0_k)_nbr·n_e) !!   hhf_k = 0.5*(h_k(c)*R_k(c) + h_k(nbr)*R_k(nbr))          (<= 0) !!   grad_blend = ((1-theta)*deta&#94;n + theta*deta&#94;{n+1})/delta_e !!   u_edge_layer(k,i,c) = anchor_k + inc_k + g*dt*grad_blend*hhf_k !! !! MASS-CONSISTENCY INVARIANT: sum_k anchor_k = U&#94;n_e (the persisted !! column total), sum_k inc_k = the predictor's increment, and !! sum_k hhf_k = -Hf, so the column sum telescopes EXACTLY to !! U*_e - g*theta*dt*Hf*grad(eta&#94;{n+1}) — the 2D back-substitution. !! In the uniform-density inviscid limit inc_k = 0 and !! hhf_k = -dsig_k*Hf, so every layer is EXACTLY dsig_k times the 2D !! edge update (the baroclinic-limit gate); sheared columns keep !! their per-layer structure in the anchor (no cell-average !! flattening — the reason for this form over the structured pure !! cell-average, whose 2D twin averages cells too).  `h_layer` MUST !! be the SAME time-n field that fed the tridiagonal. !! !! DIRICHLET boundary edge (the structured estuary-mouth lesson, !! applied inline): the ghost is a Dirichlet DOF with NO solved !! column response and no saved momentum, so ghost increment = 0, !! ghost R = -1 exactly, and the ghost per-layer thickness is the !! sigma split of the prescribed column h_ghost = max(eta_bc - b_c, !! 0): h_k_ghost = dsig_k*h_ghost.  Then sum_k hhf = -0.5*(Hhat_c + !! h_ghost) = -Hf exactly — the recovered open-edge transport matches !! the Helmholtz flux, so continuity and tracers share the mouth flux !! and uniform tracers stay invariant (the freshening-defect guard). type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nz !! Number of layers. integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( nz , nct ) !! Layer thicknesses [m] at time n (the tridiagonal's field). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu_layer0 ( nz , nct ), hv_layer0 ( nz , nct ) !! PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the increment reference). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dsig ( nz ) !! Sigma layer fractions (sum = 1). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: bed ( nct ) !! Bed elevation [m] (the Dirichlet ghost column depth). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: g_col_u ( nz , nct ), g_col_v ( nz , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r_col ( nz , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_n ( nct ) !! Old-time surface eta&#94;n at circumcentres. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_np1 ( nct ) !! New-time surface eta&#94;{n+1} (the CG solution). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_ghost_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) !! Seeded Dirichlet ghost surface (frozen over the step — used for !! BOTH the eta&#94;n and eta&#94;{n+1} gradients, as on the structured !! path where the ghost persists across the interior-only CG). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt , theta real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: u_edge_layer ( nz , EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) !! Per-layer edge transports [m&#94;2/s], + outward normal: the !! persisted anchor on entry, the recovered U&#94;{n+1} on exit. integer :: c , i , k , kn real ( wp ) :: inv_delta , grad_blend , inc_k , hhf , enx , eny real ( wp ) :: h_ghost , hk_ghost do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) & local ( i , k , kn , inv_delta , grad_blend , inc_k , hhf , enx , eny , & h_ghost , hk_ghost ) do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI if ( Hf_edge ( i , c ) > 0.0_wp ) then inv_delta = 1.0_wp / max ( mesh % edge_delta ( i , c ), DELTA_EPS ) enx = mesh % edge_n1 ( i , c ) eny = mesh % edge_n2 ( i , c ) kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , c ) if ( kn > 0 ) then grad_blend = (( 1.0_wp - theta ) * ( eta_n ( kn ) - eta_n ( c )) & + theta * ( eta_np1 ( kn ) - eta_np1 ( c ))) * inv_delta do k = 1 , nz inc_k = 0.5_wp * (( h_layer ( k , c ) * g_col_u ( k , c ) - hu_layer0 ( k , c ) & + h_layer ( k , kn ) * g_col_u ( k , kn ) - hu_layer0 ( k , kn )) * enx & + ( h_layer ( k , c ) * g_col_v ( k , c ) - hv_layer0 ( k , c ) & + h_layer ( k , kn ) * g_col_v ( k , kn ) - hv_layer0 ( k , kn )) * eny ) hhf = 0.5_wp * ( h_layer ( k , c ) * r_col ( k , c ) & + h_layer ( k , kn ) * r_col ( k , kn )) u_edge_layer ( k , i , c ) = u_edge_layer ( k , i , c ) + inc_k & + GRAVITY * dt * grad_blend * hhf end do else ! Dirichlet edge: frozen ghost eta for both time levels; ! ghost increment = 0, ghost R = -1, h_k = dsig_k*h_ghost. grad_blend = (( 1.0_wp - theta ) * ( eta_ghost_edge ( i , c ) - eta_n ( c )) & + theta * ( eta_ghost_edge ( i , c ) - eta_np1 ( c ))) * inv_delta h_ghost = max ( eta_ghost_edge ( i , c ) - bed ( c ), 0.0_wp ) do k = 1 , nz hk_ghost = dsig ( k ) * h_ghost inc_k = 0.5_wp * (( h_layer ( k , c ) * g_col_u ( k , c ) - hu_layer0 ( k , c )) * enx & + ( h_layer ( k , c ) * g_col_v ( k , c ) - hv_layer0 ( k , c )) * eny ) hhf = 0.5_wp * ( h_layer ( k , c ) * r_col ( k , c ) & + hk_ghost * ( - 1.0_wp )) u_edge_layer ( k , i , c ) = u_edge_layer ( k , i , c ) + inc_k & + GRAVITY * dt * grad_blend * hhf end do end if else do k = 1 , nz u_edge_layer ( k , i , c ) = 0.0_wp end do end if end do end do end subroutine si_unstr_recover_edge_layers","tags":"","url":"proc/si_unstr_recover_edge_layers.html"},{"title":"si_unstr_update_thickness_ml – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine si_unstr_update_thickness_ml(nz, nct, nco, eta, bed, dsig, stage, height, h_layer) h&#94;{n+1} = max(eta&#94;{n+1} - b, 0) (exactly the edge-flux continuity\nupdate) + the sigma slaving h_layer_k = dsig_k*h, and the stage\nrefresh stage = eta. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bed (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: stage (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: height (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h_layer (nz,nct) Calls proc~~si_unstr_update_thickness_ml~~CallsGraph proc~si_unstr_update_thickness_ml si_unstr_update_thickness_ml local local proc~si_unstr_update_thickness_ml->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~si_unstr_update_thickness_ml~~CalledByGraph proc~si_unstr_update_thickness_ml si_unstr_update_thickness_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml si_unstr_step_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml->proc~si_unstr_update_thickness_ml proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit->proc~si_unstr_step_ml proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_