se: rki_ml_keps S2 / N2 / dz_if / a / b / c / rhs / cp — written\n    at ni = nz + 1 . rki_si_unstr_closures kapS / kapT —\n    written at nz + 1 . rki_ml_tracers ml_settling_tracer — the augmented settling\n    column is nz + 1 deep, and it calls remap_column_ppm(nz+1, …) ,\n    so the remap kernel’s own z_old(0:NZ_STACK_MAX) / q_L / q_R / q6 must also hold nz + 1 . rki_ocean_diag_fills z_iface — needs n_bin + 2 , which the n_bin <= NZ_STACK_MAX - 1 output-level guard bounds by nz + 1 . NOT 2*nz + 2 : the Redi neutral-surface locals that motivated the\n256 bump are declared 2*NZ_STACK_MAX + 2 and so scale with the\nconstant — they need only NZ_STACK_MAX >= nz . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Return Value integer Called by proc~~nz_stack_required~~CalledByGraph proc~nz_stack_required nz_stack_required proc~nz_stack_is_sufficient nz_stack_is_sufficient proc~nz_stack_is_sufficient->proc~nz_stack_required proc~validate_config validate_config proc~validate_config->proc~nz_stack_required proc~validate_config->proc~nz_stack_is_sufficient proc~vcoord_init vcoord_t%vcoord_init proc~vcoord_init->proc~nz_stack_required proc~vcoord_init->proc~nz_stack_is_sufficient proc~multilayer_state_init multilayer_state_t%multilayer_state_init proc~multilayer_state_init->proc~vcoord_init proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~validate_config proc~rki_unstr_set_vcoord rki_unstr_set_vcoord proc~rki_unstr_set_vcoord->proc~vcoord_init proc~unstr_multilayer_init unstr_multilayer_state_t%unstr_multilayer_init proc~unstr_multilayer_init->proc~vcoord_init proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function nz_stack_required ( nz ) result ( req ) !! Smallest `NZ_STACK_MAX` that safely covers a run of `nz` layers. !! !! `nz + 1`.  Derived from a survey of every `NZ_STACK_MAX`-dimensioned !! array in the tree; the binding consumers are the ones that index a !! plainly-`NZ_STACK_MAX`-declared array to `nz+1` rather than the !! `NZ_STACK_MAX+1` an interface array would use: !! !!   * `rki_ml_keps` `S2`/`N2`/`dz_if`/`a`/`b`/`c`/`rhs`/`cp` — written !!     at `ni = nz + 1`. !!   * `rki_si_unstr_closures` `kapS`/`kapT` — !!     written at `nz + 1`. !!   * `rki_ml_tracers` `ml_settling_tracer` — the augmented settling !!     column is `nz + 1` deep, and it calls `remap_column_ppm(nz+1, …)`, !!     so the remap kernel's own `z_old(0:NZ_STACK_MAX)` / `q_L`/`q_R`/`q6` !!     must also hold `nz + 1`. !!   * `rki_ocean_diag_fills` `z_iface` — needs `n_bin + 2`, which the !!     `n_bin <= NZ_STACK_MAX - 1` output-level guard bounds by `nz + 1`. !! !! NOT `2*nz + 2`: the Redi neutral-surface locals that motivated the !! 256 bump are declared `2*NZ_STACK_MAX + 2` and so scale with the !! constant — they need only `NZ_STACK_MAX >= nz`. integer , intent ( in ) :: nz integer :: req req = nz + 1 end function nz_stack_required","tags":"","url":"proc/nz_stack_required.html"},{"title":"restart_read_unstr – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine restart_read