spatches to the per-backend helper !! for the coastal HLL/HLLC + KNP dynamical core.  Any non-coastal !! `sim_type` is rejected fail-loud by `validate_config`; guard !! again here so a programmatic caller that skips validation can !! never silently fall through to the wrong dynamical core. type ( config_t ), intent ( inout ) :: cfg if ( trim ( cfg % sim_type ) /= \"coastal\" ) then call logger % error ( \"driver_run: sim_type='\" // trim ( cfg % sim_type ) // & \"' is not supported by this build (coastal only)\" ) error stop \"driver_run: unsupported sim_type\" end if if ( trim ( cfg % grid_type ) == \"unstructured\" ) then call driver_run_coastal_unstr ( cfg ) else call driver_run_coastal ( cfg ) end if end subroutine driver_run","tags":"","url":"proc/driver_run.html"},{"title":"driver_run_coastal – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine driver_run_coastal(cfg) Run the full lifecycle for the structured coastal regime. Allocates and initialises state, configures BCs / forcing / nesting / output / gauges, places\ndata on GPU, runs the time-stepping loop with periodic\ndiagnostics and output, then finalises (D2H, final snapshot,\ndiagnostics, profiler, resource cleanup). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg Calls proc~~driver_run_coastal~~CallsGraph proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal get_elapsed_time get_elapsed_time proc~driver_run_coastal->get_elapsed_time get_knowledge get_knowledge proc~driver_run_coastal->get_knowledge info info proc~driver_run_coastal->info proc~compute_total_mass compute_total_mass proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~compute_total_mass proc~emit_periodic_status emit_periodic_status proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~emit_periodic_status proc~finalize_output finalize_output proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~finalize_output proc~flush_restart flush_restart proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_restart proc~flush_snapshot flush_snapshot proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_snapshot proc~forcing_destroy forcing_dest