_ml->proc~si_unstr_wetdry_fill_bsub proc~ssp_combine_unstr->reduce proc~ssp_combine_unstr->local proc~move_level move_level proc~trim_levels->proc~move_level Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~driver_run_coastal_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: depth real(kind=wp), private :: elapsed real(kind=wp), private :: lx real(kind=wp), private :: ly type( mesh_unstr_t ), private :: mesh integer, private :: ncells integer, private :: nz logical, private :: si_ok type( unstr_state_t ), private :: state integer, private, allocatable :: tri_v (:,:) real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: vert_x (:) real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: vert_y (:) type(timer_type), private :: wall_timer Source Code subroutine driver_run_coastal_unstr ( cfg ) !! End-to-end unstructured coastal run on a native regular-triangulation !! mesh (Python-free).  Routed from `driver_run` when !! `grid_type==\"unstructured\"`; reuses `&grid_nml` (nx,ny,dx,dy) for the !! mesh and `nz_layers` for the column.  Flat bed, lake at rest, !! horizontally-uniform IC. type ( config_t ), intent ( inout ) :: cfg type ( mesh_unstr_t ) :: mesh type ( unstr_state_t ) :: state type ( timer_type ) :: wall_timer real ( wp ), allocatable :: vert_x (:), vert_y (:) integer , allocatable :: tri_v (:, :) integer :: ncells , nz real ( wp ) :: lx , ly , depth , elapsed logical :: si_ok nz = max ( cfg % nz_layers , 1 ) lx = real ( cfg % nx , wp ) * cfg % dx ly = real ( cfg % ny , wp ) * cfg % dy depth = cfg % h0 ! flat bed at the configured still-water depth (h0) ! The semi-implicit TPFA operator needs an acute-Delaunay mesh: the ! plain right-triangle split has coincident circumcentres per quad ! (edge_delta = 0) and the SI quality gate rejects it.  The explicit ! path keeps the regular split (bit-identity for existing runs). if ( parse_time_scheme ( cfg % time_scheme ) == TIME_SEMI_IMPLICIT ) then call gen_delaunay_triangulation ( cfg % nx , cfg % ny , lx , ly , vert_x , vert_y , tri_v ) else call gen_regular_triangulation ( cfg % nx , cfg % ny , lx , ly , vert_x , vert_y , tri_v ) end if call mesh_unstr_init_from_triangles ( mesh , vert_x , vert_y , tri_v ) ncells = mesh % ncells_owned call logger % info ( \"Coastal unstructured run: \" // to_string ( cfg % nx ) // \" x \" // & to_string ( cfg % ny ) // \" regular mesh (\" // & to_string ( 2 * cfg % nx * cfg % ny ) // \" triangles), nz = \" // & to_string ( nz )) ! Vertical coordinate is set before init -- it drives the multilayer ! vcoord setup inside state_unstr_init. state % multilayer % vcoord % coord_type = parse_vcoord_type ( cfg % vcoord_type ) ! Closure knobs that GATE allocations inside state_unstr_init must be ! set BEFORE it (the SI k-eps Picard save slots allocate only when ! vmix_use_keps .and. keps_si_picard > 1 — a post-init sync would ! leave them unallocated and the Picard loop would hit unallocated ! arrays).  Mirrors the structured init_from_config ordering. state % multilayer % vmix_use_keps = cfg % vmix_use_keps state % multilayer % vmix_use_kpp = cfg % vmix_use_kpp state % multilayer % keps_si_picard = cfg % keps_si_picard call state_unstr_init ( state , mesh , nz_ml = nz ) ! Physics from the namelist: the structured coastal knobs mapped onto the ! unstructured state (EOS + tracers + vmix + lateral mixing + forcing). state % cfl = cfg % cfl state % time_scheme = parse_time_scheme ( cfg % time_scheme ) ! The selectable explicit integrator (euler/rk3/rk43) is wired into ! the 2D barotropic path only; multilayer keeps SSP-RK2 (per-layer ! BPG / mixing stages sit between the Euler update and the combine). ! Semi-implicit is exempt: the SI step has its own 3D column solve. if ( state % time_scheme /= TIME_RK2 . and . state % time_scheme /= TIME_SEMI_IMPLICIT & . and . state % use_multilayer ) then error stop \"time_scheme: euler/rk3/rk43 require the 2D barotropic \" // & \"unstructured path (nz_layers <= 1); multilayer runs use rk2.\" end if ! Semi-implicit (Casulli) mode: run the fail-loud TPFA mesh-quality ! gate and allocate the si slot now — after state_unstr_init (nz_ml ! known) and before state_unstr_enter_data (the slot maps with the ! state).  The knob envelope (dt_fixed > 0, wall/tidal/clamped edges, ! single rank, precond) was already validated at configure time. if ( state % time_scheme == TIME_SEMI_IMPLICIT ) then call state_unstr_enable_si ( state , mesh , & parse_si_precond_unstr ( cfg % si_precond ), & cfg % si_rtol , cfg % dt_fixed , si_ok , & wetdry = cfg % si_wetdry , n_sub = cfg % si_wetdry_nsub , & bsub_fill = parse_si_bsub_fill ( cfg % si_wetdry_bsub_fill )) if (. not . si_ok ) then error stop \"driver: mesh failed the semi-implicit TPFA quality \" // & \"gate (non-Delaunay / obtuse cell pairs); refine the mesh or \" // & \"use the explicit path.\" end if end if state % multilayer % rho_0 = cfg % rho_0 state % multilayer % alpha_T = cfg % alpha_T state % multilayer % beta_S = cfg % beta_S ! Coastal EOS selector (&tracer_nml eos_form) — mirrors the ! structured wiring in rki_state: default \"linear\" keeps the ! legacy kernel; \"wright\" / \"roquet_spv\" opt in to the shared ! nonlinear EOS (handle is a flat POD, no device map needed). block use rki_ml_eos , only : ml_parse_eos_form call ml_parse_eos_form ( cfg % eos_form , & state % multilayer % eos_use_shared , & state % multilayer % eos % variant ) end block state % multilayer % eos % rho0 = cfg % rho_0 state % multilayer % eos % S_ref = cfg % S_ref state % multilayer % eos % T_ref = cfg % T_ref state % multilayer % eos % alpha_T = cfg % alpha_T state % multilayer % eos % beta_S = cfg % beta_S state % multilayer % eos % is_init = . true . state % multilayer % initial_salinity = cfg % initial_salinity state % multilayer % S_init_surface = cfg % S_init_surface state % multilayer % S_init_bottom = cfg % S_init_bottom state % multilayer % initial_temperature = cfg % initial_temperature state % multilayer % T_init_surface = cfg % T_init_surface state % multilayer % T_init_bottom = cfg % T_init_bottom state % multilayer % kappa_S_bg = cfg % kappa_S_bg state % multilayer % kappa_T_bg = cfg % kappa_T_bg state % multilayer % use_ppm_tracer = cfg % use_ppm_tracer ! (vmix_use_keps / vmix_use_kpp / keps_si_picard synced BEFORE ! state_unstr_init above — they gate init allocations.) state % multilayer % keps_stability = keps_stability_from_string ( cfg % keps_stability ) state % multilayer % smagorinsky_cs = cfg % smagorinsky_cs state % multilayer % evap_mass_sink = cfg % evap_mass_sink state % multilayer % evap_latent_cooling = cfg % evap_latent_cooling state % multilayer % hdiff_kappa = cfg % hdiff_kappa state % barotropic % manning_n = cfg % manning_n state % barotropic % wind_tau_x = cfg % wind_stress_x state % barotropic % wind_tau_y = cfg % wind_stress_y state % barotropic % coriolis_f = cfg % coriolis_f ! Flat bed, lake at rest. state % barotropic % bed_cv = - depth state % barotropic % stage_cv = 0.0_wp state % barotropic % xmom_cv = 0.0_wp state % barotropic % ymom_cv = 0.0_wp state % barotropic % height_cv = state % barotropic % stage_cv - state % barotropic % bed_cv call mesh_unstr_enter_data ( mesh ) call profiler_start ( \"unstr_enter_data\" ) call state_unstr_enter_data ( state ) call profiler_stop ( \"unstr_enter_data\" ) call solver_unstr_init_multilayer ( state , mesh ) call logger % info ( \"Starting time evolution: target \" // to_string ( cfg % t_end ) // \" s\" ) call wall_timer % start () call solver_unstr_advance ( state , mesh , cfg % t_end ) call wall_timer % stop () elapsed = real ( wall_timer % get_elapsed_time (), wp ) call profiler_start ( \"unstr_exit_data\" ) call state_unstr_exit_data ( state ) call profiler_stop ( \"unstr_exit_data\" ) call mesh_unstr_exit_data ( mesh ) call logger % info ( \"Unstructured run complete: \" // to_string ( state % step_count ) // & \" steps in \" // to_string ( elapsed ) // \" s\" ) call report_throughput ( real ( ncells , wp ), state % step_count , elapsed ) call state_unstr_destroy ( state ) call mesh_unstr_destroy ( mesh ) end subroutine driver_run_coastal_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/driver_run_coastal_unstr.html"},{"title":"emit_periodic_status – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine emit_periodic_status(state, cfg, n_steps, t_current, wall_elapsed, console_stats) Periodic status: the slim Step / t / dt / Wall / Remaining\nrow, then the shared MOM6-style [stats] block (Mass / Salt / Heat drift + energy), computed +\nall-reduced by coastal_console_stats_report . state i