that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine emit_periodic_status ( state , cfg , n_steps , t_current , & wall_elapsed , console_stats ) !! Periodic status: the slim Step / t / dt / Wall / Remaining !! row, then the shared MOM6-style !! `[stats]` block (Mass / Salt / Heat drift + energy), computed + !! all-reduced by `coastal_console_stats_report`.  `state` is !! `intent(inout)` because the device reductions require it. type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg integer , intent ( in ) :: n_steps real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t_current real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: wall_elapsed type ( console_stats_t ), intent ( inout ) :: console_stats call print_status_line ( n_steps , t_current , state % dt , & wall_elapsed , cfg % t_end ) call coastal_console_stats_report ( console_stats , state , state % dt , & t_current , n_steps ) end subroutine emit_periodic_status","tags":"","url":"proc/emit_periodic_status.html"},{"title":"finalize_output – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine finalize_output(state, ostate, t_current, use_netcdf_output) End-of-run output: write the final snapshot and close the file. state has already been pulled D->H by the caller. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( output_state_t ), intent(inout) :: ostate real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t_current logical, intent(in) :: use_netcdf_output Calls proc~~finalize_output~~CallsGraph proc~finalize_output finalize_output proc~output_close output_close proc~finalize_output->proc~output_close proc~output_write_snapshot output_write_snapshot proc~finalize_output->proc~output_write_snapshot info info proc~output_close->info proc~nc_close nc_close proc~output_close->proc~nc_c