ce Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine flush_snapshot ( state , ostate , cfg , t_current , next_output_time , & n_snapshots ) !! Flush one NetCDF snapshot mid-run: D->H, write locally, H->D, bump !! the snapshot counter + cadence cursor.  Caller !! gates on `use_netcdf_output .and. t_current >= next_output_time`. type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( output_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: ostate type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t_current real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: next_output_time integer , intent ( inout ) :: n_snapshots call profiler_start ( \"sync_output\" ) call solver_exit_data ( state ) call output_write_snapshot ( ostate , state , t_current ) call solver_enter_data ( state ) call profiler_stop ( \"sync_output\" ) n_snapshots = n_snapshots + 1 call logger % info ( \"  >> Snapshot \" // to_string ( n_snapshots ) // & \" at t = \" // to_string ( t_current ) // \" s\" ) next_output_time = next_output_time + cfg % output_interval end subroutine flush_snapshot","tags":"","url":"proc/flush_snapshot.html"},{"title":"init_bc_chapman – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine init_bc_chapman(state) Allocate and initialise Chapman BC arrays from state Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Calls proc~~init_bc_chapman~~CallsGraph proc~init_bc_chapman init_bc_chapman proc~bc_init_chapman bc_init_chapman proc~init_bc_chapman->proc~bc_init_chap