Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~init_local_state~~CalledByGraph proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, private :: loaded_ml Source Code subroutine init_local_state ( cfg , state , t_current , total_mass_initial ) !! Build the ready-to-run state: allocate, load bathymetry, read a !! restart or set the initial conditions, log the run header and the !! bathymetry diagnostics, and fill the ghost bathymetry. type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: t_current real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: total_mass_initial logical :: loaded_ml t_current = 0.0_wp total_mass_initial = 0.0_wp call state % init_from_config ( cfg ) ! Load bathymetry from file or use flat bottom if ( len_trim ( cfg % bathymetry_file ) > 0 ) then call load_bathymetry ( trim ( cfg % bathymetry_file ), state ) end if ! Load restart file or set up initial conditions if ( len_trim ( cfg % restart_file ) > 0 ) then call restart_read ( trim ( cfg % restart_file ), state , t_current , & loaded_multilayer = loaded_ml ) call logger % info ( \"Warm start from restart at t = \" // to_string ( t_current ) // \" s\" ) if ( state % use_multilayer ) then if ( loaded_ml ) then call restore_multilayer_after_restart ( state ) else ! Barotropic-only restart under a multilayer config: lay the ! layers out from the restored barotropic state. call init_multilayer_from_barotropic ( state , cfg ) end if end if else call init_from_config ( state , cfg ) end if total_mass_initial = compute_total_mass ( state ) call diagnose_bathymetry ( state , cfg ) call log_run_header ( cfg , total_mass_initial , state ) ! Extrapolate domain-edge ghost bathymetry call fill_bathymetry_ghosts ( state ) end subroutine init_local_state","tags":"","url":"proc/init_local_state.html"},{"title":"log_final_diagnostics – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine log_final_diagnostics(state, cfg, n_steps, wall_elapsed, wall_total, mcells_per_sec, total_mass_final, total_mass_initial, use_netcdf_output) Rank-0 end-of-run summary: step / time / throughput / mass-change log\nlines, the ASCII fallback dump when NetCDF output is off, and the\nmerge hint.  Caller stops the wall timer and passes its elapsed time. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(in) :: state type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg integer, intent(in) :: n_steps real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wall_elapsed real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wall_total real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mcells_per_sec real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: total_mass_final real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: total_mass_initial logical, intent(in) :: use_netcdf_output Calls proc~~log_final_diagnostics~~CallsGraph proc~log_final_diagnostics log_final_diagnostics info info proc~log_final_diagnostics->info proc~write_ascii_output write_ascii_output proc~log_final_diagnostics->proc~write_ascii_output to_string to_string proc~log_final_diagnostics->to_string proc~write_ascii_output->info error error proc~write_ascii_output->error warning warning proc~write_ascii_output->warning Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~log_final_diagnostics~~CalledByGraph proc~log_final_diagnostics log_final_diagnostics proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~log_final_diagnostics proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine log_final_diagnostics ( state , cfg , n_steps , wall_elapsed , wall_total , & mcells_per_sec , total_mass_final , & total_mass_initial , use_netcdf_output ) !! Rank-0 end-of-run summary: step / time / throughput / mass-change log !! lines, the ASCII fallback dump when NetCDF output is off, and the !! merge hint.  Caller stops the wall timer and passes its elapsed time. type ( state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg integer , intent ( in ) :: n_steps real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: wall_elapsed real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: wall_total real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mcells_per_sec real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: total_mass_final real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: total_mass_initial logical , intent ( in ) :: use_netcdf_output call logger % info ( \"Total steps: \" // to_string ( n_steps )) call logger % info ( \"Solver time: \" // to_string ( wall_elapsed ) // \" s\" ) call logger % info ( \"Total wall time: \" // to_string ( wall_total ) // \" s\" ) call logger % info ( \"Mcells/s: \" // to_string ( mcells_per_sec )) call logger % info ( \"Final mass: \" // to_string ( total_mass_final )) call logger % info ( \"Mass change: \" // & to_string ( abs ( total_mass_final - total_mass_initial ))) ! ASCII fallback output if (. not . use_netcdf_output ) then call write_ascii_output ( state , cfg % output_dir ) end if end subroutine log_final_diagnostics","tags":"","url":"proc/log_final_diagnostics.html"},{"title":"log_run_header – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine log_run_header(cfg, total_mass_initial, state) Startup summary: banner + grid / spacing / layers / duration /\nmass / fixed-dt note / counted memory\nfootprint.  Pure logger output. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: total_mass_initial type( state_t ), intent(in) :: state State the footprint is counted from. Calls proc~~log_run_header~~CallsGraph proc~log_run_header log_run_header info info proc~log_run_header->info proc~mem_log_computed_budget mem_log_computed_budget proc~log_run_header->proc~mem_log_computed_budget proc~mem_log_computed_line mem_log_computed_line proc~log_run_header->proc~mem_log_computed_line proc~print_banner print_banner proc~log_run_header->proc~print_banner proc~state_bytes state_t%state_bytes proc~log_run_header->proc~state_bytes to_char_count to_char_count proc~log_run_header->to_char_count to_string to_string proc~log_run_header->to_string warning warning proc~log_run_header->warning proc~mem_log_computed_budget->info proc~mem_format_bytes mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_computed_budget->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_computed_line->info proc~mem_log_computed_line->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~print_banner->info get_knowledge get_knowledge proc~print_banner->get_knowledge interface~arr_bytes arr_bytes proc~state_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~barotropic_state_bytes barotropic_state_t%barotropic_state_bytes proc~state_bytes->proc~barotropic_state_bytes proc~arr_bytes_i1 arr_bytes_i1 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_i1 proc~arr_bytes_i2 arr_bytes_i2 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_i2 proc~arr_bytes_i3 arr_bytes_i3 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_i3 proc~arr_bytes_l1 arr_bytes_l1 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_l1 proc~arr_bytes_l2 arr_bytes_l2 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_l2 proc~arr_bytes_l3 arr_bytes_l3 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_l3 proc~arr_bytes_r1 arr_bytes_r1 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_r1 proc~arr_bytes_r2 arr_bytes_r2 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_r2 proc~arr_bytes_r3 arr_bytes_r3 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_r3 proc~arr_bytes_r4 arr_bytes_r4 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_r4 proc~barotropic_state_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~two_dp two_dp proc~mem_format_bytes->proc~two_dp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~log_run_header~~CalledByGraph proc~log_run_header log_run_header proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~log_run_header proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=32), private :: mass_str Source Code subroutine log_run_header ( cfg , total_mass_initial , state ) !! Startup summary: banner + grid / spacing / layers / duration / !! mass / fixed-dt note / counted memory !! footprint.  Pure logger output. type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: total_mass_initial type ( state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state !! State the footprint is counted from. character ( len = 32 ) :: mass_str call print_banner ( cfg % sim_type ) call logger % info ( \"\" ) call logger % info ( \"  Grid:     \" // to_string ( cfg % nx ) // \" x \" // to_string ( cfg % ny ) // & \" (\" // to_char_count ( int ( cfg % nx , int64 ) * int ( cfg % ny , int64 )) // \")\" ) call logger % info ( \"  Spacing:  dx = \" // to_string ( cfg % dx ) // \" m, dy = \" // & to_string ( cfg % dy ) // \" m\" ) if ( cfg % use_multilayer ) then call logger % info ( \"  Layers:   \" // to_string ( cfg % nz_layers ) // \" (multilayer hydrostatic)\" ) else if ( cfg % use_nonhydrostatic ) then call logger % info ( \"  Layers:   \" // to_string ( cfg % nz_layers ) // \" (non-hydrostatic)\" ) else call logger % info ( \"  Layers:   1 (2D barotropic)\" ) end if call logger % info ( \"  Duration: \" // to_string ( cfg % t_end ) // \" s\" ) write ( mass_str , \"(ES14.6)\" ) total_mass_initial call logger % info ( \"  Mass:     \" // trim ( adjustl ( mass_str ))) if ( cfg % dt_fixed > 0.0_wp ) then call logger % warning ( \"  Fixed dt: \" // to_string ( cfg % dt_fixed ) // \" s (CFL disabled)\" ) end if ! Counted state-array footprint (exact allocatable sum; gated-off ! sub-slots count 0, so the breakdown reflects conditional allocation). block integer ( int64 ) :: b_total , b_baro , b_forcing b_total = state % bytes () b_baro = state % barotropic % bytes () b_forcing = state % forcing % bytes () call mem_log_computed_budget ( \"coastal state\" , b_total ) call mem_log_computed_line ( \"barotropic\" , b_baro ) call mem_log_computed_line ( \"surface forcing\" , b_forcing ) if ( state % use_multilayer ) then call mem_log_computed_line ( \"multilayer + tracers\" , state % multilayer % bytes ()) end if if ( state % use_nonhydrostatic ) then call mem_log_computed_line ( \"non-hydrostatic\" , state % nh % bytes ()) end if end block call logger % info ( \"\" ) end subroutine log_run_header","tags":"","url":"proc/log_run_header.html"},{"title":"log_time_evolution_banner – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine log_time_evolution_banner(cfg, use_netcdf_output) “Starting time evolution” banner + status-table header.  On\nnon-GPU builds, detects the multicore thread count from ACC_NUM_CORES\n(then OMP_NUM_THREADS). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg logical, intent(in) :: use_netcdf_output Calls proc~~log_time_evolution_banner~~CallsGraph proc~log_time_evolution_banner log_time_evolution_banner info info proc~log_time_evolution_banner->info to_string to_string proc~log_time_evolution_banner->to_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~log_time_evolution_banner~~CalledByGraph proc~log_time_evolution_banner log_time_evolution_banner proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~log_time_evolution_banner proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine log_time_evolution_banner ( cfg , use_netcdf_output ) !! \"Starting time evolution\" banner + status-table header.  On !! non-GPU builds, detects the multicore thread count from ACC_NUM_CORES !! (then OMP_NUM_THREADS). type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg logical , intent ( in ) :: use_netcdf_output call logger % info ( \"\" ) #ifdef RAKALI_GPU_OFFLOAD call logger % info ( \"Starting time evolution: target \" // to_string ( cfg % t_end ) // & \" s, GPU\" ) #else block integer :: n_threads character ( len = 64 ) :: env_val character ( len = 128 ) :: ios_msg integer :: env_len , env_stat , ios n_threads = 0 ! NVHPC -stdpar=multicore / -acc=multicore reads ACC_NUM_CORES first, ! then falls back to OMP_NUM_THREADS. Gcc -ftree-parallelize-loops ! bakes the count in at compile time (RAKALI_NPROC) and ignores both. call get_environment_variable ( \"ACC_NUM_CORES\" , env_val , env_len , env_stat ) if ( env_stat == 0 . and . env_len > 0 ) then read ( env_val , * , iostat = ios , iomsg = ios_msg ) n_threads if ( ios /= 0 ) n_threads = 0 end if if ( n_threads <= 0 ) then call get_environment_variable ( \"OMP_NUM_THREADS\" , env_val , env_len , env_stat ) if ( env_stat == 0 . and . env_len > 0 ) then read ( env_val , * , iostat = ios , iomsg = ios_msg ) n_threads if ( ios /= 0 ) n_threads = 0 end if end if if ( n_threads > 1 ) then call logger % info ( \"Starting time evolution: target \" // to_string ( cfg % t_end ) // & \" s, \" // to_string ( n_threads ) // \" CPU threads\" ) else call logger % info ( \"Starting time evolution: target \" // to_string ( cfg % t_end ) // & \" s, CPU\" ) end if end block #endif if ( use_netcdf_output ) then call logger % info ( \"  Output every \" // to_string ( cfg % output_interval ) // \" s\" ) end if call logger % info ( \"\" ) ! Slim table; the conserved quantities are ! reported below each row in the shared [stats] block. call logger % info ( \"     Step         t (s)         dt (s)     Wall (s)  Remaining (s)\" ) call logger % info ( \"  -------  ------------  ------------  -----------  -------------\" ) end subroutine log_time_evolution_banner","tags":"","url":"proc/log_time_evolution_banner.html"},{"title":"print_status_line – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine print_status_line(step, t, dt, wall, t_end, mass, mean_S, mean_T) Print a table-formatted status line with estimated remaining time.\nWhen mean_S / mean_T are present, two extra columns are written\nbetween Mass and Wall so the multilayer header lines up. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: step real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wall real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t_end real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: mass real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: mean_S real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: mean_T Calls proc~~print_status_line~~CallsGraph proc~print_status_line print_status_line info info proc~print_status_line->info Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~print_status_line~~CalledByGraph proc~print_status_line print_status_line proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~print_status_line proc~emit_periodic_status emit_periodic_status proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~emit_periodic_status proc~emit_periodic_status->proc~print_status_line proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=256), private :: line real(kind=wp), private :: remaining Source Code subroutine print_status_line ( step , t , dt , wall , t_end , mass , mean_S , mean_T ) !! Print a table-formatted status line with estimated remaining time. !! When mean_S / mean_T are present, two extra columns are written !! between Mass and Wall so the multilayer header lines up. integer , intent ( in ) :: step real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t , dt , wall , t_end real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: mass real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: mean_S , mean_T real ( wp ) :: remaining character ( len = 256 ) :: line if ( t > 0.0_wp ) then remaining = wall * ( t_end - t ) / t else remaining = 0.0_wp end if if ( present ( mass ) . and . present ( mean_S ) . and . present ( mean_T )) then write ( line , \"(I9,F14.2,F14.4,ES13.3,F13.4,F13.4,F13.2,F15.2)\" ) & step , t , dt , mass , mean_S , mean_T , wall , remaining else if ( present ( mass )) then write ( line , \"(I9,F14.2,F14.4,ES13.3,F13.2,F15.2)\" ) & step , t , dt , mass , wall , remaining else write ( line , \"(I9,F14.2,F14.4,13X,F13.2,F15.2)\" ) & step , t , dt , wall , remaining end if call logger % info ( \"  \" // trim ( line )) end subroutine print_status_line","tags":"","url":"proc/print_status_line.html"},{"title":"report_throughput – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine report_throughput(n_cells, n_steps, elapsed, total_mcells) Log horizontal throughput (cells x steps / wall time).  Throughput is\nhorizontal cells x steps, NOT x nz (the codebase convention).\nOptionally returns the figure so a caller can thread it into a later\nsummary. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: n_cells integer, intent(in) :: n_steps real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: elapsed real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: total_mcells Calls proc~~report_throughput~~CallsGraph proc~report_throughput report_throughput info info proc~report_throughput->info to_string to_string proc~report_throughput->to_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~report_throughput~~CalledByGraph proc~report_throughput report_throughput proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~report_throughput proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~report_throughput proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: total Source Code subroutine report_throughput ( n_cells , n_steps , elapsed , total_mcells ) !! Log horizontal throughput (cells x steps / wall time).  Throughput is !! horizontal cells x steps, NOT x nz (the codebase convention). !! Optionally returns the figure so a caller can thread it into a later !! summary. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: n_cells integer , intent ( in ) :: n_steps real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: elapsed real ( wp ), intent ( out ), optional :: total_mcells real ( wp ) :: total total = 0.0_wp if ( elapsed > 0.0_wp ) then total = n_cells * real ( n_steps , wp ) / elapsed / 1.0e6_wp end if if ( present ( total_mcells )) total_mcells = total call logger % info ( \"  throughput: \" // to_string ( total ) // \" Mcells/s\" ) end subroutine report_throughput","tags":"","url":"proc/report_throughput.html"},{"title":"write_gauges – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine write_gauges(gauges, state, cfg, t_current, next_gauge_time) Pull the gauge cells D->H and append one gauge time-series record,\nadvancing the cadence cursor.  Caller gates on gauges%active and the\ngauge cadence. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( gauge_output_t ), intent(inout) :: gauges type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t_current real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: next_gauge_time Calls proc~~write_gauges~~CallsGraph proc~write_gauges write_gauges proc~gauges_write gauges_write proc~write_gauges->proc~gauges_write nf90_put_var nf90_put_var proc~gauges_write->nf90_put_var nf90_sync nf90_sync proc~gauges_write->nf90_sync proc~nc_check nc_check proc~gauges_write->proc~nc_check error error proc~nc_check->error nf90_strerror nf90_strerror proc~nc_check->nf90_strerror Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~write_gauges~~CalledByGraph proc~write_gauges write_gauges proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~write_gauges proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: g integer, private :: i0 integer, private :: j0 Source Code subroutine write_gauges ( gauges , state , cfg , t_current , next_gauge_time ) !! Pull the gauge cells D->H and append one gauge time-series record, !! advancing the cadence cursor.  Caller gates on gauges%active and the !! gauge cadence. type ( gauge_output_t ), intent ( inout ) :: gauges type ( state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t_current real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: next_gauge_time integer :: g , i0 , j0 do g = 1 , gauges % n_local i0 = gauges % ix0 ( g ) j0 = gauges % iy0 ( g ) !$acc update self(state%barotropic%h(i0:i0 + 1, j0:j0 + 1)) !$acc update self(state%barotropic%hu(i0:i0 + 1, j0:j0 + 1)) !$acc update self(state%barotropic%hv(i0:i0 + 1, j0:j0 + 1)) end do call gauges_write ( gauges , state , t_current ) if ( cfg % gauge_output_interval > 0.0_wp ) then next_gauge_time = next_gauge_time + cfg % gauge_output_interval end if end subroutine write_gauges","tags":"","url":"proc/write_gauges.html"},{"title":"nml_dirname – Rakali","text":"public pure function nml_dirname(path) result(dir) Directory part of path with a trailing ‘/’, or ‘’ if none. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~nml_dirname~~CalledByGraph proc~nml_dirname nml_dirname proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~nml_dirname proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: i Source Code pure function nml_dirname ( path ) result ( dir ) !! Directory part of `path` with a trailing '/', or '' if none. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path character ( len = :), allocatable :: dir integer :: i dir = \"\" do i = len_trim ( path ), 1 , - 1 if ( path ( i : i ) == \"/\" ) then dir = path ( 1 : i ) return end if end do end function nml_dirname","tags":"","url":"proc/nml_dirname.html"},{"title":"eos_density_point – Rakali","text":"public pure function eos_density_point(eos, T, S, p) result(rho) Scalar density evaluation at a point — the same formulas the\n3D eos_*_impl kernels apply, exposed for finite-difference\nverification of eos_specvol_derivs and for host-side\ndiagnostics.  Takes the shared eos_t handle by value.\nThe else is unreachable-by-contract (see eos_validate ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eos_t ), intent(in) :: eos real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: T real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: S real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: p Return Value real(kind=wp) Calls proc~~eos_density_point~~CallsGraph proc~eos_density_point eos_density_point proc~roquet_spv_point roquet_spv_point proc~eos_density_point->proc~roquet_spv_point Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~eos_density_point~~CalledByGraph proc~eos_density_point eos_density_point proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr->proc~eos_density_point proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr proc~si_unstr_step_ml si_unstr_step_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_finalize rki_unstr_finalize proc~rki_unstr_finalize->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit->proc~si_unstr_step_ml proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: T_sq real(kind=wp), private :: alpha_0 real(kind=wp), private :: d_dum1 real(kind=wp), private :: d_dum2 real(kind=wp), private :: lambda real(kind=wp), private :: p_0 real(kind=wp), private :: p_plus_p0 real(kind=wp), private :: sv_roq Source Code pure function eos_density_point ( eos , T , S , p ) result ( rho ) !! Scalar density evaluation at a point — the same formulas the !! 3D `eos_*_impl` kernels apply, exposed for finite-difference !! verification of `eos_specvol_derivs` and for host-side !! diagnostics.  Takes the shared `eos_t` handle by value. !! The `else` is unreachable-by-contract (see !! `eos_validate`). !$acc routine seq type ( eos_t ), intent ( in ) :: eos real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: T , S , p real ( wp ) :: rho real ( wp ) :: T_sq , alpha_0 , p_0 , lambda , p_plus_p0 real ( wp ) :: sv_roq , d_dum1 , d_dum2 if ( eos % variant == EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV ) then call roquet_spv_point ( T , S , p , sv_roq , d_dum1 , d_dum2 ) rho = 1.0_wp / sv_roq else if ( eos % variant == EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 ) then T_sq = T * T alpha_0 = WRIGHT_A0 + WRIGHT_A1 * T + WRIGHT_A2 * S p_0 = WRIGHT_B0 + WRIGHT_B1 * T + WRIGHT_B2 * T_sq + WRIGHT_B3 * T_sq * T + & WRIGHT_B4 * S + WRIGHT_B5 * S * T lambda = WRIGHT_C0 + WRIGHT_C1 * T + WRIGHT_C2 * T_sq + WRIGHT_C3 * T_sq * T + & WRIGHT_C4 * S + WRIGHT_C5 * S * T p_plus_p0 = p + p_0 rho = p_plus_p0 / ( lambda + alpha_0 * p_plus_p0 ) else rho = eos % rho0 + eos % beta_S * ( S - eos % S_ref ) - eos % alpha_T * ( T - eos % T_ref ) end if end function eos_density_point","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_density_point.html"},{"title":"eos_freezing_point – Rakali","text":"public pure elemental function eos_freezing_point(eos, S, p) result(T_f) Seawater freezing point T_f (degC) at salinity S and pressure p — the ocean-side prerequisite for the sea-ice port\n(PLAN_SEA_ICE.md, PR 1).  Same point-function style as eos_density_point (flat-POD eos_t by value, device-\ncallable), plus elemental so callers can evaluate whole\nsalinity arrays in one reference. v1 is the SIS2/MOM6 LINEAR liquidus for EVERY eos%variant : T_f = TFR_S_COEFF·S + TFR_P_COEFF·p (μ = −0.054 °C per g/kg, MOM6 TFREEZE_FORM = \"LINEAR\" — MOM6\nkeeps the linear form as its default even under the Wright /\nTEOS-10 density branches, so applying it across variants is\nparity, not a shortcut.)  A TEOS-10 t_freezing(SA, p) polynomial slots in later as an eos%variant ==\nEOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV / EOS_VARIANT_TEOS10 branch, mirroring\nthe dispatch in eos_density_point . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eos_t ), intent(in) :: eos Shared EOS handle (variant tag), by value.  Read for the\nfuture per-variant dispatch; every variant takes the linear\nbranch in v1. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: S Salinity (PSU / g/kg). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: p Pressure (Pa), hydrostatic surface-relative (0 at the\nsurface — the frazil kernel’s use case). Return Value real(kind=wp) Source Code pure elemental function eos_freezing_point ( eos , S , p ) result ( T_f ) !! Seawater freezing point T_f (degC) at salinity `S` and pressure !! `p` — the ocean-side prerequisite for the sea-ice port !! (PLAN_SEA_ICE.md, PR 1).  Same point-function style as !! `eos_density_point` (flat-POD `eos_t` by value, device- !! callable), plus `elemental` so callers can evaluate whole !! salinity arrays in one reference. !! !! v1 is the SIS2/MOM6 LINEAR liquidus for EVERY `eos%variant`: !! !!   T_f = TFR_S_COEFF·S + TFR_P_COEFF·p !! !! (μ = −0.054 °C per g/kg, MOM6 `TFREEZE_FORM = \"LINEAR\"` — MOM6 !! keeps the linear form as its default even under the Wright / !! TEOS-10 density branches, so applying it across variants is !! parity, not a shortcut.)  A TEOS-10 `t_freezing(SA, p)` !! polynomial slots in later as an `eos%variant == !! EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV / EOS_VARIANT_TEOS10` branch, mirroring !! the dispatch in `eos_density_point`. !$acc routine seq type ( eos_t ), intent ( in ) :: eos !! Shared EOS handle (variant tag), by value.  Read for the !! future per-variant dispatch; every variant takes the linear !! branch in v1. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: S !! Salinity (PSU / g/kg). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p !! Pressure (Pa), hydrostatic surface-relative (0 at the !! surface — the frazil kernel's use case). real ( wp ) :: T_f ! Variant dispatch seam: v1 = the same linear liquidus for all ! variants (see docstring), so `eos%variant` is read only by the ! future TEOS-10 branch — which slots in as !   if (eos%variant == EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV) then ... else ! without touching this default expression. T_f = TFR_S_COEFF * S + TFR_P_COEFF * p end function eos_freezing_point","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_freezing_point.html"},{"title":"parse_eos_variant – Rakali","text":"public pure function parse_eos_variant(name) result(code) Translate a &ocean_eos_nml eos=... string into an EOS_VARIANT_* code.  Unrecognised values fall back to EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR (the default = bit-identical to runs that\nomit the knob).  Membership in the device-callable set is\nenforced separately by eos_validate at configure time. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Return Value integer Source Code pure function parse_eos_variant ( name ) result ( code ) !! Translate a `&ocean_eos_nml eos=...` string into an !! `EOS_VARIANT_*` code.  Unrecognised values fall back to !! `EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR` (the default = bit-identical to runs that !! omit the knob).  Membership in the device-callable set is !! enforced separately by `eos_validate` at configure time. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name integer :: code select case ( trim ( adjustl ( name ))) case ( \"linear\" , \"LINEAR\" ) code = EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR case ( \"wright\" , \"WRIGHT\" , \"wright_97\" , \"wright97\" ) code = EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 case ( \"roquet_spv\" , \"ROQUET_SPV\" , \"roquet\" , \"ROQUET\" ) code = EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV case ( \"teos10\" , \"TEOS10\" , \"teos-10\" ) code = EOS_VARIANT_TEOS10 case default code = EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR end select end function parse_eos_variant","tags":"","url":"proc/parse_eos_variant.html"},{"title":"eos_compute_arrays – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine eos_compute_arrays(eos, h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer, nx, ny, nz) Variant dispatch on bare 3D arrays — the regime-agnostic body of ocean_eos_compute (the ocean C-grid shim, hosted in rki_ocean_eos_compute ).  That shim forwards the C-grid\nmultilayer state’s registry arrays here; the coastal opt-in path\n( rki_ml_eos::ml_equation_of_state_shared , &tracer_nml\neos_form ) forwards the A-grid multilayer arrays — the two\nregimes share one EOS through this single dispatch.  All impls\nevaluate at the fixed reference pressure eos%p_ref (default 0\n⇒ surface/potential density) with the H_VANISHED vanishing-\nlayer fallback to eos%rho0 . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eos_t ), intent(in) :: eos real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_layer (nx,ny,nz) integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz Calls proc~~eos_compute_arrays~~CallsGraph proc~eos_compute_arrays eos_compute_arrays proc~eos_linear_impl eos_linear_impl proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_linear_impl proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl eos_roquet_spv_impl proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl proc~eos_wright_impl eos_wright_impl proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_wright_impl local local proc~eos_linear_impl->local proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl->local proc~roquet_spv_point roquet_spv_point proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl->proc~roquet_spv_point proc~eos_wright_impl->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~eos_compute_arrays~~CalledByGraph proc~eos_compute_arrays eos_compute_arrays proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared->proc~eos_compute_arrays proc~refresh_multilayer_derived refresh_multilayer_derived proc~refresh_multilayer_derived->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->proc~refresh_multilayer_derived proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart restore_multilayer_after_restart proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart->proc~refresh_multilayer_derived proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~api_init_multilayer api_init_multilayer proc~api_init_multilayer->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~init_from_config init_from_config proc~init_from_config->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_local_state->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_local_state->proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal proc~rki_finalize rki_finalize proc~rki_finalize->proc~api_init_multilayer proc~rki_finalize->proc~init_from_config Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine eos_compute_arrays ( eos , h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , & rho_layer , nx , ny , nz ) !! Variant dispatch on bare 3D arrays — the regime-agnostic body of !! `ocean_eos_compute` (the ocean C-grid shim, hosted in !! `rki_ocean_eos_compute`).  That shim forwards the C-grid !! multilayer state's registry arrays here; the coastal opt-in path !! (`rki_ml_eos::ml_equation_of_state_shared`, `&tracer_nml !! eos_form`) forwards the A-grid multilayer arrays — the two !! regimes share one EOS through this single dispatch.  All impls !! evaluate at the fixed reference pressure `eos%p_ref` (default 0 !! ⇒ surface/potential density) with the `H_VANISHED` vanishing- !! layer fallback to `eos%rho0`. type ( eos_t ), intent ( in ) :: eos integer , intent ( in ) :: nx , ny , nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hS_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hT_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) select case ( eos % variant ) case ( EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR ) call eos_linear_impl ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , rho_layer , & eos % rho0 , eos % beta_S , eos % S_ref , & eos % alpha_T , eos % T_ref , & nx , ny , nz ) case ( EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 ) call eos_wright_impl ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , rho_layer , & eos % rho0 , eos % p_ref , & nx , ny , nz ) case ( EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV ) call eos_roquet_spv_impl ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , rho_layer , & eos % rho0 , eos % p_ref , & nx , ny , nz ) case default error stop \"eos_compute_arrays: unknown eos%variant\" end select end subroutine eos_compute_arrays","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_compute_arrays.html"},{"title":"eos_specvol_derivs – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine eos_specvol_derivs(eos, T, S, p, dsv_dt, dsv_ds) Analytic specific-volume sensitivities dSV/dT and dSV/dS\n(SV = 1/rho) at a point.  Needed by the EPBL energy\nbookkeeping (pressure-weighted PE-per-unit-tracer-change\nweights) and kappa-shear buoyancy — dSV/dX = -(1/rho&#94;2)\nd(rho)/dX. Takes the shared eos_t handle BY VALUE (flat POD,\nno allocatable) so the device copy is register-resident.\nThe select case (eos%variant) body is warp-uniform (one\nvariant per run) — ~free. Linear variant: rho = rho0 + beta_S (S - S_ref) - alpha_T\n(T - T_ref) gives constant dSV/dT = +alpha_T/rho0&#94;2 and\ndSV/dS = -beta_S/rho0&#94;2 (evaluated at the reference density,\nconsistent with the Boussinesq weights that consume them). Wright (1997) variant: SV = alpha_0(T,S) + lambda(T,S)/P with\nP = p + p_0(T,S), differentiable in closed form from the\nTable A1 polynomials:\n  dSV/dX = d(alpha_0)/dX + d(lambda)/dX / P\n           - lambda * d(p_0)/dX / P&#94;2.\nThe else is unreachable-by-contract: eos_validate guarantees eos%variant is in the device-callable set at\nconfigure time (device code cannot error stop ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eos_t ), intent(in) :: eos Shared EOS handle (variant + scalar coeffs), by value. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: T In-situ temperature (degC) and salinity (PSU). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: S In-situ temperature (degC) and salinity (PSU). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: p Pressure (Pa), hydrostatic surface-relative. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: dsv_dt dSV/dT (m&#94;3/kg/degC); > 0 for warm-expands water. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: dsv_ds dSV/dS (m&#94;3/kg/PSU); < 0 (salt contracts). Calls proc~~eos_specvol_derivs~~CallsGraph proc~eos_specvol_derivs eos_specvol_derivs proc~roquet_spv_point roquet_spv_point proc~eos_specvol_derivs->proc~roquet_spv_point Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: T_sq real(kind=wp), private :: big_p real(kind=wp), private :: dlam_ds real(kind=wp), private :: dlam_dt real(kind=wp), private :: dp0_ds real(kind=wp), private :: dp0_dt real(kind=wp), private :: inv_p real(kind=wp), private :: inv_p2 real(kind=wp), private :: lambda real(kind=wp), private :: p_0 real(kind=wp), private :: sv_roq Source Code pure subroutine eos_specvol_derivs ( eos , T , S , p , dsv_dt , dsv_ds ) !! Analytic specific-volume sensitivities dSV/dT and dSV/dS !! (SV = 1/rho) at a point.  Needed by the EPBL energy !! bookkeeping (pressure-weighted PE-per-unit-tracer-change !! weights) and kappa-shear buoyancy — dSV/dX = -(1/rho&#94;2) !! d(rho)/dX. !! !! Takes the shared `eos_t` handle BY VALUE (flat POD, !! no allocatable) so the device copy is register-resident. !! The `select case (eos%variant)` body is warp-uniform (one !! variant per run) — ~free. !! !! Linear variant: rho = rho0 + beta_S (S - S_ref) - alpha_T !! (T - T_ref) gives constant dSV/dT = +alpha_T/rho0&#94;2 and !! dSV/dS = -beta_S/rho0&#94;2 (evaluated at the reference density, !! consistent with the Boussinesq weights that consume them). !! !! Wright (1997) variant: SV = alpha_0(T,S) + lambda(T,S)/P with !! P = p + p_0(T,S), differentiable in closed form from the !! Table A1 polynomials: !!   dSV/dX = d(alpha_0)/dX + d(lambda)/dX / P !!            - lambda * d(p_0)/dX / P&#94;2. !! The `else` is unreachable-by-contract: `eos_validate` !! guarantees `eos%variant` is in the device-callable set at !! configure time (device code cannot `error stop`). !$acc routine seq type ( eos_t ), intent ( in ) :: eos !! Shared EOS handle (variant + scalar coeffs), by value. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: T , S !! In-situ temperature (degC) and salinity (PSU). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p !! Pressure (Pa), hydrostatic surface-relative. real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: dsv_dt !! dSV/dT (m&#94;3/kg/degC); > 0 for warm-expands water. real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: dsv_ds !! dSV/dS (m&#94;3/kg/PSU); < 0 (salt contracts). real ( wp ) :: T_sq , p_0 , lambda , big_p , inv_p , inv_p2 real ( wp ) :: dp0_dt , dlam_dt , dp0_ds , dlam_ds real ( wp ) :: sv_roq if ( eos % variant == EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV ) then call roquet_spv_point ( T , S , p , sv_roq , dsv_dt , dsv_ds ) else if ( eos % variant == EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 ) then T_sq = T * T p_0 = WRIGHT_B0 + WRIGHT_B1 * T + WRIGHT_B2 * T_sq + WRIGHT_B3 * T_sq * T + & WRIGHT_B4 * S + WRIGHT_B5 * S * T lambda = WRIGHT_C0 + WRIGHT_C1 * T + WRIGHT_C2 * T_sq + WRIGHT_C3 * T_sq * T + & WRIGHT_C4 * S + WRIGHT_C5 * S * T dp0_dt = WRIGHT_B1 + 2.0_wp * WRIGHT_B2 * T + 3.0_wp * WRIGHT_B3 * T_sq + & WRIGHT_B5 * S dlam_dt = WRIGHT_C1 + 2.0_wp * WRIGHT_C2 * T + 3.0_wp * WRIGHT_C3 * T_sq + & WRIGHT_C5 * S dp0_ds = WRIGHT_B4 + WRIGHT_B5 * T dlam_ds = WRIGHT_C4 + WRIGHT_C5 * T big_p = p + p_0 inv_p = 1.0_wp / big_p inv_p2 = inv_p * inv_p dsv_dt = WRIGHT_A1 + dlam_dt * inv_p - lambda * dp0_dt * inv_p2 dsv_ds = WRIGHT_A2 + dlam_ds * inv_p - lambda * dp0_ds * inv_p2 else dsv_dt = eos % alpha_T / ( eos % rho0 * eos % rho0 ) dsv_ds = - eos % beta_S / ( eos % rho0 * eos % rho0 ) end if end subroutine eos_specvol_derivs","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_specvol_derivs.html"},{"title":"eos_validate – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine eos_validate(eos) Uses pic_logger proc~~eos_validate~~UsesGraph proc~eos_validate eos_validate pic_logger pic_logger proc~eos_validate->pic_logger Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Host-side fail-loud gate over the device-supported variant\nset.  Device point routines ( !$acc routine seq ) cannot error stop , so membership in the device-callable set is\nguaranteed HERE at configure time; the device else branch\nis then unreachable-by-contract. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( eos_t ), intent(in) :: eos Calls proc~~eos_validate~~CallsGraph proc~eos_validate eos_validate error error proc~eos_validate->error Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine eos_validate ( eos ) !! Host-side fail-loud gate over the device-supported variant !! set.  Device point routines (`!$acc routine seq`) cannot !! `error stop`, so membership in the device-callable set is !! guaranteed HERE at configure time; the device `else` branch !! is then unreachable-by-contract. use pic_logger , only : global_logger type ( eos_t ), intent ( in ) :: eos select case ( eos % variant ) case ( EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR , EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 , EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV ) ! Device-callable — OK. case ( EOS_VARIANT_TEOS10 ) call global_logger % error ( \"ocean_eos: TEOS-10 variant is not \" // & \"yet device-callable\" ) error stop \"ocean_eos: TEOS-10 not yet device-callable\" case default call global_logger % error ( \"ocean_eos: unknown eos%variant\" ) error stop \"ocean_eos: unknown eos%variant\" end select end subroutine eos_validate","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_validate.html"},{"title":"eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl(h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer_seed, p_edge_out, rho_insitu_out, gravity, rho_0, nx, ny, nz) FV-Wright PGF column sweep.  Top-down per-column traversal\nthat simultaneously produces the hydrostatic pressure stack p_edge_out and the in-situ density rho_insitu_out at each\nlayer centre. For each layer k from the surface (k=nz) down to the bed\n(k=1) we use a single Picard step: Seed the half-layer pressure with the surface-evaluated\n     density rho_layer_seed (= ms%rho_layer, the EOS output\n     at p_ref=0):\n        p_centre_seed = p_above + 0.5 * g * rho_seed * h Re-evaluate Wright at the seed pressure:\n        rho_insitu(k) = ρ(T_k, S_k, p_centre_seed) Accumulate the bottom edge of layer k using the in-situ\n     density:\n        p_edge(k) = p_above + g * rho_insitu(k) * h This is one Picard iteration of the implicit\n  p_centre(k) = p_above + 0.5 g ρ(T, S, p_centre(k))*h.\nFor ocean conditions (Δρ along path << ρ_0) one iteration is\nwithin ~1e-5 of the converged value. rho_layer_seed must be ms%rho_layer from ocean_eos_compute with EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 —\nthe seed is the full nonlinear ρ at p_ref=0, not a Boussinesq\nconstant; this avoids a second Picard iteration in 99% of\ncases. Vanishing-layer fallback: if h_layer(k) <= 0 the Wright eval\nis skipped and rho_insitu(k) = rho_0 — matches the existing eos_wright_impl defensive branch. Loop order: outer do concurrent (j, i) for GPU parallelism;\ninner serial k loop for the column recurrence (same shape as\nthe existing PGF Pass 1 + vdiff column kernels). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer_seed (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: p_edge_out (nx,ny,nz+1) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_insitu_out (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: gravity real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz Calls proc~~eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl~~CallsGraph proc~eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl local local proc~eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: S_k real(kind=wp), private :: T_cu real(kind=wp), private :: T_k real(kind=wp), private :: T_sq real(kind=wp), private :: alpha_0 real(kind=wp), private :: denom integer, private :: i real(kind=wp), private :: inv_h integer, private :: j integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: lambda real(kind=wp), private :: p_0 real(kind=wp), private :: p_above real(kind=wp), private :: p_centre_seed real(kind=wp), private :: p_plus_p0 real(kind=wp), private :: rho_k Source Code pure subroutine eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , & rho_layer_seed , p_edge_out , & rho_insitu_out , gravity , rho_0 , & nx , ny , nz ) !! FV-Wright PGF column sweep.  Top-down per-column traversal !! that simultaneously produces the hydrostatic pressure stack !! `p_edge_out` and the in-situ density `rho_insitu_out` at each !! layer centre. !! !! For each layer k from the surface (k=nz) down to the bed !! (k=1) we use a single Picard step: !! !!   1. Seed the half-layer pressure with the surface-evaluated !!      density `rho_layer_seed` (= ms%rho_layer, the EOS output !!      at p_ref=0): !!         p_centre_seed = p_above + 0.5 * g * rho_seed * h !!   2. Re-evaluate Wright at the seed pressure: !!         rho_insitu(k) = ρ(T_k, S_k, p_centre_seed) !!   3. Accumulate the bottom edge of layer k using the in-situ !!      density: !!         p_edge(k) = p_above + g * rho_insitu(k) * h !! !! This is one Picard iteration of the implicit !!   p_centre(k) = p_above + 0.5*g*ρ(T, S, p_centre(k))*h. !! For ocean conditions (Δρ along path << ρ_0) one iteration is !! within ~1e-5 of the converged value. !! !! `rho_layer_seed` must be `ms%rho_layer` from !! `ocean_eos_compute` with `EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97` — !! the seed is the *full* nonlinear ρ at p_ref=0, not a Boussinesq !! constant; this avoids a second Picard iteration in 99% of !! cases. !! !! Vanishing-layer fallback: if `h_layer(k) <= 0` the Wright eval !! is skipped and `rho_insitu(k) = rho_0` — matches the existing !! `eos_wright_impl` defensive branch. !! !! Loop order: outer `do concurrent (j, i)` for GPU parallelism; !! inner serial k loop for the column recurrence (same shape as !! the existing PGF Pass 1 + vdiff column kernels). integer , intent ( in ) :: nx , ny , nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hS_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hT_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho_layer_seed ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: p_edge_out ( nx , ny , nz + 1 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_insitu_out ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: gravity , rho_0 integer :: i , j , k real ( wp ) :: p_above , p_centre_seed , inv_h , S_k , T_k , T_sq , T_cu real ( wp ) :: alpha_0 , p_0 , lambda , p_plus_p0 , denom , rho_k do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx ) & local ( k , p_above , p_centre_seed , inv_h , S_k , T_k , T_sq , T_cu , & alpha_0 , p_0 , lambda , p_plus_p0 , denom , rho_k ) p_edge_out ( i , j , nz + 1 ) = 0.0_wp p_above = 0.0_wp do k = nz , 1 , - 1 if ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) > H_VANISHED ) then inv_h = 1.0_wp / h_layer ( i , j , k ) S_k = hS_layer ( i , j , k ) * inv_h T_k = hT_layer ( i , j , k ) * inv_h T_sq = T_k * T_k T_cu = T_sq * T_k p_centre_seed = p_above + 0.5_wp * gravity * rho_layer_seed ( i , j , k ) * h_layer ( i , j , k ) alpha_0 = WRIGHT_A0 + WRIGHT_A1 * T_k + WRIGHT_A2 * S_k p_0 = WRIGHT_B0 + WRIGHT_B1 * T_k + WRIGHT_B2 * T_sq + WRIGHT_B3 * T_cu + & WRIGHT_B4 * S_k + WRIGHT_B5 * S_k * T_k lambda = WRIGHT_C0 + WRIGHT_C1 * T_k + WRIGHT_C2 * T_sq + WRIGHT_C3 * T_cu + & WRIGHT_C4 * S_k + WRIGHT_C5 * S_k * T_k p_plus_p0 = p_centre_seed + p_0 denom = lambda + alpha_0 * p_plus_p0 rho_k = p_plus_p0 / denom else rho_k = rho_0 end if rho_insitu_out ( i , j , k ) = rho_k p_above = p_above + gravity * rho_k * h_layer ( i , j , k ) p_edge_out ( i , j , k ) = p_above end do end do end subroutine eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_wright_pgf_column_sweep_impl.html"},{"title":"eos_destroy – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine eos_destroy(this) Type Bound eos_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( eos_t ), intent(inout) :: this Source Code subroutine eos_destroy ( this ) class ( eos_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this this % is_init = . false . end subroutine eos_destroy","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_destroy.html"},{"title":"eos_init – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine eos_init(this, grid) Type Bound eos_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( eos_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid Source Code subroutine eos_init ( this , grid ) class ( eos_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid if (. false .) this % rho0 = real ( grid % nx_total , wp ) ! NOTE: the device-callable-variant gate is NOT run here anymore. ! `eos%variant` is still at its default at `init` time; the config ! knob (`&ocean_eos_nml eos=...`) is applied later, in ! `configure_ocean_pgf`, which calls `eos_validate` POST-config ! (so it sees the real variant) plus the FV_WRIGHT+Roquet fail-loud. this % is_init = . true . end subroutine eos_init","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_init.html"},{"title":"eos_linear_impl – Rakali","text":"private pure subroutine eos_linear_impl(h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer, rho_0, beta_S, S_ref, alpha_T, T_ref, nx, ny, nz) Linear two-tracer EOS, flat-impl form: rho_k = rho_0 + beta_S * (S_k - S_ref) - alpha_T * (T_k - T_ref) where S_k = hS_k / h_k, T_k = hT_k / h_k. beta_S and alpha_T are pre-multiplied sensitivities in kg/m³ per unit\nS / T — standard seawater values are 0.78 and 0.17. For vanishing layers ( h_layer <= H_VANISHED ) the cell falls\nback to rho_0 — same defensive branch as the coastal kernel; keeps\nthe EOS finite under ZSTAR_FULL when bed-side layers can pinch out.\nThe gate is > H_VANISHED (not > 0 ): during an active drain the\nPPM positivity limiter guarantees h >= 0 but NOT h >= H_VANISHED ,\nso a layer at e.g. h = 1e-8 with hS ≈ 35·1e-8 would pass a > 0 gate and give S = hS/h ≈ 5e2 PSU ⇒ corrupted ρ ⇒ garbage\nPGF. > H_VANISHED (the D4 vanished-layer role) returns rho_0 for\nany layer in (0, H_VANISHED] .  Bit-identical for any config whose\nlayers all exceed H_VANISHED.  CAVEAT: ZSTAR_FULL floors vanishing\nbed layers to zstar_h_min (default 1.5e-4 == H_VANISHED exactly),\nso such a bed layer now takes the rho_0 fallback instead of the\ncomputed density — a dynamically negligible change on a 0.15 mm\nlayer (PGF contribution ~1e-4 of a normal layer); the shipped\nanchors (ocean_analytical 8/8, dyn_split, baroclinic_longrun,\ndouble-gyre helpers) pass unchanged on both toolchains. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: beta_S real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: S_ref real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: alpha_T real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: T_ref integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz Calls proc~~eos_linear_impl~~CallsGraph proc~eos_linear_impl eos_linear_impl local local proc~eos_linear_impl->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~eos_linear_impl~~CalledByGraph proc~eos_linear_impl eos_linear_impl proc~eos_compute_arrays eos_compute_arrays proc~eos_compute_arrays->proc~eos_linear_impl proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared->proc~eos_compute_arrays proc~refresh_multilayer_derived refresh_multilayer_derived proc~refresh_multilayer_derived->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~ml_equation_of_state_shared proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic->proc~refresh_multilayer_derived proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart restore_multilayer_after_restart proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart->proc~refresh_multilayer_derived proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~api_init_multilayer api_init_multilayer proc~api_init_multilayer->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~init_from_config init_from_config proc~init_from_config->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~init_multilayer_from_barotropic proc~init_local_state->proc~restore_multilayer_after_restart proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: S_k real(kind=wp), private :: T_k integer, private :: i real(kind=wp), private :: inv_h integer, private :: j integer, private :: k Source Code pure subroutine eos_linear_impl ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , rho_layer , & rho_0 , beta_S , S_ref , & alpha_T , T_ref , & nx , ny , nz ) !! Linear two-tracer EOS, flat-impl form: !! !!   rho_k = rho_0 + beta_S * (S_k - S_ref) - alpha_T * (T_k - T_ref) !! !! where S_k = hS_k / h_k, T_k = hT_k / h_k.  `beta_S` and !! `alpha_T` are pre-multiplied sensitivities in kg/m³ per unit !! S / T — standard seawater values are 0.78 and 0.17. !! !! For vanishing layers (`h_layer <= H_VANISHED`) the cell falls !! back to rho_0 — same defensive branch as the coastal kernel; keeps !! the EOS finite under ZSTAR_FULL when bed-side layers can pinch out. !! The gate is `> H_VANISHED` (not `> 0`): during an active drain the !! PPM positivity limiter guarantees `h >= 0` but NOT `h >= H_VANISHED`, !! so a layer at e.g. `h = 1e-8` with `hS ≈ 35·1e-8` would pass a !! `> 0` gate and give `S = hS/h ≈ 5e2 PSU` ⇒ corrupted ρ ⇒ garbage !! PGF.  `> H_VANISHED` (the D4 vanished-layer role) returns rho_0 for !! any layer in `(0, H_VANISHED]`.  Bit-identical for any config whose !! layers all exceed H_VANISHED.  CAVEAT: ZSTAR_FULL floors vanishing !! bed layers to `zstar_h_min` (default 1.5e-4 == H_VANISHED exactly), !! so such a bed layer now takes the rho_0 fallback instead of the !! computed density — a dynamically negligible change on a 0.15 mm !! layer (PGF contribution ~1e-4 of a normal layer); the shipped !! anchors (ocean_analytical 8/8, dyn_split, baroclinic_longrun, !! double-gyre helpers) pass unchanged on both toolchains. integer , intent ( in ) :: nx , ny , nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hS_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hT_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_layer ( nx , ny , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho_0 , beta_S , S_ref , alpha_T , T_ref integer :: i , j , k real ( wp ) :: inv_h , S_k , T_k do concurrent ( k = 1 : nz , j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx ) local ( inv_h , S_k , T_k ) if ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) > H_VANISHED ) then inv_h = 1.0_wp / h_layer ( i , j , k ) S_k = hS_layer ( i , j , k ) * inv_h T_k = hT_layer ( i , j , k ) * inv_h else S_k = S_ref T_k = T_ref end if rho_layer ( i , j , k ) = rho_0 + beta_S * ( S_k - S_ref ) - alpha_T * ( T_k - T_ref ) end do end subroutine eos_linear_impl","tags":"","url":"proc/eos_linear_impl.html"},{"title":"eos_roquet_spv_impl – Rakali","text":"private pure subroutine eos_roquet_spv_impl(h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer, rho_0, p_ref, nx, ny, nz) Roquet et al. (2015) SpV EOS evaluated at a single reference\npressure p_ref .  Same outer-shim signature as eos_linear_impl / eos_wright_impl — bare 3D arrays, model\n(PT, SP) tracers, vanishing-layer fallback to rho_0 . Density = 1 / SV(CT(SR,PT), SR, p_ref) with SR = SP·(35.16504/35)\nand CT = ct_from_pt(SR, PT) — the conversions live inside the\nfused roquet_spv_point point routine (the only sqrt path). FV_LITE / FV_MOM6 PGF read rho_layer generically, so they pick\nup Roquet automatically.  (FV_WRIGHT re-evaluates Wright in its\nPicard sweep → unsupported with Roquet; gated fail-loud at\nconfigure in configure_ocean_pgf .) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_layer (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: p_ref integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz Calls proc~~eos_roquet_spv_impl~~CallsGraph proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl eos_roquet_spv_impl local local proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl->local proc~roquet_spv_point roquet_spv_point proc~eos_roquet_spv_impl->proc~roquet_spv_point Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easi