ogram Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~rki_unstr_finalize rki_unstr_finalize proc~rki_unstr_finalize->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure subroutine ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr ( state ) !! Seed the two standard tracers (salinity, temperature) from the IC !! scalars carried on `state%multilayer`, each dispatching uniform-vs- !! stratified via `ml_seed_tracer_unstr`.  Call once after !! `ml_init_layers_unstr` and before EOS.  The unstructured twin of the !! structured `multilayer_state_t%seed_tracers`; a free helper (not a !! type-bound method) because the unstructured tracer kernels take the !! top-level `unstr_state_t`, so binding on the state would close a !! `state <-> tracers_unstr` module cycle. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state call ml_seed_tracer_unstr ( state , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , & state % multilayer % initial_salinity , & state % multilayer % S_init_bottom , state % multilayer % S_init_surface ) call ml_seed_tracer_unstr ( state , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_temperature )% hTr , & state % multilayer % initial_temperature , & state % multilayer % T_init_bottom , state % multilayer % T_init_surface ) end subroutine ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr.html"},{"title":"ml_seed_tracer_unstr – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_seed_tracer_unstr(state, hTr_layer, tr_uniform, tr_bottom, tr_surface) Seed one tracer’s hTr field, dispatching between the uniform and\nthe linear-stratified profile from the tracer’s IC scalars.  When\nboth tr_bottom and tr_surface are set (non-zero) and nz > 1 a\nlinear profile is laid down from tr_bottom at the bed (k=1) to tr_surface at the surface (k=nz); otherwise every layer is filled\nwith tr_uniform .  The single stratified-vs-uniform gate shared by\nthe unstructured IC seed site (solver_unstr_init_multilayer).\nMirrors the structured ml_seed_tracer . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_uniform real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_bottom real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_surface Calls proc~~ml_seed_tracer_unstr~~CallsGraph proc~ml_seed_tracer_unstr ml_seed_tracer_unstr proc~ml_init_tracer_stratified_unstr ml_init_tracer_stratified_unstr proc~ml_seed_tracer_unstr->proc~ml_init_tracer_stratified_unstr proc~ml_init_tracer_unstr ml_init_tracer_unstr proc~ml_seed_tracer_unstr->proc~ml_init_tracer_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_seed_tracer_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_seed_tracer_unstr ml_seed_tracer_unstr proc~ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr proc~ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr->proc~ml_seed_tracer_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~rki_unstr_finalize rki_unstr_finalize proc~rki_unstr_finalize->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure subroutine ml_seed_tracer_unstr ( state , hTr_layer , tr_uniform , & tr_bottom , tr_surface ) !! Seed one tracer's `hTr` field, dispatching between the uniform and !! the linear-stratified profile from the tracer's IC scalars.  When !! both `tr_bottom` and `tr_surface` are set (non-zero) and nz > 1 a !! linear profile is laid down from `tr_bottom` at the bed (k=1) to !! `tr_surface` at the surface (k=nz); otherwise every layer is filled !! with `tr_uniform`.  The single stratified-vs-uniform gate shared by !! the unstructured IC seed site (solver_unstr_init_multilayer). !! Mirrors the structured `ml_seed_tracer`. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer (:, :) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tr_uniform , tr_bottom , tr_surface if ( tr_bottom /= 0.0_wp . and . tr_surface /= 0.0_wp . and . & state % multilayer % nz_ml > 1 ) then call ml_init_tracer_stratified_unstr ( state , hTr_layer , tr_bottom , tr_surface ) else call ml_init_tracer_unstr ( state , hTr_layer , tr_uniform ) end if end subroutine ml_seed_tracer_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_seed_tracer_unstr.html"},{"title":"ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr(state, hTr_layer, kappa_bg, dt) Ri-dependent vertical diffusion of a scalar tracer.\nUses stronger Ri suppression for tracers:\n  kappa_t = nu_max / (1 + alpha*Ri)&#94;3 + kappa_bg. Column-local — no neighbour access, safe for do concurrent . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout), contiguous :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_bg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr~~CallsGraph proc~ml_vertical_diffusion_trace