exchange: upwind selection based on w,\n50% limiter on donor layer. Uses two-pass approach: first compute all interface fluxes from\nthe current state, then apply them. This avoids the race condition\nwhere modifying layer k affects the flux computation at layer k+1. Requires w_interface to be populated by ml_compute_vertical_velocity_unstr. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout), contiguous :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr~~CallsGraph proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr_impl ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr_impl proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr->proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr_impl local local proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr_impl->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr ( state , hTr_layer , dt ) !! Vertical tracer exchange using upwind advection at interfaces. !! !! Same pattern as momentum exchange: upwind selection based on w, !! 50% limiter on donor layer. !! !! Uses two-pass approach: first compute all interface fluxes from !! the current state, then apply them. This avoids the race condition !! where modifying layer k affects the flux computation at layer k+1. !! !! Requires w_interface to be populated by ml_compute_vertical_velocity_unstr. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state real ( wp ), intent ( inout ), contiguous :: hTr_layer (:, :) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt if (. not . state % use_multilayer ) return ! Single-layer case: no vertical exchange if ( state % multilayer % nz_ml < 2 ) return call ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr_impl ( & state % multilayer % nz_ml , state % ncells_total , state % ncells_owned , & state % barotropic % height_cv , state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % w_interface , hTr_layer , dt ) end subroutine ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr.html"},{"title":"advect_tracer_one_cell – Rakali","text":"private pure subroutine advect_tracer_one_cell(state, mesh, hTr_layer, nz, dt, cell, bc_tr_ext) Per-cell body, marked pure to document the “this cell only”\nwrite pattern that makes the enclosing do concurrent safe. Per-layer mass flux uses the vanishing-layer-gated centred CWC\nsplit (mirrors the structured ml_advect_tracer ): ! For each edge (per-edge, both cells see the same value):\n  if h_here(k) > tol .and. h_nbr(k) > tol then\n     v_layer(k, e)   = -(hu_edge n1 + hv_edge n2) * L_e\n        where hu_edge = 0.5 (hu_layer(here) + hu_layer(nbr))\n     hf_layer(k, e)  = 0.5 (h_layer(here) + h_layer(nbr))\n  else\n     v_layer(k, e)   = 0     ! vanishing layer carries no flux\n     hf_layer(k, e)  = 0\n  end if\n  H_active(e) = sum_k hf_layer(k, e)\n  correction(e) = mass_flux_e - sum_k v_layer(k, e)\n  frac_e(k, e) = hf_layer(k, e) / H_active(e)   ! 0 if vanishing\n  f_layer(k, e) = v_layer(k, e) + frac_e(k, e) * correction(e) v_layer , hf_layer , and frac_e are all symmetric across\nthe edge → per-layer face mass conservation holds (the\ncontribution that this cell sees through edge e is equal-and-\nopposite to what its neighbour sees through the shared edge). sum_k f_layer = mass_flux_e (CWC). For sigma / zsigma / zstar-lite where every layer is non-\nvanishing on both sides, frac_e(k) reduces to dsig_k for\nuniform sigma, and the formula degenerates to the original\ncentred CWC scheme — zero risk to existing tests. For ZSTAR_FULL deep-shallow edges, vanishing bed layers in\nthe shallow cell are excluded from the per-layer split, so the\ncolumn flux is redistributed across the (active) non-vanishing\nlayers instead of being centred-averaged into the tiny\nvanishing receivers.  No bloat of S in vanishing layers, no\nclamp clipping, no salt-mass leak. Boundary edges have no neighbour to average against, so we\nfall back to dsig_k * mass_flux_e there (CWC preserved\ntrivially, BC-prescribed mass flux honoured as-is). Neighbour and own-cell tracer reads go through state%multilayer%tracer_advect_scratch (the frozen copy of hTr_layer taken at the start of the advect step) so CPU serial loops\nobserve the same Jacobi update GPU parallel launches do. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt integer, intent(in) :: cell real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bc_tr_ext (MAX_BC_GROUPS) External tracer for each boundary group Called by proc~~advect_tracer_one_cell~~CalledByGraph proc~advect_tracer_one_cell advect_tracer_one_cell proc~ml_advect_tracer_unstr ml_advect_tracer_unstr proc~ml_advect_tracer_unstr->proc~advect_tracer_one_cell proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~ml_advect_tracer_unstr proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: H_active (3) sum_k hf_layer(k, e) real(kind=wp), private :: L_e real(kind=wp), private :: accum integer, private :: bc_grp real(kind=wp), private :: correction (3) mass_flux_e - sum_k v_layer integer, private :: e real(kind=wp), private :: f_layer real(kind=wp), private :: f_mass real(kind=wp), private :: frac (BPG_NZ_MAX) Column-local layer fraction (boundary fallback) real(kind=wp), private :: h_here real(kind=wp), private :: h_nbr real(kind=wp), private :: h_total real(kind=wp), private :: hf_layer (BPG_NZ_MAX,3) Per-layer per-edge active thickness real(kind=wp), private :: hu_edge real(kind=wp), private :: hv_edge real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_active (3) 1 / H_active where positive real(kind=wp), private :: inv_area real(kind=wp), private :: inv_h_total integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: n1 real(kind=wp), private :: n2 integer, private :: nbr real(kind=wp), private :: tr_up real(kind=wp), private :: v_layer (BPG_NZ_MAX,3) Per-layer per-edge raw flux Source Code pure subroutine advect_tracer_one_cell ( state , mesh , hTr_layer , nz , dt , cell , & bc_tr_ext ) !! Per-cell body, marked pure to document the \"this cell only\" !! write pattern that makes the enclosing `do concurrent` safe. !! !! Per-layer mass flux uses the vanishing-layer-gated centred CWC !! split (mirrors the structured `ml_advect_tracer`): !! !!   ! For each edge (per-edge, both cells see the same value): !!   if h_here(k) > tol .and. h_nbr(k) > tol then !!      v_layer(k, e)   = -(hu_edge*n1 + hv_edge*n2) * L_e !!         where hu_edge = 0.5*(hu_layer(here) + hu_layer(nbr)) !!      hf_layer(k, e)  = 0.5*(h_layer(here) + h_layer(nbr)) !!   else !!      v_layer(k, e)   = 0     ! vanishing layer carries no flux !!      hf_layer(k, e)  = 0 !!   end if !!   H_active(e) = sum_k hf_layer(k, e) !!   correction(e) = mass_flux_e - sum_k v_layer(k, e) !!   frac_e(k, e) = hf_layer(k, e) / H_active(e)   ! 0 if vanishing !!   f_layer(k, e) = v_layer(k, e) + frac_e(k, e) * correction(e) !! !! `v_layer`, `hf_layer`, and `frac_e` are all symmetric across !! the edge → per-layer face mass conservation holds (the !! contribution that this cell sees through edge e is equal-and- !! opposite to what its neighbour sees through the shared edge). !! `sum_k f_layer = mass_flux_e` (CWC). !! !! For sigma / zsigma / zstar-lite where every layer is non- !! vanishing on both sides, frac_e(k) reduces to dsig_k for !! uniform sigma, and the formula degenerates to the original !! centred CWC scheme — zero risk to existing tests. !! !! For ZSTAR_FULL deep-shallow edges, vanishing bed layers in !! the shallow cell are excluded from the per-layer split, so the !! column flux is redistributed across the (active) non-vanishing !! layers instead of being centred-averaged into the tiny !! vanishing receivers.  No bloat of S in vanishing layers, no !! clamp clipping, no salt-mass leak. !! !! Boundary edges have no neighbour to average against, so we !! fall back to `dsig_k * mass_flux_e` there (CWC preserved !! trivially, BC-prescribed mass flux honoured as-is). !! !! Neighbour and own-cell tracer reads go through !! `state%multilayer%tracer_advect_scratch` (the frozen copy of `hTr_layer` !! taken at the start of the advect step) so CPU serial loops !! observe the same Jacobi update GPU parallel launches do. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer (:, :) integer , intent ( in ) :: nz , cell real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: bc_tr_ext ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) !! External tracer for each boundary group integer :: k , e , nbr , bc_grp real ( wp ) :: inv_area real ( wp ) :: f_mass , f_layer real ( wp ) :: h_here , h_nbr , tr_up real ( wp ) :: accum real ( wp ) :: n1 , n2 , L_e real ( wp ) :: hu_edge , hv_edge real ( wp ) :: v_layer ( BPG_NZ_MAX , 3 ) !! Per-layer per-edge raw flux real ( wp ) :: hf_layer ( BPG_NZ_MAX , 3 ) !! Per-layer per-edge active thickness real ( wp ) :: H_active ( 3 ) !! sum_k hf_layer(k, e) real ( wp ) :: inv_H_active ( 3 ) !! 1 / H_active where positive real ( wp ) :: correction ( 3 ) !! mass_flux_e - sum_k v_layer real ( wp ) :: frac ( BPG_NZ_MAX ) !! Column-local layer fraction (boundary fallback) real ( wp ) :: h_total , inv_h_total inv_area = 1.0_wp / mesh % area ( cell ) ! Column-local layer fraction h_layer(k)/H_total — used for the ! BOUNDARY-edge fallback only.  For interior edges algorithm N ! uses per-edge `frac_e = hf_layer(k, e) / H_active(e)`. h_total = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_total = h_total + state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , cell ) end do if ( h_total > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then inv_h_total = 1.0_wp / h_total do k = 1 , nz frac ( k ) = state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , cell ) * inv_h_total end do else do k = 1 , nz frac ( k ) = state % multilayer % dsig_ml ( k ) end do end if ! ---- Pass 1: build per-edge per-layer flux + active thickness + !              the CWC correction (vanishing-layer-gated centred). ---- do e = 1 , 3 nbr = mesh % neighbours ( e , cell ) f_mass = state % barotropic % mass_flux_e ( e , cell ) if ( nbr > 0 ) then n1 = mesh % edge_n1 ( e , cell ) n2 = mesh % edge_n2 ( e , cell ) L_e = mesh % edge_len ( e , cell ) correction ( e ) = f_mass H_active ( e ) = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_here = state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , cell ) h_nbr = state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , nbr ) if ( h_here > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL_UNSTR . and . h_nbr > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL_UNSTR ) then hu_edge = 0.5_wp * ( state % multilayer % hu_layer ( k , cell ) + state % multilayer % hu_layer ( k , nbr )) hv_edge = 0.5_wp * ( state % multilayer % hv_layer ( k , cell ) + state % multilayer % hv_layer ( k , nbr )) ! mass_flux_e convention: > 0 = inflow. (hu*n1 + hv*n2)*L ! is OUTFLOW for outward normal n, so negate. v_layer ( k , e ) = - ( hu_edge * n1 + hv_edge * n2 ) * L_e hf_layer ( k , e ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_here + h_nbr ) else v_layer ( k , e ) = 0.0_wp hf_layer ( k , e ) = 0.0_wp end if correction ( e ) = correction ( e ) - v_layer ( k , e ) H_active ( e ) = H_active ( e ) + hf_layer ( k , e ) end do if ( H_active ( e ) > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_active ( e ) = 1.0_wp / H_active ( e ) else inv_H_active ( e ) = 0.0_wp end if else ! Boundary edge: no neighbour. Split mass flux by the local ! layer-thickness fraction so f_layer reflects the actual ! vertical layout (matches sigma when frac == dsig_ml). correction ( e ) = 0.0_wp H_active ( e ) = 0.0_wp inv_H_active ( e ) = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz v_layer ( k , e ) = frac ( k ) * f_mass hf_layer ( k , e ) = 0.0_wp end do end if end do ! ---- Pass 2: per-layer upwind tracer flux accumulation ---- do k = 1 , nz accum = 0.0_wp h_here = state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , cell ) do e = 1 , 3 nbr = mesh % neighbours ( e , cell ) if ( nbr > 0 ) then f_layer = v_layer ( k , e ) + hf_layer ( k , e ) * inv_H_active ( e ) * correction ( e ) else ! Boundary edge: v_layer already carries the full ! frac(k)*f_mass split (no correction term needed). f_layer = v_layer ( k , e ) end if ! Pick upwind concentration. If the layer is losing mass ! (`f_layer < 0` = outflow) the upwind is this cell; ! otherwise it's the neighbour. if ( f_layer < 0.0_wp ) then ! Outflow: upwind is this cell if ( h_here > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_up = state % multilayer % tracer_advect_scratch ( k , cell ) / h_here else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if else if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then ! Inflow: upwind is neighbour or boundary if ( nbr > 0 ) then ! Interior edge: use neighbour value h_nbr = state % multilayer % h_layer ( k , nbr ) if ( h_nbr > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_up = state % multilayer % tracer_advect_scratch ( k , nbr ) / h_nbr else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if else ! Boundary inflow: use external tracer from BC group bc_grp = mesh % bc_group ( e , cell ) if ( bc_grp > 0 . and . bc_grp <= MAX_BC_GROUPS ) then tr_up = bc_tr_ext ( bc_grp ) else ! Fallback for undefined BC group tr_up = 0.0_wp end if end if else cycle end if ! hTr_K += dt/area * Tr_up * F_layer_inflow ! (positive f_layer = inflow, so sign of accum matches ! the mass change through this edge). accum = accum + tr_up * f_layer end do hTr_layer ( k , cell ) = hTr_layer ( k , cell ) + dt * inv_area * accum end do end subroutine advect_tracer_one_cell","tags":"","url":"proc/advect_tracer_one_cell.html"},{"title":"ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl – Rakali","text":"private pure subroutine ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl(nz, n, ncells_owned, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, dsig_ml, tracer_advect_scratch, lgrad_x, lgrad_y, mass_flux_e, area, neighbours, surrogate_neighbours, edge_n1, edge_n2, edge_len, edge_mid_x, edge_mid_y, centroid_x, centroid_y, bc_group, hTr_layer, dt, bc_ext_local) Flat-impl of ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr : explicit-shape dummies\nso the device kernels see contiguous raw pointers, not derived-type\ndescriptors (descriptor access inflates per-thread registers and caps\noccupancy).  Body is identical to the historical kernel modulo the\nstripped state% / mesh% prefixes and the removed associate . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n integer, intent(in) :: ncells_owned real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig_ml (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: tracer_advect_scratch (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: lgrad_x (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: lgrad_y (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_e (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: area (n) integer, intent(in) :: neighbours (3,n) integer, intent(in) :: surrogate_neighbours (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_n1 (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_n2 (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_len (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_mid_x (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_mid_y (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: centroid_x (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: centroid_y (n) integer, intent(in) :: bc_group (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bc_ext_local (MAX_BC_GROUPS) Calls proc~~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl~~CallsGraph proc~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl local local proc~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl proc~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr proc~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr->proc~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: H_active (3) sum_k hf_layer(k, e) real(kind=wp), private :: L_e real(kind=wp), private :: accum integer, private :: bc_grp integer, private :: cell real(kind=wp), private :: correction (3) real(kind=wp), private :: dq_e real(kind=wp), private :: dx_e real(kind=wp), private :: dy_e integer, private :: e real(kind=wp), private :: f_layer real(kind=wp), private :: f_mass real(kind=wp), private :: frac (BPG_NZ_MAX) Column-local layer fraction (boundary fallback) real(kind=wp), private :: gradx real(kind=wp), private :: grady real(kind=wp), private :: h_here real(kind=wp), private :: h_nbr real(kind=wp), private :: h_total real(kind=wp), private :: hf_layer (BPG_NZ_MAX,3) Per-layer per-edge active thickness real(kind=wp), private :: hu_edge real(kind=wp), private :: hv_edge real(kind=wp), private :: inv_H_active (3) 1 / H_active where positive real(kind=wp), private :: inv_area real(kind=wp), private :: inv_h_total integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: n1 real(kind=wp), private :: n2 integer, private :: nbr real(kind=wp), private :: phi real(kind=wp), private :: tr_edge_val real(kind=wp), private :: tr_here real(kind=wp), private :: tr_max real(kind=wp), private :: tr_min real(kind=wp), private :: tr_nbr real(kind=wp), private :: tr_up real(kind=wp), private :: v_layer (BPG_NZ_MAX,3) Source Code pure subroutine ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl ( nz , n , ncells_owned , & h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & dsig_ml , tracer_advect_scratch , & lgrad_x , lgrad_y , mass_flux_e , & area , neighbours , surrogate_neighbours , & edge_n1 , edge_n2 , edge_len , & edge_mid_x , edge_mid_y , & centroid_x , centroid_y , bc_group , & hTr_layer , dt , bc_ext_local ) !! Flat-impl of [[ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr]]: explicit-shape dummies !! so the device kernels see contiguous raw pointers, not derived-type !! descriptors (descriptor access inflates per-thread registers and caps !! occupancy).  Body is identical to the historical kernel modulo the !! stripped `state%`/`mesh%` prefixes and the removed `associate`. integer , intent ( in ) :: nz , n , ncells_owned real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( nz , n ), hu_layer ( nz , n ), hv_layer ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dsig_ml ( nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: tracer_advect_scratch ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: lgrad_x ( nz , n ), lgrad_y ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mass_flux_e ( 3 , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: area ( n ) integer , intent ( in ) :: neighbours ( 3 , n ), surrogate_neighbours ( 3 , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: edge_n1 ( 3 , n ), edge_n2 ( 3 , n ), edge_len ( 3 , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: edge_mid_x ( 3 , n ), edge_mid_y ( 3 , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: centroid_x ( n ), centroid_y ( n ) integer , intent ( in ) :: bc_group ( 3 , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: bc_ext_local ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) integer :: cell , k , e , nbr real ( wp ) :: tr_here , tr_nbr , tr_edge_val , tr_max , tr_min real ( wp ) :: gradx , grady , inv_area real ( wp ) :: dq_e , dx_e , dy_e , phi real ( wp ) :: n1 , n2 , L_e real ( wp ) :: f_mass , f_layer , h_here , h_nbr , tr_up , accum real ( wp ) :: hu_edge , hv_edge real ( wp ) :: v_layer ( BPG_NZ_MAX , 3 ) real ( wp ) :: hf_layer ( BPG_NZ_MAX , 3 ) !! Per-layer per-edge active thickness real ( wp ) :: H_active ( 3 ) !! sum_k hf_layer(k, e) real ( wp ) :: inv_H_active ( 3 ) !! 1 / H_active where positive real ( wp ) :: correction ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: frac ( BPG_NZ_MAX ) !! Column-local layer fraction (boundary fallback) real ( wp ) :: h_total , inv_h_total integer :: bc_grp ! Snapshot the input tracer for Jacobi consistency. do concurrent ( cell = 1 : n , k = 1 : nz ) tracer_advect_scratch ( k , cell ) = hTr_layer ( k , cell ) end do ! ---- Phase 1: Green-Gauss gradient + Barth-Jespersen limiter ---- ! Computed for ALL cells (including halo) so Phase 2 can read ! the neighbour's gradient for inflow faces. do concurrent ( cell = 1 : n ) & local ( k , e , nbr , tr_here , tr_nbr , tr_edge_val , tr_max , tr_min , & gradx , grady , inv_area , n1 , n2 , L_e , dq_e , dx_e , dy_e , phi ) inv_area = 1.0_wp / area ( cell ) do k = 1 , nz h_here = h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( h_here > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_here = tracer_advect_scratch ( k , cell ) / h_here else tr_here = 0.0_wp end if ! Green-Gauss gradient using surrogate neighbours gradx = 0.0_wp grady = 0.0_wp tr_max = tr_here tr_min = tr_here do e = 1 , 3 nbr = surrogate_neighbours ( e , cell ) h_nbr = h_layer ( k , nbr ) if ( h_nbr > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_nbr = tracer_advect_scratch ( k , nbr ) / h_nbr else tr_nbr = 0.0_wp end if tr_edge_val = 0.5_wp * ( tr_here + tr_nbr ) n1 = edge_n1 ( e , cell ) n2 = edge_n2 ( e , cell ) L_e = edge_len ( e , cell ) gradx = gradx + tr_edge_val * n1 * L_e grady = grady + tr_edge_val * n2 * L_e if ( tr_nbr > tr_max ) tr_max = tr_nbr if ( tr_nbr < tr_min ) tr_min = tr_nbr end do gradx = gradx * inv_area grady = grady * inv_area ! Barth-Jespersen limiter: find the minimum phi over all ! edge midpoints such that the extrapolated value stays ! within [tr_min, tr_max]. phi = 1.0_wp do e = 1 , 3 dx_e = edge_mid_x ( e , cell ) - centroid_x ( cell ) dy_e = edge_mid_y ( e , cell ) - centroid_y ( cell ) dq_e = gradx * dx_e + grady * dy_e if ( dq_e > 1.0e-15_wp ) then phi = min ( phi , ( tr_max - tr_here ) / dq_e ) else if ( dq_e < - 1.0e-15_wp ) then phi = min ( phi , ( tr_min - tr_here ) / dq_e ) end if end do ! Clamp phi to [0, 1] if ( phi < 0.0_wp ) phi = 0.0_wp if ( phi > 1.0_wp ) phi = 1.0_wp ! Store limited gradient (pre-multiplied by phi) lgrad_x ( k , cell ) = phi * gradx lgrad_y ( k , cell ) = phi * grady end do end do ! ---- Phase 2: MUSCL advection (same CWC flux + limited upwind) ---- do concurrent ( cell = 1 : ncells_owned ) & local ( k , e , nbr , bc_grp , inv_area , & f_mass , f_layer , h_here , h_nbr , tr_up , accum , & n1 , n2 , L_e , hu_edge , hv_edge , dx_e , dy_e , tr_here , tr_nbr , & v_layer , hf_layer , H_active , inv_H_active , & correction , frac , h_total , inv_h_total ) inv_area = 1.0_wp / area ( cell ) ! Column-local layer fraction (used only for the boundary-edge ! fallback below).  Interior edges use per-edge active frac. h_total = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_total = h_total + h_layer ( k , cell ) end do if ( h_total > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then inv_h_total = 1.0_wp / h_total do k = 1 , nz frac ( k ) = h_layer ( k , cell ) * inv_h_total end do else do k = 1 , nz frac ( k ) = dsig_ml ( k ) end do end if ! ---- Pass 1: vanishing-layer-gated centred CWC flux per edge ---- do e = 1 , 3 nbr = neighbours ( e , cell ) f_mass = mass_flux_e ( e , cell ) if ( nbr > 0 ) then n1 = edge_n1 ( e , cell ) n2 = edge_n2 ( e , cell ) L_e = edge_len ( e , cell ) correction ( e ) = f_mass H_active ( e ) = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_here = h_layer ( k , cell ) h_nbr = h_layer ( k , nbr ) if ( h_here > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL_UNSTR . and . h_nbr > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL_UNSTR ) then hu_edge = 0.5_wp * ( hu_layer ( k , cell ) + hu_layer ( k , nbr )) hv_edge = 0.5_wp * ( hv_layer ( k , cell ) + hv_layer ( k , nbr )) v_layer ( k , e ) = - ( hu_edge * n1 + hv_edge * n2 ) * L_e hf_layer ( k , e ) = 0.5_wp * ( h_here + h_nbr ) else v_layer ( k , e ) = 0.0_wp hf_layer ( k , e ) = 0.0_wp end if correction ( e ) = correction ( e ) - v_layer ( k , e ) H_active ( e ) = H_active ( e ) + hf_layer ( k , e ) end do if ( H_active ( e ) > 0.0_wp ) then inv_H_active ( e ) = 1.0_wp / H_active ( e ) else inv_H_active ( e ) = 0.0_wp end if else correction ( e ) = 0.0_wp H_active ( e ) = 0.0_wp inv_H_active ( e ) = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz v_layer ( k , e ) = frac ( k ) * f_mass hf_layer ( k , e ) = 0.0_wp end do end if end do ! ---- Pass 2: per-layer MUSCL upwind flux accumulation ---- do k = 1 , nz accum = 0.0_wp h_here = h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( h_here > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_here = tracer_advect_scratch ( k , cell ) / h_here else tr_here = 0.0_wp end if do e = 1 , 3 nbr = neighbours ( e , cell ) if ( nbr > 0 ) then f_layer = v_layer ( k , e ) + hf_layer ( k , e ) * inv_H_active ( e ) * correction ( e ) else f_layer = v_layer ( k , e ) end if if ( f_layer < 0.0_wp ) then ! Outflow: upwind is this cell, use limited extrapolation if ( h_here > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then dx_e = edge_mid_x ( e , cell ) - centroid_x ( cell ) dy_e = edge_mid_y ( e , cell ) - centroid_y ( cell ) tr_up = tr_here + lgrad_x ( k , cell ) * dx_e + lgrad_y ( k , cell ) * dy_e else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if else if ( f_layer > 0.0_wp ) then ! Inflow: upwind is neighbour or boundary if ( nbr > 0 ) then h_nbr = h_layer ( k , nbr ) if ( h_nbr > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_nbr = tracer_advect_scratch ( k , nbr ) / h_nbr ! Extrapolate from neighbour's centroid to this edge midpoint dx_e = edge_mid_x ( e , cell ) - centroid_x ( nbr ) dy_e = edge_mid_y ( e , cell ) - centroid_y ( nbr ) tr_up = tr_nbr + lgrad_x ( k , nbr ) * dx_e + lgrad_y ( k , nbr ) * dy_e else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if else bc_grp = bc_group ( e , cell ) if ( bc_grp > 0 . and . bc_grp <= MAX_BC_GROUPS ) then tr_up = bc_ext_local ( bc_grp ) else tr_up = 0.0_wp end if end if else cycle end if accum = accum + tr_up * f_layer end do hTr_layer ( k , cell ) = hTr_layer ( k , cell ) + dt * inv_area * accum end do end do end subroutine ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl.html"},{"title":"ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl – Rakali","text":"private pure subroutine ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl(nz, n, h_layer, hTr_layer, tr_min, tr_max) Flat-impl of ml_clamp_tracer_unstr : explicit-shape dummies so the\ndevice kernel addresses raw pointers, not derived-type descriptors. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_min real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_max Calls proc~~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl~~CallsGraph proc~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl local local proc~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl proc~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr ml_clamp_tracer_unstr proc~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr->proc~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl proc~si_unstr_step_ml si_unstr_step_ml proc~si_unstr_step_ml->proc~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~ml_clamp_tracer_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit->proc~si_unstr_step_ml proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: TINY_CAP = 1.0e-30_wp real(kind=wp), private :: cap_to_add real(kind=wp), private :: cap_to_remove integer, private :: cell real(kind=wp), private :: col_h real(kind=wp), private :: col_hTr real(kind=wp), private :: deficit_below real(kind=wp), private :: excess_above real(kind=wp), private :: frac real(kind=wp), private :: h_k integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: net real(kind=wp), private :: room_k real(kind=wp), private :: tr_k Source Code pure subroutine ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl ( nz , n , h_layer , hTr_layer , tr_min , tr_max ) !! Flat-impl of [[ml_clamp_tracer_unstr]]: explicit-shape dummies so the !! device kernel addresses raw pointers, not derived-type descriptors. integer , intent ( in ) :: nz , n real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hTr_layer ( nz , n ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tr_min , tr_max integer :: cell , k real ( wp ) :: h_k , tr_k , room_k real ( wp ) :: excess_above , deficit_below , cap_to_add , cap_to_remove real ( wp ) :: net , frac real ( wp ) :: col_hTr , col_h real ( wp ), parameter :: TINY_CAP = 1.0e-30_wp do concurrent ( cell = 1 : n ) & local ( k , h_k , tr_k , room_k , & excess_above , deficit_below , cap_to_add , cap_to_remove , & net , frac , col_hTr , col_h ) ! Pass 0: column mean.  The two-pass clip+redistribute below is ! EXACTLY conservative if and only if the column-mean concentration ! lies within [tr_min, tr_max] (net <= cap_to_add follows from ! mean <= tr_max; see the structured twin `ml_clamp_tracer` for the ! algebra).  Outside that range no clamp can both hold the bound and ! conserve, and the old code silently destroyed the un-absorbable ! residual.  Conservation wins: skip the column. col_hTr = 0.0_wp col_h = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then col_hTr = col_hTr + hTr_layer ( k , cell ) col_h = col_h + h_k end if end do if ( col_h > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = col_hTr / col_h if ( tr_k > tr_max . or . tr_k < tr_min ) cycle else cycle end if ! Pass 1: hard clip violators, accumulate excess/deficit and capacity. excess_above = 0.0_wp deficit_below = 0.0_wp cap_to_add = 0.0_wp cap_to_remove = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = hTr_layer ( k , cell ) / h_k if ( tr_k > tr_max ) then excess_above = excess_above + ( tr_k - tr_max ) * h_k hTr_layer ( k , cell ) = tr_max * h_k cap_to_remove = cap_to_remove + ( tr_max - tr_min ) * h_k else if ( tr_k < tr_min ) then deficit_below = deficit_below + ( tr_min - tr_k ) * h_k hTr_layer ( k , cell ) = tr_min * h_k cap_to_add = cap_to_add + ( tr_max - tr_min ) * h_k else cap_to_add = cap_to_add + ( tr_max - tr_k ) * h_k cap_to_remove = cap_to_remove + ( tr_k - tr_min ) * h_k end if end if end do ! Pass 2: redistribute net imbalance into available capacity. net = excess_above - deficit_below if ( net > 0.0_wp . and . cap_to_add > TINY_CAP ) then frac = min ( 1.0_wp , net / cap_to_add ) do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = hTr_layer ( k , cell ) / h_k room_k = ( tr_max - tr_k ) * h_k if ( room_k > 0.0_wp ) then hTr_layer ( k , cell ) = hTr_layer ( k , cell ) + frac * room_k end if end if end do else if ( net < 0.0_wp . and . cap_to_remove > TINY_CAP ) then frac = min ( 1.0_wp , ( - net ) / cap_to_remove ) do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( k , cell ) if ( h_k > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then tr_k = hTr_layer ( k , cell ) / h_k room_k = ( tr_k - tr_min ) * h_k if ( room_k > 0.0_wp ) then hTr_layer ( k , cell ) = hTr_layer ( k , cell ) - frac * room_k end if end if end do end if end do end subroutine ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl.html"},{"title":"ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer_unstr_impl – Rakali","text":"private pure subroutine ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer_unstr_impl(nz, n, ncells_owned, height_cv, h_layer, hTr_pre, area, radius, centroid_x, centroid_y, edge_len, surrogate_neighbours, hTr_layer, kappa, dt) Flat-impl of ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer_unstr : explicit-shape\ndummies so the device kernels address raw pointers, not derived-type\ndescriptors. hTr_pre is the persistent Jacobi-snapshot workspace. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n integer, intent(in) :: ncells_owned real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: height_cv (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_pre (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: area (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: radius (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: centr