ible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~gauges_init~~CalledByGraph proc~gauges_init gauges_init proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~gauges_init proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine gauges_init ( gauges , cfg , state , rank ) !! Initialise gauge output: read locations, compute weights, create file type ( gauge_output_t ), intent ( inout ) :: gauges !! Gauge output state type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg !! Simulation configuration type ( state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state !! Solution state (for grid metadata and bathymetry) integer , intent ( in ) :: rank !! File-name rank suffix (always 0; the suffix is a leftover of the removed MPI support) gauges % active = . false . ! If no gauge file specified, nothing to do if ( len_trim ( cfg % gauge_file ) == 0 ) return ! Read gauge locations from text file call read_gauge_file ( cfg % gauge_file , gauges % names , gauges % gauge_x , & gauges % gauge_y , gauges % n_gauges ) if ( gauges % n_gauges == 0 ) then call logger % info ( \"Gauges: no gauge locations found in file\" ) return end if ! Find which gauges fall inside the domain call compute_local_gauges ( gauges , state ) if ( gauges % n_local == 0 ) then call logger % info ( \"Gauges: no gauge locations inside the domain\" ) return end if ! Compute bilinear interpolation weights for local gauges call compute_interp_weights ( gauges , state ) ! Create the NetCDF output file call create_gauge_netcdf ( gauges , state , cfg , rank ) gauges % active = . true . call logger % info ( \"Gauges: \" // trim ( to_string ( gauges % n_local )) // & \" of \" // trim ( to_string ( gauges % n_gauges )) // & \" gauges active on this rank\" ) end subroutine gauges_init","tags":"","url":"proc/gauges_init.html"},{"title":"gauges_write – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine gauges_write(gauges, state, time) Write a gauge time series record (interpolated eta, u, v) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( gauge_output_t ), intent(inout) :: gauges Gauge output state type( state_t ), intent(in) :: state Solution state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: time Current simulation time (s) Calls proc~~gauges_write~~CallsGraph proc~gauges_write gauges_write nf90_put_var nf90_put_var proc~gauges_write->nf90_put_var nf90_sync nf90_sync proc~gauges_write->nf90_sync proc~nc_check nc_check proc~gauges_write->proc~nc_check error error proc~nc_check->error nf90_strerror nf90_strerror proc~nc_check->nf90_strerror Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~gauges_write~~CalledByGraph proc~gauges_write gauges_write proc~write_gauges write_gauges proc~write_gauges->proc~gauges_write proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~write_gauges proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: MIN_DEPTH = 1.0e-6_wp Minimum depth for velocity computation real(kind=wp), private :: b_interp real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: eta_buf (:) integer, private :: g real(kind=wp), private :: h_interp real(kind=wp), private :: h_safe real(kind=wp), private :: hu_interp real(kind=wp), private :: hv_interp integer, private :: i0 integer, private :: j0 integer, private :: status real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: u_buf (:) real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: v_buf (:) real(kind=wp), private :: wxg real(kind=wp), private :: wyg Source Code subroutine gauges_write ( gauges , state , time ) !! Write a gauge time series record (interpolated eta, u, v) type ( gauge_output_t ), intent ( inout ) :: gauges !! Gauge output state type ( state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state !! Solution state real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: time !! Current simulation time (s) integer :: g , i0 , j0 , status real ( wp ) :: wxg , wyg , h_interp , hu_interp , hv_interp , b_interp real ( wp ) :: h_safe real ( wp ), allocatable :: eta_buf (:), u_buf (:), v_buf (:) real ( wp ), parameter :: MIN_DEPTH = 1.0e-6_wp !! Minimum depth for velocity computation if (. not . gauges % active ) return gauges % time_index = gauges % time_index + 1 allocate ( eta_buf ( gauges % n_local )) allocate ( u_buf ( gauges % n_local )) allocate ( v_buf ( gauges % n_local )) do g = 1 , gauges % n_local i0 = gauges % ix0 ( g ) j0 = gauges % iy0 ( g ) wxg = gauges % wx ( g ) wyg = gauges % wy ( g ) ! Bilinear interpolation of h, hu, hv, b h_interp = ( 1.0_wp - wxg ) * ( 1.0_wp - wyg ) * state % barotropic % h ( i0 , j0 ) & + wxg * ( 1.0_wp - wyg ) * state % barotropic % h ( i0 + 1 , j0 ) & + ( 1.0_wp - wxg ) * wyg * state % barotropic % h ( i0 , j0 + 1 ) & + wxg * wyg * state % barotropic % h ( i0 + 1 , j0 + 1 ) hu_interp = ( 1.0_wp - wxg ) * ( 1.0_wp - wyg ) * state % barotropic % hu ( i0 , j0 ) & + wxg * ( 1.0_wp - wyg ) * state % barotropic % hu ( i0 + 1 , j0 ) & + ( 1.0_wp - wxg ) * wyg * state % barotropic % hu ( i0 , j0 + 1 ) & + wxg * wyg * state % barotropic % hu ( i0 + 1 , j0 + 1 ) hv_interp = ( 1.0_wp - wxg ) * ( 1.0_wp - wyg ) * state % barotropic % hv ( i0 , j0 ) & + wxg * ( 1.0_wp - wyg ) * state % barotropic % hv ( i0 + 1 , j0 ) & + ( 1.0_wp - wxg ) * wyg * state % barotropic % hv ( i0 , j0 + 1 ) & + wxg * wyg * state % barotropic % hv ( i0 + 1 , j0 + 1 ) b_interp = ( 1.0_wp - wxg ) * ( 1.0_wp - wyg ) * state % barotropic % b ( i0 , j0 ) & + wxg * ( 1.0_wp - wyg ) * state % barotropic % b ( i0 + 1 , j0 ) & + ( 1.0_wp - wxg ) * wyg * state % barotropic % b ( i0 , j0 + 1 ) & + wxg * wyg * state % barotropic % b ( i0 + 1 , j0 + 1 ) ! Water surface elevation: eta = h + b eta_buf ( g ) = h_interp + b_interp ! Depth-averaged velocities with thin-layer guard h_safe = max ( h_interp , MIN_DEPTH ) u_buf ( g ) = hu_interp / h_safe v_buf ( g ) = hv_interp / h_safe end do ! Write time status = nf90_put_var ( gauges % ncid , gauges % time_varid , time , & start = [ gauges % time_index ]) call nc_check ( status , \"put_var gauge time\" ) ! Write eta, u, v (station, time) — write all stations at this time index status = nf90_put_var ( gauges % ncid , gauges % eta_varid , eta_buf , & start = [ 1 , gauges % time_index ], & count = [ gauges % n_local , 1 ]) call nc_check ( status , \"put_var gauge eta\" ) status = nf90_put_var ( gauges % ncid , gauges % u_varid , u_buf , & start = [ 1 , gauges % time_index ], & count = [ gauges % n_local , 1 ]) call nc_check ( status , \"put_var gauge u\" ) status = nf90_put_var ( gauges % ncid , gauges % v_varid , v_buf , & start = [ 1 , gauges % time_index ], & count = [ gauges % n_local , 1 ]) call nc_check ( status , \"put_var gauge v\" ) deallocate ( eta_buf , u_buf , v_buf ) status = nf90_sync ( gauges % ncid ) call nc_check ( status , \"sync gauges write\" ) end subroutine gauges_write","tags":"","url":"proc/gauges_write.html"},{"title":"compute_interp_weights – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine compute_interp_weights(gauges, state) Compute bilinear interpolation indices and weights for local gauges Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( gauge_output_t ), intent(inout) :: gauges Gauge output state type( state_t ), intent(in) :: state Solution state Called by proc~~compute_interp_weights~~CalledByGraph proc~compute_interp_weights compute_interp_weights proc~gauges_init gauges_init proc~gauges_init->proc~compute_interp_weights proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~gauges_init proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: dx real(kind=wp), private :: dy integer, private :: g integer, private :: gi real(kind=wp), private :: gx real(kind=wp), private :: gy integer, private :: i_start integer, private :: ia integer, private :: ig integer, private :: il integer, private :: j_start integer, private :: ja integer, private :: jg integer, private :: jl integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx_phys integer, private :: ny_phys real(kind=wp), private :: x_centre real(kind=wp), private :: y_centre Source Code subroutine compute_interp_weights ( gauges , state ) !! Compute bilinear interpolation indices and weights for local gauges type ( gauge_output_t ), intent ( inout ) :: gauges !! Gauge output state type ( state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state !! Solution state integer :: g , gi , ig , jg , il , jl , ia , ja real ( wp ) :: x_centre , y_centre , gx , gy , dx , dy integer :: nghost , i_start , j_start , nx_phys , ny_phys dx = state % grid % dx dy = state % grid % dy nghost = state % grid % nghost i_start = 1 j_start = 1 nx_phys = state % grid % nx_phys ny_phys = state % grid % ny_phys allocate ( gauges % ix0 ( gauges % n_local )) allocate ( gauges % iy0 ( gauges % n_local )) allocate ( gauges % wx ( gauges % n_local )) allocate ( gauges % wy ( gauges % n_local )) do g = 1 , gauges % n_local gi = gauges % local_idx ( g ) gx = gauges % gauge_x ( gi ) gy = gauges % gauge_y ( gi ) ! Global physical cell containing gauge (1-based) ig = floor ( gx / dx ) + 1 jg = floor ( gy / dy ) + 1 ! Local physical cell (1-based, 1..nx_phys) il = ig - i_start + 1 jl = jg - j_start + 1 ! Array index (with ghost offset) ia = il + nghost ja = jl + nghost ! Cell centre in global coordinates x_centre = ( real ( ig , wp ) - 0.5_wp ) * dx y_centre = ( real ( jg , wp ) - 0.5_wp ) * dy ! Determine interpolation stencil: if gauge is left of centre, ! interpolate between (ia-1, ia); if right, between (ia, ia+1) if ( gx < x_centre ) then ! Gauge is left of cell centre if ( il > 1 ) then gauges % ix0 ( g ) = ia - 1 gauges % wx ( g ) = ( gx - ( x_centre - dx )) / dx else ! At left edge of the domain, clamp gauges % ix0 ( g ) = ia gauges % wx ( g ) = 0.0_wp end if else ! Gauge is right of (or at) cell centre if ( il < nx_phys ) then gauges % ix0 ( g ) = ia gauges % wx ( g ) = ( gx - x_centre ) / dx else ! At right edge of the domain, clamp gauges % ix0 ( g ) = ia gauges % wx ( g ) = 0.0_wp end if end if if ( gy < y_centre ) then if ( jl > 1 ) then gauges % iy0 ( g ) = ja - 1 gauges % wy ( g ) = ( gy - ( y_centre - dy )) / dy else gauges % iy0 ( g ) = ja gauges % wy ( g ) = 0.0_wp end if else if ( jl < ny_phys ) then gauges % iy0 ( g ) = ja gauges % wy ( g ) = ( gy - y_centre ) / dy else gauges % iy0 ( g ) = ja gauges % wy ( g ) = 0.0_wp end if end if ! Clamp weights to [0, 1] for safety gauges % wx ( g ) = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , gauges % wx ( g ))) gauges % wy ( g ) = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , gauges % wy ( g ))) end do end subroutine compute_interp_weights","tags":"","url":"proc/compute_interp_weights.html"},{"title":"compute_local_gauges – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine compute_local_gauges(gauges, state) Determine which gauges fall inside the domain Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( gauge_output_t ), intent(inout) :: gauges Gauge output state type( state_t ), intent(in) :: state Solution state (for grid metadata) Called by proc~~compute_local_gauges~~CalledByGraph proc~compute_local_gauges compute_local_gauges proc~gauges_init gauges_init proc~gauges_init->proc~compute_local_gauges proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~gauges_init proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: g integer, private :: i_start integer, private :: ig integer, private :: j_start integer, private :: jg integer, private :: n integer, private :: nx_phys integer, private :: ny_phys integer, private :: tmp_local (MAX_GAUGES) Source Code subroutine compute_local_gauges ( gauges , state ) !! Determine which gauges fall inside the domain type ( gauge_output_t ), intent ( inout ) :: gauges !! Gauge output state type ( state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state !! Solution state (for grid metadata) integer :: g , n , ig , jg integer :: i_start , j_start , nx_phys , ny_phys integer :: tmp_local ( MAX_GAUGES ) i_start = 1 j_start = 1 nx_phys = state % grid % nx_phys ny_phys = state % grid % ny_phys n = 0 do g = 1 , gauges % n_gauges ! Global physical cell containing this gauge (1-based) ig = floor ( gauges % gauge_x ( g ) / state % grid % dx ) + 1 jg = floor ( gauges % gauge_y ( g ) / state % grid % dy ) + 1 ! Check if inside the domain if ( ig >= i_start . and . ig <= i_start + nx_phys - 1 . and . & jg >= j_start . and . jg <= j_start + ny_phys - 1 ) then n = n + 1 tmp_local ( n ) = g end if end do gauges % n_local = n if ( n > 0 ) then allocate ( gauges % local_idx ( n )) gauges % local_idx ( 1 : n ) = tmp_local ( 1 : n ) end if end subroutine compute_local_gauges","tags":"","url":"proc/compute_local_gauges.html"},{"title":"create_gauge_netcdf – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine create_gauge_netcdf(gauges, state, cfg, rank) Create the gauge output NetCDF file with dimensions and static data Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( gauge_output_t ), intent(inout) :: gauges Gauge output state type( state_t ), intent(in) :: state Solution state (for bathymetry interpolation) type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg Simulation configuration integer, intent(in) :: rank File-name rank suffix (always 0; the suffix is a leftover of the removed MPI support) Calls proc~~create_gauge_netcdf~2~~CallsGraph proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2 create_gauge_netcdf info info proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->info nf90_def_var nf90_def_var proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->nf90_def_var nf90_enddef nf90_enddef proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->nf90_enddef nf90_put_var nf90_put_var proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->nf90_put_var nf90_sync nf90_sync proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->nf90_sync proc~nc_check nc_check proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->proc~nc_check proc~nc_create_file nc_create_file proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->proc~nc_create_file proc~nc_def_dim nc_def_dim proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->proc~nc_def_dim proc~nc_put_att nc_put_att proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->proc~nc_put_att proc~nc_put_att_global nc_put_att_global proc~create_gauge_netcdf~2->proc~nc_put_att_global error error proc~nc_check->error nf90_strerror nf90_strerror proc~nc_check->nf90_strerror proc~nc_create_file->proc~nc_check nf90_create nf90_create proc~nc_create_file->nf90_create proc~nc_def_dim->proc~nc_check nf90_def_dim nf90_def_dim proc~nc_def_dim->nf90_def_dim proc~nc_put_att->proc~nc_check nf90_put_att nf90_put_att proc~nc_put_att->nf90_put_att proc~nc_put_att_global->proc~nc_check proc~nc_put_att_global->nf90_put_att Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface