j ) if ( h_val > NH_MIN_DEPTH ) then do k = 1 , nz ! Horizontal Laplacian horiz = h_val * inv_dx2 * ( p ( i + 1 , j , k ) - 2.0_wp * p ( i , j , k ) + p ( i - 1 , j , k )) & + h_val * inv_dy2 * ( p ( i , j + 1 , k ) - 2.0_wp * p ( i , j , k ) + p ( i , j - 1 , k )) ! Vertical coupling: pre-computed coefficients / h vl = 0.0_wp vh = 0.0_wp if ( k > 1 ) then vl = vert_lo ( k ) / h_val * ( p ( i , j , k - 1 ) - p ( i , j , k )) end if if ( k < nz ) then vh = vert_hi ( k ) / h_val * ( p ( i , j , k + 1 ) - p ( i , j , k )) end if Ap ( i , j , k ) = horiz + vl + vh end do else do k = 1 , nz Ap ( i , j , k ) = 0.0_wp end do end if end do end subroutine apply_poisson_operator_fast","tags":"","url":"proc/apply_poisson_operator_fast.html"},{"title":"apply_vertical_preconditioner – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine apply_vertical_preconditioner(h, dsig, r, z, nx, ny, nz, nghost, dx, dy, dt) Public only for the unit-test suite (no production module imports it).\nVertical-line preconditioner: solve M*z = r per (i,j) column M is the vertical tridiagonal part of the Poisson operator plus\nthe horizontal diagonal contribution. Thomas algorithm per column\n(serial in k, parallel over i,j via do concurrent). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h (nx,ny) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r (nx,ny,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: z (nx,ny,nz) integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: nghost real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dx real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dy real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~apply_vertical_preconditioner~~CallsGraph proc~apply_vertical_preconditioner apply_vertical_preconditioner local local proc~apply_vertical_preconditioner->local Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure 