e Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: cell_dt real(kind=wp), private :: dt_local integer, private :: k Source Code subroutine compute_timestep_unstr ( state , mesh ) !! Compute the CFL-limited timestep and store it in `state%dt`. !! Reads `max_speed`, `state%cfl`, `mesh%radius` only. Must run !! after the flux kernel; before any flux pass it returns !! `cfl * TIMESTEP_LARGE` (all max_speed still 0). type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer :: k real ( wp ) :: dt_local , cell_dt dt_local = TIMESTEP_LARGE do concurrent ( k = 1 : mesh % ncells_owned ) reduce ( min : dt_local ) if ( state % barotropic % max_speed ( k ) > TIMESTEP_EPSILON ) then cell_dt = mesh % radius ( k ) / state % barotropic % max_speed ( k ) if ( cell_dt < dt_local ) dt_local = cell_dt end if end do ! Clamp +inf back to TIMESTEP_LARGE: NVHPC's reduction(min:..) can ! return +inf when the loop never updates the accumulator (all ! max_speed = 0), so the \"no characteristics => dt = cfl * ! TIMESTEP_LARGE\" contract holds bit-exactly. if (. not . ( dt_local <= TIMESTEP_LARGE )) dt_local = TIMESTEP_LARGE state % dt = state % cfl * dt_local end subroutine compute_timestep_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/compute_timestep_unstr.html"},{"title":"fused_save_state_unstr – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine fused_save_state_unstr(state, mesh) Snapshot U&#94;n into the _backup slots once at step start, for the\nselectable-integrator generic path (the convex blend reads them). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh Called by proc~~fused_save_state_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~fused_save_state_unstr fused_save_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step_generic solver_unstr_step_generic proc~solver_unstr_step_generic->proc~fused_save_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step_generic proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: k integer, private :: n Source Code subroutine fused_save_state_unstr ( state , mesh ) !! Snapshot U&#94;n into the `_backup` slots once at step start, for the !! selectable-integrator generic path (the convex blend reads them). type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer :: k , n n = mesh % ncells_owned do concurrent ( k = 1 : n ) state % barotropic % stage_backup ( k ) = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) state % barotropic % xmom_backup ( k ) = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) state % barotropic % ymom_backup ( k ) = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) end do end subroutine fused_save_state_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/fused_save_state_unstr.html"},{"title":"fused_update_stage1_unstr – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine fused_update_stage1_unstr(state, mesh, dt) Stage 1: save + Euler update + friction/wind + protect Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~fused_update_stage1_unstr~~CallsGraph proc~fused_update_stage1_unstr fused_update_stage1_unstr local local proc~fused_update_stage1_unstr->local reduce reduce proc~fused_update_stage1_unstr->reduce Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~fused_update_stage1_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~fused_update_stage1_unstr fused_update_stage1_unstr proc~solver_unstr_step solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_step->proc~fused_update_stage1_unstr proc~rki_unstr_step rki_unstr_step proc~rki_unstr_step->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~solver_unstr_advance solver_unstr_advance proc~solver_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_step proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance rki_unstr_advance proc~rki_unstr_advance->proc~solver_unstr_advance proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: cf real(kind=wp), private :: denom real(kind=wp), private :: eps4 real(kind=wp), private :: fr_max_sq real(kind=wp), private :: fr_scale real(kind=wp), private :: h real(kind=wp), private :: h4 logical, private :: has_friction logical, private :: has_wind integer, private :: k real(kind=wp), private :: mass_error_local real(kind=wp), private :: min_h integer, private :: n real(kind=wp), private :: n_sq real(kind=wp), private :: speed real(kind=wp), private :: speed_sq real(kind=wp), private :: stage real(kind=wp), private :: tau_x real(kind=wp), private :: tau_y real(kind=wp), private :: u_val real(kind=wp), private :: v_val real(kind=wp), private :: xmom real(kind=wp), private :: ymom Source Code subroutine fused_update_stage1_unstr ( state , mesh , dt ) !! Stage 1: save + Euler update + friction/wind + protect type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: k , n real ( wp ) :: stage , xmom , ymom , h , eps4 , h4 real ( wp ) :: speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale real ( wp ) :: u_val , v_val , speed , cf , denom real ( wp ) :: n_sq , min_h , tau_x , tau_y real ( wp ) :: mass_error_local logical :: has_friction , has_wind n = mesh % ncells_owned has_friction = ( state % barotropic % manning_n > 0.0_wp ) has_wind = ( state % barotropic % wind_tau_x /= 0.0_wp ) . or . & ( state % barotropic % wind_tau_y /= 0.0_wp ) . or . & state % forcing % wind_active n_sq = state % barotropic % manning_n * state % barotropic % manning_n min_h = state % minimum_allowed_height eps4 = DESING_EPS ** 4 tau_x = state % barotropic % wind_tau_x / RHO_WATER tau_y = state % barotropic % wind_tau_y / RHO_WATER mass_error_local = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : n ) & local ( stage , xmom , ymom , h , h4 , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale , & u_val , v_val , speed , cf , denom ) & reduce ( + : mass_error_local ) ! ---- Read + save backup ---- stage = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) xmom = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) ymom = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) state % barotropic % stage_backup ( k ) = stage state % barotropic % xmom_backup ( k ) = xmom state % barotropic % ymom_backup ( k ) = ymom ! ---- Euler update ---- stage = stage + dt * state % barotropic % stage_eu ( k ) xmom = xmom + dt * state % barotropic % xmom_eu ( k ) ymom = ymom + dt * state % barotropic % ymom_eu ( k ) ! ---- Friction + wind ---- h = stage - state % barotropic % bed_cv ( k ) if ( h > min_h ) then if ( has_friction ) then u_val = xmom / h v_val = ymom / h speed = sqrt ( u_val * u_val + v_val * v_val ) cf = GRAVITY * n_sq / ( h ** ( 1.0_wp / 3.0_wp )) denom = 1.0_wp + dt * cf * speed / h xmom = xmom / denom ymom = ymom / denom end if if ( has_wind ) then xmom = xmom + dt * ( tau_x + state % forcing % wind_x ( k ) / RHO_WATER ) ymom = ymom + dt * ( tau_y + state % forcing % wind_y ( k ) / RHO_WATER ) end if end if ! ---- Protect ---- if ( h < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry (or negative) -- zero momentum. xmom = 0.0_wp ymom = 0.0_wp else ! Thin-but-wet: KP07 desingularized velocity ! u = sqrt(2) h uh / sqrt(h&#94;4 + max(h&#94;4, eps&#94;4)), uh := h*u ! (identity for h >= eps, so applied only below eps), then ! the Froude backstop — blowup arrester only (triggers on a ! TRUE comparison, so NaN passes through and fails loudly). h4 = h ** 4 if ( h4 < eps4 ) then xmom = h * ( sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h * xmom / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 )) ymom = h * ( sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h * ymom / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 )) end if speed_sq = ( xmom ** 2 + ymom ** 2 ) / ( h * h ) fr_max_sq = FROUDE_BACKSTOP ** 2 * GRAVITY * h if ( speed_sq > fr_max_sq ) then fr_scale = sqrt ( fr_max_sq / speed_sq ) xmom = xmom * fr_scale ymom = ymom * fr_scale end if end if if ( h < 0.0_wp ) then mass_error_local = mass_error_local + ( - h ) * mesh % area ( k ) stage = state % barotropic % bed_cv ( k ) end if ! ---- Write back ---- state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) = stage state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) = xmom state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) = ymom end do state % mass_error = state % mass_error + mass_error_local end subroutine fused_update_stage1_unstr","tags":"","url":"proc/fused_update_stage1_unstr.html"},{"title":"fused_update_stage2_unstr – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine fused_update_stage2_unstr(state, mesh, dt) Stage 2: Euler update + friction/wind + protect + RK2 average + protect Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~fused_update_stage2_unstr~~CallsGraph proc~fused_update_stage2_unstr fused_update_stage2_unstr local local proc~fused_update_stage2_unstr->local reduce reduce proc~fused_update_stage2_unstr->reduce Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called