n->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code function device_num () result ( num ) !! Active OpenACC device number, or `-1` on CPU builds.  Kept !! private — only the budget logger needs it. integer :: num #ifdef RAKALI_HAS_OPENACC_RUNTIME num = acc_get_device_num ( acc_get_device_type ()) #else num = - 1 #endif end function device_num","tags":"","url":"proc/device_num.html"},{"title":"two_dp – Rakali","text":"private pure function two_dp(x) result(str) Format a real to exactly two decimal places without leading\nblanks ( write with an f edit descriptor, then adjustl +\ntrim). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~two_dp~~CalledByGraph proc~two_dp two_dp proc~mem_format_bytes mem_format_bytes proc~mem_format_bytes->proc~two_dp proc~mem_log_computed_budget mem_log_computed_budget proc~mem_log_computed_budget->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_computed_line mem_log_computed_line proc~mem_log_computed_line->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_device_actuals mem_log_device_actuals proc~mem_log_device_actuals->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_device_growth mem_log_device_growth proc~mem_log_device_growth->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_state_budget mem_log_state_budget proc~mem_log_state_budget->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~mem_log_device_actuals proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~mem_log_device_growth proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~mem_log_state_budget proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~log_run_header log_run_header proc~log_run_header->proc~mem_log_computed_budget proc~log_run_header->proc~mem_log_computed_line proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal proc~init_local_state->proc~log_run_header Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=32), private :: buf Source Code pure function two_dp ( x ) result ( str ) !! Format a real to exactly two decimal places without leading !! blanks (`write` with an `f` edit descriptor, then `adjustl` + !! trim). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x character ( len = :), allocatable :: str character ( len = 32 ) :: buf write ( buf , \"(f0.2)\" ) x ! `f0.2` of a value < 1 emits \".50\" on some compilers; prefix a 0. if ( buf ( 1 : 1 ) == \".\" ) then str = \"0\" // trim ( adjustl ( buf )) else str = trim ( adjustl ( buf )) end if end function two_dp","tags":"","url":"proc/two_dp.html"},{"title":"mem_log_computed_budget – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine mem_log_computed_budget(label, total_bytes) Log the COUNTED state-array footprint.  Unlike the RSS figure\n(host-only I/O buffers + library pages) and the device query\n(needs an OpenACC runtime), this is an exact sum of the state’s\nallocatable arrays — available on every toolchain, so a CPU build\ngets a real footprint line too.  Latching for the reconciliation\nis mem_set_counted_budget (separate, so the print can move to\nthe banner while the latch stays before enter_data ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: label integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: total_bytes Calls proc~~mem_log_computed_budget~~CallsGraph proc~mem_log_computed_budget mem_log_computed_budget info info proc~mem_log_computed_budget->info proc~mem_format_bytes mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_computed_budget->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~two_dp two_dp proc~mem_format_bytes->proc~two_dp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~mem_log_computed_budget~~CalledByGraph proc~mem_log_computed_budget mem_log_computed_budget proc~log_run_header log_run_header proc~log_run_header->proc~mem_log_computed_budget proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~log_run_header proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine mem_log_computed_budget ( label , total_bytes ) !! Log the COUNTED state-array footprint.  Unlike the RSS figure !! (host-only I/O buffers + library pages) and the device query !! (needs an OpenACC runtime), this is an exact sum of the state's !! allocatable arrays — available on every toolchain, so a CPU build !! gets a real footprint line too.  Latching for the reconciliation !! is `mem_set_counted_budget` (separate, so the print can move to !! the banner while the latch stays before `enter_data`). character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: total_bytes ! Two-space indent + four-space breakdown so the block nests cleanly ! under the driver's post-setup banner (top-level items at two spaces, ! sub-items at four). call logger % info ( \"  Memory:   state arrays counted ~ \" // & mem_format_bytes ( total_bytes ) // \" (\" // trim ( label ) // & \", exact allocatable footprint)\" ) end subroutine mem_log_computed_budget","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_log_computed_budget.html"},{"title":"mem_log_computed_line – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine mem_log_computed_line(label, bytes) Log one indented breakdown line for a component of the counted\nfootprint (barotropic / layers / closures / …).  Skipped when the\ncomponent is empty so gated-off slots don’t clutter the report. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: label integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: bytes Calls proc~~mem_log_computed_line~~CallsGraph proc~mem_log_computed_line mem_log_computed_line info info proc~mem_log_computed_line->info proc~mem_format_bytes mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_computed_line->proc~mem_format_bytes proc~two_dp two_dp proc~mem_format_bytes->proc~two_dp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~mem_log_computed_line~~CalledByGraph proc~mem_log_computed_line mem_log_computed_line proc~log_run_header log_run_header proc~log_run_header->proc~mem_log_computed_line proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~init_local_state->proc~log_run_header proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine mem_log_computed_line ( label , bytes ) !! Log one indented breakdown line for a component of the counted !! footprint (barotropic / layers / closures / …).  Skipped when the !! component is empty so gated-off slots don't clutter the report. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: bytes if ( bytes <= 0_int64 ) return call logger % info ( \"    \" // trim ( label ) // \": \" // mem_format_bytes ( bytes )) end subroutine mem_log_computed_line","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_log_computed_line.html"},{"title":"mem_log_device_actuals – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine mem_log_device_actuals(label) Log actual device memory after enter_data : the device-wide\nusage ( used = total - free — includes the CUDA context and\nany other process on a shared device) plus the MEASURED state\nmapping delta (free-before-mapping minus free-now; accurate to\nNVHPC pool granularity, ~a few MB).  Latches the post-mapping\nusage as the baseline for mem_log_device_growth .  Silent\nno-op when device queries are unavailable (CPU build). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: label Calls proc~~mem_log_device_actuals~~CallsGraph proc~mem_log_device_actuals mem_log_device_actuals info info proc~mem_log_device_actuals->info proc~mem_device_free_bytes mem_device_free_bytes proc~mem_log_device_actuals->proc~mem_device_free_bytes proc~mem_device_total_bytes mem_device_total_bytes proc~mem_log_device_actuals->proc~mem_device_total_bytes proc~mem_format_bytes mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_device_actuals->proc~mem_format_bytes warning warning proc~mem_log_device_actuals->warning proc~two_dp two_dp proc~mem_format_bytes->proc~two_dp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~mem_log_device_actuals~~CalledByGraph proc~mem_log_device_actuals mem_log_device_actuals proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~mem_log_device_actuals proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int64), private :: free_b integer(kind=int64), private :: total_b integer(kind=int64), private :: used_b Source Code subroutine mem_log_device_actuals ( label ) !! Log actual device memory after `enter_data`: the device-wide !! usage (`used = total - free` — includes the CUDA context and !! any other process on a shared device) plus the MEASURED state !! mapping delta (free-before-mapping minus free-now; accurate to !! NVHPC pool granularity, ~a few MB).  Latches the post-mapping !! usage as the baseline for `mem_log_device_growth`.  Silent !! no-op when device queries are unavailable (CPU build). character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label integer ( int64 ) :: free_b , total_b , used_b free_b = mem_device_free_bytes () total_b = mem_device_total_bytes () if ( free_b < 0_int64 . or . total_b < 0_int64 ) return used_b = total_b - free_b call logger % info ( \"device memory in use: \" // mem_format_bytes ( used_b ) // & \" of \" // mem_format_bytes ( total_b ) // \" (\" // trim ( label ) // & \"; includes CUDA context ~300-500 MB + other processes)\" ) if ( free_before_map >= 0_int64 ) then block integer ( int64 ) :: mapped_b , tol_b mapped_b = max ( free_before_map - free_b , 0_int64 ) call logger % info ( \"  state mapped: ~\" // mem_format_bytes ( mapped_b ) // & \" (device-measured; shared-device activity can perturb)\" ) ! Reconcile the MEASURED mapping against the COUNTED footprint. ! Overshoot past the tolerance means the device mapped more than ! every bytes() term accounts for — a state array is almost ! certainly missing from the count (the drift the counted total ! would otherwise hide).  Under-count from lazy/host-only arrays ! is expected and stays silent. if ( counted_state_bytes > 0_int64 ) then tol_b = counted_state_bytes + & int ( COUNT_RECONCILE_FRAC * real ( counted_state_bytes , wp ), int64 ) + & COUNT_RECONCILE_FLOOR if ( mapped_b > tol_b ) then call logger % warning ( \"device mapped ~\" // mem_format_bytes ( mapped_b ) // & \" but only ~\" // mem_format_bytes ( counted_state_bytes ) // & \" counted — a state array is likely missing from a \" // & \"bytes() term (memory-accounting drift)\" ) end if end if end block end if ! Baselines for post-setup growth reporting. used_after_map = used_b used_steady = - 1_int64 growth_warned = . false . end subroutine mem_log_device_actuals","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_log_device_actuals.html"},{"title":"mem_log_device_growth – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine mem_log_device_growth(label, quiet) Report device-memory growth since the post- enter_data baseline.  Two allocations land AFTER the setup-time report and\nwould otherwise stay invisible: the lazy first-call kernel\nworkspaces ( *_workspace_ensure , ~33% of the coastal device\nfootprint) and the one-off CUDA runtime/kernel reservation at\nfirst launch (GBs — module-header offset 3).  Call this in the\nend-of-run summary (prints usage + the “grew ~X after setup”\nattribution, so even a 10-step run shows the true footprint)\nand at the periodic status with quiet=.true. (no info lines).\nThe one-shot leak WARNING measures PROGRESSIVE growth — past GROWTH_WARN_FRAC of the steady baseline latched at the first\npost-setup sample — so the expected one-offs never trip it.\nSilent no-op on CPU builds or when the baseline was never\nlatched. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: label logical, intent(in), optional :: quiet Calls proc~~mem_log_device_growth~~CallsGraph proc~mem_log_device_growth mem_log_device_growth info info proc~mem_log_device_growth->info proc~mem_device_used_bytes mem_device_used_bytes proc~mem_log_device_growth->proc~mem_device_used_bytes proc~mem_format_bytes mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_device_growth->proc~mem_format_bytes warning warning proc~mem_log_device_growth->warning proc~mem_device_free_bytes mem_device_free_bytes proc~mem_device_used_bytes->proc~mem_device_free_bytes proc~mem_device_total_bytes mem_device_total_bytes proc~mem_device_used_bytes->proc~mem_device_total_bytes proc~two_dp two_dp proc~mem_format_bytes->proc~two_dp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~mem_log_device_growth~~CalledByGraph proc~mem_log_device_growth mem_log_device_growth proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~mem_log_device_growth proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int64), private :: growth_b logical, private :: quiet_mode integer(kind=int64), private :: used_b Source Code subroutine mem_log_device_growth ( label , quiet ) !! Report device-memory growth since the post-`enter_data` !! baseline.  Two allocations land AFTER the setup-time report and !! would otherwise stay invisible: the lazy first-call kernel !! workspaces (`*_workspace_ensure`, ~33% of the coastal device !! footprint) and the one-off CUDA runtime/kernel reservation at !! first launch (GBs — module-header offset 3).  Call this in the !! end-of-run summary (prints usage + the \"grew ~X after setup\" !! attribution, so even a 10-step run shows the true footprint) !! and at the periodic status with `quiet=.true.` (no info lines). !! The one-shot leak WARNING measures PROGRESSIVE growth — past !! `GROWTH_WARN_FRAC` of the steady baseline latched at the first !! post-setup sample — so the expected one-offs never trip it. !! Silent no-op on CPU builds or when the baseline was never !! latched. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label logical , intent ( in ), optional :: quiet integer ( int64 ) :: used_b , growth_b logical :: quiet_mode quiet_mode = . false . if ( present ( quiet )) quiet_mode = quiet used_b = mem_device_used_bytes () if ( used_b < 0_int64 . or . used_after_map < 0_int64 ) return growth_b = used_b - used_after_map if (. not . quiet_mode ) then call logger % info ( \"device memory in use: \" // mem_format_bytes ( used_b ) // & \" (\" // trim ( label ) // \")\" ) if ( growth_b > 0_int64 ) then call logger % info ( \"  grew ~\" // mem_format_bytes ( growth_b ) // & \" after setup (lazy kernel workspaces + one-off \" // & \"CUDA kernel/runtime reservation)\" ) end if end if if ( used_steady < 0_int64 ) then ! First post-setup sample: the one-off reservations have landed; ! this is the steady baseline for progressive-growth (leak) ! detection. used_steady = used_b else if (. not . growth_warned . and . & real ( used_b - used_steady , wp ) > & GROWTH_WARN_FRAC * real ( used_steady , wp )) then call logger % warning ( \"device memory grew ~\" // & mem_format_bytes ( used_b - used_steady ) // & \" past the steady post-setup baseline (\" // & mem_format_bytes ( used_steady ) // & \") — possible device-memory leak (\" // trim ( label ) // \")\" ) growth_warned = . true . end if end subroutine mem_log_device_growth","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_log_device_growth.html"},{"title":"mem_log_state_budget – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine mem_log_state_budget(label, host_growth_bytes) Log the pre-mapping memory budget.  Always logs the host-side\nallocation growth (ADVISORY — includes host-only I/O buffers +\nlibrary pages, NOT a device estimate); when the device queries\nsucceed it also logs the device number + free/total and latches\nthe free-memory snapshot that mem_log_device_actuals turns\ninto the measured mapping delta.  Warns when the host growth\n(a conservative upper bound on what enter_data can map)\nexceeds 95% of free device memory — the regime where enter_data is likely to abort. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: label integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: host_growth_bytes Calls proc~~mem_log_state_budget~~CallsGraph proc~mem_log_state_budget mem_log_state_budget info info proc~mem_log_state_budget->info proc~device_num device_num proc~mem_log_state_budget->proc~device_num proc~mem_device_free_bytes mem_device_free_bytes proc~mem_log_state_budget->proc~mem_device_free_bytes proc~mem_device_total_bytes mem_device_total_bytes proc~mem_log_state_budget->proc~mem_device_total_bytes proc~mem_format_bytes mem_format_bytes proc~mem_log_state_budget->proc~mem_format_bytes to_string to_string proc~mem_log_state_budget->to_string warning warning proc~mem_log_state_budget->warning proc~two_dp two_dp proc~mem_format_bytes->proc~two_dp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~mem_log_state_budget~~CalledByGraph proc~mem_log_state_budget mem_log_state_budget proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~mem_log_state_budget proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: devnum integer(kind=int64), private :: free_b integer(kind=int64), private :: total_b Source Code subroutine mem_log_state_budget ( label , host_growth_bytes ) !! Log the pre-mapping memory budget.  Always logs the host-side !! allocation growth (ADVISORY — includes host-only I/O buffers + !! library pages, NOT a device estimate); when the device queries !! succeed it also logs the device number + free/total and latches !! the free-memory snapshot that `mem_log_device_actuals` turns !! into the measured mapping delta.  Warns when the host growth !! (a conservative upper bound on what `enter_data` can map) !! exceeds 95% of free device memory — the regime where !! `enter_data` is likely to abort. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: host_growth_bytes integer ( int64 ) :: free_b , total_b integer :: devnum call logger % info ( \"Memory budget (\" // trim ( label ) // \"): host allocations across setup ~ \" // & mem_format_bytes ( host_growth_bytes ) // & \" (RSS growth; advisory, not a device estimate)\" ) free_b = mem_device_free_bytes () total_b = mem_device_total_bytes () if ( free_b < 0_int64 . or . total_b < 0_int64 ) return ! CPU build. ! Baseline for the measured mapping delta.  The property query ! above already forced CUDA context creation, so the delta across ! enter_data excludes the ~300-500 MB context cost. free_before_map = free_b devnum = device_num () call logger % info ( \"  device \" // to_string ( devnum ) // \" free before mapping: \" // & mem_format_bytes ( free_b ) // \" of \" // mem_format_bytes ( total_b ) // & \" (host-growth upper bound: \" // & mem_format_bytes ( host_growth_bytes ) // \")\" ) if ( real ( host_growth_bytes , wp ) > 0.95_wp * real ( free_b , wp )) then call logger % warning ( \"device memory likely insufficient — mapping <= \" // & mem_format_bytes ( host_growth_bytes ) // \" with only \" // & mem_format_bytes ( free_b ) // \" free\" ) end if end subroutine mem_log_state_budget","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_log_state_budget.html"},{"title":"mem_set_counted_budget – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine mem_set_counted_budget(total_bytes) Latch the COUNTED state-array footprint for the enter_data reconciliation, WITHOUT logging.  Must run before mem_log_device_actuals (the reconciliation reads this), even\nwhen the human-readable budget is printed later (e.g. folded into\nthe driver’s post-setup banner). total_bytes is the sum of\nevery state bytes() term (0 for gated-off slots). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: total_bytes Called by proc~~mem_set_counted_budget~~CalledByGraph proc~mem_set_counted_budget mem_set_counted_budget proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~mem_set_counted_budget proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine mem_set_counted_budget ( total_bytes ) !! Latch the COUNTED state-array footprint for the `enter_data` !! reconciliation, WITHOUT logging.  Must run before !! `mem_log_device_actuals` (the reconciliation reads this), even !! when the human-readable budget is printed later (e.g. folded into !! the driver's post-setup banner).  `total_bytes` is the sum of !! every state `bytes()` term (0 for gated-off slots). integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: total_bytes counted_state_bytes = total_bytes end subroutine mem_set_counted_budget","tags":"","url":"proc/mem_set_counted_budget.html"},{"title":"arr_bytes – Rakali","text":"public interface arr_bytes Byte footprint of an allocatable array (0 when unallocated), so a\ngated-off slot naturally contributes nothing to a counted total.\nThe COUNTED companion to the runtime’s MEASURED free-memory\ndelta: each *_state_t sums its own arrays through this, the\ndriver reports the total before enter_data (works on CPU\nbuilds too, where there is no device query), and mem_log_device_actuals reconciles the count against the\nmeasured mapping — a state array added without a matching bytes() term makes the measured map exceed the count and\nself-announces the drift (the anti-rot guard for the otherwise\nrot-prone per-slot count). Calls interface~~arr_bytes~~CallsGraph interface~arr_bytes arr_bytes proc~arr_bytes_i1 arr_bytes_i1 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_i1 proc~arr_bytes_i2 arr_bytes_i2 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_i2 proc~arr_bytes_i3 arr_bytes_i3 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_i3 proc~arr_bytes_l1 arr_bytes_l1 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_l1 proc~arr_bytes_l2 arr_bytes_l2 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_l2 proc~arr_bytes_l3 arr_bytes_l3 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_l3 proc~arr_bytes_r1 arr_bytes_r1 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_r1 proc~arr_bytes_r2 arr_bytes_r2 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_r2 proc~arr_bytes_r3 arr_bytes_r3 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_r3 proc~arr_bytes_r4 arr_bytes_r4 interface~arr_bytes->proc~arr_bytes_r4 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by interface~~arr_bytes~~CalledByGraph interface~arr_bytes arr_bytes proc~barotropic_state_bytes barotropic_state_t%barotropic_state_bytes proc~barotropic_state_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~multilayer_state_bytes multilayer_state_t%multilayer_state_bytes proc~multilayer_state_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~tracer_bytes tracer_t%tracer_bytes proc~multilayer_state_bytes->proc~tracer_bytes proc~nh_state_bytes nonhydrostatic_state_t%nh_state_bytes proc~nh_state_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~scratch_3d_buffer_bytes scratch_3d_buffer_t%scratch_3d_buffer_bytes proc~scratch_3d_buffer_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~state_bytes state_t%state_bytes proc~state_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~state_bytes->proc~barotropic_state_bytes proc~surface_forcing_bytes surface_forcing_t%surface_forcing_bytes proc~surface_forcing_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~tracer_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~state_bytes proc~init_local_state init_local_state proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_local_state proc~log_run_header log_run_header proc~log_run_header->proc~state_bytes proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal proc~init_local_state->proc~log_run_header Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Module Procedures private pure function arr_bytes_r1 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in), allocatable :: a (:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_r2 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in), allocatable :: a (:,:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_r3 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in), allocatable :: a (:,:,:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_r4 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in), allocatable :: a (:,:,:,:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_i1 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in), allocatable :: a (:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_i2 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in), allocatable :: a (:,:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_i3 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in), allocatable :: a (:,:,:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_l1 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical, intent(in), allocatable :: a (:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_l2 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical, intent(in), allocatable :: a (:,:) Return Value integer(kind=int64) private pure function arr_bytes_l3 (a) result(b) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical, intent(in), allocatable :: a (:,:,:) Return Value integer(kind=int64)","tags":"","url":"interface/arr_bytes.html"},{"title":"bilinear_time – Rakali","text":"private pure function bilinear_time(fld_lo, fld_hi, i0, j0, i1, j1, w00, w10, w01, w11, alpha) result(val) Bilinear spatial interpolation + linear temporal interpolation Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: fld_lo (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: fld_hi (:,:) integer, intent(in) :: i0 integer, intent(in) :: j0 integer, intent(in) :: i1 integer, intent(in) :: j1 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: w00 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: w10 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: w01 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: w11 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: alpha Return Value real(kind=wp) Called by proc~~bilinear_time~~CalledByGraph proc~bilinear_time bilinear_time proc~forcing_update forcing_update proc~forcing_update->proc~bilinear_time proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~forcing_update proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: val_hi real(kind=wp), private :: val_lo Source Code pure function bilinear_time ( fld_lo , fld_hi , i0 , j0 , i1 , j1 , & w00 , w10 , w01 , w11 , alpha ) result ( val ) !! Bilinear spatial interpolation + linear temporal interpolation real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: fld_lo (:, :), fld_hi (:, :) integer , intent ( in ) :: i0 , j0 , i1 , j1 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: w00 , w10 , w01 , w11 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: alpha real ( wp ) :: val real ( wp ) :: val_lo , val_hi val_lo = w00 * fld_lo ( i0 , j0 ) + w10 * fld_lo ( i1 , j0 ) + & w01 * fld_lo ( i0 , j1 ) + w11 * fld_lo ( i1 , j1 ) val_hi = w00 * fld_hi ( i0 , j0 ) + w10 * fld_hi ( i1 , j0 ) + & w01 * fld_hi ( i0 , j1 ) + w11 * fld_hi ( i1 , j1 ) val = ( 1.0_wp - alpha ) * val_lo + alpha * val_hi end function bilinear_time","tags":"","url":"proc/bilinear_time.html"},{"title":"drag_coefficient – Rakali","text":"private pure function drag_coefficient(wind_speed) result(cd) Large & Pond (1981) drag coefficient for 10m wind, capped at\n2.5e-3 for extreme winds. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_speed 10m wind speed magnitude (m/s) Return Value real(kind=wp) Called by proc~~drag_coefficient~~CalledByGraph proc~drag_coefficient drag_coefficient proc~forcing_update forc