ne Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~forcing_destroy~~CalledByGraph proc~forcing_destroy forcing_destroy proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~forcing_destroy proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine forcing_destroy ( forc ) !! Clean up forcing state and close NetCDF file type ( forcing_t ), intent ( inout ) :: forc if ( forc % ncid >= 0 ) then call nc_close ( forc % ncid ) forc % ncid = - 1 end if if ( allocated ( forc % lon )) deallocate ( forc % lon ) if ( allocated ( forc % lat )) deallocate ( forc % lat ) if ( allocated ( forc % time )) deallocate ( forc % time ) if ( allocated ( forc % u10_lo )) deallocate ( forc % u10_lo ) if ( allocated 