parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: varid Source Code subroutine read_forcing_grid ( forc , ncid ) !! Read lon, lat, time coordinate arrays from the forcing file type ( forcing_t ), intent ( inout ) :: forc integer , intent ( in ) :: ncid integer :: varid ! Read dimensions call nc_get_dim_len ( ncid , \"lon\" , forc % nlon ) call nc_get_dim_len ( ncid , \"lat\" , forc % nlat ) call nc_get_dim_len ( ncid , \"time\" , forc % ntime ) ! Read coordinate arrays allocate ( forc % lon ( forc % nlon )) allocate ( forc % lat ( forc % nlat )) allocate ( forc % time ( forc % ntime )) call nc_get_varid ( ncid , \"lon\" , varid ) call nc_check ( nf90_get_var ( ncid , varid , forc % lon ), \"reading lon\" ) call nc_get_varid ( ncid , \"lat\" , varid ) call nc_check ( nf90_get_var ( ncid , varid , forc % lat ), \"reading lat\" ) call nc_get_varid ( ncid , \"time\" , varid ) call nc_check ( nf90_get_var ( ncid , varid , forc % time ), \"reading time\" ) end subroutine read_forcing_grid","tags":"","url":"proc/read_forcing_grid.html"},{"title":"multilayer_state_bytes – Rakali","text":"private pure function multilayer_state_bytes(this) result(nbytes) Counted allocatable footprint of the multilayer slot: the layer\nprognostics + RK2 saves + vcoord/rho tables + the tracer registry\n(each tracer sums its own arrays) + the gated KPP / k-epsilon /\nsediment workspaces (0 when their closure is off). Type Bound multilayer_state_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multilayer_state_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=int64) Calls proc~~multilayer_state_bytes~~CallsGraph proc~multilayer_state_bytes multilayer_state_t%multilayer_state_bytes interface~arr_bytes arr_bytes proc~multilayer_state_bytes->interface~arr_bytes proc~tracer_bytes tracer_t%tracer_bytes proc~multilayer_state_bytes->proc~trace