nx integer, private :: ny integer, private :: nz_ml Source Code subroutine multilayer_state_init ( this , grid ) !! Allocate all multilayer arrays at the grid size and configured !! layer count, init the vcoord object, copy `vcoord%z_ref` into !! the GPU-mappable `vcoord_z_ref`, allocate the rho-ref profile, !! and register S + T.  Caller must set `nz_ml`, !! `vcoord%coord_type`, `vcoord%remap_method`, and any other !! vcoord parameters first. class ( multilayer_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer :: nx , ny , nz_ml nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nz_ml = this % nz_ml call this % vcoord % init ( nz_ml , this % vcoord % coord_type , & this % vcoord % remap_method ) allocate ( this % dsig_ml ( nz_ml )) this % dsig_ml = this % vcoord % dsig_target ! GPU-mappable copy of z_ref (avoids derived-type attach issues) allocate ( this % vcoord_z_ref ( 0 : nz_ml ), source = 0.0_wp ) if ( allocated ( this % vcoord % z_ref )) then this % vcoord_z_ref = this % vcoord % z_ref end if ! Full MOM6 z* per-column z_ref.  Allocated here; the per-cell ! contents are filled later from the bathymetry by ! `ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full` (called from rki_init). if ( this % vcoord % coord_type == VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL ) then allocate ( this % vcoord_z_ref_col ( 0 : nz_ml , nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if allocate ( this % h_layer ( nx , ny , nz_ml ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hu_layer ( nx , ny , nz_ml ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hv_layer ( nx , ny , nz_ml ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % h_layer0 ( nx , ny , nz_ml ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hu_layer0 ( nx , ny , nz_ml ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hv_layer0 ( nx , ny , nz_ml ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % w_ml ( nx , ny , nz_ml + 1 ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hu_ml_pre ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hv_ml_pre ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % rho_layer ( nx , ny , nz_ml ), source = 0.0_wp ) ! KPP boundary-layer workspace — only when the overlay is enabled ! (caller sets `vmix_use_kpp` before this routine).  Left ! unallocated on the default PP81 path. if ( this % vmix_use_kpp ) then allocate ( this % kpp_bl_depth ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % kpp_u_star ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % kpp_buoy_flux ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if ! k-epsilon interface-shaped prognostics — only when the closure is on. ! Seeded with small positive floors so nu_t = c_mu k&#94;2/eps is finite on ! the first step (the closure self-bootstraps from these). if ( this % vmix_use_keps ) then allocate ( this % keps_tke ( nx , ny , nz_ml + 1 ), source = 1.0e-6_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_eps ( nx , ny , nz_ml + 1 ), source = 1.0e-8_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_nut ( nx , ny , nz_ml + 1 ), source = 1.0e-4_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_kt ( nx , ny , nz_ml + 1 ), source = 1.0e-4_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_ustar_b ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_ustar_s ( nx , ny ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if ! Bed sediment reservoir — only when sediment transport is enabled ! (caller sets use_sediment + sediment_bed_init before this routine). if ( this % use_sediment ) then allocate ( this % bed_sediment ( nx , ny ), source = this % sediment_bed_init ) end if ! Reference-density profile: 100 samples, sub-metre resolution. this % nz_ref = 100 allocate ( this % rho_ref ( 0 : this % nz_ref ), source = 0.0_wp ) this % rho_ref_dz = 0.0_wp ! Default tracer registry: salinity at index 1, temperature at ! index 2.  Scalar config + CF metadata are overlaid by ! `register_default_tracers` (rki_state) on the namelist path. allocate ( this % tracers ( 2 )) this % idx_salinity = 1 this % idx_temperature = 2 call this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% init ( grid , nz_ml ) call this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% init ( grid , nz_ml ) this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% name = \"salinity\" this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% long_name = \"Sea water salinity\" this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% units = \"PSU\" this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% standard_name = \"sea_water_salinity\" this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% name = \"temperature\" this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% long_name = \"Sea water potential temperature\" this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% units = \"degC\" this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% standard_name = \"sea_water_potential_temperature\" end subroutine multilayer_state_init","tags":"","url":"proc/multilayer_state_init.html"},{"title":"semi_implicit_grid_conflict – Rakali","text":"public pure function semi_implicit_grid_conflict(cfg) result(conflict) .true. when the config asks for time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\" on\nanything but an unstructured grid.  Semi-implicit stepping exists\nonly on the triangular backend; validate_config and the state\ninitialisers reject the combination. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg Return Value logical Called by proc~~semi_implicit_grid_conflict~~CalledByGraph proc~semi_implicit_grid_conflict semi_implicit_grid_conflict proc~validate_config validate_config proc~validate_config->proc~semi_implicit_grid_conflict proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure logical function semi_implicit_grid_conflict ( cfg ) result ( conflict ) !! `.true.` when the config asks for `time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\"` on !! anything but an unstructured grid.  Semi-implicit stepping exists !! only on the triangular backend; `validate_config` and the state !! initialisers reject the combination. type ( config_t ), intent ( in ) :: cfg conflict = ( trim ( adjustl ( cfg % time_scheme )) == \"semi_implicit\" ) . and . & ( trim ( adjustl ( cfg % grid_type )) /= \"unstructured\" ) end function semi_implicit_grid_conflict","tags":"","url":"proc/semi_implicit_grid_conflict.html"},{"title":"si_bc_supported – Rakali","text":"private pure function si_bc_supported(bc_str) result(ok) .true. iff the edge type is wired into the semi-implicit\neta-solve (2D and 3D-ML paths alike): wall (mirror ghost =>\nexact zero face flux) or the two Dirichlet-eta seeds (tidal /\nclamped).  Everything else (open/Flather, chapman, sponge,\nnested, inflow, discharge) fills ghost momentum the Helmholtz\noperator walls off => a silent mass leak; validate_config\naborts on those. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: bc_str Return Value logical Called by proc~~si_bc_supported~~CalledByGraph proc~si_bc_supported si_bc_supported proc~validate_config validate_config proc~validate_config->proc~si_bc_supported proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~validate_config proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure logical function si_bc_supported ( bc_str ) result ( ok ) !! .true. iff the edge type is wired into the semi-implicit !! eta-solve (2D and 3D-ML paths alike): wall (mirror ghost => !! exact zero face flux) or the two Dirichlet-eta seeds (tidal / !! clamped).  Everything else (open/Flather, chapman, sponge, !! nested, inflow, discharge) fills ghost momentum the Helmholtz !! operator walls off => a silent mass leak; validate_config !! aborts on those. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: bc_str select case ( trim ( bc_str )) case ( \"wall\" , \"tidal\" , \"clamped\" ) ok = . true . case default ok = . false . end select end function si_bc_supported","tags":"","url":"proc/si_bc_supported.html"},{"title":"build_rakali_schema – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine build_rakali_schema(cfg, schema) Register the validated groups + the still-external groups onto schema , capturing defaults from cfg . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(out) :: schema Calls proc~~build_rakali_schema~~CallsGraph proc~build_rakali_schema build_rakali_schema proc~register_boundary register_boundary proc~build_rakali_schema->pro