graphs. Called by proc~~read_config_from_string_impl~~CalledByGraph proc~read_config_from_string_impl read_config_from_string_impl proc~read_config_from_string read_config_from_string proc~read_config_from_string->proc~read_config_from_string_impl proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~read_config_from_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=:), private, allocatable :: lines (:) integer, private :: n_lines Source Code subroutine read_config_from_string_impl ( text , cfg , sch ) !! Body of [[read_config_from_string]] — mirrors read_config_impl !! with the line array replacing the file unit. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: text type ( config_t ), target , intent ( out ) :: cfg type ( nml_schema_t ), intent ( out ) :: sch character ( len = :), allocatable :: lines (:) integer :: n_lines call build_rakali_schema ( cfg , sch ) ! Empty buffer → keep pristine defaults (mirrors the missing-file ! branch of read_config_impl). if ( len_trim ( text ) == 0 ) return call split_to_lines ( text , lines , n_lines ) ! Strict schema parse from the same lines: validate + APPLY every ! migrated group