i_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine read_config_impl ( filename , cfg , sch ) !! Body of [[read_config]]: build the strict schema (capturing !! defaults from the pristine `cfg` field initialisers), parse the !! file (validate + apply straight into `cfg`), run the post-parse !! time-unit cascade. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: filename !! Path to the namelist input file type ( config_t ), target , intent ( out ) :: cfg !! Populated configuration type ( nml_schema_t ), intent ( out ) :: sch !! Built + parsed schema (aliases into `cfg`) ! `cfg` arrives at its pristine field-initialiser defaults.  Every ! namelist group is now on the strict schema: build it (capturing ! those defaults), then parse — which validates AND applies every ! override straight into `cfg` via the schema's key pointers.  No ! native readers, no flat shadow locals, no copy-back remain. ! Build the strict schema so its key constructors capture defaults ! from the pristine `cfg` field initialisers. call build_rakali_schema ( cfg , sch ) ! A missing namelist file is not an error — the pristine `cfg` ! defaults stand (production main.F90 fails loudly on a missing ! file earlier; tests + the FFI rely on this defaults-on-absent ! behaviour).  Guard the strict parse so it never error-stops on ! \"cannot open file\". block logical :: file_exists inquire ( file = trim ( filename ), exist = file_exists ) if (. not . file_exists ) then call logger % debug ( \"Namelist file not found, keeping defaults: \" // trim ( filename )) return end if end block ! Strict schema parse: validate + APPLY every group straight into ! `cfg`.  Strict (no status/errors args) → on any unknown key / ! range / enum violation it logs the full report and error-stops, ! for EVERY caller (driver, FFI, unit tests). call sch % parse ( trim ( filename )) call apply_time_unit_cascade ( cfg ) end subroutine read_config_impl","tags":"","url":"proc/read_config_impl.html"},{"title":"register_boundary – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine register_boundary(cfg, schema) &boundary_nml : per-side BC types, tidal forcing, inflow/\ndischarge/clamped/sponge/nesting parameters.  The four bc_* keys are enums over the bc_type_from_string accepted set. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema Calls proc~~register_boundary~~CallsGraph proc~register_boundary register_boundary proc~group_add nml_group_t%group_add proc~register_boundary->proc~group_add proc~nml_enum nml_enum proc~register_boundary->proc~nml_enum proc~nml_int nml_int proc~register_boundary->proc~nml_int proc~nml_real nml_real proc~register_boundary->proc~nml_real proc~nml_real_array nml_real_array proc~register_boundary->proc~nml_real_array proc~nml_string nml_string proc~register_boundary->proc~nml_string proc~schema_add_group nml_schema_t%schema_add_group proc~register_boundary->proc~schema_add_group error error proc~group_add->error proc~lower lower proc~group_add->proc~lower proc~schema_add_group->error proc~schema_add_group->proc~lower proc~move_group move_group proc~schema_add_group->proc~move_group Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~register_boundary~~CalledByGraph proc~register_boundary register_boundary proc~build_rakali_schema build_rakali_schema proc~build_rakali_schema->proc~register_boundary proc~read_config_from_string_impl read_config_from_string_impl proc~read_config_from_string_impl->proc~build_rakali_schema proc~read_config_impl read_config_impl proc~read_config_impl->proc~build_rakali_schema proc~read_config read_config proc~read_config->proc~read_config_impl proc~read_config_from_string read_config_from_string proc~read_config_from_string->proc~read_config_from_string_impl proc~rki_create rki_create proc~rki_create->proc~read_config proc~rki_create_from_string rki_create_from_string proc~rki_create_from_string->proc~read_config_from_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_create proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_create_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=9), private, parameter :: bc_allowed (*) = [character(len=9)::\"wall\", \"open\", \"tidal\", \"nested\", \"inflow\", \"discharge\", \"clamped\", \"sponge\", \"chapman\"] type( nml_group_t ), private :: g real(kind=wp), private, pointer :: pa (:) integer, private, pointer :: pi real(kind=wp), private, pointer :: pr character(len=:), private, pointer :: ps Source Code subroutine register_boundary ( cfg , schema ) !! `&boundary_nml`: per-side BC types, tidal forcing, inflow/ !! discharge/clamped/sponge/nesting parameters.  The four `bc_*` !! keys are enums over the bc_type_from_string accepted set. type ( config_t ), target , intent ( in ) :: cfg type ( nml_schema_t ), intent ( inout ) :: schema type ( nml_group_t ) :: g real ( wp ), pointer :: pr real ( wp ), pointer :: pa (:) integer , pointer :: pi character ( len = :), pointer :: ps character ( len = 9 ), parameter :: bc_allowed ( * ) = & [ character ( len = 9 ) :: \"wall\" , \"open\" , \"tidal\" , \"nested\" , \"inflow\" , & \"discharge\" , \"clamped\" , \"sponge\" , \"chapman\" ] g % name = \"boundary\" g % doc = \"Boundary conditions, tidal forcing, inflow/discharge/sponge/nesting.\" ps => cfg % bc_west call g % add ( nml_enum ( \"bc_west\" , ps , \"West boundary type\" , allowed = bc_allowed )) ps => cfg % bc_east call g % add ( nml_enum ( \"bc_east\" , ps , \"East boundary type\" , allowed = bc_allowed )) ps => cfg % bc_south call g % add ( nml_enum ( \"bc_south\" , ps , \"South boundary type\" , allowed = bc_allowed )) ps => cfg % bc_north call g % add ( nml_enum ( \"bc_north\" , ps , \"North boundary type\" , allowed = bc_allowed )) pr => cfg % tidal_amplitude call g % add ( nml_real ( \"tidal_amplitude\" , pr , \"Tidal elevation amplitude (single-constituent)\" , units = \"m\" )) pr => cfg % tidal_period call g % add ( nml_real ( \"tidal_period\" , pr , \"Tidal period (single-constituent, default M2)\" , units = \"s\" )) pi => cfg % n_tidal_constituents call g % add ( nml_int ( \"n_tidal_constituents\" , pi , & \"Active tidal constituents (0 = legacy single)\" , min = 0 )) pa => cfg % tidal_amp call g % add ( nml_real_array ( \"tidal_amp\" , pa , \"Constituent amplitudes\" , units = \"m\" )) pa => cfg % tidal_phase call g % add ( nml_real_array ( \"tidal_phase\" , pa , \"Constituent phases\" , units = \"rad\" )) pa => cfg % tidal_omega call g % add ( nml_real_array ( \"tidal_omega\" , pa , \"Constituent angular frequencies\" , units = \"rad/s\" )) pr => cfg % inflow_velocity call g % add ( nml_real ( \"inflow_velocity\" , pr , \"Prescribed normal velocity for inflow BC\" , units = \"m/s\" )) pr => cfg % inflow_salinity call g % add ( nml_real ( \"inflow_salinity\" , pr , \"Inflow salinity (<0 = zero-gradient)\" , units = \"PSU\" )) pr => cfg % inflow_temperature call g % add ( nml_real ( \"inflow_temperature\" , pr , \"Inflow temperature (<0 = zero-gradient)\" , units = \"degC\" )) pr => cfg % discharge_flux call g % add ( nml_real ( \"discharge_flux\" , pr , \"Prescribed volume flux for discharge BC\" , units = \"m&#94;2/s\" )) pr => cfg % clamped_elevation call g % add ( nml_real ( \"clamped_elevation\" , pr , \"Prescribed surface elevation for clamped BC\" , units = \"m\" )) pi => cfg % sponge_width call g % add ( nml_int ( \"sponge_width\" , pi , \"Sponge layer width in cells\" , min = 0 )) pr => cfg % sponge_strength call g % add ( nml_real ( \"sponge_strength\" , pr , \"Sponge relaxation rate\" , units = \"1/s\" )) pr => cfg % sponge_h_ref call g % add ( nml_real ( \"sponge_h_ref\" , pr , \"Sponge reference depth\" , units = \"m\" )) ps => cfg % nesting_file call g % add ( nml_string ( \"nesting_file\" , ps , \"Parent-domain NetCDF output (empty = no nesting)\" )) pr => cfg % nesting_x_origin call g % add ( nml_real ( \"nesting_x_origin\" , pr , \"Child x-origin in parent coordinates\" , units = \"m\" )) pr => cfg % nesting_y_origin call g % add ( nml_real ( \"nesting_y_origin\" , pr , \"Child y-origin in parent coordinates\" , units = \"m\" )) call schema % add_group ( g ) end subroutine register_boundary","tags":"","url":"proc/register_boundary.html"},{"title":"register_grid – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine register_grid(cfg, schema) &grid_nml : structured-grid geometry. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema Calls proc~~register_grid~~CallsGraph proc~register_grid register_grid proc~group_add nml_group_t%group_add proc~register_grid->proc~group_add proc~nml_enum nml_enum proc~register_grid->proc~nml_enum proc~nml_int nml_int proc~register_grid->proc~nml_int proc~nml_real nml_real proc~register_grid->proc~nml_real proc~schema_add_group nml_schema_t%schema_add_group proc~register_grid->proc~schema_add_group error error proc~group_add->error proc~lower lower proc~group_add->proc~lower proc~schema_add_group->error proc~schema_add_group->proc~lower proc~move_group move_group proc~schema_add_group->proc~move_group Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~registe