 procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( nml_group_t ), private :: g integer, private, pointer :: pi logical, private, pointer :: pl real(kind=wp), private, pointer :: pr character(len=:), private, pointer :: ps Source Code subroutine register_si ( cfg , schema ) !! `&si_nml`: semi-implicit free-surface CG-solver controls.  Only !! consulted when `time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\"`; both knobs default !! to the pre-knob plain-CG behaviour (byte-identical). type ( config_t ), target , intent ( in ) :: cfg type ( nml_schema_t ), intent ( inout ) :: schema type ( nml_group_t ) :: g real ( wp ), pointer :: pr character ( len = :), pointer :: ps logical , pointer :: pl integer , pointer :: pi g % name = \"si\" g % doc = \"Semi-implicit free-surface CG-solver controls.\" ps => cfg % si_precond call g % add ( nml_enum ( \"precond\" , ps , & \"SI Helmholtz preconditioner: none (plain CG), jacobi (diagonal PCG), \" // & \"or mg (aggregation-multigrid V-cycle PCG)\" , & allowed = [ character ( len = 6 ) :: \"none\" , \"jacobi\" , \"mg\" ])) pr => cfg % si_rtol call g % add ( nml_real ( \"rtol\" , pr , & \"SI CG relative residual tolerance (||r||&#94;2 < rtol&#94;2*||rhs||&#94;2)\" , & min = 1.0e-30_wp )) pl => cfg % si_wetdry call g % add ( nml_logical ( \"wetdry\" , pl , & \"Casulli subgrid wetting/drying (V(eta) Newton diagonal); \" // & \"default off = byte-identical all-wet\" )) pi => cfg % si_wetdry_nsub call g % add ( nml_int ( \"wetdry_nsub\" , pi , & \"Subgrid sub-bottoms per cell for the wet/dry volume function \" // & \"(1 = flat cell bottom)\" , min = 1 )) ps => cfg % si_wetdry_bsub_fill call g % add ( nml_enum ( \"wetdry_bsub_fill\" , ps , & \"Sub-bottom table fill when nsub>=2: 'flat' (default, \" // & \"bit-identical) or 'linear' (analytic subgrid bed ramp)\" , & allowed = [ character ( len = 6 ) :: \"flat\" , \"linear\" ])) pi => cfg % si_newton_max call g % add ( nml_int ( \"newton_max\" , pi , & \"Casulli wet/dry Newton outer-iteration cap (only consulted \" // & \"when wetdry=.true.); default 10 = bit-identical\" , min = 1 )) pr => cfg % si_newton_tol call g % add ( nml_real ( \"newton_tol\" , pr , & \"Casulli wet/dry Newton relative residual tolerance \" // & \"(||F||&#94;2 < tol&#94;2*||rhs||&#94;2); default 1e-11 is tight (tuned for \" // & \"smooth cases) — real bathymetry typically wants ~1e-7\" , & min = 1.0e-30_wp )) call schema % add_group ( g ) end subroutine register_si","tags":"","url":"proc/register_si.html"},{"title":"register_sim – Rakali","text":"private  subroutine register_sim(cfg, schema) &sim_nml : the simulation regime selector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema Calls proc~~register_sim~~CallsGraph proc~register_sim register_sim proc~group_add nml_group_t%group_add proc~register_sim->proc~group_add proc~nml_enum nml_enum proc~register_sim->proc~nml_enum proc~schema_add_group nml_schema_t%schema_add_group proc~register_sim->proc~schema_add_group error error proc~group_add->error proc~lower lower proc~group_add->proc~lower proc~schema_add_group->error proc~schema_add_group->proc~lower proc~move_group move_group proc~schema_add_group->proc~move_group Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the mo