nown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure logical function all_neighbours_wet ( h_col , h_col_ip1 , h_col_im1 , & h_col_jp1 , h_col_jm1 ) result ( all_wet ) !$acc routine seq !! Returns `.true.` if the centre cell and its four face-neighbours all !! have total column depth >= `ML_MIN_DEPTH`. Guards central-difference !! operators (BPG, divergence) against spurious gradients at dry cells. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_col !! column depth at (i,j) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_col_ip1 !! column depth at (i+1,j) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_col_im1 !! column depth at (i-1,j) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_col_jp1 !! column depth at (i,j+1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_col_jm1 !! column depth at (i,j-1) all_wet = h_col >= ML_MIN_DEPTH . and . & h_col_ip1 >= ML_MIN_DEPTH . and . & h_col_im1 >= ML_MIN_DEPTH . and . & h_col_jp1 >= ML_MIN_DEPTH . and . & h_col_jm1 >= ML_MIN_DEPTH end function all_neighbours_wet","tags":"","url":"proc/all_neighbours_wet~2.html"},{"title":"ml_apply_layer_bcs – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_apply_layer_bcs(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, h, hu, hv, dsig, grid, nz, bc_west, bc_east, bc_south, bc_north) Enforce layer consistency in ghost cells.\nCall after applying barotropic BCs and before flux computation. Two regimes: Wall edges (BC type supplied and equal to BC_WALL ) mirror the\n  interior PER-LAYER momentum profile, normal component negated and\n  tangential mirrored — matching the barotropic wall convention in rki_boundary .  This makes a closed wall tracer-TIGHT. Every other edge distributes the barotropic ghost state\n  proportionally to the sigma fractions, as before.  There is no\n  interior profile to mirror meaningfully for inflow/tidal/open. Why the wall case needs the per-layer mirror The old code always did the dsig distribution, i.e. hu_layer(g,j,k) = dsig(k)*hu(g,j) — a SHEAR-FREE ghost.  At a wall\nthe barotropic ghost carries hu(g,j) = -hu(mirror,j) , so the layer\nmomenta sum correctly to zero net barotropic flux and WATER mass is\nconserved to machine precision.  But the per-layer face velocity v_face(k) = 0.5*(hu_ghost(k) + hu_int(k)) is then NON-ZERO in every\nlayer whenever the interior column is sheared: the ghost’s uniform\nprofile cannot cancel the interior’s sheared one layer by layer.\nEach layer therefore trades tracer with the ghost at its own\nconcentration, and the net tracer flux through a CLOSED wall is sum_k v(k)*Tr(k) /= 0 whenever Tr varies with depth. Measured before the fix, in a single ml_advect_tracer call with a\nsheared interior column (+q/-q) and Tr = 40/35 by layer beside a\nwall: water-mass change exactly 0.0, tracer change 2.000000000044e-2\nagainst the analytic prediction ny*dt/dx*(q/2)*(40-35) = 2.0e-2 —\nan exact match, confirming the mechanism.  With the per-layer mirror v_face(k) vanishes identically and the wall is tight layer by layer. The BC arguments are OPTIONAL so existing call sites that do not (or\ncannot) supply them keep the previous behaviour; callers that know\ntheir edge types should pass them. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig (nz) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in), optional :: bc_west integer, intent(in), optional :: bc_east integer, intent(in), optional :: bc_south integer, intent(in), optional :: bc_north Called by proc~~ml_apply_layer_bcs~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs ml_apply_layer_bcs proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1->proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: g integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: m integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny logical, private :: wall_e logical, private :: wall_n logical, private :: wall_s logical, private :: wall_w Source Code pure subroutine ml_apply_layer_bcs ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & h , hu , hv , dsig , & grid , nz , & bc_west , bc_east , bc_south , bc_north ) !! Enforce layer consistency in ghost cells. !! Call after applying barotropic BCs and before flux computation. !! !! Two regimes: !! !! * **Wall edges** (BC type supplied and equal to `BC_WALL`) mirror the !!   interior PER-LAYER momentum profile, normal component negated and !!   tangential mirrored — matching the barotropic wall convention in !!   `rki_boundary`.  This makes a closed wall tracer-TIGHT. !! * **Every other edge** distributes the barotropic ghost state !!   proportionally to the sigma fractions, as before.  There is no !!   interior profile to mirror meaningfully for inflow/tidal/open. !! !! ## Why the wall case needs the per-layer mirror !! !! The old code always did the `dsig` distribution, i.e. !! `hu_layer(g,j,k) = dsig(k)*hu(g,j)` — a SHEAR-FREE ghost.  At a wall !! the barotropic ghost carries `hu(g,j) = -hu(mirror,j)`, so the layer !! momenta sum correctly to zero net barotropic flux and WATER mass is !! conserved to machine precision.  But the per-layer face velocity !! `v_face(k) = 0.5*(hu_ghost(k) + hu_int(k))` is then NON-ZERO in every !! layer whenever the interior column is sheared: the ghost's uniform !! profile cannot cancel the interior's sheared one layer by layer. !! Each layer therefore trades tracer with the ghost at its own !! concentration, and the net tracer flux through a CLOSED wall is !! `sum_k v(k)*Tr(k) /= 0` whenever Tr varies with depth. !! !! Measured before the fix, in a single `ml_advect_tracer` call with a !! sheared interior column (+q/-q) and Tr = 40/35 by layer beside a !! wall: water-mass change exactly 0.0, tracer change 2.000000000044e-2 !! against the analytic prediction `ny*dt/dx*(q/2)*(40-35)` = 2.0e-2 — !! an exact match, confirming the mechanism.  With the per-layer mirror !! `v_face(k)` vanishes identically and the wall is tight layer by layer. !! !! The BC arguments are OPTIONAL so existing call sites that do not (or !! cannot) supply them keep the previous behaviour; callers that know !! their edge types should pass them. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dsig ( nz ) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: bc_west , bc_east , bc_south , bc_north integer :: i , j , k , g , m , nx , ny , nghost logical :: wall_w , wall_e , wall_s , wall_n nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost wall_w = . false . wall_e = . false . wall_s = . false . wall_n = . false . if ( present ( bc_west )) wall_w = ( bc_west == BC_WALL ) if ( present ( bc_east )) wall_e = ( bc_east == BC_WALL ) if ( present ( bc_south )) wall_s = ( bc_south == BC_WALL ) if ( present ( bc_north )) wall_n = ( bc_north == BC_WALL ) ! West ghost cells.  Mirror pairing matches `rki_boundary`: ! ghost (nghost + 1 - g)  <->  interior (nghost + g),  g = 1..nghost. do g = 1 , nghost m = 2 * nghost + 1 - g if ( wall_w ) then do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , k = 1 : nz ) h_layer ( g , j , k ) = h_layer ( m , j , k ) hu_layer ( g , j , k ) = - hu_layer ( m , j , k ) hv_layer ( g , j , k ) = hv_layer ( m , j , k ) end do else do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , k = 1 : nz ) h_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * h ( g , j ) hu_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hu ( g , j ) hv_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hv ( g , j ) end do end if end do ! East ghost cells do g = nx - nghost + 1 , nx m = 2 * ( nx - nghost ) + 1 - g if ( wall_e ) then do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , k = 1 : nz ) h_layer ( g , j , k ) = h_layer ( m , j , k ) hu_layer ( g , j , k ) = - hu_layer ( m , j , k ) hv_layer ( g , j , k ) = hv_layer ( m , j , k ) end do else do concurrent ( j = 1 : ny , k = 1 : nz ) h_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * h ( g , j ) hu_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hu ( g , j ) hv_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hv ( g , j ) end do end if end do ! South ghost cells do g = 1 , nghost m = 2 * nghost + 1 - g if ( wall_s ) then do concurrent ( i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) h_layer ( i , g , k ) = h_layer ( i , m , k ) hu_layer ( i , g , k ) = hu_layer ( i , m , k ) hv_layer ( i , g , k ) = - hv_layer ( i , m , k ) end do else do concurrent ( i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) h_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * h ( i , g ) hu_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hu ( i , g ) hv_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hv ( i , g ) end do end if end do ! North ghost cells do g = ny - nghost + 1 , ny m = 2 * ( ny - nghost ) + 1 - g if ( wall_n ) then do concurrent ( i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) h_layer ( i , g , k ) = h_layer ( i , m , k ) hu_layer ( i , g , k ) = hu_layer ( i , m , k ) hv_layer ( i , g , k ) = - hv_layer ( i , m , k ) end do else do concurrent ( i = 1 : nx , k = 1 : nz ) h_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * h ( i , g ) hu_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hu ( i , g ) hv_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hv ( i , g ) end do end if end do end subroutine ml_apply_layer_bcs","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_apply_layer_bcs.html"},{"title":"ml_apply_layer_bcs_full – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine ml_apply_layer_bcs_full(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, h, hu, hv, dsig, vcoord_z_ref_col, h_min, grid, nz) Uses rki_vcoord proc~~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full~~UsesGraph proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full ml_apply_layer_bcs_full module~rki_vcoord rki_vcoord proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full->module~rki_vcoord module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_vcoord->module~rki_constants pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_vcoord->pic_logger pic_strings pic_strings module~rki_vcoord->pic_strings pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL variant of ml_apply_layer_bcs . Rebuilds\nghost-cell h_layer from the per-column vcoord_z_ref_col profile\n(as the interior ml_distribute_with_remap_full ) so the layout is\nconsistent across the boundary — a sigma fallback would mismatch and\nmake CWC advection inject tracer at the wrong per-layer ratio.\nMomentum is still split by dsig(k) (ghost barotropic momentum\ncarries no internal shear). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: vcoord_z_ref_col (0:nz,grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_min type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz Calls proc~~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full~~CallsGraph proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full ml_apply_layer_bcs_full proc~vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full->proc~vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full ml_apply_layer_bcs_full proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~ml_apply_layer_bcs_full proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: dz_col (NZ_STACK_MAX) integer, private :: g integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: z_ref_local (0:NZ_STACK_MAX) Source Code subroutine ml_apply_layer_bcs_full ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & h , hu , hv , dsig , & vcoord_z_ref_col , h_min , & grid , nz ) !! VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL variant of `ml_apply_layer_bcs`. Rebuilds !! ghost-cell `h_layer` from the per-column `vcoord_z_ref_col` profile !! (as the interior `ml_distribute_with_remap_full`) so the layout is !! consistent across the boundary — a sigma fallback would mismatch and !! make CWC advection inject tracer at the wrong per-layer ratio. !! Momentum is still split by `dsig(k)` (ghost barotropic momentum !! carries no internal shear). use rki_vcoord , only : vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dsig ( nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: vcoord_z_ref_col ( 0 : nz , grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_min integer :: i , j , k , g , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: dz_col ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: z_ref_local ( 0 : NZ_STACK_MAX ) nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost ! West ghost cells !$acc parallel loop collapse(2) & !$acc&   present(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, h, hu, hv, dsig, & !$acc&           vcoord_z_ref_col) & !$acc&   private(k, dz_col, z_ref_local) do g = 1 , nghost do j = 1 , ny do k = 0 , nz z_ref_local ( k ) = vcoord_z_ref_col ( k , g , j ) end do call vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full ( nz , h ( g , j ), & z_ref_local ( 0 : nz ), & h_min , dz_col ) do k = 1 , nz h_layer ( g , j , k ) = dz_col ( k ) hu_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hu ( g , j ) hv_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hv ( g , j ) end do end do end do ! East ghost cells !$acc parallel loop collapse(2) & !$acc&   present(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, h, hu, hv, dsig, & !$acc&           vcoord_z_ref_col) & !$acc&   private(k, dz_col, z_ref_local) do g = nx - nghost + 1 , nx do j = 1 , ny do k = 0 , nz z_ref_local ( k ) = vcoord_z_ref_col ( k , g , j ) end do call vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full ( nz , h ( g , j ), & z_ref_local ( 0 : nz ), & h_min , dz_col ) do k = 1 , nz h_layer ( g , j , k ) = dz_col ( k ) hu_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hu ( g , j ) hv_layer ( g , j , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hv ( g , j ) end do end do end do ! South ghost cells !$acc parallel loop collapse(2) & !$acc&   present(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, h, hu, hv, dsig, & !$acc&           vcoord_z_ref_col) & !$acc&   private(k, dz_col, z_ref_local) do g = 1 , nghost do i = 1 , nx do k = 0 , nz z_ref_local ( k ) = vcoord_z_ref_col ( k , i , g ) end do call vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full ( nz , h ( i , g ), & z_ref_local ( 0 : nz ), & h_min , dz_col ) do k = 1 , nz h_layer ( i , g , k ) = dz_col ( k ) hu_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hu ( i , g ) hv_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hv ( i , g ) end do end do end do ! North ghost cells !$acc parallel loop collapse(2) & !$acc&   present(h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, h, hu, hv, dsig, & !$acc&           vcoord_z_ref_col) & !$acc&   private(k, dz_col, z_ref_local) do g = ny - nghost + 1 , ny do i = 1 , nx do k = 0 , nz z_ref_local ( k ) = vcoord_z_ref_col ( k , i , g ) end do call vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full ( nz , h ( i , g ), & z_ref_local ( 0 : nz ), & h_min , dz_col ) do k = 1 , nz h_layer ( i , g , k ) = dz_col ( k ) hu_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hu ( i , g ) hv_layer ( i , g , k ) = dsig ( k ) * hv ( i , g ) end do end do end do end subroutine ml_apply_layer_bcs_full","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_apply_layer_bcs_full.html"},{"title":"ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer – Rakali","text":"public pure subroutine ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer(hu_layer, hv_layer, h_layer, wind_x, wind_y, grid, nz, dt) Apply the surface wind stress to the TOP layer (k=nz) momentum only,\nso the wind is surface-concentrated and generates vertical shear that\nthe vertical mixing then spreads downward — instead of the\ndepth-uniform barotropic forcing ( apply_friction ).  tau =\n(wind_x, wind_y) in Pa; adds dt*tau/RHO_WATER to hu/hv_layer(:,:,nz).\nGated by wind_surface_layer ; the caller suppresses the barotropic\nwind so the stress is not applied twice. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Called by proc~~ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage->proc~ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl->proc~solver_multilayer_rk_stage proc~solver_step solver_step proc~solver_step->proc~solver_step_multilayer_impl proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_step proc~rki_advance rki_advance proc~rki_advance->proc~solver_step proc~rki_step rki_step proc~rki_step->proc~solver_step proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny Source Code pure subroutine ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer ( hu_layer , hv_layer , h_layer , & wind_x , wind_y , grid , nz , dt ) !! Apply the surface wind stress to the TOP layer (k=nz) momentum only, !! so the wind is surface-concentrated and generates vertical shear that !! the vertical mixing then spreads downward — instead of the !! depth-uniform barotropic forcing (`apply_friction`).  tau = !! (wind_x, wind_y) in Pa; adds dt*tau/RHO_WATER to hu/hv_layer(:,:,nz). !! Gated by `wind_surface_layer`; the caller suppresses the barotropic !! wind so the stress is not applied twice. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: wind_x ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: wind_y ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: i , j , nx , ny , nghost nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) if ( h_layer ( i , j , nz ) > THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) then hu_layer ( i , j , nz ) = hu_layer ( i , j , nz ) + dt * wind_x ( i , j ) / RHO_WATER hv_layer ( i , j , nz ) = hv_layer ( i , j , nz ) + dt * wind_y ( i , j ) / RHO_WATER end if end do end subroutine ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_apply_wind_to_surface_layer.html"},{"title":"ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full(b, vcoord_z_ref_col, grid, nz, h_surf_target, n_surf, stretching) Fill the per-column reference z-level array from the bathymetry.\nHost-side loop (runs at init / bathymetry change); updates the\ndevice copy after writing. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) Bed ELEVATION ( state%barotropic%b ): negative for submerged\ncells; negated here to the POSITIVE bed depth that zstar_full_build_column expects. real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: vcoord_z_ref_col (0:nz,grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_surf_target Target surface-layer thickness (m), see zstar_full_build_column integer, intent(in) :: n_surf integer, intent(in) :: stretching Calls proc~~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full~~CallsGraph proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full proc~zstar_full_build_column zstar_full_build_column proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full->proc~zstar_full_build_column Help Graph