river_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: du real(kind=wp), private :: dv real(kind=wp), private :: dz_new (NZ_STACK_MAX) real(kind=wp), private :: h_k_old real(kind=wp), private :: h_val integer, private :: i integer, private :: j integer, private :: k integer, private :: nghost integer, private :: nx integer, private :: ny real(kind=wp), private :: u_k real(kind=wp), private :: v_k real(kind=wp), private :: z_ref_local (0:NZ_STACK_MAX) Source Code subroutine ml_distribute_with_remap_full ( h , hu , hv , hu_pre , hv_pre , & z_ref_col , h_min , & h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & grid , nz ) !! VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL variant of `ml_distribute_with_remap` (momentum + !! thickness only): builds per-cell dz_new via !! `vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full` from the per-column reference !! profile `z_ref_col(0:nz,i,j)`. Per-tracer remap by `ml_remap_tracer`. !! Shares the `remap_dz_old` persistent workspace. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu_pre ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv_pre ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: z_ref_col ( 0 : nz , grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_min real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: h_val , du , dv , h_k_old , u_k , v_k real ( wp ) :: dz_new ( NZ_STACK_MAX ) real ( wp ) :: z_ref_local ( 0 : NZ_STACK_MAX ) nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost call remap_workspace_ensure ( nx , ny , nz ) do concurrent ( k = 1 : nz , j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx ) remap_dz_old ( i , j , k ) = h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do !$acc parallel loop collapse(2) & !$acc&   present(h, hu, hv, hu_pre, hv_pre, z_ref_col, & !$acc&           h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, remap_dz_old) & !$acc&   private(k, h_val, du, dv, h_k_old, u_k, v_k, & !$acc&           dz_new, z_ref_local) do j = nghost + 1 , ny - nghost do i = nghost + 1 , nx - nghost h_val = h ( i , j ) if ( h_val > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then du = ( hu ( i , j ) - hu_pre ( i , j )) / h_val dv = ( hv ( i , j ) - hv_pre ( i , j )) / h_val else du = 0.0_wp dv = 0.0_wp end if ! Copy this column's reference profile into a private stack ! slice so the pure callee sees an explicit-shape array slice. do k = 0 , nz z_ref_local ( k ) = z_ref_col ( k , i , j ) end do call vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full ( nz , h_val , & z_ref_local ( 0 : nz ), & h_min , dz_new ) do k = 1 , nz h_k_old = remap_dz_old ( i , j , k ) if ( h_k_old > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_k = hu_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k_old v_k = hv_layer ( i , j , k ) / h_k_old else u_k = 0.0_wp v_k = 0.0_wp end if h_layer ( i , j , k ) = dz_new ( k ) if ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) then hu_layer ( i , j , k ) = 0.0_wp hv_layer ( i , j , k ) = 0.0_wp else hu_layer ( i , j , k ) = h_layer ( i , j , k ) * ( u_k + du ) hv_layer ( i , j , k ) = h_layer ( i , j , k ) * ( v_k + dv ) end if end do end do end do end subroutine ml_distribute_with_remap_full","tags":"","url":"proc/ml_distribute_with_remap_full.html"},{"title":"ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup() Release the vcoord-remap persistent workspace.  Called by the\nsolver at simulation end. Arguments None Calls proc~~ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup~~CallsGraph proc~ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup proc~remap_workspace_cleanup remap_workspace_cleanup proc~ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup->proc~remap_workspace_cleanup Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup~~CalledByGraph proc~ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup proc~solver_exit_data solver_exit_data proc~solver_exit_data->proc~ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~solver_exit_data proc~flush_restart flush_restart proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_restart proc~flush_snapshot flush_snapshot proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~flush_snapshot proc~ensure_host~2 ensure_host proc~ensure_host~2->proc~solver_exit_data proc~flush_re