lver_handle_t ), private, pointer :: h Source Code subroutine handle_destroy ( c_handle ) !! Free a structured handle. Idempotent on null/already-destroyed !! handles — silently no-ops rather than aborting, so Python !! `__del__` can call this without first checking state. type ( c_ptr ), intent ( inout ) :: c_handle type ( solver_handle_t ), pointer :: h if (. not . c_associated ( c_handle )) return call c_f_pointer ( c_handle , h ) if ( h % magic /= MAGIC_STRUCTURED ) return !! garbage or already destroyed h % magic = MAGIC_DESTROYED if ( associated ( h % state )) deallocate ( h % state ) deallocate ( h ) c_handle = c_null_ptr end subroutine handle_destroy","tags":"","url":"proc/handle_destroy.html"},{"title":"handle_destroy_unstr – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine handle_destroy_unstr(c_handle) Free an unstructured handle. Idempotent on null/destroyed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), intent(inout) :: c_handle Called by proc~~handle_destroy_unstr~~CalledByGraph proc~handle_destroy_unstr handle_destroy_unstr proc~rki_unstr_destroy rki_unstr_destroy proc~rki_unstr_destroy->proc~handle_destroy_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( solver_handle_unstr_t ), private, pointer :: h Source Code subroutine handle_destroy_unstr ( c_handle ) !! Free an