sh in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: dt real(kind=wp), private :: ssp_coeff type( timestepper_t ), private :: ts Source Code subroutine solver_unstr_advance ( state , mesh , t_end ) !! Step until `state%time >= t_end`. Recomputes the CFL-limited !! timestep from the per-cell wave speeds before each step using !! `compute_timestep_unstr`. !! !! NOTE: the very first step needs `state%barotropic%max_speed` to be !! populated, which only happens after a flux pass. We bootstrap !! by running extrapolate + flux once before the loop starts so !! the CFL kernel has something to read. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: mesh real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t_end real ( wp ) :: dt , ssp_coeff type ( timestepper_t ) :: ts ! Semi-implicit mode: no SSP stage table (make_timestepper is ! fail-loud on SEMI_IMPLICIT) and no gravity-wave CFL — the eta-solve ! is unconditionally stable in the surface-wave mode and runs at the ! configured dt_fixed (stored by state_unstr_enable_si).  The ! explicit bootstrap flux pass is skipped too: max_speed feeds only ! the CFL kernel. if ( state % use_semi_implicit ) then state % dt = state % dt_fixed do while ( state % time < t_end ) dt = state % dt ! Cap the final step so we land exactly on t_end. if ( state % time + dt > t_end ) dt = t_end - state % time if ( dt <= 0.0_wp ) exit call solver_unstr_step ( state , mesh , dt ) end do return end if ! ssp_coeff scales the CFL-limited dt for schemes stable beyond the ! forward-Euler limit (rk43, C=2 -> 2x dt).  Exact x1.0 for ! euler/rk2/rk3, so the default RK2 dt is bit-identical. ts = make_timestepper ( state % time_scheme ) ssp_coeff = ts % ssp_coeff ! Bootstrap: populate state%barotropic%max_speed for the first CFL call. call extrapolate_second_order_edge_unstr ( state , mesh ) call compute_fluxes_central_unstr ( state , mesh ) call compute_timestep_unstr ( state , mesh ) state % dt = state % dt * ssp_coeff do while ( state % time < t_end ) dt = state % dt ! Cap the final step so we land exactly on t_end. if ( state % time + dt > t_end ) dt = t_end - state % time if ( dt <= 0.0_wp ) exit call solver_unstr_step ( state , mesh , dt ) ! Recompute the CFL timestep using the wave speeds the flux ! kernel just wrote. call compute_timestep_unstr ( state , mesh ) state % dt = state % dt * ssp_coeff end do end subroutine solver_unstr_advance","tags":"","url":"proc/solver_unstr_advance.html"},{"title":"solver_unstr_init_multilayer – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine solver_unstr_init_multilayer(state, mesh) Populate the layer fields from the current barotropic state\nand seed the passive tracers (S, T) from the scalar initial\nvalues carried on state . Must be called once after state_unstr_enter_data (so the\nbarotropic IC is on the device) and before the first step. After EOS, builds the horizontally-uniform reference-density\nprofile rho_ref(z) so the BPG kernels see the small density\nanomaly rho - rho_ref(z) rather than rho - rho_0 (Phase B2). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh Calls proc~~solver_unstr_init_multilayer~~CallsGraph proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full_unstr ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full_unstr proc~ml_compute_reference_density_unstr ml_compute_reference_density_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_compute_reference_density_unstr proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_equation_of_state_unstr proc~ml_init_layers_unstr ml_init_layers_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_init_layers_unstr proc~ml_init_tracer_unstr ml_init_tracer_unstr proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer->proc~ml_init_tracer_unstr proc~ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr ml