rent colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~solver_unstr_init_multilayer~~CalledByGraph proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr driver_run_coastal_unstr proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~rki_unstr_finalize rki_unstr_finalize proc~rki_unstr_finalize->proc~solver_unstr_init_multilayer proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: it Source Code subroutine solver_unstr_init_multilayer ( state , mesh ) !! Populate the layer fields from the current barotropic state !! and seed the passive tracers (S, T) from the scalar initial !! values carried on `state`. !! !! Must be called once after `state_unstr_enter_data` (so the !! barotropic IC is on the device) and before the first step. !! !! After EOS, builds the horizontally-uniform reference-density !! profile `rho_ref(z)` so the BPG kernels see the small density !! anomaly `rho - rho_ref(z)` rather than `rho - rho_0` (Phase B2). type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer :: it ! For VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL build the per-cell reference z-level ! pattern from the local bathymetry before laying out the ! initial layer profile. if ( state % multilayer % vcoord % coord_type == VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL ) then call ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full_unstr ( state ) end if call ml_init_layers_unstr ( state ) ! Seed salinity + temperature from their IC scalars (each dispatching ! uniform-vs-stratified; S_init_bottom > S_init_surface = salty bed). call ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr ( state ) ! Seed any extra registered passive tracers from their tr_init so ! the registry \"just works\" — register_passive_tracer + a uniform IC ! without the caller touching hTr directly. do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( it == state % multilayer % idx_salinity . or . it == state % multilayer % idx_temperature ) cycle call ml_init_tracer_unstr ( state , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_init ) end do call ml_equation_of_state_unstr ( state ) call ml_compute_reference_density_unstr ( state , mesh ) end subroutine solver_unstr_init_multilayer","tags":"","url":"proc/solver_unstr_init_multilayer.html"},{"title":"solver_unstr_step – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine solver_unstr_step(state, mesh, dt) Take one SSP-RK2 step at the caller-supplied timestep dt .\nUpdates (stage_cv, xmom_cv, ymom_cv) from t to t + dt .\nIncrements state%time by dt and state%step_count by 1. Multilayer mode ( state%use_multilayer ) shadows the barotropic\nstages: before each HLL update the barotropic momentum is\nsnapshotted, and after each update the barotropic acceleration\nis distributed uniformly across layers. At the very end of the\nstep the layers are RK2-averaged in their own right and the\nbarotropic fields are resynced via sum_k so the invariant sum_k hu_layer == xmom_cv holds after every call. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Calls proc~~solver_unstr_step~~CallsGraph proc~solver_unstr_step solver