colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: ii integer, private :: jj Source Code subroutine bc_init_chapman ( bc , h , b , nx_total , ny_total , nghost ) !! Allocate Chapman eta_old arrays for all four edges (so they are !! available for unconditional GPU mapping in `solver_enter_data`) !! and seed the active edges from current eta. Inactive edges keep !! their zero source value -- the kernel never reads them when the !! corresponding `bc%<side>` is not `BC_CHAPMAN`, so the zeros are !! harmless. type ( bc_params_t ), intent ( inout ) :: bc real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h (:, :) !! Water depth array (nx_total, ny_total) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: b (:, :) !! Bottom elevation array (nx_total, ny_total) integer , intent ( in ) :: nx_total !! Total cells in x including ghost cells integer , intent ( in ) :: ny_total !! Total cells in y including ghost cells integer , intent ( in ) :: nghost !! Ghost cell width integer :: ii , jj if (. not . allocated ( bc % eta_old_west )) then allocate ( bc % eta_old_west ( ny_total ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if if (. not . allocated ( bc % eta_old_east )) then allocate ( bc % eta_old_east ( ny_total ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if if (. not . allocated ( bc % eta_old_south )) then allocate ( bc % eta_old_south ( nx_total ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if if (. not . allocated ( bc % eta_old_north )) then allocate ( bc % eta_old_north ( nx_total ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if if ( bc % west == BC_CHAPMAN . or . bc % east == BC_CHAPMAN ) then do jj = 1 , ny_total bc % eta_old_west ( jj ) = h ( nghost + 1 , jj ) + b ( nghost + 1 , jj ) bc % eta_old_east ( jj ) = h ( nx_total - nghost , jj ) + b ( nx_total - nghost , jj ) end do end if if ( bc % south == BC_CHAPMAN . or . bc % north == BC_CHAPMAN ) then do ii = 1 , nx_total bc % eta_old_south ( ii ) = h ( ii , nghost + 1 ) + b ( ii , nghost + 1 ) bc % eta_old_north ( ii ) = h ( ii , ny_total - nghost ) + b ( ii , ny_total - nghost ) end do end if end subroutine bc_init_chapman","tags":"","url":"proc/bc_init_chapman.html"},{"title":"bc_init_from_config – Rakali","text":"public  subroutine bc_init_from_config(bc, cfg) Initialise boundary condition parameters from config Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( bc_params_t ), intent(inout) :: bc type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg Calls proc~~bc_init_from_config~~CallsGraph proc~bc_init_from_config bc_init_from_config proc~bc_type_from_string bc_type_from_string proc~bc_init_from_config->proc~bc_type_from_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~bc_init_from_config~~CalledByGraph proc~bc_init_from_config bc_init_from_config proc~init_bc_from_config init_bc_from_config proc~init_bc_from_config->proc~bc_init_from_config proc~rki_finalize rki_finalize proc~rki_finalize->proc~bc_init_from_config proc~driver_run_coastal driver_run_coastal proc~driver_run_coastal->proc~init_bc_from_config proc~rki_create_from_namelist rki_create_from_namelist proc~rki_create_from_namelist->proc~rki_finalize proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string rki_create_from_namelist_string proc~rki_create_from_namelist_string->proc~rki_finalize proc~driver_run driver_run proc~driver_run->proc~driver_run_coastal Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine S