ells in y including ghosts Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: init => grid_init Subroutines private  subroutine grid_init (this, nx_phys, ny_phys, nghost, dx, dy) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( hgrid_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer, intent(in) :: nx_phys integer, intent(in) :: ny_phys integer, intent(in) :: nghost real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dx real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dy","tags":"","url":"module/rki_grid.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_tracers – Rakali","text":"Horizontal advection (PPM and first-order upwind), vertical\nexchange and diffusion, distribution under the barotropic step,\nhorizontal Laplacian diffusion, surface fluxes, RK2 plumbing,\nghost-cell boundary application, and bounds clamping. Both prognostic tracers (salinity hS, temperature hT) share these\ngeneric kernels — callers pick which array to pass. The advection / PPM / horizontal-diffusion kernels are pure : the\nper-kernel scratch (PPM reconstruction snapshots, Jacobi neighbour\nsnapshots) is caller-owned through tracer_scratch_t , allocated\nonce up front by the solver ( tracer_scratch_ensure ) and released\nby tracer_scratch_destroy .  Writing an intent(out) scratch dummy\nis pure-legal, so the kernels keep purity while still avoiding the\nper-step allocate/deallocate that would stall the GPU pipeline. Uses rki_remap_column rki_boundary_types rki_constants rki_grid rki_ml_common module~~rki_ml_tracers~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_tracers rki_ml_tracers module~rki_boundary_types rki_boundary_types module~rki_ml_tracers->module~rki_boundary_types module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_ml_tracers->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_ml_tracers->module~rki_grid module~rki_ml_common rki_ml_common module~rki_ml_tracers->module~rki_ml_common module~rki_remap_column rki_remap_column module~rki_ml_tracers->module~rki_remap_column module~rki_boundary_types->module~rki_constants module~rki_config rki_config module~rki_boundary_types-