: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: BPG_NZ_MAX = 20 Per-column stack-workspace bound for the unstructured multilayer\nkernels (BPG, vertical exchange, vertical viscosity, KPP, k-eps,\ntracer advection).  Fixed size so the compiler can emit fixed-size\nthread-local storage on GPU.  DISTINCT from the structured/ocean NZ_STACK_MAX in rki_constants : the unstructured path is\nthread-per-cell with many such locals per kernel frame, so this\nbound stays deliberately small — raising it multiplies the\nper-thread local memory of every unstructured column kernel.\nBuild-configurable via -DRAKALI_BPG_NZ_MAX=<n> (CMake cache\nvariable, plumbed as the 20 preprocessor define;\ndefault 20). The requirement is BPG_NZ_MAX >= nz + 1 — see bpg_nz_required below for the derivation and the survey of\nevery consumer.  Enforced fail-loud by validate_config . real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: ML_MIN_DEPTH_UNSTR = 0.5_wp real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: VANISHING_LAYER_TOL_UNSTR = 1.5e-4_wp Functions public pure function bpg_nz_is_sufficient (nz) result(ok) .true. when the COMPILED BPG_NZ_MAX covers nz layers on\nthe unstructured multilayer path.  Callers that get .false. must refuse the run: exceeding the bound is NOT a crash — the\nunstructured BPG kernels silently return (no baroclinic\npressure gradient at all) and the unguarded column kernels\nsilently overrun thread-local storage. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Return Value logical public pure function bpg_nz_required (nz) result(req) Smallest BPG_NZ_MAX that safely covers an unstructured\nmultilayer run of nz layers. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Return Value integer","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_common_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_flux – Rakali","text":"Net flux divergence for the shallow water equations via HLL or HLLC\nRiemann solver with hydrostatic reconstruction (Audusse et al. 2004)\nand minmod slope-limited reconstruction. HLL/HLLC differ only in the\ntransverse momentum flux. Free surface eta = h + B is reconstructed\n(not h) for the well-balanced property. Uses rki_grid rki_constants module~~rki_kernel_flux~~UsesGraph module~rki_kernel_flux rki_kernel_flux module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_kernel_flux->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_kernel_flux->module~rki_grid pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_kernel_flux~~UsedByGraph module~rki_kernel_flux rki_kernel_flux module~rki_solver rki_solver module~rki_solver->module~rki_kernel_flux module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_solver module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Functions private pure function minmod (a, b) result(m) Minmod slope limiter Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: a real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b Return Value real(kind=wp) Subroutines public pure subroutine compute_flux_hll (h, hu, hv, b, flux_h, flux_hu, flux_hv, mass_flux_x, mass_flux_y, grid) Net flux divergence at each interior cell (HLL Riemann solver).\nAlso writes the per-face HLL h-flux at the right face mass_flux_x(i, j) and top face mass_flux_y(i, j) , reused by\nthe multilayer tracer kernels for consistency-with-continuity (CWC). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: flux_h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: flux_hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: flux_hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: mass_flux_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: mass_flux_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid public pure subroutine compute_flux_hllc (h, hu, hv, b, flux_h, flux_hu, flux_hv, mass_flux_x, mass_flux_y, grid) Net flux divergence at each interior cell (HLLC Riemann solver).\nh/hu flux and mass_flux_x/y match the HLL version; only the\ntransverse momentum flux differs. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: flux_h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: flux_hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: flux_hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: mass_flux_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: mass_flux_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid private pure subroutine extract_velocity (h_val, hu_val, hv_val, u_val, v_val) Extract velocity from conserved variables, handling dry cells Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_val real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_val real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_val real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: u_val real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: v_val private pure subroutine flux_cell (h, hu, hv, b, nx, ny, i, j, dx, dy, use_hllc, out_fh, out_fhu, out_fhv, out_fmass_xL, out_fmass_xR, out_fmass_yB, out_fmass_yT) Net flux divergence for a single cell (i, j). Also returns the\nfour per-face HLL h-fluxes for the multilayer tracer kernels’ CWC. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h (nx,ny) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu (nx,ny) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv (nx,ny) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b (nx,ny) integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: i integer, intent(in) :: j real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dx real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dy logical, intent(in) :: use_hllc Selects the Riemann solver. Passed as a literal constant from\nthe two entry points, so the in-kernel branch constant-folds. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: out_fh real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: out_fhu real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: out_fhv real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: out_fmass_xL HLL h-flux at left face (i-1/2). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: out_fmass_xR HLL h-flux at right face (i+1/2). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: out_fmass_yB HLL h-flux at bottom face (j-1/2). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: out_fmass_yT HLL h-flux at top face (j+1/2). private pure subroutine hll_flux_x (h_l, hu_l, hv_l, h_r, hu_r, hv_r, f_h, f_hu, f_hv) HLL numerical flux in x-direction between left and right states Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_l real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_l real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_l real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_r real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_r real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_r real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f_h real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f_hu real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f_hv private pure subroutine hll_flux_y (h_b, hu_b, hv_b, h_t, hu_t, hv_t, g_h, g_hu, g_hv) HLL numerical flux in y-direction between bottom and top states Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_b real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_b real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_b real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_t real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_t real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_t real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: g_h real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: g_hu real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: g_hv private pure subroutine hllc_flux_x (h_l, hu_l, hv_l, h_r, hu_r, hv_r, f_h, f_hu, f_hv) HLLC numerical flux in x-direction. Transverse momentum hv is\nupwinded across the contact wave: f_hv = f_h * v_upwind\n(v_l if s_star >= 0, else v_r); h and hu match HLL. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_l real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_l real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_l real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_r real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_r real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_r real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f_h real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f_hu real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f_hv private pure subroutine hllc_flux_y (h_b, hu_b, hv_b, h_t, hu_t, hv_t, g_h, g_hu, g_hv) HLLC numerical flux in y-direction. Mirrors hllc_flux_x with\n(u, hu) and (v, hv) swapped; transverse hu is upwinded. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_b real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_b real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_b real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_t real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_t real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_t real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: g_h real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: g_hu real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: g_hv","tags":"","url":"module/rki_kernel_flux.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_truncate – Rakali","text":"Per-cell-per-layer limiter (not a closure) that clips runaway velocities\nfrom any upstream operator (BPG, vertical exchange, viscosity) to\n0.9 cfl_trunc dx/dt so a few bad cells don’t tank the global timestep. Uses rki_grid rki_constants module~~rki_ml_truncate~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_truncate rki_ml_truncate module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_ml_truncate->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_ml_truncate->module~rki_grid pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_ml_truncate~~UsedByGraph module~rki_ml_truncate rki_ml_truncate module~rki_solver rki_solver module~rki_solver->module~rki_ml_truncate module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_solver module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges 