ere possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( tracer_scratch_t ), private, save :: tracer_scratch Subroutines public  subroutine accumulate_boundary_mass_out (state, stage_weight) Accumulate the net volume that left the domain this RK stage into state%barotropic%mass_out .  By the divergence theorem the boundary\noutflux equals -Σ_interior flux_h·area (interior face fluxes\ntelescope), and flux_h is the SAME continuity tendency the update\nconsumes ( h += dt·flux_h ), so with the matching RK stage weight\nthis closes the mass budget to round-off — the console Error then\nmeasures only genuine non-conservation (e.g. dry-cell clamps). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: stage_weight Stage contribution to the step’s h update (0.5 for each SSP-RK2\nstage: h&#94;{n+1} = h&#94;n + 0.5·dt·(flux_h&#94;1 + flux_h&#94;2)). public  subroutine accumulate_mass_src (state, stage_weight, evap_mass_sink) Accumulate the net volume ADDED to the domain this RK stage by\nsurface sources into state%barotropic%mass_src . Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: stage_weight Stage contribution (0.5 per SSP-RK2 stage). logical, intent(in) :: evap_mass_sink Whether the evaporative mass-sink mode is active (real water\nremoval from h ); when .false. the virtual-salt-flux mode\nleaves h unchanged, so evap contributes nothing here. public  subroutine solver_enter_data (state) Copy state arrays to GPU device. Called once at simulation start;\nall subsequent computation runs on device until solver_exit_data. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Solution state to place on device public  subroutine solver_exit_data (state) Copy state arrays back from GPU device. Called once at simulation\nend or for final output. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Solution state to retrieve from device public  subroutine solver_step (state, dt_max, time) Advance the solution by one timestep using SSP-RK2 Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Solution state to advance real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: dt_max Maximum timestep cap (e.g. t_end - t_current) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: time Current simulation time (s), needed for tidal BCs public  subroutine solver_update_forcing (state) Copy forcing fields host->GPU (in-place !$acc update device ).\nCalled after Python/C sets wind/pressure/precip on the host\nmid-simulation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Solution state whose forcing arrays to sync public  subroutine solver_update_host (state) Copy solution fields GPU->host without removing GPU data. Uses !$acc update self(...) so the device copy stays mapped — the\nlightweight sync for callbacks (no full exit/enter round-trip). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Solution state to sync public  subroutine solver_update_state (state) Copy solution fields host->GPU (in-place !$acc update device ).\nMirror of solver_update_host (pushes the same arrays it pulls);\ncalled after Python/C injects new state mid-simulation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state Solution state whose solution arrays to push to device private  subroutine accumulate_sponge_mass_src (state, stage_weight) Accumulate the net volume change caused by the sponge h-relaxation\nthis RK stage into state%barotropic%mass_src .  The sponge applies Δh = −dt·α·(h − h_ref) , which can add or remove mass; this routine\nmeasures the actual h-change by summing h over interior cells before\nand after apply_sponge .  No-op when no sponge edge is configured. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: stage_weight Stage contribution (0.5 per SSP-RK2 stage). private pure subroutine solver_accumulate_2d (acc, f, grid) Accumulate: acc = acc + f Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: acc (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: f (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid private  subroutine solver_advance_2d_generic (state, ts) Generic N-stage explicit SSP advance for the 2D barotropic path\n(euler / rk3 / rk43).  Loops the same forward-Euler stage\nprimitive used by the fused RK2 fast path, then applies the\nShu-Osher convex blend with the start-of-step state U&#94;n: Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( timestepper_t ), intent(in) :: ts private  subroutine solver_baroclinic_rk_stage (state, nz, dt_slow) One RK stage of baroclinic step: layer distribution, w, CG Poisson, NH correction Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt_slow private  subroutine solver_barotropic_rk_stage (state, dt_fast) One RK stage of barotropic subcycling: BCs, flux, update, NH tendency, friction, sponge Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt_fast private  subroutine solver_compute_barotropic_flux (state) Dispatch to the HLL or HLLC barotropic flux kernel based on state%barotropic%use_hllc .  Runs on device — both kernels\nconsume / produce the same arrays. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state private pure subroutine solver_copy_2d (dst, src, grid) Copy: dst = src Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: dst (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: src (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid private  subroutine solver_multilayer_rk_stage (state, nz, is_stage1) One RK stage: barotropic HLL (well-balanced, handles all pressure\ngradients), distribute acceleration to layers preserving shear,\nvertical exchange. is_stage1 (nz=1 fused fast path only): also save\npre-update state into the *_0 arrays; ignored on the nz>1 path. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state integer, intent(in) :: nz logical, intent(in) :: is_stage1 private  subroutine solver_multilayer_rk_stage_nz1 (state, is_stage1) Fused RK-stage path specialised for nz_ml=1 (depth-averaged\n2D with optional tracers). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state logical, intent(in) :: is_stage1 private  subroutine solver_nh_rk_stage (state, nz, use_nh) One RK stage: BCs, flux, update, friction, then NH correction Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state integer, intent(in) :: nz logical, intent(in) :: use_nh private pure subroutine solver_save_state (h, hu, hv, h0, hu0, hv0, grid) Copy current 2D state into saved arrays Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: h0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: hu0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: hv0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid private pure subroutine solver_save_state_layers (u_layer, v_layer, w, u_layer0, v_layer0, w0, grid, nz) Copy layer state: first 3 args (source) -> last 3 args (destination)\nUsed for both save (layers -> layers0) and restore (layers0 -> layers) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: v_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: w (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz+1) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: u_layer0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: v_layer0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: w0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz+1) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz private pure subroutine solver_scale_2d (f, sc, grid) Scale: f = f * sc Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: f (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: sc type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid private  subroutine solver_step_impl (state, dt_max) SSP-RK2 step for unsplit (2D or NH without mode splitting) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: dt_max private  subroutine solver_step_multilayer_impl (state, dt_max) SSP-RK2 step for coupled hydrostatic multi-layer equations Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: dt_max private  subroutine solver_step_split_impl (state, dt_max) Split-step driver: N barotropic substeps + 1 baroclinic step Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: dt_max private  subroutine solver_tracers_enter_data (state) Map state%multilayer%tracers(:) into device memory. Two-step:\ncopyin the array descriptor first (so the device sees the shape of tracers(:) ), then per-element hTr / hTr0 . Without the parent\nmap, NVHPC stdpar can’t dereference tracers(it)%hTr from a\ndo-concurrent body (CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDRESS). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state private  subroutine solver_tracers_exit_data (state) Release the tracer registry from device memory (reverse of\nsolver_tracers_enter_data: per-element first, then the array\ndescriptor). Copies hTr back for diagnostics/tests; hTr0 (RK2\nworkspace) is dropped. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( state_t ), intent(inout) :: state private pure subroutine solver_zero_2d (f, grid) Zero a 2D field Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: f (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid","tags":"","url":"module/rki_solver.html"},{"title":"rki_safe_math – Rakali","text":"Single point of control the math functions that break bitwise\nreproducibility across compilers, GPU vendors, and optimization\nlevels would route through IF adopted: exp , log , sin , cos , sqrt , pow . Status (PR-8): the safe_* wrappers ( safe_exp , safe_log , safe_sin , safe_cos , safe_sqrt , safe_pow ) are plain\nelemental inlines around the bare intrinsic — zero overhead,\ncodegen identical to writing exp(x) directly.  This module\nused to carry a second “safe” mode, selected by the RAKALI_BITWISE_REPRO build option, that dispatched the\nwrappers to the *_polynomial implementations below instead.\nThat option was removed in PR-8 : grep across src/ / app/ found zero call sites of any safe_* wrapper from a production\nkernel (one stale comment, no calls) — the option changed\nnothing at all, so it was a lie about a capability nothing used. What SURVIVES this PR: every *_polynomial function and its\ncoefficients are correct, unit-tested ( tests/test_safe_math.F90 ,\nunconditionally compiled — no #ifdef ), and are the raw material\nfor a future bitwise-reproducibility PR.  This module is a library with no production consumer today — adopting safe_* in kernels (which would first require re-adding a build-time or\nrun-time dispatch) is future work, not a promise this module\ncurrently keeps. Would-be convention (not currently enforced by any build path):\na kernel wanting repro-safety would call the safe_* wrapper\ninstead of the bare intrinsic.  For integer exponents, a**2 / a**3 etc. compile to multiplications and are already\ndeterministic — don’t wrap those. Coverage: safe_exp , safe_log , safe_sin , safe_cos each\nhave real polynomial paths (Cody-Waite reduction + Horner\nTaylor). safe_sqrt is IEEE-correctly-rounded by mandate so\nthe intrinsic path is already deterministic. safe_pow ’s\npolynomial path is unused by safe_pow itself (which is the\nbare intrinsic ** ) — it exists for a future safe_exp(b * safe_log(a)) decomposition. Uses rki_constants iso_fortran_env module~~rki_safe_math~~UsesGraph module~rki_safe_math rki_safe_math iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~rki_safe_math->iso_fortran_env module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_safe_math->module~rki_constants pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C0 = 1.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C1 = -1.0_wp/2.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C2 = 1.0_wp/24.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C3 = -1.0_wp/720.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C4 = 1.0_wp/40320.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C5 = -1.0_wp/3628800.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C6 = 1.0_wp/479001600.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C7 = -1.0_wp/87178291200.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: COS_C8 = 1.0_wp/20922789888000.0_wp real(kind