d + linear. integer, public, parameter :: AGGLOM_MAX_LEVELS = 16 Hard cap on the level count (fixed-size level array bound). integer, public, parameter :: AGGLOM_MIN_SIZE = 150 Stop coarsening when a level has <= this many cells (prototype-tuned:\n2x pairwise coarsening down to ~150 cells, then a coarse Jacobi solve). integer, public, parameter :: AGGLOM_NU_POST = 2 Post-smoothing Jacobi sweeps per level. integer, public, parameter :: AGGLOM_NU_PRE = 2 Pre-smoothing Jacobi sweeps per level. real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: AGGLOM_OMEGA = 0.8_wp Damped-Jacobi relaxation factor (matches the structured MG). real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: DELTA_EPS = 1.0e-30_wp 1/0 armour on the circumcentre-line distance (matches the operator). integer, private, parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 Derived Types type, public :: agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t Fine-to-coarse level stack for the aggregation-MG preconditioner.\nAllocated + built only when precond == mg . Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), public, allocatable :: lev (:) integer, public :: n_levels = 0 Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: destroy => agglom_hierarchy_destroy procedure, public, non_overridable :: enter_data => agglom_hierarchy_enter_data procedure, public, non_overridable :: exit_data => agglom_hierarchy_exit_data type, public :: agglom_level_unstr_t One aggregation-MG level: the compact variable-valence Helmholtz\noperator (symmetric Ahat) on nc cells + the V-cycle work buffers +\nthe aggregation map to the next coarser level.  Structure arrays\n(nbr / n_nbr / agg_of / member CSR) are STATIC (built once); the\ncoefficient arrays (ke / diag / dinv) are refreshed per step.  All\narrays explicit-shape; the level loop dereferences on the HOST and\npasses flat args to the device kernels. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, allocatable :: agg_of (:) Aggregate id in the NEXT COARSER level for each of this level’s\ncells, shape (nc).  Drives prolongation (fine cell reads its\nparent).  Unallocated on the coarsest level. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: diag (:) Operator diagonal, shape (nc). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: dinv (:) 1/diag (Jacobi), shape (nc). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: e (:) Error iterate, shape (nc). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: ke (:,:) Transmissibility coef*K_e per edge, shape (mv, nc); off-diag = -ke. integer, public, allocatable :: mlist (:) Member cell ids on the finer level, shape (n_finer). integer, public, allocatable :: mstart (:) Member CSR offsets, shape (nc+1).  Unallocated on the finest level. integer, public :: mv = 0 Max valence (fixed leading dim of nbr/ke; unused slots padded\nnbr=1, ke=0 so the apply loop is branchless). integer, public, allocatable :: n_nbr (:) Valence per cell, shape (nc). integer, public, allocatable :: nbr (:,:) Neighbour cell id on THIS level, shape (mv, nc); padded slots = 1. integer, public :: nc = 0 Cells on this level. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: r (:) Level RHS / residual, shape (nc). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: tmp (:) Jacobi ping-pong / residual scratch, shape (nc). Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: destroy => agglom_level_destroy procedure, public, non_overridable :: enter_data => agglom_level_enter_data procedure, public, non_overridable :: exit_data => agglom_level_exit_data Functions private  function find_slot (nbr, n, tgt) result(t) Locate the coarse-edge slot for neighbour tgt in nbr(1:n).  The\ntarget is ALWAYS present — the coarse adjacency + the Galerkin fold\nare built from the same aggregation map, so every folded fine edge has\na coarse slot.  A not-found here means that invariant broke; fail loud\n(host-only build path) rather than silently mislocate a coefficient\ninto slot 1. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nbr (:) integer, intent(in) :: n integer, intent(in) :: tgt Return Value integer private pure function itoa (i) result(s) Minimal integer->string for the build log line. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: i Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Subroutines public  subroutine agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build (this, mesh, nco) Build the level stack for nco owned cells.  Only the mesh GEOMETRY\nis needed: the aggregation strength is the geometric transmissibility len/delta (a uniform- Hf , coef=1 proxy).  Greedy pairwise\naggregation picks the MAX-strength neighbour, which is invariant to a\nuniform positive scale, so the live per-step coef*Hf (folded in at\nrefresh) never changes the STRUCTURE — the hierarchy is static.\nHost-only (runs before enter_data); the diag/ke are placeholders here\nand are overwritten by the first refresh before any solve. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nco public  subroutine agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh (this, mesh, nco, coef, Hf_edge) Rebuild every level’s ke/diag/dinv from the current frozen per-edge Hf_edge (the same array the operator + RHS use) + push to the\ndevice.  Fine level from the mesh; coarse levels by the Galerkin\ncascade.  Structures are static.  Runs ONCE PER STEP (host loop), NOT\nper V-cycle. Hf_edge is device-resident; the caller pulls it self\nbefore calling (host build reads it). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nco real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: coef real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nco) public  subroutine agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond (this, r, z, area, nct, nco) z = M&#94;{-1} r for the AREA-WEIGHTED outer PCG: form rhs_hat = area*r,\nrun ONE V(2,2) cycle of the symmetric Ahat from zero, copy the\ncorrection into z (owned cells). r / z / area are the fine\n(ncell_total-shaped) device arrays; only the first nco owned entries\nare touched (ghost band left as the caller set it — pre-zeroed). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: z (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: area (nct) integer, intent(in) :: nct integer, intent(in) :: nco private  subroutine agglom_copy (src, dst, nc) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: src (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: dst (nc) integer, intent(in) :: nc private  subroutine agglom_copy_out (src, dst, nct, nco) dst(1:nco) = src (level-1 buffer -> state z, owned cells). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: src (nco) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: dst (nct) integer, intent(in) :: nct integer, intent(in) :: nco private  subroutine agglom_hierarchy_destroy (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine agglom_hierarchy_enter_data (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine agglom_hierarchy_exit_data (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine agglom_jacobi_one (e_old, e_new, r, nbr, ke, diag, dinv, mv, nc, omega) One damped-Jacobi sweep e_new = e_old + omega (r - Ahat e_old)/diag —\nreads e_old only, writes e_new only (race-free). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: e_old (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: e_new (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r (nc) integer, intent(in) :: nbr (mv,nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: ke (mv,nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: diag (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dinv (nc) integer, intent(in) :: mv integer, intent(in) :: nc real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: omega private  subroutine agglom_jacobi_sweeps (e, r, tmp, nbr, ke, diag, dinv, mv, nc, omega, nu) nu damped-Jacobi sweeps, ping-pong (e,tmp); latest iterate in e . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: e (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: tmp (nc) integer, intent(in) :: nbr (mv,nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: ke (mv,nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: diag (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dinv (nc) integer, intent(in) :: mv integer, intent(in) :: nc real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: omega integer, intent(in) :: nu private  subroutine agglom_level_destroy (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine agglom_level_enter_data (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine agglom_level_enter_data_impl (lev) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: lev private  subroutine agglom_level_exit_data (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine agglom_level_exit_data_impl (lev) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: lev private  subroutine agglom_prolong_add (ec, ef, agg_of, ncf, ncc) ef += P ec: each fine cell adds its parent aggregate’s correction\n(piecewise-constant inject; fine cell writes only its own entry). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: ec (ncc) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: ef (ncf) integer, intent(in) :: agg_of (ncf) integer, intent(in) :: ncf integer, intent(in) :: ncc private  subroutine agglom_residual (e, r, res, nbr, ke, diag, mv, nc) res = r - Ahat*e. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: e (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r (nc) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: res (nc) integer, intent(in) :: nbr (mv,nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: ke (mv,nc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: diag (nc) integer, intent(in) :: mv integer, intent(in) :: nc private  subroutine agglom_restrict (rf, rc, mstart, mlist, ncc, ncf) rc = P&#94;T rf: each coarse cell sums its own fine members (cell-centric,\nrace-free — a coarse cell writes only its own entry). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rf (ncf) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rc (ncc) integer, intent(in) :: mstart (ncc+1) integer, intent(in) :: mlist (ncf) integer, intent(in) :: ncc integer, intent(in) :: ncf private  subroutine agglom_scale_into_shim (src, fac, dst, nct, nco) dst(1:nco) = fac*src (explicit-shape ncell_total state arrays -> the\nlevel-1 RHS buffer). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: src (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: fac (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: dst (nco) integer, intent(in) :: nct integer, intent(in) :: nco private recursive subroutine agglom_vcycle (this, l) One V(nu_pre,nu_post) cycle solving Ahat*e = r on level l from ZERO.\nOn entry lev(l)%r holds the RHS; on exit lev(l)%e holds the solution. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer, intent(in) :: l private  subroutine agglom_zero (a, nc) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: a (nc) integer, intent(in) :: nc private  subroutine aggregate_and_build_coarse (this, l, strength) Greedy pairwise aggregation of level l (strongest-transmissibility\npartner), then build level l+1’s static structure: nc, member CSR,\ncoarse adjacency (nbr / n_nbr / mv). strength(mv,nc) = |ke| per\nedge on level l. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer, intent(in) :: l real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: strength (:,:) private  subroutine alloc_level_coeffs (lev) Allocate the per-step coefficient + V-cycle work arrays of a level. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: lev private  subroutine build_coarse_adjacency (levf, levc, aggof) Build coarse-level neighbour lists from the fine adjacency: coarse\ncells I,J are neighbours iff some fine edge crosses the I-J aggregate\nboundary.  Sets levc%mv / n_nbr / nbr (unique neighbours per coarse\ncell).  Host, O(fine edges). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: levf type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: levc integer, intent(in) :: aggof (:) private  subroutine build_level1_structure (this, mesh, nco) Allocate the level array + fill level 1’s static interior-neighbour\nstructure from the mesh (mv = EDGES_PER_TRI = 3). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nco private  subroutine galerkin_operator (levf, levc, strength) Build the coarse operator ke/diag/dinv by the Galerkin cascade from\nthe finer level’s ke/diag (== rediscretized agglomerate-TPFA for 0/1\naggregation). strength(mvc,ncc) returns |ke| for the NEXT\naggregation.  HOST; caller pushes to the device. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: levf type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: levc real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: strength (levc%mv,levc%nc) |ke| per coarse edge for the NEXT aggregation (BUILD only; the\nper-step refresh omits it). private  subroutine level1_operator (mesh, nco, coef, Hf_edge, lev, strength) Fill level 1’s ke/diag/dinv from the mesh geometry + the per-edge\nfrozen Hf (still-water synthetic at build, the live Hf_edge at\nrefresh).  Mirrors si_unstr_compute_diag + the interior off-diagonals\nof si_unstr_apply_helmholtz , so the symmetric Ahat row is exact:\n  diag(k) = area_k + coef*sum_{Hf>0} K_e   (interior + Dirichlet)\n  off-diag ke to interior neighbours only.\nA Dirichlet boundary edge carries Hf>0 with no CG-unknown neighbour =>\nit lands on the diagonal (ghost = homogeneous 0 in the error\noperator).  Wall edges carry Hf=0 => dropped. strength returns |ke|\nper interior edge for aggregation.  HOST; caller pushes to the device. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nco real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: coef real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nco) type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: lev real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: strength (lev%mv,nco) |ke| per edge for the NEXT aggregation.  Needed at BUILD only;\nthe per-step refresh omits it (no scratch allocation in the\nper-step path). private  subroutine level_coeffs_to_device (lev) Push the host-refreshed coefficient arrays to the device. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: lev private  subroutine move_level (src, dst) move_alloc every component from src to dst (host, pre-enter_data). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: src type( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: dst private  subroutine push_unique (list, n, val) Append val to list(1:n) if not already present; bump n. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(inout) :: list (:) integer, intent(inout) :: n integer, intent(in) :: val private  subroutine trim_levels (this) Move-shrink the over-allocated level array to n_levels. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this","tags":"","url":"module/rki_si_unstr_mg.html"},{"title":"rki_output – Rakali","text":"Writes solution snapshots to NetCDF with CF conventions and\nprovides restart file read/write for continuing simulations. Uses pic_logger netcdf rki_constants rki_state rki_config rki_io_netcdf pic_strings module~~rki_output~~UsesGraph module~rki_output rki_