->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Functions public pure function rho_ref_at (z, rho_ref, dz, nz_ref, rho_0) result(rho) Linear interpolation of the reference-density profile at depth z .\nOut-of-range values fall back to the nearest endpoint.\nWhen the profile is unset ( dz == 0 ) returns rho_0 so the\nkernel reduces to its pre-B2 behaviour. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: z real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_ref (0:nz_ref) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dz integer, intent(in) :: nz_ref real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 Return Value real(kind=wp) Subroutines public  subroutine ml_compute_reference_density_unstr (state, mesh) Build the horizontally-uniform reference-density profile rho_ref(z) from the current rho_layer , sampled on a uniform\nz-grid 0..rho_ref_dz*nz_ref and area-weighted across owned\ncells. Subtracted by both BPG kernels so the integrand is the\nanomaly rho - rho_ref(z) , scaling the residual sigma PGE down.\nCalled once at solver init after the first EOS evaluation, on\nthe host (one-time D2H+H2D). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh public pure subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared_unstr (h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer, eos, nz, n) Opt-in SHARED (ocean) equation of state on the unstructured (nz, ncells) layout — the axis order is opposite to the\nstructured shim, so this evaluates eos_density_point per\n(layer, cell) instead of forwarding to the structured 3D impls. eos_density_point is pure + !$acc routine seq and takes\nthe flat-POD eos_t by value, so the handle rides into\nthe kernel as a register copy — no device mapping.  Evaluation\nis at eos%p_ref (default 0 ⇒ surface/potential density). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_layer (nz,n) type( eos_t ), intent(in) :: eos integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n public  subroutine ml_equation_of_state_unstr (state) Linear two-tracer EOS, per-cell, per-layer:\n  rho_k = rho_0 + beta_S (S_k - S_ref) - alpha_T (T_k - T_ref)\nwith S_k = hS_k/h_k, T_k = hT_k/h_k. Dry layers fall back to the\nreference state. Computed over all cells (interior + halo) so the\nBPG gradient kernel reads neighbour rho without a separate halo. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state private pure subroutine ml_equation_of_state_impl (h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer, S_ref, T_ref, rho_0, beta_S, alpha_T, nz, n) Inner kernel — flat-array dummies so the device-side do concurrent doesn’t chase the tracer-registry indirection. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: S_ref real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: T_ref real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: beta_S real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: alpha_T integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_eos_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_state – Rakali","text":"Manages the conserved variables, bathymetry, and flux arrays All arrays use SoA layout with dimensions (nx_total, ny_total) where\nnx_total = nx_physical + 2*nghost. The first index (i / x-direction)\nis the fast-varying index for coalesced GPU memory access. Uses rki_barotropic_state rki_multilayer_state rki_mem_report rki_boundary_types rki_vcoord rki_constants rki_timestepper iso_fortran_env rki_tracer rki_grid rki_config rki_bathymetry rki_nonhydrostatic_state rki_surface_forcing module~~rki_state~~UsesGraph module~rki_state rki_state iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~rki_state->iso_fortran_env module~rki_barotropic_state rki_barotropic_state module~rki_state->module~rki_barotropic_state module~rki_bathymetry rki_bathymetry module~rki_state->module~rki_bathymetry module~rki_boundary_types rki_boundary_types module~rki_state->module~rki_boundary_types module~rki_config rki_config module~rki_state->module~rki_config module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_state->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_state->module~rki_grid module~rki_mem_report rki_mem_report module~rki_state->module~rki_mem_report module~rki_multilayer_state rki_multilayer_state module~rki_state->module~rki_multilayer_state module~rki_nonhydrostatic_state rki_nonhydrostatic_state module~rki_state->module~rki_nonhydrostatic_state module~rki_surface_forcing rki_surface_forcing module~rki_state->module~rki_surface_forcing module~rki_timestepper rki_timestepper module~rki_state->module~rki_timestepper module~rki_tracer rki_tracer module~rki_state->module~rki_tracer module~rki_vcoord rki_vcoord module~rki_state->module~rki_vcoord module~rki_barotropic_state->iso_fortran_env module~rki_barotropic_state->module~rki_constants module~rki_barotropic_state->module~rki_grid module~rki_barotropic_state->module~rki_mem_report module~rki_bathymetry->module~rki_constants module~rki_bathymetry->module~rki_grid module~rki_io_netcdf rki_io_netcdf module~rki_bathymetry->module~rki_io_netcdf netcdf netcdf module~rki_bathymetry->netcdf pic_logger pic_logger module~