his Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Subroutines public  subroutine ml_compute_reference_density (h_layer, rho_layer, rho_ref, rho_ref_dz, nz_ref, rho_0, grid, nz) Build the horizontally-uniform reference-density profile rho_ref(z) from the current rho_layer .  Sampled on a uniform\nz-grid 0..rho_ref_dz*nz_ref , area-weighted across interior cells. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_ref (0:nz_ref) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_ref_dz integer, intent(in) :: nz_ref real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz public pure subroutine ml_equation_of_state (h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer, rho_0, beta_S, S_ref, alpha_T, T_ref, grid, nz) Linear two-tracer equation of state:\n  rho_k = rho_0 + beta_S * (S_k - S_ref) - alpha_T * (T_k - T_ref)\nwhere S_k = hS_k / h_k and T_k = hT_k / h_k. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 Reference density (kg/m&#94;3) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: beta_S Haline contraction coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per PSU) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: S_ref Reference salinity (PSU) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: alpha_T Thermal expansion coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per degC) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: T_ref Reference temperature (degC) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz public  subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared (h_layer, hS_layer, hT_layer, rho_layer, eos, grid, nz) Opt-in coastal entry to the SHARED (ocean) equation of state —\nselected by &tracer_nml eos_form = \"wright\" | \"roquet_spv\" .\nThin forwarding shim onto the regime-agnostic eos_compute_arrays variant dispatch; evaluation is at eos%p_ref (default 0 Pa ⇒ surface/potential density — the\nright choice for the coastal depth range) with the shared H_VANISHED vanishing-layer fallback to eos%rho0 (note: the\nlegacy coastal kernel gates on DRY_TOLERANCE instead).  The eos_t handle is a flat POD — its scalars are read on\nthe host here and passed by value into the device kernels, so\nno device mapping of the handle is required. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hT_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rho_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) type( eos_t ), intent(in) :: eos Shared EOS handle (variant + scalar coefficients). type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz public  subroutine ml_parse_eos_form (name, use_shared, variant) Translate the coastal &tracer_nml eos_form knob into the\n(use_shared, EOS_VARIANT_*) pair held on the multilayer state. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name logical, intent(out) :: use_shared integer, intent(out) :: variant","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_eos.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_update – Rakali","text":"Advances the conserved variables: forward Euler update (each RK\nstage) and the SSP-RK2 averaging step. Thin-cell treatment (all three kernels, in order):\n 1. negative depths are clamped to zero (momentum zeroed);\n 2. genuinely dry cells ( h < DRY_TOLERANCE ) have momentum zeroed;\n 3. thin-but-wet cells ( h < eps = DESING_EPS ) get the\n    Kurganov & Petrova (2007) desingularized velocity u = sqrt(2) h hu / sqrt(h&#94;4 + max(h&#94;4, eps&#94;4)) with momentum\n    reconstructed as hu := h*u .  For h >= eps the formula is the\n    identity u = hu/h , so well-resolved cells are left bit-exact;\n 4. a last-resort Froude backstop |u| <= FROUDE_BACKSTOP*sqrt(g h) arrests the thin-film velocity runaway that develops at wet/dry\n    fronts on sloping beds (measured: u -> 4e3 m/s at h ~ 3.5 mm and\n    a ~2000x dt collapse without it).  It is far above any depth\n    ratio this scheme can resolve, so it never shapes the physics —\n    see the constant’s docstring for the measurements. eps is the same DESING_EPS used by compute_timestep , so the\nupdate and the CFL estimator agree about what “thin” means. Uses rki_grid rki_constants module~~rki_kernel_update~~UsesGraph module~rki_kernel_update rki_kernel_update module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_kernel_update->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_kernel_update->module~rki_grid pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_kernel_update~~UsedByGraph module~rki_kernel_update rki_kernel_update module~rki_solver rki_solver module~rki_solver->module~rki_kernel_update module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_solver module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Subroutines public pure subroutine compute_rk2_average (h, hu, hv, h0, hu0, hv0, grid) SSP-RK2 averaging step: U&#94;{n+1} = 0.5 (U&#94;n + U *), averaging the\noriginal state (h0, hu0, hv0) with the twice-advanced (h, hu, hv). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid public pure subroutine compute_ssp_combine (h, hu, hv, h0, hu0, hv0, a_n, grid) Generalized SSP Shu-Osher combine: U = a_n U&#94;n + (1 - a_n) U,\nwhere U is the post-Euler-stage iterate and (h0,hu0,hv0) = U&#94;n.\nReduces exactly to compute_rk2_average for a_n = 0.5.  Applies the\nsame positivity + thin-cell treatment so each stage stays\nwet/dry-safe. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv0 (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: a_n Blend weight on the start-of-step state U&#94;n. type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid public pure subroutine compute_update (h, hu, hv, flux_h, flux_hu, flux_hv, grid, dt) Forward Euler update U = U + dt*RHS (each SSP-RK2 stage). Also\nenforces non-negative depth, zeroes momentum in dry cells, and\ndesingularizes thin-cell velocity (KP07) with a Froude backstop. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: flux_h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: flux_hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: flux_hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Timestep (s)","tags":"","url":"module/rki_kernel_update.html"},{"title":"rki_vcoord – Rakali","text":"Defines vcoord_t , a lightweight config type for the vertical coordinate.\nType-bound procedures dispatch via select case on an integer enum (no\nruntime polymorphism) so the type is GPU-safe. Implemented ( VCOORD_* ):\n  - SIGMA       — pure terrain-following (no remap).\n  - ZSIGMA      — smoothstep blend sigma (shallow) → fixed z-levels (deep);\n                  reduces sigma PGE on steep bathymetry. Conservative remap.\n  - ZSTAR       — z -lite SSH-tracking: a global z_ref stretched per column\n                  by H/z_ref(nz) so sum(dz)=H, relative spacing preserved as\n                  η changes (no sigma distortion at large SSH).\n  - ZSTAR_FULL  — per-column z_ref from local bathymetry (vanishing layers).\n  - ZSTAR_SIGMA — smoothstep blend of sigma (shallow) and z -lite (deep). Uses pic_strings rki_constants pic_logger module~~rki_vcoord~~UsesGraph module~rki_vcoord rki_vcoord module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_vcoord->module~rki_constants pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_vcoord->pic_logger pi