split_ratio = 1 Barotropic-baroclinic split: 0=auto, 1=unsplit, N>1=fixed real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: u_layer (:,:,:) Per-layer x-velocity real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: u_layer0 (:,:,:) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: v_layer (:,:,:) Per-layer y-velocity real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: v_layer0 (:,:,:) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: w (:,:,:) Vertical velocity at interfaces (nx_total, ny_total, nz+1) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: w0 (:,:,:) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: bytes => nh_state_bytes procedure, public, non_overridable :: destroy => nh_state_destroy procedure, public, non_overridable :: init => nh_state_init Functions private pure function nh_state_bytes (this) result(nbytes) Counted allocatable footprint of the non-hydrostatic slot: layer\nvelocities + NH pressure + RK2 saves + CG Poisson workspace + the\ngated mode-splitting buffers (0 when split_ratio == 1). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( nonhydrostatic_state_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=int64) Subroutines private  subroutine nh_state_destroy (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( nonhydrostatic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine nh_state_init (this, grid) Allocate all NH arrays at the grid size and the configured\nlayer count.  Mode-splitting arrays are allocated only when split_ratio /= 1 .  PCG preconditioner workspace cg_z is\nalways allocated; the OpenACC enter data directive is\nconditional on nh_preconditioner so unused PCG state isn’t\nmapped to the device. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( nonhydrostatic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid","tags":"","url":"module/rki_nonhydrostatic_state.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_pressure – Rakali","text":"Two BPG implementations:\n  - ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient (sigma method): differences\n    internal pressure at the same sigma level. Cheap; PGE ~ dH/dx\n    on steep bathymetry.\n  - ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient_jacobian (Shchepetkin &\n    McWilliams 2003): interpolates neighbour-column pressure to the\n    centre column’s z-mid level. Eliminates the leading sigma PGE;\n    ~3x more expensive per cell.\nBoth use the density anomaly rho - rho_ref(z) to keep the\nintegrand small. rho_ref_at and all_neighbours_wet are private\nsame-module helpers because the BPG kernels call them inside do concurrent , where NVHPC stdpar can’t lower cross-module calls. Uses rki_grid rki_constants rki_ml_common module~~rki_ml_pressure~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_pressure rki_ml_pressure module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_ml_pressure->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_ml_pressure->module~rki_grid module~rki_ml_common rki_ml_common module~rki_ml_pressure->module~rki_ml_common pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants module~rki_ml_common->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_ml_pressure~~UsedByGraph module~rki_ml_pressure rki_ml_pressure module~rki_solver rki_solver module~rki_solver->module~rki_ml_pressure module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_solver module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Functions private pure function all_neighbours_wet (h_col, h_col_ip1, h_col_im1, h_col_jp1, h_col_jm1) result(all_wet) Returns .true. if the centre cell and its four face-neighbours all\nhave a total column depth at or above ML_MIN_DEPTH . Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_col column depth at (i,j) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_col_ip1 column depth at (i+1,j) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_col_im1 column depth at (i-1,j) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_col_jp1 column depth at (i,j+1) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_col_jm1 column depth at (i,j-1) Return Value logical private pure function rho_ref_at (z, rho_ref, dz, nz_ref, rho_0) result(rho) Linear interpolation of the reference-density profile at depth z.\nOut-of-range falls back to the nearest endpoint. When the profile\nis unset ( dz == 0 ) returns rho_0 so the kernel reduces to the\npre-B2 anomaly. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: z real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_ref (0:nz_ref) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dz integer, intent(in) :: nz_ref real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 Return Value real(kind=wp) Subroutines public pure subroutine ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient (h_layer, rho_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, rho_0, rho_ref, rho_ref_dz, nz_ref, grid, nz, dt) Apply baroclinic pressure gradient as explicit source term —\nonly the density-driven part; the barotropic PGF (g·deta/dx) is\nhandled by the HLL step. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_ref (0:nz_ref) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_ref_dz integer, intent(in) :: nz_ref type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient_jacobian (h_layer, rho_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, rho_0, rho_ref, rho_ref_dz, nz_ref, grid, nz, dt) Baroclinic pressure gradient via the pressure Jacobian method\n(Shchepetkin & McWilliams 2003): the pressure gradient along\nconstant-z surfaces, interpolating the neighbour column’s pressure\nto the centre column’s physical depth. Uniform density ⇒ zero BPG. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_ref (0:nz_ref) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_ref_dz integer, intent(in) :: nz_ref type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_pressure.html"},{"title":"rki_si_unstr_step_ml – Rakali","text":"One semi-implicit (Casulli/SCHISM-style) step for the UNSTRUCTURED 3D\nmultilayer coastal path ( time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\" + use_multilayer , nz>1 , sigma) — built on the P3.1 TPFA eta-solve (the operator\nnever changes; only the Hf/Gbar fills do — the “strict superset”\ncontract) and the (nz, ncells) column kernels of rki_si_unstr_column .  The step (one implicit theta-step; the theta\nscheme IS the integrator): save U&#94;n edges + layer state; eta&#94;n = stage at circumcentres; explicit predictor tendencies IN PLACE on hu/hv_layer:\n     baroclinic PGF, Coriolis, Smagorinsky (existing unstructured\n     kernels), and surface wind stress on the TOP layer (k=nz) —\n     dt*tau/RHO_WATER from the uniform scalar wind (rides the\n     pure-u&#94;n predictor into G_k; R_k / Hhat / the operator are\n     untouched by linearity; no momentum self-advection — the SI\n     target regime is advection-weak, same envelope as structured); PP81 interface viscosity + per-column implicit solve\n     (G_k, R_k, Hhat = -sum h_k R_k, Gbar = sum h_k G_k); Hf from Hhat via the P3.1 edge face-depth kernel reused verbatim\n     (Hhat passed as the cell “depth”; a Dirichlet edge gets\n     0.5*(Hhat_c + h_ghost) with h_ghost = eta_bc - b — the\n     structured ghost-Hhat seed, edge-wise), edge predictor from the\n     face-averaged Gbar, theta-blend RHS + area-weighted CG — ALL\n     P3.1 machinery reused verbatim; per-layer edge-transport recovery (column sums telescope EXACTLY\n     to the 2D back-substituted edge transport => mass to round-off;\n     Dirichlet ghost R = -1 seed inline — the estuary-mouth lesson); tracers: every registry tracer advected depth-proportionally\n     with the EXACT blended edge mass flux the eta update used\n     (uniform tracers invariant per layer; OUTER SHIM: the host\n     registry loop passes tracers(it)%hTr/hTr0 into the flat-impl\n     kernel — the array-of-derived-types device rule); h&#94;{n+1} = eta&#94;{n+1} - b; h_layer = dsig*h; per-layer cell\n     momenta = least-squares edge reconstruction; barotropic momenta\n     = layer sums; U&#94;{n+1} edge prognostic = column sums; tracer vertical diffusion, surface fluxes, clamp, EOS — the\n     existing unstructured kernels reused as-is.  NO diasurface\n     exchange: the dsig-proportional advection makes sigma surfaces\n     material for the transported fields (the structured design\n     decision, carried over). The step ends with valid barotropic stage/xmom/ymom/height +\nmultilayer *_layer state — downstream (output, gauges, restart)\nunchange