rom a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_si_unstr_step_ml~~UsedByGraph module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_solver_unstr rki_solver_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private, parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 Triangles only. Subroutines public  subroutine si_unstr_step_ml (state, mesh, dt, iter_out) Advance the unstructured 3D multilayer state one semi-implicit\nstep.  The caller ( solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit ) has already\nhalo-exchanged; Dirichlet boundary coupling reads state%bc_type / state%bc_eta_ext (tidal/clamped) inside the\nedge kernels — the P3.1 coefficient-space route. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt integer, intent(out) :: iter_out private pure subroutine si_ml_save_and_eta (nct, nco, stage, bed, height, eta, u_edge, u_n_edge) Save the edge transports U&#94;n, refresh height = max(stage - b, 0),\nand form eta&#94;n = stage at circumcentres (the CG warm start). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: stage (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bed (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: height (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: eta (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: u_n_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) private pure subroutine si_ml_wetdry_face_depths (mesh, nct, nco, n_bc, eta, b_min, Hhat, bc_type, bc_eta_ext, Hf_edge, eta_ghost_edge) Frozen wet/dry edge depths for the 3D column-integrated eta-solve —\nthe triangular twin of the structured si_ml_wetdry_face_depths :\nthe effective CONVEYANCE is the Hhat-based two-cell average (as the\nall-wet ML path uses), GATED by the geometric max-eta/sill wet/dry\nrule so an edge dead by geometry (higher surface below the higher\nbed) carries Hf=0 — a wall — regardless of Hhat.  The surface\ngeometry decides wet/dead; where wet, the implicit column response\nHhat sets the conveyance magnitude.  b_min = the geometric sill bed\n(deepest sub-bottom).  Dirichlet edges gate the ghost-coupled face\nthe same way (ghost surface = the prescribed eta_bc; ghost sill\nmirrors the cell sill).  All-wet Hhat basins reduce this EXACTLY to\nthe P3.1 si_unstr_face_depths conveyance (0.5*(Hhat_c+Hhat_nbr)),\nso the wet/dry branch is a strict superset.  Cell-centric\ndouble-visit (3,ncell) , cell-index-last. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. integer, intent(in) :: n_bc BC group table size. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta (nct) eta&#94;n at circumcentres (the FROZEN surface). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b_min (nct) Geometric sill bed (deepest sub-bottom) at cells (m). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hhat (nct) Column effective depth (conveyance magnitude, m). integer, intent(in) :: bc_type (n_bc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bc_eta_ext (n_bc) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: eta_ghost_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) private  subroutine si_ml_wetdry_newton (state, mesh, nct, nco, g_theta2_dt2, iter_out) Newton outer loop for the 3D column-integrated wet/dry eta-solve on\nthe triangulation — the triangular twin of the structured si_ml_wetdry_newton (and the 2D-unstr si_unstr_advance_wetdry ’s\nNewton loop).  The column responses (g_col/r_col/Hhat/Gbar) and the\nfrozen Hf are held FIXED (they depend on h_layer at time n, not eta),\nso only the surface mass system F = v(eta) + T*eta - rhs_d iterates,\nwith T the Hhat-weighted TPFA stiffness and the surface wet-fraction\nNewton diagonal a(eta)+floor.  On entry state%si%eta_r holds the\nLINEAR RHS (leading eta&#94;n from si_unstr_compute_rhs); this swaps the\nleading term for v(eta&#94;n) once, then Newton-solves.  Host-side\norchestration; flat device kernels.  Writes state%si%newton_iters\nand state%si%mass_res = the NONLINEAR mass residual ||F||&#94;2 at\nNewton exit (the conservation diagnostic — NOT the inner-CG residual\nof the last delta-solve, which is an internal solver number). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nct integer, intent(in) :: nco real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_theta2_dt2 integer, intent(out) :: iter_out Inner CG iterations summed over the Newton outers. private pure subroutine si_ml_zero_dead_edges (nct, nco, Hf_edge, u_n_edge) Zero the saved U&#94;n on dead (wall / Hf=0) edges — Casulli rule R3:\na dead edge carries no (1-theta) flux into the theta-blend RHS. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: u_n_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct)","tags":"","url":"module/rki_si_unstr_step_ml.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_keps_unstr – Rakali","text":"Unstructured (triangular) port of the structured rki_ml_keps : the same\nclean-room k-epsilon closure (Launder-Spalding; Rodi 1987; Warner 2005)\nper water column, cell-centric on the unstructured C-grid. dk/dt   = d/dz(nu_t/sig_k dk/dz) + P + B - eps\n  deps/dt = d/dz(nu_t/sig_e deps/dz) + (eps/k)(ce1 P + ce3 B - ce2 eps)\n  nu_t = c_mu k&#94;2/eps,  kappa_t = c_mu’ k&#94;2/eps Staggering (bottom-up, ROMS): velocity/density at layer centres\n(1..nz); k/eps/nu_t/kappa_t at interfaces (1..nz+1, 1=bed, nz+1=surface).\nPer cell: implicit (Thomas) vertical diffusion + semi-implicit (Patankar)\ndissipation sinks for positivity.  Stability functions come from the\nshared rki_keps_stability (constant / Galperin / Canuto) as a pure !$acc routine seq (cross-module — a cheap device call, not inlined). The kernel is a flat explicit-shape _impl (arrays as (nz, ncell) )\ninvoked through a thin state-passed shim — keeps the device loop free of\nderived-type dereferences and is directly unit-testable like the\nstructured ml_keps_update .\npublic for unit testing\npublic for unit testing\npublic for unit testing Uses rki_keps_stability rki_state_unstr rki_constants rki_ml_common_unstr module~~rki_ml_keps_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_keps_unstr rki_ml_keps_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_ml_keps_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_keps_stability rki_keps_stability module~rki_ml_keps_unstr->module~rki_keps_stability module~rki_ml_common_unstr rki_ml_common_unstr module~rki_ml_keps_unstr->module~rki_ml_common_unstr module~rki_state_unstr rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_keps_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_keps_stability->module~rki_constants module~rki_ml_common_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_b