in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CE1 = 1.44_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CE2 = 1.92_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CE3 = -0.4_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: CMU = 0.09_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: EPS_MIN = 1.0e-12_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: KAPPA_EFF = 0.4327_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: K_MIN = 1.0e-8_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: NUT_MAX = 10.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: NUT_MIN = 1.0e-6_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: SIG_E = 1.3_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: SIG_K = 1.0_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: Z0_BED = 0.01_wp real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: Z0_SURF = 0.01_wp Subroutines public  subroutine ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer_unstr (state, hTr, kappa_bg, dt) State-passed shim: implicit vertical diffusion of one tracer with the\nkeps diffusivity kt + a background floor.  No-flux top/bottom (surface\ntracer fluxes are separate), conserves the column tracer content. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_bg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer_unstr_impl (nz, n, h_layer, hTr, kt, kappa_bg, height_cv, dt) Per-cell implicit tracer diffusion on flat explicit-shape arrays.  Same\ntridiagonal as the momentum apply but with the scalar diffusivity\nkt + kappa_bg and a single RHS (the tracer concentration hTr/h). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kt (nz+1,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_bg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: height_cv (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public  subroutine ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr (state, dt) State-passed shim: apply the keps eddy viscosity to layer momentum by\nan implicit (Thomas) vertical-diffusion sweep.  No-flux at bed/surface\n(wind + bottom drag are separate kernels), conserves the column total. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr_impl (nz, n, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, nut, height_cv, dt) Per-cell implicit vertical diffusion of momentum on flat explicit-shape\narrays.  Implicit (not the explicit PP81 clamp) – the keps nu_t can\nreach NUT_MAX.  One factorisation, two RHS (u, v). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: nut (nz+1,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: height_cv (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine ml_keps_friction_velocities_unstr (state) Per-cell surface + bed friction velocities feeding the keps wall\nfunctions.  Surface: u_ s = sqrt(|tau_wind|/rho_0) from the (uniform)\nunstructured wind stress.  Bed: quadratic Manning u_ b = sqrt(C_d)*|u_b|,\nC_d = g n&#94;2 / H&#94;(1/3), from the bottom (k=1) layer speed.  Writes\nkeps_ustar_s/b on the multilayer state. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public  subroutine ml_keps_update_unstr (state, dt, use_walls) State-passed shim: advance k/eps one step per cell and recover\nnu_t/kappa_t. use_walls imposes the Dirichlet log-law wall functions\n(from keps_ustar_s/b); .false. uses the zero-gradient closure (the\nstandalone unit tests).  Extracts the flat arrays and calls the impl. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt logical, intent(in) :: use_walls public pure subroutine ml_keps_update_unstr_impl (nz, n, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, rho_layer, tke, eps, nut, kt, ustar_s, ustar_b, height_cv, rho_0, dt, use_walls, scheme) Per-cell k/eps advance on flat explicit-shape arrays.  One do concurrent over cells (thread-per-cell — full occupancy for the\nshort vertical dimension); sequential vertical sweep per cell with\nBPG_NZ_MAX stack workspace, same pattern as the unstructured PP81/KPP. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: tke (nz+1,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eps (nz+1,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: nut (nz+1,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: kt (nz+1,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: ustar_s (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: ustar_b (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: height_cv (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt logical, intent(in) :: use_walls integer, intent(in) :: scheme private pure subroutine keps_tridiag_solve_noflux_u (a, b, c, rhs, cp, nn) In-place Thomas solve over rows 1..nn with the boundary closure already\nbaked into a/b/c by the caller (no row override, unlike keps_tridiag_solve_u ).  a/b/c read-only so one factorisation serves\nmultiple RHS.  Duplicate of the structured keps_tridiag_solve_noflux,\nkept same-module so it inlines in the per-cell apply loop. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: a (nn) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b (nn) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: c (nn) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: rhs (nn) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: cp (nn) integer, intent(in) :: nn private pure subroutine keps_tridiag_solve_u (a, b, c, rhs, cp, ni) In-place Thomas solve over interfaces 1..ni with zero-gradient\n(no-flux) boundary rows. rhs returns the solution; cp scratch.\n(Duplicate of the structured keps_tridiag_solve; tiny standard\nalgorithm — can be consolidated into a shared module later.) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: a (ni) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: b (ni) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: c (ni) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: rhs (ni) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: cp (ni) integer, intent(in) :: ni","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_keps_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_sponge_unstr – Rakali","text":"Explicit volumetric damping of h and momentum toward a reference\nstate at cells adjacent to boundary edges tagged BC_SPONGE . Algorithm: for each owned cell, scan the three edges.  If any edge\nis a boundary edge ( mesh%neighbours(e, cell) < 0 ) belonging to a\nBC_SPONGE group, collect the group’s strength [1/s] and h_ref [m]. When multiple sponge edges exist (a corner cell), use the\nmaximum strength and its paired h_ref .  Then apply one forward-\nEuler relaxation step: h <- h - dt alpha (h - h_ref)\n  xmom <- xmom (1 - dt alpha)\n  ymom <- ymom (1 - dt alpha) where h = stage_cv - bed_cv and alpha = bc_sponge_strength(g) . The kernel self-gates: cells not adjacent to any active BC_SPONGE\nedge are skipped implicitly (alpha stays at 0).  No-op when strength <= 0 for all sponge groups. v1 limitation: the sponge band is one cell deep — only cells with\na direct boundary edge are affected.  Graded-width profiles require\ncell-distance information that is not available on triangular meshes\nwithout additional mesh topology data.  On the structured side the\ndistance is implicit in the (i,j) indices; no such shortcut exists\nhere.  Multi-cell sponge widths are deferred. Uses rki_mesh_unstr rki_boundary_unstr rki_state_unstr rki_constants module~~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr rki_kernel_sponge_unstr module~rki_boundary_unstr rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_kernel_s