h it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Subroutines public pure subroutine apply_sponge_unstr (state, mesh, dt) Apply sponge relaxation to all owned cells adjacent to a BC_SPONGE edge. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt","tags":"","url":"module/rki_kernel_sponge_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_si_unstr_helmholtz – Rakali","text":"The elliptic (wave-continuity) machinery for the semi-implicit\nfree-surface mode on the UNSTRUCTURED (triangular) backend — the\ntwo-point flux (TPFA, Casulli & Walters 2000) scheme.  Substituting the semi-implicit edge momentum into\ndepth-integrated continuity gives a Helmholtz system for eta&#94;{n+1} at\nthe circumcentres: [ M - g theta&#94;2 dt&#94;2 * div_c( Hf grad_e ) ] eta&#94;{n+1} = RHS with the CELL-CENTRED FV divergence (÷area_c, depth units) and the\nper-edge TPFA transmissibility K_e = Hf_e * len_e / delta_e ( delta_e = circumcentre-to-circumcentre distance). M is the cell\nmass coefficient (1 on the all-wet 2D path; the wet/dry Newton diagonal\nin P3.3). THE LOAD-BEARING DETAIL: the operator (T eta)_c = -(coef/area_c) *\nsum_e sign_e K_e (eta_nbr - eta_c) is self-adjoint in the AREA-WEIGHTED\ninner product = sum_c area_c x_c y_c, NOT the plain dot — variable\ncell areas scale the rows.  Every CG/Jacobi reduction here carries the area weight; uniform area recovers the structured harness.  Get it\nwrong and CG stalls (prototype §7.5). CELL-CENTRIC DOUBLE-VISIT: every apply computes each cell’s own row\nfrom its own 3 edges (reads neighbour eta, writes own Ap) — the house\nflux pattern, GPU-race-free.  Interior edges are visited twice (once\nfrom each side); no scatter, no atomics.  Single-rank, owned-cell loops. Uses rki_mesh_unstr rki_constants rki_si_unstr_mg module~~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz~~UsesGraph module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz rki_si_unstr_helmholtz module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_mg rki_si_unstr_mg module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz->module~rki_si_unstr_mg pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants pic_io pic_io module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_io pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_types module~rki_si_unstr_mg->module~rki_constants module~rki_si_unstr_mg->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_mg->pic_logger Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz~~UsedByGraph module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz rki_si_unstr_helmholtz module~rki_si_unstr_step rki_si_unstr_step module~rki_si_unstr_step->module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_si_unstr_step module~rki_solver_unstr rki_solver_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: DELTA_EPS = 1.0e-30_wp 1/0 armour on the circumcentre-line distance (never fires on a\ngated mesh — the quality gate rejects delta<=0 at configure). integer, private, parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 Triangles only. integer, private, parameter :: SI_MAX_ITER = 4000 CG iteration cap (triangle plain-CG is ~7x the structured count at\nmatched Courant — prototype study 4; the cap leaves headroom). Functions public pure function si_unstr_edge_flux (hf, eta_c, eta_nbr, inv_delta) result(flux) The single discrete edge-normal transport used by the TPFA\noperator’s div(Hf grad eta) , the edge predictor’s explicit PGF,\nand the edge back-substitution:\n  flux = Hf * (eta_nbr - eta_c) / delta   (along the outward normal)\nSharing ONE flux function across the operator/back-sub is what makes\nthe back-substituted edge transports satisfy discrete continuity\nidentically (mass consistency). !$acc routine seq for device\ndo-concurrent bodies. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hf Frozen edge effective depth Hf_e. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_c eta at this cell / the across-edge neighbour (or Dirichlet ghost). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_nbr eta at this cell / the across-edge neighbour (or Dirichlet ghost). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: inv_delta 1/delta_e (circumcentre-line distance reciprocal). Return Value real(kind=wp) private pure function si_unstr_face_depth_linear (h_c, h_nbr) result(hf) All-wet (2D barotropic) edge effective depth: the arithmetic mean of\nthe two cells’ still-water depths, Hf = 0.5*(h_c + h_nbr) .  This is\nthe gated-mean rule ( face_depth_wetdry ) in its\nall-wet limit — it reduces EXACTLY to the linear edge depth.  Wall edges never call\nthis (Hf stays 0); Dirichlet edges pass the ghost h . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_c real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_nbr Return Value real(kind=wp) Subroutines public pure subroutine si_unstr_apply_helmholtz (mesh, ncell_total, ncell_owned, eta, Ap, Hf_edge, g_theta2_dt2, mass_diag) Matrix-free apply Ap = A*eta for the SPD TPFA Helmholtz operator: Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: ncell_total Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer, intent(in) :: ncell_owned Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: Ap (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_theta2_dt2 real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: mass_diag (ncell_total) Per-cell Newton mass diagonal (wet/dry); absent => 1.0. public  subroutine si_unstr_cg_solve (mesh, ncell_total, ncell_owned, eta, cg_r, cg_p, cg_Ap, cg_z, eta_diag, Hf_edge, g_theta2_dt2, precond, rtol, iter_out, mass_res_out, mass_diag, mg) Area-weighted (optionally preconditioned) CG for the TPFA Helmholtz\neta-solve, warm-started from eta&#94;n.  On entry cg_r holds the RHS and eta the warm start.  EVERY dot product carries the mesh%area weight (the operator is self-adjoint in _A only — prototype\n§7.5); the convergence gate is the area-weighted relative residual ||r||_A&#94;2 < rtol&#94;2 ||rhs||_A&#94;2 on the UNPRECONDITIONED residual in\nevery mode (comparable iteration counts).  Preconditioners:\nNONE (plain), JACOBI ( z = eta_diag*r ), MG (aggregation-multigrid\nV-cycle via mg , z = Vcycle_Ahat(area*r) — the same area*r symmetric-space RHS the Jacobi apply implicitly uses). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: ncell_total Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer, intent(in) :: ncell_owned Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: cg_r (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: cg_p (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: cg_Ap (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: cg_z (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta_diag (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_theta2_dt2 integer, intent(in) :: precond real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rtol integer, intent(out) :: iter_out real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: mass_res_out Area-weighted interior residual sum at solve end (mass diagnostic). real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: mass_diag (ncell_total) type( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout), optional :: mg Aggregation-MG hierarchy (required when precond == MG); its\noperator must already be refreshed for this step’s frozen Hf. public pure subroutine si_unstr_compute_diag (mesh, ncell_total, ncell_owned, Hf_edge, eta_diag, g_theta2_dt2, mass_diag) Precompute the reciprocal of the TPFA Helmholtz operator diagonal\n(Jacobi preconditioner):\n  diag_c = M_c + (g theta&#94;2 dt&#94;2/area_c) * sum_{e in c} K_e\nstored as 1/diag.  M_c = 1 (linear) or a+floor (wet/dry, present mass_diag ).  Wall edges (Hf=0) drop out => diag -> M there. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: ncell_total Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer, intent(in) :: ncell_owned Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: eta_diag (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_theta2_dt2 real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: mass_diag (ncell_total) public  subroutine si_unstr_compute_rhs (mesh, ncell_total, ncell_owned, eta_n, u_star, u_n, rhs, dt, theta, Hf_edge, eta_ghost_edge, g_theta2_dt2) Assemble the theta-blend RHS from the CELL edge transports:\n  RHS_c = eta&#94;n_c - (dt/area_c) * sum_{e in c} sign_e *\n            [theta U _e + (1-theta) U&#94;n_e] * len_e\n            + (coef/area_c) * sum_{Dirichlet e in c} K_e * eta_ghost_e\nU _e / U&#94;n_e are per-edge transports (double-visit (3,ncell)); the\nblend flux telescopes over interior edges (each shared by 2 cells\nwith opposite outward normals) and every wall edge carries 0\n(Hf=0 kills the predictor PGF, and U&#94;n is zeroed on dead edges), so\ntotal mass is conserved to CG tolerance + round-off by construction.\nThe Dirichlet term is the coefficient-space route: the operator\n( si_unstr_apply_helmholtz ) treats the fixed ghost eta as 0, so its\nreal value is carried here. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: ncell_total Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer, intent(in) :: ncell_owned Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_n (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_star (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_n (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rhs (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_ghost_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_theta2_dt2 public pure subroutine si_unstr_face_depths (mesh, ncell_total, ncell_owned, n_bc, height, bed, bc_type, bc_eta_ext, Hf_edge, eta_ghost_edge) Build the per-edge frozen effective depth Hf_e (2D all-wet path) AND\nthe per-edge Dirichlet ghost surface eta_ghost_edge :\n  interior/partition edge: Hf = 0.5 (h_c + h_nbr); ghost unused (0).\n  WALL edge: Hf = 0 (no coupling — no-flux Neumann in the coeffs).\n  TIDAL/CLAMPED (Dirichlet) edge: the ghost surface is the prescribed\n    eta_bc; the ghost bed mirrors the cell bed so the ghost depth is\n    h_ghost = eta_bc - b_c, and Hf = 0.5 (h_c + h_ghost).  The ghost\n    eta is stashed in eta_ghost_edge(i,k) for the operator + RHS +\n    back-sub (the coefficient-space Dirichlet route). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: ncell_total Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer, intent(in) :: ncell_owned Owned-cell loop bound. integer, intent(in) :: n_bc BC group table size ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: height (ncell_total) Still-water depth h at cells (m). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bed (ncell_total) Bed elevation b at cells (m). integer, intent(in) :: bc_type (n_bc) Per-group BC type ( state%bc_type ), the boundary lookup. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bc_eta_ext (n_bc) Per-group Dirichlet external surface eta (m) ( state%bc_eta_ext ). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) Edge effective depth (m). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: eta_ghost_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,ncell_total) Dirichlet ghost surface eta (m) on Dirichlet boundary edges;\n0 elsewhere (unread — Hf=0 there). private  subroutine si_unstr_precond_apply (mesh, ncell_total, ncell_owned, r, z, eta_diag, use_mg, mg) Preconditioner apply z = M&#94;{-1} r for the area-weighted PCG.\nJACOBI: z = eta_diag*r (diagonal).  MG: one aggregation-multigrid\nV-cycle of the symmetric Ahat on the area-weighted RHS\n( agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond folds the area*r ), which reduces to\nthe Jacobi apply when the V-cycle is a single diagonal sweep — the\ngeneralisation is exact (module header).  Owned cells only; the ghost\nband of z is left as the caller set it (pre-zeroed). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: ncell_total integer, intent(in) :: ncell_owned real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: z (ncell_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_diag (ncell_total) logical, intent(in) :: use_mg type( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout), optional :: mg","tags":"","url":"module/rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_friction – Rakali","text":"Manning quadratic bottom friction on the bottom layer (k=1) and per-layer\nCoriolis rotation of every layer’s momentum ( ml_apply_coriolis ). Per-layer (vs depth-averaged) friction/Coriolis damps and rotates the\nbaroclinic shear (gravity currents, dense overflows) using each layer’s\nown velocity. Replaces the depth-averaged apply_coriolis on the\nmultilayer path; the barotropic-only path keeps the depth-averaged version. Layers are bottom-up (k=1 bed, k=nz surface): bed friction acts at k=1.\nSemi-implicit friction: hu_new = hu_old / (1 + dt C_d |u_b|/h_k),\nC_d = g*n&#94;2/H&#94;{1/3}. Uses rki_grid rki_constants rki_ml_common module~~rki_ml_friction~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_friction rki_ml_friction module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_ml_friction->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_ml_friction->module~rki_grid module~rki_ml_common rki_ml_common module~rki_ml_friction->module~rki_ml_common pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants module~rki_ml_common->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_ml_friction~~UsedByGraph module~rki_ml_friction rki_ml_friction module~rki_solver rki_solver module~rki_solver->module~rki_ml_friction module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_solver module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Subroutines public pure subroutine ml_apply_bottom_friction (h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, manning_n, use_linear_drag, drag_r, grid, nz, dt) Apply bottom friction to the lowest active layer (k=1, bottom-up) using\nthat layer’s velocity. Two semi-implicit drag laws:\n  quadratic Manning (default):  hu_new = hu / (1 + dt C_d |u_b|/h_k),\n    C_d = g n&#94;2/H&#94;{1/3}, H = total column depth.\n  linear Rayleigh ( use_linear_drag ):  hu_new = hu / (1 + dt r). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: manning_n logical, intent(in) :: use_linear_drag Use linear (Rayleigh) drag with rate drag_r instead of Manning. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: drag_r Linear bottom-drag rate (1/s); only read when use_linear_drag. type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine ml_apply_coriolis (h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, grid, nz, dt, f) Per-layer Coriolis rotation: rotate every layer’s (hu_k, hv_k) through angle f*dt via the closed-form (energy-conserving, det=1)\nrotation matrix\n  hu_new =  hu_old cos(f dt) + hv_old sin(f dt)\n  hv_new = -hu_old sin(f dt) + hv_old cos(f dt) f is a scalar (latitude-only). Skips layers below the dry-cell\nthreshold so already-zeroed momentum is untouched. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: f","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_friction.html"},{"title":"rki_recon_weno – Rakali","text":"Uses rki_grid rki_constants rki_ml_common module~~rki_recon_weno~~UsesGraph module~rki_recon_weno rki_recon_weno module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_recon_weno->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_recon_weno->module~rki_grid module~rki_ml_common rki_ml_common module~rki_recon_weno->module~rki_ml_common pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants module~rki_ml_common->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_recon_weno~~UsedByGraph module~rki_recon_weno rki_recon_weno module~rki_solver rki_solver module~rki_solver->module~rki_recon_weno proc~state_init_from_config state_t%state_init_from_config proc~state_init_from_config->module~rki_recon_weno proc~validate_config validate_config proc~validate_config->module~rki_recon_weno module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_solver module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_OK = 0 Config honours the requested tracer_recon code. integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_PPM = 0 Use PPM (the default path — does not call this module). integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_REJECT_NO_ML = 4 weno* requested on a coastal run without multilayer tracers. integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_REJECT_OCEAN = 3 weno* requested on sim_type=’ocean’ (coastal-only in wave 1). integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_REJECT_PQM = 1 “pqm” requested — deferred, not implemented on any config. integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_REJECT_UNKNOWN = 2 Unrecognised tracer_recon string. integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_WENO5 = 1 WENO5-Z (Jiang-Shu 1996 + Borges 2008 Z-weights), nghost >= 3. integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_WENO7 = 2 WENO7-Z (Balsara-Shu 2000), nghost >= 4. integer, public, parameter :: TRACER_RECON_WENO9 = 3 WENO9-Z (Balsara-Shu 2000), nghost >= 5. Functions public pure function parse_tracer_recon (str) result(code) Map a namelist string onto a TRACER_RECON_* code. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: str Return Value integer public pure function plm_face_swept (qm1, q0, qp1, sigma) result(face) PLM (piecewise-linear) swept-average face value. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm1 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: q0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp1 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: sigma Return Value real(kind=wp) public pure function recon_rung_for_face (avail_up, avail_down, rung_max) result(rung) Return the highest feasible reconstruction rung for one face. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: avail_up Interior cells from domain-west to face (including upwind cell c). integer, intent(in) :: avail_down Interior cells from face downwind side to domain-east. integer, intent(in) :: rung_max Maximum internal rung allowed (4 = WENO9, 3 = WENO7, 2 = WENO5). Return Value integer public pure function tracer_recon_required_nghost (code) result(ng) Minimum nghost required for a given TRACER_RECON_* code. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: code TRACER_RECON_* constant. Return Value integer public pure function tracer_recon_support_status (recon_code, is_ocean, has_multilayer_tracers) result(status) Decide whether a parsed tracer_recon code is honoured on this\nconfig, independent of the multilayer nghost/use_ppm_tracer\nquality guards (those apply only once this returns OK for a weno\nrung).  Factored out as a pure predicate so the fail-loud\ndecision is unit-testable without triggering error stop. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: recon_code parse_tracer_recon(cfg%tracer_recon) result. logical, intent(in) :: is_ocean .true. when sim_type == ‘ocean’. logical, intent(in) :: has_multilayer_tracers cfg%use_multilayer — the coastal multilayer tracer registry. Return Value integer public pure function weno5_face_swept (qm2, qm1, q0, qp1, qp2, sigma) result(face) WENO5-Z swept-average face value (u > 0, upwind cell = q0). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm2 Cell averages at i-2, i-1, i, i+1, i+2. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm1 Cell averages at i-2, i-1, i, i+1, i+2. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: q0 Cell averages at i-2, i-1, i, i+1, i+2. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp1 Cell averages at i-2, i-1, i, i+1, i+2. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp2 Cell averages at i-2, i-1, i, i+1, i+2. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: sigma CFL of upwind cell: |u_eff|*dt/dx. Return Value real(kind=wp) public pure function weno7_face_swept (qm3, qm2, qm1, q0, qp1, qp2, qp3, sigma) result(face) WENO7-Z swept-average face value (u > 0, upwind cell = q0). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm3 Cell averages at i-3 through i+3. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm2 Cell averages at i-3 through i+3. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm1 Cell averages at i-3 through i+3. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: q0 Cell averages at i-3 through i+3. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp1 Cell averages at i-3 through i+3. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp2 Cell averages at i-3 through i+3. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp3 Cell averages at i-3 through i+3. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: sigma CFL of upwind cell: |u_eff|*dt/dx. Return Value real(kind=wp) public pure function weno9_face_swept (qm4, qm3, qm2, qm1, q0, qp1, qp2, qp3, qp4, sigma) result(face) WENO9-Z swept-average face value (u > 0, upwind cell = q0). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm4 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm3 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm2 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qm1 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: q0 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp1 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp2 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp3 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: qp4 Cell averages at i-4 through i+4. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: sigma CFL of upwind cell: |u_eff|*dt/dx. Return Value real(kind=wp) Subroutines public pure subroutine ml_advect_tracer_weno (h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, mass_flux_x, mass_flux_y, hTr_layer, weno_tr_snap, grid, nz, dt, recon) Per-layer WENO horizontal advection of a scalar tracer hTr = h*Tr. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Layer depths (m), bottom-up: k=1 bed, k=nz surface. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Layer x-momentum flux (m&#94;2/s). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Layer y-momentum flux (m&#94;2/s). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) Barotropic x mass flux (m&#94;2/s). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) Barotropic y mass flux (m&#94;2/s). real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Tracer h Tr (m [units]), updated in-place. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: weno_tr_snap (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) Caller-owned concentration-snapshot scratch (Tr = hTr/h); filled\nthen read here.  Passed in (not module state) to keep this pure . type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of vertical layers. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Timestep (s). integer, intent(in) :: recon TRACER_RECON_WENO5/7/9 code.","tags":"","url":"module/rki_recon_weno.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_protect_unstr – Rakali","text":"Negative-depth guard after each flux + update step. Cells with\ndepth h = stage - bed below DRY_TOLERANCE have their centroid\nmomenta zeroed; thin-but-wet cells ( h < eps = DESING_EPS ,\nthe Kurganov & Petrova 2007 desingularization length shared with the\nstructured kernels) get the desingularized velocity u = sqrt(2) h uh / sqrt(h&#94;4 + eps&#94;4) and uh := h*u , which\nbounds thin-cell velocity smoothly instead of freezing thin water\n(the old hard zero below minimum_allowed_height pinned wet/dry\nfronts); a FROUDE_BACKSTOP rescale arrests thin-film velocity\nrunaway (see the constant’s docstring for the measurements).\nStrictly-negative cells clip stage back to bed (h=0) and\naccumulate the removed mass (-h)*area into state%mass_error .\nUses !$acc parallel loop reduction(+:..) (array write + scalar\nreduction don’t fit do concurrent ). Uses rki_mesh_unstr rki_state_unstr rki_constants module~~rki_kernel_protect_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_kernel_protect_unstr rki_kernel_protect_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_kernel_protect_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_kernel_protect_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_state_unstr rki_state_unstr module~rki_kernel_protect_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants pic_io pic_io module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_io pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_types module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr rki_barotropic_state_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr module~rki_boundary_unstr rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr rki_multilayer_state_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr module~rki_si_common rki_si_common module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_si_common module~rki_si_unstr_state rki_si_unstr_state module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_state module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_timestepper rki_timestepper module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_timestepper module~rki_state_unstr->pic_io module~rki_state_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->mod