nel_protect_unstr module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Subroutines public  subroutine protect_unstr (state, mesh) Apply the negative-depth and shallow-cell guards. Adds the\nclipped negative mass to state%mass_error (does not reset). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh","tags":"","url":"module/rki_kernel_protect_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity – Rakali","text":"Smagorinsky (1963) eddy-viscosity + biharmonic closures on the\nstructured multilayer grid.  Owns persistent per-step\nmomentum-snapshot workspaces, torn down via ml_horizontal_viscosity_cleanup at simulation end. Uses rki_grid rki_constants rki_ml_common module~~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity->module~rki_grid module~rki_ml_common rki_ml_common module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity->module~rki_ml_common pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants module~rki_ml_common->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity~~UsedByGraph module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity module~rki_solver rki_solver module~rki_solver->module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_solver module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: bih_lap_u (:,:,:) real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: bih_lap_v (:,:,:) real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: horvisc_hu_pre (:,:,:) real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: horvisc_hv_pre (:,:,:) Subroutines public  subroutine ml_horizontal_viscosity_biharmonic (h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, nu_4, grid, nz, dt) Biharmonic (del&#94;4) lateral viscosity on layer momentum:\nd(hu)/dt = -nu_4 h del&#94;2(del&#94;2 u) in two Laplacian passes (pass 1\nover interior + one ghost ring; pass 2 over the interior).\nScale-selective vs the harmonic Smagorinsky operator. nu_4 capped at the explicit stability limit\nnu_4 dt ((pi/dx)&#94;2+(pi/dy)&#94;2)&#94;2 <= 2.  Assumes nghost >= 2. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: nu_4 type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public  subroutine ml_horizontal_viscosity_cleanup () Release the lateral-viscosity persistent workspaces.  Called by the\nsolver at simulation end. Arguments None public  subroutine ml_horizontal_viscosity_smag (h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, cs, grid, nz, dt) Smagorinsky (1963) horizontal viscosity for layer momentum:\nnu_h = (Cs delta)&#94;2 |S| Laplacian diffusion, delta=sqrt(dx*dy). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total,nz) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: cs type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt private  subroutine bih_workspace_ensure (nx, ny, nz) Lazy-allocate the biharmonic intermediate-Laplacian scratch. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz private  subroutine horvisc_workspace_ensure (nx, ny, nz) Lazy-allocate the Smagorinsky momentum-snapshot scratch. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nx integer, intent(in) :: ny integer, intent(in) :: nz","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity.html"},{"title":"rki_timestepper – Rakali","text":"Holds the Shu-Osher coefficient table for the selectable explicit\ntime integrator ( time_scheme ).  Every scheme is built from the same\nforward-Euler stage primitive: stage i advances the running iterate by beta(i)*dt , then blends with the start-of-step state U&#94;n : E       = U&#94;(i-1) + beta(i)*dt * L(U&#94;(i-1))     ! Euler step\nU&#94;(i)   = alpha(i)*U&#94;n + (1 - alpha(i))*E       ! convex blend All four schemes are strong-stability-preserving (SSP) so the per-stage\nconvex structure keeps the wetting/drying positivity of forward Euler. ssp_coeff is the factor by which the stable timestep exceeds the\nforward-Euler CFL limit (1 for euler/rk2/rk3, 2 for rk43). Data, not polymorphism: a concrete container + an enum, mirroring the vcoord_type / EOS-variant / use_hllc dispatch idiom.  The type is\nhost-side orchestration only (its weights reach kernels as scalars by\nvalue) so it is never device-mapped. Uses rki_constants module~~rki_timestepper~~UsesGraph module~rki_timestepper rki_timestepper module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_timestepper->module~rki_constants pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_timestepper~~UsedByGraph module~rki_timestepper rki_timestepper module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_timestepper module~rki_solver_unstr rki_solver_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_state_unstr rki_state_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_gauges_unstr rki_gauges_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_gauges_unstr module~rki_handle rki_handle module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_handle module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr rki_kernel_timestep_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr module~rki_output_unstr rki_output_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->modul