ded from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: MAX_STAGES = 4 Largest stage count across the supported schemes. integer, public, parameter :: TIME_EULER = 1 Forward Euler, SSPRK(1,1): 1st order, 1 stage. integer, public, parameter :: TIME_RK2 = 2 Heun / SSPRK(2,2): 2nd order, 2 stages (the default). integer, public, parameter :: TIME_RK3 = 3 Shu-Osher SSPRK(3,3): 3rd order, 3 stages. integer, public, parameter :: TIME_RK43 = 4 SSPRK(4,3): 3rd order, 4 stages, SSP coefficient 2 (2x timestep). integer, public, parameter :: TIME_SEMI_IMPLICIT = 5 Semi-implicit free-surface (Casulli): implicit gravity wave via a CG Helmholtz\neta-solve. Not an SSP stage table — dispatched separately in solver_step. Derived Types type, public :: timestepper_t Concrete Shu-Osher coefficient table for one scheme.  Host-side only. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public :: alpha (MAX_STAGES) = 0.0_wp Per-stage blend weight on U&#94;n (combine = alpha U&#94;n + (1-alpha) E). real(kind=wp), public :: beta (MAX_STAGES) = 0.0_wp Per-stage Euler-step fraction of dt . real(kind=wp), public :: c (MAX_STAGES) = 0.0_wp Per-stage time abscissa (fraction of dt ) for time-dependent BCs. integer, public :: n_stages = 2 Number of forward-Euler stages. integer, public :: scheme = TIME_RK2 Active scheme tag ( TIME_* ). real(kind=wp), public :: ssp_coeff = 1.0_wp Stable-dt multiplier vs the forward-Euler CFL limit. Functions public pure function make_timestepper (scheme) result(ts) Build the coefficient table for a scheme tag. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: scheme Return Value type( timestepper_t ) public pure function parse_time_scheme (name) result(scheme) Map a namelist string to a TIME_* tag.  Unrecognised -> TIME_RK2. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Return Value integer","tags":"","url":"module/rki_timestepper.html"},{"title":"rki_flux_dump – Rakali","text":"Diagnostic snapshot of the barotropic state arrays as they sit\nbetween the flux call and the update call inside an RK stage. Reads the existing state%barotropic%{h, hu, hv, b, flux_*,\nmass_flux_*} arrays that the solver has already populated on\ndevice — does not re-run the kernel.  The dump must be\ninserted between solver_compute_barotropic_flux and compute_update so that (h, hu, hv, b) are still the flux\nkernel’s inputs and flux_* / mass_flux_* are the matching\noutputs.  After compute_update , h/hu/hv are overwritten. Input fields are written over the full ghost-padded array shape (nx_total, ny_total) ; outputs are written over the interior (nx_phys, ny_phys) .  Combined with the nghost global\nattribute, that lets a reader reconstruct the 9-point cross\nstencil (i-2..i+2, j) + (i, j-2..j+2) that each interior cell\nconsumes. Uses rki_io_netcdf rki_constants pic_logger rki_state module~~rki_flux_dump~~UsesGraph module~rki_flux_dump rki_flux_dump module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_flux_dump->module~rki_constants module~rki_io_netcdf rki_io_netcdf module~rki_flux_dump->module~rki_io_netcdf module~rki_state rki_state module~rki_flux_dump->module~rki_state pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_flux_dump->pic_logger pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_io_netcdf->module~rki_constants module~rki_io_netcdf->pic_logger iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~rki_io_netcdf->iso_fortran_env netcdf netcdf module~rki_io_netcdf->netcdf module~rki_state->module~rki_constants module~rki_state->iso_fortran_env module~rki_barotropic_state rki_barotropic_state module~rki_state->module~rki_barotropic_state module~rki_bathymetry rki_bathymetry module~rki_state->module~rki_bathymetry module~rki_boundary_types rki_boundary_types modul