dule~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr module~rki_tracer_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr proc~si_unstr_face_depths si_unstr_face_depths proc~si_unstr_face_depths->module~rki_boundary_unstr proc~si_unstr_wetdry_face_depths si_unstr_wetdry_face_depths proc~si_unstr_wetdry_face_depths->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_gauges_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_handle->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_handle->module~rki_gauges_unstr module~rki_handle->module~rki_output_unstr module~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr module~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_kernel_friction_unstr rki_kernel_friction_unstr module~rki_kernel_friction_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr rki_kernel_fused_unstr module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_kernel_protect_unstr rki_kernel_protect_unstr module~rki_kernel_protect_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_kernel_update_unstr rki_kernel_update_unstr module~rki_kernel_update_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_eos_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_friction_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_keps_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_pressure_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_pressure_unstr->module~rki_ml_eos_unstr module~rki_ml_tracers_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_truncate_unstr rki_ml_truncate_unstr module~rki_ml_truncate_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr module~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_output_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_restart_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_flux_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_friction_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_protect_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_update_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_eos_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_friction_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_keps_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_pressure_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_tracers_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_truncate_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_handle Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: BC_CHAPMAN = 9 Chapman / Orlanski radiating boundary. No per-group external\nparameter; instead the kernel keeps a per-boundary-edge\npersistent state state%chapman_eta_old(i, k) (the previous\nstep’s eta at edge i of cell k ) and reconstructs the ghost\nstage each call from a phase-speed estimate\n  c = -(deta/dt) / (deta/dn_inward)\nclamped to [0, sqrt(g*h_int)] . Spatial gradient is\napproximated from the cell’s centroid stage and the extrapolated\nedge-midpoint stage; temporal gradient uses state%dt . The\ncomputed ghost target is then dispatched through the\nFlather/ BC_TIDAL algebra in compute_boundary_state so the\nghost momentum reconstruction matches BC_TIDAL . Matches\nstructured BC_CHAPMAN=9 semantics. integer, public, parameter :: BC_CLAMPED = 7 Prescribed free-surface elevation with transmissive momentum\n(no Flather radiation term). The per-group parameter state%bc_eta_ext(g) is the absolute stage (m); the kernel\nclamps the ghost stage to it and copies interior momentum\nacross unchanged. Pick this when you need a Dirichlet stage\nwithout wave-radiation coupling. Matches structured BC_CLAMPED=7 . integer, public, parameter :: BC_DISCHARGE = 6 Prescribed momentum flux per unit width (m&#94;2/s) along the\noutward normal. The per-group parameter state%bc_Qn_ext(g) carries the specific discharge; positive means out of the\ndomain (along the outward normal). Ghost momentum is rebuilt\nfrom (-bc_Qn_ext * n1, -bc_Qn_ext * n2) so a negative Qn\npumps mass in without a separate sign flip at the call site.\nDepth at the ghost follows the interior extrapolation. Useful\nwhen the driving quantity is a measured river flow per unit\nwidth rather than a velocity. Matches structured BC_DISCHARGE. integer, public, parameter :: BC_INFLOW = 5 Prescribed normal velocity. The per-group parameter state%bc_un_ext(g) is the velocity component along the\noutward normal – so a value of -2.0 means flow into the\ndomain at 2 m/s on a boundary whose outward normal points\nout of the domain. The Python wrapper exposes set_bc_inflow_speed(g, v) which negates internally so\npositive v always means inflow. Depth at the ghost state\nis the extrapolated interior depth. integer, public, parameter :: BC_INTERIOR = 0 Sentinel for interior edges. Never appears in state%bc_type(:) itself – it’s the value of bc_group(i, k) on edges that\nwere not assigned to a group at mesh-build time. integer, public, parameter :: BC_NESTED = 4 Nested boundary: Flather radiation driven by a parent-model\nprescribed elevation per BC group.  At smoke level this is\nidentical to BC_TIDAL — per-group bc_eta_ext(g) supplies\nthe external stage and the outward-normal ghost velocity is\nreconstructed from the Riemann invariant.  Full parent-model\ncoupling (live eta from a coarser grid) is deferred. Matches\nstructured BC_NESTED = 4 . integer, public, parameter :: BC_OPEN = 2 Transmissive (zero-gradient) radiation. The right-side ghost\nstate copies the left state, so the central-upwind solver\nemits the physical flux of the interior with no reflection.\nStateless: uses no per-group parameters. integer, public, parameter :: BC_OUTFLOW = 10 Prescribed depth at the boundary. The per-group parameter state%bc_h_ext(g) is the depth (m) the kernel clamps to;\nmomentum is transmissive. Useful as a downstream water level\ncondition for steady-state channel runs. Unstructured-only;\nno structured analog, numbered past the structured range. integer, public, parameter :: BC_SPONGE = 8 Sponge layer: explicit relaxation of h and momentum toward a\nprescribed reference state.  Per-group parameters state%bc_sponge_strength(g) [1/s] and state%bc_sponge_h_ref(g) [m] are consumed by apply_sponge_unstr (separate kernel, not\nthe flux kernel): the sponge falls through to BC_WALL ghost\nstate in the flux pass, and relaxation is applied after each\nRK2 stage update.  Matches structured BC_SPONGE = 8 . integer, public, parameter :: BC_TIDAL = 3 Prescribed free-surface elevation with Flather radiation.\nThe per-group parameter state%bc_eta_ext(g) is the absolute\nstage (m, in the same datum as the bed) the kernel clamps the\nghost stage to. Ghost outward-normal velocity is rebuilt as\n  u_n_ghost = u_n_int + sqrt(g/h_int)*(eta_int - eta_ext)\nso interior-going waves enter driven by the stage anomaly and\noutgoing waves leave cleanly. Update the value between steps\nto drive a tide. Matches structured BC_TIDAL semantics. integer, public, parameter :: BC_WALL = 1 Reflective wall. The right-side ghost state mirrors the left\nstate across the edge normal: stage / depth / bed are the\nsame, momentum has its normal component negated. Implemented\nin compute_boundary_state . integer, public, parameter :: MAX_BC_GROUPS = 32 Maximum number of boundary groups per mesh. Plenty for any\nrealistic coastal case (most have 2-5: open ocean, river\nmouths, walls). Fixed-size so the table lives inside the\nstate struct without needing a separate map(to:) .","tags":"","url":"module/rki_boundary_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_si_common – Rakali","text":"Sub-bottom fill modes for the Casulli wet/dry subgrid volume\n( &si_nml wetdry_bsub_fill ), their parser, and the conservation\nconflict predicate used by the state-enable guards. Uses pic_logger module~~rki_si_common~~UsesGraph module~rki_si_common rki_si_common pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_si_common->pic_logger Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_si_common~~UsedByGraph module~rki_si_common rki_si_common module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_si_common module~rki_state_unstr rki_state_unstr module~rki_driver->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr rki_