ments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: tag Return Value integer public pure function si_bsub_ml_conflict (bsub_fill, n_sub, use_multilayer, nz) result(conflict) The CONSERVATION conflict predicate (shared by both backends’ enable\nguards): the linear subgrid b_sub fill (n_sub >= 2) is incompatible\nwith the multilayer (nz > 1) wet/dry step.  The free-surface solve\nconserves the subgrid wetted volume v_cell(eta) = mean_s\nmax(eta - b_sub_s, 0), but the ML thickness update + recovery\nDirichlet ghost consume max(eta - b, 0) on the PLAIN bed; under linear these diverge across the partial-flooding band => mass leaks\nat the wet/dry front. flat + ML (b_sub == b, conservative) and linear + 2D (barotropic uses v_cell throughout) both return\n.false.  A v_cell-consistent ML update is a documented deferred\nlimitation; until then callers must reject a .true. combination\nfail-loud.  Pure so tests can assert it directly (the enable path\nerror-stops, which cannot be caught in-process). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: bsub_fill SI_BSUB_FILL_* fill mode. integer, intent(in) :: n_sub Subgrid sub-bottoms per cell. logical, intent(in) :: use_multilayer Multilayer (3D) mode on. integer, intent(in) :: nz Layer count (only matters together with use_multilayer). Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"module/rki_si_common.html"},{"title":"rki_barotropic_state – Rakali","text":"Depth-integrated conserved variables, bathymetry, flux-divergence\nand per-face mass-flux scratch, RK2 save buffers, and the scalar\nphysics params the barotropic kernels read (Manning n , Coriolis f ).  Lives at state%barotropic ; multilayer code reads h, hu,\nhv and mass_flux_x/y from here (produced by the barotropic step,\nconsumed by layer-distribute + CWC tracer advection). Uses rki_grid rki_constants rki_mem_report iso_fortran_env module~~rki_barotropic_state~~UsesGraph module~rki_barotropic_state rki_barotropic_state iso_fortran_env