ng rki_forcing module~rki_driver->module~rki_forcing module~rki_gauges rki_gauges module~rki_driver->module~rki_gauges module~rki_driver->module~rki_init module~rki_nesting rki_nesting module~rki_driver->module~rki_nesting module~rki_driver->module~rki_output module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver module~rki_flux_dump rki_flux_dump module~rki_flux_dump->module~rki_state module~rki_forcing->module~rki_state module~rki_gauges->module~rki_state module~rki_handle->module~rki_state module~rki_init->module~rki_state module~rki_nesting->module~rki_state module~rki_output->module~rki_state module~rki_solver->module~rki_state module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_handle Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Derived Types type, public :: barotropic_state_t Depth-integrated conserved variables and the workspace they\nproduce / consume each step. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: b (:,:) Bottom elevation (m, positive up) real(kind=wp), public :: bottom_drag_r = 0.0_wp Linear bottom-drag rate (1/s); used when use_linear_bottom_drag. real(kind=wp), public :: coriolis_f = 0.0_wp Coriolis parameter f (1/s), typically 2 Omega sin(lat) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: flux_h (:,:) Net flux divergence for h real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: flux_hu (:,:) Net flux divergence for hu real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: flux_hv (:,:) Net flux divergence for hv real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: h (:,:) Water depth (m) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: h0 (:,:) Saved h at start of RK step real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hu (:,:) x-momentum, h * u (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hu0 (:,:) Saved hu at start of RK step real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hv (:,:) y-momentum, h * v (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hv0 (:,:) Saved hv at start of RK step real(kind=wp), public :: manning_n = 0.0_wp Manning roughness coefficient (s/m&#94;{1/3}) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: mass_flux_x (:,:) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: mass_flux_y (:,:) real(kind=wp), public :: mass_out = 0.0_wp Cumulative net volume that has left the domain through its\nboundaries since t=0 (m³, positive = outflow), accumulated per\nRK stage from the scheme’s own flux divergence so the console\nconservation Error closes to round-off even with open BCs.\nSee rki_console_stats / the driver’s budget wiring. logical, public :: mass_out_tracked = .false. Set .true. once the solver has accumulated mass_out .\nCovered paths: 2D-barotropic SSP-RK2 fused path + coastal\nmultilayer nz>1.  Not set by: nz=1 ML fused fast path (safe\nraw-drift fallback — see solver note), semi-implicit, generic-RK. real(kind=wp), public :: mass_src = 0.0_wp Cumulative volume ADDED to the domain by surface sources since\nt=0 (m³, positive = added), accumulated per RK stage from\nprecipitation ( h += dt·P ), the evaporative mass sink\n( evap_mass_sink=.true. ; negative contribution), and the sponge\nh-relaxation Δh.  Feeds budget%mass_src in rki_console_stats so the residual (total−ref) + out − src stays ~round-off on\nforced runs instead of growing monotonically with the forcing. logical, public :: mass_src_tracked = .false. Set .true. once the solver has accumulated mass_src for the\ncurrent run.  Same coverage as mass_out_tracked : 2D-barotropic\nfused path + coastal multilayer nz>1.  The closed budget\n( budget%mass_active ) is enabled in the console only when BOTH\nflags are set. logical, public :: use_hllc = .false. Use HLLC (with contact wave for transverse momentum) instead\nof HLL for the barotropic Riemann flux.  Structured-only —\nthe unstructured solver always uses KNP central-upwind, which\nresolves contact discontinuities natively.  Default .false. . logical, public :: use_linear_bottom_drag = .false. Use linear (Rayleigh) bottom drag instead of quadratic Manning. logical, public :: wind_surface_layer = .false. Apply wind stress to the top layer (surface-concentrated) instead\nof the depth-uniform barotropic mode.  Multilayer only. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: bytes => barotropic_state_bytes procedure, public, non_overridable :: destroy => barotropic_state_destroy procedure, public, non_overridable :: init => barotropic_state_init Functions private pure function barotropic_state_bytes (this) result(nbytes) Counted allocatable footprint of the barotropic slot (0 for any\nunallocated array).  One arr_bytes term per allocatable — add a\nterm here whenever a new array joins the type. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( barotropic_state_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=int64) Subroutines private  subroutine barotropic_state_destroy (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( barotropic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine barotropic_state_init (this, grid) Allocate all arrays at the grid size, zero-filled.  Scalars\n( manning_n , coriolis_f ) are populated by state_init_from_config from the namelist after this routine returns. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( barotropic_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid","tags":"","url":"module/rki_barotropic_state.html"},{"title":"rki_si_unstr_step – Rakali","text":"One semi-implicit (Casulli) step for the 2D barotropic free surface on\nthe UNSTRUCTURED (triangular) backend — the TPFA / edge-transport\nscheme.  INTERNALLY STAGGERED: the predictor / back-sub\ntransports live on EDGES (per-cell double-visit u_edge(3,ncell) ,\ntransport along each edge’s outward normal), matching Casulli’s\nstaggered scheme, so the eta update is an exact edge-flux\nfinite-volume continuity step (mass conserved to CG tolerance +\nround-off).  eta lives at the triangle CIRCUMCENTRE.  The step: save U&#94;n (u_edge -> u_n_edge) and form eta&#94;n = stage_cv at\n     circumcentres (stage = h + b already; eta == stage); build per-edge frozen effective depths Hf (wall edges 0, Dirichlet\n     edges real) + the per-edge Dirichlet ghost eta; EDGE predictor U _e = U&#94;n_e - g(1-theta) dt*edge_flux(Hf,eta&#94;n) wind, gated on Hf>0 (dead edges => exactly 0); theta-blend RHS from the edge transports (+ Dirichlet ghost fold); area-weighted CG solve of the SPD TPFA Helmholtz for eta&#94;{n+1}\n     (warm-started from eta&#94;n; the load-bearing area weight); EDGE back-substitution U&#94;{n+1}_e = U _e - g theta dt edge_flux(Hf,\n     eta&#94;{n+1}) — the identical frozen Hf the operator used, so the\n     edge transports satisfy discrete continuity EXACTLY; reconstruct the A-grid cell momenta (Green-Gauss from the edge\n     normals) for the KNP seam + recover h&#94;{n+1} = eta&#94;{n+1} - b. Single-rank, owned-cell loops (no per-CG-iteration halo).  The step\nends with barotropic stage_cv/xmom_cv/ymom_cv/height_cv valid, so BCs,\ndiagnostics, output, gauges work unchanged. Uses pic_logger rki_si_unstr_wetdry rki_mesh_unstr rki_si_unstr_mg rki_constants rki_si_unstr_state rki_state_unstr rki_si_unstr_helmholtz module~~rki_si_unstr_step~~UsesGraph module~rki_si_unstr_step rki_si_unstr_step module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_si_unstr_step->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz rki_si_unstr_helmholtz module~rki_si_unstr_step->module~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz module~rki_si_unstr_mg rki_si_unstr_mg module~rki_si_unstr_step->module~rki_si_unstr_mg module~rki_si_unstr_state rki_si_