rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_MAX = 10 Cap on the wet/dry Newton outer iterations per step (prototype\nmeasured 1-3 outer/step on triangles, max 5; fail-loud ceiling). real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_TOL = 1.0e-11_wp Newton convergence tolerance on the relative nonlinear residual,\ncombined with a frozen wet active set (matches structured). real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: SI_UNSTR_THETA = 0.6_wp Implicitness parameter.  theta >= 0.5 => unconditionally stable for\nthe gravity wave; theta > 0.5 adds damping ~(theta-0.5). real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: DELTA_EPS = 1.0e-30_wp 1/0 armour on the circumcentre-line distance. integer, private, parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 Triangles only. Subroutines public pure subroutine si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta (mesh, nct, nco, u_edge, xmom, ymom) Least-squares reconstruction of the cell-centre transport vector\n(hu, hv) from the three edge-normal transports U_e = (hu,hv)·n_e:\n  M = sum_e len_e * n_e n_e&#94;T,   rhs = sum_e len_e * U_e * n_e,\n  (hu, hv) = M&#94;{-1} rhs.\nExact for a constant transport field (the three normals span R&#94;2 on\na non-degenerate triangle => M SPD, invertible).  The KNP seam only\nneeds a diagnostic cell momentum; eta/mass already closed on the\nedges.  Shared by the 2D step and (per layer) the ML step. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total) — the explicit-shape dim. integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Edge-normal transports (m&#94;2/s), + along the outward normal. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: xmom (nct) Reconstructed cell transport vector (m&#94;2/s). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: ymom (nct) Reconstructed cell transport vector (m&#94;2/s). public  subroutine si_unstr_step (state, mesh, dt, iter_out) Advance the 2D barotropic free surface one semi-implicit step on the\ntriangulation.  Reads the frozen Hf / ghost from the current\nsurface, solves the Helmholtz eta-system, and back-substitutes the\nedge transports. iter_out returns the CG iteration count (summed\nover the Newton outers in wet/dry mode). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt integer, intent(out) :: iter_out private  subroutine si_unstr_advance (mesh, nct, nco, n_bc, stage, xmom, ymom, bed, height, eta, eta_r, eta_p, eta_Ap, eta_z, eta_diag, u_edge, u_star, Hf_edge, eta_ghost_edge, u_n_edge, bc_type, bc_eta_ext, wind_tau_x, wind_tau_y, dt, theta, g_theta2_dt2, gtheta_dt, g_omtheta_dt, precond, rtol, iter_out, mass_res_out, mg) Flat-impl core: explicit-shape state arrays only (NVHPC device\ncodegen — assumed-shape dummies in do-concurrent kernels emit\nper-launch descriptor-walk memcpys).  The edge workspaces eta_ghost_edge / u_n_edge are persistent slots on the SI state\n(mapped in its enter_data — no per-step allocation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total) — the explicit-shape dim. integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. integer, intent(in) :: n_bc BC group table size ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ). real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: stage (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: xmom (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: ymom (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bed (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: height (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta_r (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta_p (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta_Ap (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta_z (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta_diag (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: u_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: u_star (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: eta_ghost_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: u_n_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) integer, intent(in) :: bc_type (n_bc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bc_eta_ext (n_bc) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_tau_x real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_tau_y real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_theta2_dt2 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: gtheta_dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_omtheta_dt integer, intent(in) :: precond real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rtol integer, intent(out) :: iter_out real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: mass_res_out type( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent(inout), optional :: mg Aggregation-MG hierarchy (present iff precond == MG); its operator\nis refreshed here for this step’s frozen Hf before the solve. private  subroutine si_unstr_advance_wetdry (state, mesh, nct, nco, n_bc, dt, theta, g_theta2_dt2, gtheta_dt, g_omtheta_dt, iter_out) One Casulli wetting/drying SI step on the triangulation — the\nNewton wrapper around the area-weighted TPFA CG (the structured si_advance_wetdry , edge-wise; V/a/Newton per-cell, prototype-\nconfirmed mesh-agnostic).  The nonlinear system is\n  F(eta) = v(eta) + T*eta - rhs_d = 0,  J = diag(a+floor) + T\nwith T the SAME frozen-Hf stiffness the linear code has (gated-mean\nedge depths — all-wet reduces exactly to the linear edge depth) and\nthe constant mass 1 replaced per cell by the wet fraction a.\nV convex => plain Newton converges monotonically (no line search). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nct integer, intent(in) :: nco integer, intent(in) :: n_bc real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_theta2_dt2 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: gtheta_dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_omtheta_dt integer, intent(out) :: iter_out Inner CG iterations summed over the Newton outers.","tags":"","url":"module/rki_si_unstr_step.html"},{"title":"rki_si_unstr_column – Rakali","text":"The SCHISM-inspired (Casulli 1990; Casulli & Cattani 1994; Zhang &\nBaptista 2008) per-column algebra of the 3D semi-implicit multilayer\nstep, ported per-cell to the (nz, ncells) axis layout (k FIRST,\ncell LAST — the unstructured convention, OPPOSITE of the structured (nx,ny,nz) ), plus the edge-wise recovery / tracer kernels that\nreplace the structured face kernels: si_unstr_build_nu_interface — PP81 Richardson interface viscosity. si_unstr_column_solve — plain-u&#94;n predictor responses G_k/R_k\n   (face/edge-based PGF split: the predictor carries NO surface PGF),\n   Thomas factorisation, three-RHS back-solve, Hhat/Gbar integrals.\n   Bottom drag: Manning quadratic on the bed row (the unstructured\n   barotropic state carries no linear-drag knob — Manning-only,\n   documented deviation from the structured use_linear_drag option). si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges — the theta-blend RHS edge\n   predictor U*_e from the face-averaged Gbar (vector projected on\n   the outward edge-normal) minus the explicit (1-theta) surface PGF. si_unstr_recover_edge_layers — post-CG per-layer EDGE transport\n   recovery; column sums telescope EXACTLY to the 2D back-substituted\n   edge transport (the mass-consistency invariant).  Dirichlet\n   boundary edges use the structured mouth-consistency seeds inline:\n   ghost G = 0, ghost R = -1, ghost h_k = dsig_k*max(eta_bc - b_c, 0). si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges — the blended column edge flux the\n   eta update used (drives the dsig tracer split + next step’s U&#94;n). si_unstr_advect_tracer_dsig — depth-proportional, race-free,\n   first-order-upwind tracer advection: per-layer edge flux EXACTLY dsig_k * mass_flux_e (the only split consistent with the\n   dsig-slaved thickness update => uniform tracers invariant per\n   layer); upwind values read from the PRE-STEP snapshot only.\n   FLAT-IMPL: called per registry tracer through the outer shim in\n   the step module (the array-of-derived-types device rule). si_unstr_edge_layers_to_cells — per-layer least-squares A-grid\n   cell-momentum reconstruction (the 2D reconstruction, per layer). si_unstr_update_thickness_ml — h&#94;{n+1} = eta&#94;{n+1} - b and the\n   sigma slaving h_k = dsig_k*h. si_unstr_apply_wind_top_layer — dt*tau/rho on the surface layer\n   (k = nz) transport; the uniform-scalar unstructured wind. Layer convention (load-bearing): BOTTOM-UP — k=1 bed, k=nz surface.\nCell-centric double-visit throughout (each cell owns its 3 edge\nvalues; interior edges computed twice, bit-exactly antisymmetric —\nno scatter, no atomics).  Explicit-shape dummies in every DC kernel\n(NVHPC descriptor-walk rule); fixed-size local columns NZ_STACK_MAX . Uses rki_mesh_unstr rki_constants module~~rki_si_unstr_column~~UsesGraph module~rki_si_unstr_column rki_si_unstr_column module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_si_unstr_column->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_column->module~rki_mesh_unstr pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants pic_io pic_io module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_io pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_si_unstr_column~~UsedByGraph module~rki_si_unstr_column rki_si_unstr_column module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_si_unstr_column module~rki_solver_unstr rki_solver_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: DELTA_EPS = 1.0e-30_wp 1/0 armour on the circumcentre-line distance (gated mesh => never\nfires). integer, private, parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 Triangles only. Subroutines public pure subroutine si_unstr_advect_tracer_dsig (mesh, nz, nct, nco, n_bc, dsig, h_layer, mass_flux_edge, tr_bc_ext, hTr_old, hTr, dt) Depth-proportional, race-free, first-order-upwind tracer advection\nfor the sigma SI path — the structured si_ml_advect_tracer_dsig ,\nedge-wise (cell-centric double-visit).  The per-layer edge flux is\nEXACTLY dsig_k * mass_flux_e * len_e * T_upwind — the only split\nconsistent with the dsig-slaved thickness update, so a uniform\ntracer stays uniform PER LAYER to CG tolerance and total tracer is\nconserved to round-off (interior edge fluxes are bit-exactly\nantisymmetric between the two visits; dead edges carry 0). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. integer, intent(in) :: n_bc BC group table size. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig (nz) Sigma layer fractions. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,nct) PRE-update layer thicknesses (time n) — upwind T denominators. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Blended column edge flux [m&#94;2/s], + outward. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_bc_ext (n_bc) Per-group external tracer value for Dirichlet inflow. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hTr_old (nz,nct) Pre-step tracer snapshot (upwind source; never written here). real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr (nz,nct) Tracer field updated in place (each cell writes only itself). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine si_unstr_apply_wind_top_layer (nz, nct, nco, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, wind_tau_x, wind_tau_y, dt) Surface wind stress into the TOP layer (k = nz) transport:\ndt*tau/RHO_WATER — the explicit forcing that rides the pure-u&#94;n\npredictor into G_k (by linearity R_k / Hhat / the Helmholtz\noperator are untouched; zero wind => bit-identical).  The\nunstructured wind is the uniform scalar pair on the barotropic\nstate ( wind_tau_x/y ), so this is a trivially cheap kernel.\nGated on a wet surface layer. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_tau_x Uniform surface wind stress [Pa]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_tau_y Uniform surface wind stress [Pa]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine si_unstr_build_nu_interface (nz, nzp1, nct, nco, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, rho_layer, rho_0, nu_max, nu_bg, ri_alpha, nu_iface) PP81 Richardson-number interface viscosity, per cell (mirror of the\nstructured si_build_nu_interface , (nz, ncells) order):\n  nu_iface(1, c)      = 0   (bed interface)\n  nu_iface(k+1, c)    = nu between layers k and k+1\n  nu_iface(nz+1, c)   = 0   (surface interface)\nRi = g (drho/rho_0) h_avg / |du|&#94;2 (floored at 0);\nnu = nu_max/(1 + ri_alpha*Ri)&#94;2 + nu_bg; vanished layers decouple. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nzp1 nz + 1 (the interface-array leading dim, explicit-shape). integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,nct) Layer thicknesses [m], bottom-up (k=1 bed). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (nz,nct) Layer x-transports [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (nz,nct) Layer y-transports [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer (nz,nct) Layer densities [kg/m&#94;3]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 Reference density [kg/m&#94;3]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: nu_max Maximum (convective) eddy viscosity [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: nu_bg Background viscosity floor [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: ri_alpha Richardson tuning coefficient (PP81: 5.0). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: nu_iface (nzp1,nct) Interface viscosity [m&#94;2/s], vdiff convention. public pure subroutine si_unstr_column_solve (nz, nzp1, nct, nco, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, nu_iface, manning_n, dt, g_col_u, g_col_v, r_col, Hhat_cell, Gbar_cell_x, Gbar_cell_y) Per-column semi-implicit solve — the structured si_column_solve ported per-cell ( (nz, ncells) order).  Predictor: PLAIN old-time\nvelocity u&#94;n_k = hu_k/max(h_k, H_VANISHED) — NO surface PGF (the\nedge-based PGF split: by linearity of the tridiagonal, all surface\nPGF applies at edges via the -1 response R_k).  Bottom drag:\nManning quadratic on the bed row (the unstructured barotropic\nstate carries no linear-drag knob):\n  cf = g n&#94;2 / H_total&#94;{1/3};  lambda = cf |u_bed| / h_1\nfolded into the bed diagonal as +dt*lambda.  Tridiagonal, Thomas\nfactorisation, three back-solves (u&#94;n, v&#94;n, -1), then\n  Gbar = sum_k h_k G_k,  Hhat = -sum_k h_k R_k  (>= 0).\nR_k is axis-independent (u and v share the matrix). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nzp1 nz + 1 (the interface-array leading dim, explicit-shape). integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,nct) Layer thicknesses [m], bottom-up. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (nz,nct) Layer x-transports [m&#94;2/s] (predictor tendencies already folded). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (nz,nct) Layer y-transports [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: nu_iface (nzp1,nct) Interface viscosity [m&#94;2/s] (vdiff convention). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: manning_n Manning roughness n [s/m&#94;{1/3}]; <= 0 disables bottom drag. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Time step [s]. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: g_col_u (nz,nct) Column velocity response to u&#94;n (G_k&#94;u) [m/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: g_col_v (nz,nct) Column velocity response to v&#94;n (G_k&#94;v) [m/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: r_col (nz,nct) Column velocity response to -1 (R_k) [m/s] (<= 0). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: Hhat_cell (nct) Effective column depth Hhat = -sum_k h_k R_k [m] (>= 0). real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: Gbar_cell_x (nct) Column-integrated predictor transport sum_k h_k G_k&#94;u [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: Gbar_cell_y (nct) Column-integrated y predictor transport [m&#94;2/s]. public pure subroutine si_unstr_edge_layers_to_cells (mesh, nz, nct, nco, u_edge_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer) Per-layer least-squares A-grid cell-momentum reconstruction from\nthe three per-layer edge-normal transports — the 2D si_unstr_reconstruct_cell_momenta , per layer (the documented\nreconstruction compromise; restart round-trips through the cell\nlayer momenta). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_edge_layer (nz,EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu_layer (nz,nct) Cell layer momenta [m&#94;2/s]; owned cells overwritten. real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv_layer (nz,nct) Cell layer momenta [m&#94;2/s]; owned cells overwritten. public pure subroutine si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges (nz, nct, nco, u_edge_layer, u_n_edge, Hf_edge, theta, mass_flux_edge, u_edge) The blended column edge flux the eta update used:\n  F_e = theta sum_k u_edge_layer_k + (1-theta) U&#94;n_e\n(gated Hf > 0; dead edges exactly 0) — feeds the dsig tracer split\nso continuity and tracers share edge fluxes exactly.  Also stores\nthe NEW column-total edge transport U&#94;{n+1}_e = sum_k u_edge_layer\ninto u_edge (the 2D prognostic the next step’s (1-theta) side\nreads — the telescoped 2D back-substitution). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_edge_layer (nz,EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_n_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Saved U&#94;n edge transports (dead edges already zeroed, R3). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: mass_flux_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Blended column edge flux [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: u_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) New column-total edge transport [m&#94;2/s]. public pure subroutine si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges (mesh, nz, nct, nco, Gbar_cell_x, Gbar_cell_y, hu_layer0, hv_layer0, u_n_edge, eta, Hf_edge, eta_ghost_edge, u_star, g_omtheta_dt) EDGE predictor for the theta-blend RHS — ANCHOR + INCREMENT form: Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Gbar_cell_x (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Gbar_cell_y (nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer0 (nz,nct) PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the X0 columns). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer0 (nz,nct) PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the X0 columns). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: u_n_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Persisted U&#94;n edge transports (dead edges zeroed). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta (nct) eta&#94;n at circumcentres. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_ghost_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: u_star (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_omtheta_dt g (1-theta) dt. public pure subroutine si_unstr_recover_edge_layers (mesh, nz, nct, nco, h_layer, hu_layer0, hv_layer0, dsig, bed, g_col_u, g_col_v, r_col, eta_n, eta_np1, Hf_edge, eta_ghost_edge, dt, theta, u_edge_layer) Recover the per-layer EDGE transports after the eta solve — the\nstructured si_recover_face_transports in the ANCHOR + INCREMENT\nform matching si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges .  Per edge i of cell\nc (gated Hf > 0; dead edges stay exactly 0) and layer k: Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of layers. integer, intent(in) :: nct Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer, intent(in) :: nco Owned-cell loop bound. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,nct) Layer thicknesses [m] at time n (the tridiagonal’s field). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer0 (nz,nct) PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the increment reference). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer0 (nz,nct) PRE-tendency saved layer transports (the increment reference). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig (nz) Sigma layer fractions (sum = 1). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bed (nct) Bed elevation [m] (the Dirichlet ghost column depth). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_col_u (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: g_col_v (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r_col (nz,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_n (nct) Old-time surface eta&#94;n at circumcentres. real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_np1 (nct) New-time surface eta&#94;{n+1} (the CG solution). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Hf_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eta_ghost_edge (EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Seeded Dirichlet ghost surface (frozen over the step — used for\nBOTH the eta&#94;n and eta&#94;{n+1} gradients, as on the structured\npath where the ghost persists across the interior-only CG). real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: theta real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: u_edge_layer (nz,EDGES_PER_TRI,nct) Per-layer edge transports [m&#94;2/s], + outward normal: the\npersisted anchor on entry, the recovered U&#94;{n+1} on exit. public pure subroutine si_unstr_update_thickness_ml (nz, nct, nco, eta, bed, dsig, stage, height, h_layer) h&#94;{n+1} = max(eta&#94;{n+1} - b, 0) (exactly the edge-flux continuity\nupdate) + the sigma slaving h_layer_k = dsig_k*h, and the stage\nrefresh stage = eta. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Number of 