submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: BPG_NZ_MAX = NZ_STACK_MAX Backward-compatible alias for NZ_STACK_MAX. real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: CP_WATER = 4000.0_wp Specific heat capacity of seawater (J/(kg·K)).  Converts surface\nheat flux Q_net [W/m²] to kinematic heat flux Q_net/(rho_0·cp) [m·K/s]. real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: DEG2RAD = PI/180.0_wp Degrees → radians conversion factor. real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: DESING_EPS = H_VANISHED Kurganov & Petrova (2007) desingularization depth eps (m) for\nthe 2D barotropic update/protect kernels AND the CFL timestep\nestimator: the velocity\n    u = sqrt(2) h hu / sqrt(h&#94;4 + max(h&#94;4, eps&#94;4))\nequals hu/h exactly for h >= eps and rolls off quadratically\nbelow, and momentum is reconstructed as hu := h*u.  Momentum in\ncells thinner than eps is smoothly suppressed, NOT zeroed — the\npre-2026-08 hard zero below THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD (together with FROUDE_CAP = 10 , see FROUDE_BACKSTOP) froze thin water at\nwet/dry fronts: Ritter dry-bed tip at 1.49 c0 instead of 2 c0,\nbeach films that never drained.  One value shared by the update\nkernels and the dt estimator, so both agree about what “thin”\nmeans.  (Earlier the estimator alone used eps = max(1e-3, 0.01*min(dx,dy)) ; the grid term is gone — on\ncoarse grids it made the estimator blind to real velocities in\ncells shallower than 1% of the cell width, a latent CFL bug.) Value: tied to H_VANISHED — the codebase’s established\n“dynamically vanished” depth below which a column has no\nmeaningful velocity.  Measured dose-response on the Ritter\ndry-bed tip (dx = 0.25 m, exact celerity 2 c0, no-clamp ceiling\n1.888 c0 at this resolution; design sweep at FROUDE_BACKSTOP=100):\n    eps = 1e-3    -> 1.617 c0\n    eps = 1.5e-4  -> ~1.73 c0   (this value; 1.736 in the final\n                                 backstop=50 configuration)\n    eps = 3e-5    -> 1.776 c0\nDiminishing returns below H_VANISHED, and the front position at\na RESOLVABLE depth (1 cm) is best at 1.5e-4 (lag 0.36 m of\n62.6 m travelled, 0.6%). real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: DRY_TOLERANCE = 1.0e-6_wp Minimum depth to consider a cell wet (m) real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: FROUDE_BACKSTOP = 50.0_wp Last-resort Froude bound at wet/dry fronts: momentum is rescaled\nso |u| <= FROUDE_BACKSTOP sqrt(g h).  This is a blowup ARRESTER,\nnot physics shaping — it replaced FROUDE_CAP = 10 (2026-08),\nwhich bound exactly where the physics lives: the exact Ritter\ndry-bed tongue has Fr = 2(sqrt(h_l/h) - 1), unbounded at the tip,\nand the leading wet cell measured at exactly Fr = 10 (tip\ncelerity 1.49 c0 instead of 2 c0).  A Fr-shaped cap that binds a\ndraining film also freezes it structurally: saturated cells obey\nhu = Fr sqrt(g) h&#94;1.5, so a uniform film has zero flux divergence\nand dh/dt = 0 (measured: ~40 consecutive beach cells all at\nu = -10*sqrt(g h), shoreline pinned). Why it exists at all: without it, a thin draining film on a\nsloping bed develops a genuine velocity runaway ABOVE the\ndesingularization depth, where KP07 is an identity — measured\nu -> 4e3 m/s at h ~ 3.5e-3 m and a ~2000x CFL dt collapse on the\nCarrier-Greenspan beach fixture. Why 50 (all measured at DESING_EPS = 1.5e-4, dx = 0.25 m; the\n200 row is from the design sweep, where it matched 100 exactly):\n    backstop =  50 -> Ritter tip 1.736 c0, beach max|u| ~10.6 m/s\n    backstop = 100 -> Ritter tip 1.744 c0, beach max|u| ~17.8 m/s\n    backstop = 200 -> Ritter tip = the 100 value, max|u| ~31.5 m/s\nThe dry-front tongue is insensitive to the value (the KP07\ndesingularization governs it), but the Carrier-Greenspan runup\nDISCRIMINATES: at backstop 100 the freed runup jet overshoots and\nstrands a cm-scale wedge on the beach through rundown (excursion\nat a 1 cm detector 11.8 m vs exact 20 m); at 50 the excursion is\n18.9 m (5.6% of exact) with the rundown edge at x = 83.9 m vs the\nexact 80 m.  50 is also the lowest measured value that leaves the\nRitter tongue unchanged; going much lower re-approaches the\nmeasured cap-10 film-freeze pathology (Fr-shaped caps bind at\ndrainage velocities once Fr*sqrt(g h) ~ a few m/s at cm depths).\nNaN safety: the rescale triggers only on a TRUE comparison, so a\nNaN speed passes through un-“corrected” and fails loudly instead\nof being laundered into a plausible extreme value (see CLAUDE.md\non NaN-blind clamps). real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: GRAVITY = 9.80665_wp Gravitational acceleration (m/s&#94;2) real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: H_DIV_EPS = 1.0e-20_wp Pure division-safety epsilon (m), far below any physical thickness:\nadding it ( 1/(h+H_DIV_EPS) ) only prevents a 1/0, never changes a\nwell-posed result.  Use where a divisor is ALREADY guaranteed\npositive (MOM6 H_subroundoff role). real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: H_VANISHED = 1.5e-4_wp Dynamic-vanish threshold (m).  A layer thinner than this is\ndynamically VANISHED — skip / merge into a neighbour, do NOT clamp.\nWhen dividing by h_layer for a PHYSICAL result, gate on this.\nSame value/role as coastal VANISHING_LAYER_TOL (_UNSTR). integer, public, parameter :: KEPS_STAB_CANUTO = 2 Canuto et al. (2001) Model A second-moment-closure stability functions\n(rational alpha_M / alpha_N form per Umlauf & Burchard 2003). integer, public, parameter :: KEPS_STAB_CONSTANT = 0 Constant c_mu (=0.09) / Pr_t (=1) – standard high-Re k-epsilon\n(default; bit-identical to the original closure). integer, public, parameter :: KEPS_STAB_GALPERIN = 1 Galperin et al. (1988) quasi-equilibrium stratification-aware\nstability functions (Mellor-Yamada level-2.5 algebraic form). real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: LAND_DEPTH_THRESHOLD = 2.0_wp Cell bathymetry depth (m, positive-down) below which an ocean cell\nis treated as LAND for surface-forcing masking.  Consumed by ocean_state_seed_from_cfg to populate multilayer%wet_mask . real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: LATENT_HEAT_VAPORIZATION = 2.5e6_wp Latent heat of vaporization of water (J/kg).  A representative\nnear-surface value (2.501e6 at 0 °C, weakly T-dependent).  Used by\nthe evaporative latent-heat surface cooling: a net evaporation of\nE [m/s] withdraws a heat flux ρ_water·E·L_v [W/m²] from the top of\nthe water column as the evaporated mass changes phase. real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: NH_MIN_DEPTH = 1.0e-1_wp Minimum depth for non-hydrostatic pressure operations (m).\nCells shallower than this are treated as hydrostatic to avoid\n1/h singularities in the NH Poisson operator. integer, public, parameter :: NZ_STACK_MAX = 128 Maximum vertical layers for per-column stack workspace inside do concurrent .  Stack arrays in the BPG, remap, kappa-shear,\nRedi and diag-remap kernels are dimensioned by this constant so\nthe compiler can emit fixed-size thread-local storage on GPU. The requirement is NZ_STACK_MAX >= nz + 1 — see nz_stack_required below for the derivation and the survey of\nevery consumer.  Enforced fail-loud by validate_config . History: 100 -> 256 (2026-06-19), on the belief that the Redi\nneutral-diffusion sweep needed 2*nz+2 of this constant .  It\ndoes not: Redi’s nsurf locals are declared 2*NZ_STACK_MAX+2 ( rki_ocean_redi.F90 PoLc / PoRc / KoLc / KoRc / hEc ), so they\nscale with the constant and only need NZ_STACK_MAX >= nz .\nLowered 256 -> 128 (2026-08-05) after that measurement: 256 was\n~2x larger than any consumer needed and cost ~4 GB of CUDA\nper-thread local memory, which the driver reserves at each\nkernel’s first launch and never returns.  128 covers the largest\nshipped case (nz=90, acc_channel_kitchensink_xl.nml ) and the\nlargest test (nz=100) with headroom. Heap-allocated workspace arrays (PPM snapshots, remap snapshots)\nhave no such limit — they are allocated at runtime. real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: OMEGA_EARTH = 7.2921e-5_wp Earth angular velocity (rad/s) real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: PI = 4.0_wp*atan(1.0_wp) Pi real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: RAD2DEG = 180.0_wp/PI Radians → degrees conversion factor. integer, public, parameter :: REMAP_PCM = 1 Piecewise constant (0th order, donor cell) integer, public, parameter :: REMAP_PLM = 2 Piecewise linear with minmod limiter (1st order) integer, public, parameter :: REMAP_PPM = 3 Piecewise parabolic (2nd order, Colella & Woodward) integer, public, parameter :: REMAP_PPM_H4 = 4 Piecewise parabolic with non-uniform 4th-order (H4) edge values —\nthickness-weighted edge estimate (White & Adcroft 2008) feeding the\nsame Colella & Woodward parabola + monotonicity limiter as REMAP_PPM integer, public, parameter :: REMAP_PQM = 5 Piecewise quartic (4th-order, PQM_IH4IH3 — White & Adcroft 2008):\nimplicit-h4 edge values + implicit-h3 edge slopes + a quartic per-cell\nreconstruction with the White & Adcroft monotonicity limiter and a\nconservative quartic overlap integral.  Requires nz >= 5; falls back to\nREMAP_PPM for thinner columns.  Boundary cells are PCM. real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: RHO_WATER = 1035.0_wp Seawater density (kg/m&#94;3) real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD = 1.0e-3_wp Thin-LAYER depth scale (m) for the MULTILAYER per-layer\nstabilisers (skip/zero thresholds in friction, horizontal\nviscosity, tracer diffusion, layer distribute/truncate).  The 2D\nbarotropic update/protect kernels no longer hard-zero momentum at\nthis depth — they desingularize at DESING_EPS instead (the old\nhard zero froze wet/dry fronts; see DESING_EPS ). real(kind=wp), public, parameter :: TWO_PI = 8.0_wp*atan(1.0_wp) 2*Pi integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_EULERIAN_Z = 0 Ignore SSH when forming target_h ; layer thicknesses follow\nthe static H · dsig(k) decomposition.  Used by the ocean\npath as the “do nothing, leave the IC layers alone” default\nbefore the user picks a remap-aware coord_type.  Was originally\ndeclared in rki_ocean_vcoord as an orphan; moved here so the\nVCOORD enum lives in one place. integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_HYCOM = 9 Hybrid z /isopycnal coordinate (P3, Bleck 2002 / MOM6 coord_hycom ).  Runs the exact VCOORD_RHO density-space\ninversion (same ocean_vcoord_compute_target_h_rho kernel, hybrid=.true. ) but adds two HYCOM deltas around it: a\nbottom-up density monotonize before the inversion, and a z nominal-floor sweep after it that pushes too-shallow interfaces\ndown to a fixed-resolution surface band ( dsig·(H+η) ).  Net\neffect: a fixed-res near-surface z* band (no surface collapse)\nwith an isopycnal interior — the production GVC coordinate.\nReuses rho_target / rho_ref_pressure ; no new knobs. integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_LAGRANGIAN = -1 Pure Lagrangian / isopycnal — h_layer evolves freely and is\nnever remapped. compute_target_h returns the current h unchanged and the ALE remap step is a no-op.  Distinct from VCOORD_EULERIAN_Z (which targets the static H · dsig decomposition): LAGRANGIAN tracks material surfaces, so for\nadiabatic flow it reproduces MOM6’s COORD_CONFIG=\"gprime\" NK=2 isopycnal layering.  Parsed from “lagrangian” / “isopycnal”. integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_RHO = 8 Isopycnal coordinate (P2).  Layer interfaces are placed on\nprescribed potential-density surfaces rho_target(0:nz) (monotone-increasing, referenced to rho_ref_pressure ).  The\nALE regrid inverts a PPM reconstruction of the column density\nprofile for the depth where ρ equals each interior target, then\nremaps T/S/tracers/velocities onto the new grid.  Bottom-up\nconvention: rho_target(0) (lightest) anchors the surface\ninterface (k=nz); rho_target(nz) (densest) the bed (k=1).\nValidation-grade alone (weakly-stratified columns collapse);\nHYCOM hybrid is the production follow-on (P3).  See rki_ocean_vcoord :: ocean_vcoord_compute_target_h_rho_impl . integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_SIGMA = 1 Pure terrain-following sigma coordinate (default) integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_ZSIGMA = 2 z-sigma hybrid: z-levels in deep/steep, sigma in shallow integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_ZSTAR = 4 z-star “lite” (MOM6-like quasi-horizontal): single global z_ref pattern stretched proportionally per column by H/z_ref(nz) integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL = 5 z-star “full” MOM6: per-column z_ref anchored to local\nbathymetry with vanishing layers below the bed.  Surface\nlayers stay at a fixed physical thickness independent of H integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_ZSTAR_SIGMA = 6 z /sigma hybrid: smoothstep blend from pure sigma in shallow\nwater (H ≤ depth_transition) to z -lite in deep water\n(H ≥ depth_transition + blend_width).  Coastal wet/dry\nfriendliness in shallow zones, SSH-tracking in deep zones integer, public, parameter :: VCOORD_Z_FIXED = 7 Fixed-z interfaces with vanishing layers in shallow water.\nALE remap pulls h_layer(k) → h_target(k) where the targets\ncome from absolute-depth interfaces z_target = (0, h_nominal,\n2·h_nominal, ..., h_ref) with h_nominal = h_ref/nz_ml .\nIn deep cells the interfaces stay locked at those depths; in\nshallow cells the bed-side layers vanish to a minimum\nthickness h_min while the surface layer absorbs the residual.\nMirrors MOM6’s COORD_CONFIG = \"gprime\" layer structure and\nthe existing seed_h_layer_z_fixed_impl IC algorithm — used\nas a per-step ALE target rather than an init-only seed so the\ninterface stays anchored as the simulation evolves. integer, public, parameter :: wp = sp Working precision kind parameter (single) Functions public pure function nz_stack_is_sufficient (nz) result(ok) .true. when the COMPILED NZ_STACK_MAX covers nz layers.\nCallers that get .false. must refuse the run — the overflow is\na silent thread-local-storage overrun, not a crash. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Return Value logical public pure function nz_stack_required (nz) result(req) Smallest NZ_STACK_MAX that safely covers a run of nz layers. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz Return Value integer","tags":"","url":"module/rki_constants.html"},{"title":"rki_restart_unstr – Rakali","text":"Writes and reads checkpoint files for the unstructured solver.\nStores (stage_cv, xmom_cv, ymom_cv, bed_cv) for owned cells,\nplus simulation time and step count as global attributes. File format: NetCDF-4 with one dimension face = ncells_owned .\nCell global ids stored if available. Uses pic_logger netcdf rki_mesh_unstr rki_constants pic_strings rki_io_netcdf rki_state_unstr module~~rki_restart_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_restart_unstr rki_restart_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_restart_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_io_netcdf rki_io_netcdf module~rki_restart_unstr->module~rki_io_netcdf module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_restart_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_state_unstr rki_state_unstr module~rki_restart_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr netcdf netcdf module~rki_restart_unstr->netcdf pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_restart_unstr->pic_logger pic_strings pic_strings module~rki_restart_unstr->pic_strings pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_io_netcdf->module~rki_constants module~rki_io_netcdf->netcdf module~rki_io_netcdf->pic_logger iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~rki_io_netcdf->iso_fortran_env module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_logger pic_io pic_io module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_io module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_types module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr rki_barotropic_state_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr module~rki_boundary_unstr rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr modu