l surface freshwater flux (m/s), positive for net\nevaporation.  Applied as a virtual salt flux on the top\nlayer: hS(1) += dt * (E-P) * S_top.  Does not change h_layer. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: heat_flux (:,:) Net surface heat flux (W/m&#94;2), positive into ocean.\nApplied to top layer hT only; does not change h_layer. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: precipitation (:,:) Precipitation rate (m/s), adds volume to barotropic h real(kind=wp), public :: wind_stress_x = 0.0_wp real(kind=wp), public :: wind_stress_y = 0.0_wp real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: wind_x (:,:) Surface wind stress in x-direction (Pa) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: wind_y (:,:) Surface wind stress in y-direction (Pa) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: bytes => surface_forcing_bytes procedure, public, non_overridable :: destroy => surface_forcing_destroy procedure, public, non_overridable :: init => surface_forcing_init Functions private pure function surface_forcing_bytes (this) result(nbytes) Counted allocatable footprint of the surface-forcing slot. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( surface_forcing_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=int64) Subroutines private  subroutine surface_forcing_destroy (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( surface_forcing_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine surface_forcing_init (this, grid) Allocate the surface-forcing arrays sized to the grid, zero-filled.\nUniform fallbacks (wind_stress_x/y) are set by the caller from config. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( surface_forcing_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid","tags":"","url":"module/rki_surface_forcing.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_common – Rakali","text":"State and helpers shared by every multilayer sub-module (dynamics,\ntracers, pressure, EOS, momentum). Uses rki_constants module~~rki_ml_common~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_common rki_ml_common module~rki