 ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_pressure_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_surface_forcing_unstr – Rakali","text":"Container for the spatially-varying surface forcing fields applied\nby the unstructured multilayer pipeline.  Currently only the two\ntracer-side forcings are supported: heat_flux net surface heat flux (W/m&#94;2, positive into\n                      ocean) applied to the top layer’s hT field\n                      via hT(1,c) += dt * Q / (rho_0 * cp) . evap_minus_precip virtual surface freshwater flux (m/s, positive\n                      for net evaporation) applied as a virtual\n                      salt flux on the top layer: hS(1,c) += dt * (E-P) * S_top .\n                      Does not change h_layer – pure tracer\n                      forcing in the ROMS / MOM convention. wind_x / wind_y per-cell surface wind STRESS (Pa) added to the\n                      barotropic momentum in the fused update kernel: hu += dt * wind_x / RHO_WATER , on top of the\n                      spatially-uniform barotropic%wind_tau_* .\n                      Pushed per owned cell via rki_unstr_set_wind_field . Atmospheric pressure / precipitation will be added when those ports\nland; this container will gain them to mirror surface_forcing_t . Uses rki_mesh_unstr rki_constants module~~rki_surface_forcing_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants pic_io pic_io module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_io pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Subm