es\nusing a SHEAR-AWARE consistency-with-continuity (CWC) per-layer\nmass flux. Mirrors what the structured ml_advect_tracer does\nwith its 0.5*(hu_layer left + right) face flux, but reshaped\nfor the cell-centric triangle pattern. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: bc_tr_ext (MAX_BC_GROUPS) External tracer concentration for each boundary group.\nUsed for inflow BCs. If not provided, inflow boundaries\nuse zero tracer concentration. public pure subroutine ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes_unstr (state, hS_layer, hT_layer) Apply prescribed surface fluxes to the top layer (k=nz) of every\ncell.  Two evaporation modes, mirroring the structured ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes : Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hS_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hT_layer (:,:) public  subroutine ml_apply_tracer_bcs_unstr (state, mesh, hTr_layer, bc_tr_ext) Apply tracer boundary conditions for inflow edges. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bc_tr_ext (MAX_BC_GROUPS) public  subroutine ml_clamp_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer, tr_min, tr_max) Enforce physical tracer bounds [tr_min, tr_max] conservatively\nwithin each column.  Two-pass column-conservative limiter\n(mirror of the structured ml_clamp_tracer ): Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout), contiguous :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_min real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_max public pure subroutine ml_distribute_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer) Preserve tracer concentration across a barotropic depth change. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) public  subroutine ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer_unstr (state, mesh, hTr_layer, kappa, dt) Horizontal Laplacian diffusion of a scalar tracer on triangles\nin flux form, conservative per-edge under non-uniform layer\nthicknesses. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(inout), contiguous :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine ml_init_tracer_stratified_unstr (state, hTr_layer, tr_bottom, tr_surface) Seed a tracer with a linear vertical profile: tr_bottom at k=1\n(bed) to tr_surface at k=nz (surface), per the bottom-up layer\nconvention.  The per-column entry point anticipated by ml_init_tracer_unstr .  The profile is computed inline from the\ntwo scalars (no host-side per-layer array) so the seed runs\ncorrectly on the device after enter_data .  Caller guarantees\nnz > 1.\n  hTr_k(cell) = h_layer_k(cell) * [tr_bottom + dtr*(k - 1)] Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_bottom real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_surface public pure subroutine ml_init_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer, tr_init) Initialise a tracer field from a uniform scalar value:\n  hTr_k(cell) = h_layer_k(cell) * tr_init\nCalled once per tracer after ml_init_layers_unstr has\npopulated h_layer . Future phases will accept per-column\nprofiles via a separate entry point. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_init public pure subroutine ml_rk2_average_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer, hTr_layer0) RK2 blend for tracer fields: hTr := 0.5*(hTr + hTr&#94;n). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hTr_layer0 (:,:) public pure subroutine ml_save_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer, hTr_layer0) Snapshot a tracer field at step start for SSP-RK2 averaging. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer0 (:,:) public pure subroutine ml_seed_standard_tracers_unstr (state) Seed the two standard tracers (salinity, temperature) from the IC\nscalars carried on state%multilayer , each dispatching uniform-vs-\nstratified via ml_seed_tracer_unstr .  Call once after ml_init_layers_unstr and before EOS.  The unstructured twin of the\nstructured multilayer_state_t%seed_tracers ; a free helper (not a\ntype-bound method) because the unstructured tracer kernels take the\ntop-level unstr_state_t , so binding on the state would close a state <-> tracers_unstr module cycle. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public pure subroutine ml_seed_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer, tr_uniform, tr_bottom, tr_surface) Seed one tracer’s hTr field, dispatching between the uniform and\nthe linear-stratified profile from the tracer’s IC scalars.  When\nboth tr_bottom and tr_surface are set (non-zero) and nz > 1 a\nlinear profile is laid down from tr_bottom at the bed (k=1) to tr_surface at the surface (k=nz); otherwise every layer is filled\nwith tr_uniform .  The single stratified-vs-uniform gate shared by\nthe unstructured IC seed site (solver_unstr_init_multilayer).\nMirrors the structured ml_seed_tracer . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_uniform real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_bottom real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_surface public pure subroutine ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer, kappa_bg, dt) Ri-dependent vertical diffusion of a scalar tracer.\nUses stronger Ri suppression for tracers:\n  kappa_t = nu_max / (1 + alpha*Ri)&#94;3 + kappa_bg. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout), contiguous :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_bg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public  subroutine ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer, dt) Vertical tracer exchange using upwind advection at interfaces. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout), contiguous :: hTr_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt private pure subroutine advect_tracer_one_cell (state, mesh, hTr_layer, nz, dt, cell, bc_tr_ext) Per-cell body, marked pure to document the “this cell only”\nwrite pattern that makes the enclosing do concurrent safe. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (:,:) integer, intent(in) :: nz real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt integer, intent(in) :: cell real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bc_tr_ext (MAX_BC_GROUPS) External tracer for each boundary group private pure subroutine ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr_impl (nz, n, ncells_owned, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, dsig_ml, tracer_advect_scratch, lgrad_x, lgrad_y, mass_flux_e, area, neighbours, surrogate_neighbours, edge_n1, edge_n2, edge_len, edge_mid_x, edge_mid_y, centroid_x, centroid_y, bc_group, hTr_layer, dt, bc_ext_local) Flat-impl of ml_advect_tracer_muscl_unstr : explicit-shape dummies\nso the device kernels see contiguous raw pointers, not derived-type\ndescriptors (descriptor access inflates per-thread registers and caps\noccupancy).  Body is identical to the historical kernel modulo the\nstripped state% / mesh% prefixes and the removed associate . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n integer, intent(in) :: ncells_owned real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dsig_ml (nz) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: tracer_advect_scratch (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: lgrad_x (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: lgrad_y (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: mass_flux_e (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: area (n) integer, intent(in) :: neighbours (3,n) integer, intent(in) :: surrogate_neighbours (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_n1 (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_n2 (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_len (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_mid_x (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_mid_y (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: centroid_x (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: centroid_y (n) integer, intent(in) :: bc_group (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: bc_ext_local (MAX_BC_GROUPS) private pure subroutine ml_clamp_tracer_unstr_impl (nz, n, h_layer, hTr_layer, tr_min, tr_max) Flat-impl of ml_clamp_tracer_unstr : explicit-shape dummies so the\ndevice kernel addresses raw pointers, not derived-type descriptors. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_min real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_max private pure subroutine ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer_unstr_impl (nz, n, ncells_owned, height_cv, h_layer, hTr_pre, area, radius, centroid_x, centroid_y, edge_len, surrogate_neighbours, hTr_layer, kappa, dt) Flat-impl of ml_horizontal_diffusion_tracer_unstr : explicit-shape\ndummies so the device kernels address raw pointers, not derived-type\ndescriptors. hTr_pre is the persistent Jacobi-snapshot workspace. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n integer, intent(in) :: ncells_owned real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: height_cv (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_pre (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: area (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: radius (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: centroid_x (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: centroid_y (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: edge_len (3,n) integer, intent(in) :: surrogate_neighbours (3,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt private pure subroutine ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr_impl (nz, n, ncells_owned, height_cv, h_layer, hu_layer, hv_layer, rho_layer, rho_0, vmix_ri_alpha, vmix_nu_max, hTr_layer, kappa_bg, dt) Flat-impl of ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr : explicit-shape\ndummies so the device kernel addresses raw pointers, not derived-type\ndescriptors.  Column-local; no neighbour access. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n integer, intent(in) :: ncells_owned real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: height_cv (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hu_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hv_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rho_0 real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: vmix_ri_alpha real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: vmix_nu_max real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_bg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt private pure subroutine ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr_impl (nz, n, ncells_owned, height_cv, h_layer, w_interface, hTr_layer, dt) Flat-impl of ml_vertical_exchange_tracer_unstr : explicit-shape dummies\nso the device kernel addresses raw pointers, not derived-type descriptors. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: nz integer, intent(in) :: n integer, intent(in) :: ncells_owned real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: height_cv (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: w_interface (nz+1,n) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (nz,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_tracers_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_dynamics_unstr – Rakali","text":"Continuity-side machinery: layer initialisation from the barotropic\nstate, distribute / distribute-with-remap (sigma + zsigma ALE),\nbarotropic recompute from layer momenta, save / RK2-average for\nlayer fields, diagnostic vertical velocity, vertical exchange of\nmomentum. Layer index convention : k = 1 is the BOTTOM sigma layer, k = nz_ml is the TOP / surface layer. w_interface is indexed 1..nz+1 with w_interface(1) = 0 at the bed and w_interface(nz+1) at the free surface. Uses rki_remap_column rki_mesh_unstr rki_vcoord rki_constants rki_ml_common_unstr rki_state_unstr module~~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr rki_ml_dynamics_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_ml_common_unstr rki_ml_common_unstr module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr->module~rki_ml_common_unstr module~rki_remap_column rki_remap_column module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr->module~rki_remap_column module~rki_state_unstr rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_vcoord rki_vcoord module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr->module~rki_vcoord pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants pic_io pic_io module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_io pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_types module~rki_ml_common_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_remap_column->module~rki_constants module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr rki_barotropic_state_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr module~rki_boundary_unstr rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr rki_multilayer_state_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr module~rki_si_common rki_si_common module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_si_common module~rki_si_unstr_state rki_si_unstr_state module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_state module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_timestepper rki_timestepper module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_timestepper module~rki_state_unstr->pic_io module~rki_state_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_vcoord->module~rki_constants module~rki_vcoord->pic_logger pic_strings pic_strings module~rki_vcoord->pic_strings module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_vcoord module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_eos rki_eos module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_eos module~rki_tracer_unstr rki_tracer_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_tracer_unstr module~rki_si_common->pic_logger module~rki_si_unstr_state->module~rki_constants module~rki_si_unstr_state->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_state->pic_logger module~rki_si_unstr_mg rki_si_unstr_mg module~rki_si_unstr_state->module~rki_si_unstr_mg module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_timestepper->module~rki_constants module~rki_eos->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_eos->module~rki_grid module~rki_si_unstr_mg->module~rki_constants module~rki_si_unstr_mg->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_mg->pic_logger module~rki_tracer_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_tracer_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_tracer_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr~~UsedByGraph module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr rki_ml_dynamics_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr rki_solver_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Subroutines public  subroutine ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full_unstr (state) Fill the per-cell reference z-level array from the bathymetry.\nRuns once at solver init (host-side loop); pushes vcoord_z_ref_col to the device when done. bed_cv is bed\nelevation (negative when submerged); its magnitude is h_bed . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public pure subroutine ml_compute_barotropic_momentum_unstr (state) Depth-integrate layer momentum back onto the barotropic fields:\n  HU = sum_k hu_k,  HV = sum_k hv_k.\nAlso refreshes height_cv = sum_k h_k and stage_cv from the\nupdated height so the 2D barotropic state stays in sync with\nthe layers. Called between RK stages and at the end of the\nstep after the layer RK2 average. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public pure subroutine ml_compute_total_depth_unstr (state) Public only for the unit-test suite (no production module imports it);\nignore when developing production code in other modules.\nRefresh height_cv = sum_k h_k without touching momentum.\nUseful when only the layer thicknesses have changed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public pure subroutine ml_compute_vertical_velocity_unstr (state, mesh) Compute diagnostic vertical velocity from horizontal divergence. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh public pure subroutine ml_distribute_barotropic_unstr (state) Distribute the barotropic HLL acceleration across layers (sigma):\n  du = (hu_new - hu_pre)/H_new; u_k_old = hu_k_old/h_k_old;\n  h_k = dsig_k H_new; hu_k = h_k (u_k_old + du)\nso the acceleration lands uniformly while preserving shear.\nRequires xmom_pre / ymom_pre from ml_save_barotropic_pre_unstr . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public  subroutine ml_distribute_with_remap_full_unstr (state) VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL variant of ml_distribute_with_remap_unstr (momentum + thickness only).  Builds the per-cell target dz_new\nvia vcoord_target_dz_column_zstar_full from the cell’s local vcoord_z_ref_col(:, cell) slice.  Per-tracer remap is done by\nml_remap_tracer_unstr (looped over the registry by the solver),\nwhich is vcoord-agnostic — it reads the new h_layer this routine\nwrites.  Shares the remap_dz_old workspace with the sigma path. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public  subroutine ml_distribute_with_remap_unstr (state) Barotropic-to-layer distribution with vcoord reshaping for\nnon-sigma coords (z-sigma hybrid, zstar-lite) — momentum +\nthickness only:\n1. Save old thicknesses into remap_dz_old (read by\n   ml_remap_tracer_unstr for the per-tracer remap).\n2. Compute new target thicknesses via vcoord, write h_layer.\n3. Distribute the barotropic acceleration to the new layers.\nPer-tracer remap is done by ml_remap_tracer_unstr (looped over\nthe registry by the solver); touches only top-level allocatables\nso no outer shim needed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public  subroutine ml_init_layers_unstr (state) Fill the per-layer arrays from the barotropic state. Pure sigma:\n  h_k = dsig_k H, hu_k = dsig_k HU, hv_k = dsig_k*HV.\nFor zsigma / hybrid coords vcoord_target_dz_column lays out the\nper-column thicknesses (matching distribute_with_remap), so the\nfirst step’s tracer RK2 average stays geometrically coherent. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public  subroutine ml_remap_tracer_unstr (state, hTr_layer) Conservatively remap ONE tracer from the saved pre-update layer\nthicknesses (state%multilayer%remap_dz_old, written by the\ndistribute-with-remap routines) onto the current h_layer (the new\nvcoord target).  Vcoord-agnostic: shared by the sigma / zsigma /\nzstar-lite and the ZSTAR_FULL paths, since both write the new\ntarget into h_layer before this runs.  Split out of the fused\nremap so the solver can loop it over the whole tracer registry;\nthe per-tracer arithmetic is exactly what the fused impls used\nfor S/T (scale dz_old to sum to H_new, depth-weighted column-mean\nfallback at vanishing layers, conservative remap_column), so\nsalinity / temperature results are unchanged. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hTr_layer (state%multilayer%nz_ml,state%ncells_total) public pure subroutine ml_rk2_average_layers_unstr (state) Public only for the unit-test suite (no production module imports it);\nignore when developing production code in other modules.\nFinal RK2 blend:  Q := 0.5 * Q + 0.5 * Q&#94;n\nThe barotropic blend is done in fused_update_stage2_unstr ;\nthis routine handles the layer fields. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public pure subroutine ml_save_barotropic_pre_unstr (state) Snapshot the barotropic momentum before the HLL update so the\ndistribute kernel can compute the acceleration increment du = (hu_new - hu_pre) / H_new at cell level. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public pure subroutine ml_save_layer_state_unstr (state) Snapshot the layer state at the start of the step for the\nSSP-RK2 average. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state public pure subroutine ml_vertical_exchange_unstr (state, dt) Vertical momentum exchange using upwind advection at interfaces. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_dynamics_unstr.html