easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_ml_kpp_unstr~~UsedByGraph module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr rki_ml_kpp_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr rki_solver_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: EPS = 1.0e-20_wp Shear² floor in the interior gradient-Ri (matches PP81 kernels). real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: SHEAR2_FLOOR = 1.0e-10_wp Velocity-difference floor in the bulk-Ri denominator (matches\nthe structured KPP); stops Ri_bulk blowing up in quiescent water. Subroutines public pure subroutine ml_kpp_boundary_layer_unstr (state, hS_layer) Pass 1: per-cell u_ , B_0, and the bulk-Ri boundary-layer depth.\nMirrors ml_kpp_boundary_layer (structured) on the cell-centric\nlayout.  u_ uses the uniform barotropic wind stress; B_0 uses\nthe per-cell surface heat / virtual-salt fluxes. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hS_layer (:,:) public pure subroutine ml_kpp_diffusion_tracers_unstr (state, hS_layer, hT_layer, kappa_S_bg, kappa_T_bg, dt) Pass 2 (tracers): PP81 cubic interior diffusivity with the KPP\noverlay max’d in, plus the non-local counter-gradient transport\nfolded into the interface flux, applied two-pass on salinity +\ntemperature.  Fuses the two ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr calls; bit-identical to them where the overlay + non-local\nterms vanish. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hS_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hT_layer (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_S_bg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_T_bg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public pure subroutine ml_kpp_viscosity_unstr (state, dt) Pass 2 (momentum): PP81 interior viscosity with the KPP shape-\nfunction overlay max’d in, then the explicit CFL-clamped\ndiffusive flux applied to hu/hv (two-pass, mirroring ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt","tags":"","url":"module/rki_ml_kpp_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_timestep_unstr – Rakali","text":"Global CFL-limited timestep from the per-cell wave speeds the flux\nkernel writes into state%barotropic%max_speed(k) . Per cell\n  dt_k = mesh%radius(k) / max_speed(k)\nwhere radius(k) is the min centroid-to-edge-midpoint distance\n(ANUGA radii ); global dt = cfl * min_k dt_k . Cells with max_speed below epsilon are skipped. Reduction via !$acc parallel loop reduction(min:..) . Uses rki_mesh_unstr rki_state_unstr rki_constants module~~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr rki_kernel_timestep_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_state_unstr rki_state_unstr module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants pic_io pic_io 