ESTEP_LARGE = huge(1.0_wp) Initial running minimum (effectively infinity); huge fits\neither precision ( 1.0e+100_wp overflows real32 ). real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: TIMESTEP_EPSILON = 1.0e-15_wp Cells with max_speed below this contribute nothing to the\ntimestep reduction (no characteristic to constrain). Subroutines public  subroutine compute_timestep_unstr (state, mesh) Compute the CFL-limited timestep and store it in state%dt .\nReads max_speed , state%cfl , mesh%radius only. Must run\nafter the flux kernel; before any flux pass it returns cfl * TIMESTEP_LARGE (all max_speed still 0). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh","tags":"","url":"module/rki_kernel_timestep_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_fused_unstr – Rakali","text":"Uses rki_mesh_unstr rki_state_unstr rki_constants module~~rki_kernel_fused_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr rki_kernel_fused_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_state_unstr rki_state_unstr module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants pic_io pic_io module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_io pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_mesh_unstr->pic_types module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr rki_barotropic_state_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr module~rki_boundary_unstr rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr rki_multilayer_state_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr module~rki_si_common rki_si_common module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_si_common module~rki_si_unstr_state rki_si_unstr_state module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_state module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_timestepper rki_timestepper module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_timestepper module~rki_state_unstr->pic_io module~rki_state_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_barotropic_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->pic_logger module~rki_eos rki_eos module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_eos module~rki_tracer_unstr rki_tracer_unstr module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_tracer_unstr module~rki_vcoord rki_vcoord module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr->module~rki_vcoord module~rki_si_common->pic_logger module~rki_si_unstr_state->module~rki_constants module~rki_si_unstr_state->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_state->pic_logger module~rki_si_unstr_mg rki_si_unstr_mg module~rki_si_unstr_state->module~rki_si_unstr_mg module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_timestepper->module~rki_constants module~rki_eos->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_eos->module~rki_grid module~rki_si_unstr_mg->module~rki_constants module~rki_si_unstr_mg->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_mg->pic_logger module~rki_tracer_unstr->module~rki_constants module~rki_tracer_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_tracer_unstr->module~rki_boundary_unstr module~rki_vcoord->module~rki_constants module~rki_vcoord->pic_logger pic_strings pic_strings module~rki_vcoord->pic_strings module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_kernel_fused_unstr~~UsedByGraph module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr rki_kernel_fused_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr rki_solver_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr module~rki_api_unstr rki_api_unstr module~rki_api_unstr->module~rki_solver_unstr module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver_unstr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Subroutines public  subroutine fused_save_state_unstr (state, mesh) Snapshot U&#94;n into the _backup slots once at step start, for the\nselectable-integrator generic path (the convex blend reads them). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh public  subroutine fused_update_stage1_unstr (state, mesh, dt) Stage 1: save + Euler update + friction/wind + protect Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public  subroutine fused_update_stage2_unstr (state, mesh, dt) Stage 2: Euler update + friction/wind + protect + RK2 average + protect Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public  subroutine fused_update_stage_generic_unstr (state, mesh, dt) One forward-Euler stage for the selectable-integrator path:\nEuler update + friction/wind + protect, scaled by the per-stage dt ( beta(i)*dt_step ).  Identical to fused_update_stage1_unstr\nminus the start-of-step backup writes (taken once by\nfused_save_state_unstr) so every scheme shares one source-term body. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt public  subroutine ssp_combine_unstr (state, mesh, a_n) Generalized SSP Shu-Osher combine: U = a_n U&#94;n + (1 - a_n) U,\nwhere U is the post-Euler-stage iterate and _backup = U&#94;n.\nReduces exactly to the 0.5 average in fused_update_stage2_unstr for\na_n = 0.5.  Applies the same post-blend protect (mass-error bucket\nincluded) so each stage stays wet/dry-safe. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( unstr_state_t ), intent(inout) :: state type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: a_n","tags":"","url":"module/rki_kernel_fused_unstr.html"},{"title":"rki_mem_report – Rakali","text":"Free procedures that estimate, log, and verify the device memory\nfootprint of the simulation state before the OpenACC enter_data mapping is attempted — so an over-budget run reports\na readable diagnostic instead of dying opaquely inside the CUDA\nruntime (the motivating failure: a 10M-cell ocean config that\nexhausted device memory at enter_data with no setup-time hint). Design decision (no hand-maintained per-slot byte counts — those\nrot the moment a slot is added): the ONLY trustworthy figures are\nthe OpenACC runtime’s own free-memory queries.  The device\nfootprint of the state mapping is measured , not estimated, as\nthe drop in free device memory across enter_data ( mem_log_state_budget snapshots free-before; mem_log_device_actuals reports the delta).  Host RSS growth\nacross state init is still logged, but ONLY as an advisory\nhost-side figure + a conservative upper bound for the pre-flight\nOOM warning — it includes host-only allocations (NetCDF/HDF5\nlibrary pages, I/O buffers, host mirrors of the device arrays) and\nmeasured 6-31x larger than the true device map (2026-07 audit), so\nit must never be read as a device estimate. Three structural offsets to keep in mind when reconciling these\nfigures against nvidia-smi (audited 2026-07 on V100):\n  1. CUDA context + CUBIN load : ~300-500 MB per process,\n     created at the first OpenACC API call / directive.  It is\n     inside used = total - free and inside nvidia-smi’s\n     per-process figure, but is NOT state — a tiny config still\n     shows ~300 MB in use.\n  2. Device-wide accounting + pool granularity : used = total - free counts EVERY process on the device\n     (shared-device activity perturbs it and the measured mapping\n     delta), and the NVHPC pool allocator rounds small maps up by\n     a few MB.\n  3. One-off CUDA runtime/kernel reservation at first launch :\n     the first time-loop step grows per-process device usage by\n     GBs (measured: ~3.0 GB coastal, ~8.6 GB ocean on V100) —\n     constant thereafter, independent of step count and of NV_ACC_MEM_MANAGE , and NOT proportional to grid size.\n     Consistent with the driver’s local-memory/stack backing for\n     stack-heavy kernels (fixed-size local() arrays), which\n     scales with the binary’s kernels x device SM count.  It is\n     real per-process usage (visible in nvidia-smi) but is not a\n     leak; the growth WARNING therefore measures against the\n     steady post-first-sample baseline, not the post- enter_data one. Post-setup growth ( mem_log_device_growth ) makes drift\nself-announcing: kernels that lazy-allocate device workspaces on\nfirst call (the coastal *_workspace_ensure pattern — measured at\n~33% of the coastal device footprint) land AFTER enter_data , so\nthe periodic status re-checks and the end-of-run summary reports\nthe growth, warning above GROWTH_WARN_FRAC . Device queries use the OpenACC property API\n( acc_get_property with acc_property_memory / acc_property_free_memory ).  They are compiled only when the\nOpenACC runtime module is available ( RAKALI_HAS_OPENACC_RUNTIME ,\nset by cmake/compiler_flags.cmake for NVHPC + Cray — covers both\nthe -acc=gpu and -mp=gpu NVHPC backends).  On every other\ntoolchain (gfortran, ifx) the device functions return -1 and the\nloggers degrade to the host-only line. Uses pic_strings rki_constants pic_logger iso_fortran_env module~~rki_mem_report~~UsesGraph module~rki_mem_report rki_mem_report iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~rki_mem_report->iso_fortran_env module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_mem_report->module~rki_constants pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_mem_report->pic_logger pic_strings pic_strings module~rki_mem_report->pic_strings pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_mem_report~~UsedByGraph module~rki_mem_report rki_mem_report module~rki_barotropic_state rki_barotropic_state module~rki_barotropic_state->module~rki_mem_report module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_mem_report module~rki_state rki_state module~rki_driver->module~rki_state module~rki_coastal_console_stats rki_coastal_console_stats module~rki_driver->module~rki_coastal_console_stats mo