given different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Derived Types type, public :: multilayer_state_t Per-layer prognostic arrays + multilayer scalar config. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public :: S_init_bottom = 0.0_wp Linear-S(z) stratification, bed (k=1) value.  See S_init_surface. real(kind=wp), public :: S_init_surface = 0.0_wp Linear-S(z) stratification, surface (k=nz) value.  When both\nS_init_surface and S_init_bottom are non-zero (and nz>1) the\nsalinity seed becomes a linear profile from S_init_bottom at\nthe bed (k=1) to S_init_surface at the surface; otherwise the\nuniform initial_salinity is used.  Stable polarity is the\ninverse of temperature: S_init_bottom > S_init_surface (salty\nbed, fresh surface). real(kind=wp), public :: S_max = 40.0_wp Upper physical salinity bound (PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: S_min = 0.0_wp Lower physical salinity bound (PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: S_ref = 0.0_wp Reference salinity in EOS (PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: T_init_bottom = 0.0_wp Linear-T(z) stratification, bed (k=1) value.  See T_init_surface. real(kind=wp), public :: T_init_surface = 0.0_wp Linear-T(z) stratification, surface (k=nz) value.  When both\nT_init_surface and T_init_bottom are non-zero (and nz>1) the\ntemperature seed becomes a linear profile from T_init_bottom at\nthe bed (k=1) to T_init_surface at the surface; otherwise the\nuniform initial_temperature is used.  Mirrors the ocean path. real(kind=wp), public :: T_max = 40.0_wp Upper physical temperature bound (degC) real(kind=wp), public :: T_min = -2.0_wp Lower physical temperature bound (degC) real(kind=wp), public :: T_ref = 15.0_wp Reference temperature in EOS (degC) real(kind=wp), public :: alpha_T = 0.17_wp Thermal expansion coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per degC).\nSet to 0 to make temperature a passive tracer. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: bed_sediment (:,:) Bed sediment mass reservoir (kg/m&#94;2), per column.  Allocated when\nuse_sediment.  Settling deposits into it; total (suspended + bed)\nsediment is conserved. real(kind=wp), public :: beta_S = 0.78_wp Haline contraction coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: biharmonic_nu4 = 0.0_wp Biharmonic (del&#94;4) lateral viscosity coefficient (m&#94;4/s); 0 = off real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: dsig_ml (:) Sigma layer fractions (nz_ml), sum = 1 type( eos_t ), public :: eos Shared EOS handle (variant tag + scalar coefficients) for\nthe opt-in path.  Flat POD (no allocatable components):\nread on the host at dispatch time and passed by value into\nthe device kernels, so it needs NO enter_data/exit_data\nmapping. eos%rho0 mirrors rho_0 (vanishing-layer\nfallback density); eos%p_ref stays 0 ⇒ surface/potential\ndensity. logical, public :: eos_use_shared = .false. When .true. the EOS call sites route through the shared rki_eos dispatch ( ml_equation_of_state_shared )\ninstead of the legacy coastal linear kernel.  Default off ⇒\nevery existing coastal config is bit-identical by\nconstruction.  Set from &tracer_nml eos_form via ml_parse_eos_form (state_init / driver). logical, public :: evap_latent_cooling = .false. When true (needs evap_mass_sink), evaporation also withdraws its\nlatent heat of vaporization from the surface layer (k=nz) — an\nadditional cooling on top of the sensible heat that leaves with\nthe removed water.  Default false = bit-identical. logical, public :: evap_mass_sink = .false. When true, net evaporation is a real top-layer water-mass sink\n(h_top -= E*dt) with salt held (concentration rises) and heat\ncarried away with the water.  Default false = virtual salt flux. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: h_layer (:,:,:) Layer thickness real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: h_layer0 (:,:,:) real(kind=wp), public :: hdiff_kappa = 0.0_wp Horizontal diffusion coefficient for tracers (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hu_layer (:,:,:) Layer x-momentum h_k*u_k real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hu_layer0 (:,:,:) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hu_ml_pre (:,:) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hv_layer (:,:,:) Layer y-momentum h_k*v_k real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hv_layer0 (:,:,:) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: hv_ml_pre (:,:) integer, public :: idx_salinity = 0 Index into tracers(:) for salinity. 0 = not registered. integer, public :: idx_sediment = 0 Index into tracers(:) for suspended sediment. 0 = not registered. integer, public :: idx_temperature = 0 Index into tracers(:) for temperature. 0 = not registered. real(kind=wp), public :: initial_salinity = 35.0_wp Initial salinity for all layers (PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: initial_temperature = 15.0_wp Initial temperature for all layers (degC) real(kind=wp), public :: kappa_S_bg = 1.0e-5_wp Background vertical salinity diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: kappa_T_bg = 1.0e-5_wp Background vertical temperature diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: keps_eps (:,:,:) TKE dissipation rate at interfaces (m&#94;2/s&#94;3). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: keps_kt (:,:,:) k-eps turbulent (scalar) diffusivity at interfaces (m&#94;2/s). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: keps_nut (:,:,:) k-eps turbulent viscosity at interfaces (m&#94;2/s); read as the old\nvalue by the next diffusion step, so it persists across steps. integer, public :: keps_stability = KEPS_STAB_CONSTANT Stability-function scheme for nu_t / kappa_t (KEPS_STAB_*): constant\nc_mu (default) or Galperin stratification-aware quasi-equilibrium. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: keps_tke (:,:,:) Turbulent kinetic energy at interfaces (m&#94;2/s&#94;2), shape (nx,ny,nz+1). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: keps_ustar_b (:,:) Bed friction velocity for the k-eps wall functions (m/s), (nx,ny).\nRecomputed each step from the bottom-drag law; kept as a field\n(not scratch) so it maps to the device like the KPP u_star. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: keps_ustar_s (:,:) Surface friction velocity for the k-eps wall functions (m/s). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: kpp_bl_depth (:,:) Diagnosed boundary-layer depth (m, positive down).  Persists\nacross steps — the previous value seeds the V_t&#94;2 velocity\nscale (self-bootstraps from zero on the first call). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: kpp_buoy_flux (:,:) Surface buoyancy flux B_0 (m&#94;2/s&#94;3); <0 = destabilizing. real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_c_vt2 = 1.8_wp Unresolved-turbulence coefficient for V_t&#94;2 (LMD94 eq 23). real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_cs_nonlocal = 6.3_wp Non-local transport coefficient C_s (LMD94 eq 20). real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_ri_crit = 0.3_wp Critical bulk Richardson number for the BL-depth sweep. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: kpp_u_star (:,:) Surface friction velocity sqrt(|tau|/rho_0) (m/s), per column. integer, public :: nz_ml = 1 Number of multilayer sigma layers integer, public :: nz_ref = 0 Highest valid index in rho_ref(0:nz_ref) . 0 = unset. logical, public :: registry_locked = .false. Set by solver_tracers_enter_data , cleared by solver_tracers_exit_data .  While locked, register_passive_tracer REFUSES: the device map snapshots tracers(:) element-by-element, so growing the registry\nreallocates the array (and deep-copies every element’s hTr / hTr0 ), stranding every existing tracer’s device\nmapping on freed host addresses — an illegal address or a\nsilent stale-host read on the mem:separate GPU build. real(kind=wp), public :: rho_0 = 1000.0_wp Reference density for EOS (kg/m&#94;3) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: rho_layer (:,:,:) (nx_total, ny_total, nz_ml) real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: rho_ref (:) Reference density profile sampled at iz * rho_ref_dz for iz = 0..nz_ref . Index 0 = surface. real(kind=wp), public :: rho_ref_dz = 0.0_wp Reference-grid spacing (m). 0 = unset. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_bed_init = 0.0_wp Uniform initial bed sediment mass (kg/m&#94;2). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_erosion_rate = 0.0_wp Ariathurai erosion-rate coefficient E0 (kg/m&#94;2/s; 0 = off). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_initial_conc = 0.0_wp Uniform initial suspended-sediment concentration (kg/m&#94;3). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_porosity = 0.0_wp Bed porosity (0-1); erosion scaled by (1 - porosity). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_tau_crit_erosion = 0.0_wp Critical bed shear stress for erosion (Pa; 0 = erosion off). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_w_s = 0.0_wp Settling (sinking) velocity (m/s, downward; 0 = no settling). real(kind=wp), public :: smagorinsky_cs = 0.0_wp Smagorinsky horizontal viscosity coefficient integer, public :: tracer_recon_code = 0 Parsed TRACER_RECON_* code (0 = PPM, 1 = WENO5, 2 = WENO7,\n3 = WENO9).  Set at state init from config%tracer_recon. type( tracer_t ), public, allocatable :: tracers (:) Registered prognostic tracers (allocated when use_multilayer) logical, public :: use_bpg_jacobian = .true. Use the pressure-Jacobian BPG (Shchepetkin & McWilliams 2003).\nDEFAULT ON.  The sigma alternative differences the integrated\ndensity anomaly at constant SIGMA INDEX, which over sloping\nbathymetry produces a fictitious force proportional to\n(uniform density anomaly) x (bed slope) – so a column of\nspatially UNIFORM density whose value differs from rho_0 is\nspuriously accelerated, and the resulting flow leaks mass\n(measured: 1.7e-6 relative over 400 steps, vs 1.3e-14 with the\nJacobian).  Pinned by test_bpg_uniform_density . logical, public :: use_ppm_tracer = .true. Use PPM for tracer advection (false = first-order upwind) logical, public :: use_sediment = .false. Master switch for sediment transport (default off). type( vcoord_t ), public :: vcoord Coordinate type (sigma / zsigma), remap method, parameters real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: vcoord_z_ref (:) Reference z-level interfaces (0:nz_ml), GPU-mapped copy of\nvcoord%z_ref.  Top-level allocatable so OpenACC can map it\nwithout derived-type attach issues. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: vcoord_z_ref_col (:,:,:) Per-column reference z-level interfaces for VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL,\nshape (0:nz_ml, nx_total, ny_total).  Built once at solver\ninit from local bathymetry; static thereafter.  Only\nallocated when coord_type == VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL. real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_nu_bg = 1.0e-4_wp Background vertical viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_nu_max = 0.01_wp Pacanowski-Philander max turbulent viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_ri_alpha = 5.0_wp Richardson number scaling coefficient (shared S+T in PP81) logical, public :: vmix_use_keps = .false. Master switch for the two-equation k-epsilon closure (default\noff = PP81/KPP).  Interface-shaped prognostic fields below\nare allocated only when this is set. logical, public :: vmix_use_kpp = .false. Master switch for the KPP overlay (default off = pure PP81). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: w_ml (:,:,:) (nx_total, ny_total, nz_ml+1) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: build_vcoord_reference => multilayer_build_vcoord_reference procedure, public, non_overridable :: bytes => multilayer_state_bytes procedure, public, non_overridable :: destroy => multilayer_state_destroy procedure, public, non_overridable :: init => multilayer_state_init procedure, public, non_overridable :: init_layers => multilayer_init_layers procedure, public, non_overridable :: register_passive_tracer => multilayer_register_passive_tracer procedure, public, non_overridable :: seed_tracers => multilayer_seed_tracers Functions private pure function multilayer_state_bytes (this) result(nbytes) Counted allocatable footprint of the multilayer slot: the layer\nprognostics + RK2 saves + vcoord/rho tables + the tracer registry\n(each tracer sums its own arrays) + the gated KPP / k-epsilon /\nsediment workspaces (0 when their closure is off). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multilayer_state_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=int64) Subroutines private  subroutine multilayer_build_vcoord_reference (this, barotropic, grid) For VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL, build the per-column reference z-level\npattern vcoord_z_ref_col from the bathymetry.  No-op for the\nother vertical coordinates.  Needed both on a cold start (called\nby init_layers ) and after a restart read, which restores the\nprognostic layer fields but not this derived array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multilayer_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( barotropic_state_t ), intent(in) :: barotropic type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid private  subroutine multilayer_init_layers (this, barotropic, grid) Lay out the initial per-layer distribution from the barotropic\nstate: for VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL first build the per-column\nreference z-level pattern from the bathymetry, then split the\nbarotropic (h, hu, hv) across layers via the sigma weights dsig_ml .  Call once after init and before seed_tracers /\nEOS. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multilayer_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( barotropic_state_t ), intent(in) :: barotropic type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid private  subroutine multilayer_register_passive_tracer (this, grid, name, tr_init, tr_min, tr_max, kappa_bg, hdiff_kappa) Append a passive tracer (eos_coeff = 0) to the registry,\ngrowing tracers(:) past the default S/T pair.  Must be called\nAFTER init and BEFORE the solver’s enter_data (so the new hTr gets device-mapped) — enforced via registry_locked :\nonce the solver has mapped the registry the call logs an error\nand returns without touching it.  Caller populates hTr once\nlayer thicknesses are known.  S/T keep their indices. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multilayer_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid character(len=*), intent(in) :: name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_init real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_min real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tr_max real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: kappa_bg real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: hdiff_kappa private pure subroutine multilayer_seed_tracers (this, grid) Seed salinity + temperature from the IC scalars on the state,\neach dispatching uniform-vs-stratified via ml_seed_tracer .\nCall once after the layer thicknesses are laid out and before\nEOS. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multilayer_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid private  subroutine multilayer_state_destroy (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multilayer_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine multilayer_state_init (this, grid) Allocate all multilayer arrays at the grid size and configured\nlayer count, init the vcoord object, copy vcoord%z_ref into\nthe GPU-mappable vcoord_z_ref , allocate the rho-ref profile,\nand register S + T.  Caller must set nz_ml , vcoord%coord_type , vcoord%remap_method , and any other\nvcoord parameters first. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( multilayer_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid","tags":"","url":"module/rki_multilayer_state.html"},{"title":"rki_config – Rakali","text":"Reads simulation parameters from a namelist input file Uses rki_nml_schema pic_strings rki_constants pic_logger module~~rki_config~~UsesGraph module~rki_config rki_config module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_config->module~rki_constants module~rki_nml_schema rki_nml_schema module~rki_config->module~rki_nml_schema pic_logger pic_logger module~rki_config->pic_logger pic_strings pic_strings module~rki_config->pic_strings pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_nml_schema->module~rki_constants module~rki_nml_schema->pic_logger Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it