l salinity at the surface layer (k=nz_ml, PSU).\nActivates linear S(z) stratification when set non-zero\ntogether with S_init_bottom . real(kind=wp), public :: S_max = 40.0_wp Upper physical bound for salinity (PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: S_min = 0.0_wp Lower physical bound for salinity (PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: S_ref = 0.0_wp Reference salinity in EOS (PSU); density anomaly = beta_S*(S - S_ref) real(kind=wp), public :: T_init_bottom = 0.0_wp Initial temperature at the bed (k=1, degC). real(kind=wp), public :: T_init_surface = 0.0_wp Initial temperature at the surface layer (k=nz_ml, degC).\nActivates linear T(z) stratification when set non-zero\ntogether with T_init_bottom . real(kind=wp), public :: T_max = 40.0_wp Upper physical bound for temperature (degC) real(kind=wp), public :: T_min = -2.0_wp Lower physical bound for temperature (degC); seawater freezing real(kind=wp), public :: T_ref = 15.0_wp Reference temperature in EOS (degC); density anomaly = -alpha_T*(T - T_ref) real(kind=wp), public :: alpha_T = 0.17_wp Thermal expansion coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per degC); ~0.17 near 15 degC.\nSet to 0 to decouple temperature from dynamics (pure passive tracer). integer, public :: async_buffer_slots = 4 Number of ring buffer slots for async output (default: 4) logical, public :: async_output = .false. Use async ring-buffered output (CUDA Fortran only, ignored otherwise) character(len=256), public :: bathymetry_file = \"\" Path to NetCDF bathymetry file (empty = flat bottom) character(len=16), public :: bc_east = \"wall\" East boundary: “wall”, “open”, “tidal”, “nested” character(len=16), public :: bc_north = \"wall\" North boundary: “wall”, “open”, “tidal”, “nested” character(len=16), public :: bc_south = \"wall\" South boundary: “wall”, “open”, “tidal”, “nested” character(len=16), public :: bc_west = \"wall\" West boundary: “wall”, “open”, “tidal”, “nested” real(kind=wp), public :: beta_S = 0.78_wp Haline contraction coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per PSU) real(kind=wp), public :: biharmonic_nu4 = 0.0_wp Biharmonic (del&#94;4) lateral viscosity coefficient (m&#94;4/s) for layer\nmomentum; 0 = off.  Capped at the explicit-step stability limit.\nnu_h = (Cs * dx)&#94;2 * |S| where |S| is the strain rate.\nProvides grid-aware dissipation at sharp velocity gradients. real(kind=wp), public :: bottom_drag_r = 0.0_wp Linear bottom-drag rate (1/s); used when use_linear_bottom_drag. character(len=16), public :: bpg_method = \"jacobian\" BPG computation method: “jacobian” (Shchepetkin-McWilliams,\nDEFAULT) or “sigma” (cheaper, but see below). Read more… real(kind=wp), public :: cfl = 0.45_wp CFL number for adaptive timestep integer, public :: cfl_interval = 1 Recompute CFL timestep every N steps (1 = every step) real(kind=wp), public :: clamped_elevation = 0.0_wp Prescribed surface elevation for clamped BC (m) integer, public :: compress_level = 1 Deflate compression level (1=fast, 9=max). 1 is usually optimal. logical, public :: compress_output = .false. Enable deflate compression for NetCDF output (NetCDF4/HDF5) real(kind=wp), public :: coriolis_f = 0.0_wp Coriolis parameter f (1/s), typically 2 Omega sin(lat) real(kind=wp), public :: discharge_flux = 0.0_wp Prescribed volume flux for discharge BC (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: dry_threshold = 0.001_wp Depth below which a cell is considered dry (m) real(kind=wp), public :: dt_fixed = 0.0_wp Fixed timestep (s), 0 = adaptive CFL.  Same convention\nas dt_max — always seconds. real(kind=wp), public :: dt_max = 1.0e10_wp Maximum allowable timestep (s) — always in seconds, NOT\naffected by time_unit .  Timesteps are naturally short\nand CFL-bounded; writing them in \"day\" would force\nawkward fractional values. real(kind=wp), public :: dx = 1.0_wp Cell size in x-direction (m) real(kind=wp), public :: dy = 1.0_wp Cell size in y-direction (m) character(len=16), public :: eos_form = \"linear\" COASTAL equation-of-state selector (both backends):\n“linear” (default) keeps the legacy coastal linear kernel rho = rho_0 + beta_S*(S-S_ref) - alpha_T*(T-T_ref) —\nbit-identical by construction for every existing config.\n“wright” (Wright 1997 rational) / “roquet_spv” (Roquet et\nal. 2015 TEOS-10 polynomial) route density through the\nSHARED nonlinear EOS ( rki_eos ), evaluated at p=0\n(surface/potential density); alpha_T/beta_S/S_ref/T_ref\nare then ignored by the density computation.  CAVEAT: the\ncoastal KPP surface buoyancy-flux estimate B_0 =\n(g/rho_0)(alpha_T F_T - beta_S F_S) still reads the\nnamelist alpha_T/beta_S as constant expansion coefficients\n— set them to locally representative values when pairing\neos_form with vmix_use_kpp (interior Ri mixing reads\nrho_layer directly and is fully consistent).  The ocean\nregime ignores this knob ( &ocean_pgf_nml eos= instead). real(kind=wp), public :: eta_initial = 0.0_wp Initial free-surface elevation for still_water IC (m, relative to bathymetry datum) logical, public :: evap_latent_cooling = .false. Latent-heat cooling of the surface from evaporation (v2).  When\ntrue (and evap_mass_sink is also true), the water that evaporates\nwithdraws its latent heat of vaporization from the top layer:\nan ADDITIONAL surface heat sink Q_lat = rho_water E_eff L_v [W/m²]\napplied to k=nz, where E_eff is the effective (clamped) evaporation\nrate actually removed.  This is distinct from — and does NOT\ndouble-count — the sensible heat that already leaves with the\nremoved water mass (that is handled by the proportional hT scaling\nin evap_mass_sink).  Requires evap_mass_sink=.true.; no-op\notherwise (fail-loud at configure).  Default .false. = bit-identical. logical, public :: evap_mass_sink = .false. Treat net evaporation (evap_minus_precip > 0) as a real surface\nwater-mass sink at the top layer (k=nz) instead of a virtual salt\nflux.  Removes water: h_top -= E dt; salinity mass hS is left\nunchanged so concentration rises; heat leaves with the water\n(hT_top -= E dt*T_top) so temperature concentration is preserved.\nDefault .false. = bit-identical (legacy virtual-salt-flux path). character(len=256), public :: forcing_file = \"\" Path to NetCDF atmospheric forcing file (empty = uniform config values) real(kind=wp), public :: forcing_x_origin = 0.0_wp Model grid x-origin in forcing file coordinates real(kind=wp), public :: forcing_y_origin = 0.0_wp Model grid y-origin in forcing file coordinates character(len=256), public :: gauge_file = \"\" Path to gauge locations text file (empty = no gauge output) real(kind=wp), public :: gauge_output_interval = 0.0_wp Gauge output interval in seconds (0 = every timestep) character(len=16), public :: grid_type = \"structured\" Grid discretization: “structured” (Cartesian) or “unstructured”\n(triangular).  “unstructured” routes the coastal regime through the\nnative mesh generator + unstructured solver (Python-free). real(kind=wp), public :: h0 = 1.0_wp Background depth for gaussian_hump IC (m) real(kind=wp), public :: hdiff_kappa = 0.0_wp Horizontal diffusion coefficient for tracers (m&#94;2/s).\nSmooths sharp density fronts to reduce BPG overshoot.\nTypical values: 1-10 m&#94;2/s depending on grid resolution. real(kind=wp), public :: hump_amplitude = 0.05_wp Perturbation amplitude for gaussian_hump IC (m) real(kind=wp), public :: hump_sigma = 5.0_wp Gaussian width for gaussian_hump IC (m) real(kind=wp), public :: hump_x_offset = 0.0_wp Hump centre x-offset from domain centre (m) real(kind=wp), public :: hump_y_offset = 0.0_wp Hump centre y-offset from domain centre (m) real(kind=wp), public :: inflow_salinity = -1.0_wp Prescribed salinity for inflow BC (PSU); <0 = zero-gradient real(kind=wp), public :: inflow_temperature = -999.0_wp Prescribed temperature for inflow BC (degC); <0 = zero-gradient real(kind=wp), public :: inflow_velocity = 0.0_wp Prescribed normal velocity for inflow BC (m/s) character(len=32), public :: init_condition = \"dam_break\" Initial condition: “dam_break”, “gaussian_hump”, “castro_dam_break”, or “still_water” real(kind=wp), public :: init_u_shear = 0.0_wp Initial vertical shear: top layer gets +val, bottom gets -val (m/s) real(kind=wp), public :: initial_salinity = 35.0_wp Initial salinity for all layers (PSU).  Used as a uniform IC\nunless S_init_surface and S_init_bottom are BOTH set\nnon-zero, in which case the seed builds a linear S(z) profile\nfrom S_init_bottom at k=1 (bed) to S_init_surface at\nk=nz (surface).  NOTE the stable polarity is the inverse of\ntemperature: salty/dense water belongs at the bed, so a stable\nhaline column has S_init_bottom > S_init_surface (fresh\nsurface, e.g. a river-plume column). real(kind=wp), public :: initial_temperature = 15.0_wp Initial potential temperature for all layers (degC).  Used\nas a uniform IC unless T_init_surface and T_init_bottom are BOTH set non-zero, in which case the seed builds a\nlinear T(z) profile from T_init_bottom at k=1 (bed) to T_init_surface at k=nz (surface).  Stratified IC is the\nprerequisite for baroclinic-instability-driven eddies. character(len=256), public :: institution = \"\" Institution name for CF global attribute (empty = omitted) real(kind=wp), public :: kappa_S_bg = 1.0e-5_wp Background vertical salinity diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: kappa_T_bg = 1.0e-5_wp Background vertical temperature diffusivity (m&#94;2/s) integer, public :: keps_si_picard = 1 Picard passes of the k<->eps coupling per semi-implicit step\n( time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\" + vmix_use_keps only; the\nexplicit path ignores it).  1 (default) = single pass, the\nshipped explicit cadence — steady-state-exact per the Q1\nprototype (local_archive/prototypes/si_closures).  2 (the certified\nsetting; up to 3 accepted) re-runs the k/eps solve with the\nrefreshed nu_t production coefficient for transient-fidelity\nstudies.  Fixed pass count (GPU column-parallel, no per-column\ndivergence). character(len=16), public :: keps_stability = \"constant\" k-epsilon stability functions: “constant” (default; c_mu=0.09,\nPr_t=1), “galperin” (quasi-equilibrium), or “canuto” (Canuto-A). real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_c_vt2 = 1.8_wp Unresolved-turbulence coefficient for the V_t&#94;2 term in the\nbulk-Ri denominator (LMD94 eq 23).  Set 0 to disable V_t&#94;2. real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_cs_nonlocal = 6.3_wp Non-local (counter-gradient) transport coefficient C_s\n(LMD94 eq 20, limit value). real(kind=wp), public :: kpp_ri_crit = 0.3_wp Critical bulk Richardson number for the KPP BL-depth sweep. character(len=16), public :: log_level = \"info\" Log verbosity: “debug”, “verbose”, “info”, “performance”, “warning”, “error” real(kind=wp), public :: manning_n = 0.0_wp Manning roughness coefficient real(kind=wp), public :: ml_min_depth = 0.5_wp Minimum total water depth for vertical layer operations (m).\nColumns shallower than this skip vertical exchange, mixing,\nsalinity advection, and BPG.  Increase if instabilities appear\nnear wetting/drying fronts. integer, public :: n_tidal_constituents = 0 Number of active tidal constituents (0 = use legacy single) character(len=256), public :: nesting_file = \"\" Path to parent domain NetCDF output (empty = no nesting) real(kind=wp), public :: nesting_x_origin = 0.0_wp Child grid x-origin in parent coordinates (m) real(kind=wp), public :: nesting_y_origin = 0.0_wp Child grid y-origin in parent coordinates (m) integer, public :: nghost = 3 Number of ghost cells on each side.  Default 3 (not 2): a\n5-point PPM reconstruction stencil means a rank-seam face’s\nghost-side donor needs two neighbours beyond itself —\nfull-order reconstruction AT the seam requires three ghost\ncolumns.  At nghost=2 the PPM\nlocal-array-edge fallback fires at the seam and degrades the\nface to first order, producing a seam-inconsistent tracer mass\nflux: it conserves a uniform tracer (constant field cancels)\nbut LEAKS a structured one (advecting T with rank-A-out /=\nrank-B-in on the shared seam face drifts hT), invisible to the\nmass/salt closure gates.  Measured on seamount_bench_full\n(np2 x-split): heat closure grew to +5e-11 by day 2 at nghost=2,\nstays at round-off (~5e-14, no growth) at nghost=3.  Single-rank\nruns are unaffected by the wider halo (same interior); the extra\nghost column only costs a little memory. integer, public :: nh_max_iterations = 100 Maximum CG iterations for NH pressure logical, public :: nh_preconditioner = .false. Enable vertical-line preconditioner for CG solver integer, public :: nh_solve_interval = 1 Solve NH pressure every N steps (1 = every step, N > 1 = reuse q_nh) real(kind=wp), public :: nh_tolerance = 1.0e-6_wp CG convergence tolerance for NH pressure integer, public :: nx = 200 Number of physical cells in x-direction integer, public :: ny = 1 Number of physical cells in y-direction integer, public :: nz_layers = 2 Number of sigma layers for NH solver logical, public :: out_density = .false. Output layer density logical, public :: out_h_layer = .true. Output layer thickness logical, public :: out_salinity = .true. Output layer salinity logical, public :: out_temperature = .true. Output layer temperature logical, public :: out_velocity = .true. Output layer velocity (u_ml, v_ml) logical, public :: out_w = .false. Output vertical velocity at interfaces character(len=256), public :: output_dir = \"./output\" Directory for output files character(len=16), public :: output_format = \"netcdf\" Output format: “ascii” or “netcdf” real(kind=wp), public :: output_interval = 0.0_wp Time between output snapshots (s) logical, public :: output_to_file = .false. Enable file output (NetCDF snapshots) character(len=64), public :: reference_time = \"\" Time origin for CF output, e.g. “2026-01-01 00:00:00” (empty = idealized run) character(len=16), public :: remap_method = \"ppm\" Vertical remapping method: “pcm”, “plm”, “ppm”, “ppm_h4”, “pqm”.  Default PPM\n(piecewise parabolic, Colella & Woodward 1984) — the state-of-the-art\nconservative vertical-remap stencil for the coastal ALE coords. “pqm” is\npiecewise quartic (White & Adcroft 2008); it falls back to PPM for nz < 5. character(len=256), public :: restart_file = \"\" Path to restart file for warm start (empty = cold start) real(kind=wp), public :: restart_interval = 0.0_wp Time between restart file writes (s), 0 = no restarts real(kind=wp), public :: rho_0 = 1000.0_wp Reference density for EOS (kg/m&#94;3) real(kind=wp), public :: rho_ref_pressure = 2.0e7_wp Reference pressure (Pa, default 2e7 = 2000 dbar) for the\npotential density that defines the VCOORD_RHO coordinate. real(kind=wp), public :: rho_target_dense = 1030.0_wp Densest target interface potential density (kg/m³) — the bed\ninterface for VCOORD_RHO.  See rho_target_light . real(kind=wp), public :: rho_target_light = 1020.0_wp Lightest target interface potential density (kg/m³) — the\nsurface interface for VCOORD_RHO.  With rho_target_dense builds the uniform light→dense target-density linspace\n(MOM6 ALE_COORDINATE_CONFIG=UNIFORM analogue for the RHO\nmode).  A stretched (RFNC1-style) profile is a P3 follow-up. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_bed_init = 0.0_wp Uniform initial bed sediment mass (kg/m&#94;2). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_erosion_rate = 0.0_wp Ariathurai erosion-rate coefficient E0 (kg/m&#94;2/s). 0 = erosion off. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_initial_conc = 0.0_wp Uniform initial suspended-sediment concentration (kg/m&#94;3). real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_porosity = 0.0_wp Bed porosity (0-1); erosion scaled by (1 - porosity).\n0 = off, typical 0.1-0.2. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_tau_crit_erosion = 0.0_wp Critical bed shear stress for erosion (Pa). 0 = erosion off. real(kind=wp), public :: sediment_w_s = 0.0_wp Settling (sinking) velocity (m/s, downward; 0 = no settling). logical, public :: semi_implicit = .false. Derived (not a namelist key): .true. when time_scheme==”semi_implicit”.\nSet in apply_time_unit_cascade (runs at the end of the config read,\nbefore validate_config ) so downstream code branches on the logical,\nnot the string. integer, public :: si_newton_max = 10 Casulli wet/dry Newton outer-iteration cap ( &si_nml newton_max ).\nDefault 10 matches the historical hardcoded value (bit-identical).\nReal intertidal bathymetry with a shuffling active set may need\nmore.  Only consulted when si_wetdry=.true. . real(kind=wp), public :: si_newton_tol = 1.0e-11_wp Casulli wet/dry Newton RELATIVE residual tolerance\n( &si_nml newton_tol ): converged when ||F||&#94;2 < newton_tol&#94;2 * ||rhs||&#94;2 AND the active set is frozen.\nDefault 1e-11 matches the historical hardcoded value\n(bit-identical) — tight, tuned for smooth validation cases; real\nbathymetry typically converges to ~1e-7 and wants that here.\nOnly consulted when si_wetdry=.true. . character(len=8), public :: si_precond = \"none\" Preconditioner for the SI Helmholtz eta-solve: \"none\" (unpreconditioned CG, default), \"jacobi\" (diagonal PCG, z = eta_diag*r ), or \"mg\" (aggregation-multigrid V-cycle\nPCG).\nFail-loud allowlist.  Default \"none\" is byte-identical to the\npre-knob plain-CG path. real(kind=wp), public :: si_rtol = 1.0e-10_wp CG RELATIVE residual tolerance: converge when ||r||&#94;2 < si_rtol&#94;2 * ||rhs||&#94;2 .  Default 1e-10 reproduces\nthe historical hardcoded SI_TOL_REL bit-for-bit; relaxable\n(1e-8/1e-6) to cut iterations — si%mass_res is the audit\ninstrument for the resulting mass consistency. logical, public :: si_wetdry = .false. Casulli (2009) subgrid wetting/drying for the SI free surface:\nreplaces the linear 1.0 cell-mass term by the exact wetted-\nvolume V(eta) (per-cell wet-fraction Newton diagonal) so\nintertidal flats dry at minute-scale dt.  Default .false. is\nbyte-identical (all-wet configs unchanged).  Structured coastal\nSI: 2D barotropic + 3D sigma multilayer.  Unstructured coastal\nSI: 2D barotropic + 3D sigma multilayer (the triangular wet/dry\nNewton).  See si_wetdry_bsub_fill for the subgrid bed option. character(len=32), public :: si_wetdry_bsub_fill = \"flat\" Sub-bottom table fill mode when si_wetdry_nsub>=2 : \"flat\" (default) — all sub-bottoms = the plain bed b , so the\n    volume reduces to the flat-bottom case ⇒ BIT-IDENTICAL to nsub=1 (and to today’s behaviour). \"linear\" — the analytic subgrid variant: n_sub equal-area\n    sub-bottoms evenly spaced across a per-cell relief band [b - half, b + half] where half = 0.5*max neighbour bed\n    difference (a linear sub-cell bed ramp; Casulli 2009 subgrid\n    bathymetry).  The mean sub-bottom is exactly b , so the\n    still-water volume is unchanged; only the partial-flooding\n    regime near eta≈b gains breakpoints ⇒ a coarse tidal flat\n    drains/floods SMOOTHLY (wet fraction ramps 1/n_sub per\n    breakpoint instead of a binary 0→1 cell jump).  On flat bed\n    ( half=0 ) ⇒ identical to \"flat\" .  Only consulted when si_wetdry=.true. and si_wetdry_nsub>=2 . integer, public :: si_wetdry_nsub = 1 Subgrid sub-bottoms per cell for the wet/dry volume function\n(>=1). 1 (default) = v1 flat cell bottoms (V piecewise-linear,\none breakpoint per cell). >=2 = the subgrid variant (a per-cell\ndepth distribution; see si_wetdry_bsub_fill ).  Only consulted\nwhen si_wetdry=.true. . character(len=16), public :: sim_type = \"coastal\" Simulation regime: “coastal” is the only supported value real(kind=wp), public :: smagorinsky_cs = 0.0_wp Smagorinsky horizontal viscosity coefficient for layer momentum. logical, public :: split_averaging = .true. ROMS-style time averaging over barotropic substeps integer, public :: split_ratio = 1 Barotropic-baroclinic split ratio: 0=auto, 1=unsplit, N>1=fixed real(kind=wp), public :: sponge_h_ref = 0.0_wp Sponge reference depth (m) real(kind=wp), public :: sponge_strength = 0.0_wp Sponge relaxation rate (1/s) integer, public :: sponge_width = 0 Sponge layer width in cells real(kind=wp), public :: status_interval = 0.0_wp Print status every N seconds of simulation time (0 = default every 100 steps) real(kind=wp), public :: t_end = 1.0_wp Simulation end time, interpreted in time_unit (default s). real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_amp (MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS) = 0.0_wp Constituent amplitudes (m) real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_amplitude = 0.0_wp Tidal elevation amplitude (m) — single-constituent legacy real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_omega (MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS) = 0.0_wp Constituent angular frequencies (rad/s) real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_period = 44712.0_wp Tidal period (s), default M2 = 12.42 h — single-constituent legacy real(kind=wp), public :: tidal_phase (MAX_TIDAL_CONSTITUENTS) = 0.0_wp Constituent phases (radians) character(len=16), public :: time_scheme = \"rk2\" Explicit time integrator (coastal 2D barotropic path):\n“euler” (1st), “rk2” (default, 2nd), “rk3” (3rd), “rk43”\n(3rd, SSP coeff 2 -> 2x dt).  All SSP for wet/dry positivity. character(len=8), public :: time_unit = \"s\" Unit applied to the long-time fields: t_end and status_interval (logging cadence). dt_fixed and dt_max stay in\nseconds — see their docstrings.  Read at namelist parse,\nthen multiplied through so the rest of the code keeps\nusing seconds internally.  Valid values: \"s\" , \"min\" , \"hr\" , \"day\" , \"year\" .  Year is 365.25 days (Julian,\nmatches MOM6 / UDUNITS convention).  Default \"s\" preserves backward compatibility — every existing nml is\nbit-identical. character(len=8), public :: tracer_recon = \"ppm\" Tracer horizontal-advection face reconstruction (structured coastal):\n“ppm” (default, CW84 PPM), “weno5” (Jiang-Shu 1996 + Borges 2008,\nnghost>=3), “weno7” (Balsara-Shu 2000, nghost>=4), “weno9”\n(Balsara-Shu 2000, nghost>=5). “pqm” is deferred.\nBit-identical to ppm when tracer_recon=”ppm”. logical, public :: use_hllc = .false. Use the HLLC approximate Riemann solver for the structured\nbarotropic flux instead of HLL.  HLLC adds a contact wave so\ntransverse momentum ( hv across an x-face, hu across a\ny-face) is upwinded across the shear interface; reduces\nnumerical diffusion for shear-aligned flow at the cost of\na few extra flops per face.  Default .false. (HLL). logical, public :: use_linear_bottom_drag = .false. Use linear (Rayleigh) bottom drag instead of quadratic Manning. logical, public :: use_multilayer = .false. Enable coupled hydrostatic vertical layers (alternative to NH) logical, public :: use_nonhydrostatic = .false. Enable multi-layer NH pressure correction logical, public :: use_ppm_tracer = .true. Use high-order tracer advection: PPM (structured) or MUSCL\n(unstructured). When false, falls back to first-order upwind. logical, public :: use_sediment = .false. Master switch for suspended-sediment transport. real(kind=wp), public :: vcoord_blend_width = 50.0_wp z-sigma hybrid: blending zone width (m) real(kind=wp), public :: vcoord_depth_transition = 100.0_wp z-sigma hybrid: depth (m) where blending starts character(len=16), public :: vcoord_type = \"sigma\" Vertical coordinate type: “sigma”, “zsigma”, “zstar”, etc. real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_nu_bg = 1.0e-4_wp Background vertical viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_nu_max = 0.01_wp Pacanowski-Philander max turbulent viscosity (m&#94;2/s) real(kind=wp), public :: vmix_ri_alpha = 5.0_wp Richardson number scaling coefficient (shared between momentum and tracers) logical, public :: vmix_use_keps = .false. Enable the two-equation k-epsilon vertical-mixing closure\n(rki_ml_keps).  Default off = PP81.  When on it overrides\nboth PP81 and the KPP overlay: the solver advances k/eps and\napplies the k-epsilon eddy viscosity to momentum (tracer\nmixing is wired in a later increment). logical, public :: vmix_use_kpp = .false. Enable the KPP (Large et al. 1994) surface-boundary-layer\noverlay on top of the PP81 interior closure.  Default off:\nthe coastal multilayer path runs pure PP81 (bit-identical\nto pre-KPP).  When on, the solver swaps the three PP81\nvmix calls for the KPP kernels (BL-depth + shape-function\nenhanced diffusivity + non-local transport). real(kind=wp), public :: wind_stress_x = 0.0_wp Surface wind stress in x-direction (Pa) real(kind=wp), public :: wind_stress_y = 0.0_wp Surface wind stress in y-direction (Pa) logical, public :: wind_surface_layer = .false. Apply surface wind stress to the top layer only (surface-\nconcentrated, generates vertical shear) instead of the\ndepth-uniform barotropic mode.  Multilayer (nz>1) only; off by\ndefault (= bit-identical depth-uniform forcing). real(kind=wp), public :: zstar_h_min = 1.0e-4_wp Vanishing-layer floor (m).  Layers that would land below the\nlocal bed get clipped to this thickness rather than going to zero. real(kind=wp), public :: zstar_h_surf_target = 0.0_wp Target physical thickness of the surface layer (m).\n0 => auto: fall back to the lite (uniform sigma) profile\nper column (effectively zstar-lite per-column).  Set > 0 to\nanchor the surface layer at a fixed thickness regardless of H. integer, public :: zstar_n_surf = 0 Number of “fine” near-surface layers using stretching.\n0 => auto (use max(1, nz/3)) character(len=16), public :: zstar_stretching = \"log\" Surface-concentration stretching: “log” | “uniform” Functions public pure function semi_implicit_grid_conflict (cfg) result(conflict) .true. when the config asks for time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\" on\nanything but an unstructured grid.  Semi-implicit stepping exists\nonly on the triangular backend; validate_config and the state\ninitialisers reject the combination. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg Return Value logical private pure function si_bc_supported (bc_str) result(ok) .true. iff the edge type is wired into the semi-implicit\neta-solve (2D and 3D-ML paths alike): wall (mirror ghost =>\nexact zero face flux) or the two Dirichlet-eta seeds (tidal /\nclamped).  Everything else (open/Flather, chapman, sponge,\nnested, inflow, discharge) fills ghost momentum the Helmholtz\noperator walls off => a silent mass leak; validate_config\naborts on those. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: bc_str Return Value logical Subroutines public  subroutine build_rakali_schema (cfg, schema) Register the validated groups + the still-external groups onto schema , capturing defaults from cfg . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(out) :: schema public  subroutine read_config (filename, cfg, schema) Read simulation configuration from a namelist file. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: filename Path to the namelist input file type( config_t ), intent(out), target :: cfg Populated configuration type( nml_schema_t ), intent(out), optional :: schema Built + parsed schema (aliases into cfg ); for doc dumps. public  subroutine read_config_from_string (text, cfg, schema) In-memory sibling of read_config : build + strict-parse +\napply a namelist held entirely in the text buffer (newline-\nseparated), with NO filesystem touch — no temp file, no chdir ,\nno cleanup.  Same validation + error-stop behaviour as the\nfile path (the schema parser runs from the in-memory line array). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text Whole namelist as one string (records separated by ‘\\n’). type( config_t ), intent(out), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(out), optional :: schema public  subroutine validate_config (cfg) Validate configuration parameters after reading Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in) :: cfg private  subroutine apply_time_unit_cascade (cfg) Post-parse time-unit fixup shared by the file + string config\npaths. t_end and status_interval are given\nin time_unit from &time_nml ; multiply through to SI seconds. dt_fixed / dt_max stay in seconds; default time_unit=\"s\" gives a 1× factor (bit-identical to before). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(inout) :: cfg private  subroutine read_config_from_string_impl (text, cfg, sch) Body of read_config_from_string — mirrors read_config_impl\nwith the line array replacing the file unit. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text type( config_t ), intent(out), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(out) :: sch private  subroutine read_config_impl (filename, cfg, sch) Body of read_config : build the strict schema (capturing\ndefaults from the pristine cfg field initialisers), parse the\nfile (validate + apply straight into cfg ), run the post-parse\ntime-unit cascade. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: filename Path to the namelist input file type( config_t ), intent(out), target :: cfg Populated configuration type( nml_schema_t ), intent(out) :: sch Built + parsed schema (aliases into cfg ) private  subroutine register_boundary (cfg, schema) &boundary_nml : per-side BC types, tidal forcing, inflow/\ndischarge/clamped/sponge/nesting parameters.  The four bc_* keys are enums over the bc_type_from_string accepted set. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_grid (cfg, schema) &grid_nml : structured-grid geometry. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_initial_condition (cfg, schema) &initial_condition_nml : coastal IC selector + parameters. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_logging (cfg, schema) &logging_nml : logger verbosity + status cadence. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_metadata (cfg, schema) &metadata_nml : CF-output global attributes. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_nonhydrostatic (cfg, schema) &nonhydrostatic_nml : NH/multilayer switches, CG-Poisson\ncontrols, PP81 vmix, KPP knobs, k-eps, Smagorinsky, BPG, mode\nsplit. keps_stability and bpg_method are enums. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_output (cfg, schema) &output_nml : file output + I/O + forcing/restart/gauge files. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_physics (cfg, schema) &physics_nml : barotropic physics + bottom drag + wind stress. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_si (cfg, schema) &si_nml : semi-implicit free-surface CG-solver controls.  Only\nconsulted when time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\" ; both knobs default\nto the pre-knob plain-CG behaviour (byte-identical). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_sim (cfg, schema) &sim_nml : the simulation regime selector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_time (cfg, schema) &time_nml : time-integration controls. t_end is interpreted\nin time_unit and converted to seconds by the post-parse\ncascade in read_config; dt_fixed / dt_max stay in seconds. time_unit is a plain string (the cascade validates its set). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_tracer (cfg, schema) &tracer_nml : salinity + temperature IC/EOS/bounds + sediment. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine register_vcoord (cfg, schema) &vcoord_nml : vertical-coordinate + ALE-remap controls. vcoord_type / remap_method / zstar_stretching are enums\nwith the canonical sets accepted by the rki_vcoord parsers. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( config_t ), intent(in), target :: cfg type( nml_schema_t ), intent(inout) :: schema private  subroutine split_to_lines (text, lines, n_lines) Split a newline-separated buffer into a fixed-len character array\n(one record per line, trailing CR stripped) for internal-file\nreads + the schema line walker. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text character(len=:), intent(out), allocatable :: lines (:) integer, intent(out) :: n_lines private  subroutine warn_unknown_bc (bc_str, param_name) Warn if a BC string does not match any known type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: bc_str character(len=*), intent(in) :: param_name","tags":"","url":"module/rki_config.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_dynamics – Rakali","text":"Barotropic-baroclinic coupling and vertical structure: distribute\nbarotropic acceleration to layers (preserving shear), maintain layer\nthickness (sigma constraint or vcoord remap), diagnostic w + interface\nmomentum exchange, layer-state RK2 plumbing and BC distribution.\nOwns the persistent vcoord-remap workspace; teardown via ml_dynamics_workspaces_cleanup . Uses rki_remap_column rki_vcoord rki_boundary_types rki_constants rki_grid rki_ml_common module~~rki_ml_dynamics~~UsesGraph module~rki_ml_dynamics rki_ml_dynamics module~rki_boundary_types rki_boundary_types module~rki_ml_dynamics->module~rki_boundary_ty