zontal_viscosity_unstr rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_keps_unstr rki_ml_keps_unstr module~rki_ml_keps_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr rki_ml_kpp_unstr module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_pressure_unstr rki_ml_pressure_unstr module~rki_ml_pressure_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_pressure_unstr->module~rki_ml_eos_unstr module~rki_ml_tracers_unstr rki_ml_tracers_unstr module~rki_ml_tracers_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_truncate_unstr rki_ml_truncate_unstr module~rki_ml_truncate_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr module~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_output_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_restart_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_si_unstr_step module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_eos_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_friction_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_keps_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_pressure_unstr module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml->module~rki_ml_tracers_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_flux_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_friction_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_fused_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_protect_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_kernel_update_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_eos_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_friction_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_keps_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_pressure_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_tracers_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_truncate_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr module~rki_solver_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_step_ml module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_handle Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: SI_PRECOND_JACOBI = 1 Diagonal (Jacobi) PCG: z = eta_diag*r.  Matters MORE on triangles\nthan on the structured grid — variable cell areas put real\ndisparity on the Helmholtz diagonal even at uniform depth\n(measured diag spread O(100-1000)x on a jittered basin;\n~2.5x iteration win — prototype study 4). integer, public, parameter :: SI_PRECOND_MG = 2 Aggregation (agglomeration) multigrid V(2,2)-cycle PCG — the triangle\nplateau-breaker ( rki_si_unstr_mg ).  Greedy pairwise cell-graph\ncoarsening + Galerkin coarse operators + damped-Jacobi smoothing;\nnumpy-prototype-validated to collapse the plain-CG plateau of\nthousands to tens of iters (Q12).  Opt-in; the hierarchy mg slot is\nbuilt at enable_si and refreshed once per step. integer, public, parameter :: SI_PRECOND_NONE = 0 Unpreconditioned CG (area-weighted plain CG). integer, private, parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 Triangles only. Derived Types type, public :: semi_implicit_state_unstr_t CG workspace + edge face-depths for the 2D free-surface Helmholtz\nsolve on the triangulation. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: Gbar_cell_x (:) Column-integrated predictor transport sum_k h_k G_k&#94;u\n(ncells_total) [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: Gbar_cell_y (:) Column-integrated y predictor transport (ncells_total) [m&#94;2/s]. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: Hf_edge (:,:) Edge effective depth (m), shape (3, ncells_total). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: Hhat_cell (:) Effective column depth Hhat = -sum_k h_k R_k (ncells_total) [m]. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: a_wet (:) Wet fraction a(eta) in [0,1] at the current Newton iterate. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: b_min (:) Deepest sub-bottom per cell (m) — the sill bed at edges. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: b_sub (:,:) Per-cell SORTED sub-bottom bed elevations (n_sub, ncells) (m). integer, public :: bsub_fill = 0 Sub-bottom fill mode ( SI_BSUB_FILL_* from rki_si_common; 0=FLAT\ndefault ⇒ bit-identical, 1=LINEAR ⇒ analytic subgrid ramp).  Set\nby state_unstr_enable_si . integer, public :: cg_iters = 0 CG iterations on the most recent step (go/no-go cost number). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: eta (:) Surface elevation eta&#94;{n+1} (m), size ncells_total.  eta = h + b\nat circumcentres.  Warm-started from eta&#94;n each step; the CG\niterate.  Boundary/halo entries hold the seeded Dirichlet ghost. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: eta_Ap (:) Operator apply A*p. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: eta_diag (:) 1/diag of the Helmholtz operator (Jacobi preconditioner). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: eta_ghost_edge (:,:) Dirichlet ghost surface eta (m) on tidal/clamped boundary edges,\nshape (3, ncells_total); 0 elsewhere (unread — Hf=0 there).\nFilled alongside Hf_edge each step (frozen, rule R2). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: eta_p (:) Search direction p. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: eta_r (:) Residual r = rhs - A*eta. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: eta_z (:) Preconditioned residual z = M&#94;{-1} r (Jacobi); unread on plain CG. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: g_col_u (:,:) Column x-velocity response G_k&#94;u = solve(u&#94;n + tendencies)\n(nz, ncells_total) [m/s]. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: g_col_v (:,:) Column y-velocity response G_k&#94;v (nz, ncells_total) [m/s]. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: mass_diag (:) Newton mass diagonal a+floor — the operator’s M term. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: mass_flux_edge (:,:) Blended column edge mass flux theta sum_k u_edge_layer +\n(1-theta) U&#94;n_e (EDGES_PER_TRI, ncells_total) [m&#94;2/s] — the\nEXACT flux the eta update used; drives the dsig tracer split. real(kind=wp), public :: mass_res = 0.0_wp Area-weighted interior residual sum at solve end (m&#94;3) — the\nper-step mass-consistency diagnostic. type( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), public :: mg Fine-to-coarse aggregation-MG level stack ( rki_si_unstr_mg ). integer, public :: n_sub = 1 Subgrid sub-bottoms per cell (1 = v1 flat bottom). integer, public :: ncells_total = 0 Cell count cached at init (all CG vectors are this long). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: newton_F (:) Nonlinear residual F = v + T*eta - rhs. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: newton_Jeta (:) Scratch for the full mass-diag operator apply J eta (the\nstiffness is recovered as J eta - mass_diag*eta). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: newton_dz (:) Newton increment: the inner CG solves J*dz = -F from zero. integer, public :: newton_iters = 0 Wet/dry Newton outer iterations on the most recent step (host\nscalar; read by tests / logging). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: nu_iface (:,:) PP81 interface viscosity (nz+1, ncells_total) [m&#94;2/s]; index k\n= interface BELOW layer k (bed row 1 and surface row nz+1 = 0). integer, public :: nz_si = 0 Layer count for the 3D SI path (0 or 1 = 2D-only; > 1 = the\nP3.2 multilayer column slots below are allocated). integer, public :: precond = SI_PRECOND_NONE Preconditioner ( SI_PRECOND_* ): NONE = plain CG (default),\nJACOBI = diagonal PCG, MG = aggregation-multigrid PCG. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: r_col (:,:) Column response R_k = solve(-1) (nz, ncells_total) [m/s]\n(<= 0); axis-independent — u and v share the tridiagonal. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: rhs_d (:) Depth-units Newton RHS v(eta&#94;n) - dt*div[blend] — held across\nthe Newton loop. real(kind=wp), public :: rtol = 1.0e-10_wp CG relative residual tolerance (area-weighted\n||r||&#94;2 < rtol&#94;2*||rhs||&#94;2). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: u_edge (:,:) Edge-normal transport (m&#94;2/s), shape (3, ncells_total); + along\nthe stored outward edge-normal. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: u_edge_layer (:,:,:) Recovered per-layer edge-normal transports\n(nz, EDGES_PER_TRI, ncells_total) [m&#94;2/s] — double-visit, same\noutward-normal convention as u_edge .  Column sums telescope to\nthe 2D back-substituted edge transport (mass consistency). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: u_n_edge (:,:) Saved U&#94;n edge transport (m&#94;2/s), shape (3, ncells_total) — the\n(1-theta) side of the theta-blend RHS; dead edges zeroed (R3). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: u_star (:,:) Predictor U*_e (m&#94;2/s), shape (3, ncells_total). logical, public :: use_mg = .false. MG preconditioner active (host scalar; set by enable_si). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: v_cell (:) Wetted mean depth v(eta) at the current iterate (m). logical, public :: wetdry = .false. Wet/dry mode on (host scalar; set by state_unstr_enable_si ). Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public, non_overridable :: build_mg => si_unstr_state_build_mg procedure, public, non_overridable :: destroy => si_unstr_state_destroy procedure, public, non_overridable :: enter_data => si_unstr_state_enter_data procedure, public, non_overridable :: exit_data => si_unstr_state_exit_data procedure, public, non_overridable :: init => si_unstr_state_init Functions public  function parse_si_precond_unstr (tag) result(precond) Map the &si_nml precond string to its SI_PRECOND_* enum on the\nunstructured path.  Fail-loud allowlist: an unknown tag aborts.  MG is\naggregation (agglomeration) multigrid here ( rki_si_unstr_mg ) — the\ntriangle plateau-breaker — NOT the structured geometric MG. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: tag Return Value integer Subroutines private  subroutine si_unstr_state_build_mg (this, mesh) Build the aggregation-MG preconditioner hierarchy for this state.\nHost-only; call from enable_si (after init , before enter_data )\nwhen precond == SI_PRECOND_MG .  Structure only (geometric\naggregation); the operator coefficients are filled by the first\nper-step refresh . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( semi_implicit_state_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh private  subroutine si_unstr_state_destroy (this) Deallocate all workspace arrays. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( semi_implicit_state_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine si_unstr_state_enter_data (this) Attach the workspace arrays to the device.  Arrays-only — the parent unstr_state_t is mapped by state_unstr_enter_data before this\nruns.  TBP wraps a non-polymorphic _impl (the class(...) box\nmaps to stack under AMD libomptarget; delegate to type(...) ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( semi_implicit_state_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine si_unstr_state_enter_data_impl (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( semi_implicit_state_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine si_unstr_state_exit_data (this) Detach the workspace arrays from the device. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( semi_implicit_state_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine si_unstr_state_exit_data_impl (this) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( semi_implicit_state_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine si_unstr_state_init (this, mesh, nz, wetdry, n_sub) Allocate workspace arrays at the mesh size, zero-filled.  When nz is present and > 1 the P3.2 (3D multilayer) column slots are also\nallocated; when wetdry is present and .true. the P3.3 Casulli\nwet/dry slots are (with n_sub sub-bottoms, default 1); otherwise\nonly the 2D barotropic slots exist and the 2D path is unchanged.\nPlain host allocation (runs before enter_data , so a device loop\nwould round-trip). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( semi_implicit_state_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh integer, intent(in), optional :: nz Number of vertical layers.  Absent or <= 1 selects the 2D path. logical, intent(in), optional :: wetdry Casulli wetting/drying on.  Absent/.false. => slots unallocated. integer, intent(in), optional :: n_sub Subgrid sub-bottoms per cell (>= 1).  Absent => 1 (flat bottom).","tags":"","url":"module/rki_si_unstr_state.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_friction – Rakali","text":"Source terms for the momentum and continuity equations:\nFriction -c_f u sqrt(u&#94;2+v&#94;2), c_f = g n&#94;2/h&#94;(1/3) (semi-implicit IMEX);\nwind tau_s/rho; pressure -(h/rho) grad(p_atm); rain dh/dt += P (all explicit). Uses rki_grid rki_constants module~~rki_kernel_friction~~UsesGraph module~rki_kernel_friction rki_kernel_friction module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_kernel_friction->module~rki_constants module~rki_grid rki_grid module~rki_kernel_friction->module~rki_grid pic_types pic_types module~rki_constants->pic_types module~rki_grid->module~rki_constants Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~rki_kernel_friction~~UsedByGraph module~rki_kernel_friction rki_kernel_friction module~rki_solver rki_solver module~rki_solver->module~rki_kernel_friction module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_solver module~rki_driver rki_driver module~rki_driver->module~rki_solver Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Subroutines public pure subroutine apply_coriolis (h, hu, hv, grid, dt, f) Apply Coriolis via the exact (energy-conserving) rotation:\n  hu_new =  hu cos(f dt) + hv sin(f dt)\n  hv_new = -hu sin(f dt) + hv cos(f dt) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: h (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu (:,:) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv (:,:) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: f public pure subroutine apply_friction (h, hu, hv, grid, dt, manning_n, wind_x, wind_y, atm_pressure, precipitation, forcing_active, include_wind) Apply bottom friction, wind stress, atmospheric pressure gradient,\nand precipitation to (h, hu, hv). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: h (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hu (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: hv (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) type( hgrid_t ), intent(in) :: grid real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dt Timestep (s) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: manning_n Manning roughness coefficient (s/m&#94;{1/3}) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_x (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: wind_y (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: atm_pressure (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: precipitation (grid%nx_total,grid%ny_total) logical, intent(in), optional :: forcing_active When .false., skip wind/pressure/precipitation (default: .true.) logical, intent(in), optional :: include_wind When .false., skip the wind stress (it is applied to the surface\nlayer instead — wind_surface_layer).  Default: .true.","tags":"","url":"module/rki_kernel_friction.html"},{"title":"rki_mesh_unstr – Rakali","text":"Cell-centric unstructured mesh, flat 1D layout. Stores per-cell geometry (centroid, area, CFL radius) and\nper-edge-of-cell quantities (length, outward normal, midpoint, neighbour\ncell, neighbour-side edge index, boundary group). Edges are implicit:\nevery triangle has exactly three edges, indexed locally as i in 1..3.\nEdge i is the edge opposite local vertex i. Per-edge-of-cell arrays use shape (3, ncells_total) so the three\nedges of cell k are contiguous in memory and the cell index is the\nslow-varying (column-major) axis – the natural Fortran layout for\na do concurrent (k = 1:ncells_owned) hot loop. All cells are owned ( ncells_owned == ncells_total ). Geometry is built\nonce at init and never modified during the run. Uses pic_types pic_io rki_constants pic_logger module~~rki_mesh_unstr~~UsesGraph module~rki_mesh_unstr rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_constants rki_constants module~rki_mesh_unstr->module~rki_constants pic_io pic_io m