str module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_multilayer_state_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_si_unstr_state module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_state_unstr->module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr module~rki_surface_forcing_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_tracer_unstr->module~rki_mesh_unstr module~rki_api rki_api module~rki_api->module~rki_handle module~rki_ml_friction_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_keps_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_kpp_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr module~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr->module~rki_state_unstr proc~si_unstr_cg_solve si_unstr_cg_solve proc~si_unstr_cg_solve->module~rki_si_unstr_state Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private, parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 Triangles only. real(kind=wp), private, parameter :: SI_MAX_DEV_ANGLE_DEG = 5.0_wp Fail-loud ceiling on the max circumcentre-line deviation angle for\nthe semi-implicit TPFA operator.  A clean Delaunay mesh measures\n< 1e-2 deg (edge orthogonal to the circumcentre line by\nconstruction); anything above 5 deg means a non-Delaunay / corrupted\ntriangulation that TPFA would solve inconsistently — abort at\nconfigure rather than silently return a subtly-wrong eta. Derived Types type, public :: mesh_unstr_t Triangular mesh in flat layout. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: area (:) Cell area, size ncells_total. integer, public, allocatable :: bc_group (:,:) Boundary group id on edge i of cell k, 0 on interior edges. integer(kind=int64), public, allocatable :: cell_global_id (:) Cell ids 1..ncells_total , written to the output / restart\nfiles. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: centroid_x (:) Cell centroid x, size ncells_total. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: centroid_y (:) Cell centroid y, size ncells_total. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: circumcentre_x (:) Cell circumcentre x, size ncells_total.  eta lives here on the\nSI path.  Computed from the three vertices in compute_geometry . real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: circumcentre_y (:) Cell circumcentre y, size ncells_total. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: edge_delta (:,:) Circumcentre-to-circumcentre distance across edge i of cell k,\nshape (3, ncells_total) (m).  Interior edge: |cc(nbr) - cc(k)|.\nBoundary edge: circumcentre-to-edge-midpoint distance (the\nDirichlet ghost sits at the mirror across the edge).  The TPFA\ntransmissibility is Hf * edge_len / edge_delta .  Built in a\nsecond pass ( compute_si_geometry ) once neighbours are known. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: edge_dev_angle (:,:) Deviation angle (degrees) between the outward edge-normal and the\ncircumcentre line across edge i of cell k, shape (3, ncells_total).\n0 = orthogonal (ideal Delaunay).  The mesh-quality-gate metric;\nboundary edges carry 0 (not meaningful for the Dirichlet ghost). real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: edge_len (:,:) Length of edge i of cell k. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: edge_mid_x (:,:) Edge midpoint x. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: edge_mid_y (:,:) Edge midpoint y. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: edge_n1 (:,:) Outward unit normal x-component for edge i of cell k. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: edge_n2 (:,:) Outward unit normal y-component for edge i of cell k. real(kind=wp), public :: max_dev_angle = 0.0_wp Max interior edge_dev_angle over the owned cells (degrees) — the\nfail-loud quality-gate scalar (abort if > ~5 deg on the SI path). real(kind=wp), public :: min_edge_delta = 0.0_wp Smallest SIGNED circumcentre-line projection on the outward\nedge-normal over the owned interior edges (m) — the quality-gate\nscalar.  Non-positive = a degenerate (coincident circumcentres,\nright-triangle split) or locally non-Delaunay (flipped) pair =>\nzero / wrong-signed TPFA transmissibility => abort. integer, public, allocatable :: n_boundaries (:) Number of boundary edges on each cell, 0..3, size ncells_total. integer, public :: n_boundary_edges = 0 Total boundary edges across owned cells. integer, public :: ncells_owned = 0 Number of cells (live at indices 1..ncells_owned). integer, public :: ncells_total = 0 Equal to ncells_owned . integer, public, allocatable :: neighbour_edges (:,:) Local edge index (1..3) of the neighbour that matches edge i\nof cell k, or -1 on a physical boundary. integer, public, allocatable :: neighbours (:,:) Neighbouring cell index across edge i of cell k, or -1 if the\nedge is on a physical boundary. integer, public :: nverts = 0 Number of unique vertices. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: radius (:) Inscribed-circle radius, size ncells_total. Used as the CFL\nlength scale for CFL computation. integer, public, allocatable :: surrogate_neighbours (:,:) Same as neighbours, but k itself if the edge is a physical\nboundary. Used by the gradient stencil so the reconstruction\nkernel never branches on boundaries. integer, public, allocatable :: tri_v (:,:) Vertex ids of each triangle, shape (3, ncells_total). Ordered\ncounter-clockwise; local vertex i is opposite local edge i. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: vert_x (:) Vertex x coordinate, size nverts. real(kind=wp), public, allocatable :: vert_y (:) Vertex y coordinate, size nverts. Subroutines public  subroutine mesh_unstr_destroy (mesh) Release all allocatable arrays. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: mesh public  subroutine mesh_unstr_enter_data (mesh) Map the read-only mesh geometry and topology arrays into device\nmemory. Called once at solver init alongside state_unstr_enter_data . Vertex coords + raw triangle vertex\nlist stay host-only (kernels never read them after init). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: mesh public  subroutine mesh_unstr_exit_data (mesh) Release the device copies of the mesh arrays. Counterpart to mesh_unstr_enter_data . Mesh data is read-only on the device,\nso nothing needs to be copied back. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: mesh public  subroutine mesh_unstr_init_from_triangles (mesh, vert_x, vert_y, tri_v, bc_tags) Build a mesh_unstr_t from raw vertex coordinates and triangle\nvertex lists. Computes geometry, neighbour topology and the\nsurrogate-neighbour table. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(out) :: mesh real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: vert_x (:) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: vert_y (:) integer, intent(in) :: tri_v (:,:) integer, intent(in), optional :: bc_tags (:,:) public  subroutine mesh_unstr_si_quality_gate (mesh, ok) Fail-loud mesh-quality gate for the semi-implicit TPFA operator\n(Casulli & Walters 2000 orthogonal-centre requirement, made\nexplicit).  Aborts via ok=.false. (the caller error-stops) when\neither\n  * the max circumcentre-line deviation angle exceeds SI_MAX_DEV_ANGLE_DEG (a non-Delaunay / corrupted mesh), or\n  * the smallest interior edge_delta is non-positive (an obtuse\n    triangle put its circumcentre outside itself => a flipped /\n    zero transmissibility K_e = Hf*len/delta ).\nA clean Delaunay mesh (meshpy/pymetis pipeline) passes trivially. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(in) :: mesh logical, intent(out) :: ok private  subroutine build_neighbours (mesh) Build the neighbours / neighbour_edges tables by matching edges\nthat share the same unordered vertex pair. Uses a single sort of\n64-bit composite keys instead of a hash table – O(M log M) where\nM = 3 * ncells_total, and avoids dragging in any container code. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: mesh private  subroutine build_surrogate_neighbours (mesh) Surrogate neighbours: same as neighbours but the cell itself\nstands in for boundary edges. Lets the gradient\nkernel index neighbour values without branching on -1.\nFilled for every cell – halo cells included – so that any\nkernel that happens to dereference surrogate_neighbours(:, k) for a halo k still gets a valid index. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: mesh private  subroutine compute_geometry (mesh) Compute per-cell area, centroid, CFL radius, and per-edge\nlength, outward normal, and midpoint for every cell – owned\nAND halo. Halo cells need real geometry too because the\nreconstruction kernel reads neighbour centroids when computing\nedge values across partition edges. Edge i is opposite local\nvertex i; in CCW orientation that gives an outward normal. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: mesh private  subroutine compute_si_geometry (mesh) Fill the semi-implicit TPFA edge geometry: the circumcentre-to-\ncircumcentre distance edge_delta and the edge/centre-line\ndeviation angle edge_dev_angle for every edge of every cell, plus\nthe mesh-wide quality-gate scalars max_dev_angle / min_edge_delta over the OWNED interior edges.  Runs after build_neighbours so\nneighbour circumcentres are available.  Host-only (init-time; the\ndevice never re-derives geometry). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mesh_unstr_t ), intent(inout) :: mesh private  subroutine count_boundary_edges (mesh) Tally n_boundaries(k) for every cell (owned AND halo) and\nthe total boundary-edge count across owned cells. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional A