d-configurable via `-DRAKALI_BPG_NZ_MAX=<n>` (CMake cache !! variable, plumbed as the `RKI_BPG_NZ_MAX` preprocessor define; !! default 20). !! !! **The requirement is `BPG_NZ_MAX >= nz + 1`** — see !! `bpg_nz_required` below for the derivation and the survey of !! every consumer.  Enforced fail-loud by `validate_config`. contains pure function bpg_nz_required ( nz ) result ( req ) !! Smallest `BPG_NZ_MAX` that safely covers an unstructured !! multilayer run of `nz` layers. !! !! `nz + 1`.  Derived from a survey (2026-08) of every !! `BPG_NZ_MAX`-dimensioned local in the unstructured kernels; the !! binding consumer is the one that indexes a plainly-`BPG_NZ_MAX` !! array to `nz + 1` rather than the `BPG_NZ_MAX + 1` an interface !! array would use: !! !!   * `rki_ml_keps_unstr` `ml_keps_update_unstr_impl` !!     `S2`/`N2`/`dz_if`/`a`/`b`/`c`/`rhs`/`cp` — written and read !!     at `ni = nz + 1` (interface-indexed; `keps_tridiag_solve_u` !!     touches rows `1..ni` of all five solver arrays). !! !! Every other consumer needs only `nz`: !! !!   * `rki_ml_pressure_unstr` `p_int`/`p_int_nbr` — max index `nz` !!     (the interface arrays `z_if`/`p_if`/`zn_if_e`/`pn_if_e` are !!     declared `BPG_NZ_MAX + 1` and carry their own slack). !!   * `rki_ml_tracers_unstr` `v_layer`/`hf_layer`/`frac` — max !!     `nz`; `flux_iface` — max `nz - 1`. !!   * `rki_ml_dynamics_unstr`, `rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr`, !!     `rki_ml_kpp_unstr` `flux_*_iface` — max `nz - 1`. !!   * `rki_ml_keps_unstr` momentum/tracer applies !!     `a`/`b`/`c`/`ru`/`rv`/`r`/`cp` — max `nz`. integer , intent ( in ) :: nz integer :: req req = nz + 1 end function bpg_nz_required pure function bpg_nz_is_sufficient ( nz ) result ( ok ) !! `.true.` when the COMPILED `BPG_NZ_MAX` covers `nz` layers on !! the unstructured multilayer path.  Callers that get `.false.` !! must refuse the run: exceeding the bound is NOT a crash — the !! unstructured BPG kernels silently return (no baroclinic !! pressure gradient at all) and the unguarded column kernels !! silently overrun thread-local storage. integer , intent ( in ) :: nz logical :: ok ok = bpg_nz_required ( nz ) <= BPG_NZ_MAX end function bpg_nz_is_sufficient end module rki_ml_common_unstr","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_ml_common_unstr.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_flux.F90 – Rakali","text":"HLL / HLLC Riemann solver with hydrostatic reconstruction and minmod limiter This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_kernel_flux.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_flux.f90 rki_kernel_flux.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_flux.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_flux.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_kernel_flux.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_flux.f90 rki_kernel_flux.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 rki_solver.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_flux.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! HLL / HLLC Riemann solver with hydrostatic reconstruction and minmod limiter module rki_kernel_flux !! Net flux divergence for the shallow water equations via HLL or HLLC !! Riemann solver with hydrostatic reconstruction (Audusse et al. 2004) !! and minmod slope-limited reconstruction. HLL/HLLC differ only in the !! transverse momentum flux. Free surface eta = h + B is reconstructed !! (not h) for the well-balanced property. use rki_constants , only : wp , GRAVITY , DRY_TOLERANCE , THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD use rki_grid , only : hgrid_t implicit none private public :: compute_flux_hll , compute_flux_hllc contains pure subroutine compute_flux_hll ( h , hu , hv , b , flux_h , flux_hu , flux_hv , & mass_flux_x , mass_flux_y , grid ) !! Net flux divergence at each interior cell (HLL Riemann solver). !! Also writes the per-face HLL h-flux at the right face !! `mass_flux_x(i, j)` and top face `mass_flux_y(i, j)`, reused by !! the multilayer tracer kernels for consistency-with-continuity (CWC). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & b ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: flux_h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & flux_hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & flux_hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: mass_flux_x ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & mass_flux_y ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) integer :: i , j , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: dx , dy real ( wp ) :: fh , fhu , fhv , fmxL , fmxR , fmyB , fmyT logical , parameter :: use_hllc = . false . nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost dx = grid % dx dy = grid % dy do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( fh , fhu , fhv , fmxL , fmxR , fmyB , fmyT ) call flux_cell ( h , hu , hv , b , nx , ny , i , j , dx , dy , use_hllc , & fh , fhu , fhv , fmxL , fmxR , fmyB , fmyT ) flux_h ( i , j ) = fh flux_hu ( i , j ) = fhu flux_hv ( i , j ) = fhv ! mass_flux_x(i, j) = right face of cell i (face i+1/2); the ! leftmost interior cell also writes its left face into (i-1, j). mass_flux_x ( i , j ) = fmxR mass_flux_y ( i , j ) = fmyT if ( i == nghost + 1 ) mass_flux_x ( i - 1 , j ) = fmxL if ( j == nghost + 1 ) mass_flux_y ( i , j - 1 ) = fmyB end do end subroutine compute_flux_hll pure subroutine compute_flux_hllc ( h , hu , hv , b , flux_h , flux_hu , flux_hv , & mass_flux_x , mass_flux_y , grid ) !! Net flux divergence at each interior cell (HLLC Riemann solver). !! h/hu flux and `mass_flux_x/y` match the HLL version; only the !! transverse momentum flux differs. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & b ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: flux_h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & flux_hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & flux_hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: mass_flux_x ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ), & mass_flux_y ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) integer :: i , j , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: dx , dy real ( wp ) :: fh , fhu , fhv , fmxL , fmxR , fmyB , fmyT logical , parameter :: use_hllc = . true . nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost dx = grid % dx dy = grid % dy do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( fh , fhu , fhv , fmxL , fmxR , fmyB , fmyT ) call flux_cell ( h , hu , hv , b , nx , ny , i , j , dx , dy , use_hllc , & fh , fhu , fhv , fmxL , fmxR , fmyB , fmyT ) flux_h ( i , j ) = fh flux_hu ( i , j ) = fhu flux_hv ( i , j ) = fhv mass_flux_x ( i , j ) = fmxR mass_flux_y ( i , j ) = fmyT if ( i == nghost + 1 ) mass_flux_x ( i - 1 , j ) = fmxL if ( j == nghost + 1 ) mass_flux_y ( i , j - 1 ) = fmyB end do end subroutine compute_flux_hllc pure subroutine flux_cell ( h , hu , hv , b , nx , ny , i , j , dx , dy , use_hllc , & out_fh , out_fhu , out_fhv , & out_fmass_xL , out_fmass_xR , & out_fmass_yB , out_fmass_yT ) !! Net flux divergence for a single cell (i, j). Also returns the !! four per-face HLL h-fluxes for the multilayer tracer kernels' CWC. integer , intent ( in ) :: nx , ny , i , j real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h ( nx , ny ), hu ( nx , ny ), hv ( nx , ny ), b ( nx , ny ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dx , dy logical , intent ( in ) :: use_hllc !! Selects the Riemann solver. Passed as a literal constant from !! the two entry points, so the in-kernel branch constant-folds. real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: out_fh , out_fhu , out_fhv real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: out_fmass_xL !! HLL h-flux at left face (i-1/2). real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: out_fmass_xR !! HLL h-flux at right face (i+1/2). real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: out_fmass_yB !! HLL h-flux at bottom face (j-1/2). real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: out_fmass_yT !! HLL h-flux at top face (j+1/2). real ( wp ) :: eta_c , eta_im1 , eta_ip1 , eta_im2 , eta_ip2 real ( wp ) :: eta_jm1 , eta_jp1 , eta_jm2 , eta_jp2 real ( wp ) :: seta_x , shu_x , shv_x , seta_y , shu_y , shv_y real ( wp ) :: seta_x_nb , shu_x_nb , shv_x_nb real ( wp ) :: seta_y_nb , shu_y_nb , shv_y_nb real ( wp ) :: eta_L , eta_R , hu_L , hv_L , hu_R , hv_R real ( wp ) :: h_L , h_R real ( wp ) :: b_max , h_hyd_l , h_hyd_r real ( wp ) :: u_l , v_l , u_r , v_r real ( wp ) :: fx_h_l , fx_hu_l , fx_hv_l real ( wp ) :: fx_h_r , fx_hu_r , fx_hv_r real ( wp ) :: fy_h_b , fy_hu_b , fy_hv_b real ( wp ) :: fy_h_t , fy_hu_t , fy_hv_t real ( wp ) :: h_hyd_left , h_pre_left real ( wp ) :: h_hyd_right , h_pre_right real ( wp ) :: h_hyd_bottom , h_pre_bottom real ( wp ) :: h_hyd_top , h_pre_top real ( wp ) :: half_g half_g = 0.5_wp * GRAVITY ! Precompute free surface eta = h + B eta_c = h ( i , j ) + b ( i , j ) eta_im1 = h ( i - 1 , j ) + b ( i - 1 , j ) eta_ip1 = h ( i + 1 , j ) + b ( i + 1 , j ) eta_im2 = h ( i - 2 , j ) + b ( i - 2 , j ) eta_ip2 = h ( i + 2 , j ) + b ( i + 2 , j ) eta_jm1 = h ( i , j - 1 ) + b ( i , j - 1 ) eta_jp1 = h ( i , j + 1 ) + b ( i , j + 1 ) eta_jm2 = h ( i , j - 2 ) + b ( i , j - 2 ) eta_jp2 = h ( i , j + 2 ) + b ( i , j + 2 ) ! Fall back to first-order (zero slopes) near wet/dry fronts. if ( h ( i , j ) < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD & . or . h ( i - 1 , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE & . or . h ( i + 1 , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then seta_x = 0.0_wp shu_x = 0.0_wp shv_x = 0.0_wp else seta_x = minmod ( eta_c - eta_im1 , eta_ip1 - eta_c ) shu_x = minmod ( hu ( i , j ) - hu ( i - 1 , j ), hu ( i + 1 , j ) - hu ( i , j )) shv_x = minmod ( hv ( i , j ) - hv ( i - 1 , j ), hv ( i + 1 , j ) - hv ( i , j )) end if if ( h ( i , j ) < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD & . or . h ( i , j - 1 ) < DRY_TOLERANCE & . or . h ( i , j + 1 ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then seta_y = 0.0_wp shu_y = 0.0_wp shv_y = 0.0_wp else seta_y = minmod ( eta_c - eta_jm1 , eta_jp1 - eta_c ) shu_y = minmod ( hu ( i , j ) - hu ( i , j - 1 ), hu ( i , j + 1 ) - hu ( i , j )) shv_y = minmod ( hv ( i , j ) - hv ( i , j - 1 ), hv ( i , j + 1 ) - hv ( i , j )) end if ! ============================================================ ! x-direction: LEFT interface (i-1/2) ! ============================================================ eta_R = eta_c - 0.5_wp * seta_x hu_R = hu ( i , j ) - 0.5_wp * shu_x hv_R = hv ( i , j ) - 0.5_wp * shv_x h_R = max ( 0.0_wp , eta_R - b ( i , j )) h_pre_left = h_R if ( h ( i - 1 , j ) < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD & . or . h ( i - 2 , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE & . or . h ( i , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then seta_x_nb = 0.0_wp shu_x_nb = 0.0_wp shv_x_nb = 0.0_wp else seta_x_nb = minmod ( eta_im1 - eta_im2 , eta_c - eta_im1 ) shu_x_nb = minmod ( hu ( i - 1 , j ) - hu ( i - 2 , j ), hu ( i , j ) - hu ( i - 1 , j )) shv_x_nb = minmod ( hv ( i - 1 , j ) - hv ( i - 2 , j ), hv ( i , j ) - hv ( i - 1 , j )) end if eta_L = eta_im1 + 0.5_wp * seta_x_nb hu_L = hu ( i - 1 , j ) + 0.5_wp * shu_x_nb hv_L = hv ( i - 1 , j ) + 0.5_wp * shv_x_nb h_L = max ( 0.0_wp , eta_L - b ( i - 1 , j )) b_max = max ( b ( i - 1 , j ), b ( i , j )) h_hyd_l = max ( 0.0_wp , h_L + b ( i - 1 , j ) - b_max ) h_hyd_r = max ( 0.0_wp , h_R + b ( i , j ) - b_max ) h_hyd_left = h_hyd_r call extract_velocity ( h_L , hu_L , hv_L , u_l , v_l ) call extract_velocity ( h_R , hu_R , hv_R , u_r , v_r ) if ( use_hllc ) then call hllc_flux_x ( h_hyd_l , h_hyd_l * u_l , h_hyd_l * v_l , & h_hyd_r , h_hyd_r * u_r , h_hyd_r * v_r , & fx_h_l , fx_hu_l , fx_hv_l ) else call hll_flux_x ( h_hyd_l , h_hyd_l * u_l , h_hyd_l * v_l , & h_hyd_r , h_hyd_r * u_r , h_hyd_r * v_r , & fx_h_l , fx_hu_l , fx_hv_l ) end if ! ============================================================ ! x-direction: RIGHT interface (i+1/2) ! ============================================================ eta_L = eta_c + 0.5_wp * seta_x hu_L = hu ( i , j ) + 0.5_wp * shu_x hv_L = hv ( i , j ) + 0.5_wp * shv_x h_L = max ( 0.0_wp , eta_L - b ( i , j )) h_pre_right = h_L if ( h ( i + 1 , j ) < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD & . or . h ( i , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE & . or . h ( i + 2 , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then seta_x_nb = 0.0_wp shu_x_nb = 0.0_wp shv_x_nb = 0.0_wp else seta_x_nb = minmod ( eta_ip1 - eta_c , eta_ip2 - eta_ip1 ) shu_x_nb = minmod ( hu ( i + 1 , j ) - hu ( i , j ), hu ( i + 2 , j ) - hu ( i + 1 , j )) shv_x_nb = minmod ( hv ( i + 1 , j ) - hv ( i , j ), hv ( i + 2 , j ) - hv ( i + 1 , j )) end if eta_R = eta_ip1 - 0.5_wp * seta_x_nb hu_R = hu ( i + 1 , j ) - 0.5_wp * shu_x_nb hv_R = hv ( i + 1 , j ) - 0.5_wp * shv_x_nb h_R = max ( 0.0_wp , eta_R - b ( i + 1 , j )) b_max = max ( b ( i , j ), b ( i + 1 , j )) h_hyd_l = max ( 0.0_wp , h_L + b ( i , j ) - b_max ) h_hyd_r = max ( 0.0_wp , h_R + b ( i + 1 , j ) - b_max ) h_hyd_right = h_hyd_l call extract_velocity ( h_L , hu_L , hv_L , u_l , v_l ) call extract_velocity ( h_R , hu_R , hv_R , u_r , v_r ) if ( use_hllc ) then call hllc_flux_x ( h_hyd_l , h_hyd_l * u_l , h_hyd_l * v_l , & h_hyd_r , h_hyd_r * u_r , h_hyd_r * v_r , & fx_h_r , fx_hu_r , fx_hv_r ) else call hll_flux_x ( h_hyd_l , h_hyd_l * u_l , h_hyd_l * v_l , & h_hyd_r , h_hyd_r * u_r , h_hyd_r * v_r , & fx_h_r , fx_hu_r , fx_hv_r ) end if ! ============================================================ ! y-direction: BOTTOM interface (j-1/2) ! ============================================================ eta_R = eta_c - 0.5_wp * seta_y hu_R = hu ( i , j ) - 0.5_wp * shu_y hv_R = hv ( i , j ) - 0.5_wp * shv_y h_R = max ( 0.0_wp , eta_R - b ( i , j )) h_pre_bottom = h_R if ( h ( i , j - 1 ) < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD & . or . h ( i , j - 2 ) < DRY_TOLERANCE & . or . h ( i , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then seta_y_nb = 0.0_wp shu_y_nb = 0.0_wp shv_y_nb = 0.0_wp else seta_y_nb = minmod ( eta_jm1 - eta_jm2 , eta_c - eta_jm1 ) shu_y_nb = minmod ( hu ( i , j - 1 ) - hu ( i , j - 2 ), hu ( i , j ) - hu ( i , j - 1 )) shv_y_nb = minmod ( hv ( i , j - 1 ) - hv ( i , j - 2 ), hv ( i , j ) - hv ( i , j - 1 )) end if eta_L = eta_jm1 + 0.5_wp * seta_y_nb hu_L = hu ( i , j - 1 ) + 0.5_wp * shu_y_nb hv_L = hv ( i , j - 1 ) + 0.5_wp * shv_y_nb h_L = max ( 0.0_wp , eta_L - b ( i , j - 1 )) b_max = max ( b ( i , j - 1 ), b ( i , j )) h_hyd_l = max ( 0.0_wp , h_L + b ( i , j - 1 ) - b_max ) h_hyd_r = max ( 0.0_wp , h_R + b ( i , j ) - b_max ) h_hyd_bottom = h_hyd_r call extract_velocity ( h_L , hu_L , hv_L , u_l , v_l ) call extract_velocity ( h_R , hu_R , hv_R , u_r , v_r ) if ( use_hllc ) then call hllc_flux_y ( h_hyd_l , h_hyd_l * u_l , h_hyd_l * v_l , & h_hyd_r , h_hyd_r * u_r , h_hyd_r * v_r , & fy_h_b , fy_hu_b , fy_hv_b ) else call hll_flux_y ( h_hyd_l , h_hyd_l * u_l , h_hyd_l * v_l , & h_hyd_r , h_hyd_r * u_r , h_hyd_r * v_r , & fy_h_b , fy_hu_b , fy_hv_b ) end if ! ============================================================ ! y-direction: TOP interface (j+1/2) ! ============================================================ eta_L = eta_c + 0.5_wp * seta_y hu_L = hu ( i , j ) + 0.5_wp * shu_y hv_L = hv ( i , j ) + 0.5_wp * shv_y h_L = max ( 0.0_wp , eta_L - b ( i , j )) h_pre_top = h_L if ( h ( i , j + 1 ) < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD & . or . h ( i , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE & . or . h ( i , j + 2 ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then seta_y_nb = 0.0_wp shu_y_nb = 0.0_wp shv_y_nb = 0.0_wp else seta_y_nb = minmod ( eta_jp1 - eta_c , eta_jp2 - eta_jp1 ) shu_y_nb = minmod ( hu ( i , j + 1 ) - hu ( i , j ), hu ( i , j + 2 ) - hu ( i , j + 1 )) shv_y_nb = minmod ( hv ( i , j + 1 ) - hv ( i , j ), hv ( i , j + 2 ) - hv ( i , j + 1 )) end if eta_R = eta_jp1 - 0.5_wp * seta_y_nb hu_R = hu ( i , j + 1 ) - 0.5_wp * shu_y_nb hv_R = hv ( i , j + 1 ) - 0.5_wp * shv_y_nb h_R = max ( 0.0_wp , eta_R - b ( i , j + 1 )) b_max = max ( b ( i , j ), b ( i , j + 1 )) h_hyd_l = max ( 0.0_wp , h_L + b ( i , j ) - b_max ) h_hyd_r = max ( 0.0_wp , h_R + b ( i , j + 1 ) - b_max ) h_hyd_top = h_hyd_l call extract_velocity ( h_L , hu_L , hv_L , u_l , v_l ) call extract_velocity ( h_R , hu_R , hv_R , u_r , v_r ) if ( use_hllc ) then call hllc_flux_y ( h_hyd_l , h_hyd_l * u_l , h_hyd_l * v_l , & h_hyd_r , h_hyd_r * u_r , h_hyd_r * v_r , & fy_h_t , fy_hu_t , fy_hv_t ) else call hll_flux_y ( h_hyd_l , h_hyd_l * u_l , h_hyd_l * v_l , & h_hyd_r , h_hyd_r * u_r , h_hyd_r * v_r , & fy_h_t , fy_hu_t , fy_hv_t ) end if ! ============================================================ ! Net flux divergence with well-balanced correction ! ============================================================ out_fh = - ( fx_h_r - fx_h_l ) / dx & - ( fy_h_t - fy_h_b ) / dy out_fhu = - ( fx_hu_r - fx_hu_l ) / dx & - ( fy_hu_t - fy_hu_b ) / dy & - half_g * ( h_hyd_left ** 2 - h_pre_left ** 2 & - h_hyd_right ** 2 + h_pre_right ** 2 ) / dx out_fhv = - ( fx_hv_r - fx_hv_l ) / dx & - ( fy_hv_t - fy_hv_b ) / dy & - half_g * ( h_hyd_bottom ** 2 - h_pre_bottom ** 2 & - h_hyd_top ** 2 + h_pre_top ** 2 ) / dy ! Per-face HLL mass fluxes (each interior face computed twice but ! symmetric, so values match exactly). out_fmass_xL = fx_h_l out_fmass_xR = fx_h_r out_fmass_yB = fy_h_b out_fmass_yT = fy_h_t end subroutine flux_cell pure function minmod ( a , b ) result ( m ) !! Minmod slope limiter real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: a , b real ( wp ) :: m if ( a * b <= 0.0_wp ) then m = 0.0_wp else if ( abs ( a ) < abs ( b )) then m = a else m = b end if end function minmod pure subroutine extract_velocity ( h_val , hu_val , hv_val , u_val , v_val ) !! Extract velocity from conserved variables, handling dry cells real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_val , hu_val , hv_val real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: u_val , v_val if ( h_val > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_val = hu_val / h_val v_val = hv_val / h_val else u_val = 0.0_wp v_val = 0.0_wp end if end subroutine extract_velocity pure subroutine hll_flux_x ( h_l , hu_l , hv_l , h_r , hu_r , hv_r , & f_h , f_hu , f_hv ) !! HLL numerical flux in x-direction between left and right states real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_l , hu_l , hv_l real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_r , hu_r , hv_r real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: f_h , f_hu , f_hv real ( wp ) :: u_l , u_r , v_l , v_r , a_l , a_r real ( wp ) :: s_l , s_r , denom real ( wp ) :: fl_h , fl_hu , fl_hv real ( wp ) :: fr_h , fr_hu , fr_hv if ( h_l > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_l = hu_l / h_l v_l = hv_l / h_l else u_l = 0.0_wp v_l = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_r > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_r = hu_r / h_r v_r = hv_r / h_r else u_r = 0.0_wp v_r = 0.0_wp end if a_l = sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( h_l , 0.0_wp )) a_r = sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( h_r , 0.0_wp )) ! Wave-speed estimate.  Davis (min/max of the one-sided speeds) is right ! for a genuine two-sided WET Riemann problem, but wrong at a wet/dry ! front and must be replaced there. ! ! With the right state dry, `a_R = 0` and `u_R = 0`, so Davis returns ! `s_r = u_L + a_L`.  The exact dry-front speed is `u_L + 2 a_L` — the ! Ritter (1892) result — so Davis underestimates the right-going wave by ! up to a factor of two and the front cannot advance at the right rate. ! The dry-state speeds below are the standard fix (Toro, \"Riemann ! Solvers and Numerical Methods for Fluid Dynamics\", 3rd ed. S10.4; ! Einfeldt et al. 1991). ! ! Measured consequence before this branch existed: the Ritter dry-bed ! tip advanced at 1.49 c0 rather than 2 c0, the leading tongue below ! ~1 % of the upstream depth was absent, and on a sloping beach a thin ! film would not recede at all (validation phases 4 and 5). if ( h_r <= DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry on the RIGHT: the right-going wave IS the dry front. s_l = u_l - a_l s_r = u_l + 2.0_wp * a_l else if ( h_l <= DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry on the LEFT: mirror image. s_l = u_r - 2.0_wp * a_r s_r = u_r + a_r else s_l = min ( u_l - a_l , u_r - a_r ) s_r = max ( u_l + a_l , u_r + a_r ) end if fl_h = hu_l fl_hu = hu_l * u_l + 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * h_l * h_l fl_hv = hu_l * v_l fr_h = hu_r fr_hu = hu_r * u_r + 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * h_r * h_r fr_hv = hu_r * v_r if ( s_l >= 0.0_wp ) then f_h = fl_h f_hu = fl_hu f_hv = fl_hv else if ( s_r <= 0.0_wp ) then f_h = fr_h f_hu = fr_hu f_hv = fr_hv else denom = 1.0_wp / ( s_r - s_l ) f_h = ( s_r * fl_h - s_l * fr_h & + s_l * s_r * ( h_r - h_l )) * denom f_hu = ( s_r * fl_hu - s_l * fr_hu & + s_l * s_r * ( hu_r - hu_l )) * denom f_hv = ( s_r * fl_hv - s_l * fr_hv & + s_l * s_r * ( hv_r - hv_l )) * denom end if end subroutine hll_flux_x pure subroutine hll_flux_y ( h_b , hu_b , hv_b , h_t , hu_t , hv_t , & g_h , g_hu , g_hv ) !! HLL numerical flux in y-direction between bottom and top states real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_b , hu_b , hv_b real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_t , hu_t , hv_t real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: g_h , g_hu , g_hv real ( wp ) :: u_b , u_t , v_b , v_t , a_b , a_t real ( wp ) :: s_l , s_r , denom real ( wp ) :: gl_h , gl_hu , gl_hv real ( wp ) :: gr_h , gr_hu , gr_hv if ( h_b > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_b = hu_b / h_b v_b = hv_b / h_b else u_b = 0.0_wp v_b = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_t > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_t = hu_t / h_t v_t = hv_t / h_t else u_t = 0.0_wp v_t = 0.0_wp end if a_b = sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( h_b , 0.0_wp )) a_t = sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( h_t , 0.0_wp )) ! Wave-speed estimate.  Davis (min/max of the one-sided speeds) is right ! for a genuine two-sided WET Riemann problem, but wrong at a wet/dry ! front and must be replaced there. ! ! With the right state dry, `a_R = 0` and `u_R = 0`, so Davis returns ! `s_r = u_L + a_L`.  The exact dry-front speed is `u_L + 2 a_L` — the ! Ritter (1892) result — so Davis underestimates the right-going wave by ! up to a factor of two and the front cannot advance at the right rate. ! The dry-state speeds below are the standard fix (Toro, \"Riemann ! Solvers and Numerical Methods for Fluid Dynamics\", 3rd ed. S10.4; ! Einfeldt et al. 1991). ! ! Measured consequence before this branch existed: the Ritter dry-bed ! tip advanced at 1.49 c0 rather than 2 c0, the leading tongue below ! ~1 % of the upstream depth was absent, and on a sloping beach a thin ! film would not recede at all (validation phases 4 and 5). if ( h_t <= DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry on the RIGHT: the right-going wave IS the dry front. s_l = v_b - a_b s_r = v_b + 2.0_wp * a_b else if ( h_b <= DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry on the LEFT: mirror image. s_l = v_t - 2.0_wp * a_t s_r = v_t + a_t else s_l = min ( v_b - a_b , v_t - a_t ) s_r = max ( v_b + a_b , v_t + a_t ) end if gl_h = hv_b gl_hu = hu_b * v_b gl_hv = hv_b * v_b + 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * h_b * h_b gr_h = hv_t gr_hu = hu_t * v_t gr_hv = hv_t * v_t + 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * h_t * h_t if ( s_l >= 0.0_wp ) then g_h = gl_h g_hu = gl_hu g_hv = gl_hv else if ( s_r <= 0.0_wp ) then g_h = gr_h g_hu = gr_hu g_hv = gr_hv else denom = 1.0_wp / ( s_r - s_l ) g_h = ( s_r * gl_h - s_l * gr_h & + s_l * s_r * ( h_t - h_b )) * denom g_hu = ( s_r * gl_hu - s_l * gr_hu & + s_l * s_r * ( hu_t - hu_b )) * denom g_hv = ( s_r * gl_hv - s_l * gr_hv & + s_l * s_r * ( hv_t - hv_b )) * denom end if end subroutine hll_flux_y pure subroutine hllc_flux_x ( h_l , hu_l , hv_l , h_r , hu_r , hv_r , & f_h , f_hu , f_hv ) !! HLLC numerical flux in x-direction. Transverse momentum hv is !! upwinded across the contact wave: f_hv = f_h * v_upwind !! (v_l if s_star >= 0, else v_r); h and hu match HLL. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_l , hu_l , hv_l real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_r , hu_r , hv_r real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: f_h , f_hu , f_hv real ( wp ) :: u_l , u_r , v_l , v_r , a_l , a_r real ( wp ) :: s_l , s_r , denom , denom_star , s_star real ( wp ) :: fl_h , fl_hu , fl_hv real ( wp ) :: fr_h , fr_hu , fr_hv if ( h_l > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_l = hu_l / h_l v_l = hv_l / h_l else u_l = 0.0_wp v_l = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_r > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_r = hu_r / h_r v_r = hv_r / h_r else u_r = 0.0_wp v_r = 0.0_wp end if a_l = sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( h_l , 0.0_wp )) a_r = sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( h_r , 0.0_wp )) ! Wave-speed estimate.  Davis (min/max of the one-sided speeds) is right ! for a genuine two-sided WET Riemann problem, but wrong at a wet/dry ! front and must be replaced there. ! ! With the right state dry, `a_R = 0` and `u_R = 0`, so Davis returns ! `s_r = u_L + a_L`.  The exact dry-front speed is `u_L + 2 a_L` — the ! Ritter (1892) result — so Davis underestimates the right-going wave by ! up to a factor of two and the front cannot advance at the right rate. ! The dry-state speeds below are the standard fix (Toro, \"Riemann ! Solvers and Numerical Methods for Fluid Dynamics\", 3rd ed. S10.4; ! Einfeldt et al. 1991). ! ! Measured consequence before this branch existed: the Ritter dry-bed ! tip advanced at 1.49 c0 rather than 2 c0, the leading tongue below ! ~1 % of the upstream depth was absent, and on a sloping beach a thin ! film would not recede at all (validation phases 4 and 5). if ( h_r <= DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry on the RIGHT: the right-going wave IS the dry front. s_l = u_l - a_l s_r = u_l + 2.0_wp * a_l else if ( h_l <= DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry on the LEFT: mirror image. s_l = u_r - 2.0_wp * a_r s_r = u_r + a_r else s_l = min ( u_l - a_l , u_r - a_r ) s_r = max ( u_l + a_l , u_r + a_r ) end if fl_h = hu_l fl_hu = hu_l * u_l + 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * h_l * h_l fl_hv = hu_l * v_l fr_h = hu_r fr_hu = hu_r * u_r + 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * h_r * h_r fr_hv = hu_r * v_r if ( s_l >= 0.0_wp ) then f_h = fl_h f_hu = fl_hu f_hv = fl_hv else if ( s_r <= 0.0_wp ) then f_h = fr_h f_hu = fr_hu f_hv = fr_hv else denom = 1.0_wp / ( s_r - s_l ) f_h = ( s_r * fl_h - s_l * fr_h & + s_l * s_r * ( h_r - h_l )) * denom f_hu = ( s_r * fl_hu - s_l * fr_hu & + s_l * s_r * ( hu_r - hu_l )) * denom ! Contact-wave speed (Toro). Fall back to the arithmetic mean ! when the denominator vanishes. denom_star = h_r * ( u_r - s_r ) - h_l * ( u_l - s_l ) if ( abs ( denom_star ) > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then s_star = ( s_l * h_r * ( u_r - s_r ) - s_r * h_l * ( u_l - s_l )) / denom_star else s_star = 0.5_wp * ( u_l + u_r ) end if if ( s_star >= 0.0_wp ) then f_hv = f_h * v_l else f_hv = f_h * v_r end if end if end subroutine hllc_flux_x pure subroutine hllc_flux_y ( h_b , hu_b , hv_b , h_t , hu_t , hv_t , & g_h , g_hu , g_hv ) !! HLLC numerical flux in y-direction. Mirrors hllc_flux_x with !! (u, hu) and (v, hv) swapped; transverse hu is upwinded. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_b , hu_b , hv_b real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_t , hu_t , hv_t real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: g_h , g_hu , g_hv real ( wp ) :: u_b , u_t , v_b , v_t , a_b , a_t real ( wp ) :: s_l , s_r , denom , denom_star , s_star real ( wp ) :: gl_h , gl_hu , gl_hv real ( wp ) :: gr_h , gr_hu , gr_hv if ( h_b > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_b = hu_b / h_b v_b = hv_b / h_b else u_b = 0.0_wp v_b = 0.0_wp end if if ( h_t > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then u_t = hu_t / h_t v_t = hv_t / h_t else u_t = 0.0_wp v_t = 0.0_wp end if a_b = sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( h_b , 0.0_wp )) a_t = sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( h_t , 0.0_wp )) ! Wave-speed estimate.  Davis (min/max of the one-sided speeds) is right ! for a genuine two-sided WET Riemann problem, but wrong at a wet/dry ! front and must be replaced there. ! ! With the right state dry, `a_R = 0` and `u_R = 0`, so Davis returns ! `s_r = u_L + a_L`.  The exact dry-front speed is `u_L + 2 a_L` — the ! Ritter (1892) result — so Davis underestimates the right-going wave by ! up to a factor of two and the front cannot advance at the right rate. ! The dry-state speeds below are the standard fix (Toro, \"Riemann ! Solvers and Numerical Methods for Fluid Dynamics\", 3rd ed. S10.4; ! Einfeldt et al. 1991). ! ! Measured consequence before this branch existed: the Ritter dry-bed ! tip advanced at 1.49 c0 rather than 2 c0, the leading tongue below ! ~1 % of the upstream depth was absent, and on a sloping beach a thin ! film would not recede at all (validation phases 4 and 5). if ( h_t <= DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry on the RIGHT: the right-going wave IS the dry front. s_l = v_b - a_b s_r = v_b + 2.0_wp * a_b else if ( h_b <= DRY_TOLERANCE ) then ! Dry on the LEFT: mirror image. s_l = v_t - 2.0_wp * a_t s_r = v_t + a_t else s_l = min ( v_b - a_b , v_t - a_t ) s_r = max ( v_b + a_b , v_t + a_t ) end if gl_h = hv_b gl_hu = hu_b * v_b gl_hv = hv_b * v_b + 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * h_b * h_b gr_h = hv_t gr_hu = hu_t * v_t gr_hv = hv_t * v_t + 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * h_t * h_t if ( s_l >= 0.0_wp ) then g_h = gl_h g_hu = gl_hu g_hv = gl_hv else if ( s_r <= 0.0_wp ) then g_h = gr_h g_hu = gr_hu g_hv = gr_hv else denom = 1.0_wp / ( s_r - s_l ) g_h = ( s_r * gl_h - s_l * gr_h & + s_l * s_r * ( h_t - h_b )) * denom g_hv = ( s_r * gl_hv - s_l * gr_hv & + s_l * s_r * ( hv_t - hv_b )) * denom denom_star = h_t * ( v_t - s_r ) - h_b * ( v_b - s_l ) if ( abs ( denom_star ) > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then s_star = ( s_l * h_t * ( v_t - s_r ) - s_r * h_b * ( v_b - s_l )) / denom_star else s_star = 0.5_wp * ( v_b + v_t ) end if if ( s_star >= 0.0_wp ) then g_hu = g_h * u_b else g_hu = g_h * u_t end if end if end subroutine hllc_flux_y end module rki_kernel_flux","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_kernel_flux.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_truncate.F90 – Rakali","text":"CFL-based velocity truncation for layer momentum (MOM6-style limiter). This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_ml_truncate.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_ml_truncate.f90 rki_ml_truncate.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_truncate.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_truncate.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_ml_truncate.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_ml_truncate.f90 rki_ml_truncate.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 rki_solver.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_truncate.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! CFL-based velocity truncation for layer momentum (MOM6-style limiter). module rki_ml_truncate !! Per-cell-per-layer limiter (not a closure) that clips runaway velocities !! from any upstream operator (BPG, vertical exchange, viscosity) to !! 0.9*cfl_trunc*dx/dt so a few bad cells don't tank the global timestep. use rki_constants , only : wp , THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD use rki_grid , only : hgrid_t implicit none private public :: ml_truncate_velocity contains pure subroutine ml_truncate_velocity ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & grid , nz , dt , & cfl_trunc ) !! Clip any layer velocity with CFL > cfl_trunc to 0.9*cfl_trunc*dx/dt. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: cfl_trunc integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: dx , dy real ( wp ) :: u_abs , v_abs , h_k , vel_max_x , vel_max_y nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost dx = grid % dx dy = grid % dy vel_max_x = 0.9_wp * cfl_trunc * dx / max ( dt , 1.0e-10_wp ) vel_max_y = 0.9_wp * cfl_trunc * dy / max ( dt , 1.0e-10_wp ) do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , u_abs , v_abs , h_k ) do k = 1 , nz h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( h_k < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) cycle u_abs = abs ( hu_layer ( i , j , k )) / h_k v_abs = abs ( hv_layer ( i , j , k )) / h_k if ( u_abs > vel_max_x ) then hu_layer ( i , j , k ) = sign ( vel_max_x * h_k , hu_layer ( i , j , k )) end if if ( v_abs > vel_max_y ) then hv_layer ( i , j , k ) = sign ( vel_max_y * h_k , hv_layer ( i , j , k )) end if end do end do end subroutine ml_truncate_velocity end module rki_ml_truncate","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_ml_truncate.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_api_unstr.F90 – Rakali","text":"C-compatible API for the unstructured Rakali solver Provides bind(C) entrypoints for Python (and any other ctypes/cffi\ncaller) to drive the unstructured central-upwind solver without going\nthrough any file I/O.  The mesh and all initial state come from numpy\narrays handed across the ctypes boundary. Multi-instance: each call to rki_unstr_create returns an opaque void* handle.  Multiple unstructured handles can coexist in one\nprocess, and a structured + unstructured handle can coexist too\n(they are separate types tracked by distinct magic numbers). rki_unstr_set_log_level intentionally stays module-level: the logger\nis process-global, not per simulation. Lifecycle: void h;\n  rki_unstr_create(nverts, ntri, vert_x, vert_y, tri_v, bc_tags, &h)\n  rki_unstr_set_bathymetry(h, bed)             – centroid array\n  rki_unstr_set_initial_stage(h, stage)        – centroid array\n  rki_unstr_set_initial_xmom(h, xmom)          – optional\n  rki_unstr_set_initial_ymom(h, ymom)          – optional\n  rki_unstr_set_bc_type(h, group, bc_type)\n  rki_unstr_set_manning(h, n)                  – optional\n  rki_unstr_set_wind(h, tau_x, tau_y)          – optional, uniform Pa\n  rki_unstr_set_wind_field(h, wind_x, wind_y)  – optional, per-cell Pa\n  rki_unstr_finalize(h)\n  rki_unstr_step(h, dt) / rki_unstr_advance(h, t_end)\n  rki_unstr_get_ _ptr(h, ptr, n)\n  rki_unstr_destroy(&h) Error codes (mirror rki_api):\n  0     success\n  -1    not initialised / output not open / etc.\n  -2    range / already-open / grid-mismatch\n  -3    multilayer not active / restart read failure\n -100   invalid handle This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_api_unstr.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_banner.f90 rki_banner.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_banner.f90 sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 rki_boundary_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_gauges_unstr.f90 rki_gauges_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_gauges_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 rki_handle.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 sourcefile~rki_kern