rcefile~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_output_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_restart_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Agglomeration-multigrid V-cycle preconditioner for the unstructured SI !! eta-solve. module rki_si_unstr_mg !! Aggregation (agglomeration) multigrid V(2,2)-cycle preconditioner for the !! TRIANGLE semi-implicit free-surface Helmholtz system — geometric MG has no !! triangle hierarchy, so we coarsen the CELL GRAPH by greedy pairwise !! aggregation instead.  The design is !! numpy-prototype-validated (`local_archive/prototypes/q12_agglom_mg`, !! STRONG GO: plain-CG plateau of thousands -> tens of MG-PCG iters). !! !! WHAT IT PRECONDITIONS.  The Fortran CG (`si_unstr_cg_solve`) runs the !! AREA-WEIGHTED PCG on the operator `A` (`si_unstr_apply_helmholtz`), inner !! product `<x,y>_area = sum_c area_c x_c y_c`.  This module works in the !! genuinely-SYMMETRIC space `Ahat = diag(area)*A` (SPD M-matrix): !!   Ahat[c,c]   = area_c + coef*sum_e K_e      (coef = g*theta&#94;2*dt&#94;2) !!   Ahat[c,nbr] = -coef*K_e ,   K_e = Hf_e*len_e/delta_e !! The Jacobi preconditioner the code already ships is, in this space, !! exactly `z = Ahat_diag&#94;{-1} (area*r)`; the MG apply is the direct !! generalisation `z = Vcycle_Ahat(area*r)` — one V(2,2) cycle from a zero !! guess (SPD + linear => a valid CG preconditioner).  Passing `area*r` !! (not `r`) into the symmetric V-cycle is what makes it consistent with the !! area-weighted outer PCG (prototype driver §Ahat). !! !! HIERARCHY.  Cell graph coarsened ~2x/level by greedy pairwise !! aggregation (strongest-transmissibility partner).  Built ONCE at init !! (static mesh).  Every level's operator is stored in a COMPACT !! variable-valence edge form `nbr(mv,nc)` / `ke(mv,nc)` / `diag(nc)`; a !! coarse level's operator is the GALERKIN `P&#94;T Ahat P` with a 0/1 !! piecewise-constant P — which for aggregation equals a rediscretized !! agglomerate-TPFA (coarse mass = sum member areas, coarse transmissibility !! = sum of fine transmissibilities across the cut) EXACTLY, so the coarse !! STENCIL DOES NOT GROW (prototype: Galerkin == rediscretized to !! round-off).  Transfers are P (inject) / R = P&#94;T (sum-gather) — exact !! transpose by construction, no scaling factor. !! !! REFRESH.  Only the transmissibilities `ke` + diagonals depend on the !! per-step frozen `Hf` (coef is fixed).  The STRUCTURE (aggregates, coarse !! adjacency, member lists) is static; `ke`/`diag`/`dinv` are rebuilt ONCE !! PER STEP on the HOST (fine level from the mesh geometry + current Hf, !! coarse levels by the Galerkin cascade) and pushed to the device — the !! same host-side per-step operator refresh the structured MG uses.  NOT per !! V-cycle. !! !! GPU.  Each level owns explicit-shape device arrays + enter/exit_data. !! The level loop runs on the HOST; every device kernel (apply / damped- !! Jacobi smooth / residual / restrict / prolong) is called with FLAT !! EXPLICIT-SHAPE arguments — the level array is NEVER dereferenced inside a !! `do concurrent` (the array-of-derived-types device-indirection gotcha). !! Kernels are cell-centric (each cell writes only its own row / entry; !! restriction sums a coarse cell's own members) — no neighbour scatter, no !! atomics.  Damped Jacobi ping-pongs (read old, write new) — race-free. !! Single-rank v1 (no per-cycle halo). use rki_constants , only : wp use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t use pic_logger , only : global_logger implicit none private public :: agglom_level_unstr_t , agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t public :: agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build , agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh public :: agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond public :: AGGLOM_MIN_SIZE , AGGLOM_MAX_LEVELS , AGGLOM_OMEGA public :: AGGLOM_NU_PRE , AGGLOM_NU_POST , AGGLOM_COARSE_SWEEPS integer , parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 integer , parameter :: AGGLOM_MIN_SIZE = 150 !! Stop coarsening when a level has <= this many cells (prototype-tuned: !! 2x pairwise coarsening down to ~150 cells, then a coarse Jacobi solve). integer , parameter :: AGGLOM_MAX_LEVELS = 16 !! Hard cap on the level count (fixed-size level array bound). real ( wp ), parameter :: AGGLOM_OMEGA = 0.8_wp !! Damped-Jacobi relaxation factor (matches the structured MG). ! NU_PRE == NU_POST is LOAD-BEARING: the V-cycle is self-adjoint (and ! therefore a valid plain-PCG preconditioner) only with symmetric ! pre/post smoothing — an unequal edit silently breaks SPD. integer , parameter :: AGGLOM_NU_PRE = 2 !! Pre-smoothing Jacobi sweeps per level. integer , parameter :: AGGLOM_NU_POST = 2 !! Post-smoothing Jacobi sweeps per level. integer , parameter :: AGGLOM_COARSE_SWEEPS = 40 !! Coarsest-level Jacobi sweeps (approximate solve from zero).  FIXED (not !! convergence-gated) on purpose: a fixed sweep count makes the whole !! V-cycle a FIXED LINEAR SPD operator, which the outer STANDARD (non- !! flexible) area-weighted PCG requires — a residual-gated coarse solve !! would vary the sweep count with the RHS, making M RHS-dependent !! (flexible preconditioning) and breaking the constant-M PCG assumption. !! EFFICIENCY CAVEAT: for a very stiff Helmholtz (large SI dt) 40 sweeps !! can under-resolve the ~<=150-cell coarse system and lift the outer PCG !! count on larger/stiffer meshes; the funnel CI case is well inside the !! budget.  Robustify (if ever needed) by raising this constant, not by !! gating — keep the operator fixed + linear. real ( wp ), parameter :: DELTA_EPS = 1.0e-30_wp !! 1/0 armour on the circumcentre-line distance (matches the operator). type :: agglom_level_unstr_t !! One aggregation-MG level: the compact variable-valence Helmholtz !! operator (symmetric Ahat) on `nc` cells + the V-cycle work buffers + !! the aggregation map to the next coarser level.  Structure arrays !! (nbr / n_nbr / agg_of / member CSR) are STATIC (built once); the !! coefficient arrays (ke / diag / dinv) are refreshed per step.  All !! arrays explicit-shape; the level loop dereferences on the HOST and !! passes flat args to the device kernels. integer :: nc = 0 !! Cells on this level. integer :: mv = 0 !! Max valence (fixed leading dim of nbr/ke; unused slots padded !! nbr=1, ke=0 so the apply loop is branchless). ! --- STATIC operator STRUCTURE (built once at init) --- integer , allocatable :: n_nbr (:) !! Valence per cell, shape (nc). integer , allocatable :: nbr (:, :) !! Neighbour cell id on THIS level, shape (mv, nc); padded slots = 1. integer , allocatable :: agg_of (:) !! Aggregate id in the NEXT COARSER level for each of this level's !! cells, shape (nc).  Drives prolongation (fine cell reads its !! parent).  Unallocated on the coarsest level. ! Member CSR: which cells of the NEXT FINER level belong to each of THIS ! level's cells (this level is the coarse side).  Drives restriction (a ! coarse cell sums its own members) + the host Galerkin build. integer , allocatable :: mstart (:) !! Member CSR offsets, shape (nc+1).  Unallocated on the finest level. integer , allocatable :: mlist (:) !! Member cell ids on the finer level, shape (n_finer). ! --- PER-STEP coefficients (host + device; refreshed each step) --- real ( wp ), allocatable :: ke (:, :) !! Transmissibility coef*K_e per edge, shape (mv, nc); off-diag = -ke. real ( wp ), allocatable :: diag (:) !! Operator diagonal, shape (nc). real ( wp ), allocatable :: dinv (:) !! 1/diag (Jacobi), shape (nc). ! --- V-cycle work buffers (device) --- real ( wp ), allocatable :: e (:) !! Error iterate, shape (nc). real ( wp ), allocatable :: r (:) !! Level RHS / residual, shape (nc). real ( wp ), allocatable :: tmp (:) !! Jacobi ping-pong / residual scratch, shape (nc). contains procedure , non_overridable :: enter_data => agglom_level_enter_data procedure , non_overridable :: exit_data => agglom_level_exit_data procedure , non_overridable :: destroy => agglom_level_destroy end type agglom_level_unstr_t type :: agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t !! Fine-to-coarse level stack for the aggregation-MG preconditioner. !! Allocated + built only when `precond == mg`. integer :: n_levels = 0 type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), allocatable :: lev (:) contains procedure , non_overridable :: enter_data => agglom_hierarchy_enter_data procedure , non_overridable :: exit_data => agglom_hierarchy_exit_data procedure , non_overridable :: destroy => agglom_hierarchy_destroy end type agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t contains ! ====================================================================== !  BUILD (init, host) — aggregate the cell graph, size + fill the static !  structure of every level.  Uses the STILL-DEPTH Hf as the aggregation !  strength; the per-step refresh overwrites ke/diag with the live Hf. ! ====================================================================== subroutine agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build ( this , mesh , nco ) !! Build the level stack for `nco` owned cells.  Only the mesh GEOMETRY !! is needed: the aggregation strength is the geometric transmissibility !! `len/delta` (a uniform-`Hf`, `coef=1` proxy).  Greedy pairwise !! aggregation picks the MAX-strength neighbour, which is invariant to a !! uniform positive scale, so the live per-step `coef*Hf` (folded in at !! refresh) never changes the STRUCTURE — the hierarchy is static. !! Host-only (runs before enter_data); the diag/ke are placeholders here !! and are overwritten by the first `refresh` before any solve. class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nco integer :: l , nc , l_alloc , k , i , kn real ( wp ), allocatable :: str_l (:, :) real ( wp ), allocatable :: hf0 (:, :) ! ---- Level 1: the fine mesh operator structure (mv = 3) ---- call build_level1_structure ( this , mesh , nco ) call alloc_level_coeffs ( this % lev ( 1 )) allocate ( str_l ( this % lev ( 1 )% mv , this % lev ( 1 )% nc )) ! Uniform per-edge Hf=1 on interior edges => aggregation strength = ! len/delta (the geometric transmissibility).  Boundary edges left 0. allocate ( hf0 ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nco ), source = 0.0_wp ) do k = 1 , nco do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , k ) if ( kn > 0 . and . kn <= nco ) hf0 ( i , k ) = 1.0_wp end do end do call level1_operator ( mesh , nco , 1.0_wp , hf0 , this % lev ( 1 ), str_l ) deallocate ( hf0 ) l = 1 do nc = this % lev ( l )% nc if ( nc <= AGGLOM_MIN_SIZE . or . l >= AGGLOM_MAX_LEVELS ) exit ! Aggregate level l (strength = |ke| = str_l) -> define level l+1. call aggregate_and_build_coarse ( this , l , str_l ) if ( this % lev ( l + 1 )% nc >= nc ) then ! No coarsening achieved: drop the stub level, stop. call this % lev ( l + 1 )% destroy () this % n_levels = l exit end if call alloc_level_coeffs ( this % lev ( l + 1 )) if ( allocated ( str_l )) deallocate ( str_l ) allocate ( str_l ( this % lev ( l + 1 )% mv , this % lev ( l + 1 )% nc )) call galerkin_operator ( this % lev ( l ), this % lev ( l + 1 ), str_l ) l = l + 1 this % n_levels = l end do if ( allocated ( str_l )) deallocate ( str_l ) ! Shrink the level array to n_levels (it was over-allocated). l_alloc = size ( this % lev ) if ( this % n_levels < l_alloc ) call trim_levels ( this ) call global_logger % info ( \"si_unstr_mg: built \" // & itoa ( this % n_levels ) // \" levels (fine nc=\" // & itoa ( this % lev ( 1 )% nc ) // \", coarse nc=\" // & itoa ( this % lev ( this % n_levels )% nc ) // \")\" ) end subroutine agglom_hierarchy_unstr_build subroutine build_level1_structure ( this , mesh , nco ) !! Allocate the level array + fill level 1's static interior-neighbour !! structure from the mesh (mv = EDGES_PER_TRI = 3). class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nco integer :: k , i , kn , ns allocate ( this % lev ( AGGLOM_MAX_LEVELS )) this % n_levels = 1 this % lev ( 1 )% nc = nco this % lev ( 1 )% mv = EDGES_PER_TRI allocate ( this % lev ( 1 )% n_nbr ( nco ), source = 0 ) allocate ( this % lev ( 1 )% nbr ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nco ), source = 1 ) do k = 1 , nco ns = 0 do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , k ) if ( kn > 0 . and . kn <= nco ) then ns = ns + 1 this % lev ( 1 )% nbr ( ns , k ) = kn end if end do this % lev ( 1 )% n_nbr ( k ) = ns end do end subroutine build_level1_structure subroutine level1_operator ( mesh , nco , coef , Hf_edge , lev , strength ) !! Fill level 1's ke/diag/dinv from the mesh geometry + the per-edge !! frozen Hf (still-water synthetic at build, the live `Hf_edge` at !! refresh).  Mirrors `si_unstr_compute_diag` + the interior off-diagonals !! of `si_unstr_apply_helmholtz`, so the symmetric Ahat row is exact: !!   diag(k) = area_k + coef*sum_{Hf>0} K_e   (interior + Dirichlet) !!   off-diag ke to interior neighbours only. !! A Dirichlet boundary edge carries Hf>0 with no CG-unknown neighbour => !! it lands on the diagonal (ghost = homogeneous 0 in the error !! operator).  Wall edges carry Hf=0 => dropped.  `strength` returns |ke| !! per interior edge for aggregation.  HOST; caller pushes to the device. type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nco real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: coef real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nco ) type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: lev real ( wp ), intent ( out ), optional :: strength ( lev % mv , nco ) !! |ke| per edge for the NEXT aggregation.  Needed at BUILD only; !! the per-step refresh omits it (no scratch allocation in the !! per-step path). integer :: k , i , kn , ns real ( wp ) :: kloc , diagk if ( present ( strength )) strength = 0.0_wp lev % ke = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nco diagk = mesh % area ( k ) ns = 0 do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , k ) ! Diagonal: every Hf>0 edge contributes coef*K_e (interior OR ! Dirichlet boundary edge — the latter lands on the diagonal with ! no CG-unknown neighbour slot).  Hf<=0 (wall / dried edge) => 0. if ( Hf_edge ( i , k ) > 0.0_wp ) then kloc = coef * Hf_edge ( i , k ) * mesh % edge_len ( i , k ) & / max ( mesh % edge_delta ( i , k ), DELTA_EPS ) diagk = diagk + kloc else kloc = 0.0_wp end if ! Off-diagonal slot: advance `ns` on the SAME interior-edge ! predicate as `build_level1_structure` so the ke slot index stays ! LOCKED to the nbr slot index — independent of whether this edge's ! Hf is zero.  An interior edge that dries (Hf<=0) writes a ZERO ! (wall-like) transmissibility into its own aligned slot rather than ! skipping it, keeping the operator symmetric + SPD even with mixed ! zero/nonzero interior Hf (the plain 2D-barotropic dry-cell path). if ( kn > 0 . and . kn <= nco ) then ns = ns + 1 lev % ke ( ns , k ) = kloc if ( present ( strength )) strength ( ns , k ) = kloc end if end do lev % diag ( k ) = diagk lev % dinv ( k ) = 1.0_wp / diagk end do end subroutine level1_operator subroutine aggregate_and_build_coarse ( this , l , strength ) !! Greedy pairwise aggregation of level l (strongest-transmissibility !! partner), then build level l+1's static structure: nc, member CSR, !! coarse adjacency (nbr / n_nbr / mv).  `strength(mv,nc)` = |ke| per !! edge on level l. class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer , intent ( in ) :: l real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: strength (:, :) integer :: nf , k , s , j , best , nc , i real ( wp ) :: bw , w integer , allocatable :: aggof (:) nf = this % lev ( l )% nc allocate ( aggof ( nf ), source = 0 ) nc = 0 do k = 1 , nf if ( aggof ( k ) /= 0 ) cycle best = - 1 bw = 0.0_wp do s = 1 , this % lev ( l )% n_nbr ( k ) j = this % lev ( l )% nbr ( s , k ) if ( aggof ( j ) /= 0 ) cycle w = strength ( s , k ) if ( w > bw ) then bw = w best = j end if end do nc = nc + 1 aggof ( k ) = nc if ( best > 0 ) aggof ( best ) = nc end do ! Store agg_of on level l (drives prolongation). allocate ( this % lev ( l )% agg_of ( nf )) this % lev ( l )% agg_of = aggof ! Level l+1 skeleton. this % lev ( l + 1 )% nc = nc ! Member CSR (which level-l cells belong to each coarse cell), STANDARD ! 1-based: members of coarse cell I are mlist(mstart(I):mstart(I+1)-1). allocate ( this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart ( nc + 1 ), source = 0 ) do k = 1 , nf this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart ( aggof ( k ) + 1 ) = & this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart ( aggof ( k ) + 1 ) + 1 ! count(I) into slot I+1 end do this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart ( 1 ) = 1 do i = 1 , nc this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart ( i + 1 ) = this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart ( i ) & + this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart ( i + 1 ) end do allocate ( this % lev ( l + 1 )% mlist ( nf )) block integer , allocatable :: cursor (:) allocate ( cursor ( nc )) cursor = this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart ( 1 : nc ) ! cursor(I) = mstart(I) do k = 1 , nf i = aggof ( k ) this % lev ( l + 1 )% mlist ( cursor ( i )) = k cursor ( i ) = cursor ( i ) + 1 end do deallocate ( cursor ) end block call build_coarse_adjacency ( this % lev ( l ), this % lev ( l + 1 ), aggof ) deallocate ( aggof ) end subroutine aggregate_and_build_coarse subroutine build_coarse_adjacency ( levf , levc , aggof ) !! Build coarse-level neighbour lists from the fine adjacency: coarse !! cells I,J are neighbours iff some fine edge crosses the I-J aggregate !! boundary.  Sets levc%mv / n_nbr / nbr (unique neighbours per coarse !! cell).  Host, O(fine edges). type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: levf type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: levc integer , intent ( in ) :: aggof (:) integer :: nc , k , s , j , capI , capJ , mv , i integer , allocatable :: cnt (:), tmpnbr (:, :) nc = levc % nc allocate ( cnt ( nc ), source = 0 ) ! First pass: over-estimate max valence = sum of member valences. mv = 0 do capI = 1 , nc capJ = 0 do i = levc % mstart ( capI ), levc % mstart ( capI + 1 ) - 1 k = levc % mlist ( i ) capJ = capJ + levf % n_nbr ( k ) end do mv = max ( mv , capJ ) end do mv = max ( mv , 1 ) allocate ( tmpnbr ( mv , nc ), source = 0 ) do capI = 1 , nc do i = levc % mstart ( capI ), levc % mstart ( capI + 1 ) - 1 k = levc % mlist ( i ) do s = 1 , levf % n_nbr ( k ) j = aggof ( levf % nbr ( s , k )) if ( j == capI ) cycle call push_unique ( tmpnbr (:, capI ), cnt ( capI ), j ) end do end do end do levc % mv = max ( maxval ( cnt ), 1 ) allocate ( levc % n_nbr ( nc )) allocate ( levc % nbr ( levc % mv , nc ), source = 1 ) do capI = 1 , nc levc % n_nbr ( capI ) = cnt ( capI ) do s = 1 , cnt ( capI ) levc % nbr ( s , capI ) = tmpnbr ( s , capI ) end do end do deallocate ( cnt , tmpnbr ) end subroutine build_coarse_adjacency subroutine push_unique ( list , n , val ) !! Append val to list(1:n) if not already present; bump n. integer , intent ( inout ) :: list (:) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n integer , intent ( in ) :: val integer :: s do s = 1 , n if ( list ( s ) == val ) return end do n = n + 1 list ( n ) = val end subroutine push_unique subroutine galerkin_operator ( levf , levc , strength ) !! Build the coarse operator ke/diag/dinv by the Galerkin cascade from !! the finer level's ke/diag (== rediscretized agglomerate-TPFA for 0/1 !! aggregation).  `strength(mvc,ncc)` returns |ke| for the NEXT !! aggregation.  HOST; caller pushes to the device. type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: levf type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: levc real ( wp ), intent ( out ), optional :: strength ( levc % mv , levc % nc ) !! |ke| per coarse edge for the NEXT aggregation (BUILD only; the !! per-step refresh omits it). integer :: capI , i , k , s , j , capJ , t real ( wp ) :: diagI , v if ( present ( strength )) strength = 0.0_wp levc % ke = 0.0_wp do capI = 1 , levc % nc diagI = 0.0_wp do i = levc % mstart ( capI ), levc % mstart ( capI + 1 ) - 1 k = levc % mlist ( i ) diagI = diagI + levf % diag ( k ) do s = 1 , levf % n_nbr ( k ) j = levf % nbr ( s , k ) v = levf % ke ( s , k ) capJ = levf % agg_of ( j ) if ( capJ == capI ) then diagI = diagI - v ! internal edge folds to diag else t = find_slot ( levc % nbr (:, capI ), levc % n_nbr ( capI ), capJ ) ! ke >= 0 invariant (Hf >= 0 => level-1 ke >= 0 => Galerkin ! sums stay >= 0), so the signed ke doubles as the next ! aggregation strength; a negative ke would silently ! degrade coarsening to singletons. levc % ke ( t , capI ) = levc % ke ( t , capI ) + v if ( present ( strength )) strength ( t , capI ) = levc % ke ( t , capI ) end if end do end do levc % diag ( capI ) = diagI levc % dinv ( capI ) = 1.0_wp / diagI end do end subroutine galerkin_operator integer function find_slot ( nbr , n , tgt ) result ( t ) !! Locate the coarse-edge slot for neighbour `tgt` in nbr(1:n).  The !! target is ALWAYS present — the coarse adjacency + the Galerkin fold !! are built from the same aggregation map, so every folded fine edge has !! a coarse slot.  A not-found here means that invariant broke; fail loud !! (host-only build path) rather than silently mislocate a coefficient !! into slot 1. integer , intent ( in ) :: nbr (:) integer , intent ( in ) :: n , tgt integer :: s t = 0 do s = 1 , n if ( nbr ( s ) == tgt ) then t = s return end if end do call global_logger % error ( \"si_unstr_mg: find_slot could not locate coarse \" // & \"neighbour \" // itoa ( tgt ) // \" in the coarse adjacency \" // & \"— Galerkin fold inconsistent with the aggregation map\" ) error stop \"si_unstr_mg: find_slot: coarse neighbour not found\" end function find_slot subroutine alloc_level_coeffs ( lev ) !! Allocate the per-step coefficient + V-cycle work arrays of a level. type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: lev allocate ( lev % ke ( lev % mv , lev % nc ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( lev % diag ( lev % nc ), source = 1.0_wp ) allocate ( lev % dinv ( lev % nc ), source = 1.0_wp ) allocate ( lev % e ( lev % nc ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( lev % r ( lev % nc ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( lev % tmp ( lev % nc ), source = 0.0_wp ) end subroutine alloc_level_coeffs subroutine trim_levels ( this ) !! Move-shrink the over-allocated level array to n_levels. class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), allocatable :: keep (:) integer :: l allocate ( keep ( this % n_levels )) do l = 1 , this % n_levels call move_level ( this % lev ( l ), keep ( l )) end do call move_alloc ( keep , this % lev ) end subroutine trim_levels subroutine move_level ( src , dst ) !! move_alloc every component from src to dst (host, pre-enter_data). type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: src type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: dst dst % nc = src % nc dst % mv = src % mv if ( allocated ( src % n_nbr )) call move_alloc ( src % n_nbr , dst % n_nbr ) if ( allocated ( src % nbr )) call move_alloc ( src % nbr , dst % nbr ) if ( allocated ( src % agg_of )) call move_alloc ( src % agg_of , dst % agg_of ) if ( allocated ( src % mstart )) call move_alloc ( src % mstart , dst % mstart ) if ( allocated ( src % mlist )) call move_alloc ( src % mlist , dst % mlist ) if ( allocated ( src % ke )) call move_alloc ( src % ke , dst % ke ) if ( allocated ( src % diag )) call move_alloc ( src % diag , dst % diag ) if ( allocated ( src % dinv )) call move_alloc ( src % dinv , dst % dinv ) if ( allocated ( src % e )) call move_alloc ( src % e , dst % e ) if ( allocated ( src % r )) call move_alloc ( src % r , dst % r ) if ( allocated ( src % tmp )) call move_alloc ( src % tmp , dst % tmp ) end subroutine move_level ! ====================================================================== !  REFRESH (per step, host build + device push) ! ====================================================================== subroutine agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh ( this , mesh , nco , coef , Hf_edge ) !! Rebuild every level's ke/diag/dinv from the current frozen per-edge !! `Hf_edge` (the same array the operator + RHS use) + push to the !! device.  Fine level from the mesh; coarse levels by the Galerkin !! cascade.  Structures are static.  Runs ONCE PER STEP (host loop), NOT !! per V-cycle.  `Hf_edge` is device-resident; the caller pulls it self !! before calling (host build reads it). class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nco real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: coef real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nco ) integer :: l call level1_operator ( mesh , nco , coef , Hf_edge , this % lev ( 1 )) call level_coeffs_to_device ( this % lev ( 1 )) do l = 2 , this % n_levels call galerkin_operator ( this % lev ( l - 1 ), this % lev ( l )) call level_coeffs_to_device ( this % lev ( l )) end do end subroutine agglom_hierarchy_unstr_refresh subroutine level_coeffs_to_device ( lev ) !! Push the host-refreshed coefficient arrays to the device. type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: lev !$acc update device(lev%ke, lev%diag, lev%dinv) end subroutine level_coeffs_to_device ! ====================================================================== !  DEVICE KERNELS (flat explicit-shape args; cell-centric, race-free) ! ====================================================================== subroutine agglom_jacobi_one ( e_old , e_new , r , nbr , ke , diag , dinv , & mv , nc , omega ) !! One damped-Jacobi sweep e_new = e_old + omega*(r - Ahat*e_old)/diag — !! reads e_old only, writes e_new only (race-free). integer , intent ( in ) :: mv , nc real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: e_old ( nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: e_new ( nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r ( nc ) integer , intent ( in ) :: nbr ( mv , nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ke ( mv , nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: diag ( nc ), dinv ( nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: omega integer :: k , s real ( wp ) :: acc do concurrent ( k = 1 : nc ) local ( s , acc ) acc = diag ( k ) * e_old ( k ) do s = 1 , mv acc = acc - ke ( s , k ) * e_old ( nbr ( s , k )) end do e_new ( k ) = e_old ( k ) + omega * ( r ( k ) - acc ) * dinv ( k ) end do end subroutine agglom_jacobi_one subroutine agglom_jacobi_sweeps ( e , r , tmp , nbr , ke , diag , dinv , & mv , nc , omega , nu ) !! nu damped-Jacobi sweeps, ping-pong (e,tmp); latest iterate in `e`. integer , intent ( in ) :: mv , nc , nu real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: e ( nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r ( nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: tmp ( nc ) integer , intent ( in ) :: nbr ( mv , nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ke ( mv , nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: diag ( nc ), dinv ( nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: omega integer :: s , np np = nu / 2 do s = 1 , np call agglom_jacobi_one ( e , tmp , r , nbr , ke , diag , dinv , mv , nc , omega ) call agglom_jacobi_one ( tmp , e , r , nbr , ke , diag , dinv , mv , nc , omega ) end do if ( mod ( nu , 2 ) == 1 ) then call agglom_jacobi_one ( e , tmp , r , nbr , ke , diag , dinv , mv , nc , omega ) call agglom_copy ( tmp , e , nc ) end if end subroutine agglom_jacobi_sweeps subroutine agglom_residual ( e , r , res , nbr , ke , diag , mv , nc ) !! res = r - Ahat*e. integer , intent ( in ) :: mv , nc real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: e ( nc ), r ( nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: res ( nc ) integer , intent ( in ) :: nbr ( mv , nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ke ( mv , nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: diag ( nc ) integer :: k , s real ( wp ) :: acc do concurrent ( k = 1 : nc ) local ( s , acc ) acc = diag ( k ) * e ( k ) do s = 1 , mv acc = acc - ke ( s , k ) * e ( nbr ( s , k )) end do res ( k ) = r ( k ) - acc end do end subroutine agglom_residual subroutine agglom_restrict ( rf , rc , mstart , mlist , ncc , ncf ) !! rc = P&#94;T rf: each coarse cell sums its own fine members (cell-centric, !! race-free — a coarse cell writes only its own entry). integer , intent ( in ) :: ncc , ncf real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rf ( ncf ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rc ( ncc ) integer , intent ( in ) :: mstart ( ncc + 1 ) integer , intent ( in ) :: mlist ( ncf ) integer :: capI , i real ( wp ) :: acc do concurrent ( capI = 1 : ncc ) local ( i , acc ) acc = 0.0_wp do i = mstart ( capI ), mstart ( capI + 1 ) - 1 acc = acc + rf ( mlist ( i )) end do rc ( capI ) = acc end do end subroutine agglom_restrict subroutine agglom_prolong_add ( ec , ef , agg_of , ncf , ncc ) !! ef += P ec: each fine cell adds its parent aggregate's correction !! (piecewise-constant inject; fine cell writes only its own entry). integer , intent ( in ) :: ncf , ncc real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ec ( ncc ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: ef ( ncf ) integer , intent ( in ) :: agg_of ( ncf ) integer :: k do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncf ) ef ( k ) = ef ( k ) + ec ( agg_of ( k )) end do end subroutine agglom_prolong_add subroutine agglom_copy ( src , dst , nc ) integer , intent ( in ) :: nc real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: src ( nc ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: dst ( nc ) integer :: k do concurrent ( k = 1 : nc ) dst ( k ) = src ( k ) end do end subroutine agglom_copy subroutine agglom_zero ( a , nc ) integer , intent ( in ) :: nc real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: a ( nc ) integer :: k do concurrent ( k = 1 : nc ) a ( k ) = 0.0_wp end do end subroutine agglom_zero ! ====================================================================== !  V-CYCLE + PRECONDITIONER APPLY ! ====================================================================== recursive subroutine agglom_vcycle ( this , l ) !! One V(nu_pre,nu_post) cycle solving Ahat*e = r on level l from ZERO. !! On entry lev(l)%r holds the RHS; on exit lev(l)%e holds the solution. class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer , intent ( in ) :: l integer :: nc , ncc nc = this % lev ( l )% nc call agglom_zero ( this % lev ( l )% e , nc ) if ( l == this % n_levels ) then call agglom_jacobi_sweeps ( this % lev ( l )% e , this % lev ( l )% r , this % lev ( l )% tmp , & this % lev ( l )% nbr , this % lev ( l )% ke , & this % lev ( l )% diag , this % lev ( l )% dinv , & this % lev ( l )% mv , nc , & AGGLOM_OMEGA , AGGLOM_COARSE_SWEEPS ) return end if call agglom_jacobi_sweeps ( this % lev ( l )% e , this % lev ( l )% r , this % lev ( l )% tmp , & this % lev ( l )% nbr , this % lev ( l )% ke , & this % lev ( l )% diag , this % lev ( l )% dinv , & this % lev ( l )% mv , nc , & AGGLOM_OMEGA , AGGLOM_NU_PRE ) call agglom_residual ( this % lev ( l )% e , this % lev ( l )% r , this % lev ( l )% tmp , & this % lev ( l )% nbr , this % lev ( l )% ke , this % lev ( l )% diag , & this % lev ( l )% mv , nc ) ncc = this % lev ( l + 1 )% nc call agglom_restrict ( this % lev ( l )% tmp , this % lev ( l + 1 )% r , & this % lev ( l + 1 )% mstart , this % lev ( l + 1 )% mlist , ncc , nc ) call agglom_vcycle ( this , l + 1 ) call agglom_prolong_add ( this % lev ( l + 1 )% e , this % lev ( l )% e , & this % lev ( l )% agg_of , nc , ncc ) call agglom_jacobi_sweeps ( this % lev ( l )% e , this % lev ( l )% r , this % lev ( l )% tmp , & this % lev ( l )% nbr , this % lev ( l )% ke , & this % lev ( l )% diag , this % lev ( l )% dinv , & this % lev ( l )% mv , nc , & AGGLOM_OMEGA , AGGLOM_NU_POST ) end subroutine agglom_vcycle subroutine agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond ( this , r , z , area , nct , nco ) !! z = M&#94;{-1} r for the AREA-WEIGHTED outer PCG: form rhs_hat = area*r, !! run ONE V(2,2) cycle of the symmetric Ahat from zero, copy the !! correction into z (owned cells).  `r`/`z`/`area` are the fine !! (ncell_total-shaped) device arrays; only the first `nco` owned entries !! are touched (ghost band left as the caller set it — pre-zeroed). class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer , intent ( in ) :: nct , nco real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: z ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: area ( nct ) ! Direct-API belt: enable_si always builds; a caller that sets ! precond=mg without build_mg would deref unallocated levels. if ( this % n_levels < 1 ) then error stop \"agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond: hierarchy not built \" // & \"(state_unstr_enable_si builds it; direct callers must too)\" end if ! rhs_hat = area * r  ->  lev(1)%r  (symmetric-space RHS) call agglom_scale_into_shim ( r , area , this % lev ( 1 )% r , nct , nco ) call agglom_vcycle ( this , 1 ) call agglom_copy_out ( this % lev ( 1 )% e , z , nct , nco ) end subroutine agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond subroutine agglom_scale_into_shim ( src , fac , dst , nct , nco ) !! dst(1:nco) = fac*src (explicit-shape ncell_total state arrays -> the !! level-1 RHS buffer). integer , intent ( in ) :: nct , nco real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: src ( nct ), fac ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: dst ( nco ) integer :: k do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) dst ( k ) = fac ( k ) * src ( k ) end do end subroutine agglom_scale_into_shim subroutine agglom_copy_out ( src , dst , nct , nco ) !! dst(1:nco) = src (level-1 buffer -> state z, owned cells). integer , intent ( in ) :: nct , nco real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: src ( nco ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: dst ( nct ) integer :: k do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) dst ( k ) = src ( k ) end do end subroutine agglom_copy_out ! ====================================================================== !  enter/exit/destroy ! ====================================================================== subroutine agglom_level_enter_data ( this ) class ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this select type ( this ) type is ( agglom_level_unstr_t ) call agglom_level_enter_data_impl ( this ) end select end subroutine agglom_level_enter_data subroutine agglom_level_enter_data_impl ( lev ) type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: lev !$acc enter data copyin(lev%nbr, lev%n_nbr, lev%ke, lev%diag, lev%dinv) !$acc enter data copyin(lev%e, lev%r, lev%tmp) if ( allocated ( lev % agg_of )) then !$acc enter data copyin(lev%agg_of) end if if ( allocated ( lev % mstart )) then !$acc enter data copyin(lev%mstart, lev%mlist) end if end subroutine agglom_level_enter_data_impl subroutine agglom_level_exit_data ( this ) class ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this select type ( this ) type is ( agglom_level_unstr_t ) call agglom_level_exit_data_impl ( this ) end select end subroutine agglom_level_exit_data subroutine agglom_level_exit_data_impl ( lev ) type ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: lev if ( allocated ( lev % mstart )) then !$acc exit data delete(lev%mstart, lev%mlist) end if if ( allocated ( lev % agg_of )) then !$acc exit data delete(lev%agg_of) end if !$acc exit data delete(lev%e, lev%r, lev%tmp) !$acc exit data delete(lev%nbr, lev%n_nbr, lev%ke, lev%diag, lev%dinv) end subroutine agglom_level_exit_data_impl subroutine agglom_level_destroy ( this ) class ( agglom_level_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this if ( allocated ( this % n_nbr )) deallocate ( this % n_nbr ) if ( allocated ( this % nbr )) deallocate ( this % nbr ) if ( allocated ( this % agg_of )) deallocate ( this % agg_of ) if ( allocated ( this % mstart )) deallocate ( this % mstart ) if ( allocated ( this % mlist )) deallocate ( this % mlist ) if ( allocated ( this % ke )) deallocate ( this % ke ) if ( allocated ( this % diag )) deallocate ( this % diag ) if ( allocated ( this % dinv )) deallocate ( this % dinv ) if ( allocated ( this % e )) deallocate ( this % e ) if ( allocated ( this % r )) deallocate ( this % r ) if ( allocated ( this % tmp )) deallocate ( this % tmp ) this % nc = 0 this % mv = 0 end subroutine agglom_level_destroy subroutine agglom_hierarchy_enter_data ( this ) class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer :: l do l = 1 , this % n_levels call this % lev ( l )% enter_data () end do end subroutine agglom_hierarchy_enter_data subroutine agglom_hierarchy_exit_data ( this ) class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer :: l do l = 1 , this % n_levels call this % lev ( l )% exit_data () end do end subroutine agglom_hierarchy_exit_data subroutine agglom_hierarchy_destroy ( this ) class ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer :: l if ( allocated ( this % lev )) then do l = 1 , size ( this % lev ) call this % lev ( l )% destroy () end do deallocate ( this % lev ) end if this % n_levels = 0 end subroutine agglom_hierarchy_destroy pure function itoa ( i ) result ( s ) !! Minimal integer->string for the build log line. integer , intent ( in ) :: i character ( len = :), allocatable :: s character ( len = 32 ) :: buf write ( buf , \"(I0)\" ) i s = trim ( buf ) end function itoa end module rki_si_unstr_mg","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_si_unstr_mg.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_output.F90 – Rakali","text":"NetCDF solution output and restart file I/O This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_output.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_output.f90 rki_output.F90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90 rki_config.F90 sourcefile~rki_output.f90->sourcefile~rki_config.f90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_output.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_io_netcdf.f90 rki_io_netcdf.F90 sourcefile~rki_output.f90->sourcefile~rki_io_netcdf.f90 sourcefile~rki_state.f90 rki_state.F90 sourcefile~rki_output.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common_unstr.f90 rki_ml_common_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_common_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_nml_schema.f90 rki_nml_schema.F90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90->sourcefile~rki_nml_schema.f90 sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90 rki_recon_weno.F90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90->sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90 sourcefile~rki_io_netcdf.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_config.f90 sourcefile~rki_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_barotropic