f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_friction_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_keps_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_kpp_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_pressure_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_tracers_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_flux_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_fused_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_protect_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_update_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_dynamics_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_eos_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_friction_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_keps_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_kpp_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_pressure_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_tracers_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_truncate_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Multilayer (3D hydrostatic) solution state for the unstructured solver. module rki_multilayer_state_unstr !! Per-layer prognostic arrays (`(nz_ml, ncells_total)` axis order — !! layer index fastest, matching column-stencil kernels), vcoord !! definition + GPU mirror, diagnostic vertical velocity, EOS density !! + reference profile, tracer registry, per-step Jacobi/gradient !! workspaces, and the scalar physics parameters the kernels read. !! !! Lives at `state%multilayer`. Allocated by `state_unstr_init` when !! `nz_ml` is passed. Mirrors structured `multilayer_state_t` with the !! cell-centric axis order swapped. use rki_constants , only : wp , VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL , KEPS_STAB_CONSTANT use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t use rki_vcoord , only : vcoord_t use rki_tracer_unstr , only : unstr_tracer_t use rki_eos , only : eos_t use rki_boundary_unstr , only : MAX_BC_GROUPS use pic_logger , only : global_logger implicit none private public :: unstr_multilayer_state_t type :: unstr_multilayer_state_t !! Per-layer prognostic arrays + tracer registry + multilayer scalar config. ! Layer count integer :: nz_ml = 1 !! Number of multilayer sigma layers. ! Vertical coordinate definition + GPU mirror type ( vcoord_t ) :: vcoord !! Coordinate type (sigma / zsigma), remap method, parameters. real ( wp ), allocatable :: dsig_ml (:) !! Sigma layer fractions (nz_ml), sum = 1. real ( wp ), allocatable :: vcoord_z_ref (:) !! Reference z-level interfaces (0:nz_ml), GPU-mapped copy of !! `vcoord%z_ref`.  Top-level allocatable so OpenACC can map !! it without nested derived-type pointer issues. real ( wp ), allocatable :: vcoord_z_ref_col (:, :) !! Per-cell reference z-level interfaces for VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL, !! shape (0:nz_ml, ncells_total).  Built once at solver init !! from local bathymetry; static thereafter.  Only allocated !! when coord_type == VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL. ! Layer prognostic arrays (nz_ml, ncells_total) real ( wp ), allocatable :: h_layer (:, :) real ( wp ), allocatable :: hu_layer (:, :) real ( wp ), allocatable :: hv_layer (:, :) ! RK2 saves (dynamics only — tracer RK2 saves live on tracers(it)%hTr0) real ( wp ), allocatable :: h_layer0 (:, :) real ( wp ), allocatable :: hu_layer0 (:, :) real ( wp ), allocatable :: hv_layer0 (:, :) ! EOS-derived density real ( wp ), allocatable :: rho_layer (:, :) ! Diagnostic vertical velocity at layer interfaces real ( wp ), allocatable :: w_interface (:, :) !! `(nz_ml + 1, ncells_total)`. Index 1 = bed, nz_ml+1 = surface. ! Generic tracer registry. Salinity / temperature live as the ! first two entries by default; sediment / passive tracers append. type ( unstr_tracer_t ), allocatable :: tracers (:) integer :: idx_salinity = 0 !! Index into tracers(:) for salinity. 0 = not registered. integer :: idx_temperature = 0 !! Index into tracers(:) for temperature. 0 = not registered. logical :: registry_locked = . false . !! Set by `tracers_enter_data` (rki_state_unstr), cleared by !! `tracers_exit_data`.  While locked, !! `register_passive_tracer` REFUSES: the device map snapshots !! `tracers(:)` element-by-element, so growing the registry !! reallocates the array (and deep-copies every element's !! `hTr`/`hTr0`), stranding every existing tracer's device !! mapping on freed host addresses — an illegal address or a !! silent stale-host read on the `mem:separate` GPU build. ! Reference-density profile. Subtracted in both BPG kernels so the ! integrand is `rho - rho_ref(z)` rather than `rho - rho_0` ! -- 10-100x smaller in stratified water. integer :: nz_ref = 0 real ( wp ) :: rho_ref_dz = 0.0_wp real ( wp ), allocatable :: rho_ref (:) !! Reference density profile sampled at `iz * rho_ref_dz` for !! `iz = 0..nz_ref`. Index 0 = surface. ! Per-step kernel workspaces (allocated alongside the prognostic ! arrays; mapped at enter_data so kernels never allocate per step). real ( wp ), allocatable :: tracer_advect_scratch (:, :) !! Jacobi snapshot for `ml_advect_tracer_unstr` / MUSCL. real ( wp ), allocatable :: ml_lgrad_x (:, :) !! Limited Green-Gauss gradient (x) for MUSCL advection. real ( wp ), allocatable :: ml_lgrad_y (:, :) real ( wp ), allocatable :: ml_hdiff_hTr_pre (:, :) !! Jacobi snapshot for the horizontal-diffusion kernel. real ( wp ), allocatable :: ml_horvisc_hu_pre (:, :) !! Jacobi snapshot for the Smagorinsky horizontal-viscosity kernel. real ( wp ), allocatable :: ml_horvisc_hv_pre (:, :) ! Barotropic momentum snapshot (saved before HLL update so ! `ml_distribute_barotropic_unstr` can spread the increment). real ( wp ), allocatable :: xmom_pre (:) real ( wp ), allocatable :: ymom_pre (:) ! Saved layer thicknesses before vertical-coordinate update. ! Only allocated when vcoord%needs_remap(). real ( wp ), allocatable :: remap_dz_old (:, :) ! ----- Scalar physics parameters ----- real ( wp ) :: initial_salinity = 3 5.0_wp real ( wp ) :: S_init_surface = 0.0_wp !! Linear-S(z) stratification, surface (k=nz) value.  When both !! S_init_surface and S_init_bottom are non-zero (and nz>1) the !! salinity seed becomes a linear profile from S_init_bottom at !! the bed (k=1) to S_init_surface at the surface; otherwise the !! uniform initial_salinity is used.  Stable polarity is the !! inverse of temperature: S_init_bottom > S_init_surface (salty !! bed, fresh surface). real ( wp ) :: S_init_bottom = 0.0_wp !! Linear-S(z) stratification, bed (k=1) value.  See S_init_surface. real ( wp ) :: S_ref = 0.0_wp real ( wp ) :: beta_S = 0.78_wp real ( wp ) :: S_min = 0.0_wp real ( wp ) :: S_max = 4 0.0_wp real ( wp ) :: kappa_S_bg = 1.0e-5_wp real ( wp ) :: initial_temperature = 1 5.0_wp real ( wp ) :: T_init_surface = 0.0_wp !! Linear-T(z) stratification, surface (k=nz) value.  When both !! T_init_surface and T_init_bottom are non-zero (and nz>1) the !! temperature seed becomes a linear profile from T_init_bottom at !! the bed (k=1) to T_init_surface at the surface; otherwise the !! uniform initial_temperature is used.  Mirrors the ocean path. real ( wp ) :: T_init_bottom = 0.0_wp !! Linear-T(z) stratification, bed (k=1) value.  See T_init_surface. real ( wp ) :: T_ref = 1 5.0_wp real ( wp ) :: alpha_T = 0.17_wp real ( wp ) :: T_min = - 2.0_wp real ( wp ) :: T_max = 4 0.0_wp real ( wp ) :: kappa_T_bg = 1.0e-5_wp real ( wp ) :: rho_0 = 100 0.0_wp !! Reference density for the linear EOS / Boussinesq scaling. ! Shared (ocean) nonlinear EOS — opt-in via `&tracer_nml eos_form` logical :: eos_use_shared = . false . !! When .true. `ml_equation_of_state_unstr` routes through the !! shared `rki_eos` point evaluation instead of the !! legacy linear kernel.  Default off ⇒ bit-identical.  Set !! from `&tracer_nml eos_form` via `ml_parse_eos_form` !! (driver). type ( eos_t ) :: eos !! Shared EOS handle (variant tag + scalar coefficients) for !! the opt-in path.  Flat POD — passed by value into the !! device kernel, no enter_data/exit_data mapping needed. !! `eos%rho0` mirrors `rho_0`; `eos%p_ref` stays 0 ⇒ !! surface/potential density. ! Pacanowski-Philander vertical mixing real ( wp ) :: vmix_nu_max = 0.01_wp real ( wp ) :: vmix_nu_bg = 1.0e-4_wp real ( wp ) :: vmix_ri_alpha = 5.0_wp ! KPP (Large et al. 1994) surface-boundary-layer overlay. When ! `vmix_use_kpp` is on, the solver swaps PP81 vmix for the KPP ! kernels (`rki_ml_kpp_unstr`): bulk-Ri BL-depth sweep, shape- ! function-enhanced diffusivity over PP81, non-local counter- ! gradient tracer transport. Per-cell fields allocated ! unconditionally (API can flip vmix_use_kpp after init; gating the ! allocation would leave them unmapped). logical :: vmix_use_kpp = . false . !! Master switch for the KPP overlay (default off = pure PP81). real ( wp ) :: kpp_ri_crit = 0.3_wp !! Critical bulk Richardson number for the BL-depth sweep. real ( wp ) :: kpp_cs_nonlocal = 6.3_wp !! Non-local transport coefficient C_s (LMD94 eq 20). real ( wp ) :: kpp_c_vt2 = 1.8_wp !! Unresolved-turbulence coefficient for V_t&#94;2 (LMD94 eq 23). real ( wp ), allocatable :: kpp_bl_depth (:) !! Diagnosed boundary-layer depth (m, positive down), per cell. !! Persists across steps — the previous value seeds the V_t&#94;2 !! velocity scale (self-bootstraps from zero on the first call). real ( wp ), allocatable :: kpp_u_star (:) !! Surface friction velocity sqrt(|tau|/rho_0) (m/s), per cell. real ( wp ), allocatable :: kpp_buoy_flux (:) !! Surface buoyancy flux B_0 (m&#94;2/s&#94;3); <0 = destabilizing. ! k-epsilon (two-equation GLS) vertical mixing. When `vmix_use_keps` ! is on, the solver swaps PP81/KPP for `rki_ml_keps_unstr`. Allocated ! unconditionally (mirrors KPP). Default off = bit-identical. logical :: vmix_use_keps = . false . !! Master switch for the k-epsilon closure (default off). integer :: keps_stability = KEPS_STAB_CONSTANT !! Stability-function scheme: constant / galperin / canuto. integer :: keps_si_picard = 1 !! Picard iteration count for the SI k-eps solve (1 = single pass; !! 2+ enables save/restore of the pre-step tke/eps and re-runs !! ml_keps_update_unstr from the same initial state with the !! refreshed nu_t production coefficient).  Mirrors the structured !! `keps_si_picard` knob. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_tke0 (:, :) !! Pre-step TKE save slot (nz+1, ncells_total); allocated only when !! vmix_use_keps .and. keps_si_picard > 1. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_eps0 (:, :) !! Pre-step dissipation-rate save slot (nz+1, ncells_total); co- !! allocated with keps_tke0. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_tke (:, :) !! Turbulent kinetic energy at interfaces (nz+1, ncell); state. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_eps (:, :) !! Dissipation rate at interfaces (nz+1, ncell); state. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_nut (:, :) !! Eddy viscosity at interfaces (nz+1, ncell); carried across steps. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_kt (:, :) !! Scalar (tracer) diffusivity at interfaces (nz+1, ncell); carried. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_ustar_s (:) !! Surface friction velocity sqrt(|tau_wind|/rho_0) (m/s), per cell. real ( wp ), allocatable :: keps_ustar_b (:) !! Bed friction velocity (m/s), per cell. ! Horizontal mixing real ( wp ) :: hdiff_kappa = 0.0_wp real ( wp ) :: smagorinsky_cs = 0.0_wp ! Scheme flags logical :: use_bpg_jacobian = . true . !! Use the pressure-Jacobian BPG (Shchepetkin & McWilliams 2003). !! DEFAULT ON.  The sigma alternative differences the integrated !! density anomaly at constant SIGMA INDEX, which over sloping !! bathymetry produces a fictitious force proportional to !! (uniform density anomaly) x (bed slope) -- so a column of !! spatially UNIFORM density whose value differs from `rho_0` is !! spuriously accelerated, and the resulting flow leaks mass !! (measured: 1.7e-6 relative over 400 steps, vs 1.3e-14 with the !! Jacobian).  Pinned by `test_bpg_uniform_density`. logical :: use_ppm_tracer = . true . !! Use MUSCL for tracer advection (false = first-order upwind). logical :: evap_mass_sink = . false . !! When true, net evaporation is a real water-mass sink removed !! COLUMN-PROPORTIONALLY (salt held, heat carried away with the !! water) rather than a virtual salt flux.  Mirrors the structured !! `evap_mass_sink`.  Default false = bit-identical (virtual salt). logical :: evap_latent_cooling = . false . !! When true (needs evap_mass_sink), evaporation additionally !! withdraws its latent heat of vaporization from the surface layer !! (k=nz).  Mirrors the structured `evap_latent_cooling`.  Default !! false = bit-identical. ! ----- Per-BC-group tracer inflow values ----- real ( wp ) :: bc_S_ext ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = 3 5.0_wp real ( wp ) :: bc_T_ext ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = 1 5.0_wp contains procedure , non_overridable :: init => unstr_multilayer_init procedure , non_overridable :: destroy => unstr_multilayer_destroy procedure , non_overridable :: enter_data => unstr_multilayer_enter_data procedure , non_overridable :: exit_data => unstr_multilayer_exit_data procedure , non_overridable :: register_passive_tracer => unstr_multilayer_register_passive_tracer end type unstr_multilayer_state_t contains subroutine unstr_multilayer_init ( this , mesh , nz_ml ) !! Allocate every multilayer array at the cell counts in `mesh` !! and the configured layer count.  Initialises `vcoord` from !! its (already-set) `coord_type` / `remap_method`, allocates !! the rho-ref profile, and registers the salinity + temperature !! tracers in the tracer registry. !! !! Caller must have set `this%nz_ml` (or pass it via `nz_ml`), !! `this%vcoord%coord_type` / `remap_method`, and any other !! vcoord parameters before calling. class ( unstr_multilayer_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nz_ml integer :: n , nz n = mesh % ncells_total nz = nz_ml this % nz_ml = nz call this % vcoord % init ( nz , this % vcoord % coord_type , & this % vcoord % remap_method ) allocate ( this % dsig_ml ( nz )) this % dsig_ml = this % vcoord % dsig_target ! GPU-mappable copy of z_ref allocate ( this % vcoord_z_ref ( 0 : nz ), source = 0.0_wp ) if ( allocated ( this % vcoord % z_ref )) then this % vcoord_z_ref = this % vcoord % z_ref end if ! Full z* per-cell z_ref. Allocated here; per-cell contents filled ! from bathymetry by `ml_build_vcoord_zstar_full_unstr` later. if ( this % vcoord % coord_type == VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL ) then allocate ( this % vcoord_z_ref_col ( 0 : nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if allocate ( this % h_layer ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hu_layer ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hv_layer ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % rho_layer ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % w_interface ( nz + 1 , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % h_layer0 ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hu_layer0 ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % hv_layer0 ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) ! KPP per-cell boundary-layer workspace (always allocated; tiny). allocate ( this % kpp_bl_depth ( n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % kpp_u_star ( n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % kpp_buoy_flux ( n ), source = 0.0_wp ) ! k-epsilon interface state — allocated unconditionally (mirrors KPP). ! Seeds mirror the structured path. allocate ( this % keps_tke ( nz + 1 , n ), source = 1.0e-6_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_eps ( nz + 1 , n ), source = 1.0e-8_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_nut ( nz + 1 , n ), source = 1.0e-4_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_kt ( nz + 1 , n ), source = 1.0e-4_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_ustar_s ( n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_ustar_b ( n ), source = 0.0_wp ) ! Picard save slots: only needed when keps_si_picard > 1.  The caller ! (rki_driver / test) sets keps_si_picard BEFORE calling init, so the ! allocation can happen here. if ( this % vmix_use_keps . and . this % keps_si_picard > 1 ) then allocate ( this % keps_tke0 ( nz + 1 , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % keps_eps0 ( nz + 1 , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if allocate ( this % tracer_advect_scratch ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % ml_lgrad_x ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % ml_lgrad_y ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % ml_hdiff_hTr_pre ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % ml_horvisc_hu_pre ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % ml_horvisc_hv_pre ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % xmom_pre ( n ), source = 0.0_wp ) allocate ( this % ymom_pre ( n ), source = 0.0_wp ) if ( this % vcoord % needs_remap ()) then allocate ( this % remap_dz_old ( nz , n ), source = 0.0_wp ) end if ! Reference-density profile: 100 piecewise-linear samples. this % nz_ref = 100 allocate ( this % rho_ref ( 0 : this % nz_ref ), source = 0.0_wp ) this % rho_ref_dz = 0.0_wp ! Default tracer registry: salinity at index 1, temperature at index 2. allocate ( this % tracers ( 2 )) this % idx_salinity = 1 this % idx_temperature = 2 call this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% init ( mesh , nz ) call this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% init ( mesh , nz ) this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% name = \"salinity\" this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% long_name = \"Sea water salinity\" this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% units = \"PSU\" this % tracers ( this % idx_salinity )% standard_name = \"sea_water_salinity\" this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% name = \"temperature\" this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% long_name = \"Sea water potential temperature\" this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% units = \"degC\" this % tracers ( this % idx_temperature )% standard_name = \"sea_water_potential_temperature\" end subroutine unstr_multilayer_init subroutine unstr_multilayer_register_passive_tracer ( this , mesh , name , tr_init , & tr_min , tr_max , kappa_bg , & hdiff_kappa ) !! Append a passive tracer (eos_coeff = 0) to the registry. Must be !! called AFTER `init` and BEFORE `state_unstr_enter_data` (so the !! new tracer's `hTr` gets device-mapped) — enforced via !! `registry_locked`: once the registry is device-mapped the call !! logs an error and returns without touching it. S/T keep their !! indices. class ( unstr_multilayer_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tr_init , tr_min , tr_max , kappa_bg , hdiff_kappa type ( unstr_tracer_t ), allocatable :: tmp (:) integer :: n_old , it if ( this % registry_locked ) then call global_logger % error ( \"unstr_multilayer_state: register_passive_tracer(\" // & trim ( name ) // \") refused — registry locked by \" // & \"enter_data (growing the registry now would strand \" // & \"every existing tracer's device mapping on the \" // & \"mem:separate GPU build)\" ) return end if n_old = size ( this % tracers ) call move_alloc ( this % tracers , tmp ) allocate ( this % tracers ( n_old + 1 )) ! Deep-copy the existing tracers (intrinsic assignment reallocates ! the allocatable hTr / hTr0 components and copies their data). do it = 1 , n_old this % tracers ( it ) = tmp ( it ) end do it = n_old + 1 call this % tracers ( it )% init ( mesh , this % nz_ml ) this % tracers ( it )% name = trim ( name ) this % tracers ( it )% long_name = trim ( name ) this % tracers ( it )% units = \"1\" this % tracers ( it )% standard_name = \"\" this % tracers ( it )% tr_init = tr_init this % tracers ( it )% tr_inflow = tr_init this % tracers ( it )% bc_ext = tr_init this % tracers ( it )% tr_min = tr_min this % tracers ( it )% tr_max = tr_max this % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg = kappa_bg this % tracers ( it )% hdiff_kappa = hdiff_kappa this % tracers ( it )% eos_coeff = 0.0_wp this % tracers ( it )% eos_ref = 0.0_wp end subroutine unstr_multilayer_register_passive_tracer subroutine unstr_multilayer_destroy ( this ) class ( unstr_multilayer_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer :: it call this % vcoord % cleanup () if ( allocated ( this % vcoord_z_ref )) deallocate ( this % vcoord_z_ref ) if ( allocated ( this % vcoord_z_ref_col )) deallocate ( this % vcoord_z_ref_col ) if ( allocated ( this % dsig_ml )) deallocate ( this % dsig_ml ) if ( allocated ( this % h_layer )) deallocate ( this % h_layer ) if ( allocated ( this % hu_layer )) deallocate ( this % hu_layer ) if ( allocated ( this % hv_layer )) deallocate ( this % hv_layer ) if ( allocated ( this % h_layer0 )) deallocate ( this % h_layer0 ) if ( allocated ( this % hu_layer0 )) deallocate ( this % hu_layer0 ) if ( allocated ( this % hv_layer0 )) deallocate ( this % hv_layer0 ) if ( allocated ( this % rho_layer )) deallocate ( this % rho_layer ) if ( allocated ( this % w_interface )) deallocate ( this % w_interface ) if ( allocated ( this % kpp_bl_depth )) deallocate ( this % kpp_bl_depth ) if ( allocated ( this % kpp_u_star )) deallocate ( this % kpp_u_star ) if ( allocated ( this % kpp_buoy_flux )) deallocate ( this % kpp_buoy_flux ) if ( allocated ( this % keps_tke )) deallocate ( this % keps_tke ) if ( allocated ( this % keps_eps )) deallocate ( this % keps_eps ) if ( allocated ( this % keps_nut )) deallocate ( this % keps_nut ) if ( allocated ( this % keps_kt )) deallocate ( this % keps_kt ) if ( allocated ( this % keps_ustar_s )) deallocate ( this % keps_ustar_s ) if ( allocated ( this % keps_ustar_b )) deallocate ( this % keps_ustar_b ) if ( allocated ( this % keps_tke0 )) deallocate ( this % keps_tke0 ) if ( allocated ( this % keps_eps0 )) deallocate ( this % keps_eps0 ) if ( allocated ( this % rho_ref )) deallocate ( this % rho_ref ) if ( allocated ( this % tracer_advect_scratch )) deallocate ( this % tracer_advect_scratch ) if ( allocated ( this % ml_lgrad_x )) deallocate ( this % ml_lgrad_x ) if ( allocated ( this % ml_lgrad_y )) deallocate ( this % ml_lgrad_y ) if ( allocated ( this % ml_hdiff_hTr_pre )) deallocate ( this % ml_hdiff_hTr_pre ) if ( allocated ( this % ml_horvisc_hu_pre )) deallocate ( this % ml_horvisc_hu_pre ) if ( allocated ( this % ml_horvisc_hv_pre )) deallocate ( this % ml_horvisc_hv_pre ) if ( allocated ( this % xmom_pre )) deallocate ( this % xmom_pre ) if ( allocated ( this % ymom_pre )) deallocate ( this % ymom_pre ) if ( allocated ( this % remap_dz_old )) deallocate ( this % remap_dz_old ) this % nz_ml = 1 this % nz_ref = 0 this % rho_ref_dz = 0.0_wp if ( allocated ( this % tracers )) then do it = 1 , size ( this % tracers ) call this % tracers ( it )% destroy () end do deallocate ( this % tracers ) end if this % idx_salinity = 0 this % idx_temperature = 0 this % registry_locked = . false . end subroutine unstr_multilayer_destroy subroutine unstr_multilayer_enter_data ( this ) !! Map the multilayer allocatables onto the device. Parent !! `state%multilayer` rides over with the parent `copyin(state)`; !! only the inner allocatables need explicit attaches. The tracer !! registry's two-step attach is handled by `tracers_enter_data` !! (in `rki_state_unstr`). class ( unstr_multilayer_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this !$acc enter data copyin(this%dsig_ml, & !$acc&                  this%h_layer, this%hu_layer, this%hv_layer, & !$acc&                  this%rho_layer, this%w_interface, & !$acc&                  this%h_layer0, this%hu_layer0, this%hv_layer0, & !$acc&                  this%rho_ref, & !$acc&                  this%kpp_bl_depth, this%kpp_u_star, this%kpp_buoy_flux) !$acc enter data create(this%xmom_pre, this%ymom_pre, & !$acc&                  this%tracer_advect_scratch, & !$acc&                  this%ml_lgrad_x, this%ml_lgrad_y, & !$acc&                  this%ml_hdiff_hTr_pre, & !$acc&                  this%ml_horvisc_hu_pre, this%ml_horvisc_hv_pre) !$acc enter data copyin(this%keps_tke, this%keps_eps, this%keps_nut, & !$acc&                  this%keps_kt, this%keps_ustar_s, this%keps_ustar_b) if ( allocated ( this % keps_tke0 )) then !$acc enter data copyin(this%keps_tke0, this%keps_eps0) end if if ( allocated ( this % vcoord_z_ref )) then !$acc enter data copyin(this%vcoord_z_ref) end if if ( allocated ( this % vcoord_z_ref_col )) then !$acc enter data copyin(this%vcoord_z_ref_col) end if if ( allocated ( this % remap_dz_old )) then !$acc enter data create(this%remap_dz_old) end if end subroutine unstr_multilayer_enter_data subroutine unstr_multilayer_exit_data ( this ) class ( unstr_multilayer_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this !$acc exit data copyout(this%h_layer, this%hu_layer, this%hv_layer, & !$acc&                  this%rho_layer, this%w_interface) !$acc exit data delete(this%dsig_ml, & !$acc&                 this%h_layer0, this%hu_layer0, this%hv_layer0, & !$acc&                 this%xmom_pre, this%ymom_pre, & !$acc&                 this%tracer_advect_scratch, & !$acc&                 this%ml_lgrad_x, this%ml_lgrad_y, & !$acc&                 this%ml_hdiff_hTr_pre, & !$acc&                 this%ml_horvisc_hu_pre, this%ml_horvisc_hv_pre, & !$acc&                 this%rho_ref, & !$acc&                 this%kpp_bl_depth, this%kpp_u_star, this%kpp_buoy_flux) !$acc exit data delete(this%keps_tke, this%keps_eps, this%keps_nut, & !$acc&                 this%keps_kt, this%keps_ustar_s, this%keps_ustar_b) if ( allocated ( this % keps_tke0 )) then !$acc exit data delete(this%keps_tke0, this%keps_eps0) end if if ( allocated ( this % vcoord_z_ref_col )) then !$acc exit data delete(this%vcoord_z_ref_col) end if if ( allocated ( this % vcoord_z_ref )) then !$acc exit data delete(this%vcoord_z_ref) end if if ( allocated ( this % remap_dz_old )) then !$acc exit data delete(this%remap_dz_old) end if end subroutine unstr_multilayer_exit_data end module rki_multilayer_state_unstr","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_friction_unstr.F90 – Rakali","text":"Bottom friction + wind stress kernel for the unstructured solver This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90 rki_kernel_friction_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 rki_mesh_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 rki_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90 rki_barotropic_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 rki_boundary_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90 rki_multilayer_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_common.f90 rki_si_common.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90 rki_si_unstr_state.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_surface_forcing_unstr.f90 rki_surface_forcing_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_surface_forcing_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_timestepper.f90 rki_timestepper.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_timestepper.f90 sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90 rki_eos.F90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_eos.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90 rki_tracer_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90 rki_vcoord.F90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 rki_si_unstr_mg.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 sourcefile~rki_surface_forcing_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_surface_forcing_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_timestepper.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90 rki_kernel_friction_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 rki_solver_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Bottom friction + wind stress kernel for the unstructured solver module rki_kernel_friction_unstr !! Apply Manning bottom friction and surface wind stress to the !! centroid momenta (bundled to mirror the structured solver). !! !! Friction (semi-implicit, unconditionally stable): !!   c_f = g*n&#94;2/h&#94;{1/3}; denom = 1 + dt*c_f*|u|/h; M /= denom. !! Wind stress (explicit): M += dt*tau/RHO_WATER, with the uniform !! `state%wind_tau_{x,y}` in Pa. !! !! No-ops by default: friction skips when `manning_n == 0`, wind when !! both components are zero; both inactive returns immediately. Dry !! cells (depth below `state%minimum_allowed_height`) are skipped to !! avoid the `1/h&#94;{4/3}` singularity. use rki_constants , only : wp , GRAVITY , RHO_WATER use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t use rki_state_unstr , only : unstr_state_t implicit none private public :: apply_manning_friction_unstr contains pure subroutine apply_manning_friction_unstr ( state , mesh , dt ) !! Semi-implicit Manning friction + explicit wind stress over !! every owned cell. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: k real ( wp ) :: h_val , u_val , v_val , speed , cf , denom real ( wp ) :: n_sq , min_h , tau_x_over_rho , tau_y_over_rho logical :: has_friction , has_wind if ( dt <= 0.0_wp ) return has_friction = state % barotropic % manning_n > 0.0_wp has_wind = ( state % barotropic % wind_tau_x /= 0.0_wp ) . or . ( state % barotropic % wind_tau_y /= 0.0_wp ) if (. not . has_friction . and . . not . has_wind ) return n_sq = state % barotropic % manning_n * state % barotropic % manning_n min_h = state % minimum_allowed_height tau_x_over_rho = state % barotropic % wind_tau_x / RHO_WATER tau_y_over_rho = state % barotropic % wind_tau_y / RHO_WATER do concurrent ( k = 1 : mesh % ncells_owned ) & local ( h_val , u_val , v_val , speed , cf , denom ) h_val = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) - state % barotropic % bed_cv ( k ) if ( h_val > min_h ) then if ( has_friction ) then u_val = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) / h_val v_val = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) / h_val speed = sqrt ( u_val * u_val + v_val * v_val ) cf = GRAVITY * n_sq / ( h_val ** ( 1.0_wp / 3.0_wp )) denom = 1.0_wp + dt * cf * speed / h_val state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) / denom state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) / denom end if if ( has_wind ) then state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) + dt * tau_x_over_rho state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) + dt * tau_y_over_rho end if end if end do end subroutine apply_manning_friction_unstr end module rki_kernel_friction_unstr","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_kernel_friction_unstr.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_eos.F90 – Rakali","text":"Equation of state and reference-density profile for the structured\nmultilayer solver. This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_ml_eos.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90 rki_ml_eos.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90 rki_eos.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_eos.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90 rki_ml_common.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_ml_eos.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90 rki_ml_eos.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90 sourcefile~rki_init.f90 rki_init.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_init.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 rki_solver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 sourcefile~rki_state.f90 rki_state.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_coastal_console_stats.f90 rki_coastal_console_stats.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_coastal_console_stats.f90 sourcefile~rki_forcing.f90 rki_forcing.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_forcing.f90 sourcefile~rki_gauges.f90 rki_gauges.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_gauges.f90 sourcefile~rki_nesting.f90 rki_nesting.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_nesting.f90 sourcefile~rki_output.f90 rki_output.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_output.f90 sourcefile~rki_init.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90 sourcefile~rki_init.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_eos.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_init.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 rki_handle.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_output.f90 sourcefile~rki_coastal_console_stats.f90->sourcefile~rki_init.f90 sourcefile~rki_coastal_console_stats.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_flux_dump.f90 rki_flux_dump.F90 sourcefile~rki_flux_dump.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_forcing.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_gauges.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_handle.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_nesting.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_output.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Equation of state and reference-density profile for the structured !! multilayer solver. module rki_ml_eos !! Linear two-tracer EOS `rho = rho_0 + beta_S*(S-S_ref) - alpha_T*(T-T_ref)` !! and the horizontally-uniform `rho_ref(z)` profile used by the !! Jacobian baroclinic pressure gradient. use rki_constants , only : wp , DRY_TOLERANCE use rki_grid , only : hgrid_t use rki_ml_common , only : ML_MIN_DEPTH use rki_eos , only : eos_t , eos_compute_arrays , & EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR , EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 , & EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV implicit none private public :: ml_equation_of_state public :: ml_equation_of_state_shared public :: ml_parse_eos_form public :: ml_compute_reference_density contains subroutine ml_parse_eos_form ( name , use_shared , variant ) !! Translate the coastal `&tracer_nml eos_form` knob into the !! (use_shared, EOS_VARIANT_*) pair held on the multilayer state. !! !! `\"linear\"` (the default) keeps the legacy coastal linear kernel !! (`ml_equation_of_state` / `ml_equation_of_state_unstr`) — the !! bit-identity-by-construction path.  `\"wright\"` / `\"roquet_spv\"` !! opt in to the shared nonlinear EOS (`rki_eos`) via !! `ml_equation_of_state_shared{,_unstr}`.  The shared !! `EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR` is deliberately NOT reachable from this !! knob: it is a different linear formulation from the coastal !! kernel and exposing both invites silent near-miss configs. !! Unknown strings fail loud (configure time). character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name logical , intent ( out ) :: use_shared integer , intent ( out ) :: variant select case ( trim ( adjustl ( name ))) case ( \"linear\" , \"\" ) use_shared = . false . variant = EOS_VARIANT_LINEAR case ( \"wright\" , \"wright_97\" , \"wright97\" ) use_shared = . true . variant = EOS_VARIANT_WRIGHT_97 case ( \"roquet_spv\" , \"roquet\" ) use_shared = . true . variant = EOS_VARIANT_ROQUET_SPV case default error stop \"ml_parse_eos_form: unknown eos_form (use linear | \" // & \"wright | roquet_spv)\" end select end subroutine ml_parse_eos_form subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , & rho_layer , eos , grid , nz ) !! Opt-in coastal entry to the SHARED (ocean) equation of state — !! selected by `&tracer_nml eos_form = \"wright\" | \"roquet_spv\"`. !! Thin forwarding shim onto the regime-agnostic !! `eos_compute_arrays` variant dispatch; evaluation is at !! `eos%p_ref` (default 0 Pa ⇒ surface/potential density — the !! right choice for the coastal depth range) with the shared !! `H_VANISHED` vanishing-layer fallback to `eos%rho0` (note: the !! legacy coastal kernel gates on `DRY_TOLERANCE` instead).  The !! `eos_t` handle is a flat POD — its scalars are read on !! the host here and passed by value into the device kernels, so !! no device mapping of the handle is required. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hS_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hT_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) type ( eos_t ), intent ( in ) :: eos !! Shared EOS handle (variant + scalar coefficients). call eos_compute_arrays ( eos , h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , & rho_layer , grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) end subroutine ml_equation_of_state_shared pure subroutine ml_equation_of_state ( h_layer , hS_layer , hT_layer , rho_layer , & rho_0 , beta_S , S_ref , & alpha_T , T_ref , & grid , nz ) !! Linear two-tracer equation of state: !!   rho_k = rho_0 + beta_S * (S_k - S_ref) - alpha_T * (T_k - T_ref) !! where S_k = hS_k / h_k and T_k = hT_k / h_k. !! !! Setting alpha_T = 0 makes temperature a passive tracer (no density !! feedback).  Setting S_ref = 0 reproduces the one-tracer legacy form !! rho = rho_0 + beta_S*S. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hS_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hT_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho_0 !! Reference density (kg/m&#94;3) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: beta_S !! Haline contraction coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per PSU) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: S_ref !! Reference salinity (PSU) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: alpha_T !! Thermal expansion coefficient (kg/m&#94;3 per degC) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: T_ref !! Reference temperature (degC) integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny real ( wp ) :: S_k , T_k , inv_h nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total ! Compute rho for ALL cells including ghost cells, because the ! baroclinic pressure gradient uses central differences that access ! ghost cell rho values.  Ghost cells already have valid h_layer ! (from ml_apply_layer_bcs) and hS/hT_layer (from ml_apply_tracer_bcs). do concurrent ( k = 1 : nz , j = 1 : ny , i = 1 : nx ) & local ( S_k , T_k , inv_h ) if ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) > DRY_TOLERANCE ) then inv_h = 1.0_wp / h_layer ( i , j , k ) S_k = hS_layer ( i , j , k ) * inv_h T_k = hT_layer ( i , j , k ) * inv_h else S_k = S_ref T_k = T_ref end if rho_layer ( i , j , k ) = rho_0 + beta_S * ( S_k - S_ref ) - alpha_T * ( T_k - T_ref ) end do end subroutine ml_equation_of_state subroutine ml_compute_reference_density ( h_layer , rho_layer , & rho_ref , rho_ref_dz , nz_ref , & rho_0 , & grid , nz ) !! Build the horizontally-uniform reference-density profile !! `rho_ref(z)` from the current `rho_layer`.  Sampled on a uniform !! z-grid `0..rho_ref_dz*nz_ref`, area-weighted across interior cells. !! !! Subtracted by both BPG kernels so the integrand becomes the !! density anomaly `rho - rho_ref(z)` -- 10-100x smaller than !! `rho - rho_0` in stratified water (Phase B2). !! !! Computed on the host: copies layer fields back from the device, !! builds the profile, and pushes `rho_ref` to the device.  Single !! one-time D2H+H2D, negligible at init. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz , nz_ref real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_ref ( 0 : nz_ref ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rho_ref_dz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rho_0 integer :: i , j , k , iz , ncells , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: H_max , H_col , dz , z , z_top , z_bot , rho_at_z real ( wp ), allocatable :: sum_rho (:) nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost !$acc update self(h_layer, rho_layer) if_present H_max = 0.0_wp do j = nghost + 1 , ny - nghost do i = nghost + 1 , nx - nghost H_col = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz H_col = H_col + h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do if ( H_col > H_max ) H_max = H_col end do end do if ( H_max <= 0.0_wp ) then rho_ref = rho_0 rho_ref_dz = 0.0_wp !$acc update device(rho_ref) if_present return end if H_max = 1.05_wp * H_max dz = H_max / real ( nz_ref , wp ) rho_ref_dz = dz allocate ( sum_rho ( 0 : nz_ref ), source = 0.0_wp ) ncells = 0 do j = nghost + 1 , ny - nghost do i = nghost + 1 , nx - nghost H_col = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , nz H_col = H_col + h_layer ( i , j , k ) end do if ( H_col < ML_MIN_DEPTH ) cycle ncells = ncells + 1 do iz = 0 , nz_ref z = real ( iz , wp ) * dz z_top = 0.0_wp rho_at_z = rho_layer ( i , j , nz ) if ( z >= H_col ) then rho_at_z = rho_layer ( i , j , 1 ) else do k = nz , 1 , - 1 z_bot = z_top + h_layer ( i , j , k ) if ( z >= z_top . and . z <= z_bot ) then rho_at_z = rho_layer ( i , j , k ) exit end if z_top = z_bot end do end if sum_rho ( iz ) = sum_rho ( iz ) + rho_at_z end do end do end do if ( ncells > 0 ) then do iz = 0 , nz_ref rho_ref ( iz ) = sum_rho ( iz ) / real ( ncells , wp ) end do else rho_ref = rho_0 end if deallocate ( sum_rho ) !$acc update device(rho_ref) if_present end subroutine ml_compute_reference_density end module rki_ml_eos","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_ml_eos.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_update.F90 – Rakali","text":"Conservative state update kernels This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_kernel_update.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_update.f90 rki_kernel_update.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_update.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_update.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_kernel_update.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_update.f90 rki_kernel_update.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 rki_solver.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_update.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Conservative state update kernels module rki_kernel_update !! Advances the conserved variables: forward Euler update (each RK !! stage) and the SSP-RK2 averaging step. !! !! Thin-cell treatment (all three kernels, in order): !!  1. negative depths are clamped to zero (momentum zeroed); !!  2. genuinely dry cells (`h < DRY_TOLERANCE`) have momentum zeroed; !!  3. thin-but-wet cells (`h < eps = DESING_EPS`) get the !!     Kurganov & Petrova (2007) desingularized velocity !!     `u = sqrt(2) h hu / sqrt(h&#94;4 + max(h&#94;4, eps&#94;4))` with momentum !!     reconstructed as `hu := h*u`.  For `h >= eps` the formula is the !!     identity `u = hu/h`, so well-resolved cells are left bit-exact; !!  4. a last-resort Froude backstop `|u| <= FROUDE_BACKSTOP*sqrt(g h)` !!     arrests the thin-film velocity runaway that develops at wet/dry !!     fronts on sloping beds (measured: u -> 4e3 m/s at h ~ 3.5 mm and !!     a ~2000x dt collapse without it).  It is far above any depth !!     ratio this scheme can resolve, so it never shapes the physics — !!     see the constant's docstring for the measurements. !! !! `eps` is the same DESING_EPS used by `compute_timestep`, so the !! update and the CFL estimator agree about what \"thin\" means. use rki_constants , only : wp , GRAVITY , DRY_TOLERANCE , DESING_EPS , & FROUDE_BACKSTOP use rki_grid , only : hgrid_t implicit none private public :: compute_update public :: compute_rk2_average public :: compute_ssp_combine contains pure subroutine compute_update ( h , hu , hv , flux_h , flux_hu , flux_hv , & grid , dt ) !! Forward Euler update U = U + dt*RHS (each SSP-RK2 stage). Also !! enforces non-negative depth, zeroes momentum in dry cells, and !! desingularizes thin-cell velocity (KP07) with a Froude backstop. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: flux_h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: flux_hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: flux_hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt !! Timestep (s) integer :: i , j , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: eps4 , h4 , u_val , v_val , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost eps4 = DESING_EPS ** 4 do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( h4 , u_val , v_val , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale ) h ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) + dt * flux_h ( i , j ) hu ( i , j ) = hu ( i , j ) + dt * flux_hu ( i , j ) hv ( i , j ) = hv ( i , j ) + dt * flux_hv ( i , j ) ! Non-negative depth + dry-cell momentum zeroing; clamp h only ! for negative undershoots (preserves mass).  Thin-but-wet cells ! keep a desingularized (KP07) momentum instead of being zeroed. if ( h ( i , j ) < 0.0_wp ) then h ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp else if ( h ( i , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp else h4 = h ( i , j ) ** 4 if ( h4 < eps4 ) then ! u = sqrt(2) h hu / sqrt(h&#94;4 + max(h&#94;4, eps&#94;4)); hu := h*u. ! Identity for h >= eps, so applied only below eps. u_val = sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h ( i , j ) * hu ( i , j ) / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 ) v_val = sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h ( i , j ) * hv ( i , j ) / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 ) hu ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) * u_val hv ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) * v_val end if ! Froude backstop: blowup arrester only (triggers on a TRUE ! comparison, so NaN passes through and fails loudly). speed_sq = ( hu ( i , j ) ** 2 + hv ( i , j ) ** 2 ) / h ( i , j ) ** 2 fr_max_sq = FROUDE_BACKSTOP ** 2 * GRAVITY * h ( i , j ) if ( speed_sq > fr_max_sq ) then fr_scale = sqrt ( fr_max_sq / speed_sq ) hu ( i , j ) = hu ( i , j ) * fr_scale hv ( i , j ) = hv ( i , j ) * fr_scale end if end if end do end subroutine compute_update pure subroutine compute_rk2_average ( h , hu , hv , h0 , hu0 , hv0 , grid ) !! SSP-RK2 averaging step: U&#94;{n+1} = 0.5*(U&#94;n + U**), averaging the !! original state (h0, hu0, hv0) with the twice-advanced (h, hu, hv). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) integer :: i , j , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: eps4 , h4 , u_val , v_val , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost eps4 = DESING_EPS ** 4 do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( h4 , u_val , v_val , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale ) h ( i , j ) = 0.5_wp * ( h0 ( i , j ) + h ( i , j )) hu ( i , j ) = 0.5_wp * ( hu0 ( i , j ) + hu ( i , j )) hv ( i , j ) = 0.5_wp * ( hv0 ( i , j ) + hv ( i , j )) ! Same dry clamp + KP07 desingularization + backstop as ! compute_update. if ( h ( i , j ) < 0.0_wp ) then h ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp else if ( h ( i , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp else h4 = h ( i , j ) ** 4 if ( h4 < eps4 ) then u_val = sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h ( i , j ) * hu ( i , j ) / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 ) v_val = sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h ( i , j ) * hv ( i , j ) / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 ) hu ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) * u_val hv ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) * v_val end if speed_sq = ( hu ( i , j ) ** 2 + hv ( i , j ) ** 2 ) / h ( i , j ) ** 2 fr_max_sq = FROUDE_BACKSTOP ** 2 * GRAVITY * h ( i , j ) if ( speed_sq > fr_max_sq ) then fr_scale = sqrt ( fr_max_sq / speed_sq ) hu ( i , j ) = hu ( i , j ) * fr_scale hv ( i , j ) = hv ( i , j ) * fr_scale end if end if end do end subroutine compute_rk2_average pure subroutine compute_ssp_combine ( h , hu , hv , h0 , hu0 , hv0 , a_n , grid ) !! Generalized SSP Shu-Osher combine: U = a_n*U&#94;n + (1 - a_n)*U, !! where U is the post-Euler-stage iterate and (h0,hu0,hv0) = U&#94;n. !! Reduces exactly to compute_rk2_average for a_n = 0.5.  Applies the !! same positivity + thin-cell treatment so each stage stays !! wet/dry-safe. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hu0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hv0 ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: a_n !! Blend weight on the start-of-step state U&#94;n. integer :: i , j , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: a_prev , eps4 , h4 , u_val , v_val , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost a_prev = 1.0_wp - a_n eps4 = DESING_EPS ** 4 do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( h4 , u_val , v_val , speed_sq , fr_max_sq , fr_scale ) h ( i , j ) = a_n * h0 ( i , j ) + a_prev * h ( i , j ) hu ( i , j ) = a_n * hu0 ( i , j ) + a_prev * hu ( i , j ) hv ( i , j ) = a_n * hv0 ( i , j ) + a_prev * hv ( i , j ) if ( h ( i , j ) < 0.0_wp ) then h ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp else if ( h ( i , j ) < DRY_TOLERANCE ) then hu ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp hv ( i , j ) = 0.0_wp else h4 = h ( i , j ) ** 4 if ( h4 < eps4 ) then u_val = sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h ( i , j ) * hu ( i , j ) / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 ) v_val = sqrt ( 2.0_wp ) * h ( i , j ) * hv ( i , j ) / sqrt ( h4 + eps4 ) hu ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) * u_val hv ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) * v_val end if speed_sq = ( hu ( i , j ) ** 2 + hv ( i , j ) ** 2 ) / h ( i , j ) ** 2 fr_max_sq = FROUDE_BACKSTOP ** 2 * GRAVITY * h ( i , j ) if ( speed_sq > fr_max_sq ) then fr_scale = sqrt ( fr_max_sq / speed_sq ) hu ( i , j ) = hu ( i , j ) * fr_scale hv ( i , j ) = hv ( i , j ) * fr_scale end if end if end do end subroutine compute_ssp_combine end module rki_kernel_update","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_kernel_update.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_vcoord.F90 – Rakali","text":"Vertical coordinate type for hybrid z-sigma and ALE support This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_vcoord.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90 rki_vcoord.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_vcoord.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90 rki_vcoord.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90 sourcefile~rki_state.f90 rki_state.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_coastal_console_stats.f90 rki_coastal_console_stats.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~r