->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_kernel_flux_unstr.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_flux_unstr.f90 rki_kernel_flux_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 rki_solver_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_flux_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Central-upwind flux kernel for the unstructured solver module rki_kernel_flux_unstr !! Net flux divergence at every owned cell via the !! Kurganov-Noelle-Petrova central-upwind scheme on triangles. !! !! Cell-centric: each triangle loops its three edges, computes the !! central-upwind flux from both sides, and accumulates ONLY into its !! own update arrays. Each interior edge is visited twice (once per !! neighbour) -- no scatter, no race, no atomics -- which is what !! makes the kernel safe for `do concurrent` on GPU. Boundary edges !! (`mesh%neighbours(i, k) < 0`) dispatch per-edge BC state; group 0 !! falls through to BC_WALL (normal-momentum mirror). The !! well-balanced gravity bed-slope source is added per cell, then !! accumulators are normalised by area to flux divergence (per unit !! area), ready to be multiplied by `dt` in the update step. use rki_constants , only : wp , GRAVITY use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t use rki_state_unstr , only : unstr_state_t use rki_boundary_unstr , only : BC_WALL , BC_OPEN , BC_INFLOW , BC_OUTFLOW , & BC_TIDAL , BC_NESTED , BC_CLAMPED , BC_DISCHARGE , BC_CHAPMAN implicit none private public :: compute_fluxes_central_unstr ! Pointwise central-upwind constants. Defined locally so the `*_impl` ! helpers below inline in NVHPC device codegen (same TU). The ! LOW_FROUDE_* values duplicate the `rki_state_unstr` params -- keep ! in sync. real ( wp ), parameter :: FLUX_EPSILON = 1.0e-15_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: FLUX_DENOM_FLOOR = 1.0e-100_wp integer , parameter :: LOW_FROUDE_OFF = 0 integer , parameter :: LOW_FROUDE_1 = 1 integer , parameter :: LOW_FROUDE_2 = 2 contains pure subroutine compute_fluxes_central_unstr ( state , mesh ) !! Top-level driver: zero `(stage_eu, xmom_eu, ymom_eu)` and !! recompute them from the current edge values produced by the !! extrapolation kernel. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer :: k do concurrent ( k = 1 : mesh % ncells_owned ) call flux_one_cell ( state , mesh , k ) end do end subroutine compute_fluxes_central_unstr pure subroutine flux_one_cell ( state , mesh , k ) !! Per-cell body of the flux pass. Pure: never writes to any cell !! other than `k`. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: k integer :: i , neighbour , m integer :: bc_group , bc_kind real ( wp ) :: bc_eta_ext , bc_un_ext , bc_h_ext , bc_Qn_ext real ( wp ) :: q_left ( 3 ), q_right ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: edgeflux ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: hc , zc , hle , hre , zl , zr , h_left , h_right , z_half real ( wp ) :: n1 , n2 , length real ( wp ) :: max_speed_local , pressure_flux , speed_max_last real ( wp ) :: pressuregrad_work real ( wp ) :: stage_eu_acc , xmom_eu_acc , ymom_eu_acc real ( wp ) :: inv_area ! Centroid values for this cell -- needed by the bed-slope source. hc = state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ) zc = state % barotropic % bed_cv ( k ) ! Loop-private accumulators; avoid touching state%*_eu in the inner ! loop so the writes coalesce. stage_eu_acc = 0.0_wp xmom_eu_acc = 0.0_wp ymom_eu_acc = 0.0_wp speed_max_last = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , 3 ! Left state (this cell's edge values from the extrapolation pass). q_left ( 1 ) = state % barotropic % stage_ev ( i , k ) q_left ( 2 ) = state % barotropic % xmom_ev ( i , k ) q_left ( 3 ) = state % barotropic % ymom_ev ( i , k ) zl = state % barotropic % bed_ev ( i , k ) hle = state % barotropic % height_ev ( i , k ) ! Edge geometry. length = mesh % edge_len ( i , k ) n1 = mesh % edge_n1 ( i , k ) n2 = mesh % edge_n2 ( i , k ) neighbour = mesh % neighbours ( i , k ) if ( neighbour < 0 ) then ! Boundary edge -- dispatch the edge's BC group. Group <= 0 ! falls through to BC_WALL (inline wall mirror). bc_group = mesh % bc_group ( i , k ) if ( bc_group <= 0 ) then bc_kind = BC_WALL bc_eta_ext = 0.0_wp bc_un_ext = 0.0_wp bc_h_ext = 0.0_wp bc_Qn_ext = 0.0_wp else bc_kind = state % bc_type ( bc_group ) bc_eta_ext = state % bc_eta_ext ( bc_group ) bc_un_ext = state % bc_un_ext ( bc_group ) bc_h_ext = state % bc_h_ext ( bc_group ) bc_Qn_ext = state % bc_Qn_ext ( bc_group ) end if if ( bc_kind == BC_CHAPMAN ) then ! Orlanski radiation: advect the persistent eta_old(i, k) ! along the estimated outward phase speed, then dispatch ! through the BC_TIDAL/Flather algebra with that ghost ! target. call compute_chapman_eta_target ( state , mesh , k , i , & hle , bc_eta_ext ) bc_kind = BC_TIDAL end if call compute_boundary_state_impl ( q_left , n1 , n2 , zl , hle , bc_kind , & bc_eta_ext , bc_un_ext , bc_h_ext , & bc_Qn_ext , q_right , zr , hre ) else ! Interior edge -- read the matching edge of the neighbour. m = mesh % neighbour_edges ( i , k ) q_right ( 1 ) = state % barotropic % stage_ev ( m , neighbour ) q_right ( 2 ) = state % barotropic % xmom_ev ( m , neighbour ) q_right ( 3 ) = state % barotropic % ymom_ev ( m , neighbour ) zr = state % barotropic % bed_ev ( m , neighbour ) hre = state % barotropic % height_ev ( m , neighbour ) end if ! KP draining: shared edge bed is the higher of the two sides; ! effective heights clipped at zero from below. z_half = max ( zl , zr ) h_left = max ( hle + zl - z_half , 0.0_wp ) h_right = max ( hre + zr - z_half , 0.0_wp ) if ( h_left == 0.0_wp . and . h_right == 0.0_wp ) then ! Both sides dry -- no flux, no pressure contribution. edgeflux ( 1 ) = 0.0_wp edgeflux ( 2 ) = 0.0_wp edgeflux ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp max_speed_local = 0.0_wp pressure_flux = 0.0_wp else call cu_flux_pointwise_impl ( q_left , q_right , & h_left , h_right , & hle , hre , & n1 , n2 , & state % low_froude_mode , & edgeflux , max_speed_local , pressure_flux ) end if ! Edge length * negate: accumulate -div(F) so the update reads ! `Q&#94;{n+1} = Q&#94;n + dt * stage_eu`. edgeflux ( 1 ) = - length * edgeflux ( 1 ) edgeflux ( 2 ) = - length * edgeflux ( 2 ) edgeflux ( 3 ) = - length * edgeflux ( 3 ) ! Stash the barotropic mass flux (net inflow into cell `k` ! across edge `i`, m&#94;3/s, positive = gaining) for the tracer ! advection kernel to reuse (consistent-with-continuity). state % barotropic % mass_flux_e ( i , k ) = edgeflux ( 1 ) stage_eu_acc = stage_eu_acc + edgeflux ( 1 ) xmom_eu_acc = xmom_eu_acc + edgeflux ( 2 ) ymom_eu_acc = ymom_eu_acc + edgeflux ( 3 ) speed_max_last = max ( speed_max_last , max_speed_local ) ! Well-balanced bed-slope source: discrete hydrostatic-pressure ! work plus centroid-to-edge bed-slope term, plus `pressure_flux` ! from the central-upwind helper; telescopes to zero for lake at ! rest. pressuregrad_work = length * ( - GRAVITY * 0.5_wp * & ( h_left * h_left - hle * hle & - ( hle + hc ) * ( zl - zc )) & + pressure_flux ) xmom_eu_acc = xmom_eu_acc - n1 * pressuregrad_work ymom_eu_acc = ymom_eu_acc - n2 * pressuregrad_work end do ! Normalise by cell area so the accumulators hold flux divergence ! per unit area, ready for the explicit update step. if ( mesh % area ( k ) > 0.0_wp ) then inv_area = 1.0_wp / mesh % area ( k ) else inv_area = 0.0_wp end if state % barotropic % stage_eu ( k ) = stage_eu_acc * inv_area state % barotropic % xmom_eu ( k ) = xmom_eu_acc * inv_area state % barotropic % ymom_eu ( k ) = ymom_eu_acc * inv_area state % barotropic % max_speed ( k ) = speed_max_last end subroutine flux_one_cell pure subroutine compute_chapman_eta_target ( state , mesh , k , i , hle , eta_target ) !$acc routine seq !! Orlanski-style radiating ghost stage at boundary edge `i` of !! cell `k`. Advects the persistent `chapman_eta_old(i, k)` toward !! the interior centroid stage along the phase speed, writes back !! the new `eta_old`, and returns `eta_target` as the BC_TIDAL !! ghost eta. Per-edge writes to `chapman_eta_old(i, k)` are !! race-free: each (i, k) is touched only by cell `k`. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: k , i real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hle real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: eta_target real ( wp ) :: eta_int , eta_at_edge , eta_old_val real ( wp ) :: deta_dt , deta_dn , c_phase , d_perp , edge_len , dt_local real ( wp ), parameter :: H_FLOOR = 1.0e-6_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: GRAD_FLOOR = 1.0e-10_wp eta_int = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) eta_at_edge = state % barotropic % stage_ev ( i , k ) eta_old_val = state % barotropic % chapman_eta_old ( i , k ) dt_local = state % dt edge_len = mesh % edge_len ( i , k ) if ( edge_len > 0.0_wp . and . mesh % area ( k ) > 0.0_wp ) then d_perp = 2.0_wp * mesh % area ( k ) / ( 3.0_wp * edge_len ) else d_perp = 0.0_wp end if if ( dt_local > 0.0_wp . and . d_perp > 0.0_wp ) then deta_dt = ( eta_int - eta_old_val ) / dt_local deta_dn = ( eta_int - eta_at_edge ) / d_perp ! along inward normal if ( abs ( deta_dn ) > GRAD_FLOOR ) then c_phase = - deta_dt / deta_dn else c_phase = 0.0_wp end if c_phase = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( c_phase , sqrt ( GRAVITY * max ( hle , H_FLOOR )))) eta_target = eta_old_val - c_phase * dt_local / d_perp * & ( eta_old_val - eta_int ) else ! First step or degenerate triangle -- seed with interior eta. eta_target = eta_int end if state % barotropic % chapman_eta_old ( i , k ) = eta_int end subroutine compute_chapman_eta_target ! Inlined pointwise helpers (`*_impl`): self-contained pure helpers ! in the same TU as `flux_one_cell` so NVHPC device codegen inlines ! them (cross-module `!$acc routine seq` would be a real call). pure subroutine rotate_to_normal_impl ( q , n1 , n2 ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: q ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: n1 , n2 real ( wp ) :: q1 , q2 q1 = q ( 2 ) q2 = q ( 3 ) q ( 2 ) = n1 * q1 + n2 * q2 q ( 3 ) = - n2 * q1 + n1 * q2 end subroutine rotate_to_normal_impl pure subroutine compute_velocity_terms_impl ( h , h_edge , uh_raw , vh_raw , & u , uh , v , vh ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h , h_edge , uh_raw , vh_raw real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: u , uh , v , vh real ( wp ) :: inv_h_edge if ( h_edge > 0.0_wp ) then inv_h_edge = 1.0_wp / h_edge u = uh_raw * inv_h_edge uh = h * u v = vh_raw * inv_h_edge vh = h * inv_h_edge * vh_raw else u = 0.0_wp uh = 0.0_wp v = 0.0_wp vh = 0.0_wp end if end subroutine compute_velocity_terms_impl pure function compute_s_max_impl ( u_left , u_right , c_left , c_right ) result ( s ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_left , u_right , c_left , c_right real ( wp ) :: s s = max ( u_left + c_left , u_right + c_right ) if ( s < 0.0_wp ) s = 0.0_wp end function compute_s_max_impl pure function compute_s_min_impl ( u_left , u_right , c_left , c_right ) result ( s ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_left , u_right , c_left , c_right real ( wp ) :: s s = min ( u_left - c_left , u_right - c_right ) if ( s > 0.0_wp ) s = 0.0_wp end function compute_s_min_impl pure function compute_local_froude_impl ( low_froude_mode , & u_left , u_right , & v_left , v_right , & c_left , c_right ) result ( fr ) !$acc routine seq integer , intent ( in ) :: low_froude_mode real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_left , u_right , v_left , v_right , c_left , c_right real ( wp ) :: fr real ( wp ) :: numerator , denominator , ratio select case ( low_froude_mode ) case ( LOW_FROUDE_1 ) numerator = u_right * u_right + u_left * u_left & + v_right * v_right + v_left * v_left denominator = c_left * c_left + c_right * c_right + 1.0e-10_wp ratio = numerator / denominator fr = sqrt ( max ( 0.001_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , ratio ))) case ( LOW_FROUDE_2 ) numerator = u_right * u_right + u_left * u_left & + v_right * v_right + v_left * v_left denominator = c_left * c_left + c_right * c_right + 1.0e-10_wp ratio = sqrt ( numerator / denominator ) fr = sqrt ( min ( 1.0_wp , 0.01_wp + max ( ratio - 0.01_wp , 0.0_wp ))) case default fr = 1.0_wp end select end function compute_local_froude_impl pure subroutine cu_flux_pointwise_impl ( & q_left , q_right , & h_left , h_right , & hle , hre , & n1 , n2 , & low_froude_mode , & edgeflux , max_speed , pressure_flux ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q_left ( 3 ), q_right ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_left , h_right real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hle , hre real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: n1 , n2 integer , intent ( in ) :: low_froude_mode real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: edgeflux ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: max_speed real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: pressure_flux real ( wp ) :: q_left_rot ( 3 ), q_right_rot ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: u_left , uh_left , v_left , vh_left real ( wp ) :: u_right , uh_right , v_right , vh_right real ( wp ) :: c_left , c_right real ( wp ) :: s_max , s_min , denom , inv_denom , s_max_s_min real ( wp ) :: flux_left ( 3 ), flux_right ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: local_fr q_left_rot (:) = q_left (:) q_right_rot (:) = q_right (:) call rotate_to_normal_impl ( q_left_rot , n1 , n2 ) call rotate_to_normal_impl ( q_right_rot , n1 , n2 ) call compute_velocity_terms_impl ( h_left , hle , q_left_rot ( 2 ), q_left_rot ( 3 ), & u_left , uh_left , v_left , vh_left ) call compute_velocity_terms_impl ( h_right , hre , q_right_rot ( 2 ), q_right_rot ( 3 ), & u_right , uh_right , v_right , vh_right ) c_left = sqrt ( GRAVITY * h_left ) c_right = sqrt ( GRAVITY * h_right ) s_max = compute_s_max_impl ( u_left , u_right , c_left , c_right ) s_min = compute_s_min_impl ( u_left , u_right , c_left , c_right ) local_fr = compute_local_froude_impl ( low_froude_mode , & u_left , u_right , & v_left , v_right , & c_left , c_right ) flux_left ( 1 ) = u_left * h_left flux_left ( 2 ) = u_left * uh_left flux_left ( 3 ) = u_left * vh_left flux_right ( 1 ) = u_right * h_right flux_right ( 2 ) = u_right * uh_right flux_right ( 3 ) = u_right * vh_right denom = s_max - s_min if ( denom < FLUX_EPSILON ) then edgeflux ( 1 ) = 0.0_wp edgeflux ( 2 ) = 0.0_wp edgeflux ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp max_speed = 0.0_wp pressure_flux = 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * 0.5_wp * ( h_left * h_left + h_right * h_right ) else max_speed = max ( s_max , - s_min ) inv_denom = 1.0_wp / max ( denom , FLUX_DENOM_FLOOR ) s_max_s_min = s_max * s_min edgeflux ( 1 ) = ( s_max * flux_left ( 1 ) - s_min * flux_right ( 1 ) & + s_max_s_min * ( h_right - h_left )) * inv_denom edgeflux ( 2 ) = ( s_max * flux_left ( 2 ) - s_min * flux_right ( 2 ) & + local_fr * s_max_s_min * ( uh_right - uh_left )) * inv_denom edgeflux ( 3 ) = ( s_max * flux_left ( 3 ) - s_min * flux_right ( 3 ) & + local_fr * s_max_s_min * ( vh_right - vh_left )) * inv_denom pressure_flux = 0.5_wp * GRAVITY * ( s_max * h_left * h_left & - s_min * h_right * h_right ) * inv_denom call rotate_to_normal_impl ( edgeflux , n1 , - n2 ) end if end subroutine cu_flux_pointwise_impl pure subroutine compute_boundary_state_impl ( & q_left , n1 , n2 , zl , hle , bc_type , & eta_ext , un_ext , h_ext , Qn_ext , & q_right , zr , hre ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q_left ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: n1 , n2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: zl , hle integer , intent ( in ) :: bc_type real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_ext , un_ext , h_ext , Qn_ext real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: q_right ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: zr real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: hre real ( wp ) :: normal_mom real ( wp ) :: h_guard , n_mom , u_n_int , u_n_ghost , c_speed select case ( bc_type ) case ( BC_OPEN ) q_right ( 1 ) = q_left ( 1 ) q_right ( 2 ) = q_left ( 2 ) q_right ( 3 ) = q_left ( 3 ) zr = zl hre = hle case ( BC_CLAMPED ) q_right ( 1 ) = eta_ext q_right ( 2 ) = q_left ( 2 ) q_right ( 3 ) = q_left ( 3 ) zr = zl hre = max ( eta_ext - zl , 0.0_wp ) case ( BC_TIDAL , BC_NESTED ) ! BC_NESTED: smoke-level — Flather radiation driven by per-group ! prescribed elevation, identical to BC_TIDAL; parent-model ! coupling (live eta from a coarser grid) is deferred. zr = zl hre = max ( eta_ext - zl , 0.0_wp ) q_right ( 1 ) = eta_ext h_guard = max ( hle , 1.0e-6_wp ) if ( hle > 1.0e-6_wp ) then n_mom = q_left ( 2 ) * n1 + q_left ( 3 ) * n2 u_n_int = n_mom / h_guard c_speed = sqrt ( GRAVITY / h_guard ) u_n_ghost = u_n_int + c_speed * ( q_left ( 1 ) - eta_ext ) q_right ( 2 ) = hre * u_n_ghost * n1 + ( q_left ( 2 ) - n_mom * n1 ) q_right ( 3 ) = hre * u_n_ghost * n2 + ( q_left ( 3 ) - n_mom * n2 ) else q_right ( 2 ) = q_left ( 2 ) q_right ( 3 ) = q_left ( 3 ) end if case ( BC_INFLOW ) q_right ( 1 ) = q_left ( 1 ) q_right ( 2 ) = hle * un_ext * n1 q_right ( 3 ) = hle * un_ext * n2 zr = zl hre = hle case ( BC_DISCHARGE ) q_right ( 1 ) = q_left ( 1 ) q_right ( 2 ) = Qn_ext * n1 q_right ( 3 ) = Qn_ext * n2 zr = zl hre = hle case ( BC_OUTFLOW ) zr = zl hre = h_ext q_right ( 1 ) = zr + h_ext q_right ( 2 ) = q_left ( 2 ) q_right ( 3 ) = q_left ( 3 ) case default ! BC_WALL (and any unknown type as a safe fallback). q_right ( 1 ) = q_left ( 1 ) normal_mom = q_left ( 2 ) * n1 + q_left ( 3 ) * n2 q_right ( 2 ) = q_left ( 2 ) - 2.0_wp * normal_mom * n1 q_right ( 3 ) = q_left ( 3 ) - 2.0_wp * normal_mom * n2 zr = zl hre = hle end select end subroutine compute_boundary_state_impl end module rki_kernel_flux_unstr","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_kernel_flux_unstr.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_nonhydrostatic_state.F90 – Rakali","text":"Non-hydrostatic (multi-layer pressure correction) solution state. This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_nonhydrostatic_state.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_nonhydrostatic_state.f90 rki_nonhydrostatic_state.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_nonhydrostatic_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_nonhydrostatic_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_mem_report.f90 rki_mem_report.F90 sourcefile~rki_nonhydrostatic_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_mem_report.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_mem_report.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_