r.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90 rki_si_unstr_step_ml.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 rki_solver_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Semi-implicit free-surface time step — unstructured 3D hydrostatic multilayer. module rki_si_unstr_step_ml !! One semi-implicit (Casulli/SCHISM-style) step for the UNSTRUCTURED 3D !! multilayer coastal path (`time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\"` + !! `use_multilayer`, `nz>1`, sigma) — built on the P3.1 TPFA eta-solve (the operator !! never changes; only the Hf/Gbar fills do — the \"strict superset\" !! contract) and the `(nz, ncells)` column kernels of !! `rki_si_unstr_column`.  The step (one implicit theta-step; the theta !! scheme IS the integrator): !! !!   1. save U&#94;n edges + layer state; eta&#94;n = stage at circumcentres; !!   2. explicit predictor tendencies IN PLACE on hu/hv_layer: !!      baroclinic PGF, Coriolis, Smagorinsky (existing unstructured !!      kernels), and surface wind stress on the TOP layer (k=nz) — !!      dt*tau/RHO_WATER from the uniform scalar wind (rides the !!      pure-u&#94;n predictor into G_k; R_k / Hhat / the operator are !!      untouched by linearity; no momentum self-advection — the SI !!      target regime is advection-weak, same envelope as structured); !!   3. PP81 interface viscosity + per-column implicit solve !!      (G_k, R_k, Hhat = -sum h_k R_k, Gbar = sum h_k G_k); !!   4. Hf from Hhat via the P3.1 edge face-depth kernel reused verbatim !!      (Hhat passed as the cell \"depth\"; a Dirichlet edge gets !!      0.5*(Hhat_c + h_ghost) with h_ghost = eta_bc - b — the !!      structured ghost-Hhat seed, edge-wise), edge predictor from the !!      face-averaged Gbar, theta-blend RHS + area-weighted CG — ALL !!      P3.1 machinery reused verbatim; !!   5. per-layer edge-transport recovery (column sums telescope EXACTLY !!      to the 2D back-substituted edge transport => mass to round-off; !!      Dirichlet ghost R = -1 seed inline — the estuary-mouth lesson); !!   6. tracers: every registry tracer advected depth-proportionally !!      with the EXACT blended edge mass flux the eta update used !!      (uniform tracers invariant per layer; OUTER SHIM: the host !!      registry loop passes tracers(it)%hTr/hTr0 into the flat-impl !!      kernel — the array-of-derived-types device rule); !!   7. h&#94;{n+1} = eta&#94;{n+1} - b; h_layer = dsig*h; per-layer cell !!      momenta = least-squares edge reconstruction; barotropic momenta !!      = layer sums; U&#94;{n+1} edge prognostic = column sums; !!   8. tracer vertical diffusion, surface fluxes, clamp, EOS — the !!      existing unstructured kernels reused as-is.  NO diasurface !!      exchange: the dsig-proportional advection makes sigma surfaces !!      material for the transported fields (the structured design !!      decision, carried over). !! !! The step ends with valid barotropic stage/xmom/ymom/height + !! multilayer *_layer state — downstream (output, gauges, restart) !! unchanged.  Single-rank, owned-cell loops. use rki_constants , only : wp , GRAVITY , CP_WATER use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t use rki_state_unstr , only : unstr_state_t use rki_si_unstr_helmholtz , only : si_unstr_face_depths , si_unstr_compute_rhs , & si_unstr_cg_solve , si_unstr_apply_helmholtz use rki_si_unstr_step , only : SI_UNSTR_THETA , & SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_MAX , SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_TOL use rki_si_unstr_wetdry , only : si_unstr_wetdry_fill_bsub , & si_unstr_wetdry_volume , si_unstr_wetdry_wetfrac , & si_unstr_wetdry_mass_diag , & si_unstr_wetdry_newton_residual , & si_unstr_wetdry_wetcount use pic_logger , only : global_logger use rki_si_unstr_column , only : si_unstr_build_nu_interface , & si_unstr_column_solve , & si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges , & si_unstr_recover_edge_layers , & si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges , & si_unstr_advect_tracer_dsig , & si_unstr_edge_layers_to_cells , & si_unstr_update_thickness_ml , & si_unstr_apply_wind_top_layer use rki_si_unstr_closures , only : si_unstr_fill_nu_iface_from_keps , & si_unstr_keps_copy_iface , & si_unstr_build_nu_interface_kpp , & si_unstr_kpp_diffusion_tracers use rki_ml_dynamics_unstr , only : ml_save_layer_state_unstr , & ml_compute_barotropic_momentum_unstr use rki_ml_pressure_unstr , only : ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient_unstr , & ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient_jacobian_unstr use rki_ml_friction_unstr , only : ml_apply_coriolis_unstr use rki_ml_horizontal_viscosity_unstr , only : ml_horizontal_viscosity_smag_unstr use rki_ml_tracers_unstr , only : ml_save_tracer_unstr , ml_clamp_tracer_unstr , & ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr , & ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes_unstr use rki_ml_eos_unstr , only : ml_equation_of_state_unstr use rki_ml_keps_unstr , only : ml_keps_friction_velocities_unstr , & ml_keps_update_unstr , & ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer_unstr use rki_ml_kpp_unstr , only : ml_kpp_boundary_layer_unstr use rki_boundary_unstr , only : MAX_BC_GROUPS , BC_WALL , BC_TIDAL , BC_CLAMPED implicit none private public :: si_unstr_step_ml integer , parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 !! Triangles only. contains subroutine si_unstr_step_ml ( state , mesh , dt , iter_out ) !! Advance the unstructured 3D multilayer state one semi-implicit !! step.  The caller (`solver_unstr_step_semi_implicit`) has already !! halo-exchanged; Dirichlet boundary coupling reads !! `state%bc_type` / `state%bc_eta_ext` (tidal/clamped) inside the !! edge kernels — the P3.1 coefficient-space route. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer , intent ( out ) :: iter_out integer :: nct , nco , n_bc , nz , it , ip real ( wp ) :: theta , g_theta2_dt2 , g_omtheta_dt integer :: cg_it real ( wp ) :: mass_res real ( wp ) :: tr_bc ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) nct = state % ncells_total nco = state % ncells_owned n_bc = size ( state % bc_type ) nz = state % multilayer % nz_ml theta = SI_UNSTR_THETA g_theta2_dt2 = GRAVITY * theta * theta * dt * dt g_omtheta_dt = GRAVITY * ( 1.0_wp - theta ) * dt ! Mirror the explicit stage's S/T config sync onto the tracer registry ! (host scalars, idempotent) so the generic per-tracer kernels read ! per-tracer config uniformly. it = state % multilayer % idx_salinity if ( it > 0 ) then state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg = state % multilayer % kappa_S_bg state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hdiff_kappa = state % multilayer % hdiff_kappa state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_min = state % multilayer % S_min state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_max = state % multilayer % S_max state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% bc_ext = state % multilayer % bc_S_ext end if it = state % multilayer % idx_temperature if ( it > 0 ) then state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg = state % multilayer % kappa_T_bg state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hdiff_kappa = state % multilayer % hdiff_kappa state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_min = state % multilayer % T_min state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_max = state % multilayer % T_max state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% bc_ext = state % multilayer % bc_T_ext end if ! ---- 1. Save U&#94;n edges + layer state; eta&#94;n = stage; height ---- call si_ml_save_and_eta ( nct , nco , state % barotropic % stage_cv , & state % barotropic % bed_cv , state % barotropic % height_cv , & state % si % eta , state % si % u_edge , state % si % u_n_edge ) call ml_save_layer_state_unstr ( state ) ! ---- 2. Explicit predictor tendencies IN PLACE on hu/hv_layer ---- ! EOS FIRST (the unstructured house order — the explicit stage also ! runs EOS immediately before the BPG): rho_layer is zero-initialised, ! so a BPG before the first EOS would see a -rho_0 anomaly kick. call ml_equation_of_state_unstr ( state ) if ( state % multilayer % use_bpg_jacobian ) then call ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient_jacobian_unstr ( state , mesh , dt ) else call ml_baroclinic_pressure_gradient_unstr ( state , mesh , dt ) end if call ml_apply_coriolis_unstr ( state , dt ) if ( state % multilayer % smagorinsky_cs > 0.0_wp ) then call ml_horizontal_viscosity_smag_unstr ( state , mesh , dt ) end if call si_unstr_apply_wind_top_layer ( nz , nct , nco , state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % barotropic % wind_tau_x , & state % barotropic % wind_tau_y , dt ) ! ---- 3. Closure nu (PP81 / k-eps / KPP) + per-column implicit solve ---- ! The column solve consumes ANY interface viscosity through nu_iface ! (R = solve(-1) is nu-independent), so closures are pure FILLS: ! * k-eps: the UNCHANGED ml_keps_update_unstr at SI cadence — already !   backward-Euler/Patankar (see local_archive/prototypes/si_closures); then !   keps_nut copied into nu_iface.  Optional keps_si_picard > 1 !   Picard: save pre-step k/eps, re-run from the same initial state !   with the refreshed nu_t production coefficient.  The IMPLICIT !   momentum apply is the column tridiagonal — do NOT call !   ml_keps_apply_momentum_unstr here. ! * KPP: ml_kpp_boundary_layer_unstr reused verbatim (diagnostic), !   then the LMD94 shape-function overlay MAX'd onto PP81 in nu_iface !   — the implicit tridiagonal replaces the explicit CFL-clamped flux. ! * default (PP81): bit-identical to the unextended step. if ( state % multilayer % vmix_use_keps ) then call ml_keps_friction_velocities_unstr ( state ) if ( state % multilayer % keps_si_picard > 1 ) then call si_unstr_keps_copy_iface ( nz + 1 , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % keps_tke , & state % multilayer % keps_tke0 ) call si_unstr_keps_copy_iface ( nz + 1 , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % keps_eps , & state % multilayer % keps_eps0 ) end if do ip = 1 , max ( state % multilayer % keps_si_picard , 1 ) if ( ip > 1 ) then ! Picard: restore pre-step k/eps; production now reads ! the pass-(ip-1) nu_t (the refreshed coefficient). call si_unstr_keps_copy_iface ( nz + 1 , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % keps_tke0 , & state % multilayer % keps_tke ) call si_unstr_keps_copy_iface ( nz + 1 , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % keps_eps0 , & state % multilayer % keps_eps ) end if call ml_keps_update_unstr ( state , dt , . true .) end do call si_unstr_fill_nu_iface_from_keps ( nz , nz + 1 , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % keps_nut , & state % si % nu_iface ) else if ( state % multilayer % vmix_use_kpp ) then call ml_kpp_boundary_layer_unstr ( state , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr ) call si_unstr_build_nu_interface_kpp ( nz , nz + 1 , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , & state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_max , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_bg , & state % multilayer % vmix_ri_alpha , & state % multilayer % kpp_u_star , & state % multilayer % kpp_buoy_flux , & state % multilayer % kpp_bl_depth , & state % si % nu_iface ) else call si_unstr_build_nu_interface ( nz , nz + 1 , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , & state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_max , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_bg , & state % multilayer % vmix_ri_alpha , & state % si % nu_iface ) end if call si_unstr_column_solve ( nz , nz + 1 , nct , nco , state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , state % si % nu_iface , & state % barotropic % manning_n , dt , & state % si % g_col_u , state % si % g_col_v , & state % si % r_col , state % si % Hhat_cell , & state % si % Gbar_cell_x , state % si % Gbar_cell_y ) ! ---- 4. Hf from Hhat; zero dead-edge U&#94;n (R3); edge predictor; RHS; CG ---- ! WET/DRY (state%si%wetdry): the Hhat conveyance is GATED by the ! geometric max-eta/sill wet/dry rule (a face dead by geometry — the ! higher surface below the higher bed — carries no conveyance even where ! Hhat is nonzero), then a Newton outer loop wraps the eta-solve with the ! surface wet-fraction mass diagonal a(eta)+floor.  Everything else — ! the R3 dead-edge zeroing (STRUCTURAL here: the RHS consumes per-edge ! transports directly), the frozen-column responses (g/r/Hhat/Gbar ! depend on h_layer at time n, not eta), the dsig scale-together dry ! columns, the hold-last-wet tracer drain — is the all-wet ML machinery ! reused verbatim.  All-wet Hhat basins reduce the gated conveyance ! exactly to the P3.1 face depth => the wet/dry branch is a strict ! superset (the structured \"strict superset\" contract, edge-wise). if ( state % si % wetdry ) then call si_unstr_wetdry_fill_bsub ( mesh , state % si % n_sub , nct , nco , & state % barotropic % bed_cv , & state % si % bsub_fill , state % si % b_sub , & state % si % b_min ) call si_ml_wetdry_face_depths ( mesh , nct , nco , n_bc , state % si % eta , & state % si % b_min , state % si % Hhat_cell , & state % bc_type , state % bc_eta_ext , & state % si % Hf_edge , state % si % eta_ghost_edge ) else call si_unstr_face_depths ( mesh , nct , nco , n_bc , state % si % Hhat_cell , & state % barotropic % bed_cv , state % bc_type , & state % bc_eta_ext , state % si % Hf_edge , & state % si % eta_ghost_edge ) end if call si_ml_zero_dead_edges ( nct , nco , state % si % Hf_edge , state % si % u_n_edge ) call si_unstr_fill_predictor_edges ( mesh , nz , nct , nco , state % si % Gbar_cell_x , & state % si % Gbar_cell_y , & state % multilayer % hu_layer0 , & state % multilayer % hv_layer0 , & state % si % u_n_edge , state % si % eta , & state % si % Hf_edge , state % si % eta_ghost_edge , & state % si % u_star , g_omtheta_dt ) call si_unstr_compute_rhs ( mesh , nct , nco , state % si % eta , state % si % u_star , & state % si % u_n_edge , state % si % eta_r , dt , theta , & state % si % Hf_edge , state % si % eta_ghost_edge , & g_theta2_dt2 ) if ( state % si % wetdry ) then ! The Newton wrapper writes state%si%mass_res / newton_iters directly. call si_ml_wetdry_newton ( state , mesh , nct , nco , g_theta2_dt2 , cg_it ) else call si_unstr_cg_solve ( mesh , nct , nco , state % si % eta , state % si % eta_r , & state % si % eta_p , state % si % eta_Ap , state % si % eta_z , & state % si % eta_diag , state % si % Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , & state % si % precond , state % si % rtol , cg_it , mass_res ) state % si % mass_res = mass_res end if state % si % cg_iters = cg_it iter_out = cg_it ! ---- 5. Per-layer edge-transport recovery ---- ! eta&#94;n is still in stage_cv (untouched until step 7); eta&#94;{n+1} in ! si%eta.  h_layer is still the time-n field that fed the tridiagonal ! (one-h-per-stage rule). call si_unstr_recover_edge_layers ( mesh , nz , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer0 , & state % multilayer % hv_layer0 , & state % multilayer % dsig_ml , & state % barotropic % bed_cv , & state % si % g_col_u , state % si % g_col_v , & state % si % r_col , state % barotropic % stage_cv , & state % si % eta , state % si % Hf_edge , & state % si % eta_ghost_edge , dt , theta , & state % si % u_edge_layer ) ! ---- 6. Blended mass flux + dsig tracer advection (registry loop, !         OUTER SHIM: plain arrays into the flat-impl kernel) ---- call si_unstr_fill_mass_flux_edges ( nz , nct , nco , state % si % u_edge_layer , & state % si % u_n_edge , state % si % Hf_edge , & theta , state % si % mass_flux_edge , & state % si % u_edge ) do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if (. not . state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_horizontal_advection ) cycle call ml_save_tracer_unstr ( state , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr0 ) ! Pass the Dirichlet inflow table through a FRESH host copy: the ! tracers array-of-DTs is device-mapped at enter_data, so the ! per-step host-side config sync above never reaches the device ! copy of the inline `bc_ext` component — a kernel reading ! `tracers(it)%bc_ext` directly sees a STALE (init-time) device ! value and the flood tide injects tracer 0 (measured 29-PSU ! freshening on GPU, invisible on the CPU builds where host == ! device).  A local array is never in the present table => the ! launch copies the current host values in. tr_bc = state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% bc_ext call si_unstr_advect_tracer_dsig ( mesh , nz , nct , nco , n_bc , & state % multilayer % dsig_ml , & state % multilayer % h_layer , & state % si % mass_flux_edge , & tr_bc , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr0 , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , dt ) end do ! ---- 7. Thickness + momentum closers ---- call si_unstr_update_thickness_ml ( nz , nct , nco , state % si % eta , & state % barotropic % bed_cv , & state % multilayer % dsig_ml , & state % barotropic % stage_cv , & state % barotropic % height_cv , & state % multilayer % h_layer ) call si_unstr_edge_layers_to_cells ( mesh , nz , nct , nco , & state % si % u_edge_layer , & state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer ) call ml_compute_barotropic_momentum_unstr ( state ) ! ---- 8. Tracer vertical diffusion + surface fluxes + clamp + EOS ---- ! Closure-aware tracer vertical diffusion (mirrors the structured ! SI dispatch, but implicit-capable kernels only — SI step sizes): ! * k-eps: implicit Thomas diffusion with the k-eps scalar diffusivity !   kt for EVERY registry tracer (conservative). ! * KPP: implicit Thomas diffusion with the PP81-cubic + overlay !   diffusivity + non-local transport for S/T; extra passive tracers !   fall back to the PP81 kernel (as on the explicit path). ! * default: the PP81 kernel, unchanged (bit-identical). if ( state % multilayer % vmix_use_keps ) then do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_vertical_diffusion ) then call ml_keps_apply_diffusion_tracer_unstr ( state , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg , & dt ) end if end do else if ( state % multilayer % vmix_use_kpp ) then call si_unstr_kpp_diffusion_tracers ( nz , nz + 1 , nct , nco , & state % multilayer % h_layer , state % multilayer % hu_layer , & state % multilayer % hv_layer , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_temperature )% hTr , & state % multilayer % rho_layer , state % multilayer % rho_0 , & state % multilayer % vmix_nu_max , & state % multilayer % kappa_S_bg , state % multilayer % kappa_T_bg , & state % multilayer % vmix_ri_alpha , & state % multilayer % kpp_cs_nonlocal , & state % forcing % heat_flux , state % forcing % evap_minus_precip , & CP_WATER , state % multilayer % kpp_u_star , & state % multilayer % kpp_buoy_flux , state % multilayer % kpp_bl_depth , dt ) ! Extra passive tracers (not S/T) fall back to PP81. do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( it == state % multilayer % idx_salinity . or . & it == state % multilayer % idx_temperature ) cycle if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_vertical_diffusion ) then call ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr ( state , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg , & dt ) end if end do else do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_vertical_diffusion ) then call ml_vertical_diffusion_tracer_unstr ( state , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% kappa_bg , & dt ) end if end do end if if ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity > 0 . and . & state % multilayer % idx_temperature > 0 ) then call ml_apply_surface_tracer_fluxes_unstr ( state , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_salinity )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( state % multilayer % idx_temperature )% hTr ) end if do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) if ( state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% do_clamp ) then call ml_clamp_tracer_unstr ( state , state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% hTr , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_min , & state % multilayer % tracers ( it )% tr_max ) end if end do ! (EOS runs at the TOP of the next step, before its BPG — the ! unstructured house order; no end-of-step call needed.) state % time = state % time + dt state % step_count = state % step_count + 1 state % dt = dt end subroutine si_unstr_step_ml ! ------------------------------------------------------------------ ! Flat-impl helpers (explicit-shape, do concurrent, device-resident). ! ------------------------------------------------------------------ pure subroutine si_ml_save_and_eta ( nct , nco , stage , bed , height , eta , & u_edge , u_n_edge ) !! Save the edge transports U&#94;n, refresh height = max(stage - b, 0), !! and form eta&#94;n = stage at circumcentres (the CG warm start). integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: stage ( nct ), bed ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: height ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: eta ( nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: u_n_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) integer :: c , i do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) local ( i ) do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI u_n_edge ( i , c ) = u_edge ( i , c ) end do height ( c ) = max ( stage ( c ) - bed ( c ), 0.0_wp ) eta ( c ) = stage ( c ) end do end subroutine si_ml_save_and_eta pure subroutine si_ml_zero_dead_edges ( nct , nco , Hf_edge , u_n_edge ) !! Zero the saved U&#94;n on dead (wall / Hf=0) edges — Casulli rule R3: !! a dead edge carries no (1-theta) flux into the theta-blend RHS. integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: u_n_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) integer :: c , i do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) local ( i ) do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI if ( Hf_edge ( i , c ) <= 0.0_wp ) u_n_edge ( i , c ) = 0.0_wp end do end do end subroutine si_ml_zero_dead_edges pure subroutine si_ml_wetdry_face_depths ( mesh , nct , nco , n_bc , eta , b_min , & Hhat , bc_type , bc_eta_ext , & Hf_edge , eta_ghost_edge ) !! Frozen wet/dry edge depths for the 3D column-integrated eta-solve — !! the triangular twin of the structured `si_ml_wetdry_face_depths`: !! the effective CONVEYANCE is the Hhat-based two-cell average (as the !! all-wet ML path uses), GATED by the geometric max-eta/sill wet/dry !! rule so an edge dead by geometry (higher surface below the higher !! bed) carries Hf=0 — a wall — regardless of Hhat.  The surface !! geometry decides wet/dead; where wet, the implicit column response !! Hhat sets the conveyance magnitude.  b_min = the geometric sill bed !! (deepest sub-bottom).  Dirichlet edges gate the ghost-coupled face !! the same way (ghost surface = the prescribed eta_bc; ghost sill !! mirrors the cell sill).  All-wet Hhat basins reduce this EXACTLY to !! the P3.1 `si_unstr_face_depths` conveyance (0.5*(Hhat_c+Hhat_nbr)), !! so the wet/dry branch is a strict superset.  Cell-centric !! double-visit `(3,ncell)`, cell-index-last. type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nct !! Cell array extent (ncells_total). integer , intent ( in ) :: nco !! Owned-cell loop bound. integer , intent ( in ) :: n_bc !! BC group table size. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta ( nct ) !! eta&#94;n at circumcentres (the FROZEN surface). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: b_min ( nct ) !! Geometric sill bed (deepest sub-bottom) at cells (m). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hhat ( nct ) !! Column effective depth (conveyance magnitude, m). integer , intent ( in ) :: bc_type ( n_bc ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: bc_eta_ext ( n_bc ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: eta_ghost_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , nct ) integer :: c , i , kn , g , bt real ( wp ) :: geo , eta_bc do concurrent ( c = 1 : nco ) local ( i , kn , g , bt , geo , eta_bc ) do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI eta_ghost_edge ( i , c ) = 0.0_wp Hf_edge ( i , c ) = 0.0_wp kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , c ) if ( kn > 0 ) then ! Interior edge: geometric sill gate on eta&#94;n, Hhat conveyance. geo = max ( max ( eta ( c ), eta ( kn )) - max ( b_min ( c ), b_min ( kn )), 0.0_wp ) if ( geo > 0.0_wp ) Hf_edge ( i , c ) = 0.5_wp * ( Hhat ( c ) + Hhat ( kn )) else g = mesh % bc_group ( i , c ) bt = BC_WALL if ( g >= 1 . and . g <= n_bc ) bt = bc_type ( g ) if (( bt == BC_TIDAL . or . bt == BC_CLAMPED ) . and . g >= 1 ) then eta_bc = bc_eta_ext ( g ) ! Ghost sill mirrors the cell sill.  Where geometrically wet, ! the conveyance is the SAME 0.5*(Hhat_c + h_ghost) mean the ! all-wet P3.1 path uses (Hhat interior, geometric ghost ! depth eta_bc - b) — matching it exactly so the recovery ! reads the same Dirichlet Hf the eta-solve used (the ! estuary-mouth mass<->tracer consistency lesson). geo = max ( max ( eta ( c ), eta_bc ) - b_min ( c ), 0.0_wp ) if ( geo > 0.0_wp ) Hf_edge ( i , c ) = & 0.5_wp * ( Hhat ( c ) + max ( eta_bc - b_min ( c ), 0.0_wp )) eta_ghost_edge ( i , c ) = eta_bc end if end if end do end do end subroutine si_ml_wetdry_face_depths subroutine si_ml_wetdry_newton ( state , mesh , nct , nco , g_theta2_dt2 , iter_out ) !! Newton outer loop for the 3D column-integrated wet/dry eta-solve on !! the triangulation — the triangular twin of the structured !! `si_ml_wetdry_newton` (and the 2D-unstr `si_unstr_advance_wetdry`'s !! Newton loop).  The column responses (g_col/r_col/Hhat/Gbar) and the !! frozen Hf are held FIXED (they depend on h_layer at time n, not eta), !! so only the surface mass system F = v(eta) + T*eta - rhs_d iterates, !! with T the Hhat-weighted TPFA stiffness and the surface wet-fraction !! Newton diagonal a(eta)+floor.  On entry `state%si%eta_r` holds the !! LINEAR RHS (leading eta&#94;n from si_unstr_compute_rhs); this swaps the !! leading term for v(eta&#94;n) once, then Newton-solves.  Host-side !! orchestration; flat device kernels.  Writes state%si%newton_iters !! and state%si%mass_res = the NONLINEAR mass residual ||F||&#94;2 at !! Newton exit (the conservation diagnostic — NOT the inner-CG residual !! of the last delta-solve, which is an internal solver number). type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: nct , nco real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: g_theta2_dt2 integer , intent ( out ) :: iter_out !! Inner CG iterations summed over the Newton outers. integer :: k , nit , cg_it , cg_it_total , wetcount , wetcount_prev real ( wp ) :: rhs2 , f2 , tol2 , mass_res logical :: converged associate ( si => state % si ) ! rhs_d = eta_r + (v(eta&#94;n) - eta&#94;n): swap the linear RHS leading ! term for the wetted volume (same as the 2D/structured wet/dry). call si_unstr_wetdry_volume ( si % n_sub , nct , nco , si % eta , si % b_sub , si % v_cell ) do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) si % rhs_d ( k ) = si % eta_r ( k ) + ( si % v_cell ( k ) - si % eta ( k )) end do rhs2 = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) reduce ( + : rhs2 ) rhs2 = rhs2 + si % rhs_d ( k ) * si % rhs_d ( k ) end do tol2 = max ( SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_TOL * SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_TOL * rhs2 , 1.0e-60_wp ) cg_it_total = 0 cg_it = 0 mass_res = 0.0_wp wetcount_prev = - 1 converged = . false . do nit = 1 , SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_MAX call si_unstr_wetdry_wetfrac ( si % n_sub , nct , nco , si % eta , si % b_sub , si % a_wet ) call si_unstr_wetdry_volume ( si % n_sub , nct , nco , si % eta , si % b_sub , si % v_cell ) call si_unstr_wetdry_mass_diag ( nct , nco , si % a_wet , si % Hf_edge , si % mass_diag ) call si_unstr_apply_helmholtz ( mesh , nct , nco , si % eta , si % newton_Jeta , & si % Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , & mass_diag = si % mass_diag ) call si_unstr_wetdry_newton_residual ( nct , nco , si % eta , si % newton_Jeta , & si % mass_diag , si % v_cell , & si % rhs_d , si % newton_F , f2 ) call si_unstr_wetdry_wetcount ( si % n_sub , nct , nco , si % eta , si % b_sub , wetcount ) if ( nit > 1 . and . wetcount == wetcount_prev . and . f2 < tol2 ) then converged = . true . exit end if wetcount_prev = wetcount ! Solve J*dz = -F from zero (full-array zero so the ghost band of ! the search space stays 0); eta += dz. do concurrent ( k = 1 : nct ) si % newton_dz ( k ) = 0.0_wp end do do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) si % eta_r ( k ) = - si % newton_F ( k ) end do call si_unstr_cg_solve ( mesh , nct , nco , si % newton_dz , si % eta_r , & si % eta_p , si % eta_Ap , si % eta_z , si % eta_diag , & si % Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , si % precond , & si % rtol , cg_it , mass_res , & mass_diag = si % mass_diag ) cg_it_total = cg_it_total + cg_it do concurrent ( k = 1 : nco ) si % eta ( k ) = si % eta ( k ) + si % newton_dz ( k ) end do end do si % newton_iters = min ( nit , SI_UNSTR_NEWTON_MAX ) ! Report the NONLINEAR mass residual ||F||&#94;2 (the conservation ! diagnostic), not `mass_res` (the inner-CG residual of the final ! delta-solve — an internal solver number that misleads anyone ! reading state%si%mass_res as a mass defect). si % mass_res = f2 if (. not . converged ) then call global_logger % warning ( \"si_ml_wetdry_newton: Newton did not \" // & \"converge in the iteration cap; last ||F||&#94;2 above tol.\" ) end if end associate iter_out = cg_it_total end subroutine si_ml_wetdry_newton end module rki_si_unstr_step_ml","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_keps_unstr.F90 – Rakali","text":"Two-equation k-epsilon vertical-mixing closure (unstructured multilayer). This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_ml_keps_unstr.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_ml_keps_unstr.f90 rki_ml_keps_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_keps_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_keps_stability.f90 rki_keps_stability.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_keps_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_keps_stability.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common_unstr.f90 rki_ml_common_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_keps_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_common_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 rki_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_keps_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_keps_stability.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90 rki_barotropic_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 rki_boundary_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_bound