lid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr.f90 rki_kernel_sponge_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 rki_solver_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Sponge layer relaxation kernel for the unstructured solver module rki_kernel_sponge_unstr !! Explicit volumetric damping of h and momentum toward a reference !! state at cells adjacent to boundary edges tagged `BC_SPONGE`. !! !! Algorithm: for each owned cell, scan the three edges.  If any edge !! is a boundary edge (`mesh%neighbours(e, cell) < 0`) belonging to a !! BC_SPONGE group, collect the group's `strength` [1/s] and `h_ref` !! [m]. When multiple sponge edges exist (a corner cell), use the !! maximum strength and its paired `h_ref`.  Then apply one forward- !! Euler relaxation step: !! !!   h <- h - dt*alpha*(h - h_ref) !!   xmom <- xmom*(1 - dt*alpha) !!   ymom <- ymom*(1 - dt*alpha) !! !! where `h = stage_cv - bed_cv` and `alpha = bc_sponge_strength(g)`. !! !! The kernel self-gates: cells not adjacent to any active BC_SPONGE !! edge are skipped implicitly (alpha stays at 0).  No-op when !! `strength <= 0` for all sponge groups. !! !! v1 limitation: the sponge band is one cell deep — only cells with !! a direct boundary edge are affected.  Graded-width profiles require !! cell-distance information that is not available on triangular meshes !! without additional mesh topology data.  On the structured side the !! distance is implicit in the (i,j) indices; no such shortcut exists !! here.  Multi-cell sponge widths are deferred. use rki_constants , only : wp use rki_state_unstr , only : unstr_state_t use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t use rki_boundary_unstr , only : BC_SPONGE implicit none private public :: apply_sponge_unstr contains pure subroutine apply_sponge_unstr ( state , mesh , dt ) !! Apply sponge relaxation to all owned cells adjacent to a BC_SPONGE edge. !! !! Relaxes `h = stage_cv - bed_cv` toward `bc_sponge_h_ref(g)` and !! `xmom_cv`/`ymom_cv` toward 0.  No-op when no sponge edges exist or !! all sponge strengths are 0. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt integer :: cell , e , g real ( wp ) :: alpha , h_ref_best , h_water , h_new do concurrent ( cell = 1 : state % ncells_owned ) & local ( e , g , alpha , h_ref_best , h_water , h_new ) ! Scan all three edges for the highest-strength sponge group. alpha = 0.0_wp h_ref_best = 0.0_wp do e = 1 , 3 if ( mesh % neighbours ( e , cell ) < 0 ) then g = mesh % bc_group ( e , cell ) if ( g > 0 ) then if ( state % bc_type ( g ) == BC_SPONGE . and . & state % bc_sponge_strength ( g ) > alpha ) then alpha = state % bc_sponge_strength ( g ) h_ref_best = state % bc_sponge_h_ref ( g ) end if end if end if end do if ( alpha > 0.0_wp ) then h_water = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( cell ) - state % barotropic % bed_cv ( cell ) h_new = h_water - dt * alpha * ( h_water - h_ref_best ) state % barotropic % stage_cv ( cell ) = h_new + state % barotropic % bed_cv ( cell ) state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( cell ) = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( cell ) * ( 1.0_wp - dt * alpha ) state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( cell ) = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( cell ) * ( 1.0_wp - dt * alpha ) end if end do end subroutine apply_sponge_unstr end module rki_kernel_sponge_unstr","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_kernel_sponge_unstr.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.F90 – Rakali","text":"Matrix-free TPFA Helmholtz operator + RHS for the unstructured SI surface. This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90 rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.F90 sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 rki_boundary_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 rki_mesh_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 rki_si_unstr_mg.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90 rki_si_unstr_state.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90 rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step.f90 rki_si_unstr_step.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90 rki_si_unstr_step_ml.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 rki_solver_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Matrix-free TPFA Helmholtz operator + RHS for the unstructured SI surface. module rki_si_unstr_helmholtz !! The elliptic (wave-continuity) machinery for the semi-implicit !! free-surface mode on the UNSTRUCTURED (triangular) backend — the !! two-point flux (TPFA, Casulli & Walters 2000) scheme.  Substituting the semi-implicit edge momentum into !! depth-integrated continuity gives a Helmholtz system for eta&#94;{n+1} at !! the circumcentres: !! !!   [ M - g*theta&#94;2*dt&#94;2 * div_c( Hf grad_e ) ] eta&#94;{n+1} = RHS !! !! with the CELL-CENTRED FV divergence (÷area_c, depth units) and the !! per-edge TPFA transmissibility `K_e = Hf_e * len_e / delta_e` !! (`delta_e` = circumcentre-to-circumcentre distance).  `M` is the cell !! mass coefficient (1 on the all-wet 2D path; the wet/dry Newton diagonal !! in P3.3). !! !! THE LOAD-BEARING DETAIL: the operator (T eta)_c = -(coef/area_c) * !! sum_e sign_e K_e (eta_nbr - eta_c) is self-adjoint in the AREA-WEIGHTED !! inner product <x,y> = sum_c area_c x_c y_c, NOT the plain dot — variable !! cell areas scale the rows.  Every CG/Jacobi reduction here carries the !! `area` weight; uniform area recovers the structured harness.  Get it !! wrong and CG stalls (prototype §7.5). !! !! CELL-CENTRIC DOUBLE-VISIT: every apply computes each cell's own row !! from its own 3 edges (reads neighbour eta, writes own Ap) — the house !! flux pattern, GPU-race-free.  Interior edges are visited twice (once !! from each side); no scatter, no atomics.  Single-rank, owned-cell loops. use rki_constants , only : wp , GRAVITY use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t use rki_si_unstr_mg , only : agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t , & agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond implicit none private public :: si_unstr_edge_flux public :: si_unstr_face_depths public :: si_unstr_apply_helmholtz public :: si_unstr_compute_diag public :: si_unstr_compute_rhs public :: si_unstr_cg_solve integer , parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 !! Triangles only. real ( wp ), parameter :: DELTA_EPS = 1.0e-30_wp !! 1/0 armour on the circumcentre-line distance (never fires on a !! gated mesh — the quality gate rejects delta<=0 at configure). integer , parameter :: SI_MAX_ITER = 4000 !! CG iteration cap (triangle plain-CG is ~7x the structured count at !! matched Courant — prototype study 4; the cap leaves headroom). contains pure function si_unstr_edge_flux ( hf , eta_c , eta_nbr , inv_delta ) result ( flux ) !! The single discrete edge-normal transport used by the TPFA !! operator's `div(Hf grad eta)`, the edge predictor's explicit PGF, !! and the edge back-substitution: !!   flux = Hf * (eta_nbr - eta_c) / delta   (along the outward normal) !! Sharing ONE flux function across the operator/back-sub is what makes !! the back-substituted edge transports satisfy discrete continuity !! identically (mass consistency).  `!$acc routine seq` for device !! do-concurrent bodies. !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hf !! Frozen edge effective depth Hf_e. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_c , eta_nbr !! eta at this cell / the across-edge neighbour (or Dirichlet ghost). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: inv_delta !! 1/delta_e (circumcentre-line distance reciprocal). real ( wp ) :: flux flux = hf * ( eta_nbr - eta_c ) * inv_delta end function si_unstr_edge_flux pure function si_unstr_face_depth_linear ( h_c , h_nbr ) result ( hf ) !! All-wet (2D barotropic) edge effective depth: the arithmetic mean of !! the two cells' still-water depths, `Hf = 0.5*(h_c + h_nbr)`.  This is !! the gated-mean rule (`face_depth_wetdry`) in its !! all-wet limit — it reduces EXACTLY to the linear edge depth.  Wall edges never call !! this (Hf stays 0); Dirichlet edges pass the ghost `h`. !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_c , h_nbr real ( wp ) :: hf hf = 0.5_wp * ( h_c + h_nbr ) end function si_unstr_face_depth_linear pure subroutine si_unstr_face_depths ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , n_bc , & height , bed , bc_type , bc_eta_ext , & Hf_edge , eta_ghost_edge ) !! Build the per-edge frozen effective depth Hf_e (2D all-wet path) AND !! the per-edge Dirichlet ghost surface `eta_ghost_edge`: !!   interior/partition edge: Hf = 0.5*(h_c + h_nbr); ghost unused (0). !!   WALL edge: Hf = 0 (no coupling — no-flux Neumann in the coeffs). !!   TIDAL/CLAMPED (Dirichlet) edge: the ghost surface is the prescribed !!     eta_bc; the ghost bed mirrors the cell bed so the ghost depth is !!     h_ghost = eta_bc - b_c, and Hf = 0.5*(h_c + h_ghost).  The ghost !!     eta is stashed in `eta_ghost_edge(i,k)` for the operator + RHS + !!     back-sub (the coefficient-space Dirichlet route). !! !! Cell-centric double-visit `(3, ncell)`: each cell fills its own 3 !! edge values from its own `height`/`bed` + the neighbour's `height` !! (read-only); interior edges are visited twice with the same result. use rki_boundary_unstr , only : BC_WALL , BC_TIDAL , BC_CLAMPED type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_total !! Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_owned !! Owned-cell loop bound. integer , intent ( in ) :: n_bc !! BC group table size (`MAX_BC_GROUPS`). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: height ( ncell_total ) !! Still-water depth h at cells (m). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: bed ( ncell_total ) !! Bed elevation b at cells (m). integer , intent ( in ) :: bc_type ( n_bc ) !! Per-group BC type (`state%bc_type`), the boundary lookup. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: bc_eta_ext ( n_bc ) !! Per-group Dirichlet external surface eta (m) (`state%bc_eta_ext`). real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) !! Edge effective depth (m). real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: eta_ghost_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) !! Dirichlet ghost surface eta (m) on Dirichlet boundary edges; !! 0 elsewhere (unread — Hf=0 there). integer :: k , i , kn , g , bt real ( wp ) :: h_ghost , eta_bc do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) local ( i , kn , g , bt , h_ghost , eta_bc ) do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI eta_ghost_edge ( i , k ) = 0.0_wp kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , k ) if ( kn > 0 ) then ! Interior / partition edge: arithmetic-mean still depth. Hf_edge ( i , k ) = si_unstr_face_depth_linear ( height ( k ), height ( kn )) else g = mesh % bc_group ( i , k ) bt = BC_WALL if ( g >= 1 . and . g <= n_bc ) bt = bc_type ( g ) if (( bt == BC_TIDAL . or . bt == BC_CLAMPED ) . and . g >= 1 ) then eta_bc = bc_eta_ext ( g ) h_ghost = max ( eta_bc - bed ( k ), 0.0_wp ) Hf_edge ( i , k ) = si_unstr_face_depth_linear ( height ( k ), h_ghost ) eta_ghost_edge ( i , k ) = eta_bc else Hf_edge ( i , k ) = 0.0_wp end if end if end do end do end subroutine si_unstr_face_depths pure subroutine si_unstr_apply_helmholtz ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , & eta , Ap , Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , & mass_diag ) !! Matrix-free apply `Ap = A*eta` for the SPD TPFA Helmholtz operator: !! !!   Ap_c = M_c*eta_c - (g*theta&#94;2*dt&#94;2/area_c) * !!            sum_{e in c} sign_e * K_e * (eta_nbr - eta_c) !! !! with sign_e = +1 (flux LEAVES the cell along the outward normal), !! K_e = Hf_e*len_e/delta_e, and the divergence in depth units (÷area). !! Wall edges carry Hf=0 => no coupling (no-flux Neumann).  Dirichlet !! edges read the ghost eta the caller seeded into eta(kn) — the !! coefficient-space route (no separate elimination pass). !! !! `M_c` is the cell mass: absent `mass_diag` => M=1 (the linear !! all-wet operator); present => the wet/dry Newton diagonal a+floor. !! !! Cell-centric double-visit: reads neighbour eta, writes own Ap. type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_total !! Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_owned !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: Ap ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: g_theta2_dt2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: mass_diag ( ncell_total ) !! Per-cell Newton mass diagonal (wet/dry); absent => 1.0. integer :: k , i , kn real ( wp ) :: div_flux , ke , mass_k logical :: have_mass have_mass = present ( mass_diag ) do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) local ( i , kn , div_flux , ke , mass_k ) div_flux = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI if ( Hf_edge ( i , k ) > 0.0_wp ) then ke = Hf_edge ( i , k ) * mesh % edge_len ( i , k ) & / max ( mesh % edge_delta ( i , k ), DELTA_EPS ) kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , k ) if ( kn > 0 ) then ! Interior edge: read the neighbour eta. div_flux = div_flux + ke * ( eta ( kn ) - eta ( k )) else ! Dirichlet boundary edge (Hf>0 <=> tidal/clamped): the ! FIXED ghost eta is NOT a CG unknown, so it reads as 0 in ! the operator (A*p) — this stiffens the diagonal; the ! ghost's real value is folded into the RHS (coefficient- ! space Dirichlet route).  Contribution: ke*(0 - eta(k)). div_flux = div_flux - ke * eta ( k ) end if end if end do if ( have_mass ) then mass_k = mass_diag ( k ) else mass_k = 1.0_wp end if Ap ( k ) = mass_k * eta ( k ) - g_theta2_dt2 * div_flux / mesh % area ( k ) end do end subroutine si_unstr_apply_helmholtz pure subroutine si_unstr_compute_diag ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , & Hf_edge , eta_diag , g_theta2_dt2 , & mass_diag ) !! Precompute the reciprocal of the TPFA Helmholtz operator diagonal !! (Jacobi preconditioner): !!   diag_c = M_c + (g*theta&#94;2*dt&#94;2/area_c) * sum_{e in c} K_e !! stored as 1/diag.  M_c = 1 (linear) or a+floor (wet/dry, present !! `mass_diag`).  Wall edges (Hf=0) drop out => diag -> M there. type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_total !! Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_owned !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: eta_diag ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: g_theta2_dt2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: mass_diag ( ncell_total ) integer :: k , i real ( wp ) :: ksum , ke , mass_k , diag_k logical :: have_mass have_mass = present ( mass_diag ) do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) local ( i , ksum , ke , mass_k , diag_k ) ksum = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI if ( Hf_edge ( i , k ) > 0.0_wp ) then ke = Hf_edge ( i , k ) * mesh % edge_len ( i , k ) & / max ( mesh % edge_delta ( i , k ), DELTA_EPS ) ksum = ksum + ke end if end do if ( have_mass ) then mass_k = mass_diag ( k ) else mass_k = 1.0_wp end if diag_k = mass_k + g_theta2_dt2 * ksum / mesh % area ( k ) eta_diag ( k ) = 1.0_wp / diag_k end do end subroutine si_unstr_compute_diag subroutine si_unstr_compute_rhs ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , & eta_n , u_star , u_n , rhs , dt , theta , & Hf_edge , eta_ghost_edge , g_theta2_dt2 ) !! Assemble the theta-blend RHS from the CELL edge transports: !!   RHS_c = eta&#94;n_c - (dt/area_c) * sum_{e in c} sign_e * !!             [theta*U*_e + (1-theta)*U&#94;n_e] * len_e !!             + (coef/area_c) * sum_{Dirichlet e in c} K_e * eta_ghost_e !! U*_e / U&#94;n_e are per-edge transports (double-visit (3,ncell)); the !! blend flux telescopes over interior edges (each shared by 2 cells !! with opposite outward normals) and every wall edge carries 0 !! (Hf=0 kills the predictor PGF, and U&#94;n is zeroed on dead edges), so !! total mass is conserved to CG tolerance + round-off by construction. !! The Dirichlet term is the coefficient-space route: the operator !! (`si_unstr_apply_helmholtz`) treats the fixed ghost eta as 0, so its !! real value is carried here. !! !! The theta-blend is a STABILITY condition (not accuracy): bare !! div(U*) over-weights the explicit Laplacian by 1/theta and diverges !! at large Courant (structured proto A/B: ~1e11x growth) — same trap !! edge-wise. type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_total !! Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_owned !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_n ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_star ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: u_n ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rhs ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt , theta real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_ghost_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: g_theta2_dt2 integer :: k , i , kn real ( wp ) :: one_m_theta , divU , flux_e , ghost_sum , ke one_m_theta = 1.0_wp - theta do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) local ( i , kn , divU , flux_e , ghost_sum , ke ) divU = 0.0_wp ghost_sum = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , EDGES_PER_TRI ! Blended edge transport (m&#94;2/s); U&#94;n already zeroed on dead ! edges by the caller (R3).  +sign: leaves the cell. flux_e = theta * u_star ( i , k ) + one_m_theta * u_n ( i , k ) divU = divU + flux_e * mesh % edge_len ( i , k ) ! Dirichlet ghost coupling (boundary edge with Hf>0). kn = mesh % neighbours ( i , k ) if ( kn < 0 . and . Hf_edge ( i , k ) > 0.0_wp ) then ke = Hf_edge ( i , k ) * mesh % edge_len ( i , k ) & / max ( mesh % edge_delta ( i , k ), DELTA_EPS ) ghost_sum = ghost_sum + ke * eta_ghost_edge ( i , k ) end if end do rhs ( k ) = eta_n ( k ) - dt * divU / mesh % area ( k ) & + g_theta2_dt2 * ghost_sum / mesh % area ( k ) end do end subroutine si_unstr_compute_rhs subroutine si_unstr_cg_solve ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , & eta , cg_r , cg_p , cg_Ap , cg_z , eta_diag , & Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , precond , rtol , & iter_out , mass_res_out , mass_diag , mg ) !! Area-weighted (optionally preconditioned) CG for the TPFA Helmholtz !! eta-solve, warm-started from eta&#94;n.  On entry `cg_r` holds the RHS and !! `eta` the warm start.  EVERY dot product carries the `mesh%area` !! weight (the operator is self-adjoint in <x,y>_A only — prototype !! §7.5); the convergence gate is the area-weighted relative residual !! `||r||_A&#94;2 < rtol&#94;2 ||rhs||_A&#94;2` on the UNPRECONDITIONED residual in !! every mode (comparable iteration counts).  Preconditioners: !! NONE (plain), JACOBI (`z = eta_diag*r`), MG (aggregation-multigrid !! V-cycle via `mg`, `z = Vcycle_Ahat(area*r)` — the same `area*r` !! symmetric-space RHS the Jacobi apply implicitly uses). use rki_si_unstr_state , only : SI_PRECOND_NONE , SI_PRECOND_JACOBI , & SI_PRECOND_MG type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_total !! Cell array extent (owned + halo) — the explicit-shape dim. integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_owned !! Owned-cell loop bound. real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: eta ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: cg_r ( ncell_total ), cg_p ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: cg_Ap ( ncell_total ), cg_z ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: eta_diag ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: Hf_edge ( EDGES_PER_TRI , ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: g_theta2_dt2 , rtol integer , intent ( in ) :: precond integer , intent ( out ) :: iter_out real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: mass_res_out !! Area-weighted interior residual sum at solve end (mass diagnostic). real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: mass_diag ( ncell_total ) type ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ), optional :: mg !! Aggregation-MG hierarchy (required when precond == MG); its !! operator must already be refreshed for this step's frozen Hf. integer :: k , iter real ( wp ) :: rz , rr , rz_new , pAp , alpha , beta , tol2 , rhs2 , res_sum logical :: use_pc , use_mg , have_mass iter_out = 0 mass_res_out = 0.0_wp use_mg = ( precond == SI_PRECOND_MG ) use_pc = ( precond == SI_PRECOND_JACOBI ) . or . use_mg have_mass = present ( mass_diag ) ! Jacobi needs the operator diagonal; MG carries its own per-level diag ! (under MG `eta_diag` stays STALE and is threaded through ! si_unstr_precond_apply UNREAD — do not consume it on that branch). if ( precond == SI_PRECOND_JACOBI ) then if ( have_mass ) then call si_unstr_compute_diag ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , Hf_edge , & eta_diag , g_theta2_dt2 , mass_diag = mass_diag ) else call si_unstr_compute_diag ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , Hf_edge , & eta_diag , g_theta2_dt2 ) end if end if ! ||rhs||_A&#94;2 for the relative test (cg_r still holds the RHS). rhs2 = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) reduce ( + : rhs2 ) rhs2 = rhs2 + mesh % area ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) end do tol2 = max ( rtol * rtol * rhs2 , 1.0e-60_wp ) ! Zero the full search direction (ghost/halo band stays 0 so a ! Dirichlet ghost is never a CG unknown). do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_total ) cg_p ( k ) = 0.0_wp end do ! r = rhs - A*eta (warm start eta = eta&#94;n). if ( have_mass ) then call si_unstr_apply_helmholtz ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , eta , & cg_Ap , Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , & mass_diag = mass_diag ) else call si_unstr_apply_helmholtz ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , eta , & cg_Ap , Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 ) end if do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) cg_r ( k ) = cg_r ( k ) - cg_Ap ( k ) end do rr = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) reduce ( + : rr ) rr = rr + mesh % area ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) end do if ( rr < tol2 ) then res_sum = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) reduce ( + : res_sum ) res_sum = res_sum + mesh % area ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) end do mass_res_out = res_sum return end if if ( use_pc ) then call si_unstr_precond_apply ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , cg_r , cg_z , & eta_diag , use_mg , mg ) do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) cg_p ( k ) = cg_z ( k ) end do rz = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) reduce ( + : rz ) rz = rz + mesh % area ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) * cg_z ( k ) end do else do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) cg_p ( k ) = cg_r ( k ) end do rz = rr end if do iter = 1 , SI_MAX_ITER if ( have_mass ) then call si_unstr_apply_helmholtz ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , cg_p , & cg_Ap , Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 , & mass_diag = mass_diag ) else call si_unstr_apply_helmholtz ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , cg_p , & cg_Ap , Hf_edge , g_theta2_dt2 ) end if pAp = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) reduce ( + : pAp ) pAp = pAp + mesh % area ( k ) * cg_p ( k ) * cg_Ap ( k ) end do if ( abs ( pAp ) < 1.0e-30_wp ) exit alpha = rz / pAp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) eta ( k ) = eta ( k ) + alpha * cg_p ( k ) cg_r ( k ) = cg_r ( k ) - alpha * cg_Ap ( k ) end do rr = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) reduce ( + : rr ) rr = rr + mesh % area ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) end do iter_out = iter if ( rr < tol2 ) exit if ( use_pc ) then call si_unstr_precond_apply ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , cg_r , & cg_z , eta_diag , use_mg , mg ) rz_new = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) reduce ( + : rz_new ) rz_new = rz_new + mesh % area ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) * cg_z ( k ) end do beta = rz_new / rz rz = rz_new do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) cg_p ( k ) = cg_z ( k ) + beta * cg_p ( k ) end do else beta = rr / rz rz = rr do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) cg_p ( k ) = cg_r ( k ) + beta * cg_p ( k ) end do end if end do res_sum = 0.0_wp do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) reduce ( + : res_sum ) res_sum = res_sum + mesh % area ( k ) * cg_r ( k ) end do mass_res_out = res_sum end subroutine si_unstr_cg_solve subroutine si_unstr_precond_apply ( mesh , ncell_total , ncell_owned , r , z , & eta_diag , use_mg , mg ) !! Preconditioner apply z = M&#94;{-1} r for the area-weighted PCG. !! JACOBI: z = eta_diag*r (diagonal).  MG: one aggregation-multigrid !! V-cycle of the symmetric Ahat on the area-weighted RHS !! (`agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond` folds the `area*r`), which reduces to !! the Jacobi apply when the V-cycle is a single diagonal sweep — the !! generalisation is exact (module header).  Owned cells only; the ghost !! band of z is left as the caller set it (pre-zeroed). type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: ncell_total , ncell_owned real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: z ( ncell_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eta_diag ( ncell_total ) logical , intent ( in ) :: use_mg type ( agglom_hierarchy_unstr_t ), intent ( inout ), optional :: mg integer :: k if ( use_mg ) then ! Belt for direct callers: the wetdry-Newton / ML call sites omit ! `mg` and can never carry use_mg (enable_si fences mg to the 2D ! all-wet path) — but an absent optional here would be a silent ! deref, not a diagnosis. if (. not . present ( mg )) then error stop \"si_unstr_precond_apply: use_mg without the mg \" // & \"hierarchy argument (mg precond is 2D-barotropic-only)\" end if call agglom_unstr_vcycle_precond ( mg , r , z , mesh % area , ncell_total , & ncell_owned ) else do concurrent ( k = 1 : ncell_owned ) z ( k ) = eta_diag ( k ) * r ( k ) end do end if end subroutine si_unstr_precond_apply end module rki_si_unstr_helmholtz","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_si_unstr_helmholtz.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_ml_friction.F90 – Rakali","text":"Per-layer Manning bottom friction and per-layer Coriolis rotation. This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_ml_friction.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_ml_friction.f90 rki_ml_friction.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_friction.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_friction.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90 rki_ml_common.F90 sourcefile~rki_ml_friction.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_ml_friction.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_ml_friction.f90 rki_ml_friction.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 rki_solver.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_friction.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Per-layer Manning bottom friction and per-layer Coriolis rotation. module rki_ml_friction !! Manning quadratic bottom friction on the bottom layer (k=1) and per-layer !! Coriolis rotation of every layer's momentum (`ml_apply_coriolis`). !! !! Per-layer (vs depth-averaged) friction/Coriolis damps and rotates the !! baroclinic shear (gravity currents, dense overflows) using each layer's !! own velocity. Replaces the depth-averaged `apply_coriolis` on the !! multilayer path; the barotropic-only path keeps the depth-averaged version. !! !! Layers are bottom-up (k=1 bed, k=nz surface): bed friction acts at k=1. !! Semi-implicit friction: hu_new = hu_old / (1 + dt*C_d*|u_b|/h_k), !! C_d = g*n&#94;2/H&#94;{1/3}. use rki_constants , only : wp , GRAVITY , THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD use rki_grid , only : hgrid_t use rki_ml_common , only : VANISHING_LAYER_TOL implicit none private public :: ml_apply_bottom_friction public :: ml_apply_coriolis contains pure subroutine ml_apply_bottom_friction ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , & manning_n , use_linear_drag , drag_r , & grid , nz , dt ) !! Apply bottom friction to the lowest active layer (k=1, bottom-up) using !! that layer's velocity. Two semi-implicit drag laws: !!   quadratic Manning (default):  hu_new = hu / (1 + dt*C_d*|u_b|/h_k), !!     C_d = g*n&#94;2/H&#94;{1/3}, H = total column depth. !!   linear Rayleigh (`use_linear_drag`):  hu_new = hu / (1 + dt*r). type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: manning_n , dt logical , intent ( in ) :: use_linear_drag !! Use linear (Rayleigh) drag with rate `drag_r` instead of Manning. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: drag_r !! Linear bottom-drag rate (1/s); only read when use_linear_drag. integer :: i , j , k_bot , kk , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: h_k , h_total , u_b , v_b , speed_b , cf , denom nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost if ( use_linear_drag ) then if ( drag_r <= 0.0_wp ) return else if ( manning_n <= 0.0_wp ) return end if do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k_bot , kk , h_k , h_total , u_b , v_b , speed_b , cf , denom ) ! Find the lowest active layer (k_bot).  For VCOORD_SIGMA / ! ZSIGMA / ZSTAR (lite), k=1 is always active (the deepest ! non-vanishing layer = k=1).  For VCOORD_ZSTAR_FULL the ! bottom layer can be parked at h_min when the column is ! shallower than the reference; in that case skip up to the ! lowest layer with thickness above the vanishing threshold. k_bot = 1 do kk = 1 , nz if ( h_layer ( i , j , kk ) > VANISHING_LAYER_TOL ) then k_bot = kk exit end if end do h_k = h_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) if ( h_k < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) cycle ! Total column depth for Manning coefficient h_total = 0.0_wp do kk = 1 , nz h_total = h_total + h_layer ( i , j , kk ) end do if ( h_total < THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) cycle u_b = hu_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) / h_k v_b = hv_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) / h_k speed_b = sqrt ( u_b * u_b + v_b * v_b ) ! Semi-implicit divide: linear (constant rate) or Manning (speed- ! and depth-dependent C_d). if ( use_linear_drag ) then denom = 1.0_wp + dt * drag_r else cf = GRAVITY * manning_n * manning_n / ( h_total ** ( 1.0_wp / 3.0_wp )) denom = 1.0_wp + dt * cf * speed_b / h_k end if hu_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) = hu_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) / denom hv_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) = hv_layer ( i , j , k_bot ) / denom end do end subroutine ml_apply_bottom_friction pure subroutine ml_apply_coriolis ( h_layer , hu_layer , hv_layer , grid , nz , dt , f ) !! Per-layer Coriolis rotation: rotate every layer's `(hu_k, hv_k)` !! through angle `f*dt` via the closed-form (energy-conserving, det=1) !! rotation matrix !!   hu_new =  hu_old*cos(f*dt) + hv_old*sin(f*dt) !!   hv_new = -hu_old*sin(f*dt) + hv_old*cos(f*dt) !! `f` is a scalar (latitude-only). Skips layers below the dry-cell !! threshold so already-zeroed momentum is untouched. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid integer , intent ( in ) :: nz real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: h_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv_layer ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total , nz ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt , f integer :: i , j , k , nx , ny , nghost real ( wp ) :: cosf , sinf , hu_old , hv_old if ( f == 0.0_wp ) return nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost cosf = cos ( f * dt ) sinf = sin ( f * dt ) do concurrent ( j = nghost + 1 : ny - nghost , i = nghost + 1 : nx - nghost ) & local ( k , hu_old , hv_old ) do k = 1 , nz if ( h_layer ( i , j , k ) > THIN_LAYER_THRESHOLD ) then hu_old = hu_layer ( i , j , k ) hv_old = hv_layer ( i , j , k ) hu_layer ( i , j , k ) = hu_old * cosf + hv_old * sinf hv_layer ( i , j , k ) = - hu_old * sinf + hv_old * cosf end if end do end do end subroutine ml_apply_coriolis end module rki_ml_friction","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_ml_friction.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_recon_weno.F90 – Rakali","text":"WENO tracer face-reconstruction ladder for the structured multilayer solver. Provides a drop-in replacement for PPM tracer advection, offering a\nrung-adaptive reconstruction that automatically degrades to lower-order\nschemes near boundaries where the full stencil is unavailable. Schemes (all with Z-weights, Borges et al. 2008):\n  WENO5  — Jiang & Shu (1996),  3 quadratic candidates, nghost >= 3\n  WENO7  — Balsara & Shu (2000), 4 cubic     candidates, nghost >= 4\n  WENO9  — Balsara & Shu (2000), 5 quartic   candidates, nghost >= 5 Caveat on WENO9 order: this rung uses simplified 3-term smoothness\nindicators rather than the full quartic betas, so its effective\nconvergence is ~order 6 (not the nominal 9), and at a sharp front it\novershoots slightly MORE than WENO7 — WENO7 gives the best front L1.\nDo not assume weno9 > weno7. See the function docstring and\ndocs/REFERENCE.md for the measured comparison. At interior cells far from boundaries the requested scheme is used.\nAs a face approaches the boundary the stencil is automatically degraded:\n  WENO9 → WENO7 → WENO5 → PLM → donor-cell The swept-average form is used throughout: for upwind cell c with\nCFL sigma, the face value integrates the reconstruction over\n[c + 1/2 - sigma, c + 1/2], giving a time-averaged flux consistent\nwith the subcycled PPM approach in the rest of the solver. This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_recon_weno.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90 rki_recon_weno.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90 rki_ml_common.F90 sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_recon_weno.f90~~Afferent