Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Boundary condition type constants for the unstructured solver module rki_boundary_unstr !! Integer constants identifying the boundary condition type for !! each boundary edge group, plus a fixed maximum on the number of !! groups a single mesh can carry. Mirrors the role of !! `rki_boundary_types` on the structured side. Seven BC types are !! fully dispatched inside `compute_boundary_state_impl` !! (inlined into `rki_kernel_flux_unstr`): `BC_WALL`, `BC_OPEN`, `BC_INFLOW`, !! `BC_DISCHARGE`, `BC_OUTFLOW`, `BC_TIDAL`, `BC_CLAMPED`. `BC_CHAPMAN` !! is dispatched one level higher in the flux kernel !! (`rki_kernel_flux_unstr`) because it needs per-edge mesh access to !! compute the radiating ghost target before falling through into the !! Flather/`BC_TIDAL` algebra. The multilayer tracer advection kernel !! (`ml_advect_tracer_unstr`) honours `bc_S_ext` / `bc_T_ext` at !! inflow edges, so freshwater / clamped-tracer river inflows work !! end-to-end. Types that live on the structured side but are not yet !! ported: `BC_NESTED`, `BC_SPONGE`. !! !! `BC_TIDAL` is a Flather radiating boundary that clamps the ghost !! stage to `bc_eta_ext(g)` and reconstructs the ghost outward-normal !! velocity from the outgoing Riemann invariant. `BC_CLAMPED` does !! the same stage clamp but copies momentum transmissively (no !! radiation term) -- pick it when you want a pure Dirichlet stage !! without the wave-radiation coupling. !! !! How a mesh wires up its boundary edges: !! !!   * Every boundary edge of a triangle has `mesh%neighbours(i, k) == -1` !!     and `mesh%bc_group(i, k) >= 0`. Group 0 means \"no group set !!     -- treat as default wall\". !!   * `state%bc_type(g)` for `g = 1..MAX_BC_GROUPS` says what BC !!     type group `g` represents. Defaults to `BC_WALL` so a fresh !!     state with no explicit BC setup behaves like an all-walls !!     domain (which is what we want for lake-at-rest tests). !!   * The flux kernel reads the bc_type via this lookup and !!     dispatches inside `compute_boundary_state_impl` (inlined in !!     `rki_kernel_flux_unstr`) to build the right-side ghost state. !!   * Tracer inflow values live in `state%bc_S_ext(g)` / !!     `state%bc_T_ext(g)` and are consumed by !!     `ml_advect_tracer_unstr` on edges whose mass flux is into !!     the domain. !! !! Integer values match the structured side !! (`rki_boundary_types`): WALL=1, OPEN=2, TIDAL=3, NESTED=4, !! INFLOW=5, DISCHARGE=6, CLAMPED=7, SPONGE=8, CHAPMAN=9. Only the !! types actually dispatched here are re-declared; the rest of that !! range is reserved. `BC_OUTFLOW = 10` is unstructured-only and !! sits past the structured range to avoid future collisions. implicit none private public :: BC_INTERIOR public :: BC_WALL public :: BC_OPEN public :: BC_NESTED public :: BC_INFLOW public :: BC_DISCHARGE public :: BC_OUTFLOW public :: BC_TIDAL public :: BC_CLAMPED public :: BC_SPONGE public :: BC_CHAPMAN public :: MAX_BC_GROUPS integer , parameter :: BC_INTERIOR = 0 !! Sentinel for interior edges. Never appears in `state%bc_type(:)` !! itself -- it's the value of `bc_group(i, k)` on edges that !! were not assigned to a group at mesh-build time. integer , parameter :: BC_WALL = 1 !! Reflective wall. The right-side ghost state mirrors the left !! state across the edge normal: stage / depth / bed are the !! same, momentum has its normal component negated. Implemented !! in `compute_boundary_state`. integer , parameter :: BC_OPEN = 2 !! Transmissive (zero-gradient) radiation. The right-side ghost !! state copies the left state, so the central-upwind solver !! emits the physical flux of the interior with no reflection. !! Stateless: uses no per-group parameters. integer , parameter :: BC_NESTED = 4 !! Nested boundary: Flather radiation driven by a parent-model !! prescribed elevation per BC group.  At smoke level this is !! identical to `BC_TIDAL` — per-group `bc_eta_ext(g)` supplies !! the external stage and the outward-normal ghost velocity is !! reconstructed from the Riemann invariant.  Full parent-model !! coupling (live eta from a coarser grid) is deferred. Matches !! structured `BC_NESTED = 4`. integer , parameter :: BC_TIDAL = 3 !! Prescribed free-surface elevation with Flather radiation. !! The per-group parameter `state%bc_eta_ext(g)` is the absolute !! stage (m, in the same datum as the bed) the kernel clamps the !! ghost stage to. Ghost outward-normal velocity is rebuilt as !!   u_n_ghost = u_n_int + sqrt(g/h_int)*(eta_int - eta_ext) !! so interior-going waves enter driven by the stage anomaly and !! outgoing waves leave cleanly. Update the value between steps !! to drive a tide. Matches structured `BC_TIDAL` semantics. integer , parameter :: BC_INFLOW = 5 !! Prescribed normal velocity. The per-group parameter !! `state%bc_un_ext(g)` is the velocity component along the !! outward normal -- so a value of -2.0 means flow into the !! domain at 2 m/s on a boundary whose outward normal points !! out of the domain. The Python wrapper exposes !! `set_bc_inflow_speed(g, v)` which negates internally so !! positive `v` always means inflow. Depth at the ghost state !! is the extrapolated interior depth. integer , parameter :: BC_DISCHARGE = 6 !! Prescribed momentum flux per unit width (m&#94;2/s) along the !! outward normal. The per-group parameter `state%bc_Qn_ext(g)` !! carries the specific discharge; positive means *out of* the !! domain (along the outward normal). Ghost momentum is rebuilt !! from `(-bc_Qn_ext * n1, -bc_Qn_ext * n2)` so a negative Qn !! pumps mass in without a separate sign flip at the call site. !! Depth at the ghost follows the interior extrapolation. Useful !! when the driving quantity is a measured river flow per unit !! width rather than a velocity. Matches structured BC_DISCHARGE. integer , parameter :: BC_CLAMPED = 7 !! Prescribed free-surface elevation with transmissive momentum !! (no Flather radiation term). The per-group parameter !! `state%bc_eta_ext(g)` is the absolute stage (m); the kernel !! clamps the ghost stage to it and copies interior momentum !! across unchanged. Pick this when you need a Dirichlet stage !! without wave-radiation coupling. Matches structured !! `BC_CLAMPED=7`. integer , parameter :: BC_CHAPMAN = 9 !! Chapman / Orlanski radiating boundary. No per-group external !! parameter; instead the kernel keeps a per-boundary-edge !! persistent state `state%chapman_eta_old(i, k)` (the previous !! step's eta at edge `i` of cell `k`) and reconstructs the ghost !! stage each call from a phase-speed estimate !!   c = -(deta/dt) / (deta/dn_inward) !! clamped to `[0, sqrt(g*h_int)]`. Spatial gradient is !! approximated from the cell's centroid stage and the extrapolated !! edge-midpoint stage; temporal gradient uses `state%dt`. The !! computed ghost target is then dispatched through the !! Flather/`BC_TIDAL` algebra in `compute_boundary_state` so the !! ghost momentum reconstruction matches `BC_TIDAL`. Matches !! structured `BC_CHAPMAN=9` semantics. integer , parameter :: BC_SPONGE = 8 !! Sponge layer: explicit relaxation of h and momentum toward a !! prescribed reference state.  Per-group parameters !! `state%bc_sponge_strength(g)` [1/s] and `state%bc_sponge_h_ref(g)` !! [m] are consumed by `apply_sponge_unstr` (separate kernel, not !! the flux kernel): the sponge falls through to `BC_WALL` ghost !! state in the flux pass, and relaxation is applied after each !! RK2 stage update.  Matches structured `BC_SPONGE = 8`. integer , parameter :: BC_OUTFLOW = 10 !! Prescribed depth at the boundary. The per-group parameter !! `state%bc_h_ext(g)` is the depth (m) the kernel clamps to; !! momentum is transmissive. Useful as a downstream water level !! condition for steady-state channel runs. Unstructured-only; !! no structured analog, numbered past the structured range. integer , parameter :: MAX_BC_GROUPS = 32 !! Maximum number of boundary groups per mesh. Plenty for any !! realistic coastal case (most have 2-5: open ocean, river !! mouths, walls). Fixed-size so the table lives inside the !! state struct without needing a separate `map(to:)`. end module rki_boundary_unstr","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_boundary_unstr.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_si_common.F90 – Rakali","text":"Semi-implicit settings shared by the explicit config path and the\nunstructured semi-implicit solver. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_si_common.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_si_common.f90 rki_si_common.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 rki_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 rki_solver_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_wetdry.f90 rki_si_unstr_wetdry.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_wetdry.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_gauges_unstr.f90 rki_gauges_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_gauges_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 rki_handle.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr.f90 rki_kernel_timestep_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_timestep_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_output_unstr.f90 rki_output_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_output_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_restart_unstr.f90 rki_restart_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_restart_unstr.f90 sourcefil