tr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_kpp_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_pressure_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_tracers_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_truncate_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_vertical_viscosity_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step.f90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_step_ml.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_handle.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Solution state for the unstructured central-upwind solver module rki_state_unstr !! Composition wrapper around the unstructured solver state. !! Mirrors the structured `state_t` decomposition: this type is a !! thin shell that owns mode flags + timing + BC config + the four !! slope-limiter knobs, and composes the sub-state objects: !! !!   `state%barotropic`  -- depth-integrated CV + edge reconstruction !!                          + RK2 saves + Chapman state + per-edge !!                          mass flux + barotropic physics scalars. !!   `state%multilayer`  -- per-layer dynamics + tracer registry + !!                          vcoord + workspaces + EOS / mixing !!                          / BPG scalar config. !! !! The mesh metadata stays as a separate `mesh_unstr_t` argument !! threaded through the kernels (not embedded on `state`) -- same !! convention as before the split. !! !! Variable conventions: !!   stage = w  = h + b           (free-surface elevation) !!   xmom  = uh                   (x-momentum) !!   ymom  = vh                   (y-momentum) !!   bed   = b                    (bathymetry, static after init) !!   height = h                   (= stage - bed, recomputed each step) !! !! All centroid arrays are sized to `mesh%ncells_total` so halo !! cells are available to the kernels without special-casing. use rki_constants , only : wp use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t , mesh_unstr_si_quality_gate use rki_boundary_unstr , only : BC_WALL , MAX_BC_GROUPS use rki_barotropic_state_unstr , only : unstr_barotropic_state_t use rki_multilayer_state_unstr , only : unstr_multilayer_state_t use rki_surface_forcing_unstr , only : unstr_surface_forcing_t use rki_si_unstr_state , only : semi_implicit_state_unstr_t , SI_PRECOND_MG use rki_si_common , only : si_bsub_ml_conflict use rki_timestepper , only : TIME_RK2 use pic_logger , only : logger => global_logger use pic_io , only : to_char implicit none private public :: unstr_state_t public :: LOW_FROUDE_OFF , LOW_FROUDE_1 , LOW_FROUDE_2 integer , parameter :: EDGES_PER_TRI = 3 !! Number of edges per cell. Triangles only for now. ! Low-Froude correction modes for the central-upwind flux. Mirrored ! by the inlined `compute_local_froude_impl` copies in ! `rki_kernel_flux_unstr`; the kernel-side copies are intentional ! duplicates so NVHPC can inline the helper into `flux_one_cell`. integer , parameter :: LOW_FROUDE_OFF = 0 integer , parameter :: LOW_FROUDE_1 = 1 integer , parameter :: LOW_FROUDE_2 = 2 type :: unstr_state_t !! Container for the solution state, factored into sub-objects. ! ----- sizes (cached from the source mesh) ----- integer :: ncells_owned = 0 !! Cells owned by this rank. integer :: ncells_total = 0 !! ncells_owned + ncells_halo. All centroid/edge arrays are this long. ! ----- sub-state objects ----- type ( unstr_barotropic_state_t ) :: barotropic !! Centroid CV + edge reconstruction + per-step accumulators !! + RK2 saves + Chapman BC state + per-edge mass flux + !! barotropic scalar physics.  See `rki_barotropic_state_unstr`. ! Coupled hydrostatic multilayer logical :: use_multilayer = . false . !! When true, `multilayer` is initialised and mapped. type ( unstr_multilayer_state_t ) :: multilayer !! Per-layer arrays, vcoord, tracer registry, workspaces, and !! all multilayer scalar config.  See `rki_multilayer_state_unstr`. ! Surface forcing fields (heat flux + virtual freshwater flux). ! Always allocated and zero-filled so the surface-flux kernel can ! run unconditionally; non-zero values are pushed in via the C API. type ( unstr_surface_forcing_t ) :: forcing !! Surface tracer forcing.  See `rki_surface_forcing_unstr`. ! Semi-implicit (Casulli) free-surface mode. logical :: use_semi_implicit = . false . !! When true, `si` is initialised + mapped and the solver dispatches !! to the unstructured SI step (`time_scheme=\"semi_implicit\"`). type ( semi_implicit_state_unstr_t ) :: si !! CG workspace + edge face-depths for the TPFA Helmholtz eta-solve. !! Allocated only when `use_semi_implicit`.  See `rki_si_unstr_state`. real ( wp ) :: dt_fixed = 0.0_wp !! Fixed timestep (s) for the semi-implicit mode (bypasses the !! gravity-wave CFL).  Set from cfg%dt_fixed at init; 0 on the !! explicit path. ! ----- physics knobs (config-loaded later) ----- real ( wp ) :: minimum_allowed_height = 1.0e-3_wp !! Minimum allowed depth. Cells below this are treated as dry. real ( wp ) :: cfl = 0.5_wp !! Default CFL for the unstructured solver. ! ----- slope-limiter beta values ----- ! Wet/dry blending uses `hfactor` to interpolate between the dry ! value (small, conservative) and the wet value (close to 1). real ( wp ) :: beta_w = 1.0_wp real ( wp ) :: beta_w_dry = 0.2_wp real ( wp ) :: beta_uh = 0.8_wp real ( wp ) :: beta_uh_dry = 0.2_wp real ( wp ) :: beta_vh = 0.8_wp real ( wp ) :: beta_vh_dry = 0.2_wp logical :: extrapolate_velocity_second_order = . true . !! When true, the extrapolation kernel converts centroid momenta !! to velocities before reconstruction and back at the edge !! midpoints.  Much better behaved at wet/dry fronts. integer :: low_froude_mode = LOW_FROUDE_OFF !! Low-Froude correction mode for the central-upwind flux !! (LOW_FROUDE_OFF / _1 / _2). ! ----- boundary condition lookup table ----- ! Fixed-size integer array: lives inside the struct itself, so ! `map(to: state)` carries it across to the device automatically. integer :: bc_type ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = BC_WALL !! BC type for each boundary group `g = 1..MAX_BC_GROUPS`. real ( wp ) :: bc_eta_ext ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = 0.0_wp !! Per-group external stage (m) for `BC_TIDAL`. real ( wp ) :: bc_un_ext ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = 0.0_wp !! Per-group external normal velocity (m/s) for `BC_INFLOW`. real ( wp ) :: bc_h_ext ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = 0.0_wp !! Per-group external depth (m) for `BC_OUTFLOW`. real ( wp ) :: bc_Qn_ext ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = 0.0_wp !! Per-group specific discharge (m&#94;2/s) for `BC_DISCHARGE`. real ( wp ) :: bc_sponge_strength ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = 0.0_wp !! Sponge relaxation rate [1/s] per BC group (0 = inactive). !! Consumed by `apply_sponge_unstr`. Rides the struct copyin !! like `bc_eta_ext` — no separate device map needed. real ( wp ) :: bc_sponge_h_ref ( MAX_BC_GROUPS ) = 0.0_wp !! Sponge reference depth h_ref [m] per BC group. !! `apply_sponge_unstr` relaxes `h = stage - bed` toward this value. ! ----- timing + diagnostics ----- real ( wp ) :: dt = 0.0_wp !! Current timestep (s). real ( wp ) :: time = 0.0_wp !! Current simulation time (s). integer :: step_count = 0 !! Total steps taken since init. real ( wp ) :: mass_error = 0.0_wp !! Cumulative negative-mass clipped by `protect`. integer :: time_scheme = TIME_RK2 !! Explicit time integrator (`TIME_*` from rki_timestepper). !! Default RK2 reproduces the historical SSP-RK2 path bit-for-bit. !! 2D barotropic path only; multilayer keeps RK2. end type unstr_state_t public :: state_unstr_init public :: state_unstr_enable_si public :: state_unstr_destroy public :: state_unstr_enter_data public :: state_unstr_exit_data contains subroutine state_unstr_init ( state , mesh , nz_ml ) !! Allocate every array in `state` to match the cell counts in !! `mesh`. All arrays are zero-initialised.  Calling on an !! already-initialised state is safe -- it destroys first. !! !! When `nz_ml` is present and >= 1, the multilayer sub-object !! is initialised: `use_multilayer` is set and !! `state%multilayer` allocates per-layer arrays + tracer registry. !! If `nz_ml` is absent the state stays 2D depth-averaged. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ), optional :: nz_ml integer :: n call state_unstr_destroy ( state ) n = mesh % ncells_total state % ncells_owned = mesh % ncells_owned state % ncells_total = n call state % barotropic % init ( mesh ) call state % forcing % init ( mesh ) state % dt = 0.0_wp state % time = 0.0_wp state % step_count = 0 state % mass_error = 0.0_wp if ( present ( nz_ml )) then if ( nz_ml < 1 ) then call logger % error ( \"state_unstr: nz_ml must be >= 1 (got \" // & to_char ( nz_ml ) // \")\" ) return end if state % use_multilayer = . true . call state % multilayer % init ( mesh , nz_ml ) call logger % info ( \"state_unstr: multilayer enabled with nz_ml = \" // & to_char ( nz_ml )) end if call logger % info ( \"state_unstr: allocated for \" // to_char ( state % ncells_owned ) // & \" owned cells (\" // to_char ( n ) // \" total)\" ) end subroutine state_unstr_init subroutine state_unstr_enter_data ( state ) !! Map the unstructured state arrays into device memory. !! !! Called once after `state_unstr_init` and bathymetry/IC setup, !! before any kernel runs.  All subsequent kernel work happens !! on the device until `state_unstr_exit_data` is called. !! Mirrors `rki_solver::solver_enter_data`. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state ! Map the parent struct descriptor first so the device knows the ! shape of `unstr_state_t`.  Components (and the value-type ! sub-objects' allocatables) attach to it below.  Without the ! parent map first, NVHPC stdpar can't dereference component ! arrays from inside a do-concurrent body. !$acc enter data copyin(state) call state % barotropic % enter_data () call state % forcing % enter_data () if ( state % use_semi_implicit ) then call state % si % enter_data () end if if ( state % use_multilayer ) then call state % multilayer % enter_data () ! Generic tracer registry: two-step attach pattern (parent ! array descriptor first, then per-element hTr/hTr0).  Mirrors ! the structured `solver_tracers_enter_data`.  Without this, ! NVHPC stdpar can't dereference `tracers(it)%hTr` from a ! do-concurrent body and the kernel hits CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDRESS. if ( allocated ( state % multilayer % tracers )) then call tracers_enter_data ( state ) end if end if end subroutine state_unstr_enter_data subroutine tracers_enter_data ( state ) !! Per-element copyin for the tracer registry.  Split out so the !! enclosing routine stays linear. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state integer :: it !$acc enter data copyin(state%multilayer%tracers) do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) !$acc enter data copyin(state%multilayer%tracers(it)%hTr, & !$acc&                  state%multilayer%tracers(it)%hTr0) end do ! The device map above is an element-by-element snapshot: growing ! the registry after this point would strand every mapping. ! register_passive_tracer refuses while locked. state % multilayer % registry_locked = . true . end subroutine tracers_enter_data subroutine state_unstr_exit_data ( state ) !! Copy state arrays back from the device and release device !! memory.  Counterpart to `state_unstr_enter_data`. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state ! Components first, parent struct last (mirror of enter_data order). if ( state % use_multilayer ) then ! Generic tracer registry: per-element components first, then ! the array descriptor (mirror of enter_data order). if ( allocated ( state % multilayer % tracers )) then call tracers_exit_data ( state ) end if call state % multilayer % exit_data () end if if ( state % use_semi_implicit ) then call state % si % exit_data () end if call state % forcing % exit_data () call state % barotropic % exit_data () ! Parent struct descriptor last. !$acc exit data delete(state) end subroutine state_unstr_exit_data subroutine tracers_exit_data ( state ) !! Per-element copyout/delete for the tracer registry. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state integer :: it do it = 1 , size ( state % multilayer % tracers ) !$acc exit data copyout(state%multilayer%tracers(it)%hTr) !$acc exit data delete(state%multilayer%tracers(it)%hTr0) end do !$acc exit data delete(state%multilayer%tracers) state % multilayer % registry_locked = . false . end subroutine tracers_exit_data subroutine state_unstr_destroy ( state ) !! Release every allocatable array and reset counters. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state call state % barotropic % destroy () call state % multilayer % destroy () call state % forcing % destroy () call state % si % destroy () state % ncells_owned = 0 state % ncells_total = 0 state % dt = 0.0_wp state % time = 0.0_wp state % step_count = 0 state % mass_error = 0.0_wp state % use_multilayer = . false . state % use_semi_implicit = . false . state % dt_fixed = 0.0_wp end subroutine state_unstr_destroy subroutine state_unstr_enable_si ( state , mesh , precond , rtol , dt_fixed , ok , & wetdry , n_sub , bsub_fill ) !! Enable the semi-implicit (Casulli) free-surface mode on this state: !! run the fail-loud TPFA mesh-quality gate, allocate the `si` slot !! (with the P3.2 multilayer column slots when `use_multilayer`, AND/OR !! the P3.3 Casulli wet/dry slots when `wetdry` — the two slot groups !! gate independently, so 3D + wet/dry coexist), and stash the CG !! controls.  Call AFTER `state_unstr_init` (so the multilayer !! sub-state exists and `nz_ml` is known) and BEFORE !! `state_unstr_enter_data`.  `ok=.false.` (gate failure or a bad !! precond having already error-stopped) leaves `use_semi_implicit` !! off so the caller can abort cleanly. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: precond !! `SI_PRECOND_*` (already parsed; MG = aggregation multigrid here). real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rtol !! CG relative residual tolerance. real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt_fixed !! Fixed timestep (s); the SI mode bypasses the gravity-wave CFL. logical , intent ( out ) :: ok logical , intent ( in ), optional :: wetdry !! Casulli wetting/drying (2D barotropic + 3D sigma multilayer; !! the linear b_sub fill is 2D-only — see si_bsub_ml_conflict). !! Default .false. integer , intent ( in ), optional :: n_sub !! Subgrid sub-bottoms per cell (>= 1).  Default 1 (flat bottom). integer , intent ( in ), optional :: bsub_fill !! Sub-bottom fill mode (`SI_BSUB_FILL_*`).  Default 0 (FLAT). logical :: wd integer :: ns , nzml , bf wd = . false . if ( present ( wetdry )) wd = wetdry ns = 1 if ( present ( n_sub )) ns = max ( 1 , n_sub ) bf = 0 if ( present ( bsub_fill )) bf = bsub_fill ! CONSERVATION GUARD (fail-loud): the `linear` subgrid b_sub fill ! (n_sub >= 2) is INCOMPATIBLE with the multilayer (nz > 1) wet/dry ! step.  The free-surface eta-solve conserves the SUBGRID wetted volume ! v_cell(eta) = mean_s max(eta - b_sub_s, 0) (si_unstr_wetdry_volume), ! but `si_unstr_update_thickness_ml` and the recovery Dirichlet ghost ! consume max(eta - b, 0) on the PLAIN bed.  Under `flat` (b_sub == b) ! these are identical so mass conserves; under `linear` they diverge ! across the partial-flooding band => mass leaks at the wet/dry front — ! the exact defect the port exists to prevent.  A v_cell-consistent ML ! thickness update is a documented deferred limitation; until then ! `linear + ML` is rejected rather than run silently.  `flat + ML` ! (conservative, tested) and `linear + 2D` (barotropic uses v_cell ! throughout) both stay allowed. if ( si_bsub_ml_conflict ( bf , ns , state % use_multilayer , state % multilayer % nz_ml )) then call logger % error ( \"state_unstr_enable_si: wetdry_bsub_fill='linear' \" // & \"(n_sub>=2) is not supported with the multilayer \" // & \"(nz>1) wet/dry step — the ML thickness update \" // & \"consumes the plain bed, not the subgrid v_cell, so \" // & \"mass leaks at the wet/dry front.  Use \" // & \"wetdry_bsub_fill='flat' with multilayer, or 'linear' \" // & \"only with the 2D barotropic path.\" ) error stop \"state_unstr_enable_si: linear b_sub incompatible with multilayer wet/dry\" end if call mesh_unstr_si_quality_gate ( mesh , ok ) if (. not . ok ) return ! The multilayer column slots (nz>1) and the wet/dry slots gate ! INDEPENDENTLY in `si%init`, so 3D + wet/dry coexist: the ML wet/dry ! step (`si_unstr_step_ml`, wet/dry branch) reuses the mesh-agnostic ! V(eta)/a/Newton primitives + the dsig scale-together column drain. if ( state % use_multilayer . and . state % multilayer % nz_ml > 1 ) then nzml = state % multilayer % nz_ml call state % si % init ( mesh , nz = nzml , wetdry = wd , n_sub = ns ) else call state % si % init ( mesh , wetdry = wd , n_sub = ns ) end if state % si % bsub_fill = bf state % si % precond = precond state % si % rtol = rtol state % dt_fixed = dt_fixed state % use_semi_implicit = . true . ! Aggregation-MG preconditioner: v1 is the 2D barotropic path only ! (wet/dry Newton + multilayer column solves keep plain/Jacobi CG). ! Fail loud rather than silently ignore an MG request there. if ( precond == SI_PRECOND_MG ) then if ( wd . or . ( state % use_multilayer . and . state % multilayer % nz_ml > 1 )) then call logger % error ( \"state_unstr_enable_si: precond='mg' (aggregation \" // & \"multigrid) is 2D-barotropic only in v1 — the wet/dry \" // & \"Newton and multilayer column solves are not yet wired \" // & \"to the MG hierarchy.  Use precond='jacobi' with \" // & \"wet/dry or multilayer.\" ) error stop \"state_unstr_enable_si: mg precond not supported with wetdry/multilayer (v1)\" end if ! Build the (static) level hierarchy now (geometric aggregation; ! operator coefficients are filled per step by the refresh in the SI ! step).  Host-only; runs before enter_data. call state % si % build_mg ( mesh ) end if end subroutine state_unstr_enable_si end module rki_state_unstr","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_state_unstr.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.F90 – Rakali","text":"Second-order extrapolation kernel for the unstructured solver This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90 rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 rki_mesh_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 rki_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90 rki_barotropic_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 rki_boundary_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90 rki_multilayer_state_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_common.f90 rki_si_common.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90 rki_si_unstr_state.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90 sourcefile~rki_surface_forcing_unstr.f90 rki_surface_forcing_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_surface_forcing_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_timestepper.f90 rki_timestepper.F90 sourcefile~rki_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_timestepper.f90 sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_barotropic_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90 rki_eos.F90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_eos.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90 rki_tracer_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90 rki_vcoord.F90 sourcefile~rki_multilayer_state_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 rki_si_unstr_mg.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 sourcefile~rki_surface_forcing_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_surface_forcing_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_timestepper.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_eos.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_tracer_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_vcoord.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90 rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 rki_solver_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90 rki_api_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_api_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver_unstr.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Second-order extrapolation kernel for the unstructured solver module rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr !! Reconstruct cell-centroid values to edge midpoints with a per-cell !! linear gradient and slope limiter, in three passes (centroid prep, !! per-cell extrapolation, centroid restore). Cell loops are !! `do concurrent`: each iteration writes only to its own cell's !! edge-value arrays, and the pointwise helpers are all `pure`. use rki_constants , only : wp use rki_mesh_unstr , only : mesh_unstr_t use rki_state_unstr , only : unstr_state_t implicit none private public :: extrapolate_second_order_edge_unstr ! Slope-limiter / wet-dry blending constants. Defined locally so the ! `*_impl` helpers below inline in NVHPC device codegen (same TU). real ( wp ), parameter :: LIMITER_EPSILON = 1.0e-100_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: HFACTOR_A = 0.3_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: HFACTOR_B = 0.1_wp real ( wp ), parameter :: HFACTOR_C = 1.0_wp / ( HFACTOR_A - HFACTOR_B ) real ( wp ), parameter :: HFACTOR_D = 1.0_wp - HFACTOR_C * HFACTOR_A real ( wp ), parameter :: HFACTOR_HC_FLOOR = 1.0e-6_wp contains subroutine extrapolate_second_order_edge_unstr ( state , mesh ) !! Reconstruct edge-midpoint values from centroid values. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh call centroid_pass ( state , mesh ) call per_cell_extrapolation ( state , mesh ) call centroid_restore ( state , mesh ) end subroutine extrapolate_second_order_edge_unstr pure subroutine centroid_pass ( state , mesh ) !! Compute heights, zero momenta on dry cells, prep velocity-form. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer :: k real ( wp ) :: dk , xmom_out , ymom_out , inv_dk logical :: is_dry , do_extrap do concurrent ( k = 1 : mesh % ncells_total ) dk = max ( state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) - state % barotropic % bed_cv ( k ), 0.0_wp ) state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ) = dk is_dry = ( dk <= state % minimum_allowed_height ) do_extrap = state % extrapolate_velocity_second_order . and . . not . is_dry if ( is_dry ) then xmom_out = 0.0_wp ymom_out = 0.0_wp else xmom_out = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) ymom_out = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) end if if ( do_extrap ) then inv_dk = 1.0_wp / dk state % barotropic % x_centroid_work ( k ) = xmom_out state % barotropic % y_centroid_work ( k ) = ymom_out else inv_dk = 1.0_wp state % barotropic % x_centroid_work ( k ) = 0.0_wp state % barotropic % y_centroid_work ( k ) = 0.0_wp end if state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) = xmom_out * inv_dk state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) = ymom_out * inv_dk end do end subroutine centroid_pass pure subroutine per_cell_extrapolation ( state , mesh ) !! Compute edge-midpoint values for stage, height, xmom, ymom and !! recover bed_ev from the well-balanced identity. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer :: k do concurrent ( k = 1 : mesh % ncells_total ) call extrapolate_one_cell ( state , mesh , k ) end do end subroutine per_cell_extrapolation pure subroutine extrapolate_one_cell ( state , mesh , k ) !! Per-cell body of the extrapolation pass. Pure: never writes to !! any cell other than `k`. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: k real ( wp ) :: dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 real ( wp ) :: stage_ev_local ( 3 ), xmom_ev_local ( 3 ), ymom_ev_local ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: height_ev_local ( 3 ) integer :: i ! Edge-midpoint offsets from this cell's centroid. dxv0 = mesh % edge_mid_x ( 1 , k ) - mesh % centroid_x ( k ) dxv1 = mesh % edge_mid_x ( 2 , k ) - mesh % centroid_x ( k ) dxv2 = mesh % edge_mid_x ( 3 , k ) - mesh % centroid_x ( k ) dyv0 = mesh % edge_mid_y ( 1 , k ) - mesh % centroid_y ( k ) dyv1 = mesh % edge_mid_y ( 2 , k ) - mesh % centroid_y ( k ) dyv2 = mesh % edge_mid_y ( 3 , k ) - mesh % centroid_y ( k ) select case ( mesh % n_boundaries ( k )) case ( 3 ) ! Isolated triangle -- constant (zeroth-order) edge values. call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ), stage_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ), xmom_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ), ymom_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ), height_ev_local ) case ( 2 ) call extrapolate_one_neighbour_branch ( & state , mesh , k , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & stage_ev_local , xmom_ev_local , ymom_ev_local , height_ev_local ) case default ! 0 or 1 boundary edges -- full 3-neighbour reconstruction. call extrapolate_three_neighbour_branch ( & state , mesh , k , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & stage_ev_local , xmom_ev_local , ymom_ev_local , height_ev_local ) end select ! Velocity-form recovery: if on, xmom_ev/ymom_ev hold velocities; ! multiply by reconstructed height to recover momenta. if ( state % extrapolate_velocity_second_order ) then do i = 1 , 3 xmom_ev_local ( i ) = xmom_ev_local ( i ) * height_ev_local ( i ) ymom_ev_local ( i ) = ymom_ev_local ( i ) * height_ev_local ( i ) end do end if ! Commit edge values for this cell. do i = 1 , 3 state % barotropic % stage_ev ( i , k ) = stage_ev_local ( i ) state % barotropic % xmom_ev ( i , k ) = xmom_ev_local ( i ) state % barotropic % ymom_ev ( i , k ) = ymom_ev_local ( i ) state % barotropic % height_ev ( i , k ) = height_ev_local ( i ) ! Recover bed from the well-balanced identity, preserving ! stage_ev = bed_ev + height_ev exactly (lake-at-rest). state % barotropic % bed_ev ( i , k ) = stage_ev_local ( i ) - height_ev_local ( i ) end do end subroutine extrapolate_one_cell pure subroutine extrapolate_three_neighbour_branch ( & state , mesh , k , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & stage_ev_local , xmom_ev_local , ymom_ev_local , height_ev_local ) !! Full 3-neighbour reconstruction via the closed-form 2x2 !! gradient. The limiter β is blended wet->dry via `hfactor` so !! the slope dials down as cell/neighbours dry out. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: k real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: stage_ev_local ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: xmom_ev_local ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ymom_ev_local ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: height_ev_local ( 3 ) integer :: k0 , k1 , k2 real ( wp ) :: x0 , y0 , x1 , y1 , x2 , y2 real ( wp ) :: dx1 , dy1 , dx2 , dy2 , area2 , inv_area2 real ( wp ) :: hfactor real ( wp ) :: beta_stage , beta_xmom , beta_ymom k0 = mesh % surrogate_neighbours ( 1 , k ) k1 = mesh % surrogate_neighbours ( 2 , k ) k2 = mesh % surrogate_neighbours ( 3 , k ) x0 = mesh % centroid_x ( k0 ) y0 = mesh % centroid_y ( k0 ) x1 = mesh % centroid_x ( k1 ) y1 = mesh % centroid_y ( k1 ) x2 = mesh % centroid_x ( k2 ) y2 = mesh % centroid_y ( k2 ) dx1 = x1 - x0 dy1 = y1 - y0 dx2 = x2 - x0 dy2 = y2 - y0 area2 = dy2 * dx1 - dy1 * dx2 ! Collinear/coincident neighbours -> area2 vanishes; fall back to ! constant edge values. if ( abs ( area2 ) <= 1.0e-30_wp ) then call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ), stage_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ), xmom_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ), ymom_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ), height_ev_local ) return end if inv_area2 = 1.0_wp / area2 hfactor = compute_hfactor_impl ( state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ), & state % barotropic % height_cv ( k0 ), & state % barotropic % height_cv ( k1 ), & state % barotropic % height_cv ( k2 ), & state % minimum_allowed_height ) beta_stage = state % beta_w_dry + ( state % beta_w - state % beta_w_dry ) * hfactor beta_xmom = state % beta_uh_dry + ( state % beta_uh - state % beta_uh_dry ) * hfactor beta_ymom = state % beta_vh_dry + ( state % beta_vh - state % beta_vh_dry ) * hfactor call calc_edge_values_three_neighbours_impl ( & state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ), state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k0 ), state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k1 ), state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k2 ), & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & dx1 , dx2 , dy1 , dy2 , inv_area2 , & beta_stage , stage_ev_local ) call calc_edge_values_three_neighbours_impl ( & state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ), state % barotropic % height_cv ( k0 ), state % barotropic % height_cv ( k1 ), state % barotropic % height_cv ( k2 ), & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & dx1 , dx2 , dy1 , dy2 , inv_area2 , & beta_stage , height_ev_local ) call calc_edge_values_three_neighbours_impl ( & state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ), state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k0 ), state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k1 ), state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k2 ), & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & dx1 , dx2 , dy1 , dy2 , inv_area2 , & beta_xmom , xmom_ev_local ) call calc_edge_values_three_neighbours_impl ( & state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ), state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k0 ), state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k1 ), state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k2 ), & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & dx1 , dx2 , dy1 , dy2 , inv_area2 , & beta_ymom , ymom_ev_local ) end subroutine extrapolate_three_neighbour_branch pure subroutine extrapolate_one_neighbour_branch ( & state , mesh , k , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & stage_ev_local , xmom_ev_local , ymom_ev_local , height_ev_local ) !! Two-boundary fallback: gradient taken toward the single internal !! neighbour, displacement normalised by squared distance: !! `dq * (dx, dy)/|dx,dy|&#94;2 . (xv, yv)`. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( in ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer , intent ( in ) :: k real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: stage_ev_local ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: xmom_ev_local ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: ymom_ev_local ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: height_ev_local ( 3 ) integer :: i , kn real ( wp ) :: dx , dy , dist2 real ( wp ) :: grad_dx2 , grad_dy2 real ( wp ) :: dq1 , qmin , qmax real ( wp ) :: dqv ( 3 ) ! Find the single internal neighbour. kn = k do i = 1 , 3 if ( mesh % surrogate_neighbours ( i , k ) /= k ) then kn = mesh % surrogate_neighbours ( i , k ) exit end if end do if ( kn == k ) then ! Should not happen for n_boundaries == 2, but be defensive. call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ), stage_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ), xmom_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ), ymom_ev_local ) call set_constant_edge_values_impl ( state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ), height_ev_local ) return end if dx = mesh % centroid_x ( kn ) - mesh % centroid_x ( k ) dy = mesh % centroid_y ( kn ) - mesh % centroid_y ( k ) dist2 = dx * dx + dy * dy if ( dist2 > 0.0_wp ) then grad_dx2 = dx / dist2 grad_dy2 = dy / dist2 else grad_dx2 = 0.0_wp grad_dy2 = 0.0_wp end if ! Stage dq1 = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( kn ) - state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) call calc_dqv_one_neighbour_impl ( dq1 , grad_dx2 , grad_dy2 , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , dqv ) call qrange_one_diff_impl ( dq1 , qmin , qmax ) call limit_gradient_impl ( dqv , qmin , qmax , state % beta_w ) stage_ev_local ( 1 ) = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 1 ) stage_ev_local ( 2 ) = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 2 ) stage_ev_local ( 3 ) = state % barotropic % stage_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 3 ) ! Height dq1 = state % barotropic % height_cv ( kn ) - state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ) call calc_dqv_one_neighbour_impl ( dq1 , grad_dx2 , grad_dy2 , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , dqv ) call qrange_one_diff_impl ( dq1 , qmin , qmax ) call limit_gradient_impl ( dqv , qmin , qmax , state % beta_w ) height_ev_local ( 1 ) = state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 1 ) height_ev_local ( 2 ) = state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 2 ) height_ev_local ( 3 ) = state % barotropic % height_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 3 ) ! x-momentum dq1 = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( kn ) - state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) call calc_dqv_one_neighbour_impl ( dq1 , grad_dx2 , grad_dy2 , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , dqv ) call qrange_one_diff_impl ( dq1 , qmin , qmax ) call limit_gradient_impl ( dqv , qmin , qmax , state % beta_uh ) xmom_ev_local ( 1 ) = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 1 ) xmom_ev_local ( 2 ) = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 2 ) xmom_ev_local ( 3 ) = state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 3 ) ! y-momentum dq1 = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( kn ) - state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) call calc_dqv_one_neighbour_impl ( dq1 , grad_dx2 , grad_dy2 , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , dqv ) call qrange_one_diff_impl ( dq1 , qmin , qmax ) call limit_gradient_impl ( dqv , qmin , qmax , state % beta_vh ) ymom_ev_local ( 1 ) = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 1 ) ymom_ev_local ( 2 ) = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 2 ) ymom_ev_local ( 3 ) = state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) + dqv ( 3 ) end subroutine extrapolate_one_neighbour_branch pure subroutine centroid_restore ( state , mesh ) !! If velocity-form extrapolation was on, restore the original !! centroid momenta from the work arrays. type ( unstr_state_t ), intent ( inout ) :: state type ( mesh_unstr_t ), intent ( in ) :: mesh integer :: k if (. not . state % extrapolate_velocity_second_order ) return do concurrent ( k = 1 : mesh % ncells_total ) state % barotropic % xmom_cv ( k ) = state % barotropic % x_centroid_work ( k ) state % barotropic % ymom_cv ( k ) = state % barotropic % y_centroid_work ( k ) end do end subroutine centroid_restore ! Inlined pointwise helpers (`*_impl`): self-contained pure helpers ! in the same TU as `extrapolate_one_cell` so NVHPC device codegen ! inlines them. pure subroutine qrange_one_diff_impl ( dq1 , qmin , qmax ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dq1 real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: qmin , qmax if ( dq1 >= 0.0_wp ) then qmin = 0.0_wp qmax = dq1 else qmin = dq1 qmax = 0.0_wp end if end subroutine qrange_one_diff_impl pure subroutine qrange_three_diff_impl ( dq0 , dq1 , dq2 , qmin , qmax ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dq0 , dq1 , dq2 real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: qmin , qmax qmax = max ( dq0 , dq0 + dq1 , dq0 + dq2 , 0.0_wp ) qmin = min ( dq0 , dq0 + dq1 , dq0 + dq2 , 0.0_wp ) end subroutine qrange_three_diff_impl pure subroutine limit_gradient_impl ( dqv , qmin , qmax , beta ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: dqv ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: qmin , qmax , beta real ( wp ) :: r , phi , d integer :: i r = 100 0.0_wp do i = 1 , 3 d = dqv ( i ) if ( d < - LIMITER_EPSILON ) then r = min ( r , qmin / d ) else if ( d > LIMITER_EPSILON ) then r = min ( r , qmax / d ) end if end do phi = min ( r * beta , 1.0_wp ) dqv ( 1 ) = dqv ( 1 ) * phi dqv ( 2 ) = dqv ( 2 ) * phi dqv ( 3 ) = dqv ( 3 ) * phi end subroutine limit_gradient_impl pure subroutine calc_edge_values_three_neighbours_impl ( & cv_k , cv_k0 , cv_k1 , cv_k2 , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & dx1 , dx2 , dy1 , dy2 , inv_area2 , & beta , edge_values ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: cv_k , cv_k0 , cv_k1 , cv_k2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dx1 , dx2 , dy1 , dy2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: inv_area2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: beta real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: edge_values ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: dq0 , dq1 , dq2 real ( wp ) :: a , b real ( wp ) :: dqv ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: qmin , qmax dq0 = cv_k0 - cv_k dq1 = cv_k1 - cv_k0 dq2 = cv_k2 - cv_k0 a = ( dy2 * dq1 - dy1 * dq2 ) * inv_area2 b = ( dx1 * dq2 - dx2 * dq1 ) * inv_area2 dqv ( 1 ) = a * dxv0 + b * dyv0 dqv ( 2 ) = a * dxv1 + b * dyv1 dqv ( 3 ) = a * dxv2 + b * dyv2 call qrange_three_diff_impl ( dq0 , dq1 , dq2 , qmin , qmax ) call limit_gradient_impl ( dqv , qmin , qmax , beta ) edge_values ( 1 ) = cv_k + dqv ( 1 ) edge_values ( 2 ) = cv_k + dqv ( 2 ) edge_values ( 3 ) = cv_k + dqv ( 3 ) end subroutine calc_edge_values_three_neighbours_impl pure subroutine calc_dqv_one_neighbour_impl ( & dq1 , dx2 , dy2 , & dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 , dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 , & dqv ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dq1 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dx2 , dy2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dxv0 , dxv1 , dxv2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dyv0 , dyv1 , dyv2 real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: dqv ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: a , b a = dq1 * dx2 b = dq1 * dy2 dqv ( 1 ) = a * dxv0 + b * dyv0 dqv ( 2 ) = a * dxv1 + b * dyv1 dqv ( 3 ) = a * dxv2 + b * dyv2 end subroutine calc_dqv_one_neighbour_impl pure subroutine set_constant_edge_values_impl ( cv_k , edge_values ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: cv_k real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: edge_values ( 3 ) edge_values ( 1 ) = cv_k edge_values ( 2 ) = cv_k edge_values ( 3 ) = cv_k end subroutine set_constant_edge_values_impl pure function compute_hfactor_impl ( hc , h0 , h1 , h2 , min_h ) result ( hfactor ) !$acc routine seq real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: hc , h0 , h1 , h2 , min_h real ( wp ) :: hfactor real ( wp ) :: hmin , hmax , tmp1 , tmp2 hmin = min ( hc , h0 , h1 , h2 ) hmax = max ( hc , h0 , h1 , h2 ) tmp1 = HFACTOR_C * max ( hmin , 0.0_wp ) / max ( hc , HFACTOR_HC_FLOOR ) + HFACTOR_D tmp2 = HFACTOR_C * max ( hc , 0.0_wp ) / max ( hmax , HFACTOR_HC_FLOOR ) + HFACTOR_D hfactor = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( tmp1 , tmp2 , 1.0_wp )) hfactor = min ( 1.2_wp * max ( hmin - min_h , 0.0_wp ) & / ( max ( hmin , 0.0_wp ) + min_h ), hfactor ) end function compute_hfactor_impl end module rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_kernel_extrapolate_unstr.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_kernel_sponge.F90 – Rakali","text":"Sponge layer relaxation kernel This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_kernel_sponge.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge.f90 rki_kernel_sponge.F90 sourcefile~rki_boundary_types.f90 rki_boundary_types.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge.f90->sourcefile~rki_boundary_types.f90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 rki_grid.F90 sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_boundary_types.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90 rki_config.F90 sourcefile~rki_boundary_types.f90->sourcefile~rki_config.f90 sourcefile~rki_grid.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common_unstr.f90 rki_ml_common_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_common_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_nml_schema.f90 rki_nml_schema.F90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90->sourcefile~rki_nml_schema.f90 sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90 rki_recon_weno.F90 sourcefile~rki_config.f90->sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_nml_schema.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90->sourcefile~rki_grid.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90 rki_ml_common.F90 sourcefile~rki_recon_weno.f90->sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90 sourcefile~rki_ml_common.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~rki_kernel_sponge.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge.f90 rki_kernel_sponge.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 rki_solver.F90 sourcefile~rki_solver.f90->sourcefile~rki_kernel_sponge.f90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90 rki_api.F90 sourcefile~rki_api.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90 rki_driver.F90 sourcefile~rki_driver.f90->sourcefile~rki_solver.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !! Sponge layer relaxation kernel module rki_kernel_sponge !! Volumetric damping in interior cells near sponge boundaries, with a !! quadratic profile alpha(d) = strength*((width - d)/width)&#94;2 where d !! is the distance in cells from the nearest sponge boundary. use rki_constants , only : wp use rki_boundary_types , only : bc_params_t , BC_SPONGE use rki_grid , only : hgrid_t implicit none private public :: apply_sponge contains pure subroutine apply_sponge ( h , hu , hv , grid , dt , bc ) !! Apply sponge layer relaxation to h, hu, hv !! !! Cells within sponge_width of a sponge boundary are relaxed toward !! h_ref with hu_ref = hv_ref = 0. No-op when sponge_width <= 0. type ( hgrid_t ), intent ( in ) :: grid real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: h ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hu ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: hv ( grid % nx_total , grid % ny_total ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dt !! Timestep (s) type ( bc_params_t ), intent ( in ) :: bc !! Boundary condition parameters (sponge config) integer :: i , j , i_first , i_last , j_first , j_last integer :: nx , ny , nghost integer :: sw , d_west , d_east , d_south , d_north , d_min real ( wp ) :: alpha , ratio , h_ref , strength logical :: has_west , has_east , has_south , has_north nx = grid % nx_total ny = grid % ny_total nghost = grid % nghost sw = bc % sponge_width if ( sw <= 0 ) return strength = bc % sponge_strength h_ref = bc % sponge_h_ref if ( strength <= 0.0_wp ) return i_first = nghost + 1 i_last = nx - nghost j_first = nghost + 1 j_last = ny - nghost has_west = ( bc % west == BC_SPONGE ) has_east = ( bc % east == BC_SPONGE ) has_south = ( bc % south == BC_SPONGE ) has_north = ( bc % north == BC_SPONGE ) do concurrent ( j = j_first : j_last , i = i_first : i_last ) & local ( d_west , d_east , d_south , d_north , d_min , alpha , ratio ) ! Compute distance from each sponge boundary (in cells) d_min = sw + 1 ! Start beyond sponge width (no damping) if ( has_west ) then d_west = i - i_first if ( d_west < sw ) d_min = min ( d_min , d_west ) end if if ( has_east ) then d_east = i_last - i if ( d_east < sw ) d_min = min ( d_min , d_east ) end if if ( has_south ) then d_south = j - j_first if ( d_south < sw ) d_min = min ( d_min , d_south ) end if if ( has_north ) then d_north = j_last - j if ( d_north < sw ) d_min = min ( d_min , d_north ) end if if ( d_min < sw ) then ratio = real ( sw - d_min , wp ) / real ( sw , wp ) alpha = strength * ratio * ratio h ( i , j ) = h ( i , j ) - dt * alpha * ( h ( i , j ) - h_ref ) hu ( i , j ) = hu ( i , j ) - dt * alpha * hu ( i , j ) hv ( i , j ) = hv ( i , j ) - dt * alpha * hv ( i , j ) end if end do end subroutine apply_sponge end module rki_kernel_sponge","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/rki_kernel_sponge.f90.html"},{"title":"rki_si_unstr_state.F90 – Rakali","text":"Semi-implicit free-surface solver state (unstructured triangular 2D barotropic). This file depends on sourcefile~~rki_si_unstr_state.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90 rki_si_unstr_state.F90 sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 rki_constants.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 rki_mesh_unstr.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 rki_si_unstr_mg.F90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_state.f90->sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90 sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_constants.f90 sourcefile~rki_si_unstr_mg.f90->sourcefile~rki_mesh_unstr.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier 